(172, 72, 1001, 102853, 1072936800, 'Steam Beta 2.0 Starts Today', 'Steam Beta 2.0 begins today at 3 pm Pacific. The beta is open to the public, anyone can join by downloading and running the 4MB install applet.\n\n\n\nFor the first few days, this beta will include the coming versions of Counter-Strike (1.6) and Team Fortress Classic. Further updates to these games, as well as additional content, will be made available to participants throughout the beta.\n\n\n\nSteam is a broadband platform for the delivery and management of digital content. More information on Steam and this beta can be found at http://www.steampowered.com. (http://www.steampowered.com.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13465, 2425, 1026, 102173, 1072936800, 'Come Test My Admin Mod Server', 'just got adminmod to work come test it at 216.141.219.69:27015\n\n\n\nsee what you think its a dedicated T1 in Atlanta !!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13468, 2425, 1026, 102174, 1072936800, 'Yep', 'I just went and tried it out.  It works.  It even had some statsme action going on. []\n\n\n\nYay.\n\n\n\nPost how to do it, please.\n\n\n\n\n\n-Mr. Lugosi', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13657, 2425, 1026, 102175, 1072936800, '', 'how did you install metamod? i didnt find a way to install it ... []\n\n__________________\n\n-=[D.I.F]=-Pum@KA - www.team-dif.com -', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13793, 2425, 1026, 102176, 1072936800, '', 'Please post the details of your server configuration.\n\n\n\nadmin mod ver?\n\nmeta mod ver?\n\n\n\nANd how in the world did you get it to work??\n\n\n\nYou Da MAN.\n\n\n\nbtw.....im in atlanta too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13865, 2425, 1026, 102173, 1072936800, 're admin mod', 'adminmod 2.50.50  the lastest metamod released yesterday.\n\nthe way i did it was install it into my regular cstrike then took the files to my steam dedicated server counter-strike folder you must have knowlege of installing admin mod to try this... the metamod dll you need is 1.14 you can get it from there website. if you try the install to steam it cant find the exe so make sure you have regular cs installed on your server if you already have it installed just copy it and change the metamod.dll  goodluck !\n\n\n\nboth server of mine now have it 216.141.219.69 and 128.186.2.125    enjoy  \n\n\n\nthe only prob i have had is changing maps in cant find the mapcycle.txt anyone have an idea on how to fix it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(13936, 2425, 1026, 102177, 1072936800, '', 'I was actually able to get admin mod to install directly to the steam folder.  Just hit cancel when it asked for registry search and typed in:\n\n\n\nc:\\Program Files\\Steam\\SteamCache\\Dedicated Server\\hlds.exe\n\n\n\nMust only work for some users.  Then updated metamod like you said.\n\n\n\nGot statsme working also.  Maps seem to change normally.\n\n\n\nOnly thing I\'ve noticed is that the server lags now, especially when the client spk is going on (like when the bomb counts down).  Disabling that took away a lot of lag, but it still does more than before the mods.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14008, 2425, 1026, 102173, 1072936800, '', 'yes any speach you want to disable i noticed that same thing in beta 1.4 ..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14102, 2425, 1026, 102178, 1072936800, '', 'tell me how to add admins. In the users.ini file. i tried\n\nEX:      STEAM_0:94631::131071\n\n\n\nit might look wierld because i have a diff. way of getting access on my server. I do WONID::131071 on my server. it works. But i am a bit confused on my 1.6 server.  Wouldnt it mistake the \n\nSTEAM_0:94631 as 94631 as the password when actualy its my authid.\n\nim confused', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14269, 2425, 1026, 102179, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ithinkthere4iam \n\nI was actually able to get admin mod to install directly to the steam folder.  Just hit cancel when it asked for registry search and typed in:\n\n\n\nc:\\Program Files\\Steam\\SteamCache\\Dedicated Server\\hlds.exe\n\n\n\nMust only work for some users.  Then updated metamod like you said.\n\n\n\nGot statsme working also.  Maps seem to change normally.\n\n\n\nOnly thing I\'ve noticed is that the server lags now, especially when the client spk is going on (like when the bomb counts down).  Disabling that took away a lot of lag, but it still does more than before the mods.  \n\n\n\nThanks All, got mine up and running this morning as a reslult of all your posts.  Since it seems SM laggs it, I did not include it.  Damn thing filled up before I could join it too.  Son of a Bitch, gona have to reserver a few slots, hopefullly that element of adminmod works.  []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14419, 2425, 1026, 102180, 1072936800, '', 'I have a problem with mine, it gives me an error saying:\n\n\n\n[ADMIN] ERROR:\n\n\n\nYou must define either "admin_plugin_file" or "script_file" in your adminmod.cfg file before you can use Admin Mod.\n\nGo to http://www.adminmod.org/help/online/ (http://www.adminmod.org/help/online/) for more details.\n\n\n\ndoes anyone know how to fix this.\n\n\n\nThanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14457, 2425, 1026, 102178, 1072936800, '', 'that is a simple mistake . go to www.adminmod.org (http://www.adminmod.org) and click on forums.  do a search onthe forums for that and u will find something. its very easy to fix. \n\n\n\nSOMONE HELP ME ABOUT MY USERS.INI', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14481, 2425, 1026, 102179, 1072936800, '', '501 I had the same problem.  all it was is that I forgot to add\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n// Execute the Admin Mod configuration file\n\nexec addons/adminmod/config/adminmod.cfg\n\n\n\n\n\nTo my server.cfg file.  Once I did that it was cake.\n\n\n\nNow I kinda have the same problem that Mr. Lugosi has.  My admins are in the users.ini file but how do I authenticate when i log in.  I know how to do it with 1.5 but that is not working so well with 1.6.\n\n\n\nThanks in advance.  And yes i am headed over to the admin mod fourms to see what I can see there.\n\n\n\nThanks All!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(14670, 2425, 1026, 102181, 1072936800, 'Hmmmm', 'I did all this, made a folder in my SteamCache/Counter-strike/cstrike called addons like in my 1.5 folder (is this right) and what about liblist.gam? what do i change in there, i have tried running my server, but it doesnt seem to work with adminmod, (does it have to be dedicated?!?) mines just the good old, create server thing, and in the create server, how do i create a server name, no matter what i tried changing, it didnt work [] can someone please help?\n\n\n\nMSN/EMAIL CONTACT: black_fire66@hotmail.com (mailto:black_fire66@hotmail.com)\n\non CS: -|STAF|-SpydeR\n\n1.6 Friends: use email (black_fire66@hotmail.com)\n\nhelp would be greatly appreciated\n\n\n\n*EDIT-Sorry about so many questions  []-EDIT*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(16344, 2425, 1026, 102180, 1072936800, '', 'thanks everyone', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(17399, 2425, 1026, 102182, 1072936800, 'Only level 1 Access?', 'Having set adminmod up with 1.6 I only seem to have level 1 access with my users.ini set up using the SteamID::AccessLevel method.\n\n\n\nWhen I type admin_password blah I only have 16 commands. I have had adminmod working before (with 1.5) but whatever I do it won\'t work with 1.6.\n\n\n\nAnyone had this problem and know how to resolve this situation? If you need any more info to help you figure out my problem please let me know! I hate having to switch off my server just to get rid of someone who is constantly spamming/TK\'ing/nibbling teammates ect!\n\n\n\nThanks\n\nHellcat\n\n__________________\n\nWork or i\'ll bit ya! GRRR', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(15770, 2817, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 2/28 Release', 'We\'ve released an update to Steam this morning. This release does not contain the changes specific to Counter-Strike, that will come out later this week. If you exit Steam and restart now, you will automatically download this update.\n\n\n\nChanges in this release are:\n\n- Progress bar when downloading Steam desktop elements works properly now.\n\n- Friends network server capacity increased.\n\n- Fixed bug in Friends that would cause long pauses when bringing up friends list. This \n\nfix only applies to the desktop version of Friends.\n\n- Load balancing improved when downloading content for the desktop elements of Steam.\n\n\n\nThe Counter-Strike release is currently scheduled for later this week. The details of this next release can be found by right clicking on Counter-Strike in your Games list, clicking on Properties, and then clicking on �Update History�.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(15772, 2817, 1013, 100247, 1072936800, 'Steam 2/28 Release', 'quote:Originally posted by Erik Johnson \n\nWe\'ve released an update to Steam this morning. This release does not contain the changes specific to Counter-Strike, that will come out later this week. If you exit Steam and restart now, you will automatically download this update.\n\n\n\nChanges in this release are:\n\n- Progress bar when downloading Steam desktop elements works properly now.\n\n- Friends network server capacity increased.\n\n- Fixed bug in Friends that would cause long pauses when bringing up friends list. This \n\nfix only applies to the desktop version of Friends.\n\n- Load balancing improved when downloading content for the desktop elements of Steam.\n\n\n\nThe Counter-Strike release is currently scheduled for later this week. The details of this next release can be found by right clicking on Counter-Strike in your Games list, clicking on Properties, and then clicking on �Update History�.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson\n\nValve  \n\n\n\nSweet dude i\'m downloading it now, i love you []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(15775, 2817, 1013, 100022, 1072936800, '', 'nice. Gotta get that now!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(15777, 2817, 1013, 102174, 1072936800, '...', 'Ooh, updating platform dll to version 3! sexy.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(15780, 2817, 1013, 102266, 1072936800, 'Steam 2/28 Release', 'quote:Originally posted by Erik Johnson \n\nThe Counter-Strike release is currently scheduled for later this week.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson\n\nValve  \n\n\n\nSweet, can\'t wait.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
