(18113, 3193, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, 'Shield still allows bullet penetration when strafing...', 'Just finished off a series of Aztec, Cobble, and Militia with the latest 1/31/03 update and confirmed that the shield still is letting bullets penetrate when strafing. \n\n\n\nI tested standing still, crouching, crouch moving in all directions, walking and running in all directions, and jumping in all directions, with shield both deployed in front and undeployed to the side. In all cases the shield only blocked bullets when standing still, crouching, jumping, or walking/running/crouch walking/jumping forward and backward. But side strafing (running/walking/crouch walking), side jumping, and diagonal (2 arrow keys) strafeing & jumping let bullets through. \n\n\n\nBasically any movement that requires the left or right arrow to strafe allowed bullet penetration. The same effect occurs against knife slashes and stabs. They are blocked except when in a strafe movement.\n\n \n\nAnother bug is that with shield both deployed and undeployed, a player can not jump forward-left, left or rear-left when walking or crouching, only when running.\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18116, 3193, 1005, 102348, 1072936800, '', 'If you notice, when running left or right (strafing) various body parts tend to move outside of the shield\'s protection.  That may be what\'s up.  Many a time have I seen people\'s legs pop out of the shield when strafing and killed them because of it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18119, 3193, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah I am aware of that effect except I intetnionally altered standing still and strafing when someone was shooting right at my shield, and the times when the strafe arrows were pressed was when the bullets were penetrating. Also when walking or crouching while strafeing and facing the enemy, the arms are not exposed as much as when running outright. I\'m positive there were no arm/leg hits occurring to the side of the shield, as the people shooting at me were aiming center mass.\n\n\n\nThe biggest indication was the times I was crouching with shield deployed and facing the enemy directly. The movement speed is practically non existent when crouching with a deployed shield. When I tapped the left and right arrows the bullets were clearly penetrating, and when the arrow keys were released the shield blocked the bullets. There was no movement to expose arms or legs in those cases.\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18141, 3193, 1005, 102349, 1072936800, '', 'u\'r right  RaptorRage \n\n \n\n because even if people shot in the legs sheild can avoid thing like head shot cause everybody know that one bullet in the leg dont frag... so i thing there is a bug to fix and it is also te case for the buymenu []...\n\n__________________\n\nif there is no solution there is no probleme... so visite www.bluefox.fr.st and enjoy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18324, 3193, 1005, 102141, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Khaos \n\nIf you notice, when running left or right (strafing) various body parts tend to move outside of the shield\'s protection.  That may be what\'s up.  Many a time have I seen people\'s legs pop out of the shield when strafing and killed them because of it.  \n\n\n\nI have learned to awp shield carriers in the ass when it sticks out from behind the shield as they try to move. They are only truly protected when they are ducking and staying still.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18378, 3193, 1005, 100276, 1072936800, '', 'Valve has to fix this.. The shield should block at all times, otherwise it\'s pretty much useless..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18416, 3193, 1005, 102266, 1072936800, '', 'Shield is not useless, it\'s just filled with bugs and remember it\'s still beta for 3 weeks. :\\', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18671, 3193, 1005, 102350, 1072936800, '', 'ye shield is still fu*ked :\'((((((((((([]\n\n__________________\n\nProm3theus was the wisest Titan. His name means "forethought" and he was able to foretell the future\n\n\n\nIRC.quakenet.org #TsC.uT', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18685, 3193, 1005, 102141, 1072936800, '', 'I have noticed that since the last update that the shield is much harder to kill. I think you guys need to look at how the shield carriers are getting hit. I have been watching the movements of shield carriers and have noticed that body parts are exposed as they crawl and the body hitbox must extend out past the shield where the ass sticks out. It doesn\'t take much strafe movement to the side to get a shot on a piece of exposed body. It doesn\'t look like much but try shooting the ass with a scout and you\'ll see its not hard to hit. In close range a fast strafe spray will get a piece of that exposed hitbox. The freeze effect of getting hit further ensures that you will strafe around the shields faster than the shield carrier can turn towards you. He really is only safe when crouching still, but forward rushes combined with a jump and firing down from above will kill them quick.\n\n\n\nIt appears that the shield takes quite a bit of skill to use properly. It is only really effective when used with another player with a rifle. Its great for drawing fire so the guy with the rifle has the first shot in most instances. I have forced my self not to shoot the shield first and go for the guy with the rifle. But if the shield carrier is smart he will then open up and has a great chance to kill me with a pistol.\n\n\n\nThe shield is very effective as it is currently implemented, but it does require alot of skill. It is important to realize this and know the the level of protection the shield actually provides. It is most vulnerable from side angle attacks of about 40 degrees from either side. It doesn\'t take much strafing to get into that position and get that first shot which stuns. Like I said above this only compounds the problem for the shield carrier because it stuns them allowing the opponent to strafe further with each shot exposing more each time. Its a additive  effect once they are hit.\n\n\n\nI have not witnessed any headshots through the shield since the last update while the carrier is crouching. I think this latest patch has found a great balance and users must realize when they are exposed and understand that to carry a sheild alone takes great skill. It is best to team up with a guy with a rifle. Thats is the most effective strategy, not only does it allow your team the first shot (from the rifle or you depending on who the opponent goes for first) but it also prevenst the enemy from being able to strafe and to a shallow agle that leasves you exposed.\n\n\n\nGo with a rifle teamate and when you see an enemy duck and hold still. You won\'t get alot of kills but your team will and you won\'t take much damage either. Your only real oppurtunity for kills with the shield is when the enemy fires at the rifle backup first. Then it is your turn to open up and blast them. If the enemy shifts targets to you the the shield still offers limited protection and hopefully the opponent is injured enough that a few landed shots takes him out.\n\n\n\nThe shield is very balanced when you understand how to use it and how you get killed with it. There is almost no side protection. Use the buddy system and your team will benifit from your shield.\n\n\n\nI did not even go into how it effects enemy movement through choke points which is a whole other bonus. Quick example is the bridge on Aztec. This choke point is a whole new animal now with CT shields. Same with the double doors if the T\'s don\'t rush through before they set up and draw fire so the snipers have the first shots.\n\n\n\nThe last bonus for your team from using hte shield is greater ammo consumtion by the other team. I am always on my last clip at the end of the round and I am having to pickup guns as I go while playing Aztec or Dust2 because of the amount of players and choke points. The shields require more ammo to pin down.\n\n\n\nSorry but your not a tank with the sheild if you\'re alone and crouching still.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18698, 3193, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'I agree with some of the operational abilities of the shield noted above, however in my tests it was definately not bullets hitting an exposed hitbox. The bullets were penetrating the shield itself, and headshots were occurring through the shield frequently during those tests. The shield certainly is not a tank, in that it\'s a 2-d slab that only protects the front of the user and is only effective directly facing the enemy, however it should not suffer from penetration bugs while strafing the way it currently does.\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18727, 3193, 1005, 102351, 1072936800, '', 'The strafe thing is true. \n\n\n\nAnother problem I have with the shield is when you are in a vent of under some stairs with a shield and the shield sticks out and lets people know you are there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18754, 3193, 1005, 102352, 1072936800, '', 'What do you want? A tiny piece of shield that no one will ever be able to see, yet will stop anything that is shot at you, no matter which way you are moving.  I have a feeling that if the game introduced "invisible, non-penetrable body armor, you guys would forego buying guns at all, and just "BE SAFE".  Cmon now, lets get real, obviously the shield cant stop every bullet while you are MOVING, if it did, everyone would have a shield.  \n\n\n\nSo stop thinking that the shield is supposed to be the best thing since sliced bread, and learn to use it properly.  And in my opinion, properly does not include working perfectly while moving, running and jumping.\n\n\n\n-Agent', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18777, 3193, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'If the shield is meant to block bullets, and a bullet hits the shield while the user is moving sideways, the bullet should not penetrate, because it hit the shield. There\'s no problem if the bullet hits exposed parts of the player behind the shield, but if it is supposed to be impenetrable it should be so all of the time. \n\n\n\nAs to the clipping issue in vents, that specifically occurs mostly on assault, and will just have to be dealt with, unless the shield is made "solid" like a player model rather than intangible to the map like the weapons are(they stick into and through walls, doors and crates). Of course if the shield was made solid to the rest of the map environment, then you wouldn\'t even be able to enter the vent in the first place.\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18895, 3193, 1005, 102353, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, I got some weird thing: What if u r a terrorist holding only a dual berreta (nevemind the spelling). Will you be able to pick up the shield. If yes, will u be only be able to use one berreta??\n\n__________________\n\n">.< ">.< ">.<', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(18963, 3193, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'The shield can\'t be used with Dual Berettas at all. No nifty single Beretta modification for shield. So the shield works with knife (no stab), USP (no silencer), Glock (no burst), Deagle, P228, 5-7 and grenades. When a Terrorist takes out the bomb the shield just disappears completely. Must be some big pockets or other voluminous spaces that the shield is put into, probably the same place snipers put thier AWP\'s when not in use... [] []\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(20634, 3587, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 2/14 Release', 'We\'re released a new version of our products on the Steam beta. Servers will need to be restarted to come back online. If you launch your game you will automatically update.\n\n\n\nChanges are as follows:\n\n\n\nAll Games:\n\n- Fixed netgraph. \n\n\n\nDedicated Server:\n\n- Complete reworking of the user interface.\n\n\n\nCounter-Strike\n\n- Fixed streetlamp in Inferno \n\n- Fixed floating staircases in Inferno \n\n- Fixed bullet penetration problem with railings in Inferno \n\n- Fixed bug where you could throw the bomb to a place where it could not be picked up in Aztec \n\n- Fixed spawn kill probelm in Aztec \n\n- Swapped door orientation back at CT spawn \n\n- Fixed silent plant bug at A in Airstrip \n\n- Added sign crate to B in Airstrip \n\n- Fixed bug where players would get stuck behind a tree near bridge from the T spawn in Airstrip \n\n- Added in ability to buy items by name to allow for scripting. Item names are: \n\n\n\nPistols\n\n-------\n\n"glock"\n\n"usp"\n\n"p228"\n\n"deagle"\n\n"elites"\n\n"fn57"\n\n"ak47"\n\n\n\nShotguns\n\n--------\n\n"m3"\n\n"xm1014"\n\n\n\nSMG\n\n---\n\n"mac10"\n\n"tmp"\n\n"mp5"\n\n"ump45"\n\n"p90"\n\n\n\nRifles\n\n------\n\n"galil"\n\n"scout"\n\n"sg552"\n\n"awp"\n\n"g3sg1"\n\n"famas"\n\n"m4a1"\n\n"aug"\n\n"sg550"\n\n\n\nMachine Gun\n\n-----------\n\n"m249"\n\n\n\nAmmo\n\n----\n\n"primammo"\n\n"secammo"\n\n\n\nEquipment\n\n---------\n\n"defuser"\n\n"vest""shield"\n\n"vesthelm"\n\n"flash"\n\n"hegren"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(20635, 3587, 1013, 100247, 1072936800, '', 'Sweet updating now...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
