(22834, 3905, 1013, 102440, 1072936800, 'How to stop Steam from loading when your computer boots up.', 'I wrote this as an e-mail to my semi-computer illiterate friend (so please don\'t take offense to the hand-holding nature of it) since Steam caused major instability by just running on his computer.  I figure at least a few people out there might want to know how to do this too.\n\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1.  Go to the start menu and pick the "Run" option.\n\n\n\n2.  Type in "regedit."  It\'ll bring up a window with a bunch of "HKEY" blabbity blah folders.\n\n\n\n3.  The main directory for everything is "My Computer" so the path you want to go to is:\n\n\n\n"My Computer\\HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Microsoft\\\n\nWindows\\CurrentVersion\\Run"\n\n\n\n4.  In there you\'ll see a list of stuff that starts up as your computer first enters Windows.  Just delete the one that has the path to "...steam.exe" and that should stop Steam from starting up from now on.\n\n\n\nThat\'s it, just close the Registry Editor and the next time you start your computer, you won\'t accidentally start Steam up with it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(22954, 3905, 1013, 102351, 1072936800, '', 'Or you could do it the easy way... Type \'msconfig\' into the RUN box, go to STARTUP and unclick Steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(23037, 3905, 1013, 102448, 1072936800, '', 'the first one keeps the registry cleaner []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(23069, 3905, 1013, 100827, 1072936800, '', 'also, when going the regedit route, remember to back up the registry just in case something gets screwed up', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(23533, 3905, 1013, 100589, 1072936800, '', 'When does the registry ever get screwed up?\n\n\n\n*runs*\n\n__________________\n\nwww.NTFS.org\n\nMember of the elusive -=Xp0=- Clan', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(23646, 3905, 1013, 102449, 1072936800, '', 'I really would recommend using the "msconfig" method.  Editing the registry should always be considered the last result.\n\n\n\nAlso using msconfig, allows you to easily enable Steam on startup if you ever decide you\'d like it back.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(23696, 3905, 1013, 102450, 1072936800, '', 'I would have to say that anyone who doesn\'t know how, or needs to ask how to keep steam from starting with windows would be well advised to use the \'msconfig\' method, rather then the regedit method. Editing your registry isn\'t that difficult of a task, but for an inexperianced user it could cause problems that would force them to format their machine.\n\n\n\nIf your reading this topic in order to find out how to stop steam from loading with windoes then please take my advise and use the method that BetteMidler described above. Its simple and gets the job done without  causing any headaches.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(24867, 4134, 1013, 102491, 1072936800, 'I Have A Found A Fix That Will Stop The Freezing!', 'Hey guys! I found a fix that will stop the freezing until they release the patch. I too like many of you have a problem freezing when the game loads and the server rules pop up.. \n\n\n\nThis occurs on map changes in Day of defeat for thos with winxp.. To remedy that problem I run DoD in Compatibility mode with win98/me and it fixes it. So I figured hey why not run steam like that. So I ran steam in compatibility mode for win 98/me and it worked! I just got done playing for an hour and a half through two map changes. To do so all u have to do is right click on yer steam shortcut on your desktop and go to the compatibility tab. Set it to win 98/me compatibility, apply it and run the game. \n\n\n\nIt totally works! Hope this helped everyone...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
