(34292, 5501, 1013, 102700, 1072936800, 'Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'If Valve can update your CS or half life program anytime thru Steam. What would stop a hacker disguised as Valve employee (or plain hacker plugging into Steam) to write subroutines in the half life program update where it can be asked to read your entire hard disk, or activate your web cam to see into your room? We can ask antivirus to detect trojan, but in Steam where any file can be integrated right inside Half Life anytime, what would stop writing program subroutines to read hard disk,etc.?\n\n\n\nPeter', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(34294, 5501, 1013, 102281, 1072936800, '', 'Your system is really un-secure if anyone can just replace your Steam files..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(34296, 5501, 1013, 102701, 1072936800, 'Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by Peter Rye \n\nIf Valve can update your CS or half life program anytime thru Steam. What would stop a hacker disguised as Valve employee (or plain hacker plugging into Steam) to write subroutines in the half life program update where it can be asked to read your entire hard disk, or activate your web cam to see into your room? We can ask antivirus to detect trojan, but in Steam where any file can be integrated right inside Half Life anytime, what would stop writing program subroutines to read hard disk,etc.?\n\n\n\nPeter  \n\n\n\ndude your paranoid. but your right. there is a certain ammount of trust associated with steam. i bet the number of people at valve that have the ability to do updates is very limited. for that exact reason.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(34309, 5501, 1013, 102702, 1072936800, 'Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by Peter Rye \n\nIf Valve can update your CS or half life program anytime thru Steam. What would stop a hacker disguised as Valve employee (or plain hacker plugging into Steam) to write subroutines in the half life program update where it can be asked to read your entire hard disk, or activate your web cam to see into your room? We can ask antivirus to detect trojan, but in Steam where any file can be integrated right inside Half Life anytime, what would stop writing program subroutines to read hard disk,etc.?\n\n\n\nPeter  \n\n\n\nWTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!!\n\n\n\nhave u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is\n\n\n\ncs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. \n\n\n\nplus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe]\n\n\n\njust get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(34314, 5501, 1013, 102270, 1072936800, '', 'look if u get a firewall sure it will stop programs to acess the internet and  prevent people from reading files\n\n\n\n but the firewall says if it is ok for that program to use the internet\n\n\n\nWhat peter is saying  that a hacker goes THROUGH steam and if u let steam acess the internet it is only "STEAM" that is affected and the so called "hacker" uses its skill and programs  through steam. And it can look at ur files.\n\n\n\nso the firewall is use less \n\n\n\nbut it is good to have one on your pc\n\n\n\nalthough i think it is impossible for that to happen buddy unless a group of terrorists took over valve and forced a program to be uploaded to ur pc updating steam causing them to acess ur pc easily\n\n\n\nalthough that would never happen \n\n\n\nWho would want to take over Valve?\n\nI can see y someone would threaten them by blowing them up because they keep delaying the date of CS 1.6, CZ, or CS 1.7, but not take over\n\n\n\nhahahahahahahhaha []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(34316, 5501, 1013, 102701, 1072936800, 'Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by Neo Vortex \n\nWTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!!\n\n\n\nhave u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is\n\n\n\ncs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. \n\n\n\nplus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe]\n\n\n\njust get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry \n\n\n\ndude all a firewall does is block unrequested internet traffic. simply put, the way a firewall works is as follows. you open/run a program that access the net. the firewall sees this, looks to its list of filters/rules. if it finds one that matches then it allows traffic in both directions. so for someone to \'hack\' the steam system they would have to do it from inside.\n\n\n\nthat being said. nothing is 100% secure. i garentee you that if  serious hacker/cracker, not these little script kiddes that download sh*t off the net and click the \'go\' button, want to get inside your box there is no firewall/router/proxy server/nat server that will stop him/her. everything has a vunerability. everything.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44518, 5501, 1013, 100114, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by StargateX196 \n\n\n\nWho would want to take over Valve?\n\nI can see y someone would threaten them by blowing them up because they keep delaying the date of CS 1.6, CZ, or CS 1.7, but not take over\n\n\n\nhahahahahahahhaha []  \n\n\n\nBump, and I think Microsoft might consider taking over Valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44603, 5501, 1013, 102703, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Raging_Wulf \n\nBump, and I think Microsoft might consider taking over Valve.  \n\n\n\nThey might! I\'m sure they want HL and CS on thei X-Box! GOD! We\'ll have new 56k players! lol (only if Valve implements a multi-player feature)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44604, 5501, 1013, 102703, 1072936800, 'Re: Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by oDin \n\ndude all a firewall does is block unrequested internet traffic. simply put, the way a firewall works is as follows. you open/run a program that access the net. the firewall sees this, looks to its list of filters/rules. if it finds one that matches then it allows traffic in both directions. so for someone to \'hack\' the steam system they would have to do it from inside.\n\n\n\nthat being said. nothing is 100% secure. i garentee you that if  serious hacker/cracker, not these little script kiddes that download sh*t off the net and click the \'go\' button, want to get inside your box there is no firewall/router/proxy server/nat server that will stop him/her. everything has a vunerability. everything.  \n\n\n\nFirewalls have multiple functionalities (i have a linux one myself: Astaro). But the main function of a firewall is to block ports. But it is mainly in one direction: incomming. Because there is no use of blocking outgoing ports, except if you are a parent and don\'t want your children to use certain programs on the net, or you want to make people use a logged proxy, so you block port 80 and open another one. So again, the only way people would be able to hack your computer via Valve (even though they wouldn\'t b/c it is much easier with emails and other ways), they would have to modify Steam so it runs their programs everytime someone starts Steam, and then could hack Valve\'s servers to make an update... But if haxors were to hack Valve, they would erase the data because they hate Steam... [] \n\n\n\nFrankly, if you guys are that paranoid, you could also start on Windows\' breaches... You could switch to linux if you want. But remember: Choose between easy utilization, or security. Consider nothing being between those two.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44607, 5501, 1013, 100768, 1072936800, 'good points all around...', 'good points all around but the fact remains that if you have a firewall and can use steam to play cs, then you can have a firewall and have someone use steam to play you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44608, 5501, 1013, 102704, 1072936800, 'Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by Neo Vortex \n\nWTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!!\n\n\n\nhave u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is\n\n\n\ncs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. \n\n\n\nplus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe]\n\n\n\njust get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry  \n\n\n\nThis guy made a big fool of himself', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44609, 5501, 1013, 100768, 1072936800, 'Re: Isn\'t Steam Dangerous?', 'quote:Originally posted by Neo Vortex \n\nWTF ARE U TALKING ABOUT!!!!!\n\n\n\nhave u ever heard of a thing called a FIREWALL???? if not go find out what one is\n\n\n\ncs 1.5 has a system very similar to steam accept in a diiferent format. \n\n\n\nplus, no one can log into someones computer using steam its impossible the only way the can is if someone invents a super program which can hack into steam. if so it would have come up on www.elitehackers.com (http://www.elitehackers.com) a site from which you can dowload hacking and scamming programs [i visit it sometimes hehe]\n\n\n\njust get a firewall and no one can hack into your comp dont worry  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI totally agree.  Anyone who searches a publicly advertised domain such as "elitehackers.com" isnt really that leet anyway...not to mention it didnt take a superprogram to hack the gibson in "hackers" now did it...lol...jp', '127.0.0.1', 1),
