(41736, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, 'AWM reload bug', 'Right. This bug has been around forever and a lot of awm whores are abusing it. Basically it comes down to bug exploit.\n\n\n\n1) fire awm\n\n2) when reload starts switch to other weapon so you can shoot \n\n3) switch back to awm to find it reloaded and ready to fire\n\n\n\nyou don\'t have to wait for the awm to reload before you can fire again. and even tho "the leagues" accept this bug exploit, it\'s still a bug. i mean, it doesn\'t work with any other weapon, so can the people at VALVe _PLEASE_ fix this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41767, 6748, 1013, 101891, 1072936800, '', 'They already fixed it in 1.4, added a pause between gun switching for all guns which basically is the same length of time it would take to switch from pistol back to awp and shoot again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41869, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'actually, they didn\'t fix it. not in 1.4, not in 1.5 and not in 1.6 either.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41911, 6748, 1013, 102799, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, they did fix it. The only reason they still do this, is to get rid of the black out, so you can see the whole screen for a time. This helps a lot when you are awping, as you have a broader range of view for a short period of time, and any good awper would be able to pick people out in that time.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41939, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'actually, you can still have the awm reload while you pull out your pistol. give it a try.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41941, 6748, 1013, 102799, 1072936800, '', 'Time it, takes exactly the same amount of time. This has be gone over before, the fact is, you\'re wrong.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41942, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'The point is not how long it takes. The point is that while the awm is reloading you can switch to your pistol and fire that, and then switch back to your freshly reloaded awm, instead of having to wait for the awm to reload before you can shoot again.\n\n\n\nTry it with the scout. You\'ll see that while the reload is happening and you switch to pistol and back, the gun is not reloaded.\n\n\n\nAnd what just hits me: it\'s not reload as in pop in a new clip, it\'s the bolt action to reload the barrel. Altho that\'s just mincing words, I just thought I\'d mention that as well.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(41948, 6748, 1013, 102799, 1072936800, '', 'The time it takes to reload is the same as it is to switch back and forth, with scout it doesnt make a difference as the reload action is much faster, in general it makes no real difference.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42063, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s NOT ABOUT THE TIME it takes to reload.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42180, 6748, 1013, 102799, 1072936800, '', 'You don\'t get it do you. By them time you have switched to pistol and back, if you hadn\'t done that it would have reloaded already, the fact that when you switch back that it is reloaded, when you haven\'t actually reloaded it, doesn\'t make a difference.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42185, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'no, apparently you\'re the one who\'s not getting it. all i am saying is that you can fire your awm, and while it is reloading  fire your pistol, then switch back to the awm and fire that cuz it\'s ready to fire. \n\n\n\ni don\'t give a damn about the time it takes to reload the awm. it doesn\'t matter. it\'s not part of the problem. i\'m not saying i can reload my awm faster by switching to my pistol. ok? \n\n\n\nall i am saying is, that when someone is coming at you and you fire your awm, you can press reload, switch to pistol and keep firing, then switch back to awm and fire that, increasing your chances of killing that person after you missed the first shot. \n\n\n\ni know what you mean, but that is not what i am talking about.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42188, 6748, 1013, 102799, 1072936800, '', 'Shoulda described it better... My bad then.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42194, 6748, 1013, 102798, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Invader Zim \n\nIt\'s NOT ABOUT THE TIME it takes to reload.  \n\n\n\nSeems to be quite clear.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42195, 6748, 1013, 102800, 1072936800, '', 'The AWM has been a point of much heated discussion. Personally I am able to shoot a AWM of hand without zoom or use the zoom to shoot one guy and when there\'s someone standing anywhere near the person I shot aim and shoot him without zooming.\n\n\n\nI know it\'s just a game but with a weapon like an AWM there is no way you can hit anything unless you first take very carefull aim, which takes time. In CS you can just flip out a AWM and shoot anybody without even trying to aim.\n\n\n\nI feel that when you pull out an AWM for the first second or so it should be really inaccurate, thus simulating the aiming.\n\n\n\nSecond I agree with Zim. When you are reloading an AWM and intterupt the reload then the reload should start from 0 when you pull it out again. This goes for every weapon in CS btw.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42196, 6748, 1013, 100705, 1072936800, '', 'I would like to thank you people that use AW/M over awp since THEY ARENT the same gun. Thanks for keeping it straight[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42227, 6831, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 6/20 Release', 'We�ve released a new version of Steam, Counter-Strike, and Team Fortress Classic to the Steam beta.\n\n\n\nExit Steam and restart to receive the update.\n\n\n\nChanges in this update (also available here /platfor...ter-strike.html (/platform/update_history/counter-strike.html))\n\n\n\nChanges/Additions:\n\n \n\n- Server browser will display an icon next to servers that have bots playing in them. \n\n- Player list dialog now shows the friends name of all the other players on the server. \n\n- Counter-Strike new game dialog now remembers the map you selected and uses that as the default for next time. \n\n- Made knife secondary attack do significantly more damage if hitting someone in the back. \n\n- Optimized new weather effects. \n\n- Disabled Video Mode drop down menu if the video card can\'t display Widescreen modes. \n\n- Fixed random characters appearing at the end of the map overview description (on the team page) \n\n- Changed Counter-Strike text chat so Spectators can chat with dead players. \n\n- Bots only swing knife when in range to hit now. \n\n- Bots use both primary and secondary knife attacks. \n\n- Bots will try to sneak up behind victims if they are using a knife. \n\n- Bots crouch more when shooting at distant targets. \n\n- Bots jump much less during combat now. \n\n- If a bot sees a friend get killed by an unseen enemy, and it has no enemy, it acquires the killer as its enemy. \n\n- Throttled how often nav meshes are drawn (confused fast video cards). \n\n- All games are ready for Steam Linux server release. \n\n- Team Fortress Classic dedicated server will now appear in server list.\n\n\n\nBug Fixes:\n\n\n\n- Fixed font drawing problems with Windows 98/ME. \n\n- Fixed splash screen not drawing correctly in software mode. \n\n- Fixed HUD sprites not drawing correctly in OpenGL. \n\n- Fixed progress bar for launching dedicated server. \n\n- Fixed Shield/Knife model playing wrong idle animation while deployed. \n\n- Fixed Shield/Knife model using the wrong knife model. \n\n- Fixed bug where bots were finding hiding spots on floors above/below that took far too long to reach. \n\n- Bots no longer aim at enemy\'s leg with sniper rifles. \n\n- Bots wont jump after using hostages now. \n\n- Fixed bug where bots would aim at the ground if in combat with an enemy and the enemy went behind cover.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42231, 6831, 1013, 102812, 1072936800, '', 'i get an error with the new steam.\n\n\n\ncheck this forum post: /forums/...p;threadid=6832 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=6832)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42232, 6831, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, '', 'I saw that on the other thread.\n\n\n\nSomeone should be contacting you to figure out what the probelm is.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42233, 6831, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'I kept getting those errors... I just kept ending the Steam process and starting it again until the platform files finished loading. Took a while, but I think it worked...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42234, 6831, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, '', 'Try this for now:\n\n\n\n1. E-Mail me any *.mdmp files (erik@valvesoftware.com).\n\n2. Delete everything in your Steam install directory except your /config directory (and your config file in \\SteamCache\\<username>\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.\n\n3. Run Steam again.\n\n\n\nThis will likely get you running again, but I\'d like to know what caused this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42235, 6831, 1013, 102813, 1072936800, '', 'Its well fux0red for me... after the update it didnt restarted... ok it restarted but the process was stalled for alog time and needed to kill it via task manager.. Restarting the computer has no effect... guess i\'ll need to reinstall it... []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42236, 6831, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Erik Johnson \n\nTry this for now:\n\n\n\n1. E-Mail me any *.mdmp files (erik@valvesoftware.com).\n\n2. Delete everything in your Steam install directory except your /config directory (and your config file in \\SteamCache\\<username>\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.\n\n3. Run Steam again.\n\n\n\nThis will likely get you running again, but I\'d like to know what caused this.  \n\n\n\nAlright... I can\'t get CS to start at all now, and I get the Precondition Assertion error every time I start Steam instead of every time I exit...\n\n\n\nEDIT:\n\n\n\nWOW... that\'s a lot of .MDMP files!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42237, 6831, 1013, 102813, 1072936800, '', 'Ok deleting SteamCache directoy seemed to work for me... Steam now is working and redownloading de game files..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42238, 6831, 1013, 102814, 1072936800, '', 'eric i have a problem with VAC.\n\nWhen i have my server in secure mode, people cannot join and get this error:\n\n quote:*******************************************\n\n*******\n\n*\n\nYour connection has been terminated because of\n\nmemory corruption on your computer.\n\n\n\nFor help resolving this problem, visit:\n\nhttp://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html (http://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html)\n\n\n\nIf you continue playing without resolving\n\nthis problem, your computer may trigger\n\nHalf-Life\'s anti-cheat system, causing\n\nyou to be banned from playing on secure\n\nservers.\n\n **************************************************\n\n\n\n\n*\n\n \n\n\n\nthanks for any feedback Eric, im assuming you already know about this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
