(42230, 6832, 1013, 102812, 1072936800, 'problem with steam update 6/20', 'pardon the colors of these pictures, i saved them as Gifs and it fugglyed them.\n\n\n\n\n\nafter steam updated I got this error after it logged back on:\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.soporific.org/misc/steam1.gif (http://www.soporific.org/misc/steam1.gif) \n\n\n\n\n\nthen after clicking retry like it recommended:\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.soporific.org/misc/steam2.gif (http://www.soporific.org/misc/steam2.gif) \n\n\n\n\n\nthen the box closed and when i tried to run steam again I got this:\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.soporific.org/misc/steam3.gif (http://www.soporific.org/misc/steam3.gif) \n\n\n\n\n\ni restarted after this hoping it would fix the problem but when I ran steam again it just started the cycle all over again', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42419, 6832, 1013, 100517, 1072936800, '', 'Restart, start steam, select ignore...\n\n__________________\n\nwww.cs-land.ro', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42422, 6832, 1013, 102817, 1072936800, '', 'in real...i saw these bugs N times...\n\n\ni only "retry"...about 2 times...if the steam icon dispairs...\n\n\nbut the steam.exe is not gone in ur windows...\n\n\nu can use taskmgr.exe(xp/2000) to close the "steam.exe", & open again the steam again...\n\n\ntry untill u can load the game...\n\n\n\n\n\ntrust me...it\'s possible...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42284, 6844, 1013, 100694, 1072936800, 'Platform 12/13 Bug List', 'Ok, we\'re going to start fresh.  Please report all bugs here:\n\n\n\nBugs:\n\n- say command changes a semicolon to a comma\n\n- First click once in game does nothing.  Happens also when you press esc and come back.\n\n- Fonts at low resolutions\n\n- In the scoreboard, connecting players appear to have the last team and ping of a player who has previously left, and this player will appear to have this ping, team, and also appear to be dead until this player actually connects.\n\n- Dedicated Server is unavailable\n\n\n\nSuggestions:\n\n- Fonts still too large\n\n- Make all maps have 32 spawn points', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42292, 6844, 1013, 102420, 1072936800, '', 'Version 12 has changed something with the fonts. I have an ATI 9800 Pro video card, and when I run CS or TFC the fonts for the server browser, options, and other in-game windows has become all fuzzy looking, a lot like the pictures other people were posting before today\'s update.  I like to run these games in OpenGL mode with 4xFSAA & 16xAF (ATI\'s quality settings), and if I turn off FSAA and AF the fonts return to looking normal, like they did for me with FSAA & AF on in the previous version of CS & TFC.\n\n\n\nThat\'s too bad... I liked running these games in ATI\'s quality settings but at least I have a workaround, or I can try to learn to read fuzzy fonts.\n\n\n\nBTW, I am using the latest ATI 3.4 Drivers, and ATI is expected to release the next version very soon.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42295, 6844, 1013, 102822, 1072936800, '', 'that semicolumn thing in the say command happens in CS 1.5 too so i wouldnt call it a bug.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42298, 6844, 1013, 102823, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Pfc.Dunsel \n\nVersion 12 has changed something with the fonts. I have an ATI 9800 Pro video card, and when I run CS or TFC the fonts for the server browser, options, and other in-game windows has become all fuzzy looking, a lot like the pictures other people were posting before today\'s update.  I like to run these games in OpenGL mode with 4xFSAA & 16xAF (ATI\'s quality settings), and if I turn off FSAA and AF the fonts return to looking normal, like they did for me with FSAA & AF on in the previous version of CS & TFC.\n\n\n\nThat\'s too bad... I liked running these games in ATI\'s quality settings but at least I have a workaround, or I can try to learn to read fuzzy fonts.\n\n\n\nBTW, I am using the latest ATI 3.4 Drivers, and ATI is expected to release the next version very soon.  \n\n\n\nI have the same problem. \n\n\n\nI\'m running a Radeon 9700 Pro.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42303, 6844, 1013, 100827, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by super jah \n\nI have the same problem. \n\n\n\nI\'m running a Radeon 9700 Pro.  \n\n\n\ngot the same problem with geforce 4 ti4600 with latest drivers', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42306, 6844, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'I have a Geforce FX 5200 and don\'t have that problem... then again, I have antialiasing off. It really makes no difference in Counter-strike other than lower your FPS anyway, based on what I have noticed with a few different Geforce cards. I recommend setting it to "Application Controlled" on your graphics card so that it will work with other applications, and try turning it off in Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\nWait a second... I did have antialiasing on. I\'ve never had that problem, unless I was using D3D mode. If FSAA is D3D-specific, then that might be the problem. I\'m really not sure though, I\'ve never been fond of ATI cards. They always seem to have strange compatibility issues.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42311, 6844, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m not entirely sure if CS bugs go here also, but this one\'s very old:\n\n\n\nA bug that\'s bugged me for the longest time: In the scoreboard, connecting players appear to have the last team and ping of a player who has previously left, and this player will appear to have this ping, team, and also appear to be dead until this player actually connects. This often causes confusion in games, as people will check the scoreboards and notice that the teams appear to be uneven when in reality they are not.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42313, 6844, 1013, 102422, 1072936800, '', 'Damn, Nvidia really screwed us ATI users since they started being content hosters. \n\n\n\n- Initial Cs menu is very blurry\n\n- Steam is not updating(i reinstalled to try and get rid of previous inconvience)\n\n- Nvidia is @ it again... jk. \n\n\n\ngeneral specs: 9500 pro 128mb 8x agp, AMD 2100, 512mb, Turtle beach santa cruz sound card, and Windows XP.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42315, 6844, 1013, 102824, 1072936800, '', 'Im not sure if this is considered a bug or not but I really hate that you cant move while buying weapons...In 1.5 I can buy on the run.....Is it just me or does this feel awkward to others also ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42316, 6844, 1013, 102422, 1072936800, '', 'If steam doens\'t update just keep restarting until you get a new content hoster. It took me a while because i keep getting NVIDIA but i don\'t like them so i had to wait until i got redphive or fileplanet. lol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42326, 6844, 1013, 102825, 1072936800, '', 'Being frozen at the beginning of a round is a server side command that can be changed. The command mp_freezetime changes how long you are frozen for at the beginning of each round, it is not a bug.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42333, 6844, 1013, 100827, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by s0ulknight \n\nBeing frozen at the beginning of a round is a server side command that can be changed. The command mp_freezetime changes how long you are frozen for at the beginning of each round, it is not a bug.  \n\n\n\nafter the freeztime u can move around and still buy items.  u can\'t in the beta.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42335, 6844, 1013, 101849, 1072936800, '', 'Can valve PLEASE fix the no sound bug when you alt+tab??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42344, 6844, 1013, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'If you buy a shield at the beginning of a map before the game comences you will still have the shield in the next round, rather than it being cleared. Occurs when starting money is high enough to purchase shield.\n\n\n\nSeems in some cases there is no audio message when the bomb is planted or when a team wins by bombing or defusing. I don\'t think it\'s a silent plant bug related to the map.\n\n\n\nSome join lag/freeze experienced when the client requests all the pldecal.wad files from the server at once. The console shows the spam for all the requests in one shot rather than spreading them out like in 1.5\n\n\n\nWhen carrying a shield and crouching, you can\'t jump left, forward+left or backward+left. Granted that\'s probably not a maneuver used much from that position but it seems odd the other directions are not affected. Note this doesn\'t affect crouch jumping as in jumping first then pressing crouch to get onto ledges and such, however if crouch is pressed first when moving in the left directions then the player can\'t jump.\n\n\n\n\n\n---------------\n\nAnd on a more positive note it appears the shield strafe bug was finally squashed with the 6/20 release, and to boot the bullet impacts significantly slow the movement of the shield user, which is a good addition. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(42362, 6844, 1013, 102826, 1072936800, '', 'the fuzzy font think is an aa issue. i have a geforce 5200 and when i have aa set to 2x i get that if i have it set to application or off i dont. so its not just for the ati guys.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(44708, 7251, 1005, 100989, 1072936800, 'How To Use Custom Spray/logo', 'Okay, how do it...\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:HOW TO USE CUSTOM SPRAYS! \n\n\n\n\n\n1) Take your custom spray, which should be a file called pldecal.wad.\n\n\n2) Paste it under c:\\...\\steam\\steamcache\\emailaccount\\counter-strike\\cstrike\\\n\n\n3) Select overwrite\n\n\n4) Delete custom.hpk and custom.hp2(If it exists)\n\n\n5) Right click on pldecal.wad, and select properties.\n\n\n6) Here, set it\'s attribute to READ ONLY. This will prevent Steam from overwritting the file EVER AGAIN! Neat huh?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:EXAMPLE OF MAKING A SPRAY (Read more into thread for BETTER detail...) \n\n\nHere is visual proof of a spray in the making.\n\n\nThis is one i made last night, works, and kicks alot of ass!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nA picture you want to make into a spray... (http://dumbasstm.com/silenthunters/mylogo_noedit.jpg) \n\n\n\n\n\nI then took this pic, resized it to 64x128pixels, and reduced color depth to 256 colors (using the optimized octree(sp) method). \n\n\n\n\n\nFinally, I set the 255th color on the pallet to pure blue(0 0 255), and since this pic has no other pure blue colors in the pallet, I am done! All i need to do is compile it. The new spray formatted pic should look like this... (http://dumbasstm.com/silenthunters/mylogo.bmp) \n\n\n\n\n\nAnd there you have it! Visual proof that manual works better than those crappy spray makers!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThere ya go, enjoy!\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you have any issues, post here and I will resolve them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(45156, 7251, 1005, 102870, 1072936800, '', 'sweet =D\n\n\nif u do that in 1.5 will it prevent it from overrighting wen u goto customize?\n\n__________________\n\nnobody is perfect....im nobody', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(45195, 7251, 1005, 102436, 1072936800, '', 'or you could just search for the friggin info.\n\n\n\n\n\nthat\'s been posted about 15 times now.\n\n__________________\n\nmy old sig was pretty lame.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(45254, 7251, 1005, 100989, 1072936800, '', 'Yes it does apply to 1.5 as well. I just got this stickied since i\'m sick of being asked how to do it.\n\n__________________\n\n~Neme, the Soujiro\'ed one', '127.0.0.1', 1),
