(46247, 7496, 1013, 100589, 1072936800, '', 'Why would it change the gameplay?\n\n\n\n- Fixed the radar (old)\n\n- Fixed the scoreboard (old)\n\n- New version of aztec\n\n- Fixed steam shutdown issue\n\n\n\nIt\'s not like it is the final release or anything.\n\n__________________\n\nAdministrator - http://www.NTFS.org', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46250, 7496, 1013, 102724, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LittleTootie#1 \n\ndoes it change the gameplay at all what so ever? has it fixed any mistakes in counter strike that have been around since it was first released? no it just adds more junk we don\'t need or don\'t even notice.. Get your head out of your ass, Steam isnt just for CS you know, Maybe you should try playing on a super old version of Steam (you can\'t) and compare it to these new fixes, you will find a huge diffrence, quit bitching and thank the guys who make Steam for improving it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46251, 7496, 1013, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LittleTootie#1 \n\ndoes it change the gameplay at all what so ever? has it fixed any mistakes in counter strike that have been around since it was first released? no it just adds more junk we don\'t need or don\'t even notice..  \n\n\n\nHave you not been paying attention to the hundreds of changes and fixes made since January? Those not playing the beta will be completely blown away when 1.6 is released to the public. And Steam allows for constant updates even after final release, it\'s not like something will be set in stone and unchangeable for a year.\n\n\n\nAnd if you looked closer at the latest update, it fixes the radar disappearing bug, the first mouse click not registering bug, the bug not letting Steam properly shut down on exit as well as numerous other gameplay changes and additions, like Aztec slightly reworked to give the T\'s more advantage for rushing double doors.\n\n__________________\n\n"Interesting. The Emperor will want a prototype immediately." -Darth Vader', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46268, 7496, 1013, 100591, 1072936800, '', 'quote:YES!! ANOTHER POINTLESS UPDATE! I JUST LOVE HOW VALVE JUST KEEPS LISTENING TO OUR SUGGESTIONS! \n\n\n\nu c if steam holds all these updates from (platform 9 and on) and give the whole thing to us today, then u will not think it is \n\nquote:POINTLESS \n\n\n\nso f-off steams ass and be thankful that they update this fast.\n\n__________________\n\nCounter-Strike F*R*E*A*K*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46279, 7496, 1013, 102421, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m glad to hear that the new update will take care of some of the problems I have been experiencing.  It isn\'t pointless and everything that is being updated and fixed is doing so for a reason. \n\nGreat job guys on the updates!!!!!!!!![]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46280, 7496, 1013, 100440, 1072936800, '', 'You have no say in anything\n\nthey only pay attention to you if you have an actual bug report\n\nsad sad truth\n\neither that or they just like seeing you cry, so they\'re making you wait for the more convinient updates\n\n__________________\n\nAsshole by nature', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(46419, 7496, 1013, 101849, 1072936800, '', 'hmm, this new update won\'t really affect me....except for the fixing the quit bug....thats good...but you know what\'d be great?...if valve could fix the no radio bug after you alt+tab to windows. Oh well, i\'ve waited for months...another one won\'t hurt.\n\n\n\nquote:Fixed bug where first mouse click wouldn\'t work after exiting the UI. \n\n\n\nIs this the bug where you can\'t shoot the first time? If it is, then I\'ll be happy to see the end of it []\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam is improving. A few more updates to fix some pesky bugs, and it\'ll be great []\n\n__________________\n\nHTML code is OFF\n\nvB Code is OFF\n\n[img] code is OFF\n\nSmilies are ON \n\nSteam is OFF\n\n\n\n-RIP Steam 4 Platform 10-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
