(47124, 7623, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 7/4 Release', 'We\'ve released a new version of Counter-Strike and the dedicated servers (Win32 and Linux).\n\n\n\nYou don\'t need to exit Steam to get the update, it will automatically download when you launch Counter-Strike. Your dedicated servers should automatically update as well.\n\n\n\nThere are a few items from yesterday\'s reverted release that will have to wait until next week. Here is the actual changelog for today\'s:\n\n\n\nChanges:\n\n- Bots now buy armor more often. \n\n- Added "BOT" to the scoreboard for players who are bots on the server. \n\n- Reduced entity count in Aztec to improve server performance. \n\n- Improved Bot navigation on Aztec. \n\n- Improved Bot navigation on Airstrip. \n\n\n\nBug Fixes:\n\n- Fixed bug where radar would disappear during gameplay. \n\n- Fixed bug where tactical shield wasn\'t removed during a round restart. \n\n- Fixed friends and serverbrowser settings not being saved correctly if edited in-game. \n\n- Fixed bug where sounds weren\'t played properly when using Friends. \n\n- Fixed bug where progress bar would only show the first file you\'re downloading from a game server. \n\n- Fixed bug in keyboard settings list where you could scroll selection bar off the visible page using the arrow keys. \n\n- Fixed bug where the first mouse click wouldn\'t work after exiting the UI. \n\n- Fixed bug where the scoreboard would be incorrect when users were connecting. \n\n- Fixed bug where the M4A1 silencer animation wouldn\'t play the sound at the correct time.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(47133, 7623, 1013, 102921, 1072936800, '', 'so is that it..   no Steam 7   Counterstrike 16?       or will they come out later?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(47141, 7623, 1013, 102922, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by iG | frequency \n\nso is that it..   no Steam 7   Counterstrike 16?       or will they come out later?  \n\n\n\nThis is a CS update only.\n\n\n\nI\'m guessing (judging by Eric\'s other post) that some last minute problems arose with the Steam update so they held it back.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(47143, 7623, 1013, 102923, 1072936800, '', 'Isnt Erik\'s list the exact same as the 07.02.03 bug fix list?\n\n\n\nThey look identical to me.\n\n\n\nMaybe I\'m just blind.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(47144, 7623, 1013, 102921, 1072936800, '', 'thats because it is the same list..   they tried releaseing it 7-2-03 or yesterday, but things went wrong.   so thats why they released it today.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
