(48920, 7857, 1013, 102961, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Boy Wonder \n\n\nhttp://hl2hc.halflife.org/ (http://hl2hc.halflife.org/) \n\n\n\n\n\nOk... heres the scoop no the game half life 2 will not be delayed...\n\n\n\n\n\nThe movie will not be today, like the team said the movie isnt quiet ready...\n\n\n\n\n\nOk, reason being is\n\n\n1. Too busy working on half life 2 or other products and im sure you dont want a delayed half life 2 game because of the movie..\n\n\n\n\n\n2.They are adding some extras or making half life 2 movie much more exciting then the demo at E3. I mean valve has made you wait this long for half life 2 and surprised us... maybe the media too?\n\n\n\n\n\nP.S.The demo at E3 was a demo... not a movie... so turning the actual demo into a movie without the shacky camera and good quality is quiet card meaning they will probably have to code or compile it into a movie form.  \n\n\n\n\n\nit shouldn\'t be hard at all.. they would be able to easily record the demos to the computer they are playing them on.. and with brink or whatever turn them into an exe.. what i think is we might get a slightly different video than what we\'ve seen on gamespy.. seeing as how different groups at e3 were said to have seen some slightly different stuff. should be interesting whenever we get it.\n\n__________________\n\nrandom.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
