(49617, 7960, 1013, 100587, 1072936800, 'ErikJ IRC Q&A #2', 'Part One\n\n\n\n<Erik> How is Steam running for folks tonight?\n\n<jhero> Good Erik.\n\n<SiNergY> It ran good earlier\n\n<Secret-Agent> it\'s running good for me\n\n<Erik> We\'re real close on getting the first of the movies released. I don\'t have a hard date for you all yet, but it is days not weeks away. We\'re waiting for a few things to fall into place.\n\n<blob> Erik - Will you port Half-Life 2/Steam to work on a Mac, because they are fast\n\n<ErikJ> blob - It\'s not in the plans right now.\n\n<omlette> Erik - In the friends list it showed you as away all day, and everyone said you were quiet o_O\n\n<ErikJ> omlette - I was testing a number of things (mainly the movies). I was online/offline quite a bit.\n\n<Fx|PanzerOx^INFM> Erik: How many creatures from the original HL will be returning, you don\'t have to name them.\n\n<ErikJ> Fx - Not going to give out much info in the way of HL2 creatures. You\'ll have to wait.\n\n<Vitalogy> Erik, so can you GUARANTEE they will be here tomorrow?\n\n<ErikJ> Vitalogy - I can\'t guarantee the sun will rise tomorrow, let alone the movies will be release. The hostest answer is that there is an outside chance at tomorrow, but it\'s fairly unlikley. It\'s pointing more toward Thursday, but we\'re going not going to release them on Steam until we think people are going to have a good experience.\n\n<synth> ERIK: STEAM ERROR - http://paradox.homestead.com/files/steamerror.jpg (http://paradox.homestead.com/files/steamerror.jpg)\n\n<ErikJ> Synth - That is one of the problems that is holding up the movie release. We\'re working on those now.\n\n<Tachyon> so its a problem with the videos not steam? or..\n\n<ErikJ> Tach - We\'re working a bit on the videos, but they are close to done. \n\n<Halflife_84|CH> Erik - I dont seem to see many servers listed, even with no filters -- I see max of like 100....and sometimes I only see 10 or less, all my friends who live close to me see 300 +\n\n<ErikJ> Half-Life_84 - Can you do a tracert to 207.173.177.10? That is where the master server is. Make sure you have port 27010 open as well.\n\n<l0afy> erikj, are the new demos run on an updated engine from the old ones?\n\n<ErikJ> l0afy - It\'s not a demo, they are movies.\n\n<Clumsy|work> ErikJ- Sometimes I have to restart steam to get a download to start, is there anyway to start it without restarting?\n\n<ErikJ> Clumsy - We\'re working on that problem.\n\n<doom> ErikJ: when are we going to be able to pause downloads with the steam monitor\n\n<ErikJ> doom - We\'re going to add some more user definable features into that soon.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, you going to put Coming soon changelog in CS Properties?\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - Yes, we will soon. Working mostly on the movie release right now.\n\n<Cryptic[M]> Erik: Will half-life 1 ever be made open source?\n\n<ErikJ> Cryptic - There is just took much code in the engine that we can\'t release (anti-cheat, cd-key validation, etc.). When we release Source (the engine) then you\'ll be able to do much more in terms of traditional "engine" functions.\n\n<jhero> Erik - You said that all the videos would be 800 mb. Into how many videos will this be split? \n\n<ErikJ> jhero - I think there are about 8 movies I believe, but I\'m not sure. In that ballpark anyhow.\n\n<Headless> Erik: Does Half-Life 2 have weather systems? I\'ve heard about the wind entities, but can I assume there are other entities such as rain/snow and if so how modifyable are these? Also, do any weather systems work in conjunction with each other, e.g does the wind system work in conjunction with a rain system for example to give a fluctuating rainfall angle and such (like a particle effect)?\n\n<ErikJ> Headless - That would be something that would be cool to add to a MOD.\n\n<Joeysluck> Erik - sorry a little off of the steam questions but... Alot of people have had a question about water physics. If there is a glass tank full of water and its shot open... what happens to the water?\n\n<ErikJ> Joeysluck - That depends on if there is anyone around to see it.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, you guys doing something about HLAmp and VAC?\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - There isn\'t a lot we can do to fix the problem, as it hooks the client in much the same way as many of the popular cheats. It\'s really hard to allow that application and not open a gaping hole in the anti-cheat code.\n\n<Dark_Seph> Eric, Do you belive half-life2 Will run on a 1400mhz 333fsb 1gigddr ram  Radoen 9700?\n\n<ErikJ> Dark - Yes.\n\n\n\nContinued...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(49618, 7960, 1013, 100587, 1072936800, '', 'Part Two\n\n\n\n<Joeysluck> <Joeysluck> erikj - could we please.. have a rough percentage wise of what our chance is of seeing a little media bar in our games section is?....\n\n<ErikJ> Joeysluck - That\'s too hard.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, will we be able to run Steam offline\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - We\'re talking a lot about that now. I\'m not sure.\n\n<Evil^Milk> Erik - Will the Holster Animations be Fixed?\n\n<ErikJ> Evil - Yes.\n\n<Cryptic[M]> Erik: Will the people who buy hl2 off steam get a reduced price? Will they also be shipped a retail box?\n\n<ErikJ> Cryptic - Not sure, and likely no.\n\n<Dark_Seph> Erik- Every time I log into Steam, I get a message saying "Login To Steam Failed"  IS their any solution to this?\n\n<ErikJ> Dark - Can you check in your Steam\\Errorlogs directory and see if there is a text file created each time you hit this error?\n\n<[LLJK]Shin`Ali> ErikJ : What will the SDK consist of? Code, modelling software, Hammer, etc?\n\n<ErikJ> LLJK - For the most part it will be similar in the types of pieces that the current SDK has. The biggest change will be that we\'ll be including a full featured 3D editor from SoftImage called XSI. They\'ve agreed to allow up to ship their editor for free for use in Source MODs. There will likley be a 5,000 poly limit on models with this version.\n\n<synth> ERIK: if we buy off steam and it "downloads" the game instead of shipping a box, what happens if we want to reinstall?\n\n<ErikJ> synth - You redownload.\n\n<synth> erik: so steam would already know we bought the game?\n\n<ErikJ> synth - Right. The product is tied to your account, not your machine. For instance, if you wanted to got to a cyber cafe and play, you would just enter in your account name and you\'d be on your way,\n\n<Dark_Seph> eric the error is still thier after delting the blob, Do you belive my Old account would be broken?\n\n<ErikJ> Dark, hmm, it\'s hard to say. Can you try deleting your \\SteamCache\\Platform directory and trying again?\n\n<stigmata> ErikJ -- if the products are tied to you account and not your computer, doesn\'t this mean that someone could give his account email + password to 10 other people and they could download the game as well?\n\n<ErikJ> stigmata - Yes, it does. But they won\'t all be able to play at the same time.\n\n<Viscid> ErikJ: Can I use steam to bake me a cake?\n\n<ErikJ> Viscid - It\'s funny you ask, but yes, you can. It can power automobiles as well.\n\n<|MAFiA|Hopesfall> Erik you should check out Alienware to see if they want to provide bandwith..im sure theyd want to\n\n<ErikJ> Mafia - I\'d love to. Anyone that wants to run a Content Server I\'m all ears.\n\n<|Oz|FlyingMonkey> Erik, will there be any Dual proccessor support for HL2?\n\n<ErikJ> FlyingMonkey - You really don\'t get a good performance increase by doing that.\n\n<SiNergY> ErikJ - Any ideas on how much room this game will take, how many cd\'s it comes with?\n\n<ErikJ> SiNergY - Not sure yet. It\'s going to be quite large.\n\n<Headless> ErikJ - Has Valve considered a unique player name user registration for multiplayer (like tribes 2 for example), in order to combat cheating and piracy?\n\n<ErikJ> Headless - That is Steam.\n\n<Synced> Erik - will there be any updates to the engine after release for higher poly models?\n\n<ErikJ> Synced - You misread what I said up there. There is a limit on models you can build using the free version of XSI we\'ll be releasing. There isn\'t a limit in the engine itself. XSI is a pretty high end modeling suite, I think MOD makers are really going to like it.\n\n<Viscid> ErikJ: Is Steam the same project that Powerplay was-- except that is just evolved into what it is now?\n\n<ErikJ> Viscid - No.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, will DoD be soon available in Steam during beta?\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - DoD is a retail product and is still selling quite well. We\'ll release it on Steam when we can sell it to folks. If you have it already, you\'ll get it for free.\n\n<Fragment^> Erik - Will the Deagle-Awp quick switching with no animation be fixed?\n\n<ErikJ> Fragment - Yes.\n\n<Headless> ErikJ - GabeN has been noted as saying that valve will be working on some more \'fun\' projects to wind down from HL2. Are Valve considering furthuring the HL plot (or sub plots), through the much hyped (within the industry), episodic content, via steam\n\n<ErikJ> Headless - That is pretty dead on. There will be a whole bunch of things we\'ll be doing. \n\n<doom> ErikJ: For half life 2 is it just going to use steam for its server browser and so fourth instead of a hl2 gui\n\n<ErikJ> doom - It will look very similar.\n\n<SiNergY>  Erik - Will the tech demo test level be included in hl2 or as a d/l, i thought itd be fun for about 3 hours =]\n\n<ErikJ> Sin - Not sure.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, can you give us any details on the new Vampire game using HL2 Engine?\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - It\'s coming along quite well. Looked great at e3.\n\n<Dark_Seph> Erik, What is the possiblity If by punching randon 10101110 into note pad, coming up with Half-life 2?\n\n<ErikJ> Dark - You should buy a lotto ticket instead.\n\n<|MAFiA|Hopesfall> Erik...do you plan on doing anything about the constant nagging about the sheild...are you reading the forums getting ideas or are you just going to leave it as is?\n\n<ErikJ> Mafia - Yes, we\'re going to revisit it.\n\n<upbeat27> ErikJ - if we buy HL2 at a store... will we be able to play withough internet connection?\n\n<ErikJ> upbeat - Yes.\n\n<someguy_99> ErikJ: Here\'s some feedback instead of a question: The sheild, as many have said, is somewhat overpowered... I suggest (a) making the sheild go further away from the body when your firing, (b) have the sheild eventually be pushed away under heavy fire when it\'s infront of the player, and (c) have the player move much more slowly when being protected by the sheild. \n\n<ErikJ> someguy - We\'ve finally go the shield to the point where it\'s overpowering, and to be honest, we wanted to see what it\'s limits were. We\'ll be taking another look at it. One of the nice things about Steam is being able to release changes like this more rapidly.\n\n<cstone> ErikJ: what\'s to keep people from sharing a single player account via Steam?\n\n<ErikJ> cstone - Nothing really I guess. It\'s the same as sharing a CD-Key now.\n\n<Rip_The_Jacker> Erik, Whats up the lack of different races with the models?\n\n<ErikJ> Rip - Actually there are a number of different ethnic groups in the characters of Half-Life 2.\n\n<cstone> ErikJ: will single player need to be connected to the net to validate the key?\n\n<ErikJ> cstone - If you purchase it via Steam, yes.\n\n<Headless> ErikJ - What do you think about Jason Rubin\'s comments at the recent GDC which suggested improvements in graphics will no longer shift titles?\n\n<ErikJ> Headless - Didn\'t catch the comment, but clearly graphics are an important piece of telling a story.\n\n<Jeffo> ErikJ: do you know what command for the launch option changes the d3d mode to opengl?\n\n<ErikJ> Jeffo -d3d for D3D, -gl for OpenGl, -soft for software.\n\n<Efficient> Erik, is valve planning on making games other than the HL Series?\n\n<ErikJ> Efficient - There are a number of games that people at Valve want to make.\n\n<Synced> Erik - is the maximum map size for modding limited to a specific size?\n\n<ErikJ> Synced - Not artifically, it\'ll be the same as the rest of the games. I don\'t know what the actual number is though.\n\n<Rip_The_Jacker> Erik, I really Like Using in-game Voice Chat in CS 1.6 Will there be any enhancements in CS:CZ/Hl2?\n\n<ErikJ> Rip - Actually, we are going to start looking into a better codec really soon.\n\n<dexhex> erik, will steam allow voice chat when not in a game: just person to person on the friends list?\n\n<ErikJ> dexhex - That is on the wishlist, yes.\n\n<ecKo|complex|zoi> Erik - will cs:cz on xbox use xbox live to play and steam wont be needed?\n\n<ErikJ> exKo - Correct, it will use Live.\n\n<|MAFiA|Hopesfall> Erik - Are you looking to make any new Models, Weapons, or Maps for cs?\n\n<ErikJ> Mafia - We\'re always looking for ways to make the game better. Narby is working on his next CS map now.\n\n<[TNT]Zor> Erik: does HL2 have a heavy reliance on actual hdd performance for loading content on the fly?\n\n<ErikJ> TNT - That isn\'t where we\'re bound by performance.\n\n<someguy_99> Erik: What map would that be? Titles can tell a lot [].\n\n<ErikJ> someguy - De_Quarry.\n\n<Cryptic[M]> Erik: will video cards with 256MB of memory offer significally better speeds then a 128MB card?\n\n<ErikJ> Crypic - Yes, they should. \n\n<[TNT]Zor> Erik: ok so, an 8mb cache 120gb 7200rpm drive will not help you vs a 5400rpm 80gb drive?\n\n<ErikJ> TNT - That\'s hard to say, I haven\'t done any testing on that specific piece of hardware. \n\n<Efficient> I\'ve had dis question for a while erik, will Steam be launched for official 1.6?\n\n<ErikJ> Yes.\n\n<Efficient> You guys have private beta testers b4 you release it to public beta testers?\n\n<ErikJ> We test a bunch internally.\n\n<ErikJ> Have to take off for the night everyone. Thanks for the chat.\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks a bunch Erik!  I am planning on compiling a ton of questions for next Q&A.  Please post questions you\'d like me to ask him.  Here are a few of mine:\n\n\n\nWill more games be added to Friends?\n\nAre you aware of the old knife with the shield?\n\n\n\nI\'d also like to say that I am your new Moderator for the Steam Forums.\n\n\n\n~3ffici3nt', '127.0.0.1', 1),
