(55891, 8714, 1013, 103155, 1072936800, '', 'well, it\'s easy enough to check...if you have the card, you can just check the drivers CD and it should tell you.  If you don\'t, then Tomshardware.com should have some of the info you\'re looking for, i\'m sure they have a review of the 9000 Pro.  I think you should upgrade to either a Radeon 9700 or 9800, but that depends on the amount ofmoney you\'re willing to spend.  I\'m going to get a GeForce 5600 256mb DDR, unless they drop the prices majorly in the next two months for the 58 and 5900s.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(57174, 8714, 1013, 100276, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m gonna get a FX5800 or 5900 aswell end of September.. An ATI card would be an option if Asus made one, but they don\'t, and I want to have an Asus because of their good quality drivers (with OSD etc).. Atm I have a cheap GF4 MX460 (Asus V8170pro), which is fast enough for the games I play now, but won\'t cut it for HL2 I think.. So yeah, lets hope the top-end FX cards are a bit cheaper in 2 months time.. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
