(62000, 9530, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 7/24 Release', 'There is a new version of Steam that has been released to the beta. Please shut down Steam and restart it down to download the update.\n\n\n\nChangelog for this release:\n\n\n\n- Fixed problem on Linux servers where you would get an error saying "Ticket Expired".\n\n- Added the ability to encrypt data in the cache.\n\n- Fixed assert in client when the master authentication server is down.\n\n\n\nYou will have to have this update on your machine before you will be able to launch Steam products.\n\n\n\nIn a few hours we are going to begin preloading the next Half-Life 2 movie (Traptown) to the Steam beta. The movie will be available to play likely tomorrow, but we\'d like to give people the opportunity to get a head start on downloading it if they choose to. If you would not like to automatically download the movie, you can right click on "Half-Life 2 Movies" in your games and choose "Do Not Automatically Update This Game".\n\n\n\nI\'ll post in here when the movie is available.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson', '127.0.0.1', 1),
