(63358, 9665, 1013, 103192, 1072936800, 'Gabe Newell confirms.....', 'NOTE: I didn\'t send this email, somebody from the halflife2.net forums did.\n\n\n\n-----Original Message-----\n\nFrom: Mr.Radar [mailto:mr_radar@charter.net]\n\nSent: Friday, July 25, 2003 7:29 PM\n\nTo: gaben@valvesoftware.com (mailto:gaben@valvesoftware.com)\n\nSubject: 4th Video...\n\n\n\n\n\nJust in case you aren\'t paying attention to any of the fan forums(or \n\neven your own Steam forum) things aren\'t going too well. We\'ve been \n\nwaiting for this 4th video to unlock for 3 and a half hours now. Now I \n\ncan understand about the whole thing with waiting until steam got \n\nencryption but I mean jeez! We\'ve been waiting for this video for a \n\nWEEK! Can\'t you at least do whatever you need to unlock it on time?!?! \n\nIf you\'ve waiting for site like FilePlanet to upload the file then I \n\ndon\'t care if non-steam users won\'t be getting it for a while but NOT \n\nunlocking it when you say you will(ok, on the second set release \n\ndate/time) is only going to get people(like me) angry and won\'t be \n\nhelping your reputation. Even though I will still buy HL2(if I don\'t \n\nread a bad review of it, and I WILL be reading reviews) I am majorly \n\ndissapointed. Could you at least inform people of when things go wrong \n\nand what action is being taken to correct whatever is wrong? This(news \n\nand info) seems to be a major problem for Valve software. How can you \n\nclaim to be the most community oriented game developer if you can\'t even \n\ntell your fans that there are problems and you are working to correct \n\nthem and that there will be delays.\n\n\n\nGabes responce\n\nquote:Well, Erik and his wife had a baby last night, and we\'re operating a little slowly around here in his absence.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63359, 9665, 1013, 100153, 1072936800, '', 'Erik might have been absent, sure.. but is he seriously the ONLY person running Steam?\n\nNot quite a comforting thought, actually.\n\n\n\nAnyways, congrats to Erik for his lil\' Alyx or lil\' Gordon []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63361, 9665, 1013, 103290, 1072936800, '', 'ROFLROFLROFL and were operating a bit slowly in his absence ROFL! muahah thats funny...24 times slower that with him? hihii but erik if u read this GRATZ, wish good health for the baby. (hope thats not wrong english) and hope that sumone else from valve will be abled to release the vid in the next 4 hours or so []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63364, 9665, 1013, 103322, 1072936800, '...', 'My god it\'s a just a brief VIDEO. If you have the 450MB one from E3 you\'ve probably seen a bit of "Trap Town" anyhow. \n\n\n\nSome people need to calm down and stop acting like children over it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63370, 9665, 1013, 103323, 1072936800, 'amazing', 'You know... you should all take a good hard look at the "interactivity levels" of other company execs and reconsider the emails you\'re sending.  I\'ve seen a ton of emails just like that above, an essentially worthless email that they actually take time to respond to, and it baffles me.\n\n\n\nYou do understand, don\'t you, that the time they take answering these emails takes away from their other functions?  Ever heard of the concept of "flow"?  \n\n\n\nGood luck sending those to John Carmack, or George Broussard, or hell, the CEO of GM, bugging him why the 2004 Corvette isn\'t out yet.\n\n\n\nThe ability of the email\'s author to be indignant over a video that... ghhhhh...  if you don\'t get it, you don\'t get it.\n\n\n\nScary', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63372, 9665, 1013, 100708, 1072936800, '', 'I wrote a letter to Dodge explainig that my 5.2 liter 98 Ram kicked the **** out of a new 5.7 liter Hemi.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63384, 9665, 1013, 100300, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Hidden Pain \n\nI wrote a letter to Dodge explainig that my 5.2 liter 98 Ram kicked the **** out of a new 5.7 liter Hemi.  \n\n\n\nYou rock man, lol\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBig congrats from me to the big man and his wife.\n\n\n\nPersonally I don\'t care about the video, I have already seen it (albeit in lower quality)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63396, 9665, 1013, 103324, 1072936800, '', 'Congratulation Eric.  I\'m pretty sure most of the saner ones around here are more pleased for you than waiting for the video. []  You take your time.\n\n\n\n\n\nScaryberry - You make a valid point about the occasionally daft emails people seem to get responses to.  I\'m always slightly suprised when they get a response.  \n\n\n\nI think the non response you\'d usually get from John Carmack & co is part of what makes people see them as a little stand offish when in my brief experience he\'s been a very nice guy.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63416, 9665, 1013, 100598, 1072936800, '', 'You are all a buncha whiney [color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color]es.\n\n\n\n/me watches the video from fileplanet again and laughs at all these dumb whiney [color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color]es.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63430, 9665, 1013, 103325, 1072936800, 'amazing', 'quote:Originally posted by scaryberry \n\nYou know... you should all take a good hard look at the "interactivity levels" of other company execs and reconsider the emails you\'re sending.  I\'ve seen a ton of emails just like that above, an essentially worthless email that they actually take time to respond to, and it baffles me.\n\n\n\nYou do understand, don\'t you, that the time they take answering these emails takes away from their other functions?  Ever heard of the concept of "flow"?  \n\n\n\nGood luck sending those to John Carmack, or George Broussard, or hell, the CEO of GM, bugging him why the 2004 Corvette isn\'t out yet.\n\n\n\nThe ability of the email\'s author to be indignant over a video that... ghhhhh...  if you don\'t get it, you don\'t get it.\n\n\n\nScary  \n\n\n\nagreed. we should all learn that having them answer our pointless questions takes their time away from doing the work we\'re here to see.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(63436, 9665, 1013, 103326, 1072936800, '', 'Don\'t expect the video to get released this weekend.  Working at Valve is their job, and most people who work take the weekends off.  I bet it will come on Monday.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
