(70716, 10430, 1013, 100114, 1072936800, '', 'hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? hl2 or cz? \n\n\n\nHmm.... I\'ll think I\'ll take... HL2.... with physics... *drool*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(70816, 10430, 1013, 100112, 1072936800, '', 'when i first saw CZ i was like "cool" (<-- that was like a year ago before HL2 was announced). then in April HL2 was announced and i was like "cs:cz what?" so..i thought it was a bad idea for VALVe to release CS:CZ and HL2 at around the same time.\n\n\n\nb/c most if not all of the people will skip buying CS:CZ and buy HL2..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71394, 10534, 1013, 100151, 1072936800, 'Steam uses Exessive Disk Space', 'I noticed my hd had a bit less space than usual so I went checking out some folders, and found steamcache to be using 2gb of space.\n\n\n\n\n\nBefore steam, my halflife directory, with dedicated server, counter-strike, ricochet, tfc and dmc took a total of 770mb. (thats with a bunch of extra cs maps..)\n\n\n\n\n\nWhy is steam taking up so much space? I took a deeper look.. the first culprit, 400mb of bs in a halflife 2 video folder... I havnt downloaded any halflife 2 videos via steam, yet for some reason there is a 400mb file in the halflife 2 video folder... *deleted*\n\n\n\n\n\nNext I notice that there is a halflife install for EVERY MOD... why are there seperate instances of halflife for every mod? I notice also that its all in a folder according to my steam login email.. I\'d hate to think of how much space this would be taking up if I shared the computer or had multiple logins.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is excessive filespace use, why has this been created so crappily?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71396, 10534, 1013, 100152, 1072936800, '', 'Make sure in your games folder (in steam) you don\'t the "always keep this game updated" tab checked in every game. By all means, check it in the games you do play. Any mod folders in the steamcache that you dont play, delete them. But remember, if you play them, the folder will be back. The multiple users thing is handy because you can have different settings for different users. And remember, its a big folder because steam is giving you several different games to play. If you just want to play counter-strike, then it won\'t be so big.\n\n__________________\n\nvisit AWBanSunset.com and support our second amendment!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71399, 10534, 1013, 100153, 1072936800, '', 'Deadbolt, every mod is a complete standalone game.\n\n\nYou can play each mod without installing another.\n\n\nThis of course, takes up alot of space.\n\n\nSteam is for people with broadband and alot of HD space.\n\n__________________\n\nMental illness is not funny', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71406, 10534, 1013, 100051, 1072936800, '', 'This thread got me thinking, If 2 logins exist on one machine and both play counter-strike will there be 2 seperate copys of cs?  Im guessing it would since the cs folder is inside the emailaddy in steamchache.  It would be alot simpler if there existed only config files for each user.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71426, 10534, 1013, 100154, 1072936800, '', 'I agree.. your shouldn\'t need a huge cache file for each user.\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd for Mods of games they should access a base installation somewhere.. not each have their own copy.\n\n\n\n\n\nThere\'s so much redundant data in steam right now.. that should really be cut down.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71439, 10534, 1013, 100155, 1072936800, '', 'does this meam i can delete my cs etc from my original halflife directory because its stored in steam instead? if so it now makes more sence to me. but what about the 400mb file?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71443, 10534, 1013, 100156, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s somewhere to stick downloaded material, and when it\'s activated it\'s taken out of the cache file and placed in the folder. It was used for the Hl2 videos.\n\n\n\n\n\nSo don\'t delete it or you can\'t get anything. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71450, 10534, 1013, 100154, 1072936800, '', 'If it\'s deleted and is needed it\'ll be replaced by steam.. don\'t worry about deleting anything in the steamcache folder.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71522, 10534, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'Steam uses Exessive Disk Space', 'quote:Originally posted by Deadbolt00 \n\n\nNext I notice that there is a halflife install for EVERY MOD... why are there seperate instances of halflife for every mod?  \n\n\n\n\n\nIt won\'t always be this way.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:I notice also that its all in a folder according to my steam login email.. I\'d hate to think of how much space this would be taking up if I shared the computer or had multiple logins.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis might change too.\n\n__________________\n\nSteam Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71528, 10534, 1013, 100157, 1072936800, '', 'What do you mean "might?" It should change.\n\n\n\n\n\nRight now my Steam Folder is using over 3GB of hard drive space. 3.17gb to be exact. While its no big deal seeing as how my HDD is 120GB it still is pretty big. No other program I have installed even measures up to taking up that much space.\n\n__________________\n\nWhat\'s a signature?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71672, 10534, 1013, 100158, 1072936800, '', 'HoLY ***** My steam directory is 5 gigs!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71680, 10534, 1013, 100151, 1072936800, '', 'This is going to really end up being a problem, seeing as most of the people who play halflife and it\'s mods do so because they are still popular, and they run well on their old computer.\n\n\n\n\n\nI have a 2nd  computer which my GF uses, it\'s a p3 850 and only has a 30gb hd in it, I don\'t really have the room to spare 5gb on that comp for a game which should only take 700mb.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71732, 10534, 1013, 100159, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve noticed this also, not a big problem for me (120GB HDD), but it does seem excessive.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71764, 10534, 1013, 100160, 1072936800, '', 'ya it says my dedicated server is takeing up 500 MB lol and my steam file is also over 2 gigs\n\n__________________\n\nSLEEP, THOSE LITTLE SLICES OF DEATH....HOW I LOATHE THEM.... -E.A. POE\n\n\n\n\n\n"To Alcohol! The cause of-and solution to-all of Life\'s problems." - Homer Jay Simpson\n\n\n\n\n\n[img]http://swag.iwarp.com/images/katos_sig2.jpg[/img]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(71803, 10534, 1013, 100161, 1072936800, '', 'yes, steam ludicrously stores redundant data.  the hl2 movies directory is the worst.  i have 1 gig in that folder because i\'ve downloaded and saved all the movies + the 400 meg gcache file...but this is all the because i choose to keep it, so i can\'t blame valve for that.  but i have hl and cs autoupdating...so that\'s another gig taken up on my hd.  it would just be nice if valve would store the cache file in a common directory.  please stop wasting our hd space.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(72914, 10749, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Steam 8/11 Release', 'There is a new version of Steam and all products available to the beta now. You should shutdown Steam and restart now to be brought up to date.\n\n\n\nThe list of changes to each product is available here:\n\n\n\nCounter-Strike:\n\n/platfor...ter-strike.html (/platform/update_history/counter-strike.html)\n\nDedicated Server:\n\n/platfor...d%20server.html (/platform/update_history/dedicated%20server.html)\n\nOpposing Force:\n\n/platfor...ng%20force.html (/platform/update_history/opposing%20force.html)\n\nRicochet:\n\n/platfor...y/ricochet.html (/platform/update_history/ricochet.html)\n\nTeam Fortress Classic:\n\n/platfor...%20classic.html (/platform/update_history/team%20fortress%20classic.html)\n\nHalf-Life:\n\n/platfor.../half-life.html (/platform/update_history/half-life.html)\n\n\n\nWe\'ll be starting the preloading of the next Half-Life 2 movie (Barricade) later on this evening.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson', '127.0.0.1', 1),
