(87656, 11562, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by jplove71 \n\nI disagree...  Once a cheater/hacker/exploiter, always a cheater/hacker/exploiter.  People that feel the need to use any cheat/hack/exploit to play HL & the Mods for it don\'t deserve a second chance because they will most likely cheat/hack/exploit again if they feel that they can get away with it. \n\n\n\nThen simply ban them again.  Big freakin\' deal.  Besides, your key phrase was \'if they feel they can get away with it\'.  They didn\'t the first time, they probably won\'t even try a second time.  At least, not in the exact same way, for sure.  Cheat detection hasn\'t declined simply because the ban lists are being reset.\n\n\n\nNo server is cheater/hacker/exploiter proof without an admin, no matter how long the ban list is.\n\n__________________\n\n�I don\'t know half of you as well as I should like; and I like less than half of you half as well as you deserve.� � Bilbo Baggins, from his speech on his eleventy-first birthday.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(87660, 11562, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by NetGraph5 \n\nI have just gotten started running a server company and owning it I host the current 1.5 CS servers I have just recently started to use the steam server files for linux to host 1.6 servers how soon are the linux server files going to be released after the windows files our are they both being release at the same time ??? Also has there been a fix for the extreme cpu and ram usage for the server files. cause currently I can only run two 24 player servers a box which is kinda wierd cause the old cs server files i can run 4 to a box adn the box will not lagg.  I get 85% usage fromt he two steam linux servers with a max players of 24 on both. \n\n\n\nAnd info will be helpfull\n\n\n\nThanks Ben \n\n\n\nAll I know for certain is that your problems and requests will eventually be attended to.  Some of them (especially the cpu usage) should be fixed as soon as steam is final later today, but the rest I don\'t know when they\'ll be addressed.\n\n__________________\n\n�I don\'t know half of you as well as I should like; and I like less than half of you half as well as you deserve.� � Bilbo Baggins, from his speech on his eleventy-first birthday.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
