(82506, 11767, 1013, 100475, 1072936800, 'Can\'t run with OpenGL', 'I used to be able to run with OpenGL fine, and then for no reason at all. I did not change any settings, tweak anything. OpenGL was not supported. It displayed a message that said:\n\n\n\n\n\n"Video mode change failure"\n\n\n"The specified video moke is not supported."\n\n\n"The game will run in software mode"\n\n\n\n\n\n"ok" "cancel"\n\n\n\n\n\nand it just changes to software mode with 640 by 480 no matter what I press.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat\'s the problem? my drivers are fine. I run GeForce4 Ti4200 128 mb, Athlong t-bird 1.4ghz. On Win-XP Home Ed. machine.\n\n\n\n\n\nNote: I\'ve ALWAYS been able to run with OpenGL until this mysterious error came.\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks in advance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(82612, 11767, 1013, 100476, 1072936800, '', 'Re-install your video card drivers.  It is possible that another application has corrupted them. (This can often happen if you are running any beta games or participating in an online beta test for a new game.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
