(222148, 11767, 1013, 100481, 1072936800, '', 'opengl and d3d doesnt work for me anymore.\n\n__________________\n\nNewbie <Slang> /n[y]oo\'bee/ (Originally from British public-school and military slang variant of "new boy")\n\n\n1. An inexperienced user of Computer technology or the Internet.\n\n\n2. Person(s) who:\n\n\n...a. Lacks the skill to ever learn.\n\n\n...b. Who don\'t not know the meaning of the word Search.\n\n\n...c. Lacks the ability to read whats in plain view.\n\n\n...d. Like\'s to use whats called "Leet Speak".', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(222158, 11767, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Unless you guys post some details about what HW/SW and OS you are running it is very hard to help you out with these sort of problems.\n\n\n\n\n\nGo run dxdiag (start > run > dxdiag) and save all the information (hit the button) and then extract and post JUST the System Information and the Display Devices information, (please don\'t post the whole thing).\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you see any errors posted in the DxDiag Notes section, post that as well.\n\n__________________\n\nWould you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(84122, 11934, 1013, 100587, 1072936800, 'Steam Official Wednesday', 'Press Release from Doug Lombardi:\n\n\n\nquote:Steam Beta Ends, Full Version Ships Next Week \n\nThe Steam Beta has delivered several Valve games and popular Half-Life MODs to over 300,000 gamers, and will come to a close Tuesday evening (Pacific Daylight Time). The first full version of Steam, Valve\'s broadband platform for the delivery and management of digital content, will launch at 11 am PDT on Wednesday. Set up installers for the full version, which will be free of charge to existing Half-Life and Counter-Strike players, will be available from www.steampowered.com (http://www.steampowered.com) and leading game sites. Anyone interested in hosting the installer or becoming a Steam Service Provider, please email biz@steampowered.com (mailto:biz@steampowered.com). \n\n\n\nValve would like to extend its thanks to everyone who participated in this beta.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
