(89727, 12444, 1005, 100741, 1072936800, '', 'How to change fonts for that big Admin-Mod text?\n\n\n\n\n\n1.  Go to x:\\....\\steam\\skins\\<skin_color>\\Resource\n\n\n\n\n\n2. Open TrackerScheme.res with notepad\n\n\n\n\n\n3. Search  for this lines:\n\n\n\n\n\n"CreditsFont"\n\n\n		{\n\n\n			"1"\n\n\n			{\n\n\n				"name"		"Trebuchet MS"\n\n\n				"tall"		"18"\n\n\n				"weight"	"600"\n\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n\n			}\n\n\n			"2"\n\n\n			{\n\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n\n			}\n\n\n		}\n\n\n\n\n\nChange 18 in 12 (CS1.5)\n\n\n\n\n\nThe other GUI-Texts i havent tried yet, but it works the same i think.\n\n\n\n\n\nGood Luck...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89947, 12444, 1005, 100737, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by t.Wb \n\n\nhonestly... i play at 1024x768 on a 19" monitor... and the font seems fine to me...  \n\n\n\n\n\nits 1024x768... 1600x1200 on a 21" is MUCH different, i could get a screenshot...\n\n\n\n\n\n@L0ki, well that works on the most annoying text (the green/autohelp text).  Thanks, at least we know its somewhat editable.  I\'ll keep testing to try and adjust the size of the buy/radio menus as well as the chat text.  Thanks again.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOk, the chat and net_graph next is under "EngineFont" and is editable.  I\'m trying to find the text menu font now.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe buy menu is under Legacy_CreditsFont:\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://mexicanstandoff.org/cs_screens/lol.jpg (http://mexicanstandoff.org/cs_screens/lol.jpg)\n\n\n\n\n\nusing:\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:		"Legacy_CreditsFont" // Added to accomodate 3rd party server plugins, etc. This version should not scale.\n\n\n		{\n\n\n			"1"\n\n\n			{\n\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n\n				"weight"	"600"\n\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n\n				"yres"	"1 10000"\n\n\n			}\n\n\n\n\n\n(that ss is taken after editing the font, font size, and gun names)\n\n\n\n\n\nIf this is a scaling problem, then why doesn\'t valve fix it?  It\'s obviously not "Legacy" since the text-based buy menus are an option in CS 1.6, and not 3rd party.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91903, 12444, 1005, 100741, 1072936800, '', 'Iv\'e Noticed it [] I will try to maken it read-only if it works []\n\n\n\n\n\nIf that not helps, i gonna mail Valve @ that font, to change that, they can spread it over steam (updating trough steam).\n\n\n\n\n\nSorry for bad langauge (i am dutch :P )......\n\n\n\n\n\nMore info soon!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88496, 12520, 1026, 100773, 1072936800, 'Problems with the new Steam after running the beta?  Solution within!', 'The new Linux Steam client has a couple problems that can crop up on a lot of Linux-based computers.  It took me and a few others a while to track down the problem, but here are the problems, and their corresponding solutions:\n\n\n\n\n\nBroken Pipe error\n\n\nAfter downloading the hldsupdatetool.bin file, and executing it, it may abort something like this:code:Enter \'yes\' to accept this agreement, \'no\' to decline: yes\nsh: line 1: uncompress: command not found\nBroken pipe\n[hlds@funball hlds_l]$ \n\n\n\n\n\nIf it does, the error actually is telling you ecactly what the problem is- you lack the \'uncompress\' tool, which is rather common, but some Linux distros (more notable some Red Hat versions) lack.  You can get the RPM you need here (http://rpmfind.net/linux/rpm2html/search.php?query=uncompress).  Once you have it, su up to root, go to where the file is, and run this command:code:rpm -i ncompress-4.2.4-33.i386.rpm Assuming you get no error messages, you should now be able to log out as root, log back in with your HLDS user, and successfully run the .bin file.  It\'ll extract one file, \'steam\'.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe \'Connection Reset\' Problem\n\n\nAt first, this one was a bear to nail down, but it seems that we\'ve got it.\n\n\n\n\n\nYou\'ll know you ahve this problem when, when you try to run steam to update a server, or to create an account, this happens:\n\n\ncode:[hlds@funball hlds_l-steam]$ ./steam -update tfc . myusername mypasswd\nChecking bootstrapper version ...\nGetting version 0 of Steam HLDS Update Tool\nConnection Reset \n\n\n\n\n\nIf this happens, all you need to do is run this command...\n\n\ncode:rm -rf ~/.steam/...and you should be all set.  Run that command, and start from the \'create an account\' step in the Readme file.\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope this helps!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88583, 12520, 1026, 100774, 1072936800, 'Problems with the new Steam after running the beta?  Solution within!', 'quote:Originally posted by Ghoti \n\n\nThe \'Connection Reset\' Problem\n\n\nAt first, this one was a bear to nail down, but it seems that we\'ve got it.\n\n\n\n\n\nYou\'ll know you ahve this problem when, when you try to run steam to update a server, or to create an account, this happens:\n\n\ncode:[hlds@funball hlds_l-steam]$ ./steam -update tfc . myusername mypasswd\nChecking bootstrapper version ...\nGetting version 0 of Steam HLDS Update Tool\nConnection Reset \n\n\n\n\n\nIf this happens, all you need to do is run this command...\n\n\ncode:rm -rf ~/.steam/...and you should be all set.  Run that command, and start from the \'create an account\' step in the Readme file.\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope this helps!  \n\n\n\n\n\nGhoti thank you very much I would have never realized that command would fix it. If you don\'t mind me asking I am learning linux and would like to know what caused this error and why the rm -rf ~./steam/ fix it.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks Again\n\n__________________\n\nWhats cooler then being cool\n\n\n\n\n\n\'ICE COLD!!!\'', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88592, 12520, 1026, 100773, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m happy to!\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Steam beta kept the user identification information (your Steam usernamd and password) in a special directory (.steam) in your account\'s home directory.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhen the new version came out, Valve didn\'t tell us that it wan\'t \'beta-aware\', and when you ran the new Steam, it looked in ~/.steam/ for the Steam account information, which, since the Steam user database was reset, is no longer valid.  This is what causes the \'Connection Reset\' problem- it\'s more of a \'Bad Password\' problem, just badly labeled, or an overgeneralized error message.\n\n\n\n\n\n~ is Unix-ese for \'home directory\', and since the Steam data was kept in a directory \'.steam\' in your home, its path is \'~/.steam/\'.\n\n\n\n\n\nAs another side note, files and directories with names that start with a \'.\' are hidden- they won\'t show up unless you ise the \'a\' switch on the ls command, like this:code:ls -a', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88613, 12520, 1026, 100774, 1072936800, '', 'thanks man\n\n__________________\n\nWhats cooler then being cool\n\n\n\n\n\n\'ICE COLD!!!\'', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88875, 12520, 1026, 100773, 1072936800, '', 'Glad to help!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(88984, 12597, 1013, 100435, 1072936800, 'Heres the story, people: An FAQ about Steam', 'The Official Steam Client was released, along with the final of CS 1.6, and currently Valve is finalizong the Steam Content Network servers in anticipation of the relase of Half-Life 2. \n\n\n\n\n\nThis thread is for Steam users that are having difficulty with the program. If you continue to spam this thread, I will delete it, as I have no need to use the answers posted here. This means no more all caps posts, no more spammimg, no more useless crap. GOT IT?\n\n\n\n\n\nThe following is a FAQ for Steam.\n\n\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n1] Will my cd key still work?\n\n\n\n\n\nYes, it will. Steam will prompt for it during installation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2] Is WON offline?\n\n\n\n\n\nNo, it will stay up for about 2 weeks, and then the WON servers will be shut down permanently.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n3] Can I hold a LAN game?\n\n\n\n\n\nYes, you can, but, and this is quite a but, every system has to be online and connected. The likelyhood this will change is great, however.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n4] Will my MOD work under steam?\n\n\n\n\n\nIt should, but chances are that if it isnt a mainstream mod i.e. NS or DoD, then you should wait before installing it untill the next patch is released. Full MOD support is included with Steam, however, so wait before spamming the forums with complaints.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n5] I was in the beta for steam.....it will update itself, right?\n\n\n\n\n\nNo, a new steam client was released and the beta program will not work anymore. You must delete the original beta install and run the new installer.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n6] Can I still play CS 1.5?\n\n\n\n\n\nAgain, yes, for two weeks untill WON goes offline.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n7] When will CS 1.6 become final?\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Counter-Strike version 1.6 final has been released.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n8] Is there spyware in Steam?\n\n\n\n\n\nNo, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors.\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nAny other questions have more than likely had threads dedicated to them, and all one has to do is search for them.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf there are any more questions you think I may have missed, feel free to add them with the answers.\n\n\n\n\n\n~retribution', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89046, 12597, 1013, 100435, 1072936800, '', 'Also, here is some general info.\n\n\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n- The old Steam beta accounts have all been deleted. you will have to create a new account.\n\n\n\n\n\n- It is strongly recommended that if you had the beta client installed, that you uninstall and delete all of it before installing the official steam client. It is necessary for the official Steam client to work.\n\n\n\n\n\n- You will be able to install custom models for CS 1.6 under steam.\n\n\n\n\n\n- The Official FAQs are up and running once more, if having chronic problems you should head over there.\n\n\n\n\n\n- The Half-Life 2 movies have been pulled temporarily due to the extreme network usage the content servers have been experiencing.\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nmore will be posted as it comes up.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89074, 12597, 1013, 100785, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for writing this.\n\n\nHere\'s a link to the official FAQ (/faq.htm), for other questions. Towards the end are questions & answers regarding mods and custom content.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89148, 12597, 1013, 100786, 1072936800, '', 'I have some questions (yes I have visited the FAQ page)\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 1: Are the Steam content provider servers and Steam ID autherisation servers on seperate machines with seperate networks? \n\n\n\n\n\nReason I am asking is that if the authersation and content providers are on the same network it is possible that whenever a popular update/patch or a new game (HL 2) becomes available the servers will be overloaded and autherisation will be unavailable.\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 2: The FAQ wasn\'t too clear on this issue. If I understand this correctly a Steam enabled game will allow single player usage untill the player enables Steam for that game (for multiplayer or patching/updates ) thereafter even single player gameing will require a internet connection, is this true ?\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 3) If the answer to Question 2 is yes, isn\'t it a bit much to expect players to connect to the internet even if they merely want to play single player ? I mean not all of Valves supporters have the luxury of a always available or on broadband connection.\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 4) Will the updates and patches for Steam enabled games be available for manual download and deploy, and will it be possible to store these updates on media for later retrieval ?\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 4 relates to the bandwidth availability issue, if its possible to manually download, store and deploy patches/updates then those with a decent connection can download them and upload to a local server for those with dial-up.\n\n\n\n\n\nI commend Valve for thier attempts to provide a service whereby supporters can get the latest patchs/update and games, whereby a system that assists in keeping gaming cheat free and providing ease of use in finding game servers and friends, however I must add a note of caution that not all of Valves supporters have broadband options and internet connectivity can be problematical. I have faith that Valve will consider the plight of those supporters and provide other means to work around these issues.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89376, 12597, 1013, 100787, 1072936800, '', 'a question that needs an answer. say i downloaded all of the halflife game through steam, the whole lot all the levels sounds etc so that it does not require an internet connection.\n\n\n\n\n\ndo i have to be online to play the single player, even if i have all the files for it?\n\n\n\n\n\nif so WHY!?\n\n\n\n\n\nthank you\n\n\n\n\n\noh yeah and how do i find my steam id out?\n\n__________________\n\n-WHERE THE FOO IS THE TFC FORUM!-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89383, 12597, 1013, 100788, 1072936800, '', 'Q: why did valve disable the bots\n\n\n\n\n\n(possible) A: valve removed the bots themporary and they will be enabled soon.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nQ: and when will valve enable the bots?\n\n\n\n\n\nA: ???\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVALVE, could you pls. verify the first question and answer the second? ... many tnx i.a. .\n\n__________________\n\nmfg [AFB]-Mauser-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89767, 12597, 1013, 100590, 1072936800, '', 'Q) Will Steam ever work when asked to work, instead of popping up 20 minutes after double clicked on.\n\n\n\n\n\nA) ...?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90009, 12597, 1013, 100789, 1072936800, '', 'Amen to that (above)  seriously steam is having some major issues.  I hope that it is only because of a limited amount of bandwicth and all of the upgrading... Good luck steam people.. But hurry up... lol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90177, 12597, 1013, 100435, 1072936800, 'a continuation of the FAQ..........', 'quote:Question 1: Are the Steam content provider servers and Steam ID autherisation servers on seperate machines with seperate networks? \n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 2: The FAQ wasn\'t too clear on this issue. If I understand this correctly a Steam enabled game will allow single player usage untill the player enables Steam for that game (for multiplayer or patching/updates ) thereafter even single player gameing will require a internet connection, is this true ?\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 3) If the answer to Question 2 is yes, isn\'t it a bit much to expect players to connect to the internet even if they merely want to play single player ? I mean not all of Valves supporters have the luxury of a always available or on broadband connection.\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 4) Will the updates and patches for Steam enabled games be available for manual download and deploy, and will it be possible to store these updates on media for later retrieval ?\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestion 4 relates to the bandwidth availability issue, if its possible to manually download, store and deploy patches/updates then those with a decent connection can download them and upload to a local server for those with dial-up. \n\n\nIn regards to your questions:\n\n\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n1] No, they are the same, and yes, the risk is real. however, the certain upcoming addtition of bandwith will ease this congestion.\n\n\n\n\n\n2] Yes, you understand correctly. Take HL2 for example. Say that you buy the box and install the game, nut not through Steam. You will be able to play the single player offline. However, you also will not be able to dl any patches that may be released. Once you connect to Steam, all patches will dl automatically, but you will be required to stay online in order to play HL2 from then on.\n\n\n\n\n\n3] You are absoluty right, and Valve is putting serious consideration into changing this requirement. Expect news in this concern in the next week or so.\n\n\n\n\n\n4] At this point, it looks like manual download will not be enabled, although it may be possible to cache the data and store it on disk, i.e. such as was done for CS 1.6b recently.\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:say i downloaded all of the halflife game through steam, the whole lot all the levels sounds etc so that it does not require an internet connection.\n\n\n\n\n\ndo i have to be online to play the single player, even if i have all the files for it?\n\n\n\n\n\noh yeah and how do i find my steam id out?  \n\n\nAs of the moment, yes, you will be required to have a net connection while online, the reason being an allowance for automatic updates, as well as anti-piracy. Although this may not seem satifactory for 56k users and LAN event hosts, it is most likely that this will change.\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd to find your Steam ID, when connected to a server, type "status" in the consol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90822, 12597, 1013, 100790, 1072936800, '', 'Number three takes care of itself.  That decision is incredibly idiotic, and if its not done my HL days are over (BF 1942 was becoming more fun, anyway).\n\n\n\n\n\n"8] Is there spyware in Steam? \n\n\n\n\n\nNo, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors."\n\n\n\n\n\nThen what the hell else is steam using all this processing power for?  Are you seriously going to argue that the proggy requires a 1 gig processor simply do "stream content" (something it does poorly, btw)...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90830, 12597, 1013, 100790, 1072936800, '', '"4] At this point, it looks like manual download will not be enabled, although it may be possible to cache the data and store it on disk, i.e. such as was done for CS 1.6b recently."\n\n\n\n\n\nIf this is true then the only people with "hard" access to patches (ie, not through steam) will be those who pirate them.  Why inconvienence real supporters like this?\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd if the steam developers think they can keep these patches away from the warez kiddies by streaming them then their vastly underestimating the dedication people have to receiving free software.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90847, 12597, 1013, 100435, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Propagandhi \n\n\nNumber three takes care of itself.  That decision is incredibly idiotic, and if its not done my HL days are over (BF 1942 was becoming more fun, anyway).\n\n\n\n\n\n"8] Is there spyware in Steam? \n\n\n\n\n\nNo, there has never been any spyware of any kind in Steam, anything you may have heard to the contrary are baseless rumors."\n\n\n\n\n\nThen what the hell else is steam using all this processing power for?  Are you seriously going to argue that the proggy requires a 1 gig processor simply do "stream content" (something it does poorly, btw)...  \n\n\ni run steam on a 555mhz 128mb ram 6 year old hp. trust me, the requirements are not accurate, merely recommendations at best.\n\n\n\n\n\nas for number 3, valve is reconsidering its decision.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91039, 12597, 1013, 100791, 1072936800, '', 'FAQ: Why are you forcing everyone to use the bug laden software that is Steam?\n\n\n\n\n\nA: Because we are moving to the pay-to-play model and this must be done.  Trust us, it will be better for us in the long run.\n\n\n\n\n\nFAQ: Steam contains many \'features\' that users say they don\'t need or even want, why put them in?\n\n\n\n\n\nA: Well, we needed some guise to shove this thing down your throat.  See?  It\'s a "good thing"!  Think of it as \'Vaseline\' if you get my drift.\n\n\n\n\n\nI will never pay for a game that requires Steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91059, 12597, 1013, 100792, 1072936800, 'a continuation of the FAQ..........', 'quote:Originally posted by retribution \n\n\n2] Yes, you understand correctly. Take HL2 for example. Say that you buy the box and install the game, nut not through Steam. You will be able to play the single player offline. However, you also will not be able to dl any patches that may be released. Once you connect to Steam, all patches will dl automatically, but you will be required to stay online in order to play HL2 from then on.And if this doesn\'t change, it will be no HL2 for me.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve commented elsewhere (http://boards.straightdope.com/sdmb/showthread.php?s=&threadid=211017) about my strong negative feelings about this.  However, I\'ll repeat some of the objections:\n\n\n\n\n\n1) If my net connection is down, I am more likely to play SP.  Requiring online authentication means that when my net connection is down, my retail game is down as well.\n\n\n\n\n\n2) If Steam is down (unlikely, right?) that means I can\'t play SP or MP.  My shiny new box is just so much garbage.\n\n\n\n\n\n3) If something happens to Valve in the future, there is no guarantee I\'ll be able to use the software I purchased.\n\n\n\n\n\n4) There is nothing to prevent Valve discontinuing support for HL2 sometime in the future, thus preventing me from playing ever again.\n\n\n\n\n\nAll this presumes that I buy the retail box and play online or get patches and then play more SP--of course, that follows my gaming patterns with every game I have (with the exception of Homeworld, which I never played online.)\n\n\n\n\n\nIt\'s even more aggrivating that the reason for this policy is most likely to deter unlicensed copying of the game.  Of course, it won\'t deter that, but it will be a thorn in the side of legitimate players.  I don\'t like being treated like a thief first, customer second.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf this is still the case when HL2 ships, I won\'t be buying it.  I\'ll spend my money and time on Halo instead (at least they\'ve gone gold, and aren\'t deceiving their customer base about a release date).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91232, 12597, 1013, 100793, 1072936800, '', 'Amen to that!\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m a university student and have a 10mb/s line, but if/when I go home during summer (1-3 months) I don\'t want to have to use my parents dial-up connection every time I want to play an offline game, right?\n\n\n\n\n\nI guess and hope that Vavle gets their act together and makes sure you don\'t need internet access just to play at a LAN or in places where there\'s no internet access, otherwise their good reputation from half-life will go to waste...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89099, 12628, 1013, 100587, 1072936800, 'Official Steam Bug-List #1', 'Hey guys, sorry forums been down.  Feel free to post all bugs that you have encountered in the current version of Steam.  We are also accepting any suggestions that you may have to improve Steam.  \n\n\n\nBugs\n\n\n\n-Banned for cheating when your really not cheating.\n\n-Mp5 muzzle on m4a1 gun.\n\n-Shield sometimes not showing in buy menu.\n\n\n\nSuggestions\n\n\n\n-Chatroom support in Steam.\n\n-Changing Steam skins w/o restarting Steam.\n\n-More Games added to Friends.\n\n\n\nUpdate\n\nYou can also post bugs you are encountering in-game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89104, 12628, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, 'No Children Still Registered', 'Of course, the no children still registered error that we\'ve all seen at least once...\n\n\n\nI notice it most often when I\'m trying to open/close the Games window, and it hangs for a long time.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.angelfire.com/ma4/masteramerica/children.JPG (http://www.angelfire.com/ma4/masteramerica/children.JPG)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89110, 12628, 1013, 100437, 1072936800, '', 'Here you go, all the errors you\'ll ever need.\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/sho...p;threadid=7098 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=7098)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89111, 12628, 1013, 100794, 1072936800, '', 'Suggestions\n\n-MP3 support in-game (with playlists and support for streaming radio)\n\n-para to be able to penetrate the shield (since its considered "anti-tank")\n\n-MAKE THE Mp3s HIEGHER QUALITY... its pathetic to listen to the music of HL & Opfor in 28kbs (make them 128kbs)\n\n\n\n\n\nbugs\n\n-some ppl get a VERY short server list (with / without filter) <== PLEASE FIX THIS ASAP\n\n-takes a very long time to log in and get started with a game\n\n-... many more bugs....\n\n-when filtering with US WEST/EAST the server list only shows about 3 - 5 servers <=== !!!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89113, 12628, 1013, 100110, 1072936800, '', 'suggestions:\n\n\n\n-changing skins without restarting steam.\n\n\n\n-animate the (sorta)new "downloading" sys tray icon.\n\n\n\n-.....??...*shrug*\n\n\n\nbugs:\n\n\n\n-calculate cache status seems a bit iffy, sometimes it\'ll work fine, other times not so much.\n\n\n\nBTW steam\'s running alot smoother, the situation with the content providers seems to have been remidied (for the most part it anyways) it seems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89114, 12628, 1013, 100795, 1072936800, '', '-When we shoot all ammos with shield, we can active it when the pistol reloading. This make player invincible and bad reload annimation.\n\n-We can subscribe to steam with an invalid cdkey.\n\n-We can create several acount with the same cdkey.\n\n-All model/sound/sprites not loaded to cs1.6 if there are in pak0.pak (in cstrike folder). We must unpack them.\n\n-the x/y console arent\'t saved\n\n-Steam create files (40mo) in steam folder (**.mdmp)\n\n-The 3dfx users can\'t use 3dfx-mini-drivers il gldrv folder. They must copy "3dfxgl.dll" to "../opengl32.dll"\n\n-in setting, "internet connection speed" is bloqued to 128kb (rate 5000) and i have adsl 512kb\n\n-when we add mods to halflife, we not must add "launching setting" (-dev...) because steam create folder in halflife like:\n\nfirearms -dev\n\ncstrike -dev -noforcespams\n\n-in game vgui there is an option to add shortuc but dont work.\n\n-----------------------------\n\nsorry for bad english.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89119, 12628, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'Selecting gateways (US East/West, etc) doesn\'t seem to display all the servers actually available. Altogether, the summation of all the gateways\' servers would be about 300 servers, when altogether (with World selected) there are 4500+. This could be because Steam doesn\'t know which country each server is in, but I\'m not sure.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89123, 12628, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'duck button will still not close spectator GUI.  it will activate it, but not close it.   i use shift for duck, if that helps.\n\n\n\nMOTD\'s - scroll bars do not work.  and at 640, you can only see the first few lines.  well the bars work, but when you scroll down the message doesnt move.\n\n\n\nthis one may be hard to explain properly, but ill try.  i normally launch Steam to the "server" menu.  if i then launch CS from the "games" menu, when i click on "servers" i get a blank list saying no servers pass my filter requirements or whatever.  my favorites show up, when i click "spectate", what i presume to be HLTV servers show up, but when i select "internet" it will not refresh servers.  if i then quit CS, i can refresh the server list all day long with no problems.\n\n\n\nSteam still runs in background after you "Exit Steam" from system tray.  so the only way to launch Steam again is to ctrl+alt+del, end the process, and start Steam again.\n\n\n\nim sure im forgetting some...post em later', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89126, 12628, 1013, 100430, 1072936800, '', 'Well i know they already got some of this but what the heck.\n\n\n\nBugs:\n\n\n\nAfter joining a server with a nonofficial map, it crashed. And when i restarted it said there was an error in my cache, and i should flush it. The inprogram delete cache and, the flush cache option in the dialog did not work. Reinstall was the only workaround.\n\n\n\nIt was a rare bug so it\'s probably not gonna get spotted again.\n\n\n\nAlso the grey Steam skin has some of the green skin, ingame.\n\n\n\n\n\nSuggestions:\n\n\n\nRegions and closed servers: I don\'t know if this is in already. Make content servers by region. And maybe even disable access to it to people out of that region, to lure more people into hosting.\n\n\n\nError correcting cachefiles: If your cache fails, make a validate data system, where it checks every file against MD5 hashes and then patches them with proper data.\n\n\n\nLess serverchecks: Well some of the options, delete local cache and monitor and so on. Shouldn\'t need to require a servercheck.\n\n\n\nServercheck and download icon: Instead of the current working icon, make a servercheck icon, so people know when it\'s authenticating, and when it\'s working. And instead of the current working icon also include a downloading icon, so people knows when it\'s downloading.\n\n\n\nEdit: Better status: Also in conjunction with the above suggestion, dialog status boxes should be made if it has connection trouble and whatever.\n\n\n\nShares: Already in the works, but a shared license and local steam content server client.\n\n\n\nP2P - Bittorrent: Bittorrent based P2P system. http://bitconjurer.org/BitTorrent/ (http://bitconjurer.org/BitTorrent/) Should also be allowed for ingame content(maps, mods and so on) via Friends.\n\n\n\nMassive database: Steam that serves a big database of maps, mods and whatever. Which are downloaded through external sites, p2p or in some cases content servers.\n\n\n\nBetter HTML browser: With the suggestion above we will need a better working in-steam browser.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89152, 12628, 1013, 100797, 1072936800, '', 'Steam Client\n\n+ Fix properties page(includes Calculate Cache Status) hanging if content is not downloaded fully\n\n+ Disable memory dumps\n\n+ Fix GUI hangs, almost everywhere\n\n+ Logout doesn\'t exits Steam\n\n+ No lingering process after exit\n\n+ Fix monitor to show kilobytes(kB) instead of kilobits(kb)\n\n+ Use maximum bandwidth to download, not download only when the connection is idle\n\n+ Fix GUI hangs on server connects (Sometimes you cannot even click Cancel)\n\n+ Fix reset of "Automatic updates"\n\n+ Add previews for skin chooser\n\n+ News is opened in Steam, no window popups\n\n+ Screenshots for un-installed games (Aka Preview)\n\n+ Better progress bar (With percentage complete)\n\n+ Ability to cancel update (Steam main client updates)\n\n+ Enable pause / resume for downloads\n\n+ Enable multi-source(aka content server) downloading\n\n+ Menu to select which content server to use, amount of bandwidth available, country\n\n+ Limit file size of logs and errorlogs\n\n+ Disable logging and errorlogs\n\n+ History(Servers played on, frags.deaths.statistics)\n\n+ Detailed logging of bandwidth usage, average DL speed\n\n+ Fix inaccurate measurement of bandwidth\n\n+ Fix inconstant downloads, downloads blink in and blink out in Bandwidth Monitor\n\n\n\nFriends Client\n\n+ Fix games reappearing multiple times\n\n+ Add smiles\n\n+ Add groupings\n\n+ "X" people online\n\n+ Send msgs to inform other users why they should add him/her (Current system does not enable others to know who and why one should add someone to his/her friends list)\n\n\n\nView Server Info\n\n+ Show server CVARs\n\n+ Show MOTD\n\n+ Show anti-cheat options\n\n\n\nServer Browser\n\n+ Country filter for server window\n\n+ Server side filtering and pinging before sending results\n\n+ Saves serverlist so no refresh is needed (Refresh takes damn long)\n\n+ Enable third-party server browser support, eg. ASE (Provide documentation on how to add support)\n\n+ Tree list with filters, like ASE\n\n+ Customised filter options\n\n+ Scripting language to find servers with certain CVARs on\n\n\n\nRequired\n\n+ GCache explorer\n\n+ Map browser\n\n+ Skins & Models explorer\n\n+ Fast logins\n\n+ Create safe mode\n\n+ Force downloading of content\n\n+ Compression support in transfers, eg maps, textures\n\n+ MP3 player support\n\n+ Better MOD icons support\n\n+ Choosing minimum Steam Cache size, ability to increase for updates (No point leaving space for reserved updates)\n\n+ Start in offline mode\n\n+ Lite mode(No fancy GUI functions, no Friends list, just games only)\n\n+ Change of email address\n\n+ Provide manual downloadable patches and updates (Like the Steam+CS1.6 installer)\n\n\n\nStart Menu\n\n+ Start in safe mode\n\n+ Manual / Readme\n\n+ Delete all login details (Useful for LAN shops)\n\n+ Uninstall Steam\n\n\n\nIn game\n\n+ Media player\n\n+ Clock & date with timezones\n\n+ Minimise buttom\n\n+ User friendly voting functions(Like RTCW:ET)\n\n\n\nSteam Links\n\n+ Add server to favorites\n\n+ Add contact to Friends automatically onclicked\n\nEg of Steam link: steam://|friend?friend@domain.com|\n\n\n\nNote: This list will be updated. Contains bugs+requests\n\nquote:Its not a bug, its a feature', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89161, 12628, 1013, 100569, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Master_America \n\nSelecting gateways (US East/West, etc) doesn\'t seem to display all the servers actually available. Altogether, the summation of all the gateways\' servers would be about 300 servers, when altogether (with World selected) there are 4500+. This could be because Steam doesn\'t know which country each server is in, but I\'m not sure.  \n\n\n\nThe location of the server is an operator-set cvar. Valve, in their server documentation, recommends initally setting this to "World"; thus, said servers are only going to show up under world. (Do the US East/West servers show up on the World list?)\n\n\n\nAnyways, at some point in the future the World setting, at least server-side, will disappear so the region-based stuff should be correct then.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89166, 12628, 1013, 100798, 1072936800, 'quick suggestion', 'At the moment, the only way to install new items (Greyed out) is to double click on it. Probably be easier if you had an install menu option when you right-click on it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89178, 12628, 1013, 100799, 1072936800, 'DoD key doesn\'t work', 'OK, my girlfriend is hooked on CS now ever since she started playing it after watching me play it all the time. Steam beta was coming to an end, Valve states that any half-life based product CD key will unlock all the content once final Steam comes out. OK, sounds like a deal and a half, I guess I\'ll go hunt down a Half-Life product so that she can continue playing with me once Steam final is out. Only thing I can find is DoD, but, hey, they said any Half-Life based product. So that should be fine, sure hope so, nobody\'s got anything but DoD on the shelves.  Well, Steam final is out, and I install it on my machine, plug in my Half-Life key as I\'m adding CS to my \'games.\' Good to go. Install Steam final on her machine, try adding CS, plug in the key, and INVALID. Lovely. Maybe I typed it wrong, try again. Nope. Try again, nope. Try again with CAPS LOCK in case it\'s that dumb. Nope. Invalid. OK, try adding DoD. WTF, that works. And nothing else will let me add it with that key. OK, so now I just wasted good money on DoD retail that will never get played, ever? Or is this a problem that will be fixed shortly?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89194, 12628, 1013, 100800, 1072936800, '', 'Steam should get much better at dividing clients onto the avaible servers, as it is today a couple of servers get overloaded, while some barely have any traffic at all.\n\n\n\nThis is very frustrating, as according to the Steam network status (/status.html) there are over 500mbps going unused right now, and I\'m still having problems updating my server.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89201, 12628, 1013, 100156, 1072936800, '', 'the ability to download entire games instead of downloding content in real-time (this especially affects Opposing Force, not ufn when it stutters every five seconds to download a sound file or whole map).\n\n\n\nalso, I think the Opposing Force music is wrong (definately on the initial Osprey ride)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89256, 12660, 1005, 100788, 1072936800, 'Cs 1.6 Bots', 'Hi, I realy miss now the BOTs in the offizial 1.6 version.\n\n\n\nI asked in the #steam-support channel, what happend with the bots and got the answer that they will be enabled soon.\n\n\n\n\n\nIS IT CORRECT THAT VALVE WILL ENABLE THE BOTS SOON? and if yes, can we have a date?\n\n\n\n\n\nCan I have an OFFIZIAL statement please?\n\n\n\nmany tnx 4 your answer\n\n\n\nmfg [AFB]-Mauser-\n\n\n\np.s.: I luv the bots ;-)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(89467, 12660, 1005, 100801, 1072936800, '', 'hi!\n\n\n\nBecause of your "MFG" in your "signature", i expect u to be a german []\n\n\n\nFor the English speaking people:\n\n\n\nYes, valve will enable BOTS for 1.6 within the next updates.\n\nThe LAN feature will be added soon, too.\n\n\n\nSo Steam will work OFFLINE in a few weeks, or months...\n\n\n\nIt\'s just a question of time []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
