(105703, 12742, 1013, 100820, 1072936800, '', 'i was having this exact same error and i had dl\'d the steaminstall_cs.exe from 5 different mirrors all getting that i/o error in various stages of the install.\n\n\n\nwhat i did to get steam installed was to dl the smallest version of steam that had cache files in it to see if a shorter install would help... and it did.\n\n\n\nthe steam install i got was the ricochet version.. steaminstall_ricochet.exe.  the install went quick and i was able to dl the counter strike and dod files through steam once i was connected to the network.\n\n\n\nhopefully this works for you guys, let me know back if this is a viable solution to this annoying problem for everyone.\n\n\n\n\n\n*edit* if it makes any difference i got it from the fileshack mirror and it worked on the first try.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(105872, 12742, 1013, 100821, 1072936800, 'mines broken too', 'my install failed 3 separte times from 3 different downloads...\n\n\n\nerror:\n\n\n\nan i/o error occurred while installing a file. This is normally caused by bad installation media or a corrupt installation file\n\n\n\n\n\nit always fails on counter-strike.gcf\n\nim running a p4 2.4ghz 1gig ram sblive radeon 9700pro..\n\nwindows xp pro\n\n\n\nfrowny face =[\n\n\n\ni just want to play counterstrike dammit, why doesnt this work.. the beta worked fine. </mad>', '127.0.0.1', 1),
