(107068, 12742, 1013, 100822, 1072936800, '', 'Ok...heres my situation:\n\nI go to fileshack download the steamengine for CS then go to open it....\n\nIt locks up...\n\nI delete it through DOS(cause viewing the folder in windows with it in it locks it up)\n\nSo I say...ok I\'ll try it upstairs and bring it down here\n\nI download through a dif mirror just in case it was a case of bad-file-itus..... Mirror: half-life2files.com\n\nI bring it downstairs and plug the damn CD and voila......it freezes...so I say screw this and come here for help....\n\n*end story* now HELP ME!\n\n\n\nMY COMP INFO:\n\nOS: WIN ME\n\nProcessor: P4\n\nHarddrive left: 14 gigabytes\n\nRAM: 128mb RDRAM\n\n\n\nI know its not an error with any part of my hardrive....all clusters have been checked and are good........\n\nHELP ME!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(107146, 12742, 1013, 100820, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by randomthoughts \n\nOk...heres my situation:\n\nI go to fileshack download the steamengine for CS then go to open it....\n\nIt locks up...\n\nI delete it through DOS(cause viewing the folder in windows with it in it locks it up)\n\nSo I say...ok I\'ll try it upstairs and bring it down here\n\nI download through a dif mirror just in case it was a case of bad-file-itus..... Mirror: half-life2files.com\n\nI bring it downstairs and plug the damn CD and voila......it freezes...so I say screw this and come here for help....\n\n*end story* now HELP ME!\n\n\n\nMY COMP INFO:\n\nOS: WIN ME\n\nProcessor: P4\n\nHarddrive left: 14 gigabytes\n\nRAM: 128mb RDRAM\n\n\n\nI know its not an error with any part of my hardrive....all clusters have been checked and are good........\n\nHELP ME!  \n\n\n\nif the install is locking up without any errors then i would suggest disabling/shutting down all background apps (antivirus, utils, etc) and trying to install again.\n\n\n\nalso you might as well try dl\'ing the ricochet version of the steam install like i suggested just to see if that will help.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90074, 12899, 1005, 100867, 1072936800, 'Changing Fonts in CS1.6 + STEAM', '******* Check at the end of this post for new Tutorial ********\n\n******* Check the Second Post to get the Fonts + Updated Optimal TrackerScheme File!********\n\n\n\nCheck the screenshot to see how you can probably change the fonts and sizes to the maximum in CS 1.6\n\n\n\nIt\'s really easy. You can use -ANY- font that you have in your fonts foler (usually c:\\windows\\fonts) and I\'ve tested it with a lot of resolution, it works great.\n\n\n\nFirst, you\'ll need to use the GRAY skin in Steam. So load it in your steam and close steam totally.\n\n\n\nNow go to x:\\steam\\skins\\gray\\resource\n\nOpen the TrackerScheme.res file with Notepad\n\n\n\nThere will be a lot of text with comments (comments = preceeding with //) So you\'ll get your way around it.\n\n\n\nGo down to\n\n	//////////////////////// FONTS /////////////////////////////\n\n(you can change all the other colors like menu color and stuff like that if you want and are capable)\n\n\n\nNow you\'ll see a bunch of configs like\n\n"Default"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultUnderline"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"underline" "1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultSmall"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultVerySmall"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"MenuLarge"\n\n\n\nand so on.\n\n\n\nI tried out many font sizes and configurations and here\'s what\'s the best:\n\n\n\nSet all the fonts that are originally ranging from 8 to 14 to 12\n\nSet all the fonts that are originally ranging over 14 to 14.\n\n\n\nSo a font size 8 would become 12, and 18 would become 14. This has the nicest and cleanest impact on your steam console, the CS console and everything else. It might seem a bit smaller in the consoles but who cares, you can still see very clearly.\n\n\n\n**The screenshot is an example of one of my tries where fonts under 14 were set as 10  and fonts over 10 were set as 12. A bit too small, but it looks really nicer**\n\n\n\nThe only fonts that rest unchanged are the fonts in the Game Scores. (while pressing TAB)\n\n\n\nAlso, If you wonder what font I used, it\'s Square 721 BT. It really fits Counter-Strike (and it\'s easily findable)\n\n\n\nEnjoy!\n\n\n\nUpdate: If you don\'t want to use the gray skin (I just use it to keep the original font sizes) you can always use the x:\\steam\\resource\\Trackerscheme.res which will edit the fonts for the default steam skin.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*** New Font Changing Tutorial ***\n\n\n\nSo I\'ve made a few researches on the different font categories in the TrackerScheme.res configs... Here\'s what I have for you guys.\n\n\n\nFirst, Let\'s open the Tracker file in the gray skin folder: X:\\Steam\\Skins\\Gray\\Resource\\TrackerScheme.res\n\n\n\nYou will see a bunch of text and configs you can change (I\'ll talk about those later on)\n\n\n\nScroll down until you see something like /////////FONTS/////////\n\nI\'ve added NEW comments to the configs so read them!\n\nNOTE: The font i primarly use is SQUARE 721 BT \n\n//////////////////////// FONTS /////////////////////////////\n\n	//\n\n	// describes all the fonts\n\n	Fonts\n\n	{\n\n		// fonts are used in order that they are listed\n\n		// fonts listed later in the order will only be used if they fulfill a range not already filled\n\n		// if a font fails to load then the subsequent fonts will replace\n\n		"Default" // This is the default font used in all Steam consoles/windows\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultUnderline" // Same thing as above, but underlined\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"underline" "1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultSmall" // Default font formatting... (Just Ignore this if you don\'t want to change steam, but only CS1.6)\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultVerySmall" // Yet again ignore this if you don\'t wanna change STEAM\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"MenuLarge" // Same as above\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"	"1000"\n\n				"antialias" "1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"	"800"\n\n				"antialias" "1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n\n\n		// this is the symbol font\n\n		"Marlett" // This determines what font will be used in the minimize/maximize/close buttons in STEAM\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Marlett"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"symbol"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		\n\n		"EngineFont" // You guessed it, This is the font that is used in all Steam Games (That\'s where we start editing for CS1.6 fonts)\n\n		{\n\n			"1" // 1= 640*480 and LOWER resolutions. I already edited the variables so you can alter them in your file. These are the best values I\'ve tried.\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"12"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"480 599"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2" // Change this section if you are playing in 800*600 mode (again, the following variables have been changing for better ones)\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"13"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"600 767"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"3" // 1024*786 Fonts\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"768 1023"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"4" // 1280*1024 (most popular) Fonts\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"18"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"1024 1199"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"5" // Anything over 1600*1200 Fonts goes here.\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"20"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"1200 6000"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"6" // My screen can\'t handle over 1600, but I think these are for the Higher Resolutions like 1900*X . The following numbers *should* be looking good on your resolution.\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"22"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"7" // Same thing as above but probably for 2200*X + Resolutions.\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"24"\n\n				"weight"		"800"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}	\n\n		\n\n		"CreditsFont" // This doesn\'t seem to appear anywhere in the CS Engine.\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"	"600"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2" // Same as above\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n\n\n		"Legacy_CreditsFont" // Added to accomodate 3rd party server plugins, etc. This version should not scale. This is where you fix your fontsizes if things like AMX or Adminmod show HUGE fonts. The following fontsizes are optimal.\n\n		{\n\n			"1" \n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"	"700"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n				"yres"	"1 10000"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Square 721 BT"\n\n				"tall"		"16"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n	}\n\n\n\n	//\n\n\n\n*******************************\n\n\n\nNow Let\'s see how we can modify other Steam Appearance Values!\n\n\n\nRight above the ////////FONTS/////////// Line, there should be an interesting section looking like this (I added comments again)\n\n\n\nInGameDesktop // InGameDesktop is the screen with the 2 CS dudes and the menus on each sides + the Steam Windows\n\n		{\n\n			"MenuColor"// The Normal Menu Text Color		"200 200 200 255" \n\n			"ArmedMenuColor"// This is like a onmouseover color. The color that the menu text takes when the user puts his mouse over it (like highlighting)	"255 255 255 255"\n\n			"DepressedMenuColor"// Same thing as above but this is the color that appears after the user has clicked on a menu text "192 186 80 255"\n\n			"WidescreenBarColor" // This is a fun thing to play with, If you have widescreen enabled, you can change the color of the big black stripes here with RGB colors, the Last number is the visibility so set it to 255 if you put any color except black "0 0 0 0"\n\n			"MenuItemVisibilityRate" "0.03"  // time it takes for one menu item to appear No need to alter anything after this. if you do, all your menus will be weird. hehe\n\n			"MenuItemHeight"	"28" \n\n			"GameMenuInset"		"32"\n\n		}\n\n\n\n***************\n\n\n\nThere is still a LOT we can change but that\'s what I\'m giving you so far! Happy editin!\n\n\n\n******* Check the Second Post to get the Fonts + Updated Optimal TrackerScheme File!********\n\n[]Attachment: cs_assault0005.jpg (attachment.php?s=7dd387096c4c6493e71f414dd726e321&postid=90074)\n\nThis has been downloaded 4052 time(s).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90476, 12899, 1005, 100867, 1072936800, '', 'Update:\n\n\n\nFor resolutions 1280+ use the following:\n\n\n\nFonts originally under 14 = 14\n\nFonts originally over 14 = 16\n\n\n\nWith Fonts like Terbuchet MS, Arial, Verdana.\n\n\n\n** Square 721 BT Download here ** (VERY GOOD FONT FOR CS!!! (IMO))\n\n*** Download the updated TrackerScheme.res File here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&postid=93023#post93023)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90800, 12899, 1005, 100737, 1072936800, '', 'Thank God, my faith in VALVe is 60% restored, lol.  The rest will come when they fix the bugs (incl. font bug seen here): http://mexicanstandoff.org/cs_screens/lol.jpg (http://mexicanstandoff.org/cs_screens/lol.jpg) (happens when you change Legacy_CreditsFont (when it\'s not actually legacy, seeing how its used in CS 1.6.. just for text menus).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(90803, 12899, 1005, 100868, 1072936800, '', 'Hmm.. just tried this and it came out really bad. Also it didn\'t update the in game. I am going to retry this time and actually spend a little more time on it and testing it, but could you clarify where each setting changes the font in the program? If you don\'t already know, I might make a list of what each setting changes and make a better tutorial out of this. Thanks []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91048, 12899, 1005, 100869, 1072936800, '', 'Sweet, got the font down to regular sizes on 1280x1024. Just wondering if this method can be used on the default skin? I don\'t like the grey skin that much.\n\n\n\nPerhaps Valve should look into creating the option for users to customise the font size with the next steam update, as the default font for 1280x1024 is way too big.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91095, 12899, 1005, 100870, 1072936800, '', 'What settings did you use yayoism?\n\n\n\nI can\'t stand the ultra-large font. I just want it back to the way it is in 1.5 []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91105, 12899, 1005, 100869, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jackson Dane \n\nWhat settings did you use yayoism?\n\n\n\nI can\'t stand the ultra-large font. I just want it back to the way it is in 1.5 []  \n\n\n\nHere is what I\'ve setup:\n\n\n\n\n\n	//\n\n	//////////////////////// FONTS /////////////////////////////\n\n	//\n\n	// describes all the fonts\n\n	Fonts\n\n	{\n\n		// fonts are used in order that they are listed\n\n		// fonts listed later in the order will only be used if they fulfill a range not already filled\n\n		// if a font fails to load then the subsequent fonts will replace\n\n		"Default"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultUnderline"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"underline" "1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultSmall"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"DefaultVerySmall"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		"MenuLarge"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"1000"\n\n				"antialias" "1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Tahoma"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"800"\n\n				"antialias" "1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n\n\n		// this is the symbol font\n\n		"Marlett"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Marlett"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"symbol"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n		\n\n		"EngineFont"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana Bold"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"480 599"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana Bold"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"600 767"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"3"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana Bold"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"768 1023"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"4"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana Bold"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"1024 1199"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"5"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana Bold"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"0"\n\n				"yres"	"1200 6000"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"6"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Verdana"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"7"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"		"800"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}	\n\n		\n\n		"CreditsFont"\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Trebuchet MS"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"	"600"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n				"tall"		"14"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n\n\n		"Legacy_CreditsFont" // Added to accomodate 3rd party server plugins, etc. This version should not scale.\n\n		{\n\n			"1"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Trebuchet MS"\n\n				"tall"		"20"\n\n				"weight"	"700"\n\n				"antialias"	"1"\n\n				"yres"	"1 10000"\n\n			}\n\n			"2"\n\n			{\n\n				"name"		"Arial"\n\n				"tall"		"20"\n\n				"weight"		"600"\n\n				"dropshadow"	"1"\n\n			}\n\n		}\n\n	}', '127.0.0.1', 1),
