(94520, 12899, 1005, 100737, 1072936800, '', '@DashSpeed:\n\n\n\n\n\nLegacy_CreditsFont = Buy menus (text), Radio Menus\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI think I remember figuring out what CreditsFont was used for, but I forgot.. if I remember i\'ll post.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(94682, 12899, 1005, 100347, 1072936800, '', 'I saved my original file just in case I didn\'t like the changes but when I put it back, it wasn\'t right.  Anyone have the original file?\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso, can someone edit this custom file to use the original green skin.  I like the in game changes but prefer the original steam skin.\n\n\n\n\n\nThnx.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(94719, 12899, 1005, 100869, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by vegitto \n\n\n\n\n\nAlso, can someone edit this custom file to use the original green skin.  I like the in game changes but prefer the original steam skin.\n\n\n\n\n\nThnx.  \n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m using the original skin with a custom default font. Here is a screenshot of what i\'ve pulled together:\n\n\n\n\n\nClick here for screenshot (http://inept.ausclans.net/other/console_cs_font.jpg)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(94739, 12899, 1005, 100873, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s seems like everyone tries to change 1.6 to 1.5 !!\n\n\nDont understand why you guys & girls tries to change blahi blaha. It\'s an update and it\'s ment to be like it\'s delieverd, live with it and get used to it.\n\n\n\n\n\nCS 1.6 ROCKS!\n\n\nSTEAM ROCKS!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(91230, 13163, 1026, 100881, 1072936800, 'GameServer Hosting Company\'s', 'Well, first of all CS 1.6 is pretty good. I like the visual effects added and re-done models. Of course there are some less better points but that is on every game, so live with it.\n\n\n\nBut there is one thing which is very bad about steam and that is that gamehosting company\'s are going down by it. On 1 rack server it asks 30/40% of CPU power per gameserver. So we would only be able to get a stable 1.6 server by putting only 2 gameservers on 1 server in our rack. Also, a 1.6 server consumes more than 20 % of bandwith compared to 1.5. \n\n\n\nSo my question is.... Did valve also think about gameserver hosting company\'s? And why does the terms of agreement almost say that only valve can put up and control gameservers?\n\n\n\nI think this was needed to say because we from www.getfragged.nl (http://www.getfragged.nl) are now forced to buy new hardware.\n\nWe where also planning a price lowering, but thanks to 1.6 we can\'t make that anymore.\n\n\n\n/SynergY\n\n\n\nps. Yes, we got good cpu\'s and internet access. So that ain\'t the problem. (AMD 2400+ 1gb ddr SCSI and so on)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95314, 13163, 1026, 100882, 1072936800, '', 'Tell me about it!\n\n\n\nIm forced to raise prices by $1 per player! I had some really low pricing before ($3.5 per slot public) and thats gone out the window now. I wish valve would fix the linux intel binaries. I hear the amd ones work right with low usage.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95628, 13163, 1026, 100883, 1072936800, 'finding the cause', 'is any1 able to think about possible reasons for that. (system libs like glibc, plugins, ...)\n\n\n\ni am struggeling with the same problem and am neither able to understand where the problem comes from nor to really track it.\n\n\n\ncpu usage jumps between 40 and 70% on my p4 1.5gz with 512mb ram.\n\n\n\nfyi, there are other gameservers running on this machine, but none of them is in use.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95716, 13163, 1026, 100882, 1072936800, '', 'Well I am running my machines with the HZ=1000 option in param.h compiled into kernel. If you changed that then top is gonna show wrong usage. Even still tho on a box I had before doing that the usage was 40-80% on a full 16 player.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95721, 13163, 1026, 100884, 1072936800, '', 'They\'re testing new binaries for the linux Intel CPU\'s as we speak...  I\'m greatful they\'re giving the attention it needs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95727, 13163, 1026, 100882, 1072936800, '', 'Suh-weeet', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95743, 13163, 1026, 100883, 1072936800, '', 'where do you get this information from?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95753, 13163, 1026, 100884, 1072936800, '', 'Alfred has provided some test binaries as an experiment to see if whatever he\'s doing fixes this problem and makes the Intel binaries as efficient as the AMD - back in 3111d\n\n\n\nThe only problem - is I can not get enough people on this server to test the CPU load.\n\n\n\n65.164.137.163:27015\n\n\n\nOther bugs still exists - such as shield/bomb, etc (CStrike) - we just need 10-12 people on and shooting / moving around to gather the info needed for Valve to see if this will help the CPU prob.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95780, 13163, 1026, 100883, 1072936800, '', 'unfortunatly, i\'m at work and busy\n\n\n\nbut i would be willing to test your server with a couple of other ppl.\n\n\n\nsimply join #ipax on quakenet and wait for me to arrive around 2300 cet.\n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96393, 13163, 1026, 100885, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Datawire \n\nAlfred has provided some test binaries as an experiment to see if whatever he\'s doing fixes this problem and makes the Intel binaries as efficient as the AMD - back in 3111d\n\n \n\n\n\nAnd the AMD binaries are efficient?? As far as I can see, the AMD binaries are worse than the Intel binaries. If you can e-mail (merlijntjuh@hotmail.com) me these test binaries I can test them at the other half of the world (Europe) as I will not join an American server (latency will be at least 150 msec as my HLSW shows).\n\n\n\nHas someone done some tests with different kernels? At the hlds_linux list there are some voices saying the 2.4.9 kernel is far better than anything else. However, you don\'t want to run the 2.4.9 kernel because of security (except the newer 2.4.9e (Enterprise) kernel). I\'m testing the 2.4.9e kernel atm.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96893, 13163, 1026, 100883, 1072936800, '', 'i am currently running 2.4.20 with grsecurity\n\n\n\nran 2.4.18 before, showed heavy cpu usage with v1.1.1.1d too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(99690, 13163, 1026, 100881, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, the amd binaries are also very consuming... I don\'t know how to get in touch with Alfred so i can show him this topic.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(99951, 13163, 1026, 100885, 1072936800, '', 'They are aware of the CPU problem but (they say) have seen wildly conflicting reports about the CPU usage. They also are looking into \'potential\' optimizations, but do not have a concrete timeline. So don\'t expect an update soon (eq. months if you know how fast they update sometimes)...\n\n\n\nWhat one could do is doing some test (time consuming):\n\n\n\n1: install linux 2.4.9 (just for testing, not for production as it is a non-secure kernel)\n\n2: disable all plugins (doesn\'t matter much)\n\n3: do not use pingboost\n\n4: test different kernels\n\n5: test different hardware (they say Intel works better, but I couldn\'t see a difference compared to AMD)\n\n\n\nWe will have to reconsider our market-strategy and prob. have to raise the prices for almost every HL mod.\n\n\n\nValve (and Alfred) are reading these topics (I know they read the hlds_linux list), and I hope they begin to realize that this is a serious issue.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(99975, 13163, 1026, 100886, 1072936800, '', 'Does sue a bit more. I isntalled a program jsut to watch it closly when I\'m not arond. Check the ussages here http://www.clancsf.com/load/ (http://www.clancsf.com/load/)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(100108, 13163, 1026, 100887, 1072936800, '', 'My server, an AMD XP 2400+ with 1024 SDRAM uses about 6-8% cpu with 12 players online... and 6-8% memory.. (with AMX mod, statsme and -pingboost 1) So i cant say it\'s too much.\n\n\n\n//RakeeM', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(95935, 14132, 1026, 100975, 1072936800, 'HERE IS THE SOLUTION to the invaild steam ticket problem!!!!', 'I know the solution to your problem..!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you move your dedicaded server to the computer connected directly to the Internet. That should do the trick. \n\n\nThen you should be able to connect whith your SteamClient from the computer in the network to the computer with the dedicaded server witch is directly connected to the Internet.\n\n\n\n\n\nEX.1 This should work... it did for me \n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 1 with the dedicated Server connected directly to the Internet.\n\n\nIP 192.168.0.1(LAN) and IP 213.113.28.42(Internet)\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 2 with the SteamClient\n\n\nIP:192.168.0.2(LAN)\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer X with another SteamClient\n\n\nIP:192.168.0.X(LAN)\n\n\nand so on\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 1 is sharing Internet to the LAN.\n\n\nThis setup makes everybody able to connect even me :-)\n\n\n----------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nThat is what I did and it should work for you to.\n\n\nI have tried it before and it worked.\n\n\n\n\n\nBut now I don\'t have it like i descibed above because I have my SuperComputer(2.8Ghz,512Ram,128MbATI Connected directly to the Internet and my dedicaded server in the Lan on a Basic Computer(1.1Ghz)\n\n\nAnd I dont want to change my setup like in examle 1\n\n\nBecause i want it to work like this:\n\n\n----------------------\n\n\nEX.2 \n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 1 with the SteamClient connected directly to the Internet.\n\n\nIP 192.168.0.1(LAN) and IP 213.113.28.42(Internet)\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 2 with the Dedicated server \n\n\nIP:192.168.0.2(LAN)\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer X with another SteamClient (this client probably have no problem)\n\n\nIP:192.168.0.X(LAN)\n\n\nand so on\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer 1 is sharing Internet to the LAN.\n\n\nEverybody else is able to connect to my server trough the internet, while I get the annoying message Invalid Steam....\n\n\n--------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nI have tried several portmapping solutions with EX.2 but nu luck...\n\n\nSo I still have a problem. And if someone know any other solution to make it work with EX.2 I would really apreciate it.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBTW\n\n\nI have: winXP where I have my SteamClient (internet sharing)\n\n\nI have: winxp on the dedicaded server (DOS installed)\n\n\n\n\n\nI have tried to forward ports:\n\n\nUDP 1200\n\n\nUDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive\n\n\nTCP 27030 to 27039\n\n\nto both the server and the client, but im not really shure what all the ports are used for. Maybe I did it wrong to.\n\n\nAnd also:\n\n\n5273 TCP is for validating Steam client IDs, and 27012 UDP is for security modules (CS-only right now).\n\n\nI think somehow the ports are being blocked somhow, but i don\'t know how to solve it.\n\n\n-----------------------------\n\n\nOn 1.5 dedicaded server you just forwarded port like this:\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 27010:\n\n\nOutgoing connectivity to this port on remote destinations. Used for advertising a server on the master lists for server browsers.\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 27011:\n\n\nCommunicating with the BanList Server from YOUR Server\n\n\nWas formerly 27013 - much in/out traffic too\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 27015:\n\n\nIncoming connectivity to this port (or whatever port the server had been changed to, if not the default). Used for all client/server game traffic (including voice), server info requests, etc.\n\n\n--------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nSo for now if you want to connect to your own dedicated Server you should place it on the computer connected directly to the Intenet. (EX.1)\n\n\nIt doesn\'t work to have the server inside a network and connect to it from the computer connected directly to the Internet.(EX.2)\n\n\n\n\n\nI really hope that someone know how to fix the EX.2 problem.\n\n\nMaybe som advanced portmapping.\n\n\nI dont have a ROUTER!! I use servises on my connection. (settings|networkconnections|my shared internetconnection|Advanced|settings|services|add service) to portmapp.\n\n\nThank\'s in advance and good luck to you who wanna try EX.1 !!!\n\n\n\n\n\nlantz69 aka [Hlm]Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(97617, 14132, 1026, 100976, 1072936800, '', 'What fixed it for me was simply by joining my Internet server via LAN, instead of throught the external IP via Favorites...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(97860, 14132, 1026, 100975, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by tadmaz \n\n\nWhat fixed it for me was simply by joining my Internet server via LAN, instead of throught the external IP via Favorites...  \n\n\n\n\n\nWell, that works for you maybe, because you have your dedicated server connected directly to the Internet.\n\n\n\n\n\nCorrect me if im wrong about that.\n\n\n\n\n\nTo CLERIFY some things:\n\n\n\n\n\n1. This aint that invalid steam ticket id, that all you have to do is to log out and then back in. \n\n\n\n\n\n2. This is\'nt the one, that you connect into your lan server either. \n\n\n\n\n\nI am saying that this one is to STEAM dedicated server host-ers  that cannot connect into their own servers.\n\n\n\n\n\nProbably bacause they have it setup Like the EX.2 like I desribed in my BIG Post.\n\n\n\n\n\nBTW thanks for your reply tadmaz !!!\n\n\n\n\n\nHope someone has an answer like these ex below:\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you configure your ports like this bla bla bla then you solve your problem.\n\n\nOR\n\n\nIt\'s just not possible right now because............\n\n\n\n\n\nWe really need a definite answer, so we can sleep well at night ;-)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGame on\n\n\nlantz69 aka [Hlm]Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(100831, 14132, 1026, 100977, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for clearing things up a bit Lantz, but it doesnt really solve the problem - it\'s sort of a tweak to get around the fact that there is something strange with Steam.\n\n\nI used the same setup with my old 1.5 server, and it worked just fine.\n\n\n\n\n\nMy server is connected to the internet via my other computer, as in example 2.\n\n\nI don\'t want to reconfigure my network, or buy a router just for this.\n\n\nI don\'t want to be dependent on my server machine to get on the internet, it\'s a crappier computer, and I dont want to have it turned on constantly - just when i use it as server.\n\n\nSince i am using xp shared internet connection I need the computer that\'s connected directly to the internet to be ON for the other computer to get out on the internet, and I simply dont want that to be my old machine, sitting there humming when it doesnt need to.\n\n\nThere must be a solution to this.\n\n\nIs any Valve staff actually reading these forums? It would be nice to get some feedback to our problems. Like - "we are working on it, just wait.." or "Nope, we won\'t fix that - go buy a router, or go play The Sims"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(102050, 14132, 1026, 100975, 1072936800, 'we have the same problem Inkyape', 'Inkyape!!!\n\n\nThanks for the response\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYour desciption of the problem is the same as mine as I wrote in my first post. \n\n\nFrom my first post:\n\n\n\n\n\nI have my SuperComputer(2.8Ghz,512Ram,128MbATI Connected directly to the Internet and my dedicaded server in the Lan on a Basic Computer(1.1Ghz) \n\n\nAnd I dont want to change my setup like in examle 1 \n\n\n--------\n\n\n\n\n\nSo maybe you see now that I totaly agree with you. I also don\'t want to have my dedicated server on all the time making all that noice. I also used the same setup with my old 1.5 server, and it worked just fine. So why should\'t Steam do the same I wonder.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBut I know for a fact that EX.1 works just fine.\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope Steam fixes the problem soon so we can connect our dedicated server. Or maybe post all the portsettings and and what they do. for exampl port xxxx is for validating steam user ID.\n\n\n\n\n\nThat\'s all for me..\n\n__________________\n\nGame on!! Don\'t give up.\n\n\n\n\n\nRegards [Hlm]Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(103703, 14132, 1026, 100978, 1072936800, '', 'There\'s something else causing the problem.  If it\'s a port sharing problem it has to do with something not sharing ports or finding new ones.  I\'m trying to run the client/server on the same machine and I get the invalid ticket error every time I try to log into my server.  Seeing as how my computer is connected directly to the internet there shouldn\'t be any problems with this.  The server was set to use port 27016 so it wouldn\'t conflict with the client just like I\'ve done in 1.5 before.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf I remember correctly I was even able to log into someone else\'s server while leaving my server running and it ran just fine.  I can\'t double check now because I have another error I\'m trying to figure out how to get past.  Everything ran fine(except for not being able to play on my server) for a day or two but now I get some error about the local steam service not running if I just start up steam and attempt to play CS.  I can\'t play any game using steam atm.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(104864, 14132, 1026, 100977, 1072936800, '', 'welcome to the UserID error club, Anarchist.\n\n\n\n\n\nI tried your setup too, actually, running the server on the same machine, using port 27016, and i got the error - just like you.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nValve? Hello?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(104882, 14132, 1026, 100979, 1072936800, '', 'Router or no router has nothing to do with it.\n\n\n\n\n\nFor all intents and purposes my server believes it is connected to the internet (through my router) and I have still received that error atleast once (maybe twice).\n\n\n\n\n\nJust retry the download of the server files.  It may have something to do with how full the content server you are connecting to is.  \n\n\n\n\n\nIt doesnt really hurt anything to restart the download, because it picks up where it left off.\n\n\n\n\n\nPort is irrelevant on server install, which is the only place this error shows up.\n\n\n\n\n\nA possible reason yours worked when you changed setups is probably just because of the fact you tried it again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(105692, 14132, 1026, 100977, 1072936800, '', 'I have reinstalled HLDS four times now.\n\n\n3 times via hldsupdatetool and once via the full hlds install.\n\n\nI have also tried running "dedicated server" on a steam client install (on another steam account) , but nothing has worked.\n\n\nInvalid steam userid ticket.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(105895, 14132, 1026, 100980, 1072936800, '', 'lol, me even worse. \n\n\n\n\n\ni can not remember how many times I installed HLDS and how many methods i used to install it.\n\n\n\n\n\nAt last, all came out with the same problem. Invalid Steam UserID Ticket....\n\n\n\n\n\n#$^$#$%#^$\n\n\n\n\n\nNo words any more........  just wait for valve or Steam\'s solution.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(106052, 14132, 1026, 100977, 1072936800, '', 'yes, but I doubt any Steam staff actually read these forums, so they may not be aware of the problem.\n\n\nIf they DID read here, wouldn\'t you think they would take 30 seconds of their time do drop a comment?\n\n\nThey would benefit from it, since people would know that they were working on the problem, and less hate-posts would be posted. I\'m surprised that this isn\'t the case.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(106093, 14132, 1026, 100981, 1072936800, 'I feel ya man', 'This really sucks. A simple response would make me feel a lot better. Just hold tight, they will come through for us.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(106487, 14132, 1026, 100975, 1072936800, 'Invalid steam ticket IS SOLVED BY ME YEAH!!!!!!!!', 'THIS IS FOR YOU WHO CAN\'T CONNECT TO YOUR DEDICATED SERVER ON THE LAN! (EX.2 FROM THE FIRST POST)\n\n\n\n\n\nCommandline on the steam client was the trick..............\n\n\n\n\n\nIn the Games GUI: \n\n\n1. Rightclick on Counter-Strike\n\n\n2. Choose properties\n\n\n3. In the new window Click on the button Launch options\n\n\n4. Insert: -clientport 27056 +ip your_internetIP\n\n\n\n\n\nSo if your ip is 213.113.58.9\n\n\nthe line should be:\n\n\n-clientport 27056 +ip 213.113.58.9\n\n\nIf this doesn\'t work, just try to change to another port.\n\n\nDon\'t give up right away.\n\n\nThis is so fantasic for me, I just can\'t stop laughing right now.\n\n\nIt\'s such a relief, OoOoOoYeaH !!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPLZ POST IF THIS HELPS YOU TO!!!!!!\n\n__________________\n\nGame on!! Don\'t give up.\n\n\n\n\n\nRegards [Hlm]Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(108334, 14132, 1026, 100980, 1072936800, '', 'What the your_Internetip you mean?\n\n\n\n\n\nClient side\'s IP or server\'s IP?\n\n\n\n\n\nthx in advance. at least make me see the hope. gaga.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(108482, 14132, 1026, 100982, 1072936800, '', 'He is just saying don\'t use your internal IP (192.x prolly), but to use the actual IP address your clients will be connecting to, (i.e. the WAN addy of your router or the external IP addy of your computer running NAT).  \n\n\n\n\n\nI haven\'t tried steam through my router.  I\'m just usin a linux box hooked up directly to the net with two NICS running an iptables nat/firewall script.  Works great.  Players on my opposing force server and AG server are concerned bout shot registration, which seems to have greatly improved in this update. =)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96456, 14229, 1013, 100999, 1072936800, 'Router and TCP/IP Help', 'Hey guys alot of you have been asking about this so i pulled this from the FAQ if you\'re trying to use a router or connect to steam, these are the tcp/ip settings you\'ll need. Remember these are pulled from the faq so here goes! (When it says lan party that means using a router for anything so keep that in mind)\n\n\n\n\n\nHow can I have a LAN party or similar event using Steam?\n\n\n\n\n\nAny Steam game, when played on a LAN or otherwise, requires that each individual client be able to authenticate via the Internet. \n\n\n\n\n\nAt a LAN party, this means that Internet access must be available to every machine on which Steam games are being played. \n\n\n\n\n\nIf desireable, the network administrator of such an event can limit internet access to only the TCP/IP ports which Steam needs. These are:\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 1200\n\n\nUDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive\n\n\nTCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAt large events, it will be necessary for each attendee to let their games fully update before attending to avoid taxing the shared internet connection with too much content delivery.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve got Steam installed - why can\'t I connect?\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you get an error message saying that Steam cannot connect properly, please check your ports. Steam requires that your firewall have the following ports open:\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 1200\n\n\nUDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive\n\n\nTCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFor information about how to control your networking device to open those ports, check the documentation that came with your device or the manufacturer\'s web site.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(97374, 14229, 1013, 100034, 1072936800, '', 'I just have one question lets say you particapated in the steam beta, and it worked, shouldn\'t it be working now if it worked in the beta cause if i\'m not mistaken they haven\'t changed anything with which information the ports  it flows through.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(97390, 14229, 1013, 100999, 1072936800, '', 'In theory yes it should work just fine. But the same installer and steam.exe file you used in the beta WILL NOT WORK!!! You gotta download a new one (preferably with the cache files trust me on this they save you tons of headaches!) and then update from there since it is no longer in beta stages. Check out my tech post from earlier and it should clarify some stuff\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/...&threadid=14270 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=14270)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96590, 14256, 1013, 100694, 1072936800, 'ing Rules', 'Since the recent onslaught of spam here are some rules to follow. \n\n\n1) Any thread flaming another person or organization gets closed on spot. \n\n\n2) Any Swearing in the topic gets closed on spot. \n\n\n3) No "bumping" of threads because you can. There\'s is enough spam already \n\n\n4) No one is going to sympathize with the "Steam/VAVLe sucks". This happened in _every past release_. The exact same thing happens. People complain, and then they get over it. Steam isn\'t going away, so complaints/flames aren\'t going to help your cause. \n\n\n5) Please use common sense. If you wouldn\'t say it to you parents in common conversation, it\'s not appropriate here. \n\n\n\n\n\nRitchey~\n\n__________________\n\n#Steam on GamesNET\n\n\nhttp://forums.counter-strike.net\n\n\nhttp://csnation.counter-strike.net\n\n\nhttp://server.counter-strike.net', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(97410, 14256, 1013, 100045, 1072936800, '', 'If anyone posts a thread with a non-constructive rant, expect it to be deleted.  We\'ve given a lot of leeway in this respect lately, because we understand the large amount of frustration due to the rocky release.  Noone is more frustrated by it than us.  But in order to maintain some semblance of order and usability here, posts are going to be monitored a little more strictly.  \n\n\n\n\n\nIf you want your criticism to be heard, post it in a constructive manner.  Contrary to what some people believe, we do take feedback from here into account, and well-thought-out and constructive feedback is seen by the entire Steam team, whether it\'s negative or positive.\n\n\n\n\n\n(Also note, posting threads complaining about people who complain won\'t fix the problem. []  That just creates more animosity.)\n\n\n\n\n\nupdate:\n\n\n\n\n\nIt shouldn\'t need to be said, but here it is anyway:\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease do not post:\n\n\n\n\n\n- leaked emails, in part or in whole\n\n\n- images from leaked HL2 builds\n\n\n- links to any leaked content', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96703, 14270, 1013, 100999, 1072936800, 'Listen Up People!!! Server Issues!!!', 'Okay people listen up, I\'ve been running around this tech board for the past 45 minutes coming accross the same postings over and over again. I\'m puttting this post up because this should address most of your connection and account issues:\n\n\n\n\n\nAccount verification\n\n\n\n\n\nFirst off yes, the verification server is down. I don\'t know for how long it is down it happens like this randomly. The servers right now are very overloaded in case you all haven\'t noticed they just released a new steam (The 700 mb one with all the cache files) and it is fnarking with their bandwith.  So what does this mean for you guys? It means:\n\n\n\n\n\nyou cannot login if you\'re not already\n\n\nYou cannot change passwords\n\n\nYou cannot set up new accounts\n\n\nMost of the steam is unplayable\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso be adivsed that creating multiple accounts from the same installations can result in your cd key being blocked and having to go through steam technical support which is like waiting for Duke Nukem forever to come out...meaning its gonna take a while....\n\n\n\n\n\nGames\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is another souce of strife so here goes\n\n\n\n\n\nThe general consensus I\'m getting is that most of the people (inclduing me) have had numerous problems with the 500k steam installer, the one that converts all of your old installations to the steam cache. So what should you do? AVOID THIS DAMN INSTALLER! THIS HAS BEEN POSTED ON STEAM\'S NEWS AND OTHER CS WEBSITES! Use any of the installers with the cache files preloaded and you should be able to avoid alot of headaches. I repeat, they have released a steam installer with 700 mb of cache files which covers all the games: hl, cs, OpFor, tfc, dod, ricochet, and dedicated server. Any other hl mod you\'ll have to convert at your own risk. there is no general reliablity anywhere for any of the other games right now beyond those which i have mentioned.\n\n\n\n\n\nWON\n\n\n\n\n\nThere also seems to be a major confusion regarding won out there. Like it has been mentioned in steam news, WON will not be shut down until steam is fully operating AND operating smoothly. That means your old installations will still work if you can find servers for them. Valve is not going to monkeyshaft us anymore than they have to so just so you know. The general timetable for the WON shutdown has not been established but from what I\'ve been hearing it should be within a month. \n\n\n\n\n\nTechnical issues\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve already posted a lot of stuff regarding tech stuff in previous posts, heres the links for First: TCP/IP issues, and teh Second: For sound and Graphics Issues\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/...&threadid=14229 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=14229)\n\n\n\n\n\nGraphics and Sound Issues:\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/...&threadid=12366 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=12366)\n\n\n\n\n\nOkay guys? Just take this one day at a time. Yes Valve and Steam have messed up CS and whatnot but it will be ironed out just give em some time and they will get it fixed ok?\n\n\n\n\n\nHappy CS\'ing!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(96742, 14270, 1013, 101005, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for the post. Hopefully this will reduce the numerous topics being posted about login/registration issues regarding the current problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
