(116411, 17835, 1013, 103378, 1072936800, 'Could not connect to steam network, or your inet connection is down error - fix', 'Loads of people have got this error (including me).\n\n\n\nHere\'s how I fixed it.\n\n\n\n1. Remove the file called ClientRegistry.blob from your steam folder.\n\n\n\n2. Run steam again and let it update.\n\n\n\n3. Create a new account with a valid e-mail addy (dont use the same one you used before).\n\n\n\n4. You should be able to progress to the next screen after this account is created.\n\n\n\nFrom looking around the forums, it seems that some accounts have got messed up when steam was installing the first time around, or if people tried to inherit an account from the beta releases. By creating a brand new account, it seems to scrub the corrupted one and everything works fine from then on.\n\n\n\nThis fix worked fine for me, (after pulling my hair out for 5 days).\n\n\n\nIf this is indeed whats causing so much hassel for folks, then I think the Valve support team need to seriously pay attention to the posts on these forums, cos such a simple fix should have been posted by them ages ago.\n\n\n\nJust to make it easier for people to get this fix, please post a reply if this worked for your steam installation, that way it will keep getting bumped up to the top of the lists and will be seen by people quicker. - in fact rate it so it can be seen quicker, this must be the single most infuriating problem folks are having - so help them to see the answer.\n\n\n\n_________________________________________________', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116742, 17835, 1013, 103378, 1072936800, '', '/bump', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116756, 17835, 1013, 101149, 1072936800, '', 'Sooo... All we have to do is get a new CDKEY, ok!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116835, 17835, 1013, 103378, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, I\'ll try to clarify what Tor is hinting at.\n\n\n\nThere are issues associated with creating accounts on different e-mail addresses because the cd key is locked to the e-mail address of the account. This means that 2 different accounts with different e-mail addresses would run the risk of steam banning the cd number since it would assume the same cd key was being used by 2 different pc\'s.\n\n\n\nHowever. This fix is for those of us who installed the Steam Client and got the error message \'Can\'t connect to the Steam Network, etc ,etc,\'  every time they tried to use Steam.\n\n\n\nThe fix works because the original account is recognised by the authorising servers, but they do not seem to validate it. This appears to be caused by attempting to use an old account from the beta versions, or possibly by interrupting the installation of the latest steam versions. In any case, the account info is wrong and it has to be fixed (otherwise you dont get past the error message)\n\n\n\nBy creating a new account IN THIS SITUATION ONLY the problem is solved and the new account is recognised as the only valid account. The old account is no longer recognised.\n\n\n\nI hope this clears up this issue. (and I hope Valve get round to fixing the problem once and for all in the next client upgrade).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116856, 17835, 1013, 103379, 1072936800, '', 'so i\'m guessing that this fix will not work as I\'ve been playing 1.6 up to about 5 days ago, I\'m gonna have a go at doing what you said, but trying to log back onto my old email addy, or will that just take me back to square 1?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116902, 17835, 1013, 103379, 1072936800, '', '.. ffs, steam is the worst piece of **** ever. What was wrong with WON?!?  had it working okay after hours of f*cking about with it, downloaded the gcf files from bittorrent as the steam 512kb updater didn\'t work. Played 1.6 for a week which is really really bad, far too easy for 21-0 scores imo. \n\n\n\nIt\'s been not working for a week, but is for other people?! Steam have somehow forgotten (or it seems they have) about my account as I was one of the 1st to register. So i uninstall it and re-try to update, and i cant. \n\n\n\nWhy mass release something before it works?! \n\n\n\n/rant', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116917, 17835, 1013, 103378, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah G0at  - I wish they had left well alone\n\n\n\nI reckon u might be ok if you create a new account with a different e-mail addy though.\n\n\n\nSounds to me like you have missed the newer install versions and thats why it wont let you use your old account details.\n\n\n\nIts easy for me to sit here and say you should try a new account, but lets face it, if you keep getting the same old error message, you dont have much choice.\n\n\n\nI bit the bullet and it worked for me - hope it does for you too', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(116932, 17835, 1013, 103379, 1072936800, '', 'yeh, well thanks for your help. Really apprieciate it, was gonna try something similar before i saw your post. Well, i\'m sititng here with 1.6 in front of me, but with a different email address, just tried to keep the password / password question as similar as I could; so they know it\'s the same person, but just using a different email.\n\n\n\nWhat if you had multiple users on your computer that play cs - they\'d have to register individially, so there\'d be multiple emails showing up on the same key anyways - just a thought. As long as you connect through the same subnet mask / ip I\'m assuming you\'d be okay.\n\n\n\nOnce again, Eric; thanks for your help m8.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
