(121136, 18252, 1013, 100110, 1072936800, 'Net_sendpacketerror: WSAEINTR', 'quote:Originally posted by P30N \n\nRecently when I am playing 1.6, for no reason at all, I\'ll get the following error \n\nNet_sendpacketerror: WSAEINTR \n\nThis will cause steam to crash and close. \n\nI did a metacrawler search for the error, and came to 2 sites that both said I was to " Uninstal the QOS software from ur lan connection and ur internet connection" considering I saw the same fix from different people on 2 different sites, I figured to try it, since the steam forums werent helping any. unintsall went fine. I hop back on counter-strike 1.6, play 3 maps, near the end of the 3rd map, im running with my knife out, and bam I get the same \n\nNet_sendpacketerror: WSAEINTR \n\nUgh Please help \n\nThis is one fo the websites. \n\nhttp://www.techfest.com/wwwboard/messages/663.shtml (http://www.techfest.com/wwwboard/messages/663.shtml)  \n\n\n\nand.....did you follow the suggestions on the board as to how to fix it?....??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121145, 18252, 1013, 101718, 1072936800, '', 'The steam board doesnt have any suggestions to fix it.\n\nI followed the suggestions on the link that I provided, and I also explained that I did this, if you would read my post \n\n"considering I saw the same fix from different people on 2 different sites, I figured to try it, since the steam forums werent helping any. unintsall went fine. . ."', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121157, 18252, 1013, 101719, 1072936800, '', 'I helped someone on another forum earlier today that had a very similiar problem.  His error finally was tracked back to a port forwarding issue.  Granted, his problem was not identical to yours but it might be worth the time to look into you Internet connection a little closer.\n\n\n\nWhat exactly are you running?\n\n__________________\n\nDo you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some.\n\n\n\n"Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM\n\n\n\nStupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is.  Add some chlorine to the gene pool...\n\n\n\n-Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121221, 18252, 1013, 101718, 1072936800, '', 'Well i did some more searching and found this...\n\nHome > Error Messages > "NET_SendPacket ERROR: WSAEINTR"\n\n\n\n\n\nThis error may be caused by the following things:\n\n\n\n1.) Bad Winsock dll\n\n2.) Bad TCP/IP stack\n\n3.) Conflicting Ports\n\n4.) Firewall\n\n5.) VIA KT133A motherboard chipset w/o proper 4-in-1 patch\n\n6.) Windows 2k w/o service pack 2\n\n7.) Punkbuster conflict\n\n8.) Wrong vCache settings\n\n\n\nAlso, this MS Knowledge Base Article may solve this issue.\n\n\n\nPossible solutions:\n\n\n\n1. Bad Winsock dll: \n\nContact Microsoft Technical Support for step-by-step instructions on how to reinstall Winsock for your operating system. \n\n2. Bad TCP/IP stack: \n\nRemove all TCP/IP instances from Network Properties. \n\nGo to Control Panel >> Add/Remove Programs >> Windows Setup and remove all of the Communications components. Restart then repeat the same procedure, but instead check the box and install the components. Next readd the TCP/IP protocol in your network properties.\n\n\n\n3. Conflicting Ports: \n\nTry adding this to the end of your command line:\n\n+clientport 27055 \n\n4. Firewall: \n\nDisable your firewall. \n\nIf you run BlackICE setup an allow set for ports 27005 thru 27030. \n\nIf you have Windows XP disable the internal firewall, or if you use ICS disable that. \n\n5. VIA KT133A motherboard chipset w/o proper 4-in-1 patch: \n\nVisit www.via.com (http://www.via.com) and get the latest 4-in-1 patch. \n\n6. Windows 2k w/o service pack 2 \n\nRead the following Microsoft Knowledge Base article here. \n\n7. Punkbuster conflict: \n\nDisable the PunkBuster client on your machine and try non-PunkBuster servers.\n\n\n\n8. Wrong vCache settings \n\nTo fix this problem you need to go to the system.ini file and check the [vcache]. \n\nIf there is nothing there, add these lines under the word [vcache]:\n\nMinFileCache=****\n\nMaxFileCache=****\n\n\n\nIt should look like this.\n\n[vcache]\n\nMinFileCache=****\n\nMaxFileCache=****\n\n\n\n\n\nReplace **** with one of the following values:\n\n\n\nIf you have from 16-32 MB of RAM:\n\nMinFileCache=2048\n\nMaxFileCache=2048\n\n\n\nIf you have from 32-96 MB of RAM:\n\nMinFileCache=4096\n\nMaxFileCache=4096\n\n\n\nIf you have 128 MB of RAM or more:\n\nMinFileCache=8192\n\nMaxFileCache=8192 \n\n\n\nAnother way would be setting the maximum amount of RAM HL/CS is allowed to use. \n\nRight click on your CS shortcut and select "Properties". Right now the Target line should read something like this:\n\n\n\nCS retail version: C:\\Sierra\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.exe -console\n\nCS mod version: C:\\Sierra\\Half-Life\\hl.exe -game cstrike -console\n\n\n\nChange it to this: \n\nCS retail version: C:\\Sierra\\Counter-Strike\\cstrike.exe -console -heapsize ***** \n\nCS mod version: C:\\Sierra\\Half-Life\\hl.exe -game cstrike -console -heapsize *****\n\n\n\nReplace ***** with 75% of your total memory in KB, ex. you have 128 MB RAM then heapsize should be 98304. \n\n1 MB = 1024 KB.\n\nIf a steam representative would please read this and reply that would be just neat!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121267, 18252, 1013, 101719, 1072936800, '', 'Well, I doubt you\'ll get a Valve rep answering this post but my bet is on #4 (or a related issue).\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nSpecifically, do you have a router?\n\n \n\nIt might also help to include your exact system specs including motherboard and Internet connection/related hardware.\n\n__________________\n\nDo you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some.\n\n\n\n"Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM\n\n\n\nStupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is.  Add some chlorine to the gene pool...\n\n\n\n-Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121283, 18252, 1013, 101720, 1072936800, '', 'I had the same problem when I used to play on a dial-up.  The problem only occured in WinXP for whatever reason.  I read somewhere that it has something to do with noise in the line.  I know, it\'s a pretty strange theory.  Anyway, I had to switch back to Win2k to fix the problem.  If your on a dialup, try yelling into your phone while connected; and then go back to your computer to see if you get the error.  Good luck.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121386, 18252, 1013, 101718, 1072936800, '', 'I tried running CS 1.6 without my firewall and without my antivirus running to see if that was the problem, and I still got the same net_sendpacketerror:WSAEINTR\n\nI have checked just about every forum, with just about no fixes. I tried the uninstall QoS Scheduler, and that didn\'t work.\n\nI\'m not on 56k, and I\'m not using a router. This problem has only just recently happened to me (within the last 3 days) And this error only seems to come up when im doing good in CS. I\'m a little wary of trying what I listed earlier because I uninstalled the QoS scheduler in order to fix this problem, and it didnt, so I basiclly uninstalled QoS scheduler for nothing, and I dont want to mess up anything more especially with some of the stuff that I listed. Could someone with some real expertise please help.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121434, 18252, 1013, 101719, 1072936800, '', 'QoS Packet Scheduler is a bad thing to have installed if you are gaming anyway.  No great loss.\n\n\n\nAS for the rest of the post of tweaks, a lot of them are valid but I doubt seriously if any of them will help your problem.\n\n\n\nWhat *might* help me or someone else to help you would be for you to answer the questions I\'ve asked.\n\n__________________\n\nDo you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some.\n\n\n\n"Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM\n\n\n\nStupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is.  Add some chlorine to the gene pool...\n\n\n\n-Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121474, 18252, 1013, 101718, 1072936800, '', 'I answered 2 of your 3 questions\n\n#1 no its not the firewall because I was still getting the same error when my firewall and antivirus werent running, so your hunch of it being #4 is incorrect\n\n#2 I have stated several times that no I do not use a router\n\n#3 I\'m not sure what brand or type my motherboard is.  As far as network applications go, im running a Motorola SURFboard SB5100 USB Cable Modem.  If you need further information on my specs you will need to instruct me on how to find them (ie how do I find my motherboard specs?) 2.4 gh proccesor, 120 gig hard drive, gf4 Ti 4600, not sure what else you would like me to list.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(121498, 18252, 1013, 101719, 1072936800, '', 'Well, I have to go to bed now (it\'s 2:15AM here) but I would advise you to get a program called Belarc Advisor and run it.  Find the section detailing your motherboard and post that section.  It will contain enough inforamtion for someone to find what board and BIOS you are using.\n\n\n\nDO NOT post the report in it\'s entirety as it contains information that you don\'t want published on the Internet.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.belarc.com/free_download.html (http://www.belarc.com/free_download.html)\n\n\n\nThere may be other information needed but lets get this done first.  DO NOT post all of that report.  You have been warned.\n\n__________________\n\nDo you think cheat sites are going to not screw you up? If they\'ll post cheats, what will they do to your computer when they know you\'ll willingly install anything that has "cheat" in the name. Common sense here, folks. Use some.\n\n\n\n"Most peoples problems are inflicted upon themselves or by their pre-built box OS builds." - Me. 05-03-2004 04:25 PM\n\n\n\nStupidity should be painful. If you are stupid enough, it should be lethal and sometimes is.  Add some chlorine to the gene pool...\n\n\n\n-Giggles like a schoolgirl at every VAC update-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
