(125070, 18837, 1013, 101845, 1072936800, 'thank you', 'thank you so much for your post it was what i needed to do...\n\n\n\ni had not been able to play 1.6 since it came out at all... but when i turned on norton and configured a rule it let me connect to a server for the first time! awsome....\n\n\n\ni just think it is kind of wierd that i must run my firewall in order to play cs, but i guess i should run it while i am gaming anyway!\n\n\n\nthanks again for the advice, it worked for me!\n\n\n\nuA` 3nt|2opy\n\n\n\n#team`ua\n\ngamesnet', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(126149, 18837, 1013, 101846, 1072936800, 'Firewall Hell', 'I have a D-link DSL-504 Router which has a built in firewall. However I cannot run Steam - always says Steam not running of my connection is screwed - I believe in some way it is the latter!\n\n\n\nAnyone know how I can tell my firewall to allow Steam through - Dont have any probs with any other Internet program/game etc.\n\n\n\nI am beginning to wonder why I left my PC on for 5 hours to download a huge file which does.....nothing!\n\n\n\nI would appreciate some help on this before 1.6 is released (if ever) publically.\n\n\n\nCheers', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(126286, 18837, 1013, 101846, 1072936800, 'THE ANSWER TO ALL YOUR ILLS', 'Loads of people have got this error (including me). \n\n\n\nHere\'s how I fixed it. \n\n\n\n1. Remove the file called ClientRegistry.blob from your steam folder. \n\n\n\n2. Run steam again and let it update. \n\n\n\n3. Create a new account with a valid e-mail addy (dont use the same one you used before). \n\n\n\n4. You should be able to progress to the next screen after this account is created. \n\n\n\nFrom looking around the forums, it seems that some accounts have got messed up when steam was installing the first time around, or if people tried to inherit an account from the beta releases. By creating a brand new account, it seems to scrub the corrupted one and everything works fine from then on. \n\n\n\nThis fix worked fine for me, (after pulling my hair out for 5 days). \n\n\n\nIf this is indeed whats causing so much hassel for folks, then I think the Valve support team need to seriously pay attention to the posts on these forums, cos such a simple fix should have been posted by them ages ago. \n\n\n\nJust to make it easier for people to get this fix, please post a reply if this worked for your steam installation, that way it will keep getting bumped up to the top of the lists and will be seen by people quicker. - in fact rate it so it can be seen quicker, this must be the single most infuriating problem folks are having - so help them to see the answer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(126336, 18837, 1013, 101847, 1072936800, 'RxWookieRxWookieRxWookie', 'Omg RxWookie you are like my god! i\'ve been trying to get steam to work since it was a beta.. i never would have thought it was my firewall after i had changed settings on it earlier.. thankyou !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
