(129538, 18837, 1013, 101850, 1072936800, '', 'I dunno, if my problem is a port problem.\n\n\n\nWhen I refresh my server list the pings avg out to about 20-40.\n\n\n\nBut when I connect it take really long to start up and I lag like crazy.  I get a Cl_FlushEnityPacket error.  This probably happens like 95% of the time, cause i do connect with a regular speed sometimes.\n\n\n\nThis problem happens in both CS and DOD.  I tried it on TFC but I had no problems thus far.\n\n\n\nHELP PLEASE!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(130535, 18837, 1013, 101851, 1072936800, '', 'So, i have Norton FW and everything is done as said by RxWookie. The problem:\n\nmissing the HL.exe in each mod dir.\n\nHELP PLZ\n\n\n\ntschy2m', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132756, 18837, 1013, 101852, 1072936800, '', 'Just thought I\'d add to the good work by RxWookie and post the steps for ppl with the "Tiny" personal firewall, even though if you are using Tiny you prolly don\'t need me to tell you how to do it. []\n\n\n\n1) Right click on the TPF icon in the sys tray and click on Firewall Administration.\n\n\n\n2) Ensure the slider is set to "Ask me first" and click on "Advanced".\n\n\n\n3) In the config window that comes up click on "Add", a new ruleset window will appear. \n\nFill it in as follows.\n\n\n\nDescription: Whatever rocks your world []\n\nProtocol: TCP and UPD\n\nDirection: Both\n\nLocal Endpoint: (Leave it on the Default)\n\nRemote Endpoint: (Leave it on the Default)\n\nApplication: Only Selected Below. (Then use the browse button to navigate to your " c:\\programfiles\\steam\\steamapps\\youremailaddy\\coun\n\nter-strike\\" folder and select hl.exe)\n\nRule Valid: Always\n\nAction: Permit\n\n\n\nClick ok out of the rule window and click ok again out of the config window then ok again out of the admin window.\n\n\n\nHope this helps someone.\n\nHappy fraggin.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(123262, 18963, 1013, 101890, 1072936800, 'CD key is already taken?!?', 'I just set up a Steam account with my copy of half life and got a nice reply say that my copy of half-life platum pack is already authed to a different users.\n\n\n\nThe problem is that I have a "Game of the year edition" (well over a year old)  and I never give anyone my CD-keys or game disks (battle.net can be thanked for that) so as to make sure this kind of thing doesn\'t happen.\n\n\n\nSo I guess my question is, what can I do?\n\nIs there some forum I can fill out, or should I just send someone at valve a picture of me holding my CD case with the key on it?!?\n\n\n\nHELP???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
