(123632, 18963, 1013, 101890, 1072936800, '', 'umm wonderful, someone too bothered to pay for his/her own copy of HL is screwing me out of my HL.\n\n\n\nI\'ve paid for HL, about 3 times now, after forgetting disks in a move, or having CD cases getting lost (so I had to get a new one for the key) but this is just too far, I\'ve bought and paid for my right to play Half-Life!!!\n\n\n\nThe other times I had to replace my copy of HL were my fault, but I\'ll be damned before I buy a new copy because someone needed to get it for free, or because Steams database has some form of error.\n\n\n\nDoes anyone know whom I would contact (e-mail) to get things put right?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
