(123999, 18963, 1013, 101890, 1072936800, '', 'well when I forget the CD-key its one thing, but when Valve updates HL to \'make it better\' and in return I can\'t play. I think I deserve an explanation from them if nothing else (something I have not yet gotten, though I have e-mailed support)\n\n\n\nAnd why would the other CD-key be in use also if I was just to go down to EB and buy a new copy?!?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(124012, 18963, 1013, 101894, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Flynntargart \n\nwell when I forget the CD-key its one thing, but when Valve updates HL to \'make it better\' and in return I can\'t play. I think I deserve an explanation from them if nothing else (something I have not yet gotten, though I have e-mailed support)\n\n\n\nAnd why would the other CD-key be in use also if I was just to go down to EB and buy a new copy?!?  \n\n\n\nthe other copy could be in use due to a key generator.. if somone had generated this key previously, and you both tried using CS at the same time, WON would have given you authentication failure, so you obviously play at different times, and he regged with the key first.. theres little you can do about it, except, as i say, contact valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
