(130740, 20194, 1005, 102021, 1072936800, 'Managing Access to Servers', 'Now that our server has gone to 1.6, it can, of course, be found via STEAM, so far so good. \n\n\n\n\n\nBUT,  what we are finding now is that our server is becoming so busy that our old regulars can no longer get on [] and we are getting all sorts of people playing that we would probably rather not have (for various reasons).\n\n\n\n\n\nApart from permanently pwd protecting the server, has anyone got any ideas how we can manage this? We used to have a very friendly server with a couple of dozen regulars and a few hundred occaisionals, but now it doesnt feel like \'home\' any more - I might as well be on a public, except I wouldn\'t have admin there of course []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(130744, 20194, 1005, 102022, 1072936800, '', 'You could set up an unusually high number of reserved slots and list all your regulars as reserved slot users', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(130752, 20194, 1005, 102021, 1072936800, '', 'I did think about that - but my old HLSW wonid DB did have literally 100s of \'regulars\' and it would be a nightmare to maintain - it might be a good way to start though - I could reserve a number of slots for all those registered on our forum for example.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(135700, 20194, 1005, 102021, 1072936800, '', 'Any other ideas? (PLEASE)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131318, 20294, 1005, 102032, 1072936800, 'How to Install Custom Models, Sounds, Sprites, Maps, and Sprays In CS 1.6', 'I am making this thread to help those who don\'t know how to instal custom models and sprays.\n\n\n\nHere is what\'s in this tutorial (in order).\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Models\n\nInstalling Custom Sounds\n\nInstalling Custom Sprites\n\nInstalling Custom Maps\n\nMaking and Installing Custom Sprays\n\nCustomizing Autobuy\n\nCustomizing Rebuy\n\nWriting Your First Alias\n\n\n\n\n\n**The Last 3 are on page 4 of this thread!!!**\n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE:Through out this tutorial I refer to a directory C:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.com\\counter-strike\\cstrike  This is simply just your counter-strike folder, just find you steam folder, then select the folder steamapps, inside that folder is you email address, select that and then inside that choose Counter-strike and finally within counter-strike is the folder cstrike.\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Models\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Weapon Models\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo install custom weapon models, first go into the directory:\n\n\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.com\\counter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\n\n\nIn that directory add a folder called models. Within that folder you place your custom models. If you want to install a custom shield model make a folder within your models folder called: shield.  Place the shield models in there \n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE: There isn\'t a model to just replace the shield, every shield and gun combo is a different model, so if you get a five-seven shield model and the shield is different, the shield is only different for the five-seven.\n\n\n\nFrom there they should be installed and ready to be played. \n\n\n\nNOTE: NOTE: Not all P models are not compatible with steam, if you place an incompatible P model in the model folder you will be able to start up steam although you will not be able to join a game, it will just quit joining and in the console it will say something about the P model you installed. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Installing Custom Player Models \n\n\n\n\n\n**NOTE:** If you have already completed installing a custom weapon model skip ahead to the paragraph begining with "Open the models folder" \n\n\n\n\n\nTo install Custom player models first go to the directory:\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.COM\\Ycounter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\n\n\nIn that directory make a folder called Models. \n\n\n\nOpen the models folder.  In that folder create another folder called player.  In that folder you will need to create a folder for each character that you are changing model.  So if you are changing the leet krew model you need to add a folder named leet.  The folder named are below\n\n\n\n\n\n Character Name - Folder Name\n\n                                      \n\n   SAS - SAS\n\n   German GSG9 - GSG9\n\n   French GIGN - GIGN\n\n   SEAL - Urban\n\n   Phoenix Connection - Terror\n\n   Leet Krew - leet\n\n   Arctic Warfare - arctic\n\n   Guerilla Warfare - guerilla\n\n   VIP -  VIP\n\n   \n\n\n\nFrom there place the player model for that character inside his specific folder.  If you want to install a hostage model place it directly inside the model folder, not the players folder!\n\n\n\nNow your ready to play with your custom player models!\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Sounds\n\n\n\n\n\nTo install custom sounds first go to the directory:\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.COM\\counter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\nIn that directory creat a folder called Sounds.\n\n\n\nInside that folder create a folder called Weapons.\n\n\n\nWithin that folder you place your custom weapon sounds.  From there you are ready to use your custom sounds!\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Sprites\n\n\n\nTo install custom sprites first go to the directory:\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.COM\\counter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\nIn that directory create a folder called Sprites.\n\n\n\nIn that folder all you need to do is place your custom sprites and your done!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling Custom Maps\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo install a custom map first go to the directory:\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.COM\\counter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\nIn the folder cstrike create a folder called: Maps\n\n\n\n(you may already have one if you have downloaded a custom map from a server)  Place all custom maps inside that folder, and your ready to play with them!\n\n\n\n\n\nCustom Sprays\n\n\n\n**NOTE:**  If you already have your custom spray skip the Making a custom spray section and continue to installing a custom spray (section after Making a custom spray) \n\n\n\n\n\nMaking a custom spray\n\n\n\n\n\nTo make a custom spray you MUST have a more advanced "coloring" program than paint.  There are some trial versions of software available online.\n\n\n\n\n\nFirst open the program.  Go to File - New.\n\n\n\nThis is important, there is a limit on the size a spray can be, below are a few nice sizes for sprays.\n\n\n\nNOTE: These sizes are in Pixels!!! Make sure it is in pixels or it will most likely end up being too big!\n\n\n\n64x128\n\n128x64\n\n256x32\n\n32x256\n\n32x32\n\n64x64\n\n\n\n(x separates two numbers it means "by" (ex: 64 by 128);  The first number is height and second is width)\n\n\n\nThe are will seem very small so use magnified glass (or whatever tool is used to zoom in the program you are using) to zoom in if you want to.\n\n\n\nNow create your picture, put what ever you want on it!  The only other thing you must know is when you are creating it if you want to make a transparent (see-through) area it must be pure blue.  The code for pure blue is: 0000FF\n\n\n\n(Picture of Pure Blue (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut1.gif))\n\n\n\nType that in what ever box allows for it when you are selecting colors.  So if you want blue in your picture make it slightly lighter or darker because if it is pure it will be transparent!\n\n\n\n\n\nOk, now finish making your picture,  Go to File - Save As  and save your file as what ever name you want but make sure you save it as a .bmp\n\n\n\nIf it asks you for saving options leave them at default, it should be correct.  But just to be sure it should be Windows format and 24 bit compression.\n\n\n\n( Picture of Saving a BMP Correctly (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut2.gif))\n\n\n\nNow you need to download a program called Wally.\n\n\n\nClick one of the links below to begin your download:\n\n\n\nDownload Wally from 3D Downloads (http://www.3ddownloads.com/?file_id=149727#)\n\nDownload Wally from Fileplanet (http://www.fileplanet.com/dl.aspx?planethalflife/wadfather/tools/wally_155b.exe)\n\n\n\n(Although Fileplanet usually has long lines because this is not a very commonly downloaded file there are only two servers but usually no wait time)\n\n\n\nNow download and install Wally.\n\n\n\nWhen it is finished installing open the program.\n\n\n\nIn Wally in the top menu go to Wizard - HL Color Decal\n\n\n\n(Picture of Wally Menu (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut3.gif))\n\n\n\nA new menu should pop up.  First it will say please select your Half-life folder (Do not select your Half-Life, Counter-Strike, Day of Defeat etc. folder!), select what ever folder you want. Next go down to where it says Source Image.\n\n\n\n(Picture of Menu your looking at now (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut4.gif))\n\n\n\nThere are two options Clipboard and File on hard drive.  Select File on hard drive.  Then next to a big white box there is a button that says "..." Click it and browse for the picture that you just created.  Then click OK.  If you followed directions perfectly that window should close, and a new one with your picture in it should open.  \n\n\n\n(Picture of Window that Should Have Opened (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut5.gif))\n\n\n\nNow go to File - Save As\n\n\n\nSelect your desktop and save the file as pldecal (make sure it is a .wad image)\n\n\n\n(Picture of Saving your File Correctly (http://home.comcast.net/~triforce89/cstut6.gif))\n\n\n\nAnd now your ready to install your spray!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstalling a custom spray\n\n\n\n\n\nTo install your spray go to the directory:\n\n\n\nC:\\Program  Files\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUREMAIL@YOURSERVICEPROVIDE\n\nR.COM\\counter-strike\\cstrike\n\n\n\nTake your pldecal file and place it into that directory, it will have to overwrite the existing pldecal.  Then delete a file called custom.hpk\n\n\n\nNow your ready to use your spray in game!\n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE: Do not go into the options area anymore, if your change anything you will have to put your pldecal file back in the cstrike directory!  Although, you can make stop this by right clicking the file and selecting Read-Only, then you will be able to use the options menu.\n\n\n\n\n\n __________________________________________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThere you go!\n\n\n\nI hope that helps some of you.\n\n\n\nIf something is wrong please tell me and I\'ll fix it.\n\n\n\nAlso if you need anymore help you can IM me at jstr008\n\n\n\nIf anyone wants to use this tutorial it is ok with me as long as I receive credit.  Also I would appreciate it if you Private Message me or IM me a link to the site!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131428, 20294, 1005, 102033, 1072936800, '', 'THANKS!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! YOUR THE BEST!!!!!!!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
