(131884, 20407, 1005, 102060, 1072936800, 'Final Say On Fps', 'Hello.  I am starting this thread to shed some light on the FPS issues regarding CS 1.6 once and for all.  This post may seem redundant to some users but, all the other FPS threads that I\'ve seen were either inconsistent or simply "lost in the shuffle".  Let me get started with my computer setup and problems:\n\n\n\nCPU:  866 Mhz Pentium III\n\nRAM:  256 MB PC-133 SDRAM\n\nVIDEO CARD:  geForce 2 Ultra\n\nWINDOWS VERSION:  Windows 98 SE\n\nDIRECT X:  Direct X 9.0b\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS:  nVidia 45.23 Reference Drivers\n\nVIDEO METHOD:  OpenGL\n\nGAME RESOLUTION:  1024x768\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH:  32-bit\n\nV-SYNC:  ON\n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES:  4xAA\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION:  Cable\n\n\n\nIn CS 1.5, I got max FPS no matter what.  My computer NEVER slowed down except when there were a large number of smoke grenades on screen.  It was smooth, enjoyable gaming all the way.  After installation of CS 1.6, my FPS droped substantially.  It wouldn\'t matter what map I was on, some parts of the map would give me choppy FPS.  Smoke grenades would render my FPS to unplayable levels.  I would get major slowdowns whenever there were more then 5 people on screen or intense firefights.  In some circumstances and on certain levels, my FPS would drop so low, it would make the game simply unplayable and I would close Counter-Strike.  Here is what I have tried to remedy my FPS problem:\n\n\n\nSwitched to a variety of resolution and color depth combinations\n\nTurned V-SYNC off\n\nTurned AA off\n\nTweaked my video card settings in Windows\n\nTweaked my BIOS settings\n\nMASSIVE TWEAKING IN THE CS CONSOLE WITH EVERY COMMAND\n\n\n\nAfter all these changes and tweaking, I got a very MINIMAL FPS increase, nothing substantial enough to warrant a "fix" or "remedy".\n\n\n\nAs of now, I do not know if the FPS issue in CS 1.6 is isolated or widespread but, I can tell you this.  I spent most of the day yesterday and today researching this topic on the internet, I have visited numerous CS sites and entered there forums.  What I found was consistent, in every forum there was at least ONE AT THE VERY MINIMUM topic about FPS drops in 1.6.  This leaves me to believe that this problem is affecting more people then most think.  Now I know that my computer is on the lower end of the PC gaming spectrum, but I also know from reading forums and player responses in Counter-Strike, that people with much more powerful computers and video cards are experiencing FPS drops as well, sometimes severe.  After careful thinking, I think I have come to a conclusion:\n\n\n\nThe graphical updates (textures and models) that were implemented into the CS 1.6 engine are UNOPTIMIZED.\n\n\n\nI understand that VALVe is a very busy company, with the release of STEAM and CS 1.6 along with the development of Half-Life 2, they must have there hands tied.  That is my most logical explanation as to why they did not have the time nor resources to fully optimize the CS engine.  Hopfully this thread will get the attention of somebody in association with VALVe software, so they can come up with a possible fix in the near future.  Here is what I want the people who care to do.  If you are experiencing and FPS issues with CS 1.6, please list the following specifications and FPS problems you have:\n\n\n\nCPU\n\nRAM\n\nVIDEO CARD\n\nWINDOWS VERSION\n\nDIRECT X\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS\n\nVIDEO METHOD\n\nGAME RESOLUTION\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH\n\nV-SYNC\n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION\n\n\n\nLike I mentioned in the beginning of the thread, there have been other posts started about this topic but, they were inconsistent or did not display the full information needed to correctly diagnose this problem.  I think with enough participation in this thread, we can get the attention of somebody associated with VALVe and hopfully get this issue solved.  Thank you guys for taking the time to read through this horribly long post, I just felt I needed to be specific.  Thanks again!\n\n\n\nSIDE NOTE TO EVERYONE WHO SAY THEY HAVE NO FPS DROPS\n\nPURE SPECULATION\n\n\n\nUsually when I see someone post on a FPS topic saying they have no FPS drops AT ALL, they were not specific enough.  This leaves me to believe:\n\n\n\n1)  They cannot distinguish good FPS from bad FPS\n\n2)  Their FPS counter is reading wrong\n\n3)  There staring at a wall or playing by themselves\n\n4)  They don\'t know the difference between LAG and FPS\n\n5)  They are running the game at a horribly low resolution/color\n\n6)  They have a supercomputer (lol)\n\n7)  They have the luck of the Irish (lol)\n\n8)  They are lieing (lmao)\n\n\n\nLike I said above, pure speculation.  If my side note offends anybody, I am sorry, it was pure speculation.  Anyways, thanks again!  Let\'s get this issue solved!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131927, 20407, 1005, 102061, 1072936800, '', 'i uninstalled every ATI driver and program completely, then installed the old catalyst 3.5 drivers and cs runs better for me.\n\n\n\nabit-kd7\n\namd xp 2000+ \n\nradeon 9700 pro\n\nwinxp pro sp1', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131982, 20407, 1005, 102062, 1072936800, '', 'amd 2200\n\n1gb ddr ram\n\n256 mb ddr Gforce 4 graphic card\n\n2mb internet connection\n\nXP pro\n\nDirect X 9.0b \n\nnVidia 45.23 Reference Drivers \n\nOpenGL \n\n1024x768 \n\n32-bit \n\n\n\nFPS: 99-100 no lagg only on servers in usa (im in europe) []\n\n\n\nonly had less than 99 once (75 FPS) but that was due to server restrictions.\n\n\n\nRgds\n\n49th', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132044, 20407, 1005, 102063, 1072936800, '', 'CPU athlon xp 1800\n\nram 256 megs ddram\n\nvideo card ati radeon 7200 64 meg agp\n\nwindows 2000 \n\ndirect x 9.0b\n\nvideo driver ati2dvag.dll\n\nmethod opengl\n\ngame res 1024/768\n\ninternet connection dsl\n\n\n\nI dont always have bad fps but inferno, chateau and airstrip are bad in some places (drops to 5). fps is almost never as good as it used to be (100)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132053, 20407, 1005, 102064, 1072936800, '', 'First off - I know you asked us to post specs if we are having issues, but I thought I would post mine as well in case it helps. I\'m not having issues.\n\n\n\nIt\'s important to know the difference (For anyone who may post to this thread) between network lag, causing choppiness and video/CPU lag causing FPS to drop. So be sure to report the actual FPS, and not just that it\'s just choppy. (To see the FPS, pull up the console in game and type net_graph 3. To turn it off, type net_graph 0 in console) My specs:\n\n\n\nCPU                           Intel Celeron 1.8Ghz\n\nRAM                           512MB PC2100 DDR RAM\n\nVIDEO CARD              MSI GeForce 4 TI4200 64MB\n\nWINDOWS VERSION  Windows XP Home - Updated with latest downloads from windowsupdate\n\nDIRECT X                    9.0\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS          Not sure of the version offhand. Downloaded the latest one 2 days ago from NVIDIA\n\nVIDEO METHOD          OpenGL\n\nGAME RESOLUTION    Desktop at 1024*768, game looks like it is running in 800*600 ever since steam started - haven\'t tried increasing\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH  Whatever steam set it to, unchanged since updating to steam\n\nV-SYNC                      Whatever is default\n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES   None\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION  High speed DSL (130k/s downstream and 13k/s upstream max)\n\nMOTHER BOARD         ASUS P4B533-VM (I\'m using the on board sound)\n\nFPS                            Constant 60FPS, even in smoke (I have not made the change that allows it to go above 60FPS)\n\n\n\nFirebreak\n\n\n\nP.S. My game does get choppy from time to time, but when this happens I notice my ping has jumped up. My FPS is still high and everything is smooth except other players jump around the screen like they are teleporting. (Common symptom of network lag) I have noticed that pings seem to be a bit higher since 1.6, but nothing too major.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132184, 20407, 1005, 102065, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve noticed FPS drops in my games too.  Nothing so drastic as to make it unplayable.  It only happens when there are several people on the screen or there\'s ANY smoke grenades at all.  Here\'s my specs:\n\n\n\nCPU:  P4 2.6 GhZ\n\nRAM:  512 MB RAM\n\nVIDEO CARD: ATI Radeon 9800 Pro (slightly overclocked)\n\nWINDOWS VERSION:  Windows XP Pro\n\nDIRECT X: 9.0b\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS:  Latest Catalyst Drivers.  3.7 I believe. \n\nVIDEO METHOD:  OpenGL \n\nGAME RESOLUTION:  1024x768\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH: 32 BIT\n\nV-SYNC: Off \n\nINTERNET CONNECTION: Cable\n\n\n\nWhen I first started tweaking my video card I ran a little test.  I was in de_aztec in a single player game and so long as I was staring at a wall my fps stayed at a constant 150.  When I moved it dropped slightly and went back up.  There was a spot at the bridge bomb site where it dropped significantly.  I threw a smoke outside of the bridge room and my FPS dropped to 75.  Almost a 80 fps drop.  I haven\'t been playing long enough to really notice but that\'s awfully huge.  I have several screenshots where my fps was at 150 I walk into a smoke and it drops to 65-80.  \n\n\n\nMy settings have changed slightly since then by the way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132239, 20407, 1005, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Interesting cspray.  Why a ATI Radeon 9800 PRO would drop as low as 65 FPS in single player puzzles me.  Don\'t get me wrong, 65 FPS is most certainly playable and smoke grenades due tend to drop performance quite a bit in most cases, but you would expect FPS results from a 9800 PRO to be higher with V-SYNC off.  If I\'m not mistaken, ATI Radeon 9800 PRO is the best consumer video card out there?  Anways, I appreciate your response, some questions though.  Do your FPS ever drop below 65?  Have you ever tried turning V-SYNC on?  If you have the time could you possibly post some results from a typical multiplayer game session?  It would be much appreciated.  Also, for the users who are not experiencing any FPS drops, I envy you (hehe).  Anways, thanks for your participation.  Hopfully if there are FPS issues (which I still think there is) in CS 1.6, someone at VALVe will see this post, maybe a fix is on the way!  Thanks guys!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132268, 20407, 1005, 102065, 1072936800, '', 'Sure.  I\'ll see if I can\'t get a couple demos going.  Maybe a screenshot or two with my current settings.  I\'ll also include my config in the zip file.  \n\n\n\nIt is weird that I\'m getting such drastic FPS drops with a high end video card.  I\'m thinking that part of it is my RAM.  Although I have about an average amount it definitely doesn\'t suit my system.  I\'m going to get some more just as soon as I can get some more money.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132341, 20407, 1005, 102066, 1072936800, '', 'AMD athlon XP barton 2800+\n\n1giga of DDR pc 2700\n\nGforce4 TI 4600 128\n\nNvidia detonator 51.75 (beta one)\n\nDirect X 9.b\n\nwin XP Pro Sp1\n\nVideo Mode: Open GL\n\ninternet connexion : cable 1024/256\n\n\n\nplaying at 800x600 at 100fps constant. (i play usually on 800 cause i like this better)\n\nor\n\nplaying at 1152 at 100fps constant.\n\nor\n\nplaying at 1280x1024 at 85fps constant. (screen doesn\'t support higher)\n\n\n\nand i play with vsynch ON and Nvrefreshtool. and i\'ve tried all those resolution 1 hour of each. with my clan on ou clan-server, and some of them have similar comments.\n\n\n\nand only fps drop when there\'s is like 5 smoke grenades on screen (100fps to 80-85fps) that doesn\'t happen a lot []\n\n\n\nquote:1) They cannot distinguish good FPS from bad FPS \n\n2) Their FPS counter is reading wrong \n\n3) There staring at a wall or playing by themselves \n\n4) They don\'t know the difference between LAG and FPS \n\n5) They are running the game at a horribly low resolution/color \n\n6) They have a supercomputer (lol) \n\n7) They have the luck of the Irish (lol) \n\n8) They are lieing (lmao) \n\n\n\n1) Nope\n\n2) Nope either\n\n3) lol funny one []\n\n4) I do know the difference\n\n5) Nope\n\n6) Maybe [] HL is a 4 year old game so no supercomputer is needed but i guess if i don\'t drop fps then it is a super !\n\n7) Hum... no comment...\n\n8) Why lying about this :S if the game would run bad i would be the first to flame. but it isn\'t\n\n\n\nguess i could make a list for people who get fps drops but i would not make speculations like you do [] Why people who say that they have no fps drops lie?\n\n\n\nPeople have fps drops, some don\'t, then people should see how they run their computer and customize it or what grafik cards they have. Mine is well installed and runs smoothly and CS either []\n\n\n\nSome people just mess too bad with their Windows that it is a really big mess :S', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132393, 20407, 1005, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for your post Fantomas666.  Yes, you do seem to be running CS flawlessly.  One thing that caught my eye were the beta drivers you were running.  Maybe super optimized?  I have a question too, what color depth are you running CS at?  Also, are you playing CS 1.5 or CS 1.6 (lol j/k).  Anyways, I envy your FPS, I wish I got those kind of FPS at those resolutions.  Anyways thanks for your response, I appreciate it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132503, 20407, 1005, 102067, 1072936800, '', 'AMD athlon xp 2200 (1.67gh)\n\n512 ddr ram\n\ngeforce4ti 4400 128\n\nNvidia 45.23 geforce drivers\n\nDirect x 8.1 I think\n\nWin xp pro w/sp1\n\nOpen GL : 1024x768, highest colour depth, and my card\'s graphics settings are maxed\n\noh and vsync on\n\n\n\nNow, obviously I had absolutely no problem in 1.5, even if there were 6 smoke grenades on screen (I have all ingame cs graphics settings maxed too, meaning best looking smoke)\n\n\n\nNow in 1.6, I come within 25 feet of a smoke grenade and my fps drops to 10!!!! Since when is a system like mine not enough to play a halflife 1 mod to its fullest capabilites! This really annoys me and I dont feel I should have to turn down my graphics settings to play counter-strike. I mean.....its counter-strike! We are not talking battlefield 1942 here.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132605, 20407, 1005, 102066, 1072936800, '', 'Your welcome []\n\n\n\nhum i guess those detonator are super optimised, but i really don\'t know. They are the next detonator release, but there\'s no realese date at this time. But it might come from those beta [] Some people i know ran some benchmark and it saiud that they was a gain of quality (uh hope it does make sense, exscuse my bad english, but i\'m french []).\n\n\n\nand i play at highest colour depth (32 bits).\n\n\n\nand i play at CS 1.6 (lol) [] []\n\n\n\nteamcs | rasta: You hsould try to update tyour direct X 8.1 is not the new one. May solve the problems or may not [] give it a try []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132630, 20407, 1005, 102068, 1072936800, '', 'CPU 1703 mhz pentium 4\n\nRAM 512 mb SDRAM\n\nVIDEO CARD geforce 4 ti4200\n\nWINDOWS VERSION XP pro sp1 (woops)\n\nDIRECT X 9\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS 45.23 \n\nVIDEO METHOD openGL\n\nGAME RESOLUTION 640x480\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH 16\n\nV-SYNC OFF\n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES Refreshlock\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION cable <512\n\n\n\n100 fps in 1.5\n\n30-60 fps in 1.6\n\nSmoke isn\'t thick, can see though it. No extra drops on smoke.\n\nProbebly need to buy a "better" pc. \n\n\n\n(better in xtreme good.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132641, 20407, 1005, 102066, 1072936800, '', 'Hu? where did you get SP2 for win XP, it\'s not out yet :S ? or if it is then where? []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132688, 20407, 1005, 100606, 1072936800, '', 'CPU: 1455 mhz AthlonXP 1600+\n\nRAM: 512MB SDRam\n\nVideo Card: GeForce4 Ti4200 (128MB)\n\nWindows Version: XP Pro\n\nDirectX 9.0b\n\nVideo Drivers: 45.23\n\nVideo Method: OpenGL\n\nGame Resolution: 800x600\n\nGame Color Depth: 16-bit\n\nV-Sync: OFF\n\nAdditional Features: NVRefreshFix\n\nInternet Connection: Cable (can download @ speeds up to 500KB/sec)\n\n\n\n100 fps in 1.5 all the time, no exceptions,\n\ndown to 30 fps quite often in 1.6.\n\n\n\nI have also tried using Team zEx\'s 1.6 fps guide to no help, along with dumming down my settings to nothing, I still get a massive fps drop. If I\'m standing, in a single player game, in the T spawn on Aztec, my fps is 50 there, not moving or doing anything. One thing I have noticed is that my fps always goes to its lowest when I move my view left or right. Also, I have smokes on lowest quality. 2 smokes takes my fps below 10 fps.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131916, 20421, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, 'CS 1.6 and FPS', 'Hello. I am starting this thread to shed some light on the FPS issues regarding CS 1.6 once and for all. This post may seem redundant to some users but, all the other FPS threads that I\'ve seen were either inconsistent or simply "lost in the shuffle". Let me get started with my computer setup and problems: \n\n\n\nCPU: 866 Mhz Pentium III \n\nRAM: 256 MB PC-133 SDRAM \n\nVIDEO CARD: geForce 2 Ultra \n\nWINDOWS VERSION: Windows 98 SE \n\nDIRECT X: Direct X 9.0b \n\nVIDEO DRIVERS: nVidia 45.23 Reference Drivers \n\nVIDEO METHOD: OpenGL \n\nGAME RESOLUTION: 1024x768 \n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH: 32-bit \n\nV-SYNC: ON \n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES: 4xAA \n\nINTERNET CONNECTION: Cable \n\n\n\nIn CS 1.5, I got max FPS no matter what. My computer NEVER slowed down except when there were a large number of smoke grenades on screen. It was smooth, enjoyable gaming all the way. After installation of CS 1.6, my FPS droped substantially. It wouldn\'t matter what map I was on, some parts of the map would give me choppy FPS. Smoke grenades would render my FPS to unplayable levels. I would get major slowdowns whenever there were more then 5 people on screen or intense firefights. In some circumstances and on certain levels, my FPS would drop so low, it would make the game simply unplayable and I would close Counter-Strike. Here is what I have tried to remedy my FPS problem: \n\n\n\nSwitched to a variety of resolution and color depth combinations \n\nTurned V-SYNC off \n\nTurned AA off \n\nTweaked my video card settings in Windows \n\nTweaked my BIOS settings \n\nMASSIVE TWEAKING IN THE CS CONSOLE WITH EVERY COMMAND \n\n\n\nAfter all these changes and tweaking, I got a very MINIMAL FPS increase, nothing substantial enough to warrant a "fix" or "remedy". \n\n\n\nAs of now, I do not know if the FPS issue in CS 1.6 is isolated or widespread but, I can tell you this. I spent most of the day yesterday and today researching this topic on the internet, I have visited numerous CS sites and entered there forums. What I found was consistent, in every forum there was at least ONE AT THE VERY MINIMUM topic about FPS drops in 1.6. This leaves me to believe that this problem is affecting more people then most think. Now I know that my computer is on the lower end of the PC gaming spectrum, but I also know from reading forums and player responses in Counter-Strike, that people with much more powerful computers and video cards are experiencing FPS drops as well, sometimes severe. After careful thinking, I think I have come to a conclusion: \n\n\n\nThe graphical updates (textures and models) that were implemented into the CS 1.6 engine are UNOPTIMIZED. \n\n\n\nI understand that VALVe is a very busy company, with the release of STEAM and CS 1.6 along with the development of Half-Life 2, they must have there hands tied. That is my most logical explanation as to why they did not have the time nor resources to fully optimize the CS engine. Hopfully this thread will get the attention of somebody in association with VALVe software, so they can come up with a possible fix in the near future. Here is what I want the people who care to do. If you are experiencing and FPS issues with CS 1.6, please list the following specifications and FPS problems you have: \n\n\n\nCPU \n\nRAM \n\nVIDEO CARD \n\nWINDOWS VERSION \n\nDIRECT X \n\nVIDEO DRIVERS \n\nVIDEO METHOD \n\nGAME RESOLUTION \n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH \n\nV-SYNC \n\nADDITIONAL FEATURES \n\nINTERNET CONNECTION \n\n\n\nLike I mentioned in the beginning of the thread, there have been other posts started about this topic but, they were inconsistent or did not display the full information needed to correctly diagnose this problem. I think with enough participation in this thread, we can get the attention of somebody associated with VALVe and hopfully get this issue solved. Thank you guys for taking the time to read through this horribly long post, I just felt I needed to be specific. Thanks again! \n\n\n\nSIDE NOTE TO EVERYONE WHO SAY THEY HAVE NO FPS DROPS \n\nPURE SPECULATION \n\n\n\nUsually when I see someone post on a FPS topic saying they have no FPS drops AT ALL, they were not specific enough. This leaves me to believe: \n\n\n\n1) They cannot distinguish good FPS from bad FPS \n\n2) Their FPS counter is reading wrong \n\n3) There staring at a wall or playing by themselves \n\n4) They don\'t know the difference between LAG and FPS \n\n5) They are running the game at a horribly low resolution/color \n\n6) They have a supercomputer (lol) \n\n7) They have the luck of the Irish (lol) \n\n8) They are lieing (lmao) \n\n\n\nLike I said above, pure speculation. If my side note offends anybody, I am sorry, it was pure speculation. Anyways, thanks again! Let\'s get this issue solved!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(131949, 20421, 1013, 102069, 1072936800, '', 'DIRECT X  9.0b.\n\nVIDEO METHOD 4x antialising, 8x antistropic, sharp textures on.\n\nGAME RESOLUTION 1024*768.\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH 32bit.\n\nV-SYNC off.\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION 56k.\n\n\n\nrest info in my sig...\n\n\n\n\n\nyes i notice a fps drop in 1.6 too its quite alot when smoke nades go off it reminds me of my old voodoo 3 3000 card fps and i have a friggin gf4 ti 4200 128meg bla bla bla other comp info well above cs standards.\n\n\n\nin 1.5 fps were at 99 fps solid 80 per cent time and would drop to maybe 65ish with smoke nades but generaly stayed at 80-99 fps solid.\n\n\n\n1.6 i notice fps drop in heavy fire fights didnt happen in 1.5, also smoke nade drop fps like to 15 fps ???? like wtf considering my spec and didnt happen in 1.5.\n\n\n\nalso i seen fps drop to 65ish just running around map for no reason???? with 5 ppl on screen didnt happen in 1.5 either.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132007, 20421, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', '^Liquid Dreams^ I feel your pain man.  My computer is certainly not up to par with your machine but, I never so much as got ANY FPS drops in CS 1.5, only with a lot of smoke.  I know that CS 1.6 got a face lift in the graphics department, but certainly not enough to warrant this kind of performance on recent hardware.  I am almost certain that this FPS issue can be solved with a little optimization.  Thank you for your participation.  Hopfully this thread will get the attention of someone at VALVe, so they can finally address this issue with a fix and we can all put this to rest.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132344, 20421, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Also ^Liquid Dreams^, have you tried turning V-SYNC on?  If so, what were your FPS like then?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132364, 20421, 1013, 102070, 1072936800, '', 'It also happens to all steam games including 3rd party mods ... not just CS.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132381, 20421, 1013, 102071, 1072936800, '', 'CPU :  AMD Athlon XP 1900+ (1.61. Gigz)\n\nRAM : 768 DDR Ram\n\nVIDEO CARD : GF3 Ti 500\n\nWINDOWS VERSION : Windows XP HE\n\nDIRECT X : 9.0\n\nVIDEO DRIVERS : 45.23\n\nVIDEO METHOD : OpenGL\n\nGAME RESOLUTION : 800X600\n\nGAME COLOR DEPTH : 32-bit\n\nV-SYNC : Off\n\nINTERNET CONNECTION : Cable\n\n\n\nI have also noticed that on cirtain maps my FPS drops from 99 to anywhere around 40ish.  40 fps doesn\'t sound so bad, but when its dropping from 99 to 40, re-coil, rate of fire ... everything is effected.  I\'ve noticed that when my fps nears 40, when trying to go full-auto, its almost as if my gun jams, and I fire really slow.  \n\n\n\nI have noticed, that after a little work on my computer, I\'ve been able to increase my fps, and been able to play a little bit better.  After cleaning up my disk and defrangmenting I was able to get my fps to hold 99 on most maps.\n\n\n\nThey really need to fix this problem, because I know a lot of people that can\'t play CS anymore, because it is un-playable.  I hope they do something, cause not everyone out there is able to afford a top of the line comp.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132508, 20421, 1013, 102069, 1072936800, '', 'yes i turn vsync to always off.\n\n\n\nand ive updated my sig []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132748, 20421, 1013, 102072, 1072936800, '', 'ohh i thought somethin was wrong with my comp but i see other people have the same drop in fps as me.\n\n\n\nCPU: P4 1.8A Ghz@ 2.2Ghz\n\nRAM: 768 PC2700\n\nVID CARD: ASUS GF4 Ti 4200, latest Drivers\n\nOS: Win XP Home SP1, DX 9.0b\n\n\n\n1024*768 @ 32bit\n\nVSYNC off, 4x AA. 8x AF\n\n1.5mb DSL\n\n\n\nWhen i played 1.5, my FPS would be 99/100 with no drop.  Now in 1.6 it will only reach max when i am in a small room and alone.  Average now is about 60-80, with a huge loss from smoke gren (down to 20-40).  Maps where you can see a pretty far distance, ie: dust2 (long A) , aztec (water) , also make my fps drop a substantial amout.  I like quality over performance so i guess i will have to live with it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132866, 20421, 1013, 102073, 1072936800, '', 'all the problems will be fixed', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132995, 20421, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'I agree yamiblaster01.  Sooner or later this issue will be addressed by VALVe, hopfully with a fix in the near future.  Thank you guys for participating, I appreciate it.  Also, if anybody else is reading this thread and is experiencing FPS drops after installing CS 1.6, I encourage you to post.  Thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133021, 20421, 1013, 100768, 1072936800, '', 'I sympathise with all of you, i am in your situation.  Something i have found...I can only get a constant 59 fps when topped fps_max and fps_modem at 60 fps, now I am not stupid I know if I top the fps\'s at 60 I will only reach 59, however when topping at 100 it still only fluctuates at 59-60 so might as well top it at 60 and get the constant 59 right?  Also its not just fps_max u should change but fps_modem as well, it does make a difference.\n\n\n\nI can go over 60 and get 99 fps but thats in d3d, not opengl.  d3d brings a new problem...EXTREME frame and imput lag, letters show up lagged when im typing, movement is slow to register as well as everything else.  NOT mentioning how horrible fonts look in d3d, almost unreadable.  If anyone knows how to fix the imput lag suggestions would be much appreciated.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133043, 20421, 1013, 101350, 1072936800, '', 'Well shouldn\'t i just love you guys lol......if steam would work for me id praise allah or sumthin lol.......its being a mofo for me....\n\n\n\nI hate it soooo bad', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133051, 20421, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'g0d, I would not recommend using CS with Direct3D, for the Half-Life engine was designed with OpenGL in mind, Direct3D is simply just supported.  I hope this helps to answer your question and I would be happy to elaborate.  Thank you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133079, 20421, 1013, 102074, 1072936800, '', 'I have noticed something that I hadn\'t thought about before. The frame rate problem only happens with Nvidia cards. I could be wrong but it seems that everybody here is having that problem with a Nvidia board. \n\n\n\nI am not having any problems with CS 1.6 running at 1280X1024 in 32bit color with 6X AA, 16X AF, and everything set on high quality.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133256, 20421, 1013, 102075, 1072936800, '', 'P4 3.0C\n\nFX5800\n\n\n\nCS RES @ 800X600 32bit OpenGL\n\nV\'sync ON, AA/AF ON\n\nfps range from 400-350\n\n[]Attachment: ownage.jpg (attachment.php?s=316b3574b3c99382e4cd2a8d23459d56&postid=133256)\n\nThis has been downloaded 382 time(s).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(132997, 20595, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'Creating New Accounts "fixall"', 'Hey everyone,\n\n\n\nJust a quick note about trying to create a new account when you are having problems with Steam.\n\n\n\nCreating a new account is only something to try if maybe you\'ve never been able to login (ever), and suspect it\'s because something happened during your account creation. Though, if this is the case, you can email us and we\'ll try to get your account straightened out.\n\n\n\nIf you\'ve already entered one or more CD-Keys in the first account, you will not be able to re-use them in the new account.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(133981, 20760, 1013, 102081, 1072936800, 'SteamAMP', 'Hi.\n\n\n\nJust thought I\'d share with the steam community my latest little utility. It\'s called SteamAMP and it managed your MP3\'s while playing Steam enabled MODS.\n\nI developed this method after reading about the mp3 commands in the forums, and i didn\'t know there was no such util, other wise you guys would have had it a bit more than a week ago =D\n\nAs far as I know, this is an original concept, thought up by myself. Please enjoy.\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease send bugs, typos, feedback and critisism to: brok3n@iinet.net.au (mailto:brok3n@iinet.net.au). It\'s all appreciated.\n\n\n\nAlso, I am not sure if the userconfig.cfg works on startup, I did not have time to test that. Next release will have that worked out? Anyways, please ensure that you have the following keys bound:\n\n\n\nbind f6 "wait; wait; wait; wait; exec mp3command.cfg;"\n\nbind f7 "wait; wait; wait; wait; exec mp3command.cfg;"\n\nbind f8 "wait; wait; wait; wait; exec mp3command.cfg;"\n\n\n\nFor help, just click the \'?\' in the app.\n\n\n\n\n\nBrok3n.\n\n\n\nSteamAMP V1.0 Download:\n\nhttp://ii.net/~lynch1/steamamp/steamamp.zip (http://ii.net/~lynch1/steamamp/steamamp.zip)\n\n\n\nVB Runtime Files:\n\nhttp://ii.net/~lynch1/steamamp/vbruntimes.zip (http://ii.net/~lynch1/steamamp/vbruntimes.zip)\n\n\n\nI\'ll update this.... Someday.... :|', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(134311, 20760, 1013, 102082, 1072936800, '', 'You sure VAC won\'t detect it as a cheat? []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(135081, 20760, 1013, 102081, 1072936800, 'Good Point', 'Good Point, but I don\'t think VAC will\n\n1) Detect it/\n\n2) Detect it as a cheat.\n\n\n\nIt may be that cheats like that nasty anti-recoil thing that sits outside of HL and just moves the mouse down will couse this to be detected aswell. I doubt it tho =D (Hope not anyways).\n\n\n\nThanksfor pointing that out =D\n\n\n\nWhat this util does is, from the mod directory you specify, get the /mp3 directory (that you create, and put mp3\'s in), list the fiels there, and whever you press one of the control keys(F6=Stop, F7 = Prev, F8=Next) write a script file with the mp3 command and the path of the mp3, so that you do not have to make clumsy (no offense) aand time cinsuming commandmenu.txt\'s or other scripts.\n\n\n\nBut please, download it and try it. It works =D\n\nAnd please post or email me some Feedback!\n\n\n\n\n\nBrok3n.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166508, 20760, 1013, 101513, 1072936800, '', 'just thought i might bump this so anyone that is still wondering can see it. [] (its a nice little tool, props to brok3n [] )', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166526, 20760, 1013, 102083, 1072936800, '', 'It uses the build in commands for playing MP3\'s? If it would use winamp to play them and a script to contol it you will get VAC-banned.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166582, 20760, 1013, 102084, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Mr. Chris \n\nYou sure VAC won\'t detect it as a cheat? [] \n\nHeh, VAC doesn\'t detect cheats as a cheat.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166629, 20760, 1013, 102085, 1072936800, '', 'Couldn\'t exec mp3command.cfg...\n\n\n\nDid I miss something?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166714, 20760, 1013, 102081, 1072936800, 'Thankyou!', 'ok. \n\n\n\nThanks for the feadback!\n\n\n\nZell: \n\nThanks dude, i appreciate it... \n\n\n\nMad Maniak:\n\nSteamaMP uses the Steam built in MP3 console command. Really, it has no interaction wiht the game itself or anyting in memory. It just writes a .cfg file. [] \n\nI suppose Steam*AMP* was a bit misleading... I needed sometihng that immediately associated it with playing music.\n\n\n\nCircuitous: \n\nMake sure you give it the correct directory. Thats would be echoed to you becuase it canno find the file (\'mp3command.cfg\'). Likely scenario is it is outputting to the wrong directory. On first run, the path defaults to the steam Half-Life dir. You\'ll no doubt hve to change this.\n\n\n\nThanks again, I hope you find SteamAMP useful.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166745, 20760, 1013, 102085, 1072936800, '', 'I was in the right directory.\n\n\n\nAt any rate, it works for CS now, and so I guess that\'s good enough.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167269, 20760, 1013, 102086, 1072936800, '', 'Very nice - I like it.\n\n\n\nYou got a memory leak somewhere when you close the proggy with the X, so make sure you unload everything properly. Other than that, works fine for me.\n\n\n\nI\'d keep working on this as it has the potential to turn into a real nice utility when it\'s all squeaky clean. Also, with the F6 mp3 stop command, there is no need really to have that generate the config file. Obviously for playing an mp3 it is needed, but for stopping it you could just add that directly to the userconfig.cfg and get rid of it having to write to the mp3commands.cfg file.\n\n\n\nThose are my suggestions, which isn\'t much at all really. Good work mate.\n\n\n\nEDIT: Oh, and add in support for turning up and down the \'MP3Volume\' command and the \'VOLUME\' command, including buttons to auto mute either one. Like F5 to mute in game sound, and F4 to mute MP3 sound etc. That\'d be pretty dudey!\n\n\n\nFor example, you could use:\n\n\n\n----------------------------\n\n\n\nalias +mp3VolumeChanger "bind F1 MP3Volume 0.1; bind F2 MP3Volume 0.2; bind F3 MP3Volume 0.3; bind F4 MP3Volume 0.4; bind F5 MP3Volume 0.5; bind F6 MP3Volume 0.6; bind F7 MP3Volume 0.7; bind F8 MP3Volume 0.8; bind F9 MP3Volume 0.9; bind F10 MP3Volume 1; bind F11 MP3Volume 0"\n\n\n\nalias -mp3VolumeChanger "<rebind all keys to normal settings etc>"\n\n\n\nalias +VolumeChanger "bind F1 Volume 0.1; bind F2 Volume 0.2; bind F3 Volume 0.3; bind F4 Volume 0.4; bind F5 Volume 0.5; bind F6 Volume 0.6; bind F7 Volume 0.7; bind F8 Volume 0.8; bind F9 Volume 0.9; bind F10 Volume 1; bind F12 Volume 0"\n\n\n\nalias -VolumeChanger "<rebind all keys to normal settings etc>"\n\n\n\nbind F12 +mp3VolumeChanger\n\nbind F11 +VolumeChanger\n\n\n\n-------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nWith that, you\'d hold down F12 and then press F1 to set MP3Volume to 0.1, or F2 to set it to 0.2 ect up until F10 with sets it to 1.0. If you press F11 it mutes it by setting to 0.\n\nLetting go of the key rebinds F1 to F10 with their normal commands.\n\n\n\nF11 does the same with Volume settings, and F12 this time will mute it.\n\n\n\nI havn\'t tested this script but you get the drift. I\'ll shutup now because I\'m rambling on.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167698, 20760, 1013, 101513, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, (still using it ^_^ ) but maybe when they release the steamSDK you could make a prog with mp3 stop, play, skip track, foward track, volume up and down with the wheel on a mouse, etc. []  \n\n\n\nBut anyway - keep it up dude, this is a great utility. Up untill i found this I coudn\'t play mp3s. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168354, 20760, 1013, 102087, 1072936800, '', 'i cant get it to work...do i need to dl both files..do i need to unzip to a certain foler?..i unzip to my documents..n i have the mp3 path all set up but ..i even c my playlist but i cant get it to work..when ever im in game it saids couldnt exec mp3config.exec or something close to dat when i press f8 f7 f6...pls some one help step by step thank u in advance..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(169115, 20760, 1013, 102088, 1072936800, '', 'I too seem to have done everything correct and have no results.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(169287, 20760, 1013, 102085, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve noticed a few issues with SteamAMP.\n\n\n\nBut before I get to those, I think I can offer a bit of help to other users.\n\n\n\nFirst: To my knowledge, SteamAMP doesn\'t work in DoD (anyone gotten it to work there?).\n\n\n\nSecond: Make sure that "Monitor Keys" is ON before playing. This is what causes SteamAMP to write the mp3command.cfg and is the driving force behind the thing.\n\n\n\nThird: Songs do not automatically play, so when one finishes you have to hit F8 to load the next.\n\n\n\nFourth: Songs do not play right off the bat, so you\'ll have to use F8 to get them started.\n\n\n\nFifth: Use "MP3 Volume" in Audio Options to mess with the volume.\n\n\n\nNow those issues I mentioned:\n\n- I can\'t minimize SteamAMP, and I\'d kinda like to. Is there a reason behind this?\n\n- Doesn\'t work in DoD (mentioned earlier).\n\n\n\nAnd some suggestions:\n\n- Allow different keys to be used (user-defined).\n\n- Allow user to select multiple folders, and write new mp3command.cfg into all of them, so that the user doesn\'t have to select a new folder before changing games.\n\n\n\nThanks for your time. Congrats on the Sticky.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
