(138902, 21578, 1013, 102100, 1072936800, 'NAT / LAN / Dedicated Server - Invalid Steam Userid Ticket - Read This!', 'Some of you have had this problem and none of the solutions have worked for you.  I\'m going to tell you why:\n\n\n\nSteam has a rather shortsighted design approach to authentication.  It tries to tie your authentication to your IP address.  When your client PC is using NAT and has direct private access to the HLDS via LAN, you wil NOT be able to connect to your server.\n\n\n\nLook at the console of your HLDS.  When you try to connect, you will see that you\'re connecting to the server using your private IP address, not your public NAT IP address.  Your authentication is tied to your public IP address because you had to connect to Valve before you were able to play.  When the HLDS compares your authenticated IP to the IP you connected with, they DO NOT MATCH and you get kicked off.\n\n\n\nI have yet to come up with a technical workaround.  The only way to overcome it is to find a way to force NAT to translate the private IP before it gets to the HLDS.\n\n\n\nThis is a stupid stupid stupid stupid stupid approach to authentication.  They could have simply created a token that is generated using the public IP address of the client and the client Steamid.  This token could be passed to the client and requested by the server when the client connects for authentication.  Unless this type of scheme is used, many LAN players are going to be screwed so long as they have direct LAN access to the server on a private IP.\n\n\n\nIn the meantime, go back to 1.5.  As it stands, you will not be able to connect to your 1.6 servers if you are using the same approach to networking that I am.\n\n\n\n\n\nDean Connell', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(138971, 21578, 1013, 102022, 1072936800, '', '/bumpage \n\n\n\nsame problem here. You reading this valve?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139000, 21578, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'Yes. The problem isn\'t quite that simple [] , and we\'re aware of the issue and working on it. Thanks,\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139001, 21578, 1013, 102101, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, could that also be why I get the same connection-error?\n\n\n\nI have access to 2 different gateways (standard gateway is the shared building connection, and the alternative is a private ADSL inwhich me and a fellow routes the IP\'s to CS-gameservers). The error shows when I try to route certain IP\'s through the ADSL, and still have standard gateway set to the building-gateway. Whenever I change my settings to only use a single gateway (building or ADSL), everything works fine.\n\n\n\nThis is really bugging me .. but your explanation seems to make sense for me. Can anyone confirm/disprove this?\n\n\n\nedit: A quick sidenote; I have tried to route every IP related to Steam I could find, to \'trick\' it into authenticate me but it didn\'t work (could have been wrong IP\'s - could have been the wrong  approach).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139007, 21578, 1013, 102022, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by RP^ \n\nHey, could that also be why I get the same connection-error?\n\n\n\nI have access to 2 different gateways (standard gateway is the shared building connection, and the alternative is a private ADSL inwhich me and a fellow routes the IP\'s to CS-gameservers). The error shows when I try to route certain IP\'s through the ADSL, and still have standard gateway set to the building-gateway. Whenever I change my settings to only use a single gateway (building or ADSL), everything works fine.\n\n\n\nThis is really bugging me .. but your explanation seems to make sense for me. Can anyone confirm/disprove this?  \n\n\n\nYa that\'s actually closer to my problem I have 2 gateways 1 my CS server uses and the other one I use for my client computers. If I try and connect to my dedicated server I get the invalid ticket err but I can connect to any server outside my network', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139008, 21578, 1013, 102100, 1072936800, '', 'You can prove it yourself by having an admin tell you what it says your IP is.  It\'s possible there\'s a conflict between the IP Valve sees and the IP the server sees.  Just have them type status at the console.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139011, 21578, 1013, 102022, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Taylor Sherman \n\nYes. The problem isn\'t quite that simple [] , and we\'re aware of the issue and working on it. Thanks,\n\n\n\nTaylor  \n\n\n\nThank you for the reply.  Is there any timeline in which this is gonna be fixed?  hours, days, weeks, months, never?  It\'s really frustrating because I can\'t really admin my server until it is fixed', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139015, 21578, 1013, 102100, 1072936800, '', 'I can connect to any server but my own as well.  My server has a public IP on a FreeBSD server.  The FreeBSD server also runs my NAT.  I have a private LAN segment that gets used when I try to connect to my dedicated server and that causes the HLDS to see the wrong IP when it tries to validate me with Steam.  Yay.\n\n\n\n\n\nDean', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139023, 21578, 1013, 102100, 1072936800, '', 'Taylor,\n\n\n\nI didn\'t mean to imply that your developers are stupid.  I\'ve made some awfully poor choices in my own career.  This particular authentication method paints one into a corner a little.  I hope you don\'t think I\'m attacking you guys personally.  Steam is a great idea, it just needs time to be fleshed out.\n\n\n\nI\'ll be really impressed if you figure out a way around this.  In the mean time, I\'m back to running a 1.5 server.  Keep plugging away, and don\'t let the complainers get you down.  I just wanted people to understand the real problem.\n\n\n\n\n\nDean', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(139028, 21578, 1013, 102022, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by PoisOnouS \n\nI can connect to any server but my own as well.  My server has a public IP on a FreeBSD server.  The FreeBSD server also runs my NAT.  I have a private LAN segment that gets used when I try to connect to my dedicated server and that causes the HLDS to see the wrong IP when it tries to validate me with Steam.  Yay.\n\n\n\n\n\nDean  \n\n\n\nFrustrating isn\'t it. I just wanna know when it is that it\'s gonna be fixed so I can stop lurking on these boards', '127.0.0.1', 1),
