(253827, 21578, 1013, 102103, 1072936800, '', 'Come on Valve! \n\n\nWe need an update solving the NAT problem NOW.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(254489, 21578, 1013, 102104, 1072936800, '', 'I spent $25 on Day of Defeat a few months ago for the sole purpose of running a Counter-Strike server on my fast T1 line and be able to play on my own server.  I use NAT and am a Computer Tech of 10 years, and a Game Server Admin of 5 years.  To my dissapointment Steam authentication doesnt work well with NAT.  So I thought to myself, surely Valve will fix such a serious problem ASAP, it will be worth it to wait a bit for Steam to be fixed.  That was 2 months ago!  When I started up my server, watching others be able to play on it, but not be able to play on my own server, lets just say I was upset.  Luckily a nice free game called Enemy Territory came out that I was able to run a server for and play on my own server.\n\n\n\n\n\nI am not joking when I say this ... I will not buy Half-Life 2.  By then many other great games like UT2004 and DOOM3 will be taking up my time.  The fact such a major networking standard has been overlooked and then not fixed in a timely manner says a lot about where Valve holds its priorities.  I was planning on being a server admin for Half-Life2, CounterStrike2, TeamFortress2, etc.  But this has put a very sour taste in my mouth.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn summary, I want my $25 back.  I have gotten no play time out of that game.\n\n__________________\n\nGame Server Admin\n\n\nmidwestmayhem.gotdns.com', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(254722, 21578, 1013, 102105, 1072936800, '', 'I think the problem is that you need one account for the server and one for the comp ur gonna play on.  I originally had this problem, but after i made a second account, it worked!  I can connect to my lan server over the lan!\n\n\n\n\n\nhope this helps\n\n\n\n\n\n[edit] server was on another comp [/edit]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(254770, 21578, 1013, 102106, 1072936800, 'hmmm', 'ok so this right here is why im getting the pop-up window connecting to a lan game saying Steam verification error ticket(1) right? i know MANY lan centers including mine have problem and have lost ALOT of business do to it. I know ur all really busy but please try and solve this. - Thank you\n\n__________________\n\n- IDLE #Atzone', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(254850, 21578, 1013, 102107, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by DBman190 \n\n\nI think the problem is that you need one account for the server and one for the comp ur gonna play on.  I originally had this problem, but after i made a second account, it worked!  I can connect to my lan server over the lan!\n\n\n\n\n\nhope this helps\n\n\n\n\n\n[edit] server was on another comp [/edit]  \n\n\n\n\n\nI could always connect to my server via the LAN, I just couldn\'t connect to it using the internet like I can with 1.5. I have the same account for both.\n\n\nI think I found out why my server doesn\'t show on the master list. I had to port my 1.6 server to :27016 as I have a 1.5 server running on port :27015. I feel like it\'s not showing on the master list because it\'s ported on :27016. If I access the LAN to connect, it then shows BOTH servers, 1.5 and 1.6.\n\n__________________\n\n-=Capt_Fuzzy=-\n\n\nSpace Cadet Extraordinaire\n\n\n\n\n\nCS 1.5 Server: 69.162.241.137:27016\n\n\nCS 1.5 SuperHero Mod Server: 69.162.241.137:27015', '127.0.0.1', 1),
