(156680, 22178, 1013, 102140, 1072936800, '', 'LOL this Valve\'s soap opera goes exactly like I was predicting []\n\n\n\nValve said to www.halflifesource.com (http://www.halflifesource.com) that only part of code was stolen and they are back at work to release HL2. They say few things that were leaked are need to be changed.\n\n\n\nMy crystall ball says: \n\nNext time you\'ll  hear that it was part of old code, based on HL1 or something similar, anyway leaked code is useless and has nothing common with current Source builds. They will say how much they are grateful to their community. Community will respond - we love you Valve as usual, here are our all money. \n\n\n\nTill today I haven\'t seen any working app (HL1, HL2, CS, TF2, Hammer 4.0) or map. Have you ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156683, 22178, 1013, 102045, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Craftos \n\nLOL this Valve\'s soap opera goes exactly like I was predicting []\n\n\n\nValve said to www.halflifesource.com (http://www.halflifesource.com) that only part of code was stolen and they are back at work to release HL2. They say few things that were leaked are need to be changed.\n\n\n\nMy crystall ball says: \n\nNext time you\'ll  hear that it was part of old code, based on HL1 or something similar, anyway leaked code is useless and has nothing common with current Source builds. They will say how much they are grateful to their community. Community will respond - we love you Valve as usual, here are our all money. \n\n\n\nTill today I haven\'t seen any working app (HL1, HL2, CS, TF2, Hammer 4.0) or map. Have you ?  I COULDN\'T HAVE POUNDED IT INTO THE IDIOT NAY-SAYERS WHO THINKS A FULL, WORKING COPY OF hl2 IS OUT ON THE NET SOMEWHERE BETTER.\n\n\n\nI salute you in a 100% ****sexual manner.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
