(160420, 22178, 1013, 101837, 1072936800, 'The same jerkoff who cracked into Valve Software\'s network has done a lot more damage', 'than initially estimated.  Apparently they stole enough material to create an alpha build of the game.\n\n\n\nNow that this stuff has spread from here to Russia, there\'s not much Valve Software/FBI can do about the spread of the source code not to mention the alpha build.\n\n\n\nIt appears they might have stolen Condition Zero along with the Halflife 2 stuff.\n\n\n\nThis is an unfortunate turn of events for Valve Software and everyone waiting for Halflife 2 to be finished properly.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
