(144939, 22552, 1013, 102147, 1072936800, 'What the Source leak means to Valve', 'well the thing really made me think is all GPL code included in Valves code... I dont think we would have ever know about valve using this completely free open source library if the source was not leaked.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(144940, 22552, 1013, 102084, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by s3v3n \n\nTHANK YOU CHEIF OBVIOUS \n\nHave you got nothing more constructive to do with your life?\n\n__________________\n\nIf you aren\'t part of the cure then you\'re part of the problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(144942, 22552, 1013, 102128, 1072936800, '', 'how come you have huge font???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(144944, 22552, 1013, 101837, 1072936800, '"no 2003 yet"', 'Look harder.  If you look at what G. Newell said about the code, it wouldn\'t be illogical to assume this is code from only last month.  \n\n\n\nIf you want a faster way of seeing how recent this code is. . .  you can just \'grep\' through the whole source tree for the string of "2003" and get a whole mess of matches.\n\n\n\nNo doubt about it.  This is very recent, perfectly working code that just needs material for it to run on.  (i.e. art, models, music...etc)\n\n\n\nAs for GPL code in Source, that\'s FUD.  There is LGPL code in there and it\'s all part of the licenced Havoc 2 physics middleware that Valve paid for with a lot of money.\n\n\n\nDirtbox/Mr. Chris: this is totally unrelated to the topic but you\'d be better to use the ignore feature for people who don\'t bother thinking before typing.  Does me wonders and saves me groans.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(144946, 22552, 1013, 102082, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Complex-Sick \n\nay pm me the site where u downloaded it at  \n\n\n\nNO\n\n__________________\n\nNow in Anti-Steam flavor.\n\nReason - /forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=94352', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(144964, 22552, 1013, 102084, 1072936800, '', 'The likelyhood of it being the most recent version of the code at the time is fairly high, but I\'ve got more than enough experience in game development to know that theres going to be more than a few builds about in various stages of completion.\n\n\n\nI\'m *hoping* its not the most recent and a lot has been changed, including some glaring holes that need to be armour plated now.\n\n\n\nAnd yes, some is based on completely free, open source GPL code. There\'s other code in there that would have been rather expensive though. Unfortunately its now free to anyone with a net connection.\n\n\n\nPoor Valve.\n\n__________________\n\nIf you aren\'t part of the cure then you\'re part of the problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
