(149375, 22662, 1013, 103388, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by TRANCE \n\n\nLinux is MORE VUNERABLE TO ATTACKS because its OPEN SOURCE... meaning EVERYONE has the source... windows on the other hand isn\'t!1!!\n\n\n\n\n\nYES windows is MORE popular and there for A LOT of no-life hackers try to crack it...\n\n\n\n\n\nLinux will never be mainstream... at least not this decade... its NOT user friendly... incompatible with 95% of all software, vunerable (open source) and it just sucks\n\n\n\n\n\nP.S. IF U ARE CONNECTED TO THE INTERNET U ARE ALWAYS SUBJECT TO HACKER ATTACKS NO MATTER WHAT OS U ARE USING....  \n\n\n\n\n\nthere are several mainstream operating systems that are not made by MS....\n\n\n\n\n\nAnyhow, I\'d imagine, because you haven\'t studied the architecture of linux itself, you probably don\'t understand why it doesn\'t matter about the open-source bit.....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(149383, 22662, 1013, 102169, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by noitsmehoney \n\n\nthere are several mainstream operating systems that are not made by MS....\n\n\n\n\n\nAnyhow, I\'d imagine, because you haven\'t studied the architecture of linux itself, you probably don\'t understand why it doesn\'t matter about the open-source bit.....  \n\n\n\n\n\nActually there are two sides to this...\n\n\n1. A possible hacker could use the sourcecode to find possible ways of attacking the system hence this makes the system more open to attacks.\n\n\n2. There are a lot of competent people constantly reviewing the source of linux hence there a good chance that possible vulnerabilities gets discovered in time\n\n__________________\n\n*Help! the paranoids are stalkling me!*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
