(155927, 24343, 1013, 102197, 1072936800, 'FPS problems and counterstrike demos', 'Every time I record demos for matches while playing cs i get extreme fps lag it drops to 10-20 fps sometimes and makes it completely unplayable.  I have a p4 1.8ghz with an nvidia fx5600 with 256mb of ddr.  I also have 768mb of rdram.  The problem ONLY occurs when i record demos... my friends experience the same problem as well... if someone could help it would be much appreciated', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(155940, 24343, 1013, 102195, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Raimi \n\njust close and reopen Steam. worked for me.  tried doing that a LOT of times but didn\'t work', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(155943, 24343, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'Most commonly reported bugs\n\n\n\nEven if a bug has a fix, it is STILL a reported bug, and VALVe will hopefully eventually remove it from the program.  But just use the fix for now.\n\n\n\nCannot find any servers, despite not having any filter settings.\n\nFix: /forums/show...;threadid=24394 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=24394)\n\n\n\n\'Unbind all\' symptoms when dead (keyboard and mouse buttons don\'t work).\n\nCause: Having the spectator menu open when you \'spawn\' on the next round.\n\nFix: Either close the spectator menu before you spawn, or type \'spec_menu 0\' in console if it occurs.  Typing \'+duck\' and then \'-duck\' also works, but is slower.\n\n\n\nLeft handed models on return from alt tab.\n\nFix: Type cl_righthand 1 in console.\n\n\n\nMouse cursor visible on return from alt tab.\n\nFix: Open and close the in-game GUI (escape, or console).\n\n\n\nCannot see the speech tab for people using in-game voice com.  This usually occurs when holding the scoreboard open.\n\nFix: None known.\n\n\n\nFPS issues, lag and netsync issues, interp and various other tweaks.\n\nFix: None known.\n\n\n\nPlayers submerged in ground or running in sky.\n\nCause: None known.  It\'s noticed that it appears to be at either the highest elevation possible, or the lowest elevation possible, on the map, and only seems to happen on certain maps (I\'ve seen it on dust/dust2, but not elsewhere so much.)  Note also that the player doesn\'t see this for himself, and the hitboxes will still work, it\'s just the model goes flying or sinking.  Apparently, only YOU see this: they themselves, or anyone else do not see the same person doing this at the same time, except by coincidence(?).  This even works when you spectate that person from first person perspective, the viewpoint is too high or too low.\n\nFix: None known.  However, should the player in question change elevation from what he\'s currently on (go up/down a ramp, or jump), it\'s been known to fix itself.\n\n\n\nNote: If someone can find a way to repeat this bug, and the steps taken to cause it, I\'m sure it would be most helpful to VALVe.\n\n\n\nGame Not Available and/or No Children Registered.\n\nCause: Clicking Cancel on the \'Preparing to play Counter-Strike...\' window.  (Or end-tasking the program at this point.)\n\nFix: Shut down the computer, making sure the shut down is successful.  The power should be off at this point (a restart or reboot does not work).  Then turn the computer back on, try again, and this time, just be patient.  (If the three periods are moving, the program has NOT locked up.)\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease, if your bug is in this list (which I will keep updated as per the posts in this thread), PLEASE do not post it again.  I will also post fixes as well, if somebody mentions them in this thread.\n\n\n\nIf you are posting an uncommon bug, or a bug with an error message attached, then PLEASE post your SYSTEM SPECS as well.\n\n\n\nOperating System\n\nProcessor, MHz, RAM\n\nBandwidth\n\nGraphics Card, and amount of video RAM\n\nGraphics display type (Software, OGL, D3d), Resolution, and 32 bit or 16 bit', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156017, 24343, 1013, 101294, 1072936800, '', 'If your ingame, and your net disconnects (dsl, disconnect every 24 hours :-/) then you get an error about net cannot send packet instead of timing out safely, it crashes, and any favorites you set during that "session" you lose.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156087, 24343, 1013, 102198, 1072936800, '', 'After playing CS for about 2 hrs. My drop weapon key wont work. I have to go into setup and rebind the key 2 or 3 times to get it to work. I use the "G" for drop weapon. And when I go into setup it shows that "G" is setup to drop weapon. But it doesnt work.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156098, 24343, 1013, 102199, 1072936800, 'Missing servers?', 'quote:Originally posted by pstation \n\ntried doing that a LOT of times but didn\'t work  \n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve lost all servers and can\'t get a new server list either, it just says no servers meet my filter settings even tho\' I dont have ant set???????????', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156109, 24343, 1013, 102200, 1072936800, '', 'When you minimize CS (alt+tab) and then come back to the game if you use cl_righthand 1 it changes your weapon view to the left hand.. and you have to put cl_righthand 1 again... Also the cursor stays in the middle... \n\n\n\nThe server browser doesnt work at times... Sometimes it won\'t display any servers eventhough you have no filters, or If you have 2 or 3 filters it won\'t display any servers at all... I usually see like 20 servers only (<100, no pass) , but I know that there are hundreds that would bypass my filter settings...\n\n\n\nSteam takes too long to load... (maybe its because we can\' see it while its connecting to the steam network, but I would rather see a window saying connecting or something like that..)\n\n\n\nThe favorite server browser should allow you to save a private server password and also be able to set the rcon password for the server...\n\n\n\nSometimes when you just open steam, you need to click on refresh on the favorite server list to see any of your servers.. if you don\'t, it tells you that you have no favorite servers..\n\n\n\n\n\nThe fps drops while recording a demo (doesn\'t happen to me though)\n\n\n\nSometimes while in game when another person talks.. you can\'t see the right blue/red signal that says who is talking..\n\n\n\nSometimes while you have the CS in-game menu while playing, the kills aren\'t displayed on the screen.. \n\n\n\nthat\'s all I can think about now... Oh yeah the shield is still a mess...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156114, 24343, 1013, 102201, 1072936800, '', 'The server message character has to be a bug/oversight. Valve couldnt of doen this on purpose as they know the modding community would lose tons of features for there mods(amxmod, adminmod, statsme). Please fix this bug, make the gaming community happy.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156134, 24343, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by pstation \n\never since i updated all none of the server lists have worked for me  \n\n\n\ntry this:\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=24394 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=24394)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156168, 24343, 1013, 102202, 1072936800, '', 'My Bugs:\n\n\n\n- click @ \'Options\' crashes hl.exe\n\n- Steammenutitles are damaged/broken (f.e. instead of \'Server\' it displays \'STEAM_MENU_ID#2\' or somethin else)\n\n- Specmenu bug... (can\'t change playerview while deadtime w/o setting spec_menu to 0 again and again)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156222, 24343, 1013, 102022, 1072936800, '', 'STILL getting this\n\n\n\n\n\n"I"m still getting "Disconnected Invalid STEAM UserID Ticket" when I try and connect to my Dedicated Server. \n\n\n\nNetwork Setup \n\n\n\n2 IP\'s from my ISP \n\n\n\nFirst IP --->CS Dedicated Server \n\nSecond IP ---> Router ---> 2 desktop computers and the CS Dedicated Server \n\n\n\nMy desktops use the router as a Gateway \n\nThe CS server connects directly to the internet \n\n\n\nThe 2 IP\'s cannot reach each other because they\'re on different subnets (and my isp\'s routing sucks, But I am trying to get them to move them onto the same subnet but have been waiting 2 weeks because they claim it\'s a software problem with STEAM ) So I have to connect to my server VIA LAN however I get the pereviously stated error. \n\n\n\nI CAN connect to any other internet server without a problem. \n\n\n\nAnyone else seems to be able to join my server as it has been quite busy over the past couple days."', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156132, 24394, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'No servers listed', 'It looks like the best fix for people who are getting this is to:\n\n\n\n\n\n- close Steam\n\n\n- delete masterservers.vdf and serverbrowser.vdf in the config dir\n\n\n- launch Steam\n\n\n\n\n\nedit: got plenty of files already - thanks! []\n\n\n\n\n\nTaylor\n\n__________________\n\nSteam Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(156172, 24394, 1013, 102203, 1072936800, '', 'I had that problem, but it turned out to be cause by me having SPI-mode activated on my router (D-Link DI-604, w. firmware 1.81 (Euro)).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
