(157252, 24560, 1013, 102213, 1072936800, 'Hackers and Cheaters are free to attack any server', 'I monitor the hacker and Rage clans to keep updated on how to counter them but I found one thing I could do nothing about.\n\n\n\nU can by entering a new E-mail get a new STEAMid !\n\n\n\nThat means that ban lists and STEAMid databases are non functional.\n\n\n\nWe can do nothing to stop Hackers, Lamers, Rasists (yes there are many of them on the DOD severs), Cheaters and disruptive players in general.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI have when we had WONid\'s made a big database that helped to keep all these offenders out.\n\n\n\nIf Steam gets up and working a community can join my database network and we can get rid of the Cheaters and Lamers.\n\nIt will hit them harder if they get banned by like 20 communitys spanning 40-50 servers !\n\nIf anyone is interested in this project then u can e-mail me and u will get the full info on how I will do this.\n\n\n\n\n\nStalingrad', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157345, 24560, 1013, 102214, 1072936800, '', 'quote:U can by entering a new E-mail get a new STEAMid !\n\n\n\nI think its because valve has themselves a big dilemmer.\n\n\n\ntheres such a high percentage of shared CD keys, that once they enable one-cd-key-for-one-account they will lose 70-80% of their potential steam audience (people who then will not be buying stuff from steam)\n\nsecondly, steam is so garbaged atm, that an even higher percentage has registered more than one steam account for their CD for the simple fact that when they first registered their CD key on steam, it went belly up and that account was no longer useable on their machine (I know this for a fact, I\'ve got two other accounts for the same CD key, which If I try and use them, steam BSOD\'s the machine)\n\nbasically the whole thing is one great big mess for vavle, but atm, lots of free stuff for us :|', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157360, 24560, 1013, 100157, 1072936800, '', 'You can ban by IP also.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157367, 24560, 1013, 100106, 1072936800, 'Hackers and Cheaters are free to attack any server', 'quote:Originally posted by Stalingrad \n\nU can by entering a new E-mail get a new STEAMid !\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nif this is true, valve please, shut down steam, the content servers and all the crap around it!\n\nthen hire some -professionals- and fix all the sh*t on your side!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157370, 24560, 1013, 102215, 1072936800, 'I created a new steam account', 'awww man, didn\'t know that when you create a new account, ur steamid changes.\n\ni changed my steam account, because my old one has alot of problems, i hope i could stick 2 the new one.\n\ndeath 2 cheaters !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157371, 24560, 1013, 102214, 1072936800, '', 'quote:You can ban by IP also.\n\n\n\nnot in a community ban list you cant, never heard of dynamic IPs?\n\n\n\nwhat about large shared connections with one ip?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157373, 24560, 1013, 102213, 1072936800, '', 'Yes u can ban by IP but the problem is that most have DynIP. then u would have to ban a range of IP\'s and therefore ban people that does not deserve it.\n\n\n\nIf it goes by modem dial up its even worse cause their IP\'s are totally random. ie cannot be banned by IP.\n\n\n\nIts a real big problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157376, 24560, 1013, 100106, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by fjl \n\nYou can ban by IP also.  \n\n\n\nlol, for me it\'s easier to change the ip. it will take 2 seconds...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157385, 24560, 1013, 102216, 1072936800, '', 'funny thing... all this load of sh*t about hacking and cheating... so far, for me, cheating had never been an issue. I would rather play clean than having to get new email address for each time I get banned from too many servers. (not that I would cheat anyway...)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157526, 24560, 1013, 102156, 1072936800, '', 'To me it seems like the cheating has gotten MUCH worse...wallhacks seem to be everwhere and aimbots are just nonstop.\n\n\n\nHLGuard seems useless at this point and the best thing to do is just have good admins and BAN as many as possible that you suspect cheat.  I dont even care if someone is legit...if I THINK you are cheating then play somewhere else.  My server is full 24/7 so banning 20 players a day means nothing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157591, 24560, 1013, 102217, 1072936800, '', 'This is wrong. Your STEAMID is *not* your email address, therefore changing your email address will not unban you from a server.  The email address is your Steam User ID (different thing).. presumably to allow multiple licenses on a single machine.\n\n\n\n(Your STEAMID is derived from your license for the steam game that you are running - in this case - the HL CDKey.. to find your STEAMID .. join a server - bring down console and type "status" ... find your name in the list, and your steamID looks something like STEAM:0:0:231498 )', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157607, 24560, 1013, 102218, 1072936800, '', 'Valve needs to incorporate a way to ban MAC addresses; problem solved.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157627, 24560, 1013, 102219, 1072936800, '', 'So defender U ban people if without proof or nothing??? WTF is up with that. Say if their just betta than U and frag your ass non-stop. Is that an instnt ban?\n\n\n\n"U dont care if some1 is legit" To tell the truth that is just plain st00pid', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157635, 24560, 1013, 100059, 1072936800, '', 'In order to make the new SteamID useful you would need a new CD key as well.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(157638, 24560, 1013, 102086, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Bench \n\nThis is wrong. Your STEAMID is *not* your email address, therefore changing your email address will not unban you from a server.  The email address is your Steam User ID (different thing).. presumably to allow multiple licenses on a single machine.\n\n\n\n(Your STEAMID is derived from your license for the steam game that you are running - in this case - the HL CDKey.. to find your STEAMID .. join a server - bring down console and type "status" ... find your name in the list, and your steamID looks something like STEAM:0:0:231498 ) \n\nI think what they are saying is that it\'s possible to register more than one account with the one license. One CD key and five e-mail accounts, for example, could get you 5 seperate steam logins and therefore 5 different STEAMIDs. Even more than that is possible , tbh, as there is no e-mail verification check in Steam yet. Everytime you\'re banned from a server, it would be possible to just register a new steam account (without even having to bother getting a new hotmail account first, or whatever) using the same CD Key.\n\n\n\nVALVe must have records somewhere of several steamIDs assigned to just the one, same CDKey.\n\n\n\nI havn\'t tested this at all, though. I\'m just going off what I\'ve heard (even before this thread). If I am wrong and this is not possible, please say so.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(159799, 25027, 1013, 102220, 1072936800, 'Running a server with a router and playing on router with a 2nd machine', 'ok. All my other posts have lead me to make this thread. I called the tech support of my router and we worked on this together through trial and error. The main problem is that steam lists a range of ports to open up on your router to get steam to work. What they fail to tell you that "port forwarding" will only forward certian ports to one ip address, not to. So to get by this problem this is what you have to do:\n\n\n\n\n\nOpened ports for computer A (HLDS computer) \n\n\n27010-27012  UDP\n\n\n27015-27016 UPD\n\n\n27040 TCP, UPD\n\n\n5100-7500 TCP\n\n\n\n\n\nOpened ports for computer B (Steam CS computer)\n\n\n27000-27009 UPD\n\n\n27013-27014 UPD\n\n\n27030-27039 TCP\n\n\n1200 UPD\n\n\n27056   TCP, UPD  (this port is for steam ip address verification if open it will allow steam to see the ip address of the Ethernet card, not the router.)\n\n\n\n\n\nok, now everybody is looking going why only those 3 ports for the server. the reson for that is when you create a server and it logs into the Steam network it athenticates on ports 27010 and 27040. (noticed this from when you start HLDS and look in the console at the ip addresses it lists, the numbers after the colon are the port info example:\n\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.251:27040\n\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.253:27040\n\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.11:27010\n\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.12:27010).\n\n\n\n\n\n Now the reason for the 27016 port on the server machine is because when you creat the server you need to change the upd port to 27016 because you need to enable port 27015 for the gaming machine. whith this configuration I can log into my server by lan connection, my friends can log in through favorites, and it will post on the server list. (due to the port being allowed to go through the server. I know there is a lot of useless information in this but I figured you would like to know how I can to this realization. But the only way this will work for a server is if you dowload the steam HLDS program and not run the HLDS from the steam client itself.\n\n\n(getsteamnow.php (/getsteamnow.php) ) and select dedicated server. With this install you can run HLDS and also if you all ready have a server setup all you nave to do is cut and past your dedicated server info over the stuff that gets installed and it will work. (basically the machine running the server does not need to be logged into steam. the server will log itself when you connect it to the steam network)\n\n\n\n\n\nRevison: Oct. 25, 2003 (Added/changed some ports after further testing with different firewalls and also doing more research on what ports steam/WON used.)\n\n\n\n\n\nIf I have confused anybody with this let me know. I can try and talk you through it from AIM. Thanks!!\n\n__________________\n\nIm bad Ash. Your good Ash. Your little goody too shoes. Little goody too shoes, ha....."BOOM"........Good, Bad, Im the guy with the gun!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(159851, 25027, 1013, 102221, 1072936800, '', 'i can open the ports using some program?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(160085, 25027, 1013, 102222, 1072936800, 'ports', 'Dude, thank you so much for this information. I have the exact setup you described and couldnt get my server in the public list on a machine outside my LAN. I know how to forward ports n all that crap, u just never specified wich ports were TCP or UDP. If you could follow up on this tha would be great. thank you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(160330, 25027, 1013, 102220, 1072936800, 'whoops', 'i forwarded both tcp and upd. but my router does not let me pick either between the 2 types. you can probably go with the steam standard of just upd for the lower and tcp for the higher. as for ports 27016 that is just upd and for 27056 I am unsure, i would enable both or try one and then the other to see which works out for you. Glad I help someone out.\n\n__________________\n\nIm bad Ash. Your good Ash. Your little goody too shoes. Little goody too shoes, ha....."BOOM"........Good, Bad, Im the guy with the gun!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(160331, 25027, 1013, 102220, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by f-u-c-k-a-l-l \n\n\ni can open the ports using some program?  \n\n\n\n\n\nif you have a router you can do it through the routers software. (basically read the damn manual for the router) if you are using a software firewall you need to go into its settings and create the provisions in the program. look at the thread on how to configure a software firewall for more info on that respects. the thread for that is as follows:\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/...&threadid=18837 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=18837)\n\n__________________\n\nIm bad Ash. Your good Ash. Your little goody too shoes. Little goody too shoes, ha....."BOOM"........Good, Bad, Im the guy with the gun!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(160915, 25027, 1013, 102223, 1072936800, 'Running a server with a router and playing on router with a 2nd machine', '[Opened ports for computer A (HLDS computer) \n\n\n27010 \n\n\n27016 \n\n\n27040\n\n\n\n\n\nOpened ports for computer B (Steam CS computer)\n\n\n27000-27009\n\n\n27011-27015\n\n\n27030-27039\n\n\n1200\n\n\n27056    (this port is for steam ip address verification if open it will allow steam to see the ip address of the Ethernet card, not the router.)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo hosting the HLDS, you have to open this ports 27010,27016,27040 or Ports forwarding this three ports to lan IP.\n\n\n\n\n\non Steam Client side is that just open the ports one the router  27000-27009\n\n\n27011-27015, 27030-27039, 1200, 27056', '127.0.0.1', 1),
