(161287, 25027, 1013, 102225, 1072936800, 'Opening ports without a router?', 'Is there any way to open these ports if I don\'t have a router?  I have my two computers networked with a Crossover Cable and I want to do the same thing - run one computer as a dedicated server and connect and play on this server from my other computer.  When I try to connect to the dedicated server it automatically disconnects me and says, "Reason:  Invalid STEAM UserID ticket."  Is there a way to open these ports or download software to do this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(161667, 25027, 1013, 100975, 1072936800, 'Opening ports without a router?', 'quote:Originally posted by aparoche \n\n\nIs there any way to open these ports if I don\'t have a router?  I have my two computers networked with a Crossover Cable and I want to do the same thing - run one computer as a dedicated server and connect and play on this server from my other computer.  When I try to connect to the dedicated server it automatically disconnects me and says, "Reason:  Invalid STEAM UserID ticket."  Is there a way to open these ports or download software to do this?  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRead this tread: /forums/...15&pagenumber=1 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=14132&perpage=15&pagenumber=1)\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd your problem will be solved.\n\n\n\n\n\nRead the whole TREAD.. There are 2 solutions to the problem.\n\n__________________\n\nGame on!! Don\'t give up.\n\n\n\n\n\nRegards [Hlm]Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165507, 25027, 1013, 102226, 1072936800, '', 'man, but my steam wont even start! it doesnt want to log on []\n\n\nall valve does is annoying us, instead of creatin their own WON-like servers, they just had to make this complicated ****ty thing.\n\n\ni dont get it, it would be alot easier if valve would created a WON-like servers.\n\n\nhttp://blue.t35.com/littleone/steamerror.jpg (http://blue.t35.com/littleone/steamerror.jpg) - ***ed up.\n\n\nH-E-L-P\n\n\nif this doesnt solve out till WON closes, i think im just gonna quit CS, moving to battlefield.\n\n\nall valve did in making steam is losing half of their gamers.\n\n\n\n\n\nP.S.\n\n\nis there any way to open ports? i have norton internet security, and Steam doesnt even log on. says my connection is screwed or its down. My friends r playing 1.6 and im on IRC, ehh, i dont think my connection is screwed.\n\n\nSTEAM=SUX', '127.0.0.1', 1),
