(165316, 25907, 1013, 102232, 1072936800, 'How does STEAM benefit the end user?', 'Can anyone from VALVe or the community tell me why STEAM benefits me, as an end user, over the classic manual patching/WON system.\n\n\n\n\n\nI assume you are forcefully migrating users to this platform to help _them_ as well as yourselves (VALVe). Can anyone outline the details of why end users should be seeing STEAM as the way forward instead of juat a pain in the arse?\n\n\n\n\n\nMy own personal experience with STEAM has been so bad I have ended up stopping developing under HalfLife and haven\'t played since the Steam 1.0 final was released, but rather than "fl@m3z0r" VALVe,  I would prefer to hear the other side of the argument as to why users aren\'t being given the choice of either patching themselves, or using STEAM. I personally see absolutley no reason why STEAM authentication cannot be brought out as a standalone patch for 1.1.1.0 users to download and enable play on steam servers, I used to enjoy being able to set up my debugger to run "hl.exe" and pressing F5 for a quick boot of the game to check small changes to code. With STEAM this simply cannot be done, it takes about 5-10 minutes to boot the game for the majority of users, including myself, and waiting 5 minutes to test simple changes in code is just not acceptable, other engines have suddenly become more attractive.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe two main points I see given in STEAMs favour are:\n\n\n\n\n\n+ Anti Cheat\n\n\n+ Automatic patching\n\n\n\n\n\nFirstly, I dont tihnk STEAM has anything to do with anti cheat itself, you get a group of "noobs" who are under the impression STEAM will scan your hard disk for cheats and leaked HL2 files.. I really doubt this is the case. VAC was working before STEAM and, afaik, is totally seperate, so I dont see how STEAM is benefitting anyone in this way.\n\n\n\n\n\nNext I dont think the tradeoff between having to wait 5 minutes to load the game, and having patches automatically downloaded to my client is worth it. VALVe don\'t release patches that often, and to be quite honest the last few patches have casued a lot of hassle, a lot of internal engine stuff has been changed, TFC has had a few half-hearted fixes thrown in, which have obviously not been properly playtested. I understand why VALVe would want to concentrate on CounterStrike, but I hate to see a good game like TFC decline like it has, I have even offered to work on TFC for VALVe as an unpaid volunteer, VALVe simply did not reply to my E-Mail, which suggests to me thay dont _want_ anyone working on TFC, why I am not sure.\n\n\n\n\n\nCan anyone give anything that STEAM does that will make me say "wow yeah, I never thought of that, we really need STEAM after all"? If you can, or you can help me to actually get a game started under STEAM, you\'re welcome to reply.\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks for reading.\n\n\n\n\n\n- Rob.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165422, 25907, 1013, 102233, 1072936800, '', 'I ow him nothing but I could make time to read info from users on my flagship website & answer  a fair ?.\n\n\n\n\n\nRobGP you said about just having the steam bit as a anti cheat im also very happy with any new anti cheat bit.\n\n\n\n\n\nI do prefer to do my own updates & ill often take them round my mates on CD.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165455, 25907, 1013, 102232, 1072936800, '', 'Im sorry but I cant follow your post SinBin, can you reiterate what you are saying?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165486, 25907, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, 'Benefits of Steam', 'Steam\'s benefits to the end user:\n\n\n- Automatic updates\n\n\n- Friends list\n\n\n- Retrieving server lists from in game\n\n\n- Faster downloading of maps\n\n\n- GUI interface (nothing was there previously)\n\n\n- Can change options/settings in game\n\n\n- Console is now in game and doesn\'t take up that much space\n\n\n- Console commands are done with auto-complete\n\n\n(meaning type net_ and you will see net_graph, net_graphpos, etc)\n\n\n- You can play games while dead with friends\n\n\n- You can check game status while on your desktop\n\n\n- you can use steam as an instant messenger for your CS friends without being in-game\n\n\n\n\n\nWell I can\'t think of any more right now. But doesn\'t that sound like a good thing?  Yeah I know it\'s buggy right now, but trust me, a great idea it is.\n\n\n\n\n\nMost people are so focused on the bugs, they are missing the whole point of the switch.\n\n__________________\n\nI love my Steam, this is SO much better!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165509, 25907, 1013, 102232, 1072936800, '', '- Automatic updates \n\n\n\n\n\nWhats the big issue here? I mean what was so wrong with the patching system before? The lack of bandwidth on STEAM is crippling, everyone getting the patches from a central location is a bottleneck, giving downloadable modules to admins that can host them all over is a far better method of doing things in my opinion, anyway HL came with sierras autoupdate utility so the functionality was there already.\n\n\n\n\n\n- Friends list \n\n\n\n\n\nOk, so I can now have a contact list that doesnt include my friends that don\'t play Half Life.. whoop de doo. This is simply a gimmik and is reinventing the wheel.\n\n\n\n\n\n- Retrieving server lists from in game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. There was a VGUI form written by valve that actually had this functionality before STEAM. Plus, whats so bad about pressing escape and looking for a server? Are you saying that the fact you can see your game in the background whilst you look for a new server is an advantage? Or are you so skilled you can actually play whilst looking at the servers?\n\n\n\n\n\n- Faster downloading of maps \n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m sorry I\'ve yet to experience this.\n\n\n\n\n\n- GUI interface (nothing was there previously) \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. VGUI has been around since 1.0.1.3.\n\n\n\n\n\n- Can change options/settings in game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. ?? Youre reiterating the same point over and over, "dialog box xxxx can be brought up in game".. I dont understand why its such a huge issue, its not like its really any differnent to the old method. Its not like you can actually play whilst using these things.\n\n\n\n\n\n- Console is now in game and doesn\'t take up that much space \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. The old console was "in game" too, and was much better, it was easier to jump between the game and the old console than it is with this new VGUI console.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- Console commands are done with auto-complete \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. Ill give you this one, but this isnt really a STEAM thing per se, this could have easily been implemented into the old console, although the implementation is a bit iffy.\n\n\n\n\n\n- You can play games while dead with friends\n\n\n\n\n\nYoure supposed to be playing a game already!! If youre so bored to have to boot another game to play, is it really worth playing? Again this is a gimmik thrown in, although in my experience, non of the games are bug free, and onle one was even playable.\n\n\n\n\n\n- You can check game status while on your desktop \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. Im not entirely sure what you mean by this, but GameSpy3D and similar have done this for years.\n\n\n\n\n\n- you can use steam as an instant messenger for your CS friends without being in-game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. I can use ICQ too, or MSN, or AIM....\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m disappointed, very few of your reasons are actually about STEAM, most are things that could have been implemented easily without STEAM, which isn\'t what I was asking for.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165631, 25907, 1013, 102153, 1072936800, '', 'yea well posted there RobGP.\n\n\n\n\n\nI think valve tryed to make out won server costs to much ? or aleast I did read this somewhere.\n\n\n\n\n\nAs you have well pointed out there is no real reson for steam other than a way to make mo money ? and the way it runs atm we are just being used as beta tester ready for hl2 and more.\n\n\n\n\n\nValve used to be run by gamers , you could even send them a msg/email and get a reply, now its just like any other big company that thinks there the next microsoft. The accountant is running the show. you would do better to offer your services to id, atleast they seem to have kept thier feet on the ground and know where they came from.\n\n__________________\n\nOp^m0nkEy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165650, 25907, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, 'Explained again with examples', 'First of all, what are you looking for? Let me explain how all these are advantages with examples to make this more clearer.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by RobGP \n\n\nWhats the big issue here? I mean what was so wrong with the patching system before? \n\n\nLet\'s explain this one. The old system, they lead you to some site like fileplanet.com or fileshack.com. If you don\'t pay, which at least I don\'t, you wait for about 60mins for the download to start cause you are in a queue all day. Then you waited for a large 70MB file. Plus you are not sure which site to go to, how packed their servers are (so you can even download from there). \n\n\n\n\n\nP.S. Check www.steampowered.com/status (/status) You\'ll notice Steam is being hosted by the same sites that the updates were coming from originally.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Friends list \n\n\nOk, so I can now have a contact list that doesnt include my friends that don\'t play Half Life.. whoop de doo. This is simply a gimmik and is reinventing the wheel.\n\n\nSo you never wanted to invite your friend to play on the server you are on? Say you play on more than one particular server, how\'s your friend going to find you? or you going to find him? Use Gamespy? Use gametiger.net? Sure you could do that but Steam has it in game.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Retrieving server lists from in game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. There was a VGUI form written by valve that actually had this functionality before STEAM. Plus, whats so bad about pressing escape and looking for a server? Are you saying that the fact you can see your game in the background whilst you look for a new server is an advantage?\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat VGUI are you talking about? Cause there wasn\'t one with Half-Life unless it was a seperate download. Plus, in order to look for a server the old way, you had to exit the game and refresh the list which if you waited long enough took about 5 mins. In Steam, while I am dead I can see if there\'s a server playing another map I want to play or I can check on my favorite servers. \n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Faster downloading of maps \n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m sorry I\'ve yet to experience this.\n\n\nYou are missing out. In the old version, I was searching for maps I didn\'t have so I can download them and do some chores or whatever. It took so long, I just left it downloading for 10 mins or whatever. Steam downloads for me (and I am on DSL) took under 2 mins.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Can change options/settings in game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. ?? Youre reiterating the same point over and over, "dialog box xxxx can be brought up in game".. I dont understand why its such a huge issue, its not like its really any differnent to the old method. Its not like you can actually play whilst using these things.\n\n\nThe funny thing is if you wanted to change your options while you are alive in game, you can! No more hitting ESC to go back to the options. Some of the options in the old version were so far back, you had to leave the game to change it. (ie. Video, Sound) Now it\'s all done while in a server.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Console is now in game and doesn\'t take up that much space \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. The old console was "in game" too, and was much better, it was easier to jump between the game and the old console than it is with this new VGUI console.\n\n\nExactly how was this much better? How was it easier to jump between it? It\'s almost exactly the same! You still hit ~ to get between the two. This time it\'s in a window so it doesn\'t take up half the screen and has auto-complete!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- Console commands are done with auto-complete \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. Ill give you this one, but this isnt really a STEAM thing per se, this could have easily been implemented into the old console, although the implementation is a bit iffy.\n\n\nHow could it of been implemented in the old version? The old console was entirely text-based, windows weren\'t there. How does auto-complete work then? I\'ve never seen auto-complete done in pure text.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- You can play games while dead with friends\n\n\n\n\n\nYoure supposed to be playing a game already!! If youre so bored to have to boot another game to play, is it really worth playing? Again this is a gimmik thrown in, although in my experience, non of the games are bug free, and onle one was even playable.\n\n\nActually someone suggested that on another forum. It\'s fun for people who are bored when they die off too quickly and have mins to spare.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- You can check game status while on your desktop \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. Im not entirely sure what you mean by this, but GameSpy3D and similar have done this for years.\n\n\nWell they have, but isn\'t it better to have everything all in one easy to access spot instead of having your competition beat you.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\n- you can use steam as an instant messenger for your CS friends without being in-game \n\n\n\n\n\nThis isn\'t a STEAM advantage. I can use ICQ too, or MSN, or AIM....\n\n\n\n\n\nYou could...but again, all-in-one game browser \n\n\n\n\n\nHonestly, I don\'t know what you are looking for people to say. Steam has put together a browser that is now all-in-one combining features done from other software or websites into their system. They\'ve made it easier to use and easy to implement fixes.\n\n\n\n\n\nOh and another advantage of Steam. Remember losing sound in CS 1.5. Try going to desktop and coming back to the game...you still have sound.\n\n__________________\n\nI love my Steam, this is SO much better!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166084, 25907, 1013, 102234, 1072936800, '', 'I also dont see the advantages of Steam compared to other game browsers like Gamespy and All Seeing Eye. Not to mention Steam is way more bloated than any of the above.\n\n\nYou say you like the idea of auto-updates, that is until you have a virus or some other malicious attack hapen on your machine as a result of Steam auto-update. If you think it is impossible, take a look at the latest gaming headlines and subject lines in most forums about HL2. The more you say it si impossible the more hackers find it aluring to hack. To me this is just a security hole waiting to be exploited. I would rather DL the file and install it myself.\n\n\nAs for finding friends and inviting them to play on the same server, there are at least 10 other methods that dont take up half the memory and dont take forever to load as Steam so I cant see this as a possible advantage.\n\n\nI havent used the in game browser for HL in 4 yars so I cant comment on any VGUI they may or may not have had. I do know I was getting along just fine without Steam and alot faster and with better framerates.\n\n\nIf you are still DL maps from a server, all I can say is shame on you. There are more resources for DL maps on the web that are much faster than server or Steam DL than I care to list. But, if you must insist on taking server bandwidth away from other players because you are to lazy to Google a map, then shame on you.\n\n\nYou say no more hitting "Escape" to change options. Funny I still have to hit "Escape" to access the options menu. I never left the game before when I changed them except for video settings, which still happens with Steam. \n\n\nI dont have auto-complete on anything else on my computer why would I want it on my games? Just one of those useless features I see no need of. Same with the games. I am there to play a game I paid for not some silly chess game. If I wanted to play chess I will go to Yahoo or some other web hosted game site.\n\n\nI am not saying change is bad, but change should certainly for the better and so far I am not seeing the "beter" part of Steam. It is slow to load, slow to load my game, takes my framerates down, I expirience more game crashes and Steam takes more memory than any other game browser I have ever tried.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166097, 25907, 1013, 102160, 1072936800, '', 'The long forgotten advantage.\n\n\nYou can play games on any computer that has acess and spec req.\n\n\nwhen steam works this will become a more vialbe practice', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166103, 25907, 1013, 102235, 1072936800, '', 'I think that Valve is trying to move away\n\n\nfrom the large update file, and going for releasing bits and pieces as they are ready, over days-weeks-months.\n\n\n\n\n\nwhich I think is the best feature of Steam\n\n\nI`m getting this impression from the way\n\n\nthey are handling the DoD 1.1 patch..\n\n\n\n\n\n2 maps so far, more to come soon..!!\n\n\n\n\n\nRIGHT WALDO???  =)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ncya\n\n__________________\n\n"You WiLL get down on your filthy knees and crawl to the alter that is WEEN" ~Henry Rollins', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166160, 25907, 1013, 102233, 1072936800, '', 'I could say all robs info again naming other good apps but we all know & they do. Let um play there game & they can move to consols(ps2) for the kids', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166196, 25907, 1013, 102236, 1072936800, '', 'Koala it was nice of you to post, but its pretty obvious GP was just waiting for someone to post so he could rant on them. I will give you ONE POSSIBLE benefit that Steam will MOST LIKELY provide, that makes Steam x314270948720 more valuable than the old system.\n\n\n\n\n\nAn ELITE anti-cheat module that could be deployed (with notice), and UPDATED (without notice).\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is my opinon that this will happen in the somewhat near future, and that this was Valves plan all along. If everyone has to go to mirrors to get a new anti-cheat patch, thats pretty much the heads up that the hackers were looking for......duh.\n\n\n\n\n\nIN DEFENSE OF STEAM....\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam is ALOT better than 1.5s system, thats why i stopped playing 1.5 back in January. Anyone that thinks 1.5 is better is laughable at best, thats like someone back in 1992 saying:\n\n\n\n\n\n "roller skates are better than rollerblades, because no one got hurt trying to do tricks on roller skates. Now people get hurt all the time trying to do tricks on rollerblades"\n\n\n\n\n\nNow in 2003 ask yourself which is cooler? roller skates or rollerblades? In a few months ask your self which is cooler 1.5 or 1.6? To me the answer to this has NEVER been in question.\n\n\n\n\n\nNon-fuel injected cars, roller skates, and CS v1.5 worked fine right? thats why we still use them...............\n\n\n\n\n\n-Jdizzle', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166420, 25907, 1013, 102232, 1072936800, '', 'JDizzle:\n\n\n"An ELITE anti-cheat module that could be deployed (with notice), and UPDATED (without notice). "\n\n\n\n\n\nVAC was doing this before STEAM. and nodoubt continues ot do so without any interoperating with STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nKiller Koala:\n\n\n\n\n\n"The old system, they lead you to some site like fileplanet.com or fileshack.com. If you don\'t pay, which at least I don\'t, you wait for about 60mins for the download to start cause you are in a queue all day. Then you waited for a large 70MB file. Plus you are not sure which site to go to, how packed their servers are (so you can even download from there). "\n\n\n\n\n\nIts taking about 10 minutes EACH TIME to load the game, im wasting far more time than even waiting an hour every few months for a patch which was rare (usually about 20 minutes). This is basically a huge bottleneck where STEAM is concerned the bandwitdh (or lack of) is a major issue. I simply don\'t understand how you can tout it as "better than before" when even VALVe admit this.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"So you never wanted to invite your friend to play on the server you are on? Say you play on more than one particular server, how\'s your friend going to find you? or you going to find him? Use Gamespy? Use gametiger.net? Sure you could do that but Steam has it in game."\n\n\n\n\n\nIf i hear "steam has xxxxxx in game" one more time ill scream. Wowee so you can see your game running in the background, well worth the 10 minute wait to start playing. This ISNT EVEN a STEAM thing, this is just gimmikry they happen to have brought out at the same time, it could have been implemented just as easily without STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"What VGUI are you talking about? Cause there wasn\'t one with Half-Life unless it was a seperate download."\n\n\n\n\n\nVGUI was used for nearly all the menuing systems in TFC and CS after 1013.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"You are missing out..."\n\n\n\n\n\nNo ****.. I used to be able to play.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"The funny thing is if you wanted to change your options while you are alive in game, you can! No more hitting ESC to go back to the options."\n\n\n\n\n\nNo you cant!, ok so youre running around de_dust, enemy is everywhere, and you decide to get leet and change some options, you cant play whilst doing this so I fail to see the difference. You would wait until youre dead or something, in which case the old system was perfectly fine.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"How could it of been implemented in the old version? The old console was entirely text-based, windows weren\'t there. "\n\n\n\n\n\nThats the most ridiculous argument I have ever heard. Of couse it could have been bloody implemented. The old console let you run around while you were in it, the new one does not.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"Well they have, but isn\'t it better to have everything all in one easy to access spot instead of having your competition beat you."\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat competition? All in one spot? I cant even get that one spot to load properly! Are you saying I should have this much trouble loading a game I bought (given a while ago). So I can have a bloody server browser which I had already? Come on.  The server browser isnt EVEN part of what STEAM is about.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYoure simply reiterating the same old points over and over, please just either give reasons that arent about the steam gimmiky UI, I want to know about STEAM the broadand content delivery platform, and why this is so beneficial and why its to be forced on every player. Not how leet your in game dialog boxes are.\n\n\n\n\n\n"Honestly, I don\'t know what you are looking for people to say."\n\n\n\n\n\nSTEAM is needed for all players becasue xxxxxxxxxxx. You fill in the x\'s with a meaningful reason, of which you have yet to give.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166470, 25907, 1013, 102237, 1072936800, '', 'I agree wholeheartedly with RobGP\'s rhetoric.  I think the bottom line is that STEAM only provides us with services that we already had, but through an unreliable centralized application.  Granted, STEAM will eventually be reliable once the developers get all the kinks out.  The key problem I have with STEAM is its invasiveness.  By invasive, I mean STEAM is an application that is intended to run during and after you play a game session.  Most games start when you execute them, and terminate when you exit.\n\n\n\n\n\nFastforward to the paragraphs you like:\n\n\n1) Auto-updating is fine, just don\'t make us test your updates.\n\n\n2) Anti-cheat measures don\'t require a persistent, invasive service.\n\n\n3) Data validation time murders mod coders\' turnaround.\n\n\n4) The point.\n\n\n\n\n\n1)   I would personally concede that auto-updating, in general, is better than having to search for and wait "in line" to download a patch.  However, I\'ve noticed that frequent small updates tend to take the form of frequent small untested updates.  As glorifying as it would be to call myself a beta tester, I\'d prefer not to pay $10 a month for the privilage (or a $50 lump sum).  Why must auto-update be performed by an invasive application?  Couldn\'t we auto-update through a launcher like EQ or <insert random MMORPG here>?\n\n\n\n\n\n2)   Again, an application could perform cheat-detection when a client tries to connect to a registered game server.  Granted, VALVe should have a authority server that has the appropriate data to be compared, but HL could simply make the authority servers synchronize data with each game server and have the game servers check valid data among the clients.  There is no reason the anti-cheat measures must be implemented with an invasive app like STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\n3)    I\'m sorry, but if a programmer has to wait 3-5 minutes between the time that he changes code to when he can see the results, he tries to make a change to the application to reduce that turnaround time to 3-5 seconds.  Failing that, a programmer choses a different platform on which to develop.  Do you want to know the main reason that multi-platform sports game developers (SEGA, EA, etc.) decided to ditch the GameCube?  It wasn\'t just poor sales.  The GC has a turnaround time of 3-5 minutes every time you change code.  STEAM currently has a 3-5 minute turnaround.  This is God awful.\n\n\n\n\n\n4)    Well, eventually, the STEAM content servers will be so overrun with requests that VALVe will have to employ a p2p network among gamers.  A p2p network performs best when several clients participate at any given time.  What better way is there to get several gamers to participate in a p2p network than to make an application that runs during and between game sessions (qed STEAM).  Popular p2p networks provide a unique service to their users in exchange for using their bandwidth.  Generally, if I participate on a p2p network, I get to download content on my terms.  What would STEAM provide us in order to use our bandwith for content distribution?  --A friends list?  No thanks, I have 5 already.  --An auto-updater?  Thats great, but its using my pipe to work.  --The ability to play online games?  Actually, most other online games only charge $50 to play, not $50 and 50% of your upload speed.\n\n\n\n\n\n4 cont)  Perhaps we should say that STEAM, in its current implementation doesn\'t appear to be \'worth it\'.  If STEAM switches to p2p, that should remove all doubt.  Maybe we should state "STEAM doesn\'t give us enough."  Then we can ask the question "What other benefits should STEAM provide to the end user."  Lets think about that?  What is the one thing that VALVe has touted as their key asset, which is also the one thing that exists during and between game sessions?  Community.  I say that STEAM falls short by only providing a friends list and an out-of-STEAM forum.  Where are our chat-rooms?  What services can STEAM provide to support the clan community?  Tournaments?  Mod team development communication?  Fan fiction authors?  Whatever.  If we\'re gonna leave STEAM on between game sessions, provide us a real incentive.  We can give STEAM our bandwidth, but what is STEAM really gonna give us to distinguish itself from other auto-updating anti-cheat software packages?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(166540, 25907, 1013, 102232, 1072936800, '', 'I totally agree with uberdrake with everything except the fact he relates STEAM to anti cheating, so far there is no proven link between STEAM and improved anti cheat technology, as far as I know VAC was running perfectly wll before STEAM and continues to do so _alongside_ of STEAM, not an integral part of it.\n\n\n\n\n\nUnfortunatly to some users, like jdizzle and Koala, they seem to be unaware exactly what changes are actually STEAM and what are simply updates to the game engine itself, if I told you that the HL2 beta doesn\'t work with STEAM at all, yet has all the in game setting dialogs etc that the STEAM enabled HL1 has, would Koala be suprised? probably, but it just underlines the fact that the VGUI settings dialogs etc are updates the the game itself, and should not be confused with STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\n+ Nowhere has VALVe said that STEAM improves their anticheat system in any way. In fact even if it does they probably don\'t dare mention it, becasue we all know, cheaters are rampant.\n\n\n\n\n\n+ The STEAM ID system is fundamentally flawed, cheaters can reregister their cdkeys infinite times, there is no email verification etc. VALVe themselves have had their asses bitten by this as social engineering attacks have been made easy for users. (Afaik Gabe needed the password changing on the account gaben@vavlesoftware.com (mailto:gaben@vavlesoftware.com), becasue a player had registered it first)\n\n\n\n\n\n+ The in-game koala system is not part of STEAM, its a change in the engine, given some of the code is shared, but none of it could not have been implemented without STEAM\n\n\n\n\n\n+ Steam munches resources and bandwidth when no game is running - a pet hate, I have to end-task it every time I quit Half Life otherwise I experience noticable slowdown.\n\n\n\n\n\n+ Steam is still buggy software - we all know this, yet VALVe force the ENTIRE playerbase onto it without offering another migration route (i.e SteamAuth embedded in the classic client)\n\n\n\n\n\nThe only advantages I see are for VALVe, they dont have to pay publishers, they can send buggy, untested updates whenever they so choose, whtout having to inform players (which in my opinoin is a BAD thing for players, especially developers as VALVe have a history of making undocumented engine changes).\n\n\n\n\n\nBasically not one great reason has made me stand back and say, "oh yeah I never though of that, I guess STEAM hwas well though out and serves a purpose after all". VALVes silence on the matter does not fill me with confidence.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(165363, 25918, 1013, 102238, 1072936800, 'Why me!?!?!', 'Okay, When I go to log into steam, I get this Error:\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam-Error\n\n\n\n\n\nCould Not Connect To Steam Network.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis Could be due to a problem with your internet connection, or\n\n\n\n\n\nWith The Steam Network. Please Visit www.steampowered.com (http://www.steampowered.com) \n\n\n\n\n\nfor more info.\n\n\n____________________\n\n\n\n\n\nThen When I try to Create a New Account \n\n\n\n\n\nI get this error: \n\n\n\n\n\nSteamProcessCall(createaccount)failed with error 1: unknown error\n\n\n\n\n\n____________________\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is what I have done:\n\n\n\n\n\nDefragged My Computer\n\n\nRedownloaded Steam\n\n\nReinstalled Steam\n\n\nTried logging into other accounts\n\n\nRan Scandisk\n\n\nRan Virus Scan\n\n\nCussed Excessivly At My Computer\n\n\n____________________\n\n\n\n\n\nI am on the brink of formatting, But I\'d rather much not.....\n\n\nI have a Cs Server and Well, I\'d like to play on it sinces its always full now.......\n\n\n\n\n\nI have no idea whats going on, I\'ve had other people log into my accounts, \n\n\n\n\n\n___________________\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat I think may be happening\n\n\n\n\n\nI think I am missing some files....... And If I am i\'d like to know where to get them\n\n\n\n\n\nMy Steam install is The : Steaminstall_CS.exe\n\n\n\n\n\nShould I try downloading the full one?\n\n\n\n\n\n____________________\n\n\n\n\n\nMy ****** Computer Spec\'s\n\n\n\n\n\n OS: Windows 98 (4.10 - 2222) | Connection: Cable | CPU: 1-Intel P3 Celeron (Cu), 598MHz, 128KB (0% Load) | RAM 62/63MB (98.41%) | Graphics Card:  | Resolution: 800x600 16bit | \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBasically it Sucks, If you can Help me I may Reward You with admin on my server, Please respond.\n\n__________________\n\ncool.....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
