(165861, 25918, 1013, 102160, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by kev24k \n\n\nAnother noob down for the count! TY STEAM FOR WEEDING OUT THE IDIOTS!  ... hmm what an ass...\n\n\n\n\n\ndo you guys have a router? there are many conncetion problems with routers. just do a serch you should find some info.\n\n\n\n\n\nare you not using your own internet? the administrator may have blocked ports ya know.\n\n\nare you using some sort of crappy isp? maybe your internet is only allowed to acess web pages (.... welllllll maybe?... uhm nevermind)\n\n\n\n\n\nif you are having anything that may possible be blocking ports... you need these to be open\n\n\nquote:\n\n\nIf you get an error message saying that Steam cannot connect properly, please check your ports. Steam requires that your firewall have the following ports open:\n\n\n\n\n\nUDP 1200\n\n\nUDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive\n\n\nTCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive\n\n\n\n\n\nFor information about how to control your networking device to open those ports, check the documentation that came with your device or the manufacturer\'s web site.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
