(166729, 25918, 1013, 102220, 1072936800, 'I had the same problem. the fix was', 'ok, now let me tell you guys one thing. the fix I have for this (at least the one that worked for me) is for advanced computer people only and also it will only work if a router or a firewall is messing you up.  if you are running a firewall or have a router check here for a list of ports to open. /forums/...?threadid=25027 (/forums/showthread.php?threadid=25027)\n\n\n\n\n\nok. now for those just getting this error I had the same thing. what I did was uninstall CS. after the uninstall you need to go into regedit (do this by going to run and typeing regedit) go to find and type in steam. then delete all the instances of steam except the one for your download file (if you delete that one you will have to redownload) when it finds a steam referance you have to hit F3 after you delete it so it will keep looking. after it finishes searching the registry all you have to do is reboot, and then reinstall. this should help you guys out. any trouble just e-mail me or \n\n\nIM me.\n\n__________________\n\nIm bad Ash. Your good Ash. Your little goody too shoes. Little goody too shoes, ha....."BOOM"........Good, Bad, Im the guy with the gun!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
