(167408, 26425, 1013, 101793, 1072936800, 'Eating resources', 'Lateley, Steam has been eating my computers resources. I have a high end system and everything goes so **** slow. When i exit steam i goes back to normal.\n\n\n\nIts the same thing on my brothers computer.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt wasnt like this before. What happended? My Steam-monitor show nothing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167499, 26425, 1013, 102245, 1072936800, '', 'Ive been having this today too, only today (12/10/03) though.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167829, 26425, 1013, 102246, 1072936800, '', 'with the last update a nasty memory leak found it way in, the longer its open the more it takes, however a temp solution i have found is once you open up the game and everything, alt tab back and close all the windows.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167867, 26425, 1013, 100001, 1072936800, '', 'I have heard about memory leaks for ages and not to sound like a stupid n00b who knows nothing but............. what exactly is/causes a memory leak???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167898, 26425, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Shock-Front \n\nwith the last update a nasty memory leak found it way in, the longer its open the more it takes, however a temp solution i have found is once you open up the game and everything, alt tab back and close all the windows.  \n\n\n\n\n\nAlso If you open steam>games right click on counterstrike (or whatever mod) and click "create desktop shortcut". This way if you check the "remember my login", all you have to do is click the cs icon on your desktop and it will start steam and go straight into counterstrike (after the usual five minute wait >8-( ). This way you have no open steam windows, and alt-tab is not needed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167981, 26425, 1013, 102247, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by alb1221 \n\nI have heard about memory leaks for ages and not to sound like a stupid n00b who knows nothing but............. what exactly is/causes a memory leak???  \n\n\n\nI could be wrong on this, but to my understanding, a program will allocate a certian ammount of RAM for its own use.  A leak is caused when the program fails to give the ram back to the system so other programs can use it.  In turn, the ram is lost until the computer is restarted.\n\n\n\nI\'m pretty sure that\'s the basic idea, anyone else feel free to elaborate/correct me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168182, 26425, 1013, 102248, 1072936800, '', 'If you are refering to the Hard Drive grind.  Go here....\n\n\n\nwww.steampowered.com/forums/showthread.php? (/forums/showthread.php?) s=&threadid=16726&perpage=5&highlight=grind&pagenumber=1\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam will automatically check all it\'s files, after 3 incorrect shutdowns (i.e. crashes or ctrl/alt/deletes).  It may take up 15 mins depending on the size of the files and the condition of your hard drive.  Ctrl/Alt/Deleting is a waste of time, as the next time you start Steam it will start to check them from the beginning all over again.\n\n\n\nValve are aware of the problem, and are looking into an alternative solution.\n\n\n\nHope this helps', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168189, 26425, 1013, 101720, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Anxious Bob \n\nI could be wrong on this, but to my understanding, a program will allocate a certian ammount of RAM for its own use.  A leak is caused when the program fails to give the ram back to the system so other programs can use it.  In turn, the ram is lost until the computer is restarted.\n\n\n\nI\'m pretty sure that\'s the basic idea, anyone else feel free to elaborate/correct me.  \n\n\n\nGenerally they occur when a programmer allocates memory in RAM and then loses track of it somehow and thus is unable to use it again while the program runs.  The memory is then restored by the operating system when the program terminates.  The only way the memory wouldn\'t be restored is if there is a memory leak withen the os (occured a lot in the older Windows OSs).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168194, 26425, 1013, 102249, 1072936800, '', 'i love that when steam was first released they said "give us two weeks to get all the bugs/kinks worked out"... month later valve is just digging themselves into a bigger **** storm losing more and more customers. LOL!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(169793, 26425, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'Guys I have a way to reduce some of that memory that Steam might be wasting, check it out...\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=26801 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=26801)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(169799, 26425, 1013, 101720, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Zonked \n\nGuys I have a way to reduce some of that memory that Steam might be wasting, check it out...\n\n\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=26801 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=26801)  \n\n\n\nLol, there must be some really quirky coding in the Steam client.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(169804, 26425, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'Did you test it yourself? Am I just lucky or what? I mean I cant be the only one who see\'s  this huge difference.. WOW!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
