(169852, 26425, 1013, 102187, 1072936800, '', 'No kidding, this thing is fairly nasty. One good thing about Steam is valve can release small updates. The bad thing is that they may not be as well tested as when they could release patches only every few months. Ah well.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167531, 26455, 1013, 102250, 1072936800, 'Steam can go blarg it!', 'The last thing we need is another rich company thinking they are God! \n\nI am tired of it I give up.. let those in power rule I will hide in my own little house playing old lan games for the rest of my life.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167602, 26455, 1013, 102251, 1072936800, 'You may not use "BlaRG" ever again.', 'I attained the rights to say "BlaRG" in 1996. You may never use that word ever again unless you receive my express, written consent!\n\n  \n\nThat will be all. Any more infringments and I will have you slapped in the face with my friend, Mr. DMCA.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167609, 26455, 1013, 100020, 1072936800, '', 'You know whats really sad, I just brought back to life my old 500mhz, installed steam, then transferred cs gcf and a few other things, and damn first time, it worked.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167617, 26455, 1013, 102251, 1072936800, '...', 'It\'s taken me around 8 months of random testing of STEAM to finally have it working, now, 60% of the time. Excellent idea, but I still think the project, the servers, and overall amount of demand was severely underestimated. Severely. Like super-severely. Unimaginably severly, maybe? \n\n  \n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
