(167926, 26513, 1013, 100001, 1072936800, '', 'wut happened tho???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167876, 26518, 1013, 100357, 1072936800, 'Steam-thing need help', 'Out of no where Today i got this problem. When i click on counter-strike to play it gets stuck on the "preparing to play counter-strike screan and doesnt do anything. Untill this point steam was running i mean perfect. This is my 1st problem. I tryed loging out and loaging back in but i get this error.\n\nCheck it out. thx for help!\n\n[]Attachment: steam.jpg (attachment.php?s=4c45fee893d38d8ee40df261a55b5582&postid=167876)\n\nThis has been downloaded 41 time(s).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167889, 26518, 1013, 102254, 1072936800, '', 'Well first make sure there are no kids playing your computor when your not home.\n\nthis happened to me a couple of weeks ago.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167893, 26518, 1013, 100357, 1072936800, '', 'No one but me plays cs so...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167935, 26518, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve seen that error. Although I havent had it in quite a while. I\'ve heard that valve/steam is well aware of the problem, but I have yet to see any solutions or fixes, but thats to be expected. Besides they have much bigger problems than you not being able to play cs. Like making sure that their ingenious idea, which they seem so desperate to implemented in 1.6, the Shield, work proper. I mean we cant have shield going thru walls if dropped, can we? I mean do you really expect them to care about you not being able to play a game that you paid for with your hard earned money? Hey just remember how much support you got outta these guys when they ask you for your credit card.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167938, 26529, 1013, 102255, 1072936800, 'Blue Shift and Platinum Pack', 'Hey shouldn\'t Blue Shift be available to all us Platinum pack users that got a pack before Blue Shift was made?  Should this not be available via steam like Opposing Forces or Counter-Strike are?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167992, 26529, 1013, 102256, 1072936800, '', 'Blue Shift was not included in the retail Platinum Pack, so isn\'t included in the Steam one. Also, Blue Shift used a modified half life engine, and was not avaliable as a mod, which i\'ll assume is the reason it\'s not yet in Steam... Give it time, I\'m sure Blue Shift will eventually be avaliable through Steam, with the ability to apply the High-Definition packs to Half Life and Opposing Force.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(167993, 26529, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, and  at the pace that valve gets stuff done we should see it sometime before the next iceage....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168017, 26529, 1013, 102257, 1072936800, '', 'Last I heard, in a quote from an interview with Erik Johnson, Valve is working on getting both Gunman and Blue Shift into Steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168018, 26529, 1013, 102256, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, I\'d guess they are going to add it the same time they add the ability to buy CS:CZ through Steam, That way, they can also allow people who haven\'t bought it at the stores yet to buy it too through Steam, and increasing their game library', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168024, 26529, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'Sweet maybe if we are lucky Steam w/ deem all game retailers null and void. Greedy bastards just dont wanna sell their game to retailers for wholesale prices.... I mean why would they when thay can sell it straight to you at retail price and keep all the profits for themselves.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168026, 26529, 1013, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'actually, buying it through steam might be a bit cheaper, just to get people to do it, but i have to agree, getting full profit is a great idea\n\n\n\nwe should all use steam because it gets valve more money\n\nthat was NOT sarcasm or a flame, i really mean it, more money means better security and software and finally BETTER GAMES', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168029, 26529, 1013, 102258, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t think they\'ll add Gunman, cause that is not a game by valve, it\'s by Rewolf. They used the HL engine though. They\'ll probably add Blueshift, but they would have no way to tell who bought it back when it came out, or in the platinum pack, as the cd keys are the same for HL, BS, CS.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168032, 26529, 1013, 102256, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, I found the email interview where they said their adding Gunman, Blue-Shift and the HD pack:\n\n\n\n\n\nAre there any plans to support Half-Life Blue Shift through Steam? Why not?\n\n[Erik Johnson] Yes, we\'re going to look at this. There is an issue that we have to address where Blue Shift made some changes to the engine.\n\n\n\nWill you include the option for users to use High Definition Models; the new models that shipped with Half-Life Blue Shift in a High Definition Pack?\n\n[Erik Johnson] This is also something we need to deal with. I\'ll add it to our list.\n\n\n\nWill there be support for Gunman Chronicles (a forgotten Valve game that is based on HL Tech.)?\n\n[Erik Johnson] This is in the same realm as Blue Shift, but yeah, we need to get this on Steam also.\n\n\n\nRead the whole thing, it\'s the second news post down.\n\nhttp://www.planethalflife.com/news/...p;recordcount=0 (http://www.planethalflife.com/news/search.asp?function=search&advanced=1&search=gunman%2Bblue%2Bshift%2Bsteam&startmonth=6&startday=8&startyear=1996&endmonth=10&endday=12&endyear=2003&order=rankdesc&recordcount=0)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168037, 26529, 1013, 102259, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Zonked \n\nSweet maybe if we are lucky Steam w/ deem all game retailers null and void. Greedy bastards just dont wanna sell their game to retailers for wholesale prices.... I mean why would they when thay can sell it straight to you at retail price and keep all the profits for themselves. Valve is a BUSINESS. What would you do if you were in their position? In any business transaction, cutting out the middleman is always beneficial.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168039, 26529, 1013, 102259, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Comrade Cruz \n\nI don\'t think they\'ll add Gunman, cause that is not a game by valve, it\'s by Rewolf. They used the HL engine though. They\'ll probably add Blueshift, but they would have no way to tell who bought it back when it came out, or in the platinum pack, as the cd keys are the same for HL, BS, CS. Actually, I got mine in the Platinum Pack, and unless this number is something else, it does indeed have a separate CDkey.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168040, 26529, 1013, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by 007Bistromath \n\nValve is a BUSINESS. What would you do if you were in their position? In any business transaction, cutting out the middleman is always beneficial.  \n\n\n\nsee, i completely agree there, having a middleman, not including FREE middlemen, is always longer/more expensive than selling directly', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168075, 26529, 1013, 102243, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by 007Bistromath \n\nValve is a BUSINESS. What would you do if you were in their position? In any business transaction, cutting out the middleman is always beneficial.  \n\n\n\n\n\nWell lets see.. If it where my company maybe I wouldnt have waited five years to make a sequel and then try to make up my losses by jipping out retailers, hastily releasing a poorly thought out program full of bugs like Steam so that they can take your credit card numbers on their highly secure network. Oh and actually providing the paying customers w/ technical support would be a nice gesture too, considering all I see are "HELP ME" posts and not to mention the amount of people w/ plain old complaint posts about the lack of service they are being provided, all shuffled in with the countless pages of bug reports. All which seem to go unanswered by anyone representing their business. IMO Vivendi/valve/steam are primed for failiar. I\'d be curious to see what stockholders are doing w/ their share. The repeated delays, the lies in regards to how much content they actually have, and the sheer lack of support has more than proven to me that this company is hanging on by the skin of their teeth. I mean what would you call their release of DoD retail a short while back?  I\'d say it was a quick money maker to feed their bellies, considering not a whole lot of work has actually been done within the company.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168080, 26529, 1013, 102258, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, it has it\'s own cdkey, but it is the same format as hl and cs, so there is no way to tell if it is a blueshift key or not.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(168096, 26529, 1013, 102256, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Comrade Cruz \n\nYes, it has it\'s own cdkey, but it is the same format as hl and cs, so there is no way to tell if it is a blueshift key or not.  \n\n\n\nIf they were nice about it, they could do it like this: Supply one CD key, and get the Platinum Pack, supply a second one, and get Blue Shift.\n\n\n\nThis would be really nice to loyal customers who bought Half-Life and CS retail (either out of stupidity or kindness) and have 2 keys as a result, get a bonus Blue Shift.\n\n\n\nI\'m already stoked that I have the Platinum Pack thanks to Steam, I only ever bought Half-Life: Game of the Year edition, and now they have essentially thrown me Opposing Force for free. I\'m going to wait until Blue Shift is avaliable on Steam, and then, depending on what\'s easiest, I\'ll get it. (wether it be retail or through Steam) I know the story is really short, I just want the High-Definition Pack.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174850, 27611, 1013, 102260, 1072936800, 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', 'I have been dealing with Steam for awhile now, & have a major concern about their Log In system that seems to be bound to your CS key.\n\n\n\nAt first, it was a little annoying, but then I heard it could be used to set all your personal controls simply by creating your own login name may have made it worth it.  \n\n\n\nBUT: Then I notice it asks for you CD key.  This is where the problem comes in.  If you for example let your friend make an account with steam, & pull out you CD key when it asks you, you in effect are giving your buddy your CD for free.\n\n\n\nSo now, when your friend goes home to play counterstrike & gets all logged in as he normally would, he is now playing on YOUR CD Key.  Meaning you would not be able to play until he is finished & logs out.\n\n\n\nStill:  Don\'t forget that steam set it up to auto load at windows startup as well as auto log you in, so your friend may actually have your CD key used up for quite some time.\n\n\n\nI did go back and look for info of steam telling us of this issue, but so NO info warning us when creating accounts.  \n\n\n\nThanks for the bonus Steam  []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174862, 27611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'OK, this one is easy:\n\n\n\n- don\'t give people your CD key\n\n\n\n- if you do, ask them not to create a Steam account with it.\n\n\n\n- if they do, ask them to hand that account over to you (change the password to something boring, then you log in and change it to your own). It will have the "wrong" email address as the account name, but that doesn\'t really matter.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174881, 27611, 1013, 102260, 1072936800, 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', 'I hear you, but that�s kind of weak.  Why should you be afraid of entering your OWN CD Key on your OWN Computer?  \n\n\n\nSteam has no warning letting you know that the Key goes with the login name.  Something, ANYTHING to let us know what the account will carry with it.\n\n\n\nI have played CS from the very first beta, and never have we had this issue.  We have had to enter in our CD key with every beta & non-beta so far.  \n\n\n\nI thought it was natural when I let a friend play CS v1.6 on my computer before I did.  Then I created me an account and played.  Never did I realize what had just happened.\n\n\n\nIt\'s not like I gave my Key to someone else on purpose.  It\'s my computer.  I didn\'t see the problem.\n\n\n\nStill:  Steam took no time to let us know what it was doing with the key or accounts.\n\n\n\nThanks for the bonus Steam!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174890, 27611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'Sorry, I didn\'t realized he\'d created the account on your computer.\n\n\n\nDid you create your account first? if so, then you\'ll "own" that cd-key, and eventually his subscription will get canceled.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174897, 27611, 1013, 102261, 1072936800, '', 'If you already had an account on your computer then went to your friends house there is no reason for cd key.\n\nAfter install you just log in instead of creating an account.\n\nIf he already had steam you could just log in too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174899, 27611, 1013, 102260, 1072936800, 'Is Steam Helping You Give Your Own CD Key Away???', 'I thought I covered that...\n\n\n\nI let him play first.  Thats why it seemed so normal to enter in my CD key on my computer when it asked for it.  \n\n\n\nSteam took no measures to let us know of the changes they made to our game.  I repeat, Steam said NOTHING about it.\n\n\n\nTo make things worse, I have 20 Half-Life CD\'s for my home Lan set-up.  Now I have NO idea what CD Keys I let out by mistake, vs what ones I caught before letting friends create their own account.  Your new login system has put me in a real bad situation.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(174912, 27611, 1013, 102260, 1072936800, 'American Zombie Reply', '{ If you already had an account on your computer then went to your friends house there is no reason for CD key. After install you just log in instead of creating an account. If he already had steam you could just log in too. }\n\n\n\nWell I�m glad someone is happy with Steam.  In my area, you would be rare.  That is not how it worked on my computers.  \n\n\n\nPlus:  How long does it take to log out of your steam so someone else can login on your computer?\n\n\n\nYikes....\n\n\n\nThen you ad "game not available msg" after logging in.  You find yourself repeating the same thing again...  Usually ending up reinstalling before your done.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(175149, 27611, 1013, 102262, 1072936800, 'Lol, everything i hear gets worse', 'Yeah theres a point thats probably more worrying. About 500,000 folk using KEY GENERATORS, thats gonna be crazy. If i cant get playing cause some ****wits using my number i\'ll be ****ing at STEAM\'S door with my CD box to attack the development team. \n\n\n\nI hate this software so much, wont even install in my comp after 4 downloads at about 1.72GB (3* 340 MB + 700 MB) and when u goto the SUPPORT PAGE you find ****e like "IS STEAM REALLY FREE?" and "WILL I STILL BE ABLE TO BUY VALVE GAMES IN-STORE?" ****ing no real help to anyone. Only people keeping this software afloat are the folk in the forums helping each other figure out this pish.\n\n\n\nHopefully they\'ll fix this KEY issue but i wont hold my breathe, better off with monkeys on roller blades designing the software.\n\n\n\nAzraels_Fury........', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(175730, 27611, 1013, 102263, 1072936800, '', 'a warning would have been nice regardless, however I do not see this as an issue...\n\nI had someone test my account recently, since I havent been able to login for weeks... ooh it just updated and is working.\n\nthank you valve [] I missed my steam terribly much', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(175768, 27611, 1013, 102264, 1072936800, 'here is my answer to Steam!', 'I can not sit still and remain calm about this. \n\nAs myclan and friends all know I have the patients of a rock, but they have broken me. \n\n\n\nSome people are not going to want to here this. But You must!!!!!!!!!!! \n\n\n\nI have just tested something I heard from a veteran server operator/owner/admin about STEAM! \n\nThey say that this is the software that will be hooking us together weather we like it or not. \n\nI call there bluff. If we the server owners don\'t act now we will have no more game to serve. \n\n\n\nIt has been brought to my attention that the STEAM id\'s. The ID that you use to ban some jerk/cheater/sexualoffender is not \n\ngenerated by your HL cd key. It is generated by your EMAIL address you give steam. So this evening I took about 15 min \n\nand made 5 emails with hotmail.com. Then Entered my server and banned myself. \n\nExit server and log out of STEAM. Then Logged back in to steam under one of my 5 new email addy and \n\nre-entered the server no problem. If I was a Lawyer I would say rest my case but I am not finished. \n\n\n\n\n\nMy patients have now turned to a new cause. \n\n\n\nAfter adding up roughly how much money I have spent to bring this game to people as a server host "$9000 range" \n\n250,000 people bying HL added up to 10 million dollars valve has made of us. \n\nI am going to dedicate my time to stopping steam before they ruin our game we love. \n\n\n\nWe need to stand together. I recommend that you do what ever it takes to get your servers back to 1.5 \n\n\n\nIf we go back and most steam servers disappear they will hear are cry!!!! I count about 400 tfc servers. \n\nI see around 30000 people all togather allready switched. Can they fix that many id\'s? \n\n\n\nDo you think they will do something or not. \n\nIf the servers go back what can they do. \n\n\n\nThey may change alot of ways but I only four see more trouble as they try to pull out of this one. \n\nAs a client you may not see the importance of this, but as a server admin/owner this is cause for alarm. \n\n\n\nWith mygot alone on the prowl to crash servers and harm your stuff we are un protected as server owners.. \n\n\n\nI am not finished here I will send more to help get the word out. \n\nTalk to server admins of the servers you play on. Let them know.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(175927, 27611, 1013, 100517, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, and there are lots of people that have pirated half-life with cd-key (and that cd-key can be your own cd-key). Or they can create a cd-key with those stupid hacker programs that amke auto cdkey for half-life (and that also can match up your cd key). I know myself...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(175996, 27611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'smklizard -\n\n\n\nOne CD-Key can only be used ONCE - with one Steam account (Steam ID). There is a TEMPORARY situation with Steam right now, allowing all those duplicate accounts to function. We\'ve started working on the backlog, and eventually all of those accounts will be unsubscribed from the games. Only the first account to use a CD-Key will be able to play. Ban that account, and they will stay banned.\n\n\n\nThis is, in fact, the whole crux of the problem that TheWorx brought up (we need to make it more obvious that it\'s pulling your Cd-key from the registry). So, I\'m sorry you\'re so upset but don\'t worry as your concerns are rather groundless.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(176187, 27611, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'i may have not understud your story exactly but i\'ll tell you the LAW!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nThe law states that a licence you buy must be installed only on 1 computer or may be installed on multiple computers as long as only 1 copy of the software is running at one time.\n\n\n\nThats the law. Now i dont know why your installing the CD on another person\'s PC but you shouldn\'t.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(176689, 27611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Catch_ME \n\ni may have not understud your story exactly but i\'ll tell you the LAW!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nThe law states that a licence you buy must be installed only on 1 computer or may be installed on multiple computers as long as only 1 copy of the software is running at one time.\n\n\n\nThats the law. Now i dont know why your installing the CD on another person\'s PC but you shouldn\'t.  \n\n\n\nThere\'s no law that says that. What you\'re talking about is what an End-User License Agreement might say. The agreement is written by the company that sells the software. Mostly, that is typical of what a EULA says.\n\n\n\n"The Law" basically just says: as that\'s a contract, you are legally bound by it if you accept it.\n\n\n\nAnyway - I\'m not saying that the HL etc EULAs do or don\'t say that (sorry I\'m a coder not a lawyer), but I thought I would clear that point up.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(176701, 27611, 1013, 102265, 1072936800, '', 'Taylo, off-topic question ... Will there be a steam user database cleanup where all accounts get deleted and every cd-key can only be used once ? Because now, even me having a valid cd-key form HL Platinum Pack having bought it sealed in Shop, never giving my Key out, i sometimes get locked out of CS or HL due to the "Key in use" error. \n\n\n\nI can only think of one explanation: Key-Gen that per accident threw out my cd-key and someone else is using it now ... \n\n\n\nIn addition, will you give us a possibility to dlete our own acount ... I have two account for example, from the beta, where someone told me that a second account would fix some error. Its useless and can be deleted. But i cant do that and i would like to. Would be in your interest, to keep the database nice n\' small.\n\n\n\nNoVa', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(178492, 28298, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, 'No CZero or other leak posts please', 'Please, no links to CZero downloads, installer zips for models, or anything like that for CZero stuff ok?  As you probably know, anything someone\'s giving out is from leaked stuff and not legit at all.\n\n\n\nAlso a reminder of the policy on this sit that basically no tolerance for linking to, etc. the leaked stuff.   "No tolerance" translates as "ban" by the way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180696, 28740, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, 'Whiner-Operated Network.', 'If you hate steam:\n\n\n\nGO BACK TO WON.\n\n\n\nIf you hate 1.6:\n\n\n\nGO BACK TO WON.\n\n\n\nIf you hate shields:\n\n\n\nGO BACK TO WON.\n\n\n\n/index.p...382375772523900 (/index.php?area=news&archive=yes&id=106382375772523900)\n\n\n\nWON is still up.  Steam is still being worked on.  Steam will eventually fix all these stupid bugs like the CPU usage and such.\n\n\n\nYou have absolutely no right to complain about steam, whine how much WON is better, and then keep playing on steam.\n\n\n\nWON is there for your amusement.  Everyone just go back to WON and leave the mature, patient players to CS 1.6 and steam.\n\n\n\n\n\nReally.  I mean it.  All you stupid little brats whining about your 1.5 being gone...it\'s not.  Go back and play it.  It\'ll make all the CS 1.6 games I play include better, mature players.\n\n\n\nYou\'ve already got your stupid little \'elite\' low steamID number, ready and waiting for when you return after all the steam bugs are fixed.\n\n\n\nSeriously.  Go the heck away.\n\n\n\nNow.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by MaxDamagel33t \n\nTo all the people who refuse to go back to WON because they claim it\'ll be shut down anyhow:\n\n\n\nDo you refuse to eat hot food because it may get cold later? If so, then at least you\'re being consistent in your logic. If you\'ve paid ANY attention to what\'s going on, you\'ll know that Valve have stated that WON will stay up until Steam is ready to fully support the community.\n\n\n\nUntil then, if you hate Steam, DON\'T F\'ING USE IT! Simple as that. It\'s not brain surgery. You\'re being given a choice - the developers say you have a choice. You people are acting like you\'re being bundled into game-concentration camps at gunpoint and Steamed to death!\n\n\n\nThese forums are proof that people have way too much time on their hands, and that some people just get off being jackasses. If you have the clear option to go back to WON, and choose not to do so, then you have no right to whine about Steam either. Refusing to go back to WON and persisting to whine about something that you have the full option not to use is not only counterproductive, but fantastically childish.\n\n\n\nThe only half-reasonable excuse I can think of is that if you installed Steam (which recovered your old CD key), foolishly deleted your old HL directory, and then threw out your old half-life disc because you won\'t need it due to Steam.\n\n\n\nThe chances of that happening are about a billion to one, but we all know that somone out there is stupid enough to do it.\n\n\n\nEinstein was right.\n\n"Two things are infinite: the universe and human stupidity; and I\'m not sure about the universe."', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180710, 28740, 1013, 102275, 1072936800, '', 'haha, putting up with this rediculous mess, doesnt make someone more "mature". lets face iit, for now Steam is a pile of dog feces. until it works like it should we shall complain all we want.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180713, 28740, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by dRh4x \n\nhaha, putting up with this rediculous mess, doesnt make someone more "mature". lets face iit, for now Steam is a pile of dog feces. until it works like it should we shall complain all we want. \n\n\n\nGo away, whiner.\n\n\n\n#1:  Are you paying for steam?  No.\n\n\n\n#2:  Are you paying for steam?  No.\n\n\n\n#3:  Are you paying for steam?  No.\n\n\n\n#4: Are you forced to use steam?  No.\n\n\n\n#5:  Is someone smacking you over the head with a spiked club every time you use WON instead of steam?  No.\n\n\n\n#6: Go the heck away you loser whining flaming brainless git.  Play WON and get out of here.  I am sick and tired of all the useless steam-hating crap that goes on in these forums, when there is absolutely no point, and you could all be playing \'the perfect 1.5\' right this very second.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180717, 28740, 1013, 102146, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Go the heck away you loser whining flaming brainless git.\n\n\n\nDid I mistakenly read the word "mature" somewhere in there?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180725, 28740, 1013, 102261, 1072936800, '', 'Really no reason to call everyone who posts here whiners.\n\nSome of the people who post here (not me) do not have big hard drives so when they installed steam they had to delete their Sierra installs.\n\nNow they have just Steam to play on and can not go back unless they uninstall steam, reinstall previous games to Sierra folder and get all the patches to get it back up to 1.1.1.0 again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180727, 28740, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Epos Nix \n\nDid I mistakenly read the word "mature" somewhere in there? \n\n\n\nSorry, frustrated.  I didn\'t even make a complete sentence, so you can obviously see I was frustrated.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180728, 28740, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by American Zombie \n\nReally no reason to call everyone who posts here whiners.\n\nSome of the people who post here (not me) do not have big hard drives so when they installed steam they had to delete their Sierra installs.\n\nNow they have just Steam to play on and can not go back unless they uninstall steam, reinstall previous games to Sierra folder and get all the patches to get it back up to 1.1.1.0 again. \n\n\n\nThen they should do it and stop the useless drivel.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180734, 28740, 1013, 100684, 1072936800, '', 'This is really a mess tho. The new patch I thought was awsome. Chopped the loading time in half. Then they recalled it, ok no prob. Then it screwed my cs, hrm... no good. I had to reinstall, so did most other people. I have no problems with the updates, but reversing an update that screws steam... comon guys...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180740, 28740, 1013, 100443, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ixon \n\nThis is really a mess tho. The new patch I thought was awsome. Chopped the loading time in half. Then they recalled it, ok no prob. Then it screwed my cs, hrm... no good. I had to reinstall, so did most other people. I have no problems with the updates, but reversing an update that screws steam... comon guys... \n\n\n\nThe new patch had already screwed steam.  They recalled it so that anyone who hadn\'t downloaded the new patch yet would not be screwed.  They also did this very quickly, same day in fact.\n\n\n\nAnd the recall means you have to re-download.\n\n\n\nI suggest everyone heads back to fileshack and download the steam+cs installer, then patch it back from there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(180763, 28740, 1013, 102276, 1072936800, '', 'well suggest all u want.\n\ni suggest that steam get their **** together before the mass-update everyone with ****ing files that are not needed.\n\nand regardless of the fact that they screwed everyperson that just happened to open steam today, they dont even have the goddam nut to get enough ****ing server space to let everyone re-download what is necessary?\n\n\n\nsteam has been ****ed for 6 hours now. i have tried d/ing 4 times. and i still have 132min remaining.\n\n\n\n**** ALL STEAM PERSONEL.\n\nAND YOUR MOMMA\'S!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nnah, im just playing.    it does suck that i cant play tonite tho', '127.0.0.1', 1),
