(182139, 28746, 1013, 100684, 1072936800, '', 'Cookies!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(181025, 28788, 1013, 103410, 1072936800, 'Is there a definite fix the update problem?', 'Ok, Ive been scouring all the posts looking for away to get steam(half life, counterstrike etc ) working again.  Some post say to reinstall but the next will say that doesnt even work.\n\n\n\nDoes anyone know what we are really supposed to do to remedy this problem.  Steams news page was anything but specific about what to do.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(181125, 28788, 1013, 101152, 1072936800, '', 'I hear ya I can\'t get it to work either after last update. I tried reinstalling the whole thing again after the 700 mb download yet notta still stuck. I feel as If I\'m back at the very first day I installed steam non-beta. \n\n\n\nSeems like even though I got the steam installer with all games that it is trying to update all games from scratch.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(181156, 28788, 1013, 103410, 1072936800, 'fixed', 'Okay I got it working again.  Here is what i tried and here is what worked.\n\n\n\nI first tried to repair the installaion with the uninstall wizard, no luck, then i figured f it.  I uninstalled steam by itself, and then reinstalled the 723mb file.  Ran steam, it updated itself in minutes.\n\nFirst try didnt work, but then after a reboot all is well.  \n\n\n\nSide note:  I think this method will only work based upon the settings you chose when you installed steam in the first place.  \n\n\n\nI have noticed that i can no longer play half life (or locate its executable for that matter ) \n\nI tried the same method above on another computer on my network and it didnt work.  But on that computer the half life exacutable is still visible and he can still play 1.5.  I think its all hinged on your first install of steam and the option of leaving the file system intact or caching it ( i think those were the options ) \n\nbut i cant remember what i chose.  \n\n\n\nHope this is of some help to anyone.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.clanlebowski.com (http://www.clanlebowski.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185313, 29475, 1013, 102281, 1072936800, '', 'no news updates? well not on the DoD site, but if you look around you can find some info\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php...amp;news_id=245 (http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php?page=common/news.php&news_action=showitem&news_id=245)\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php...amp;news_id=254 (http://www.dodnetwork.com/index.php?page=common/news.php&news_action=showitem&news_id=254)\n\n\n\n\n\nI think it\'s coming out after the huge CZ load is over on Steam.-\n\n__________________\n\nFLeK0\n\n\nwww.Counter-Strike.hu', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185319, 29475, 1013, 102282, 1072936800, '', 'What\'s wrong with 1.0 anyway? Retail DoD is an above average WW2 shooter at best. When 1.1 comes out we will hear the usual "this release killed DoD" like with every new version. Mark my words. Learn to be patient and respect the devs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185320, 29475, 1013, 102283, 1072936800, '', 'Interacting with the community is a rather time consuming\n\n\n(and ever so often an ungrateful) job.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m very happy that they rather keep working on improving\n\n\ntheir products and stomping bugs than making a daily Q&A\n\n\nsession with the fans.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'m not saying that I don\'t understand the frustration this\n\n\nsituation causes in some of us, I\'m just saying that I\'m\n\n\ntrying to understand Valve\'s point of view as well.\n\n\n\n\n\nI am very sure that  they are working their asses off to get\n\n\nthings done as soon as possible and that they are as\n\n\nunhappy about setbacks and delays as much as we\n\n\nare (if not even moreso).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185340, 29475, 1013, 102284, 1072936800, '', 'I think half the problem is that the DOD team themselves don\'t even know when it\'s coming out. Every time Steam seems to stabilise, a new patch comes out that de-stabilises it. Steams a great concept, just needs a bit more beta testing to get it right.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve decided to just go play other games for the time being, and come back when Steam is stable and 1.1 has been released. I\'m only an occasional gamer anyway, so I can live with it.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Kiff \n\n\nGuys, don\'t take his bait. I made the mistake of doing it.\n\n\n\n\n\nIgnore him. \n\n\n\n\n\nI bit over on the DOD forums a while ago as well. The guys just a confrontational muppet with nothing better to do than be abusive to anyone and everyone about anything. Perhaps he should take his own advice and get out a bit more.\n\n\n\n\n\nOops, bit again []\n\n\n\n\n\nThank god for the ignore feature on these forums, only time I see his posts is if someone quotes him []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185348, 29475, 1013, 102285, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Funka J \n\n\nWhat\'s wrong with 1.0 anyway? Retail DoD is an above average WW2 shooter at best. When 1.1 comes out we will hear the usual "this release killed DoD" like with every new version. Mark my words. Learn to be patient and respect the devs.  \n\n\n\n\n\nThere are loads of major bugs in 1.0 that should have to been fixed ages ago. The most annoying to me is the hitbox problems. I guess you can\'t have played Dod much if you haven\'t seen the many bugs in the game. As for being patient I\'m willing to be patient if I knew why I was waiting. As far as I can understand from the dod website 1.1 has been finished months, and therefore there is no reason to delay it any longer.\n\n\n\n\n\nAll Valve have to do is give the Dod community a statement regarding the status of 1.1 and when its going to be released, and then the majority of ppl complaing about where 1.1 is, would sit and patiently wait for it. Its a simple thing that would take them less than 5 seconds, and keep many ppl happy. At least then I wouldn\'t feel Valve are just ignoring Dod', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185349, 29475, 1013, 102286, 1072936800, '', 'Fleko, if U notice the latest news U linked is from 10.10. it\'s 2 weeks since "very soon" Waldo statement. He was supposed to have a meeting after that statement with Valve t omake them release the patch at once. No info from him since then.\n\n\nlack of info in front of "very soon" release of the patch is confusing.\n\n\nSince 1.0  changed the way dod was before (in a good direction if U ask me) the game occured unbalanced.  Kar is overpowered, garand to weak and MGs lost any functionality, since walls became to difficult to penetrate.  Add the screwed up hitboxes and U will find out why the patch is needed so bad. For several months for now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185353, 29475, 1013, 100059, 1072936800, 'Day of Defeat 1.1 - A plea to Valve', 'quote:Originally posted by Kiff \n\n\nWe were informed by development team members back in August that the patch was finished but needed testing from Activision. A mid September release date looked promising. It was not to be.\n\n\n\n\n\n The problem is, with the recent stolen source issue activision has been locked out for testing[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185369, 29475, 1013, 100048, 1072936800, 'Re: Day of Defeat 1.1 - A plea to Valve', 'quote:Originally posted by Intrepid00 \n\n\nThe problem is, with the recent stolen source issue activision has been locked out for testing[] \n\n\nYep []\n\n\n\n\n\nUnfortunately this was part of the reason it was delayed. But since the hacker attack Steam updates to CS and TFC have been released. So clearly Valve are confident that the network is secure.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185370, 29475, 1013, 100059, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, but CS and TFC are fully in house. Activision does not come to Valve to test. They go through the Internet.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185373, 29475, 1013, 100048, 1072936800, '', 'Oh yeah. Sorry about that []\n\n\n\n\n\nI wish Dod was tested in house.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185377, 29475, 1013, 102282, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Samson \n\n\nI bit over on the DOD forums a while ago as well. The guys just a confrontational muppet with nothing better to do than be abusive to anyone and everyone about anything.   \n\n\n\n\n\nAccording to this ignorant poster, abusive means "proving you wrong".\n\n\n\n\n\nPeople that have me on the ignore function are testemant to the fact I tell the truth and that most people can\'t accept it. In a way when people ignore me it makes me feel good, because I know I\'ve proved another useless bigot wrong. You could say I\'m having a good time here []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185425, 29475, 1013, 102287, 1072936800, '', 'No ppl will accept something thats true. most ppl have u on ignore cos ur an annoying little bugger.\n\n\nquote:OOh dear they won\'t release 1.1!!!!!!!!! VALVE SCREWED UP!!!! DISGRACE!!!! CALL THE POLICE!!!!!!\n\n\nTheres an example of u not exactly acting as mature as u reckon u r.\n\n__________________\n\nPiro: when did Tsubasa get a cable modem?\n\n\nLargo: Sometime this morning. You should proberly tell him about it\n\n\n\n\n\nPH33R MegaTokyo. It ownz j0o f00lz', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185453, 29475, 1013, 102282, 1072936800, '', 'No maturity necessary for a thread which slags off the Valve team for not releasing DoD before breakfast.\n\n\n\n\n\nOh and why is it that I have to prove to you that if a person isn\'t acting mature 24 hours a day, they are immature? I honestly don\'t give a flying flippidy-flop what anonymous posters think of me, much less ones such as yourself.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185478, 29475, 1013, 100548, 1072936800, '', 'Here\'s what I\'m confident on as of yesterday:\n\n\n\n\n\n1) Base 1.1 testing is done and final code work implemented.\n\n\n2) 1.1 will be a small release...dll\'s and some player models.  \n\n\n3) Reworked maps will come later.\n\n\n4) There\'s at least one new map (dod_switch) but I\'m not sure if it\'s in the 1.1 release itself...it might be part of the post-release map-release period stated in 3 above.\n\n\n5) Release is imminent except for the following unknowns:\n\n\n\n\n\n    A) If the aborted Steam release is required\n\n\n    B) If a new HL.exe is required.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf either of those two are required then all bets are off \n\n\n\n\n\nA big caution:  Although DoD 1.1 changes things I caution you not to think this is as radical a change as we\'ve had in the past...a lot of the changes (other than the VGUI) are invisible for the most part and do not surface until you\'ve played for a while.  You\'ll eventually notice the player models "move" a bit differently now that 9-way animation has been implemented and you\'ll obviously see more deaths in the game now w/the hitbox, MG, wall penetration, and Kar movement-accuracy changes.  I look at a lot of these changes to be more tweeks than bug-fixes. The majority of the actual "bug-fixes" will come when the re-worked maps are released.  And I have not heard of any great fps increase other than the fix to the rain...I do not know what Valve-proper is working on w/respect to figuring out why the mask-technology models (grass, tanks, etc) cause fps drops.\n\n\n\n\n\nSince the plan of a few days ago (could have changed since then for all I know) was not to include any maps yet I think a lot of folks will say "What\'s the big deal?" when it\'s released...the hard-core DoD guys will notice things but newer players might not notice that much beyond the interface and the MG cook-off sequence. This is truly a evolutionary release...not revolutionary.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(185483, 29475, 1013, 100818, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m with you, Kiff.\n\n__________________\n\nProud Member of The [Idioteam] DoD squad.\n\n\nFeel free to embrace the Brown Side of DoD, Join [Idioteam]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186055, 29611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'If Steam asks for your CD-KEY again', 'The Steam system has begun filtering through accounts that used duplicate cd-keys to subscribe to the games. When it finds a duplicate, it unsubscribes but does not delete that account. Only the first account which used a given cd-key will remain subscribed.\n\n\n\nIf you are using one of the duplicate accounts, you\'ll see the games get moved to Available Games in the Games window, and Steam will ask you for your cd-key again if you try to play one. \n\n\n\nIf you created multiple Steam accounts using the same key, then you\'ll need to use the first one.\n\n\n\nrepeat: the first account to use a given cd-key will REMAIN subscribed and can be used to play the games.\n\n\n\nThe system will not automatically delete any accounts.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186091, 29611, 1013, 102288, 1072936800, '', 'Well that sucks. What are people supposed to do when two people use the same computer...I thought steam would be good cause it would be like two seperate accounts for me and my brother...But now its just f*cked... I just wanted to play the agme everyonce and a while....not every person who plays the game is a computer genious so keep it simple....thanks for making rainy days boringer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186128, 29611, 1013, 102247, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m hoping that in the future, you will be able to change your email address, but keep the same account (friends list, server favorites, etc.)  My inbox is becomming increasingly spammed, so i created a new email.  the only thing keeping me from deleting the old email account is steam.\n\nI just want to know how far away this feature, being able to change your email address, is from being implimented, assuming it is going to be eventually.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186232, 29611, 1013, 100799, 1072936800, '', 'spam\'s irrelevant with things like popfile\n\nhttp://sourceforge.net/projects/popfile (http://sourceforge.net/projects/popfile)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186284, 29611, 1013, 102289, 1072936800, '', 'Can we have the option to delete accounts?\n\n\n\nThe first account I created(I\'m not even sure which cd-key it uses since I never had to enter one because it copied my existing hl installation) I do not use. I decided I\'d rather use another email, so I created another.\n\n\n\nFortunately for me I have 3 cd-keys because I got the halflife platinum pack.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186377, 29611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'The email address used to create your Steam account will only be used for sending "sorry, your cd-key is in use" emails. \n\n\n\nSo - there\'s no real need to delete an account or change the email address on one right now. You may continue to use the Steam account even if you no longer have an email account at that address, without problems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186434, 29611, 1013, 102290, 1072936800, 'jus wanna know', 'just a little off topic but does or will steam be selling cd-keys???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186662, 29611, 1013, 102291, 1072936800, '', 'Aw crap.  I was letting my cousin use my cd-key to play cs (I wasn\'t using it).  But, now I\'ve started playing again, but he\'s already created a steam account.  Is there any way at all that he can deactivate it so I can create my account?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186894, 29611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'SayOne: yep - sort of. You\'ll be able to buy games on Steam (CS:CZ next month) - but since there\'s no need you won\'t get a cd-key. Your account will become subscribed to that game, that\'s all that\'s needed.\n\n\n\nSolowing: easiest thing right now is to just ask him to hand that Steam account over to you. It won\'t matter much that it\'s the wrong email address for you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(187974, 29611, 1013, 100794, 1072936800, '', 'if you have the hl patinum pack can i use the cd key form CS for one account and the cdkey from Halflife for another ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188003, 29611, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by TRANCE \n\nif you have the hl patinum pack can i use the cd key form CS for one account and the cdkey from Halflife for another ?  \n\n\n\nYes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188662, 29611, 1013, 102292, 1072936800, '', 'i origanlilly bough 2 half-life\'s with 2 cd keys . \n\n1 of my account it working perfect , on the other hand my other cd key is not because i made like 5accounts with it becasuse on my other comp i get the create account login crash on steam but early i never knew about the cd key dublicated thingy so now i got screwed over gg steam. and i forget which account/pw i made first but if i get steam all the emails i used with the cd key i bought will steam be able to give me a chance', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188973, 29611, 1013, 102293, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m getting this mail. I have the original her so what can i do? \n\nis my id getting shuttdown if the outer person ho don\'t have the original registered his first???\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam has detected that your copy of Half-Life Platinum Pack has already been \n\nregistered to another Steam user. Your product\'s CD-Key (the number printed on \n\nthe CD case which you were asked to type in after installing the game) matches \n\none already in our database. \n\n\n\nThe CD-Key you entered is: ************* \n\n\n\nYou will not be able to play Half-Life Platinum Pack unless you provide an \n\nunclaimed CD-Key. To provide an unclaimed CD-Key, you will need a copy of \n\nHalf-Life Platinum Pack which has not already been registered on Steam. \n\nDouble-click on the name of the game in Steam\'s "Games" window and then follow \n\nthe given instructions.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190251, 29611, 1013, 102294, 1072936800, '', 'hello every one \n\n\n\nI\'m pretty angry because i bought half life and now it tells me that my key is already used. I PAID for this game, so i think i\'m allowed to play... is there any solution to delete the account of the guy who stole my key to enable the activation of my account ??\n\ni\'v sent an email to support@steampowered.com (mailto:support@steampowered.com) but there is still no answer\n\n\n\nC U', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190294, 29611, 1013, 102295, 1072936800, '', 'It should be like this .... the cdkey makes the account ... and the email is just a cover up so nobody can see your cdkey ... and if the key is your account you should be able to change all the info on that "cdkey account" ... if you have the password ...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186963, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, 'FATAL ERROR (shutting down): File read failure', 'quote:\n\n[lambda@dorm213-155 lambda]$ su root\n\nPassword:\n\n[root@dorm213-155 lambda]# cd /\n\n[root@dorm213-155 /]# cd usr/steam/hlds_l\n\n[root@dorm213-155 hlds_l]# ./hlds_run -debug -game ns +port 27030 +maxplayers 12 +map ns_eclipse\n\nAuto detecting CPU\n\nUsing Pentium II Optimised binary.\n\nEnabling debug mode\n\n./hlds_run: line 1: gdb: command not found\n\nPlease install gdb first.\n\ngoto http://www.gnu.org/software/gdb/ (http://www.gnu.org/software/gdb/)\n\nAuto-restarting the server on crash\n\n\n\nConsole initialized.\n\nscandir failed:/usr/steam/hlds_l/./platform/SAVE\n\nProtocol version 46\n\nExe version 1.1.2.0/Stdio (valve)\n\nExe build: 16:27:22 Oct 13 2003 (2545)\n\ncouldn\'t exec language.cfg\n\nServer IP address 155.31.213.155:27030\n\n\n\n   Metamod version 1.16.2  Copyright (c) 2001-2003 Will Day <willday@metamod.org>\n\n   Metamod comes with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY; for details type `meta gpl\'.\n\n   This is free software, and you are welcome to redistribute it\n\n   under certain conditions; type `meta gpl\' for details.\n\n\n\nscandir failed:/usr/steam/hlds_l/./platform/SAVE\n\nFATAL ERROR (shutting down): File read failure\n\nAdd "-debug" to the ./hlds_run command line to generate a debug.log to help with solving this problem\n\nSat Oct 25 04:17:26 EDT 2003: Server restart in 10 seconds\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd I\'m activating hlds_run with this: \n\n\n\ncode:\n#!/bin/sh\ncd /usr/steam/hlds_l\necho `date` >> lognsserverstartup.txt\nsleep 1\necho "now starting the server"\nsleep 1\n./hlds_run -debug -pingboost 1 -game ns \\\n+maxplayers 18 +map ns_eclipse +port 27017 -debug\n\n\n\n\nSo I got my CS 1.6 Linux server w/amx mod running like a champ, but I added an ns server w/amx and everytime I try to run it it gives me this error and then restarts continuously. I know that AMX mod and Metamod are not the problem, because I set the "liblist.gam" back to "dll/ns_i386.so" and it gave me the same error. Not to mention you can see that Metamod loads in the quote above. \n\n\n\nI downloaded GDB in some fruitless attempt to "debug" the problem, but that is beyond me. Does anyone have any ideas?\n\n\n\nbeen working on this server for the last two days stright... lol\n\n-Rick\n\n\n\n****I edited this msg and added the above 2nd quote at 10:33am on Octover 25th, 2003****', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(186977, 29745, 1026, 102297, 1072936800, '', 'chmod -Rv 777 ? maybe?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(187239, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, '', 'Destro I\'m still learning Linux, all the stuff I did with that CS server I learned with FAQs and by searching through 3 forum communities, not because I know alot about linux . \n\n\n\nquote: chmod -Rv 777 \n\n\n\nI\'m prolly not gona have a Linux for dummies book till next week so could I ask What does the -Rv standfor?\n\n\n\nRespectfully\n\n-Rick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(187355, 29745, 1026, 100453, 1072936800, '', 'first get gdb(only way debugging will work).  it should be a package for your distro. then start hlds with this command.\n\n\n\n./hlds_run -debug -game ns +port 27030 -debug \n\n\n\nanother thing to try is remove metamod if you have a plugin that\'s really messed up it could be crashing the server.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(187913, 29745, 1026, 102297, 1072936800, '', '-Rv make the command recursive (affects the directory and all within) (R) and verbose (v).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188013, 29745, 1026, 100453, 1072936800, '', 'it\'s being run as root so it does not matter', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188080, 29745, 1026, 102298, 1072936800, '', 'fyi, whenever in doubt about a particular command someone tells you to use, simply type man command.\n\n\n\ni.e. man chmod. It will show you the manual pages on the command and give you more information than you could possibly use []\n\n\n\nAlso, unless you want to make every file in the directory structure read write and execute, I would not use the -R switch.\n\n\n\nAs for ns not loading, it appears that you have either a missing or corrupted binary. not sure which since the logs aren\'t specific about what file failed to load.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188153, 29745, 1026, 100453, 1072936800, '', 'I have seen this error a few weeks back I don\'t rember what fixed it but it was something lame.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(188525, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, '', 'ok well I did everything imaginable to get try to get this thing working. \n\n\n\nI \'chmod -Rv 777\'ed hlds_run, replaced a metamod enabled liblist.gam with a stock one, and then I totally deleted the NS folder and started from scratch after 10 other ideas of mine did not work... it wont even work without the damn metamod... with or without the 2.0-2.01 update... sigh\n\n\n\n\n\nlol... anyone have any ideas?\n\n-Rick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(189863, 29745, 1026, 102299, 1072936800, '', 'Make sure when you do admin_install you are in the directory "Adminmod"... not the old "Admin" directory []\n\n\n\nThat was my problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(189918, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, '', 'Umm... I\'m running AMX Mod, not Admin Mod. \n\n\n\n:-/\n\n-Rick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190059, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, '', 'quote:\n\nExecuting AMX Configuration File\n\nScrolling message displaying frequency: 10:00 minutes\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.251:27040\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.253:27040\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.12:27010\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.11:27010\n\nType \'amx_help\' in the console to see available commands\n\nTime Left: 59:43 min. Next Map: ns_caged\n\nstatus\n\nhostname:  Lambda NS v2.0 - darkspireclan.net\n\nversion :  46/1.1.2.0/Stdio 2545 insecure\n\ntcp/ip  :\n\nmap     :  ns_eclipse at: 0 x, 0 y, 0 z\n\nplayers :  0 active (18 max)\n\n\n\n#      name userid uniqueid frag time ping loss adr\n\n0 users\n\n\n\n\n\nWhile none of you were able to actually fix/identify the problem for me, I would like to thank you all for you\'re imput [LART IS THE MAN] -> It really helped me alot! In the last two days I\'ve learned an increadible amount about Linux ... lol 2 days ago I had never used linux!\n\n\n\nThe NS Server is running AMX Mod/Meta Mod... I\'ve yet to join it to test it out... ill keep you guys posted on it. Till then, here is what you guys made possible!\n\n\n\nPic of the CS/NS Server\n\nhttp://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/files/both.jpg (http://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/files/both.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/viewtopic.php?t=273 (http://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/viewtopic.php?t=273)\n\n\n\nPicture of the NS Server\n\nhttp://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/files/ns.jpg (http://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/files/ns.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/viewtopic.php?t=272 (http://www.darkspireclan.net/msg/viewtopic.php?t=272)\n\n\n\nYour Linux n00b,\n\n-Rick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190807, 29745, 1026, 102297, 1072936800, '', 'so what was the problem ? =P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190894, 29745, 1026, 102296, 1072936800, '', 'No clue... I deleted the NS folder then ran quote:./steam -update valve . dsc-mutter@darkspireclan.net (mailto:dsc-mutter@darkspireclan.net) ****** y\n\n\n\nBut instead of draging and droping out of the zip, I unziped it through console as root. \n\n\n\nI\'m still not outa the woods with this damn NS server. I finally got around to testing it and I can\'t join it from any of my friend\'s computers. When I try to connect to a computer w/o steam I get this error: \n\nquote:host_error: usermsg: not present on client 66\n\nand its looking like thats a client side problem that will be fixed when 2.1 comes out (see:\n\nhttp://www.natural-selection.org/fo...mp;t=50667& (http://www.natural-selection.org/forums/index.php?act=ST&f=18&t=50667&))\n\n\n\nBut when I try to join from my room mates comp the connection times out and the ns server restarts after 10 seconds.\n\n\n\nquote:   Metamod version 1.16.2  Copyright (c) 2001-2003 Will Day <willday@metamod.org>\n\n   Metamod comes with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY; for details type `meta gpl\'.\n\n   This is free software, and you are welcome to redistribute it\n\n   under certain conditions; type `meta gpl\' for details.\n\n\n\nLoaded plugin \'CS STATS\' successfully\n\nCurrently loaded plugins:\n\n      description      stat pend  file              vers      src  load  unlod\n\n [ 1] AMX              RUN   -    amx_mm_i386.so    v0.9.7    ini  ANY   ANY\n\n [ 2] <fun_ms_i386.so  badf load  fun_ms_i386.so    v -       ini   -     -\n\n [ 3] <csstats_ms_i38  badf load  csstats_ms_i386.  v -       ini   -     -\n\n [ 4] CS STATS         RUN   -    csstats_mm_i386.  v0.9.7    cmd  ANY   ANY\n\n4 plugins, 2 running\n\nLoaded plugin \'FUN\' successfully\n\nCurrently loaded plugins:\n\n      description      stat pend  file              vers      src  load  unlod\n\n [ 1] AMX              RUN   -    amx_mm_i386.so    v0.9.7    ini  ANY   ANY\n\n [ 2] <fun_ms_i386.so  badf load  fun_ms_i386.so    v -       ini   -     -\n\n [ 3] <csstats_ms_i38  badf load  csstats_ms_i386.  v -       ini   -     -\n\n [ 4] CS STATS         RUN   -    csstats_mm_i386.  v0.9.7    cmd  ANY   ANY\n\n [ 5] FUN              RUN   -    fun_mm_i386.so    v0.9.7    cmd  ANY   ANY\n\n5 plugins, 3 running\n\nscandir failed:/usr/steam/hlds_l/./platform/SAVE\n\n\n\nExecuting AMX Configuration File\n\nScrolling message displaying frequency: 10:00 minutes\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.251:27040\n\nAdding auth server 65.73.232.253:27040\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.12:27010\n\nAdding master server 207.173.177.11:27010\n\nL 10/27/2003 - 17:16:42: Login: "NSPlayer<1><STEAM_0:1:478212><>" become an admin (account "STEAM_0:1:478212") (access "abcdefghijklmnopqrstu") (address "155.31.213.103")\n\nSZ_GetSpace: overflow on MessageBegin/End\n\nFATAL ERROR (shutting down): MESSAGE_END called, but message buffer from .dll had overflowed\n\n\n\nAdd "-debug" to the ./hlds_run command line to generate a debug.log to help with solving this problem\n\nMon Oct 27 17:16:45 EST 2003: Server restart in 10 seconds\n\n\n\n\n\nSo I thought I fixed the problem, but I ended up making a new one... lol... geez\n\n\n\n-Rick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190936, 29745, 1026, 100453, 1072936800, '', 'if you have the amx cs stats plugin it can **** this up if your not running cs.  I just reminded my self of this yesterday when my server was crashing after I added amx.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(189783, 30220, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'How do I change my Steam email / login?', 'Right now, you don\'t need to. If your email address is changing it doesn\'t really matter - you can continue to log in to Steam using the old ID.\n\n__________________\n\nSteam Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(189799, 30220, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'If I log in under a different email it changes my SteamID and install driectory right?\n\n\n\n\n\nI know you don\'t consider the email addresses all that important right now but it does create a problem, and I really like my current SteamID.\n\n\n\n\n\nAre the duplicate accounts being deleted on a higher-steamID basis or on some other critera like the date the account was created?\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks Taylor!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191404, 30220, 1013, 102300, 1072936800, '', 'LOL why would it change your steamiD? if steam ever made it that way it would be cheat/hacker glore, and why would u want it changed unless u got banned for cheating/doing something stupid.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191550, 30220, 1013, 102301, 1072936800, '', 'How would it be hacker galore? People are tracked based on three things:Steam IDCD key(s) enteredE-mail addressA Steam account can be banned by banning any of the three from all Steam services. (And in most cases where banning is nessesary I would imagine all 3 would be banned)\n\n\n\n\n\nSteam ID\'s are just unique ID\'s that relate back to your account. They are unique for every e-mail address used to make a Steam account, and hold all of your vital information. (CD key[s], join date, email, etc) Of course creating a new account would give you a new Steam ID, but the account is worthless without a CD key tied to it as well.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHow is this inviting hacking/cheating? []\n\n__________________\n\nI\'m here to help, don\'t diss me or yell at me for trying to be of assistance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191664, 30220, 1013, 102302, 1072936800, '', 'hmmm...\n\n\ni had a emailadress, but now i have a new provider and an new emailadress,\n\n\nhow can i change the maildress to my account ??\n\n\nbecause i cant resend the password if i need to the old email\n\n\n\n\n\ndo you know wat i mean ??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192830, 30220, 1013, 102160, 1072936800, '', 'you say that your email adress is not importaint but you forget about the forgetfull people who forget their passwords... yes your email adress doesnt have to work but it would be good if it did to reset passwords and the such... please help the forgetfull and make a solution for changing your email adress in steam', '127.0.0.1', 1),
