(194416, 30220, 1013, 102303, 1072936800, '', 'I just bought a new computer so in total I have 3....so is it alright if I just have a cd key, download steam and just enter that and make a new email account??\n\n__________________\n\n1.6 should just be 1.5 with no steam\n\n\n\n\n\n\'Steam is bad\n\n\n\n\n\n-Chris', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(194499, 30220, 1013, 102304, 1072936800, '', 'I had to reinstall pretty much everything on my computer, but I can\'t log on.  So I go to change my password, and what does it ask me for?  An answer to my \'question\'.  Why not ask for the CD key?  Now I have to change my e-mail address just so I can use Steam.  Do I have to get another one, or will they change this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(199774, 30220, 1013, 102305, 1072936800, '', 'I had not realized that my cd-key was entered the first time I installed Steam....I\'ve been using a different email ever since then...is it possible to switch over to the second one, or will I lose all my friends and such?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(199833, 30220, 1013, 102306, 1072936800, '', 'u cant right now but i hope they will find a way...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(199834, 30220, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'cTsValkyrie:\n\n\nIf you aren\'t having problems continue to use what has been working.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you can\'t get in then use the very first email/password you used and keep on using it, doesn\'t matter if it\'s not a good email right now.\n\n\n\n\n\nUnder no circumstance create another Steam Account unless you have a totally new CDkey to use.\n\n\n\n\n\nLater on you can move your friends over when the account thing gets all cleaned up.\n\n__________________\n\nWould you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(200514, 30220, 1013, 102305, 1072936800, '', 'I got it all working...it was just a royal pain in the butt.\n\n\n\n\n\nI had to copy and paste all my friends from the account I had been using to the one that works, as well as switching all my custom content over (new maps that I had gotten in the last few weeks, my configs...etc).  Took me about an hour and a half...most being the friends list.\n\n\n\n\n\nI had changed the emails because I had changed my mind during the second install of Steam, since my second email gets a lot less spam and I check it more often.\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks though...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(202464, 30220, 1013, 102307, 1072936800, '', 'quote:u cant right now but i hope they will find a way...\n\n\nI think they just want us to buy another copy of hl.\n\n\n\n\n\nI might just end up doing that.\n\n\nSteam and its customer support are a joke.\n\n__________________\n\nSteaming with anger!\n\n\n\n\n\nWe are people too valve!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(202476, 30220, 1013, 102308, 1072936800, '', 'yes u need to use your very first email address to pig back in unfortunately. took mt several minutes to rethik wat my password was\n\n\n\n\n\ni think its ok to have one cd key on three comps, providing they all use the same email address and only one is logged in at a time, at least i think so.\n\n__________________\n\nName\'s Wu......chaplain_wu.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190398, 30309, 1005, 102309, 1072936800, 'Potential Fix for 1.6 FPS problem ?!', 'The guys from #take2 (quakenet) seem to found out what the problem for the fps problems in 1.6 was. Valve is using an old opengl driver.\n\n\n\nHere is their way to fix it:\n\n- Go to the Windows\\System32 directory and look for your opengl.dll\n\n\n\nIf you\'re using a nvidia card the nvoglnt.dll is the right one.\n\nFor Ati cards it\'s the atioglxx.dll.\n\nAnd for the rest the opengl32.dll.\n\n\n\n- copy that file to your ..\\SteamApps\\user@user.de\\counter-strike\\gldrv directory.\n\n\n\n- open the drvmap.txt in that directory and change the text to the following:\n\n\n\nDefault Default\n\ngldrv/YOURFILENAME.dll OpenGL Driver\n\n\n\nI havent tested it so far, but it might work', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190479, 30309, 1005, 100518, 1072936800, '', 'ill test that and ill tell you if it really works', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190483, 30309, 1005, 102310, 1072936800, '', 'god i just posted that as well lol\n\n\n\nworks fine by the way', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190545, 30309, 1005, 102311, 1072936800, 'Is that normal ????', 'The only thing i have in my windows/systems32 is gm.dls     \n\n\n\nand my drvmap default is Default Default\n\ngldrv/3dfxgl.dll 3Dfx Mini Driver      \n\n\n\ne... is that normal !!!    I run CS on Opengl !!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190551, 30309, 1005, 102312, 1072936800, '', 'YES THIS WORKS FINE NO PROBS!!!!\n\n\n\nI RECCOMEND THAT IF AN ADMIN/MODERATOR SEE\'S THIS POST THAT THEY MAKE IT A STICKY AS IT IS THE ANSWER TO EVERYONES PROBLEMS WITH THIER FPS!!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMAKE THIS A STICKY!!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190555, 30309, 1005, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Whenever you download new video drivers, it updates the OpenGL driver for you...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190561, 30309, 1005, 102311, 1072936800, '', 'Ok so your telling me every thing is fine !!! Good!!! :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190565, 30309, 1005, 102312, 1072936800, '', 'yeah mate it does, but take ya time to read what it sez up there.\n\n\n\nsteam uses its own opengl dll file in the steam directory, which is an old version. if you follow the instructions at the top, and replace this old 3dfxGL.dll or whatever, the fps goes to what it should be!!! my fps is flawless now!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190568, 30309, 1005, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Why would STEAM use a old OpenGL.dll file?  That\'s beyond me.  Either your wrong or VALVe overlooked something again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190574, 30309, 1005, 102312, 1072936800, '', 'valve HAVE overlooked something! i just tried this and my FPS is perfect, b4 it was very bad and i had at least a 33% loss of frame rate. Valve CAN make mistakes it isnt impossible, if you dont believe me try it yourself. or stick with what you have if your FPS is ok.\n\n\n\nthats my final word on this \n\n\n\n\n\nTRY IT! :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190579, 30309, 1005, 100788, 1072936800, '', 'hmm i tried to remove the old 3dfxGL.dll  with my new nvoglnt.dll (for nvidia detornator), but as soon as i start CS, the old file is back again and cs loads the 3dfx... driver ??? \n\n\n\nhmm any suggestions?\n\n\n\n\n\nmany tnx 4 your help', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190584, 30309, 1005, 102312, 1072936800, '', 'i dont know if it woks with the nvidia openGL file\n\n\n\ni have an Nvidia Gforce 4 MX 440 and i also use the detonator drivers, i went to; \n\n\n\n"C:/windows/system32"\n\n\n\nand copied the file opengl32.dll to the gldrv folder instead, and edited the txt file to say:\n\n\n\nDefault Default \n\ngldrv/opengl32.dll OpenGL Driver \n\n\n\nit works fine now, i think you are best off using that file instead []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190593, 30309, 1005, 102311, 1072936800, 'Your opinion !!!', 'The only file that I have in my "C:/windows/system32"  is \n\n\n\nGm.dls ???   how come I don\'t have the opengl file or the \n\n\n\nnvoglnt.dll because i use a nvidia card ? Strange to me !!!   and \n\n\n\nmy default in drvmap is  gldrv/3dfxgl.dll 3Dfx Mini Driver !!! \n\n\n\ni run cs on opengl but i cant find a damn opengl file even if i do a \n\n\n\nsearch on opengl !!!    Help plz !!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190602, 30309, 1005, 102313, 1072936800, '', 'wow i really need to update my 5 year old computer.....\n\n\n\ngood thing I am!!!\n\n\n\nw00t\n\n\n\n<is happy>', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190680, 30309, 1005, 102314, 1072936800, 'Your opinion !!!', 'quote:Originally posted by Pilami \n\nThe only file that I have in my "C:/windows/system32"  is \n\n\n\nGm.dls ???   how come I don\'t have the opengl file or the \n\n\n\nnvoglnt.dll because i use a nvidia card ? Strange to me !!!   and \n\n\n\nmy default in drvmap is  gldrv/3dfxgl.dll 3Dfx Mini Driver !!! \n\n\n\ni run cs on opengl but i cant find a damn opengl file even if i do a \n\n\n\nsearch on opengl !!!    Help plz !!!  \n\n\n\nMine is the same, there are no .dll files in my system32 driver folder either and the rest of your info is the same as mine.  I have also downloaded the other day the newest detonater drivers for my card.  The only thing I can find is a nvopenGl.dll in my NVIDEA folder but I\'m not sure if this would be the one to use.\n\nCan anybody help?  Thank You', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190692, 30309, 1005, 102315, 1072936800, '', 'Show hidden files?\n\n\ngg\n\n__________________\n\nyea but watching chickens explode is funny', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190717, 30309, 1005, 102314, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, it is set to show hidden files.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190895, 30309, 1005, 102316, 1072936800, '', 'i did what it says and when i launch cs and try to connect to a  server it just closes cs and puts the 3dfx file back in, i tried using the opengl32.dll file instead of the nvoglnt.dll and still no luck.\n\n\n\n\n\nany ideas?\n\n\n\n\n\ni have a geforce 4 mx440\n\n\n\n\n\nusing 4.0.7.2 det drivers', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190951, 30309, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'I have asked Valve\'s developers about this "fix", and the word is, it does nothing.  In fact that file is not even loaded or referenced.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n\nThe file they\'re changing isn\'t even loaded anymore, definitely a placebo.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThat said, if someone can show me a screenshot of "before" and "after" with a change in FPS, I\'ll believe it.  Can\'t be in a live server with other players, etc.  Has to be the exact same position, action,  etc.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190970, 30309, 1005, 102317, 1072936800, ':( almost good idea!!', 'Man i got so excited when i read this post.... Makes so much sense that that would fix the problem. I Copied my atioglxx.dll (9800 pro) and pasted it into my drvmap folder, change the text file.... and even changed the 3dfx files name and backed everything up of course.\n\n\n\n\n\nJoined Cs and same bs. 70 fps when im looking at people. i can stare out the wall and max fps, but wtf does this do for me. Anyways... curious cause i read the other posts i check that 3dfx.dll and sure enough it was back in my folder along with the original i changed its name. Someone was using their head when they came up wit this solution... but it is code somewhere that steam is going to load that 3dfx.dll... ALSO it didnt change the ati driver text from the .txt file i edited... strange.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso I know people say shut off ati_npatch, and ati_subdiv.... which i have and does nothing for me... but can anyone tell me what these 2 commands do???????? \n\n\n\n\n\nI miss playing CS like i used to.... feels so choppy now. Makes me wanna play my smooth ass playing HALO or Max Payne2. You would think cs is the new game with the high tech graphics. This is SUCH a big issue for cs players I so shocked VALVE hasnt addressed the problem, let alone FIX IT. I know they were robbed but a customers loyalty is only as good as the service. We arent gonna keep being [atient and supportive of you guy if you dont give us answers... or a response, yes we know its there... we will try to fix it. OR SOMETHING. \n\n\n\n\n\nBack to the subject... this fix would be sweet if we could figure out how to implement it without it changing.......... update us!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190982, 30309, 1005, 102318, 1072936800, '', 'ati_npatch "0" and ati_subdiv "0" disables TRUFORM(tm) on ATI based video cards. TRUFORM is ATI\'s method of adding more polygons to an object for more realism.\n\n\n\n\n\nD< O >A, as for your fps problem on your Radeon 9800 Pro, you can try disabling V-SYNC in your Display Properties > Settings > Advanced > 3D Tab > Open GL > Use custom settings > Click on Custom. (This is only for ATI Catalyst 3.9 drivers)\n\n\n\n\n\nOn the near bottom of the window you\'ll see "Wait for Vertical Sync", move the slider all the way to the left until it says Always Off.\n\n\n\n\n\nNext load up Counter-Strike 1.6, go into console (~ key) and type down:\n\n\n\n\n\nfps_max "101"\n\n\ndeveloper "1"\n\n\n\n\n\nfps_max "101" raises your FPS, and developer "1" uncaps the 100FPS barrier in Counter-Strike.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191028, 30309, 1005, 102315, 1072936800, '', 'Obviously it does something, because after the change the fps stayed the same, being I have it capped at 70. But, what I did notice was my screen cutting alot more when my fps dropped. Never before had I noticed it. Yet with the change it happens ever 5-10 seconds.\n\n__________________\n\nyea but watching chickens explode is funny', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191049, 30309, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by 4th3ist \n\n\nObviously it does something, because after the change the fps stayed the same, being I have it capped at 70. But, what I did notice was my screen cutting alot more when my fps dropped. Never before had I noticed it. Yet with the change it happens ever 5-10 seconds.  \n\n\n\n\n\nSo try this.  Grab some random dll out of your system file and replace it with that.  See what that does.  And I dont\' mean a driver for graphics, just some random dll.\n\n\n\n\n\nEdit - ok I just tried it.  I put "browser.dll" from my windows\\system32 folder in there and put it\'s name in the txt file.  And the game runs fine.  So clearly doing this has no impact on the game\'s ability to run.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191103, 30309, 1005, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'This does not appear to work. I tried a number of drivers and they were all ignored and the stock files are just reinstated.\n\n\n\n\n\nI even tried very old ones and I tried the very latest opengl build which I know works because I use it with Milkshape and Hammer and there is absolutely no change in performance, much less evidence that any of the drivers are being loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\nTo prove this, I ran a detailed task monitor program and actually looked to see what files were being used and found that on my Nvidia G4 4200 card these were the only functioning OPENGL drivers attached to the HL task:\n\n\n\n\n\nMicrosoft Corporation   C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\opengl32.dll\n\n\nMicrosoft Corporation   C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\GLU32.dll\n\n\nNVIDIA Corporation      C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\nvoglnt.dll\n\n\n\n\n\nwhatever was in gldrv/drvmap.txt had no effect whatsoever.\n\n\n\n\n\nMoving these files to the Steam directory serves no purpose.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn fact, this thread serves no purpose and just adds to the confusion.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191122, 30309, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'good detective work quicksilver', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191231, 30309, 1005, 102319, 1072936800, '', 'D<O>A plz explain how you are valves "customer", the product you bought had made its money. you paid for cs back in 99(or whenever) hl + cs made its money, the only thing they want to do with you, is get you to buy cs:cz. wether that means making cs "look real choppy + ****ty" and trying to offer you a "new + improved fps engine" with cs:cz or by any other means necessary. in fact i was told that valve never even made much money off cs considering vivendi stdios(or w/e the name was) made its money, then sold it to valve(making more money) so as far as valve is concerned about the current cs, they see it as a dead cause, no $$$ or worth. onto cs:cz.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191257, 30309, 1005, 102320, 1072936800, '', 'this is utter non-sense, what opengl/d3d driver do u think steam is loading? it doesn\'t have opengl/d3d hardcored into the engine, it calls whatever the system points at, which would be your current video driver api', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191285, 30309, 1005, 102317, 1072936800, '', 'I have vsync off AA off AF off everything that should be off. But this card should run 100fps WITH aa ON. They want me to buy cs:cz..... im not going to buy it if it will run like cs, ive been playing dx9 games and running so smooth. ALL IM SAYING!\n\n\n\n\n\nThere is a reason that i went from geforce fx5600 256mb with 100 fps constent to 9800 pro 250 and be having fps loss. Makes no sense. i know that they improved graphics..... but nothing that has been done comes close to touhcing any recent games that run silky smooth on my machine. Explaination?? dunno\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nand since i have truform off... it shouldnt matter what i have set in the game, right?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191289, 30309, 1005, 102321, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by nebula \n\n\nthis is utter non-sense, what opengl/d3d driver do u think steam is loading? it doesn\'t have opengl/d3d hardcored into the engine, it calls whatever the system points at, which would be your current video driver api  \n\n\n\n\n\nTru, i was actually gunna follow the instructions of this thread, till i kept reading it.\n\n\n\n\n\nAnother thing, I think the added "choppiness" is just do to Valve, or whoever updates cs, adding more graphic enhancments, on a really old game engine that isn\'t optimized for all thos FX, \n\n\n\n\n\n(Aztec rain anyone?)  Thats really the only map that gets choppy 4 me, so i dun see what the big fuss is all bout, u guys \'plaining bout 70 to 60 fps??! c\'mon!!\n\n\n\n\n\nI do a steady 30 - 35 fps, and around 15 - 20 when it chopps up.\n\n\n\n\n\nThere is no secret formula to fix it, its up to the programmers to PROGRAM better, or to OPTIMIZE the engine for faster fram rates.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191368, 30309, 1005, 102322, 1072936800, '', 'set to read only and enable mini3dfx', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(190475, 30316, 1005, 102310, 1072936800, 'the FPS FIX!! ACCTUAL FIX', 'ok valve is using an old opengl driver and thats why so many people have the FPS issues!\n\n\n\n\n\nso how do we fix it?\n\n\nsimple:\n\n\n\n\n\nin cs folder: e.g. \\Steam\\SteamApps\\user@user.de\\counter-strike\\gldrv\\  is the  3dfx*.dll file and a text file\n\n\n\n\n\nin your windows\\system32 folder is the current opengl file which you now copy to the cs open gl folder as stated above\n\n\nNOTE:\n\n\nuse the correct dll file\n\n\n\n\n\n- Detonator User: nvoglnt.dll\n\n\n\n\n\n- Standard User: opengl32.dll\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ati User: atioglxx.dll\n\n\n\n\n\nnow edit the text file drvmap.txt to this\n\n\n Default Default\n\n\n        gldrv/opengl32.dll OpenGL Driver\n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE opengl32.dll should be replaced with the dll file you copied for your graphics card\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://take2.homeip.net/100FPS_CS.html (http://take2.homeip.net/100FPS_CS.html)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191025, 30316, 1005, 102323, 1072936800, '', 'atioglxx.dll won\'t work because it from cats 3.8 onwards it doesn\'t export the gl functions.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe only reason this would fix your FPS is if you selected 3DFX mini-driver from the drop down list, or if Steam somehow selected it for you. If you did that, you can just go into the registry to HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Valve\\Half-Life\\Settings and change the EngineGLDriver value to "Default" instead.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191058, 30316, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'This does nothing, as these files are not used by the  game at all.  Please see my posts at /forums/...15&pagenumber=2 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=30309&perpage=15&pagenumber=2) for info.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you want to see how it doesn\'t make any difference, try replacing the dll with something completely unrelated to graphics.  It still runs fine.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191196, 30316, 1005, 102324, 1072936800, '', 'ill wait for valve to fix it... although ive noticed my fps is a fair bit lower than it was on 1.5. and anyone else get slowed down ALOT running through smoke?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191220, 30316, 1005, 102325, 1072936800, '', 'sorry waldo but this post is because steam doesn\'t runs fine\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Waldo \n\n\nThis does nothing, as these files are not used by the  game at all.  Please see my posts at /forums/...15&pagenumber=2 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=30309&perpage=15&pagenumber=2) for info.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you want to see how it doesn\'t make any difference, try replacing the dll with something completely unrelated to graphics.  It still runs fine.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191221, 30316, 1005, 102315, 1072936800, '', 'The 3dfx driver in the gldrv folder would appear to be the Mini-GL drivers for older Voodoo cards.\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd to answer your question about smoke, incase it hasn\'t occured to you people yet, smoke was fixed in 1.6 so it actually does something. ex. Your not susposed to be able to see through it, ex. more lag...\n\n__________________\n\nyea but watching chickens explode is funny', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191283, 30316, 1005, 102326, 1072936800, '', 'i tried, and nothing happened.. didnt make things better or worse, i conclude that steam doesnt use these files, or there is not big different  betwen the latest detonator drivers and the one that comes  with steam,...\n\n\n\n\n\neither way, thnx but not thnx  []\n\n__________________\n\n----> [TH] Jac|<aL^ |cL| <----', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191304, 30316, 1005, 102261, 1072936800, 'the FPS FIX!! ACCTUAL FIX', 'quote:Originally posted by germanjulian \n\n\nnow edit the text file drvmap.txt to this\n\n\n Default Default This tells your system to use the opengl driver you have installed when you installed your drivers.\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by germanjulian \n\n\nnow edit the text file drvmap.txt to this\n\n\ngldrv/opengl32.dll OpenGL Driver Doing this just tells it to use the opengl driver in your system too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191768, 30316, 1005, 100332, 1072936800, '', 'this is bull****, the dll file and the txt file of 1.5(1.6) is same.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(191932, 30316, 1005, 100738, 1072936800, '', 'tested it on radeon cards but didnt work\n\n\n\n\n\nCRASH @ startup', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192107, 30316, 1005, 102327, 1072936800, '', 'OK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file.\n\n\n\n\n\nJust in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192114, 30316, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bigj22 \n\n\nOK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file.\n\n\n\n\n\nJust in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out.  \n\n\n\n\n\nI did edit the txt file.  I told it to load the fax admin driver.  Still ran fine.   No errors.  And yes I\'m running OpenGL.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192118, 30316, 1005, 102323, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bigj22 \n\n\nOK obviously this threads popularity shows theres a serious issue here.As for this fix being a "placebo" your wrong thats all Im gonna say.For me the difference was dramatic enough that I can say with all honesty that it worked and yes its great.If you cant get it to work Im sorry to hear it.Took me a couple times as well.And yeah you can put a fax file in there and it will work because the 3dfx file is still present,even if you delete it STeam will load it right back into the folder when you connect like I have already said.The biggie here is editing and saving the text file.\n\n\n\n\n\nJust in case no one has mentioned this if your not using Open GL and dont have your graphic options set to it this fix will of course do absolutely nothing.If the file was useless it wouldnt be there.Go check your settings and use some common sense and maybe this might help you out.  \n\n\n\n\n\nThe point it is would only make a difference if (a) you were stupid enough to select 3DFX mini-driver in the first place and (b) you didn\'t know how to go back to the default driver from the drop-down list or via the registry.\n\n\n\n\n\nI think the current fps problem is purely due to the increasing complexity of these games and the number of times functions such as glVertex3f are wrapped both in the game engine and in the driver DLL. Older games like Half-Life call OpenGL functions for every single vertex they want to render (Half-Life even partially-transforms all the vertices itself with no acceleration) which causes massive CPU dependence and is a lot slower than using vertex buffers or display lists like newer games use.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192121, 30316, 1005, 102327, 1072936800, '', 'Well I guess the game has some kind of backup to make it idiot proof for fools who try and use fax drivers for Open GL.Try this....make sure your using open GL,delete the whole folder then run cs and tell me it causes no problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192123, 30316, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by billdoor \n\n\nThe point it is would only make a difference if (a) you were stupid enough to select 3DFX mini-driver in the first place and (b) you didn\'t know how to go back to the default driver from the drop-down list or via the registry.  \n\n\n\n\n\nHow do you "select" the 3dfx mini driver?  It\'s not anywhere on the Video options that I can see.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192709, 30673, 1013, 102328, 1072936800, 'Valve Premier Pack Errors with Counter Strike and Team Fortress', 'I get error 15: Cache Read Failure, everytime I attempt to play Counter Strike or Team Fortress with the new Valve Premier Pack I just downloaded. Could someone please tell me the problem here?\n\nthanks\n\nReleqy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(192716, 30673, 1013, 102329, 1072936800, 'Can\'t start any games', 'Hi there... \n\n\n\nI having a big problem here [] when I try starting Counter Strike I get this error\n\n\n\nSteam Has Found the following problem with your game\n\n  SteamProcessCall(WaitForAppReadyToLaunch) failed with error 15: cache Read Failure\n\n\n\nThe game data cache need to bee flushed in order to run.\n\nDid you wish to do this now?\n\n\n\nhave tried to click ok to it, but nothing happends it shows again and a again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
