(196147, 30673, 1013, 102336, 1072936800, 'i know why here\'s how to fix', 'if u installed steam later than oct 28th, or had to reinstall your steam after oct 28th with the cached install file you will have the cache error. \n\n\n\n\n\ncached install file means steam + cs or steam + cs dod etc.\n\n\nwhich is 700 or 500 mb.\n\n\n\n\n\nwhat u need to do is download \'steam only\' install file, install steam and download cs through steam server which will take forever and yes, it sucks.\n\n\n\n\n\nthanks to steam for updating constantly and screwing up !\n\n\n\n\n\nwouldn\'t you love Blizzard to run steam server?\n\n\nit will be sooooooooooooo much better :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(196234, 30673, 1013, 102337, 1072936800, '', 'Hi all\n\n\n\n\n\nI have the SteamInstall_CS.exe on a cd. As i have a 56k connection. And im sure u dont want to wait the insanely long time that it would take to download 700 odd meg of data.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe first time i had got steam working on my pc was after reinstalling it 3 times. The 3rd time only worked because of one of my mates realising how to actually update the CS cache, as mine was just saying "May Require Update".\n\n\n\n\n\nSo once i got it working and playing which was for about a week, the "recalled" update came out for steam. Which totally wrecked my steam. The day after, i lent my cd to a friend with a 56k connection, as he wanted me to sort out his CS for him. So i go to his house and put steam on for him. unfortunatly i had to leave the cd with him, as i had to get back for a clanmatch. At that time i didnt realise that my version of steam was "broke" as i had downloaded the update and turned off my pc (i dowloaded it as it was released).\n\n\n\n\n\nSo after i arrive back home and try to join the match, i realise that my version was "bust" as it was trying to redownload CS again or whatever the error was. So after that i had to wait for my mate to drop back the cd.\n\n\n       Yet again, unfortunatly for me (as it always is) my friend was going away for the weekend to world war 2 re-inactment. Also on that sunday 26th i went to a 4 day lan at a mates house. So i wouldnt be able to reinstall steam until the wednesday(yesterday), as my mate only dropped it back to me yesterday evening.\n\n\n\n\n\nSo i go to reinstall today thinking "i cant wait to get cs going again". So i install and let it update itself, then go and double click CS, thinking that it would update it, as it needs to be updated as the cache i have installed is before the cs update was released. But it didnt update it, it tries to run it, and yes i do get the error that everone else is getting about the cache being wrong. I double click to update half0life and that brings up the update window, but it doesnt update......well not in the time i let it start  []. The real reason for me writing this is that, i am not going to delete my CS and re-download the cache again. as that totally defeats the point in me having the "SteamInstall_CS.exe".\n\n\n\n\n\nSo this is too you Taylor Sherman, is my SteamInstall_CS.exe worthless now? Or will this "fix" let me update my "younger" version of the CS cache that i have? pls email frankbutcher@clanee.co.uk (mailto:frankbutcher@clanee.co.uk) with ur answer or post on here\n\n\n\n\n\nThank you for taking you\'re time to read this. \n\n\n\n\n\nP.S. im sure ur tea is very cold by now :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(196501, 30673, 1013, 102338, 1072936800, '', 'i connect at 28k..... i live in the bush in australia.... i loved 1.6 cos i got heeps of less lag......\n\n\n\n\n\nmy mate burnt me steaminstall_cs.exe to cd for me so i wouldnt have to download it on my 28k\n\n\n\n\n\nanyway will i HAVE to download 280mb of data?????? because that will take me literally 2 months', '127.0.0.1', 1),
