(198187, 31278, 1005, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Make sure the setting for your internet connection in Steam is set correctly. I\'m seeing a TON of players with the modem rate setting (2500) even though they are on dsl or cable. \n\n\n\nThis rate controls how fast content is sent to your computer including info about maps during map changes so it\'s important that it is correct (and don\'t just set it to T1, that can cause other problems unless you have one). \n\n\n\nTo check this, go to Steam Main Menu > Settings > Internet and set the correct connection type for your internet connection.\n\n\n\nI\'ve also seen several players on Win98 specifically having this problem, but that doesn\'t appear to be the issue here.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(198258, 31278, 1005, 102345, 1072936800, '', 'This error has happened to me on any map> dust2, aztec , etc as well as custom maps', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(198362, 31278, 1005, 102343, 1072936800, '', 'me connection is on DSL 256+ so that isnt the problem...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(198949, 31278, 1005, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'kaishin:\n\nIt isn\'t the type of connection you have that is the problem but what the settings are in Steam ... It doesn\'t just automatically know what type of connection you have.\n\n\n\nRead my instructions in the post and check your settings.\n\n\n\nTypical non-modem connections should have a rate of 5000 to 7500 with a maximum of 9999 for internet connections.\n\n\n\nYou can also check and change this in console, just enter "rate" and it will tell you what the setting is.\n\n\n\nYour specs also said 512k not 256k, which is correct?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(200284, 31278, 1005, 102346, 1072936800, '', 'That load failed error happens to everyone on my server so it\'s not just an individual case, there are over 3000 players that come to the server and every one of them has that problem so look a little deeper into Steams problems rather than everyone elses. If it\'s happening to every system under the sun than it\'s not a local problem, it\'s a steam problem. Also I noticed this just start happening about 2 weeks ago, maybe something in your update is buggin out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(200291, 31278, 1005, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by kaishin \n\nthx for the replys... my specs \n\n\n\nOS: Windows XP Pro SP1 \n\nCPU: Intel Pentium 4, 3.1 GHz \n\nGPU: GeForce 4 Ti 4600 128 MB \n\nPRAM: 1 GB DDRAM \n\nVRAM: 3.4 GB \n\nConnection: 512kps\n\nSettings: \n\n-1280x1024 resolution \n\n-32-bit color \n\n-OpenGL, VSync Off  \n\n\n\nWay to totally copy my specs and up the processor speed...  yah we believe you.  I doubt you even know what DDRAM stands for lol.\n\n__________________\n\nSYSTEM SPECS\n\n__________________\n\n\n\nOS: MS Windows XP Pro SP1\n\nHDs: 120 GB (NTFS) & 40 GB (FAT32)\n\nCPU: Intel Pentium 4 @ 2.53 GHz\n\nGPU: GeForce4 Ti 4600 128 MB (45.23 Drivers)\n\nPRAM: 1 GB DDRAM \n\nVMEM: 3.4 GB\n\nConnection: Comcast Cable (600/80 Kbps)\n\nSettings:\n\n-OpenGL w/VSync, AA, AF and TS Off\n\n-1280x1024 resolution\n\n-32-bit color\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.\n\n66.208.104.166:27015 - KDB pub\n\n69.56.171.228:27015 - S_c_T pub\n\n208.184.33.208:27015 - team.cH pub', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(200626, 31940, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '"Platinum Pack" in cd-key email', 'Just a note:\n\n\n\nAll of the "The cd-key you entered is already in use" emails that are sent out mention "Your purchase of the HL Platinum Pack".\n\n\n\nSorry for the confusion:\n\n\n\nAny HL cd-key currently subscribes you to all games in Steam. This subscription is called the Platinum Pack. \n\n\n\nSo, even if you enter a Counter-Strike key, or a HL key, or whatever retail package the key is from, if you get this email it will say "Platinum Pack". It\'s not a bug with the key validation.\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(205172, 32592, 1013, 102354, 1072936800, 'Steam Ate My CD-Keys !!', 'OK I\'m am seriously pissed off now, i\'ve been pantient with steam, tried not to break anything around me but i\'m just totaly over this ****\n\n\n\nI !!! OWN 3 LEGIT !! (See that Legit !! meaning i bought the game from the STORE !!!) i\'ve had all 3 computers running perfect then you guys come along saying (like you did when steam came out) \n\n\n\n"This next updates going to be the next best thing since sliced bread!" and BAM millions of peoples CD-Keys just disappear? admit it you guys ****ED UP BAD !!. you know you did - and don\'t come with me with thiongs like, well theres plenty of ways it could of gotten stole, packages are handled by many people on their way to the store - BS i bought these ages ago and have played with them with no problems (that is till steam made its way here)\n\n\n\nalso don\'t say, well you may be using a duplicate account, cause i\'m not i did NOT ! give them away, NO ONE besides me saw the keys and besides all 3 accounts are active they all just get your stupid\n\n\n\n"Your purchase of Half-Life Platinum Pack Failed"\n\n\n\nIf it failed how come about once every 15 times i enter and start Counter-Strike the launches? how come they stoped working after the last update where the new "Checking for invalid CD-Keys Upon Launch" bit came in? THEY ARE ALL VALID - THEY\'VE WORKED ALL THIS TIME AND WHEN I FINALY START TRUSTING STEAM YOU GUYS **** UP AGAIN !!!!\n\n\n\nYou Steam/Valve fellas obviously don\'t realise the point. We, the legit buyers, Lose our cd-keys after 1 "GREAT !!! NEW FANTASIC" update and you guys spin bull**** at us like we\'re dumb arse little 5 year olds that believe if we **** it\'ll make us strong - Wwll i\'m not eating your **** !!. i Suggest you guys at Steam/Valve FIX this in the next update because i\'m NOT going to buy another copy of bloody half life just cause you guys ****ed up - why should i give you MORE money because of your stuff up? and the way things are going, i\'m not waiting year for HL2 to come out before i play CS again\n\n\n\nFrom a very ANGRY AND PISSED OFF victom of your ****ty system', '127.0.0.1', 1),
