(206199, 32592, 1013, 102358, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jarin \n\nI find if I just keep putting my CD-KEY in over and over it will work 1 out of 6 times, when it works it lets me in a game and I can play for a bit\n\n\n\nbut after I quit it says CS is not installed and when I try to install it calls me a filthy dirty pirate, yet I got the BLOODY CD IN MY ****ING HAND YOU SON OF A BITCHES \n\n\n\n\n\nwhat is it with these steam error messages that puts the blame on us? im REALLY gettin sick of being told that i cant connect because of something I did, or because of my network.\n\n\n\ni have yet to come across a problem caused by me, but every erromessage i get ALWAYS starts with putting the blame on me, then SOMETIMES continuing further down with "or with steam".\n\n\n\nlets not forget how WE are the ppl finding these fixes, i have lost count how many times i have pasted a link for a question already answered OVER 7 times by US!\n\n\n\nwhere the f a r k would steam be without us helping each other out only to be told that we are using an illegal key or that we have a bad internet connection etc.\n\n\n\nim getting sick or re-installing steam 3 times to fix each problem!\n\n\n\nlatest being the "crash on exit" in win98SE. how is it possible that 1 computer connects fine, then i re-install it to see if it fixes the crashing, only to find it can not connect to a steam server because MY CONNECTION is down! wtf? im browsing with that very computer, the computer next to me connects to steam, but the one im using will not connect untill i re-install it a few times! and it DIDNT FIX THE CRASHING PROBLEM!\n\n\n\narhghhhghghg i fell better, only slightly ...\n\n__________________\n\n"GET STEAM NOW\n\nIN MINUTES, YOU\'LL BE PLAYING YOUR FAVORITE GAMES" lol ;)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
