(209325, 33060, 1013, 102366, 1072936800, 'Re: Fix Steam Now', 'quote:Originally posted by American Zombie \n\nYou may have paid for 1.5 but you did not pay for 1.6 so go on WON and play 1.5 then be happy.  \n\n\n\nHe paid to play Counter Strike simple as that, along with millions of others, not to get an update that essentially made it next to impossible for him to play. I don\'t think he cares that this update came free.\n\nBut great advice though, exactly what I\'d recommend to everyone else having problems with Steam and 1.6. I am now happily continueing to play 1.5 and it runs great even on my PC, which cannot even play Unreal Tournament (the original).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(209340, 33060, 1013, 102367, 1072936800, '', 'stop whining and just don\'t play the game noobs. and be content that valve scammed you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(209408, 33060, 1013, 102368, 1072936800, '', 'I agree with the author of this thread, it is the only thread i have seen in a long while here that is worth anything. I broke out my Cs box, which you can still buy at the store. Now some Dad is going to get this for his 15 year old son with a PC that fits the bill as stated on the box. Now lets say that they are just normal people who like to play PC games... Where would they go, what would they do? I have been playing since 1.3, everything was fine, 1.4 to 1.5 in like a week was a mess, but went off ok. Now this... I think someone should get a law suit for this. You go and pay for something it should work as the direction says! If you go buy a $20,000.00 car and they have you come back over and over for a radio update, sometimes it works... some not. Would you not do something about it? This is the same thing... different scale I know...but still, some people work hard for money, so do not, thats not the point. We all paid for this, ( Ok, there are many ways to get a CD key, not the point ) and we go buy what the product offers... this product is not standing up to what it offers, you can not use older PC\'s, you have to have something much better then what is on the box... that alone is wrong! Sure.. it is playable, i have 3 Pc\'s. One has a 450mhz, 64mb Radeon video card, 512 MB ram, worked great with 1.5, with 1.6... my kid can not play. Yoiu say stick with 1.5? Why should I (WE) have to? We paid for the samething you did, my PC meets and exceeds what is printed on the box... that should be good enough. But it is not! Thats sad!! and very wrong!\n\nSorry to ramble... but this is by far the best post I have seen here! Hats off to the author! I hope you do something about this and are not just blowing smoke or trying to make nosie.\n\nPitt', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(209471, 33060, 1013, 102239, 1072936800, '', 'A 10 year old threatening w/a lawsuit. You dont even have anything in your favor. Im sure they care what he just posted. Whoop-di-doo. \n\nI have ZERO probs with Steam...and why in the hell did you buy 5 copies? Im sure your parents wouldnt approve of that. I wouldnt.\n\nDont get me wrong...Steam is far from perfect, and I\'m not 100% happy with it yet. There is just no point to his post. Hes going to have to live with it or quit cs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(209479, 33060, 1013, 102369, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by thirdeye \n\noh... and a GF2mx400 runs just fine.... if you have CS 1.5.  \n\n\n\nI used to get 100fps with ZERO lag before steam came along and forced me to upgrade my WHOLE MACHINE!\n\n\n\nCS 1.5: ran beautifully with my old Duron 1Ghz, 512MB ram, GF2mx400, winXP.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nyour comp is very similiar to mine, except i got a gf4 mx440\n\n\n\nYeah it ran alot smoother back in the good ole 1.5 days, too bad this steam thucking pile of bull crap ruined 1.6.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(212951, 33639, 1005, 102370, 1072936800, 'Load failed on mapchange', 'Hello Steam Staff and Forum geeks []\n\n\n\nI\'m an admin of an large server hosting company, and we have some problems with our servers hanging on mapchange. It takes 10-15 seconds before the "loading" screen shows up at the clients. And the clients often get an "Connection problem" screen right before it.\n\n\n\nIn the worst cases, our clients get "Load failed..." message, and have to type "retry" in the console ( if they find the console ?! ).\n\n\n\nI\'m running 6 servers on a:\n\n\n\nAMD Athlon Dual MP2400+ server with 1GB DDR RAM. \n\n\n\nThe ping is fine (10-50), and there is  no lagg at all during gameplay. 0 ms, 0 choke and 0 loss.\n\n\n\nthanks for your help!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
