(213432, 33639, 1005, 102370, 1072936800, 'harddrive', 'I\'ve been testing this erros some more tonight, and it appears that it only happens when there are 10+ players on the server? Could this be right?.\n\n\n\nI have also tried with scsi drives, instead of ide ata drives, and it seems to work better then... Why the !"�#! does this new steam update make the resources sooooooooo much harder to load for the drive? errr... stop updating without posting what new features you update with :/\n\n\n\n*arr*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213483, 33639, 1005, 102372, 1072936800, '', 'Try increasing the cl_timeout value until it works. I had the problem, fixed it this way. Just giving CS a little more time to communicate with the server.\n\n__________________\n\nThe Hit List - Revised:\n\n*e-bitchslaps steamuser\n\n*e-bitchslaps matpatnik\n\n*e-bitchslaps trimp\n\n*e-bitchslaps Politics\n\n*e-bitchslaps Sapiens\n\n*e-bitchslaps ErrorClone\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213487, 33639, 1005, 102370, 1072936800, '', 'Heh, sorry dude, buts that an lousy and unusable solution.\n\n\n\nCant force all the clients to change their settings, that would\'nt work. The problem is within the server, and should therefore be solved within the servers settings etc.\n\n\n\nSo... where is the moderators and steam staff in this forum ?! :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213491, 33639, 1005, 102372, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox \n\nHeh, sorry dude, buts that an lousy and unusable solution.\n\n\n\nCant force all the clients to change their settings, that would\'nt work. The problem is within the server, and should therefore be solved within the servers settings etc.\n\n\n\nSo... where is the moderators and steam staff in this forum ?! :/  \n\n\n\nHow exactly is that a lousy and unusable solution? Did you even try it? How the hell do you expect a moderator to waiste his time helping you if you won\'t listen to common sense suggestions?\n\n\n\nIts simple. In your console, type \'cl_timeout\' and see what number it gives you, then increase the number. And there are thousands of reasons why you might need to set this high. 90% of those reasons have to deal with either your comp or your ISP, neither of which any server running CS is responsible for.\n\n\n\nTry a suggestion before you shoot it down next time...\n\n\n\n/EDIT: BTW, no global set of configuration settings for any game is ever going to work for every computer and every player. Every single person who has ever played CS has changed some client side setting...even if it is just their player nickname.\n\n__________________\n\nThe Hit List - Revised:\n\n*e-bitchslaps steamuser\n\n*e-bitchslaps matpatnik\n\n*e-bitchslaps trimp\n\n*e-bitchslaps Politics\n\n*e-bitchslaps Sapiens\n\n*e-bitchslaps ErrorClone\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213496, 33639, 1005, 102370, 1072936800, '', 'It seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8!\n\n\n\nThe problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures.\n\n\n\nAnd the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/\n\n\n\nAnd, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213505, 33639, 1005, 102372, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox \n\nIt seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8!\n\n\n\nThe problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures.\n\n\n\nAnd the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/\n\n\n\nAnd, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings.  \n\n\n\nEvery client? You sure? You asked every single Steam user? If all the player on your servers are suffering from this, then I would think you would want to try every possible solution. And the fact that it works with under 10 players only suggests I am right. \n\n\n\nAnd if I\'m not right then so be it. But I am telling you how I solved my problem. And this has helped others solve the same problem. Bottom line, don\'t post about a problem if you don\'t want help. And if you do want help, don\'t be so quick to jump on someone\'s back. Even if their suggestion doesn\'t work, it might lead you to the solution.\n\n__________________\n\nThe Hit List - Revised:\n\n*e-bitchslaps steamuser\n\n*e-bitchslaps matpatnik\n\n*e-bitchslaps trimp\n\n*e-bitchslaps Politics\n\n*e-bitchslaps Sapiens\n\n*e-bitchslaps ErrorClone\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213525, 33639, 1005, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox \n\nIt seems that you have misunderstood the problem m8!\n\n\n\nThe problem is that servers that NEVER had any mapchange load failures under cs 1.5 and cs 1.6 beta, now has mapchange failures.\n\n\n\nAnd the problem applies to EVERY client. So therefore its bs. that the clients have to change their settings thereselves... THE PROBLEM IS THE SERVERS :/\n\n\n\nAnd, since it works with under 10 players and scsi drives, there is nothing wrong at all with the clients cl_timeout settings.  \n\n\n\nVery, very wrong.  The reason you have to do it in 1.6 is because in 1.6 it has defaulted to a lower value than you may have needed in 1.5.  cl_timeout works in the following way; the value you give it is the maximum amount of time that CS (client-side) will wait inbetween map changes for new information (about the map, other players, etc).  If your cl_timeout value is LOWER THAN YOUR AVERAGE LATENCY to that server, you will be d/ced because CS will stop waiting.  So up it to a ping spike value (say 175-200).  This applies when you already have the map next in the server rotation.  When you do NOT have the map; it can take 2-3x as long to get new information (I don\'t know why, but it is so).  So if you\'re going to play on servers that have map rotations that you don\'t have... Take your ping and double/triple it and that should be your cl_timeout rate.\n\n__________________\n\nSYSTEM SPECS\n\n__________________\n\n\n\nOS: MS Windows XP Pro SP1\n\nHDs: 120 GB (NTFS) & 40 GB (FAT32)\n\nCPU: Intel Pentium 4 @ 2.53 GHz\n\nGPU: GeForce4 Ti 4600 128 MB (45.23 Drivers)\n\nPRAM: 1 GB DDRAM \n\nVMEM: 3.4 GB\n\nConnection: Comcast Cable (600/80 Kbps)\n\nSettings:\n\n-OpenGL w/VSync, AA, AF and TS Off\n\n-1280x1024 resolution\n\n-32-bit color\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.\n\n66.208.104.166:27015 - KDB pub\n\n69.56.171.228:27015 - S_c_T pub\n\n208.184.33.208:27015 - team.cH pub', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213587, 33639, 1005, 102370, 1072936800, '', 'Who says anything about maps that users don\'t have?\n\n\n\nAnd, my question is still, why this has been changed since cs 1.5 / early cs 1.6 versions. It hasn\'t been mentioned in any of the updates.\n\n\n\nWhy should people change there settings to play on some servers, when they could leve the settings, and play on other servers? It\'s the servers thats the problem here... how many times do I have to tell you that? :>\n\n\n\nIt would have been GREAT to get an official answer to some questions one day...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(213595, 33639, 1005, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'I gave you the reason and the solution, but you\'re choosing not to accept it - enjoy your problem ya m00c.\n\n__________________\n\nSYSTEM SPECS\n\n__________________\n\n\n\nOS: MS Windows XP Pro SP1\n\nHDs: 120 GB (NTFS) & 40 GB (FAT32)\n\nCPU: Intel Pentium 4 @ 2.53 GHz\n\nGPU: GeForce4 Ti 4600 128 MB (45.23 Drivers)\n\nPRAM: 1 GB DDRAM \n\nVMEM: 3.4 GB\n\nConnection: Comcast Cable (600/80 Kbps)\n\nSettings:\n\n-OpenGL w/VSync, AA, AF and TS Off\n\n-1280x1024 resolution\n\n-32-bit color\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.\n\n66.208.104.166:27015 - KDB pub\n\n69.56.171.228:27015 - S_c_T pub\n\n208.184.33.208:27015 - team.cH pub', '127.0.0.1', 1),
