(213608, 33639, 1005, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by loxtehfox \n\nI don\'t agree. You gave the players an soultion, not me.\n\n\n\nI, as the server admin, need an solution.  \n\n\n\nFine; here\'s a server-side solution.  FORCE a cl_timeout value of 200-300 on all your connects.  Was that too hard to think of - if they need higher cl_timeout values GIVE IT TO THEM.\n\n__________________\n\nSYSTEM SPECS\n\n__________________\n\n\n\nOS: MS Windows XP Pro SP1\n\nHDs: 120 GB (NTFS) & 40 GB (FAT32)\n\nCPU: Intel Pentium 4 @ 2.53 GHz\n\nGPU: GeForce4 Ti 4600 128 MB (45.23 Drivers)\n\nPRAM: 1 GB DDRAM \n\nVMEM: 3.4 GB\n\nConnection: Comcast Cable (600/80 Kbps)\n\nSettings:\n\n-OpenGL w/VSync, AA, AF and TS Off\n\n-1280x1024 resolution\n\n-32-bit color\n\n\n\nProud Co-Founder of the m00c Patrol.\n\n66.208.104.166:27015 - KDB pub\n\n69.56.171.228:27015 - S_c_T pub\n\n208.184.33.208:27015 - team.cH pub', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(215336, 33966, 1013, 102373, 1072936800, 'Win32 StructuredException', 'I\'m having a problem when i try to update counter-strike.\n\nWhenever i go to update it i get this error message:\n\n\n\nSteam.exe (main exception): Win32 StructuredException at 5FF32419 : Attempt to read from virtual address 0 without appropriate access rights\n\n\n\nthen when i hit \'ok\' i get:\n\n\n\nThe instruction at "0x100037bd" referenced memory at "0x01f3aae0". The memory could not be "read".\n\n\n\nI tried that panda thing but my IE doesnt work and i use msn explorer and when it asks to d/l the things during the panda scan, it wont do it cause i dont know how to set my default web browser in windows XP.\n\n\n\nplease help somebody :\\', '127.0.0.1', 1),
