(220044, 34788, 1013, 102383, 1072936800, 'Greaaaaaaaat new update now i can\'t play with direct3d', 'ok i\'m getting pretty fed up\n\n\n\n\n\nfirst i get the ID ticket error then i walk away to do something else...\n\n\n\nreconnect yay it works now i come back hours later and this new UPDATE comes up WTF another update so i download the update and BOOOOOOM! i can\'t play in direct3d it says not compatible BULL i was running it with no problems before now whats the deal?\n\n\n\ni think this may be the end of my joy with HL and its mods this is just getting rediculess...\n\n\n\nanyone able to help me out on why it won\'t let me use direct3d anymore?\n\n\n\ni\'m using a p4 1.6\n\n512MB \n\n20gig HD\n\nSiS onboard shared video card\n\n\n\nit was working perfectly before and now i\'m stuck!\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\nTim', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220078, 34788, 1013, 100145, 1072936800, '', 'One of the fixes in the most recent update is listed as...\n\n\n\nAdded fallback to software mode if selected video mode is not supported when game tries to start\n\n\n\n...it\'s possible that Steam is (incorrectly) detecting that D3D is not supported on your system. Can you post more detailed system specs including what drivers you are using?\n\n\n\nIn the meantime, have you tried running CS in OpenGL or Software mode?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220205, 34788, 1013, 102384, 1072936800, 'software mode', 'I have the same problem and when I change to software mode it changes my gun to left handed.  Sheeshh...took me tooooo long to learn to play right handed, now I have to learn all over again....  OpenGL just lags me to death, is there any fix or work around for direct3D?????  Or someone can tell me how to make it shoot right handed again-  I did go into options and advanced to be sure it was set to right hand as well as in my config file-  Thanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220228, 34788, 1013, 102385, 1072936800, '', 'Same specs as PsychiatristNET.\n\nAlways ran fine in D3D mode. Now it\'s suddenly not compatible.\n\nPretty sad how HL is falling apart now...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220462, 34788, 1013, 102386, 1072936800, '', 'd3d mode wont work for me on my lower end rig either.\n\n\n\nEven though it has been working fine for the past 5 years.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf software or opengl mode ran decent then i would use on of them.\n\n\n\nguess what though.   They dont run decent.\n\n\n\n\n\nWith the mods that are out now in day you would be very lucky if software mode ran all maps without crashing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220531, 34788, 1013, 102387, 1072936800, '', 'JESUS?? another update, this is why so many people has left CS coz of steam so buggy shoulda waited another year entill it was proply working 100% anyway im getting same problem  on both my top end PCs one AMD XP2800 and one P4 2.8ghz both with ti4200s now can sum1 please tell me wtf is going on ??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220533, 34788, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'Ok this is werid.\n\n\n\nIf Software mode is slow on a 1.6GHz CPU. Are you sure you arn\'t trying it?\n\n\n\n\n\nBecause it should go FAST!!! This is a game that run on software mode in 400MHz and ran about 30 frames per second. So you sould have no problem.\n\n\n\n\n\nI used to play CS in software mode on a 266MHz machine. It gave me at lest 20 frames.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn openGL, go to www.glsetup.com (http://www.glsetup.com) Run the application and it should install the latest OpenGL on your SYSTEM. Unless its a bran new video card.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(220578, 34788, 1013, 102386, 1072936800, '', 'Have you taken a look at software mode lately?  With mods of today?  with particle fx?  with model transparency\'s?\n\n\n\nThese new features can make some maps crash almost instantly on software mode.  \n\n\n\nHave you seen barbwire in games like dod?  nothing but an ugly blue tangle.  You cant even see through it.\n\n\n\nSome people just happen to have video cards that run better on d3d than opengl.  And no updated drivers is going to change that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
