look at them, making you think they are not looking at you,  then you get shot....\n\n\n\nalso the kar is ruined, you have basically given the allies the upper hand, you have weakened the kar, given the garrand more accuracy and left the british rifle alone..lol  i think that  needs more work too.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is not a flaming post, this is a post that needs to be read, valve your only hurting yourselves here.  Since steam has come about the entire HL community has been in kaos.  I have faith that you will correct these problems, but it would be nice to know that you actually do intend to do somethign about them...  i dunno what to suggest but maybe valve you should pop into a server or two and see for yourself.  \n\n\n\nHow do you know it bans players using Cheating-Death? \n\n\n\nYou should not be using CD if you\'re connecting to a VAC server - this warning is clearly written in the documentation for CD. Also, CD does kick you from joining a server if VAC is detected on that server.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(259896, 41362, 1005, 102483, 1072936800, '', 'but thats my point, why dont they work together and create a better community, instead of us struggling admins doing all the work and research into all these bugs and mishaps.  And it is true i have known players join my server with cheating death on and received a 8 year ban for it, yes it maybe there own fault for not checking to see if its secure or not, but should they be punished for a simple error?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(257481, 41764, 1013, 102503, 1072936800, 'Steam program opens but doesnt run', 'My steam opens up but it does not run. The icon is displayed but the game itself doesn\'t run. In the beginning, my 1.6 worked alright, but after awhile it didnot even run anymore.\n\n\n\nI am hooked up to my UC\'s connection, does that have anything to do with it? When i tried to fix it back at home it was a different problem happening then it was fixed. Once i got back to my college, the previous problem started again. Im thinking its the UC\'s connection.  I had to download certain things for the UC\'s connection to actually work on my computer.THis was in the beginning of the school year.\n\n\n\nI have tried downloading different steam_installs from different mirrors , but all have the same outcome of the steam program not running.\n\n\n\n\n\nEdit by Taylor Sherman:\n\n\n\nSo that people first reading this can find the latest easily:\n\n\n\nThis appears to be caused by a conflict between Steam and McAffee Personal Privacy / Privacy Service software. We\'re looking into what\'s going on and how to fix it.\n\n\n\nThe program "Steganos Internet Anonym" can also cause this problem.\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(257581, 41764, 1013, 102504, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same problem, any help would be great! Steam runs but i don\'t get a menu and no icon shows up in my tray. It worked fine last week. I never had any problems, then all of the sudden this happens. I tried reinstalling Steam, downloading it again, restarting computer, and everything else that was suggested in the technical support section over at Counter-strike.net forums and yet the problem continues. The problem started after the last update, it updated to 99% and then just stopped. I canceled the update and retried it and then i ran into this problem. I just wanna play the game that i paid for. I know the team is busy, but any new ideas would be helpful. \n\n\n\nP.S. \n\n\n\nPlease dont spam this thread with negative comments about Steam, because i would actuallly like one of them to respond and i never see them answer in the threads that degrade Steam!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(257587, 41764, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'Steam program opens but doesnt run', 'quote:Originally posted by Ruff619 \n\nMy steam opens up but it does not run. The icon is displayed but the game itself doesn\'t run. In the beginning, my 1.6 worked alright, but after awhile it didnot even run anymore.\n\n \n\n\n\nYou mean the icon shows up in the system tray? What happens when you double-click it?\n\n\n\nOr do you mean you launch the game from the Games window but nothing happens? I\'m confused.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(257594, 41764, 1013, 102504, 1072936800, '', 'Nothing happens when i lauch Steam. I press ctrl-alt-delete and it shows that steam is running and it gives me the option to end program, but even if i do and click lauch Steam again it still does not work.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(257735, 41764, 1013, 102505, 1072936800, '', 'i have the same problem!!  i double click steam on the desktop but nothing happens. under ctrl alt del, it shows the steam.exe process running but no icon or anything. i reinstalled and the same thing except now it uses 50% of the cpu which is ridiculous.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
