(259528, 41764, 1013, 102509, 1072936800, '', 'I have same prob from last update.\n\nafter double clicking Steam.exe,dont open steam window...[]\n\nbut steam was running background and use 100%CPU usage.\n\nI waited few minutes,but didnt run.\n\n\n\nrestart and reinstall was ineffective.\n\nI use WinXP.Then changed user and use other registry data,\n\nbut it was too(ineffective)\n\n\n\nI thought that other software installed on the previous \n\nday was the causes. I was uninstalled it.\n\nThen, steam was run!!!!!\n\nbut.....  didnt fixed this prob.It ran Only that time[]\n\ndouble click steam again,steam has become silent...\n\n\n\n\n\nI wana play CS~~[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(259590, 41764, 1013, 102510, 1072936800, '', 'it always happens.\n\nkeep trying until it works', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(261926, 41870, 1013, 100049, 1072936800, 'Bug Finding Help', 'There are a couple of bugs that we\'re having a bit of trouble tracking down. It would be extremely helpful if someone in the community could help out.\n\n\n\nThe bugs are:\n\n\n\n- Players starting the map either stuck in the floor or floating above ground.\n\n- Slow demo recording performance.\n\n- Crash on demo playback, possibly related to +showscores.\n\n\n\nIf you\'d like to help, record a demo that exhibits one or all of these behaviors and mail it to me at erik@valvesoftware.com (mailto:erik@valvesoftware.com).\n\n\n\nThanks.\n\n\n\nErik', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262086, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'Hello Erik,\n\n\n\nNot sure if this will help you or not, but MiSmith7 has found a temporary solution that seems to help.  It involves a demo fix written by Martino@valvesoftware.com (mailto:Martino@valvesoftware.com) that was dated a little over a year ago.\n\n\n\nThis was a fix for 1.5 demos that updated the GameEditor.dll and GameUI.dll in the valve\\cl_dlls folder, and the core.dll in the Counter Strike folder.  It was a "viewdemo" fix, or something like that.\n\n\n\nThe thread on how to watch demos without them crashing can be found here. (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=40705)  So far, following these steps at least allows us to watch demos without crashing, and also displays the scoreboard correctly.  (since the introduction of 1.6 they\'ve been blank, so this should be a step in the right direction, at least)\n\n\n\nI\'ll test and see if demos work launched straight from console, but I think they still crash unless you start a listenserver on the map the demo was recorded on.\n\n\n\nBut I figured maybe you could revisit these .dll\'s and figure out a way to combine them into 1.6 and maybe find the solution you\'re looking for.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262112, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'Also, as for the players floating in the air... someone in the bug list thread suggested this is caused by custom decals being downloaded to the client.  This makes perfect sense because generally the only time it happens is during the pistol round on a map change (when most decals are downloaded, obviously).  And I would bet money the random times it happens during a round is when a new player has just connected, and his decal is being uploaded.\n\n\n\nSo far, the only testing of this theory I can provide is I have had\n\n\n\ncl_allowdownload "0"\n\ncl_download_ingame "0"\n\ncl_allowupload "0"\n\n\n\nset for about a week now, and haven\'t had it happen at all.\n\n\n\nSo that\'s at least one area to look into for a fix.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262158, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, scratch that first post.  On a whim I decided to delete the DemoEditor.dll and GameUI.dll, and replaced the core.dll with the default one.  These have nothing to do with the fix.\n\n\n\nSimply starting a listenserver on the map the demo was recorded on is what allows the scoreboard to display properly and doesn\'t crash the demo, either.\n\n\n\nSo those .dll\'s had nothing to do with the demos working right.\n\n\n\n-edit- also tried launching demo straight from console via splash screen...and it crashed on first scoreboard viewing.\n\n\n\nstarting a listenserver on the map the demo was made on is the key to them not crashing.  so i hope that helps figure out why...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262324, 41870, 1013, 102292, 1072936800, '', 'radar not always on even when drawradar "1" in console\n\n\n\nd3d not working and look at my specs i use opengl fine but i like d3d to!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262607, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'dude, read the friggin\' topic and the first post.  this isn\'t a bug list thread.  it\'s a thread for people to help narrow down the 3 bugs that are listed.  not to post new ones...or rather...very old ones.  use the bug report thread.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262755, 41870, 1013, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'Indeed, turns out the viewdemo fix has nothing to do with the problem.  The demos crashing is directly related to the +showscores command.  There are currently 2 methods of fixing this, hex-edit out all the +showscores and replace them with -showscores, or this:\n\n\n\n1) Load up CS from the \'Games\' window of STEAM.\n\n\n\n2) Click on "New Server" (listen server) and load up the map the demo you are trying to view was recorded on.\n\n\n\n3) Wait for the server to load, then go into spectator mode.\n\n\n\n4) Bring up the console, and view the demo using the "viewdemo" command.\n\n\n\nNot only does this prevent the crash - it actually shows what the scores were.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(262792, 41870, 1013, 102511, 1072936800, 'Erik, your mail server is not being nice!', 'Erik,\n\nI just emailed you three times, trying to send you a link to a demo. Your mail server wont accept attachments.\n\n\n\nYour email keeps bouncing back undeliverable, even without the demo.\n\n\n\nPM me and I\'ll give you my contact information, or anything else I can help with!\n\nAnd the link to this demo is http://216.240.145.190/~viper/ocs12.zip (http://216.240.145.190/~viper/ocs12.zip)\n\n\n\nThe beginning of the demo shows a player on the back deck of the militia house, when in fact, he is under the stairway, not on the deck. As I toggled between players and back to him, he was under the stairs where he should have been.\n\n\n\nThe beginning of the next round shows the +scoreboard crash as soon as I enter the tunnel from CT spawn.\n\n\n\n \n\nThanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(263951, 41870, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Erik Johnson, I have reported about the floating/sinking player model issue many times before.  I am almost certain it is because of this:\n\n\n\nWhenever I see a player(s) shoot up in the air or sink in the ground, I check my console.  There will be a message that says:\n\n\n\n"Requesting pldecal.wad file from the server"\n\n\n\nEvery time this message appears in the console, floating/sinking player models appear.  EVERY TIME.  I have verified this throughly and many others on the same server, other servers, my friends and people on these forums have verified it before.  This doesn\'t just happen on pistol rounds/map starts.  It happens anytime the server requests a pldecal.wad file.\n\n\n\nThe server requesting pldecal.wads from players is the cause of this issue.  I hope this helps.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(265554, 41870, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', '^^ At first I was skeptical of that, but I validated it the other night.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(266975, 41870, 1013, 102060, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, I am so certain that the server requesting pldecal.wad\'s is the cause of this issue, that is why I didn\'t provide any screenshots or demos (which I can easily do).  If anybody thinks I am incorrect or if you are skeptical, see for yourself.  Next time you see your teammate shoot up into the sky, bring down your console.  I am 100% sure there will be a message saying "Requesting pldecal.wad from server".', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(267697, 41870, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Here is a little additional information.\n\n\n\nLast night during a 2x3 match in HLDM everything was fine until the match ended and we changed maps.\n\n\n\nDuring the first minute or so, one client out of the five of us saw one other player floating in midair.\n\n\n\nThe player was moving around, then suddenly fell down and was normal again.\n\n\n\nDuring this time, the HLTV proxy was recording the entire thing, but when I went back and viewed the recording, there was nothing wrong and all players were on the ground running around like normal.\n\n\n\nThis tells me that the player position data the server was sending out was good all the time, and the problem is a client related one only.\n\n\n\nThe only client that saw the problem was also the client that was closest to the server, actually on a LAN so there was no internet connection issues at all.\n\n\n\nThe rest of us were on Internet.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278028, 41870, 1013, 102511, 1072936800, '', 'Erik... any news? This thread is getting buried! Bump!!!!\n\n\n\nIf you need any more demo samples, please let us know!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278153, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'just wondering if it\'s possible to separate the pldecal wad request into it\'s own cvar.  so instead of turning off allowing all downloads we could simply turn off decal downloading.  like\n\n\n\ncl_decaldownload "0"\n\n\n\nor something.  i know a large percentage of people could care less about seeing others decals, but would still be able to get maps and sounds, etc from the server.\n\n\n\nthis would at least eliminate this bug.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278373, 41870, 1013, 102512, 1072936800, '', 'Hi Erik,\n\n\n\nI too have the same problem with demo playback. Only mine is varied slightly. about 4 days ago i could play demos. I even record some clips out of them for my cs movie. But recently I keep getting the crash problem. I took note that it only happened when +showscores was hit in the demo. Good lucky on fixing the glitch\n\n\n\n-clue', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(279576, 41870, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Fragalishus \n\njust wondering if it\'s possible to separate the pldecal wad request into it\'s own cvar.  so instead of turning off allowing all downloads we could simply turn off decal downloading.  like\n\n\n\ncl_decaldownload "0"\n\n\n\nor something.  i know a large percentage of people could care less about seeing others decals, but would still be able to get maps and sounds, etc from the server.\n\n\n\nthis would at least eliminate this bug.  \n\n\n\nThe cvar is cl_download_ingame. It\'s 1 by default. It was already posted on the first page.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(279626, 41870, 1013, 102513, 1072936800, '', 'Maybe you can compare with TFC and see the differans in the source code and fix it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(280405, 41870, 1013, 100796, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Master_America \n\nThe cvar is cl_download_ingame. It\'s 1 by default. It was already posted on the first page.  \n\n\n\nand did you read who posted it?\n\n\n\ni\'m not entirely sure that has solely to do with decals.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(280684, 41870, 1013, 102514, 1072936800, '', 'yea i have the players stuck in the ground or in mid-air.  But it usually doesnt happen at the start of a map it happens during the middle of the map.  usually i fix this by looking away from all players for a few seconds then it seems to be fixed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(307506, 41870, 1013, 102515, 1072936800, '', 'One thing I noticed is that I have never seen the floating model bug on an insecure server, but then again it may just be luck.  Since alot of people have narrowed this problem to the downloading of custom spray decals, im thinking that the download of the pldecal.wad  may be triggering, in part,  the security modules anti-wall hack.  On the other hand, I may have seen this problem before the awhack was installed back in 1.4.  Im sure I never seen the problem in cs 1.3.  \n\n\n\nA 2nd possibility is the use of colour custom sprays which are generally larger in size then the defaults.  \n\n\n\nA 3rd possibility is that the download of decals is somehow interfering with the clients model interpolation.  A mod called "Laser Mod" confirmed for me that the interpolation of visible models was causing the model to delay behind where the server tells the client where the player is. This laser mod enabled a laser showing exactly what a player was looking at while you were dead.  The laser would always lead the model, but was more accurate with a lower ex_interp value.  I noticed that the 1st person camera locks onto the interpolated model and not the exact positional data recieved from the server. 1st person is also affected by this floating models bug.  \n\n\n\nWhatever the problem is, it has to be client side as random people are affected at different times.\n\n\n\n\n\nAs for the slow demo recording performance,  I have so far managed to narrow the problem to people using 33MHz hard-drives/hard-drive cables.  So maybe the recording process is sending alot more data then is required, using excessive processor power thus causing the drop in performance while recording.  Again this could be luck, but its a working theory for now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(321536, 41870, 1013, 102472, 1072936800, '', 'lol..the demo crash is from 1.6 demos before that update the week they started..i forgot which update but, after that update previous 1.6 demos always crash upon the point where the person or w/e hits scoreboard (+showscores)~\n\n\n\nit never occurs on demos after that update\n\n\n\nthe simple fix which was known fairly common (so easy that someone made a \'utility\' to get credit for fixing everyone\'s problem, for the \'computer\' illiterate ppl i guess)..the workaround, not really a fix, was to change all the +showscores to -showscores -- so therefore +showscore never occurs during the demo (hence no crash) -- this of course was done using a hexeditor and Find&replace ^^\n\n\n\n(way to drag stuff out of proportion guys..)\n\n\n\nas for the others, neva experienced those bugs (i don\'t pub too much)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(321538, 41870, 1013, 102472, 1072936800, '', 'i forgot to mention, i have allowupload and dl set to 0, so maybe that\'s why...but y would the uploading affect anything (of a pldecal) unless maybe its a custom decal :o\n\n\n\ni think uh, custom decals are fishy nowadays aren\'t they...?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(333918, 41870, 1013, 100253, 1072936800, '', 'I dont know much but it seems to only  happen at the beginning of the round(usually on counter-strike)  and they dont notice it...and it is only noticable to you.  No one else seems to notice.  And it dosent appear as much as it did when steam first came out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(354067, 41870, 1013, 102516, 1072936800, '', 'wen i watching a demo it hapens somethimes that ct player have the skin of terror and the HEgranade is a smokegranate\n\n\n\nand wen i play cs and dod, some players are invisible (cant se them ) when they are front of me its lame its like walking and than i cant go anny furder like i going in a invisible wall and gett killet \n\nsome thimes i can se all walking in the sky \n\ni have readed an article that if you se people walking in the sky\n\nit means that one player are trying to hack the server or have turned the cheats on ...\n\nthanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(375109, 41870, 1013, 102517, 1072936800, '', 'I get the scoreboard in viewdemo... maybe i\'m just lucky?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(377017, 41870, 1013, 102518, 1072936800, '', 'Start a server with the same map as the demo before you play back the demo and the showscores will work..?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(385576, 41870, 1013, 102519, 1072936800, '', 'I found a bug with steam, when I login into steam it asks me to put in my cd key. The problem is when I made the account I put in my cd key. Why does it want me to put in my cd key again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
