(269376, 41915, 1005, 102528, 1072936800, '', 'I am running a linux with a xp2400 and i can\'t even mange 22 without bumping pings.\n\n\n\nIt\'s a complete joke and then i find a p4 2.4 can do 64 players easy. ANOTHER JOKE.\n\n\n\nI ain\'t paying **** much money for a server, when steam is so screwed up, I say everyone go bk to 3.1 as a protest. []\n\n\n\nzippy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(271276, 41915, 1005, 102529, 1072936800, '', 'I couldn\'t agree more.  It\'s a shame to see such a fantastic operating system take so much "hate" from Valve.  Either hate or just disregard.  It\'s kinda like if we were talking cars here - giving the beat up \'88 LeMans top notch fuel but throwing discount crap in the Ferrari.  I have the hardware, I have the OS - now I just need decent Steam binaries.... :\'(', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(273286, 41915, 1005, 102530, 1072936800, 'improve linux on athlon/athlon XP', 'there been roumors that the amd optimized linux files are not designed for athlon and athlon XP processors. the code is for older cpus.. (can not understand that).\n\nafter some testing it seems that a linux amd athlon XP server runs much smoother if you force hlds_run to use i686 setup..\n\nI have only tested this for a week not in full scale on our server but on a match server and it seems that the roumors are correct.. the server runs smoother and the client will feel no lag or jeryness..\n\nto test this you only  need to alter one thing\n\nedit hlds_run\n\ntheese lines\n\nHL=./hlds_i686\n\nHL_DETECT=0 (to disable autodetect)\n\n\n\nacknowledgement to XAD who brought this to my attension...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(264385, 42193, 1005, 102531, 1072936800, 'How bad is it really', 'How bad is linux compared to windows really\n\nLike if you ran a 20 player CS Server\n\n\n\nHow much does windows use\n\n\n\n\n\nHow much does linux use? in cpu', '127.0.0.1', 1),
