(275083, 43650, 1013, 102554, 1072936800, 'delete Steam.exe failed', 'in regards to your guy\'s replies for my:\n\nSteam.exe (main exception): ERROR: delete of Steam.exe failed, Win32 Error 5 "Access is denied"\n\n\n\nYes, I do have Admin privleges. Of course Steam is running, ITS TRYING TO UPDATE! :> then gets that error, and exits, its NOT running in the background after the error! I\'ll get ya\' my puter specs too, maybe that\'ll help...\n\n\n\nWindows XP home\n\nPentium 4 2gighz\n\n640mb ram\n\n64mb geforce (2 I think)\n\n120 gig hd\n\nand poopy 56k connection\n\n\n\nAnd please nobody say its my connection why im getting this error, cause I know its not!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(275085, 43650, 1013, 102554, 1072936800, 'Delete Steam.exe failed', 'Oh yeah, i\'ve even tried going into the command prompt and using:  attrib -r steam.exe.... didnt work :,<', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(275133, 43650, 1013, 102552, 1072936800, '', 'X_X yea iv tried lots of stuff too, with no effect', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(275156, 43650, 1013, 102558, 1072936800, '', 'Let me just say....w00t!!\n\n\n\nI\'ve been experiancing all the problems that you guys have. Delete steam.exe and all that junk. Well I think I found a way to fix. \n\n\n\nWhen I tried updating, it would keep giving me error messages after 26%. So I went into my steam directory and found that Steam had made two new files. SteamTMP and Steam_new Or something on the lines of that. What I did, was delete the old steam.exe and the steamtmp, and renamed the stean_new to steam_new01. Thus the steamnew file being the only .exe in the folder. Oh the steamnew file\'s size is 1.03mb I think, and the older one was 956kb or something close to that. \n\n\n\nAfter that, I tried updating with only the steam_new01 in the folder....I only got a cannot connect to network... -_- so that this morning I went into the folder, and got the idea to do the same thing I did last night, but after deleting all the other .exe files, I renamed the new .exe that was 1.03 mb, to steam.exe (same name as old one) It started to update. *i held my breath* and then once it got to 26%....it stopped, dissapeared, and then came back up again, but only to be at 29%...at that point I was overjoyed. I don\'t know why the steam.exe files are all getting screwed up, but this seems to work.\n\n\n\nI hope this has helped you guys, please post telling me what you get.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(276725, 43929, 1013, 102559, 1072936800, 'Steam Monitor...', 'why is that limit network usage and pause all updates faded out all the time, r we able to use it? or is it something valve r working on or what, i\'ve never seen it not faded b4, so what\'s the deal with that?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(276732, 43929, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'This feature hasn\'t been enabled yet, has never been enabled.\n\n\n\nShould work sometime later when everything else gets stable enough to play with it.\n\n__________________\n\nWould you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(276870, 43929, 1013, 102560, 1072936800, '', 'what does it do? monitor what games its updating?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(276908, 43929, 1013, 102561, 1072936800, 'yupp', 'everytime a game is updated, you can check the bandwith usage on the monitor.\n\n__________________\n\nP4 1.8GHz\n\nAopen AX4B mobo\n\nGeForce 3 Ti 200 64MB\n\n512MB PC-2100 DDR\n\nWD 120GB HD\n\nMicrosoft Intelli Explorer 3\n\nfUnc 1030\n\nHitachi CM640ET Monitor\n\n\n\nPlay CS @ 1024x768 @ 85Hz\n\n85 fps+/- :D , Sens 5.0', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(276990, 43929, 1013, 102562, 1072936800, 'The Monitor', 'OK, I asked this when the steam forums first started up,\n\n "What is the monitor for?, and if it is only a monitor for network usage, isn\'t it just going to use unneeeded bandwidth usage.\n\n "Does it cause any us to store any extra junk on our pcs?.\n\nI dont really need to know the network usage to tell me if I want to play, do I?.\n\n Yes, your right, I don\'t have a clue what it is for and would appreciate if someone could explain the need for the monitor.\n\n Thanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(277388, 43929, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'The monitor portion of the Steam interface only functions when content is being downloaded to your client, and at that only content associated with Steam or the MOD you play that is an update.\n\n\n\nWhen it is displaying information, it doesn\'t take any additional resources, only displays what is going on, and nothing additional (for the monitor that is) is stored on your computer.\n\n\n\nThe display of the Monitor certainly does not take any bandwidth away from your gameplay itself, although the content or update being sent to you certainly does use incoming bandwith mostly and a very small amount of outgoing bandwidth.\n\n\n\nThe graph you see just displays when and how much information is being sent to your computer as well as what MOD the content is for.\n\n\n\nThe limit rate and button are there so you can eventually control how fast you want to get content.  On dsl or cablemodem you would probably not want to limit it at all, on dial-up modem you might want to set it to a smaller value while you are playing only.\n\n\n\nThe "need" for this monitor is so you know Steam and/or MODs are being updated in the background, otherwise how would you know?\n\n__________________\n\nWould you like a little Cheeze with that Whine?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(277513, 43929, 1013, 102562, 1072936800, 'Quicksilver', 'Thanks for the info, i appreciate it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278375, 44186, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, 'If you get a crash after restarting/relogging into Steam!!!', 'If after the latest update, you get an error looking something like this...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nsteam.exe (main exception): Win32 StructuredException at 0163048B: Attempt to write to virtual address 2439276314 without appropriate access rights.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSTEAM.EXE - APPLICATION ERROR\n\n\nThe instruction at "0x1000ecd" referenced memory at "0x016470c0." The memory could not be "read." \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[edited by Greg; see note below]\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is a known issue with the Steam developers, and I am sure they will be working on a fix to push out soon.  In the mean time, an apology for this error :^(', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(279114, 44186, 1013, 100785, 1072936800, '', 'A fix for this problem has just been released -- please restart Steam to automatically download the fix. \n\n\n\n\n\nThe crash mentioned above should no longer occur. Please let us know if you continue to have problems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(318045, 44186, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'It looks like this came back. Right now, the fix is to delete the file SteamUI.dll and launch Steam.\n\n__________________\n\nSteam Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278588, 44227, 1013, 102563, 1072936800, 'problem with steam', 'I have started Steam today and i have this error message \n\nhttp://www.guardian-forces.com/balder/problem.jpg (http://www.guardian-forces.com/balder/problem.jpg)\n\ni hope you can help me because yesterday steam work with no error []\n\n\n\nps:in the channel steam has one say i deleted clientregistry.blob and now it works [] thx', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(278606, 44227, 1013, 102255, 1072936800, '', 'Its amazing what reading the forums can do for ya! :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(279527, 44227, 1013, 102564, 1072936800, 'yeah right.', 'I have started Steam today and i have this error message \n\nhttp://www.guardian-forces.com/balder/problem.jpg (http://www.guardian-forces.com/balder/problem.jpg) \n\ni hope you can help me because yesterday steam work with no error  \n\n\n\nps:in the channel steam has one say i deleted clientregistry.blob and now it works  thx\n\n\n\n\n\nBut then there\'s those of us that deleting the clientregistry.blob does nothing for.  I was a supporter of Steam, knew it was shakey, and now I\'ve got one foot on the, "I Hate Steam" bandwagon.  I\'ve been playing Counter-Strike since beta 1.7 and have never had problems, but now i\'m lucky to play at all.  Makes me sick.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(284520, 45348, 1013, 102565, 1072936800, '#Steam Ops of GamesNET on STRIKE', 'Due to the lack of adequete information(on bugs and fixes) and/or recognition from the good people at VALVE, some of the ops(including me) have gone on STRIKE.\n\n\n\n\n\nSeeing as how we know as much as the users, we have no other choice but to let VALVe handle their own customers support requests with the support department that they don\'t seem to have.\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestions, commands, or concerns can be addressed here or at fds@neonblu.com (mailto:fds@neonblu.com)\n\n\n\n\n\n-FuhrerDarqueSyde|CH\n\n\nGamesNET #Steam Master OP\n\n__________________\n\nFuhrerDarqueSyde - #Steam-Hangout\n\n\n\n\n\nTravis Gutjahr\n\n\nNeonblu Technologies', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(284527, 45348, 1013, 102566, 1072936800, '', 'Im gonna be following FDS, its very hard to help people when you have 0 Information on the patch or upcoming changes!\n\n\n<br>\n\n\nIt is also very hard to help when people are arguing with you becuase they expect us to know every thing, when we learn from only Trial and Error :\\\n\n__________________\n\nOffical steam mascot!\n\n\nCome chat with me at.\n\n\n\n\n\nGamesnet.irc   #steam-hangout', '127.0.0.1', 1),
