(566231, 46456, 1013, 103445, 1072936800, '', 'but i don get what our connection has to do wit dis...\n\n\n\n"bad prase in client command" can tat mean tat the client is doing something wrong to make this happen?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(566373, 46456, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Bad Parse means that a packet of information that your client sent to the server got messed up.\n\n\n\nRouters handle all packets from the client going out to the world and then handle all packets coming back in.\n\n\n\nIf anything is wrong with the router\'s programming then it may improperly handle the data which can lead to this problem.\n\n\n\nPlayers that can connect to insecure servers but not secure servers almost always have out-of-date router firmware.\n\n\n\nThe other source of this problem is if you have spyware on your computer like marketscore or ISPs like freeserve and some AOL connections where all your data is sent to one of their routers and the data gets messed up there.\n\n\n\nIn that case, the solution is to remove the spyware:\n\nWhat to Do About SpyWare & Virus Problems FAQ (/forums/showthread.php?threadid=76462)\n\nremove yourself from the "transparent proxy" service that the ISP has your connection on (some UK ISPs are doing this) or get a new ISP.\n\n\n\nThere are a few other things that might cause this but these ones I\'ve listed are the most common.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(566445, 46456, 1013, 103447, 1072936800, '', 'Hi Quicksilver,\n\n\n\nNice to see someone is finally helping us out. Right..I\'m getting "Bad command character in client command" what are your thoughts on this mate? I have a router but i can play any other game FINE and not get disconnected so can you really say its poor router software programming or poor programming (on values end of course) ? Is there a fix that value will release? It\'s starting to pi$$ off a lot of people now...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(566456, 46456, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Proof is in the pudding Sniffy.\n\n\n\nIf you can plug your computer directly into your modem and bypass the router and everything works then you have your answer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(568135, 46456, 1013, 103447, 1072936800, '', 'Thats my problem matey, my modem and router is built in one so i can\'t remove my router [] There might be a setting but should i have to so i can play counter-strike? Asking a bit too much for someones whos paid for it. So Value isn\'t releasing a fix for this bug? Thank you for your input Quicksilver, i really am grateful mate.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(568362, 46456, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, "Bad command character in client mod" is the one that I uassly get.\n\n\n\nBut I dont remember getting this in 1.5 or anything.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569954, 46456, 1013, 103447, 1072936800, '', 'Quick, \n\n\n\nCan ya tell us if Value are looking into a fix?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(570407, 46456, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'As far as I know right now, this is a client system problem and not a Valve problem.\n\n\n\nIn every instance that it\'s been seen in the past, it was solved by one or more of the solutions I\'ve detailed as long as the player actually tried it and followed through.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, this problem doesn\'t seem to be one of those that can be replicated easily, if at all.\n\n\n\nYou have to realise that if I was sitting there at your computer trying to solve this problem, I would follow exactly the steps I\'ve detailed ... but the difference is at each step how the problem changes tells me something that I could use for the next step.\n\n\n\nSince I\'m not there, I\'m mostly blind, and if I\'m lucky enough to get a solution in place, most players usually never even tell me they are so happy to be able to play.\n\n\n\nThe only other possible solution that has worked in the past (that I know of) was to replace the network card, but this is difficult and not a guaranteed solution either, although not that expensive these days.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297075, 46948, 1013, 102573, 1072936800, 'confirmation please?', 'hey, it seems that Erik Johnson has posted on GotFrag but it seems unlikely\n\n\n\nhttp://gotfrag.com/?node=featurec&a...CD2084#comments (http://gotfrag.com/?node=featurec&id=428&x=CFCD2084#comments)\n\ncomment #490\n\n\n\ncan we get any confirmaton on this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297113, 46948, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s legit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297118, 46948, 1013, 102583, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Waldo \n\nIt\'s legit.  \n\n\n\nYay!!!  I think I just pooped my pants!!!  The new money system and bomb-plant-timer-stop are things that will make competitive play much more interesting.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297133, 46948, 1013, 102573, 1072936800, '', 'very interesting\n\n\n\nthanks waldo!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297153, 46948, 1013, 102584, 1072936800, '', 'wont laod for me, anyone gotta quote?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297164, 46948, 1013, 102573, 1072936800, '', 'quote:There will be some changes to the Counter-Strike money system on the 14th of January that should address some of the issues raised here.\n\n\n\nWe\'re still working out the specifics, but the intention is to make the tactic of waiting for the round to end on the T side a disincentive.\n\n\n\nWe\'ll also change the round timer to shut off once the bomb has been planted on de_ maps.\n\n\n\nErik Johnson\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297286, 46948, 1013, 102585, 1072936800, '', 'Wow. Thats all I can say. I never thought I\'d see valve actually listen to gamers, especially pro-gamers(Valve seems to favor the pubbers, as thats where their money is from).\n\nThanks Valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297317, 46948, 1013, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'It\'ll improve things on the pub side as well. As with adding the +3 frag bonus for planting and defusing, altering the money system and allowing the T\'s to plant even with a second left on the round timer will mean that the T\'s have incentive to finish the objective, and also means that CTs can\'t wait out the round timer if the bomb is planted too late.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297327, 46948, 1013, 102586, 1072936800, '', 'very nice to see that valve DOES listen to the community, keep up the good work', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297338, 46948, 1013, 100849, 1072936800, 'er.....so what?', 'ok this is kinda nice but...eh...what are you all woo-hooing about?\n\nThese are minor changes I say. Dont get me wrong, it\'s good they fix these things but I think they should care more about things like these!\n\n\n\n-AA which doesnt work right now: FPS drop like MAD\n\nalso Direct3d is not quite bugless yet, altough really close.\n\n\n\n-the dual elites suck (no-one would even like them as a start-round gift like the USP or Glock. These weapons actually are useable)\n\n\n\n-almost all other pistols (non-glock, non-usp, non-deagle) are not worth buying :P... almost noone likes them well enough to actually buy them every round... no-one is serious about consistency in buying them, even when using a shield when most players will just take the "good old" desert eagle...\n\n\n\n-TMP, UMP, P90, Mac-10 are almost always not even near the effectiveness of the Mp5. \n\n\n\nThese are my suggestions for future updates.\n\n\n\nWALTER PPK WISHES A HAPPY NEW YEAR TO EVERYBODY!!!\n\nexcept to Osama bin Laden and Sadam Houssein []. **** them []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297341, 46948, 1013, 102573, 1072936800, 'er.....so what?', 'quote:Originally posted by Walter_PPK \n\nok this is kinda nice but...eh...what are you all woo-hooing about?\n\nThese are minor changes I say. Dont get me wrong, it\'s good they fix these things but I think they should care more about things like these!\n\n\n\n-AA which doesnt work right now: FPS drop like MAD\n\nalso Direct3d is not quite bugless yet, altough really close.\n\n\n\n-the dual elites suck (no-one would even like them as a start-round gift like the USP or Glock. These weapons actually are useable)\n\n\n\n-almost all other pistols (non-glock, non-usp, non-deagle) are not worth buying :P... almost noone likes them well enough to actually buy them every round... no-one is serious about consistency in buying them, even when using a shield when most players will just take the "good old" desert eagle...\n\n\n\n-TMP, UMP, P90, Mac-10 are almost always not even near the effectiveness of the Mp5. \n\n\n\nThese are my suggestions for future updates.\n\n\n\nWALTER PPK WISHES A HAPPY NEW YEAR TO EVERYBODY!!!\n\nexcept to Osama bin Laden and Sadam Houssein []. **** them [] \n\nlearn about clan-warring first then comment on the usefullness of these changes\n\n\n\nthanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297355, 46948, 1013, 102585, 1072936800, '', 'This is much bigger than two updates (both of which are actually pretty big as far as clans go), this is us(the gaming community) noticing something wrong, writing a highly informative post about it (thanks shaguar), and valve saying "hey, you have a point".', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297364, 46948, 1013, 102587, 1072936800, 'New Gametypes', 'I hope this happens.  It would be a first for Valve in quite some time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat about bringing in some new gameplay styles or scenarios?\n\n\n\nHow about having a Terrorist VIP (Mob Boss or Drug Lord) that the CT\'s have to take out? This would be the easiest to implement and it would counter as_oilrig.\n\n\n\nWhat about the Terrorists having to steal some data from multiple locations (2 objectives)?  You would have to break your teams into 2 teams with coordinated attacks and defense.  You could even do this with the CT\'s and have hostages at 2 locations.  Just like having 2 bomb points.\n\n\n\nWhat ever happened to the vehicles or at least the moving items?  cs_alpin has a gondola, which is pretty fun.  Add some more maps with elevators that can be stopped or broken.  Bring some excitement back into the game!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297368, 46948, 1013, 102588, 1072936800, '', 'Roger That :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(297374, 46948, 1013, 102585, 1072936800, '', 'at the risk of going offtopic to reply to SxRxRnR:\n\n\n\nI agree that this is a first in some time (ignoring the slight change in 1.6beta of reverting to showing DEAD on scoreboard while alive), this is much more like the days of \'the scoped m4 is unfair\', \'p90 is too powerful\', and all of the map complaints.\n\n\n\nterrorist assasination maps would have to be well made, I\'d rather see es_ brought back.\n\n\n\nRTCW style stealing two documents would be really interesting to see, as it would be a huge political shift (probably one valve wouldn\'t want to risk making). Think it through for a bit, why would \'Terrorists\' want to steal documents? Maybe its because these are documents proving government action against their country that the govt tried to coverup, thus the debate of Terrorist vs Freedom Fighter begins.\n\n\n\nAnd vehicels were removed because they were too buggy in HL1. You duck, you die. You jump, you die. You look at a jeep the wrong way, you die.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298436, 47139, 1013, 102589, 1072936800, 'The Future of Anti-Hack Technology', 'Writing anti-hack technology & programs that detect foreign objects on a machine is actually a lot like anti-virus, difference being anti-virus companies have a lot more experience at it. \n\n\n\nI\'d like to see an anti-virus company take interest in this problem. I believe an anti-virus company (jointly or not) could probly produce the most effective anti-hack software/detection ever seen. An anti-virus company could do this jointly with another (gaming) company, produce their own software/standard (like pb) or even integrate definitions into current/public AV software\n\n\n\nNot only could the anti-hack/anti-virus-like software be built into the gaming client but the definitions could also be passed over to the actual normal/public anti-virus software and/or easily could \'lock\'/remove files/modifications from the user, which it already does anyways when \'viruses\' are detected. (or even auto report to the associated gaming company that a hack has been detected) \n\n\n\nIf you had to uninstall your anti virus completely, previous to putting a hack on your system or using it at all, to get your hack to function, a lot of ppl would think twice. Push come to shove having anti-virus programs auto report a hack could eliminate the possibility of uninstalling the anti-virus to get the hack to function. What if you could only scan your system for viruses if you had the hack completely removed from your system first. Keep in mind every piece of software leaves something behind even after being \'removed\'. Current AV software can already detect viruses that have been previously removed. What if it actually came down to not being able to use any anti-virus software at all if you\'ve ever had a hack on your system. This in combo with an AV company working on some kind of AV/AH integration/detection on the actual gaming client could slow this problem way down.\n\n\n\nAnother issue to bring up is the fact that a lot of Anti-Virus companies already detect \'hacking programs/exploits\' that aren\'t viruses at all, if it was globally/widely accepted that online gaming hacks are considered to be on the same level of threat, then their definitions could be passed around such globally between AV companies. Even on this (lower) level the file(s) would be locked from the user if the AV was running/installed.\n\n\n\nWhatever anti-virus company makes the move first will surely be bringing in the profits. Lets face it, when it comes to detecting un-wanted software anti-virus companies have been doing it for quite a while, its time to stop trying to make everything from scratch, and team up with people who\'ve been doing this for a very long time. \n\n\n\nIf an anti-virus company got involved in any fashion regardless of how (joint or not) i believe would make quite a difference.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298484, 47139, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'lol, actually, a lot of the people who made punkbuster used to work for macafee and symantic.\n\n\n\nBut your idea is very interesting. But AV company\'s would want to charge for there software. It\'ll cost Valve lots for them incorperate it. Valve themselfs can do a very good job of stop lots of hack but the problem is, VAC is never updated.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf punkbuster was supported in CS and used instead of VAC, it would be a lot hacker-free.\n\n\n\nI think punkbuster is one of the best anti-hack programs ever.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298491, 47139, 1013, 102589, 1072936800, '', 'Certainly it would cost money, however i think people (including me) would be willing to pay a cpl extra dollars. Both sides could actually make money off the deal. Picture a nice big AV company stamp on the box the game comes in with something like "anti hack, powered by <x> (anti virus company)" it\'d look & sound good & it\'d work! + the AV company of choice would be able to distro a great free demo of their products with the game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298493, 47139, 1013, 102590, 1072936800, '', 'This is a really good idea! Too bad ideas like that just get burried and die. =/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298667, 47139, 1013, 102591, 1072936800, '', 'Punkbuster is the best anti cheat program by far. Look at Americas army and RTCW:ET, no hacks if any, very very very little.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298683, 47139, 1013, 102592, 1072936800, '', 'yups...have to agree it does sound interesting...but as sum1 else put it..."it will just get buried"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298685, 47139, 1013, 100355, 1072936800, '', 'your retarded man', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298962, 47139, 1013, 102593, 1072936800, '', 'You don\'t want to be looking for hacks that have already been removed, because then people who have legitimate uses for them (league admins that want to check demos against known hacks, clan leaders that want to test certain cheats so that they know what to look for when recruiting people, that sort of thing) won\'t be able to install them, use them with VAC off, delete them, and continue playing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(298994, 47139, 1013, 102594, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Blaze947 \n\nyour retarded man  \n\nAnd you are pointlessly insulting. \n\n\n\nFurthermore your inability to spell a simple word like "you\'re" is revealing. Either you are not old enough to have attended school yet or you weren\'t paying attention when you did. I suggest that you take your posting to mummy or teacher to have it checked before you submit it. Otherwise you should try acting your age.\n\n\n\nBGL:\n\n\n\nAn interesting idea but the exploits are generally particular to each game. To make a product like that commercially viable it would probably need to support more than one game/engine. This would make it considerably more difficult to program and support. It might be viewed as analogous to a single anti-virus program that works on many different operating systems? \n\n\n\nOf course there are AV programs that support more than one version of Windows, but tens or even hundreds of them might be a little too ambitious. []\n\n\n\nFinally, I am not sure that the similarity between the expertises you describe is actually relevant. Writing anti-hack programs requires knowledge of the game and the way it works. Anti-virus technologies focus primarily on the operating system so I am not sure the skills would necessarily be appropriate.\n\n\n\nHaving said that. I would not completely rule your ideas out.\n\n\n\nIt is good to see someone trying to come up with constructive suggestions, instead of fatuous abuse.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299090, 47139, 1013, 100250, 1072936800, '', 'America\'s Army and RTCW:ET are much less popular than HL/CS.\n\n\n\nThe HL engine is quite simply a bigger target for hackers than AA and RTCW:ET. It\'s like why Windows gets hacked more than Linux. Sure, it might be inherently less secure, but there\'s also a hell of a lot more Windows machines out there than Linux boxes, so it\'s much more worthwhile to find Windows exploits.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299490, 47139, 1013, 102595, 1072936800, '', 'wow guyz im f*cked three times up the @$$ because of a hack...(metacheat 4.0)...now wit steam they now have the god forsaken security modue...now ain\'t that a pissant...a major @$$ itch...i didnt even cheat im betta ten that but i did dload a hack jus for fun..ya no wen i get pissed...so 1 day i turn that son-a-b1tch on n play in a secure server (security module)now i forgot that aspect so im playin nd the hack is on but aint workin for me so i say *** it nd i play witout hackin...in 4 min. im dropped because of "cheating violations".every secure server i go into im banned due to past cheating violations. Now it\'s ben 2 weeks and sources tell me 1st bans are only for 1 week...nd its ma first ban...well ma frend who has complete ownage but he used the hack a cupl a times for fun nd that particular hack is a 5 year ban first or eigth time....now im in a new clan l westies l...there t1 server is secure nd i need to get in it for scrims nd practices...nyway so all i have to do is jus make a new account...well wen i go to make a new 1 it sayz cd key already in use...nd i have no f*cking clue how to delete my old account..im in deep froed pbaked brick oven ****....nd i need sum serious help!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299503, 47139, 1013, 102596, 1072936800, '', 'Ice is that a legitimate post or are you trying to be funny?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299545, 47139, 1013, 102595, 1072936800, '', 'no its true', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299551, 47139, 1013, 102597, 1072936800, '', 'For those who don\'t feel like sorting through the poorly pieced together paragraph, it breaks down into "I installed a cheat.  VAC caught me.  Whhaaa."\n\n\n\nIf you don\'t want to waste time responding to it, feel free to cut and paste this:\n\n\n\nHahaha', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(299642, 47139, 1013, 102598, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by staem \n\nFor those who don\'t feel like sorting through the poorly pieced together paragraph, it breaks down into "I installed a cheat.  VAC caught me.  Whhaaa."\n\n\n\nIf you don\'t want to waste time responding to it, feel free to cut and paste this:\n\n\n\nHahaha \n\n\n\n[]\n\n\n\nHahaha.\n\n\n\nYou cheated, you deserved what you got. Loser.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309381, 48716, 1013, 102599, 1072936800, 'CES Las Vegas 2004 - Valve\'s reputation hit hard in front of ALL', 'Microsoft, Apple, ATI, Sennheiser, and another several thousand computer, tech, manufacturing companies across the globe appeared at the annual CES show which showcases each year the new upcoming technologies that will appear for consumers. Keynote speakers Bill Gates, Steve Jobs, among other notable figures speaking there. \n\n\n\n\n\nGuess what? CES was sponsoring the newest International Gaming Tournament in the United States in Las Vegas. \n\n\n\n\n\nCyberXGaming! As you all will soon hear teams from South America, Europe, Asia and across the country arrived to compete in a variety of games. From Quake3, to CoD, to CS, to WC3. \n\n\n\n\n\nAs a result of the recent problems with Steam and Valve being unable to get a simple lan only CS up and running. CyberXgaming is the first International Tournament on American soil to cancel outright and send thousands of gamers back to their countries early. Fortunately for all these teams and competitors and their sponsors ( Intel, Ati, AMD, nVidia, Compusa, and others ).\n\n\n\n\n\nCyberxgaming will be covering all their costs and reimbursing them for airfare, hotel fees, food and other travel expenses. This amounts to a minimum of already 1-200,000 dollars just in reimbursements. \n\n\n\n\n\nAlready it is rumored that Valve will be facing a huge lawsuit as a result. \n\n\n\n\n\n- Valve yall should have prepared in advance for this. As I said before Valve should have been keeping in touch with the gaming community and the sponsors and the companies. Too bad.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309434, 48716, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'What\'s the source of this information?\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309438, 48716, 1013, 102600, 1072936800, '', 'I really don\'t think there are any grounds for a lawsuit against valve. Unless there were written agreements about the software. It\'s unfortunate but still not valve\'s fault. Plus they could have easily set up CS 1.5 instead of going to insane expenses.\n\n__________________\n\nWhat, Canada is attacking you? Yer not kidding... Give em some beer and they\'ll go away.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309462, 48716, 1013, 100589, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, could hav eeasily gone with 1.5\n\n\n\n\n\nSmells like bollox to me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309488, 48716, 1013, 100457, 1072936800, '', 'u cant blame valve for a power outage.\n\n\n\n\n\nsue them for natural causes?\n\n__________________\n\n_______________\n\n\n\n\n\nP4 2.4c 800mhz FSB\n\n\n512mb Corsair pc3200 DDR Ram\n\n\nThe pimpiest GeForce 2 mx 200 pci (soon will be an fx 5900)\n\n\nWindows XP SP 1\n\n\n80gb HD\n\n\n1024x 768 16bit  - 100+ fps\n\n\n__________________\n\n\n\n\n\n#teamagony', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309490, 48716, 1013, 102599, 1072936800, '', 'That problem appears to now be under control, but there is one that is out of the hands of the extremely hardworking Cyber X crew, and that is a problem with Counterstrike and Valve. There is a long series of e-mails between Valve and the Cyber X crew, in which Valve said they would be on site an offer support, and a few other things. Valve didn\'t show, and what little support it offered came way way too late to make a difference. A hint to companies, when 1200+ of your most rabid fans are in a room together playing the game that made you, and is much of your ongoing income, don\'t blow off the people who set the event up.\n\n\n\n\n\ntaken from http://www.theinquirer.net/?article=13552 (http://www.theinquirer.net/?article=13552)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309533, 48716, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'Meh, the organizers organized an event around a LAN event which they knew wasn\'t supported at that time. They screwed themselves. You can tell from the first two paragraphs it was badly organized from the beginning.\n\n\n\n\n\nRule #1: Don\'t host an event for something that\'s not fully supported or in development. (ie. LAN support = in development)\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309557, 48716, 1013, 101666, 1072936800, '', 'In contrast, VALVe did an excellent job supporting CPL.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309577, 48716, 1013, 102082, 1072936800, '', 'I mean c\'mon, LAN support SHOULDN\'T be so hard to implment, could it? []\n\n__________________\n\nHIT forum - http://www.hl-improvement.com\n\n\nBroadband news  - http://www.dslreports.com\n\n\nRemove spyware - http://www.lavasoftusa.com\n\n\nRemove spyware #2 - http://safer-networking.org\n\n\nPrevent spyware on your machine - http://www.javacoolsoftware.com\n\n\nCo-op HL! - http://www.svencoop.com', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309589, 48716, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'Well only problem I see with offline support right now...How do you check if they have the latest version with no internet connection? What if someone has an older version, how do they upgrade?\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309600, 48716, 1013, 102601, 1072936800, '', 'I think the lack of offline gaming is a backward step for CS. Why this was never a problem before steam?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309607, 48716, 1013, 100283, 1072936800, '', 'There would be no grounds for lawsuits, otherwise I could sue my gunsmith if I shot myself in the leg with a gun I purchased from him. It was their choice to choose counter-strike 1.6. That\'s like suing a car dealership becasue some idiot who bought his car at that dealership ran into you DUI.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309616, 48716, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'It wasn\'t a problem before Steam cause all you dealt with before was completed versions. Valve had little control over releasing small patches, if anything small needed to be fixed, a whole new version of the game had to be released.  Also WON doesn\'t check for an updated version automatically like Steam does.\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309625, 48716, 1013, 102599, 1072936800, 'Take the time to go to the inquirer website and read the info', 'Some of you guys that are posting are ignoring the news report from the inquirer folks who have people actually in Las Vegas at the CES. \n\n\n\n\n\nAlso KillerKoala and others are obviously ignoring the fact that every major electronics ,pc, manufacturing company , along with vendors such as Compusa are there. Seeing it all play out first hand. \n\n\n\n\n\nmore excerpts from the article :\n\n\n\n\n\nThat problem appears to now be under control, but there is one that is out of the hands of the extremely hardworking Cyber X crew, and that is a problem with Counterstrike and Valve. There is a long series of e-mails between Valve and the Cyber X crew, in which Valve said they would be on site an offer support, and a few other things. \n\n\n\n\n\n--------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nAh Valve obviously was supposed to support and did people there who didn\'t bother to help. \n\n\n\n\n\n--------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nYou guys fail to see how damaging this is to Valve\'s reputation. Who else is there? Representatives of the US Army whom designed America\'s army which is also being played there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(309636, 48716, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'But what would Valve do support them? The organizers should of already realized they can\'t support something in development.\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313014, 49167, 1013, 102602, 1072936800, 'Vac Banned my HLTV?  Why??', 'I run about 4 CS 1.6 HLDS\'s on a major gaming provider\'s network. I also have FOUR HLTV processes that login to each respective server and record demos 24/7. This is so we can later review a suspected hackers demo if necessary.\n\n\n\nToday, we noticed our HLTV "bot" was not on one of the servers. When I checked the server console, I saw this on EACH HLTV process:\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:\n\n********************************************\n\nYour connection to this secure server has been\n\nrejected.\n\n\n\nBecause of past cheating violations, you have\n\nbeen banned from playing on all secure servers\n\nuntil 2008-12-20 23:44:39.\n\n\n\nRepeat violators may be permanently banned\n\nfrom all secure servers.\n\n\n\nFor more information, visit:\n\nhttp://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html (http://www.counter-strike.net/cheat.html)\n\n********************************************\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNow, how can a HLTV possibly be VAC banned?!?!?! What must I do to get it back online?\n\n\n\nI swear, the server has NOT been tampered with in anyway. What gives?  Does an HLTV instance use a steamid?  And is it based soley on the "update" user name?\n\n\n\nThanks VERY much,\n\nDave\n\n\n\nPS, Despite all the negative comments about "steam", I like the update "delivery" system and where things have headed.  Kudos to developers.  Only problem I have had is that the linux binary is a CPU hog and does  not support multiple processors AND the update that was issued on a holiday (Thanksgiving).  Everything else has been gravy :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313163, 49167, 1013, 100163, 1072936800, '', 'LOL! Vac Ban a HLTV......GG Vac!!! Way to get those hackers. You know they say no false positive. Hahah\n\n\n\n\n\nThis is so funny, I have to copy and paste it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313184, 49167, 1013, 100922, 1072936800, '', 'Yea, it does use your cd key. Might be a bug with hltv.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313273, 49167, 1013, 102602, 1072936800, '', 'I know, it is VERY funny.  We couldn\'t stop laughing when it did.  Thats about as false positive as it can get []\n\n\n\nShadowWolf, HLTV (HLDS server) does NOT use a CD-Key...its a dedicated server.  \n\n\n\nSo for reals, as funny as it is, how do I get my little HLTV bots back in business?\n\n\n\nVxD', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313419, 49167, 1013, 102603, 1072936800, '', 'Try this:\n\n/index.php?area=cheat_form (/index.php?area=cheat_form)\n\nOmg a vac banned HLTV, now that is funny.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313917, 49167, 1013, 102602, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, I filled in the form, but I couldn\'t really fill in all the boxes (steamid, operating system, etc) being that its a linux server []  But hopefully I can get this resolved ASAP.  We need our "hacking" HLTV to catch hackers.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313923, 49167, 1013, 102604, 1072936800, '', 'Have you asked your provider(s)?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(313928, 49167, 1013, 102602, 1072936800, '', 'Well, no I haven\'t, but I don\'t see how this could have anything to do with a provider.  The HLTV instance logged onto the secure server and obviously was detected for \'hacks\'.  I have total shell access and installed the HLDS HLTV from scratch.  \n\n\n\nMy provider won\'t even know (they aren\'t familiar with CS) what i\'m talking about if I were to tell them my HLTV instance is VAC banned.\n\n\n\nI guess what it all comes down to is...\n\n\n\nDoes the HLTV "instance" have a steamid or is it based on IP?\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\nVxD', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(314296, 49167, 1013, 100163, 1072936800, '', 'Did you email support@steampowered.com (mailto:support@steampowered.com) ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(314374, 49167, 1013, 101715, 1072936800, '', 'That is crazy.\n\n\n\nWell if you are running a bot how does a anti-virus program like VAC go about banning it.\n\n\n\nHmm... I think it would have to be using a Steam ID or else it was banned solely on its name.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(314391, 49167, 1013, 102602, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for the link.  I also emailed support.\n\n\n\nEd!, its not a "bot" per se, but HLTV is basically just an installation of the server package (HLDS).  \n\n\n\nBut yes it is crazy.  I just need to know at this point...\n\n\n\nDoes VAC ban HLTV via IP, STEAMID, or name as you said.  Hoping that maybe just reinstalling will make it go away being that there is NO CDKey given during installation.  Only a steam userid.\n\n\n\nThanks\n\nVxD', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(314708, 49167, 1013, 100163, 1072936800, '', 'Update? Did they get it fix?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
