(315507, 49456, 1013, 102612, 1072936800, '', 'I think I can top that crap. []\n\n\n\n6502C runs as a screaming 1.79MHz\n\n64KB RAM\n\nPokey Audio\n\nGTIA Video\n\n\n\nI lost the Drive somewhere but I think I have an 800 baud modem somewhere.... []\n\n\n\nIf I\'m lucky I can log into Steam with it sometime in April or May.\n\n\n\nOf course, there\'s older crap than what I have. But I jumped into the business a few years too late.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(315658, 49509, 1013, 102613, 1072936800, 'Now thats what I call an update!', 'Great update this week! Thanks for all the work Valve you truely deserved all the praise.\n\n\n\nBut "Fixed exploit where when a player died they could join the other team." How is it an exploit? If a dead player can\'t change team after they died, when can they do it? Does that mean they\'re stuck on the current team for good until the next time they connect to the server?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(315676, 49509, 1013, 102614, 1072936800, '', 'There used to be an exploit that would allow someone to die, switch teams, then switch again quickly, and be able to respawn on their same team (thus getting two lives per round).  I\'m fairly sure THAT is what they fixed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(315750, 49509, 1013, 100106, 1072936800, '', 'yep, the changelog sounds good []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
