(318806, 49683, 1026, 102462, 1072936800, '', 'There was an update? lol NO WONDER NOBODY\'S JOINING MY SERVER!! lol!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(318846, 49683, 1026, 102620, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Stomper \n\nsame here playing on lan on my server before this update my latency was 14, now its 56.also the servers stats gui seems #### up.it shows server fps steady 20 whith spikes to 100,before update fps was steady 100  \n\n\n\nSame thing here (FPS).\n\nEveryone used to have pings around 30-40 (highest pings were around 110-130) on a Sven Co-Op server. Now EVERYONE including me gets an average ping of 140.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319086, 49683, 1026, 102621, 1072936800, 'Another one bites the dust :/', 'Sad to say, same thing here, my usual ping (5ms) now goes to 50 ms and people joinning got a ping around 130-150 (which is a problem since the ping limit is 150 on my server -high ping kicker-).\n\n\n\nDOH !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n\n\n\nI can t run my 1.6 dedi in this conditions, have to run good old 1.5 until they fix the problem. :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319112, 49683, 1026, 102622, 1072936800, '', 'Same here man our east server people\'s pings have increased 50% - 70% since the update. Needless to say since it was cal match night we got our rear ends handed to us. \n\n\n\nBy the way we tried switching our rates around on our match server from \n\n\n\ncl_cmdrate 10 - 40 \n\ncl_updaterate 10 - 40 \n\nrate 9000 - 2000 \n\n\n\nWe found that we could go all the way to 10 and not have high pings (on scoreboard) or any choke or loss (on netgraph) but when you played it felt really laggy. So I am not sure what is going on, all I know is we are ping high on all 3 of our servers now.\n\n\n\nPings are high from HLSW or server list as well not only when in the server.\n\n\n\nJust to update everyone I logged in this morning and it still pings high, we have 3 servers, 2 match server and 1 public server and they are all updated and have been rebooted several times. I am not sure what else to check.\n\n\n\n===Specs===\n\nWindows 2000 SP4\n\nProcessor: Dual Processors P4 3.2 ghz\n\nRam: 1 gig\n\n32 Player Server\n\nLatest Version of all Plugins\n\nLatest Version of HLDS', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319397, 49683, 1026, 102623, 1072936800, '', 'i would also very much like to hear how this problem can be fixed, my servers r varied in spec and OS, but all 3 have this lag problem since the update. My servers are running with only AMX and metamod, but I have tried running the server without these addons and the lag still remains.\n\n\n\nAny suggestions or help would be very good, as I have tried pretty much everything to solve this problem but I believe it is more to do with the new update than anything in the server config or hardware setup.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319441, 49683, 1026, 102015, 1072936800, '', 'Well, I have the exact same problem. My ping used to be something like 3~9, now it\'s 40~70! My HLDS is on the same computer I\'m playing on and I lag as much as the people who join! Stupid update!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319450, 49683, 1026, 102624, 1072936800, 'yup', 'i hope steam makes a anothere update to fix this problam because evertime ppl join my server they see the high ping and the just leave, my ping used to be like 1-10 but now it like 60 with 5ppl in it and when its full its like 150.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319468, 49683, 1026, 102623, 1072936800, '', 'I have league matches to run today and my servers are like this, however listen servers run perfectly fine. This leads me to think its something only in the HLDS update, as this lag problem happens when you start a server for ANY mod, not just CS or NS.\n\n\n\nHopefully someone can figure this out soon []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319516, 49683, 1026, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'I located the problem with the lag and solved it at least for now.\n\n\n\nThe update to the server VGUI2.DLL module is the culprit.\n\n\n\nThe good news is you can replace it with the old one and the problem will go away and there isn\'t any compatibility problems, AND you don\'t lose anything except the problem from what I can tell.\n\n\n\nIf you don\'t have a backup of the old VGUI2.DLL then you can grab a copy from here:\n\nhttp://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip)\n\n\n\nJust put it in place of the one in your HLServer directory.\n\n\n\nThe lag is caused by the fact that the server FPS with the updated VGUI2.DLL module seems to be unbelievably low, I was getting 16fps, and any ping booster just gives you totally weird results (certainly not a boost).\n\n\n\nTry the fix and let me know how it works.\n\n\n\nEdit:\n\nYou can also try and run in console mode for the server which bypasses the VGUI2.DLL, do this by adding " -console" to your launch properties.\n\n\n\nImportant update:\n\nThe 09Feb2004 Update appears to have fixed the VGUI2.DLL problem for both stand-alone and for client HLDS (yea!).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319522, 49683, 1026, 102623, 1072936800, '', 'i had a feeling about those files all along, but hey I got no idea what they are. Thanks so much for the fix quicksilver, this is a real life-saver for me and I much appreciate the help [] I am sure everyone else will also benefit a lot from your findings.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(319528, 49683, 1026, 102625, 1072936800, '', 'yes it works thankx quicksilver', '127.0.0.1', 1),
