(321442, 49683, 1026, 100028, 1072936800, 'HIGH Priority Batch File for HLDS', 'Here is a somewhat generic batch file to start your Stand-Alone HLDS Server at HIGH priority.\n\n\n\nhttp://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/Steam_HLDS.bat (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/Steam_HLDS.bat)\n\nYou can put this on your desktop for easy clicking.\n\n\n\nInside it looks like this:\n\n\n\nc:\n\ncd c:\\HLServer\n\nstart /high c:\\HLServer\\hlds.exe -port 27015 +maxplayers 9 -noipx -condebug -secure\n\n\n\nIf you don\'t have your hlserver installed on the C: drive edit the file and change it to your install disk (edit 3 places there).\n\n\n\nThe other thing you will want to change is the maxplayers (9 here).  For internet this depends on what your uplink connection can handle.\n\n\n\nIf you don\'t know, then go to www.dslreports.com (http://www.dslreports.com) and run the free speedtest.\n\n\n\nYou will see two numbers, download and upload (or uplink).\n\n\n\nDownload is how fast you can get data to the server.\n\nUpload/uplink is how fast the server can send data out to players.\n\n\n\nBasically for internet connections (bits/second):\n\n 128K uplink = 4 players\n\n 256k uplink = 7 players\n\n 320k uplink = 9 players\n\n 512k uplink = 14 players\n\n 768k uplink = 21 players\n\n1024k uplink = 28 player\n\n1140k uplink = 32 players (max number)\n\n\n\nOf course your particular line may or may not be stable enough to support the number I have listed there.  Local players on LAN are not included in this count.\n\n\n\nThe rule of thumb is 35.6Kbits per player.\n\n\n\nCertain maps and MODs may take more uplink bandwidth too.\n\n\n\nThis maxplayers setting also assumes you are running the following server rate limits (in the server.cfg file):\n\n\n\nsv_minrate 3500\n\n\n\n// no limit on maxrate for LAN only use 7500 for regular server\n\n// this controls how fast maps can be downloaded by clients\n\n//sv_maxrate 0\n\nsv_maxrate 7500\n\n\n\n// this is the minimum playable updaterate, leave this at 13\n\nsv_minupdaterate 13\n\n\n\n// 60 for updaterate is LAN ONLY use 13 for internet\n\n// 20 is default but will cut the maxplayers you can handle in 1/2\n\n// sv_maxupdaterate 60\n\nsv_maxupdaterate 13', '127.0.0.1', 1),
