(321405, 50077, 1005, 103416, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by qUiCkSiLvEr \n\nwell logos, you are an enigma wrapped in a conundrum!\n\n\n\nLets take this one step at a time.\n\n\n\n1.  shut off your server.\n\n2.  download the vgui2.dll file from this link:\n\nhttp://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/Server/vgui2.zip)\n\n\n\n3. unzip the vgui2.zip and put the vgui2.dll file into your hlserver directory.  There should be one there and it should ask you if it\'s ok to replace it.  Say YES.\n\n\n\n4. start up your server and run a map.  Wait a minute or two.\n\n\n\n5. in the server console, type:\n\n\n\nSTATS\n\n\n\nthen copy the reported information and post it back here.\n\nUse cut and paste, don\'t retype it.   Can anyone confirm for me if this works? TIA!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(321435, 50077, 1005, 102631, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by oscar \n\nCan anyone confirm for me if this works? TIA!  \n\n\n\nI am having the same problem as many others with this most recent update.   My server specs are on the low end and I am seeing what appears to be more of a load when my server reaches full. (only 8 in my case)  Before this update I had no problems, now I do see a big dip in the FPS.\n\n\n\nI have swapped in the old vgui2.dll and it does appear to be runnig better as a result.  My ping has again come back down to 10-20 (LAN) and the FPS has gone back up.\n\n\n\nI suggest trying it out, keep the new vgui2.dll file aside in case you need it.  \n\n\n\nGood Luck!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(321471, 50077, 1005, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Here is an important Note!\n\nI have had several people trying to apply the VGUI2.DLL fix to the HLDS that is part of the Steam Client.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately the Client HLDS will not allow the older VGUI2.DLL to work.\n\n\n\nHere is a summary of all (WIN) server types and if they can be fixed or not:\n\n\n\n*****************************************\n\nThere are actually three types of servers in Half-life.\n\n\n\nListen Server:\n\n==========\n\nThis is where you start a server from the game itself and play at the same time ... there is only a minimal control panel.\n\nThis requires the Steam Client to always be running.\n\nAll the stock game content is contained in a single cache file.\n\nThis version does not require the VGU2.DLL fix []\n\n\n\nClient HLDS Server:\n\n==============\n\nThis is the option in the Steam Games Menu.\n\nThis server is a full server and you have to connect to it from lan or from internet.\n\nThis requires Steam Client to always be running.\n\nThis has the full control panel.\n\nAll the stock game content is contained in a single cache file.\n\nThis version will not allow the old VGUI2.DLL fix []\n\n\n\nStand-Alone HLDS_1120 Server\n\n======================\n\nThis is a totally independent install from Steam.\n\nIt does not require Steam client to be running.\n\nThis server is a full server and you have to connect to it from lan or from internet.\n\nThere are no cache files, all the maps and things are unpacked.\n\nThis version will allow the VGUI2.DLL fix to work []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(322252, 50077, 1005, 103417, 1072936800, '', 'go back to the old ****ing update this ****ing updates always **** up steam BUT NONE OF THE RENTAL SERVERS LAGG i think they have a special program that is better than the steam hlds that ****ing sucks \n\n\n\nget this ****ing **** fixed once again my traffic is ****ed thanks steam THANKS\n\n\n\nOR U CAN ****ING HELP US ALL OUT!\n\n\n\nWHO AGREES??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(322292, 50077, 1005, 103418, 1072936800, '', 'Logos and all, \n\n\n\nqUiCkSiLvEr\'s temp fix does work. I have tested it myself. Before replacing the vgui2.dll file my FPS was about the same as Logos. \n\n\n\nThis is mine now:\n\n\n\nCPU   In    Out   Uptime  Users   FPS    Players\n\n 4.75  0.00  0.00     565    12   99.82       0\n\n\n\nSo bottom line---\n\n\n\nThe fix works and Valve/Steam are informed. \n\n\n\n----\n\n\n\nOne day the updates will almost stop entirely because of reports like qUiCkSiLvEr\'s and the rest of the HLDS admin community.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(331355, 50077, 1005, 103419, 1072936800, '', 'It really works,thx', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(338760, 50077, 1005, 103420, 1072936800, 'new DLL works!', 'CPU   In    Out   Uptime  Users   FPS    Players\n\n0.00  0.00  0.00       0     0   19.97       0\n\n\n\nCPU   In    Out   Uptime  Users   FPS    Players\n\n1.00  0.00  0.00       0     0   99.76       0\n\n\n\nHOLY S**T!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(330482, 51466, 1005, 102648, 1072936800, 'Para and the elites are going to be *UPGRADED*', 'I just watched an interview that gamers.nu made with Cliffe from Valve during the CPL last december. Cliffe mentions how well the community took the the autosniper upgrade and says how they are planning to upgrade the dual elites and the para to be "more actractive for their price". This will happen during the next few weeks/month.\n\n\n\nI\'m sorry that I can\'t provide a straight link because gamers.nu requires a gold membership to be able to download and fragbite.com is a a swedish site that requires a free registration. I hope you will find a link with google [] It weights about 184 mb.\n\n\n\nCan\'t wait to see how this future update will work in pubs/matches []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(330492, 51466, 1005, 102649, 1072936800, '', 'Well Yes to the elites, i hope they dont overdo the para too much.\n\n\n\nI thought the response to the autosnipers was rather negative.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(330527, 51466, 1005, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'The autosniper complaints came from Colt/AK/AWP users that didn\'t want any of the other 21 guns to ruin their 90% monopoly on all the kills in CS.\n\n\n\nWhat would people do if every weapon were actually useful? Complain that all the guns work too well?\n\n\n\nImprovements to the M249 and Elites are definately long overdo. Even though the Elites were originally made intentionally crappy to silence all the players that were whining at Gooseman to put akimbo weapons into the game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
