(346262, 53327, 1005, 102677, 1072936800, 'PAIN: liblist.game file', 'Why does DOD keep trying to update the liblist.gam file (in listen server mode)?\n\n\n\nFor people running DOD bots ( www.sturmbot.net (http://www.sturmbot.net) ) we require to modify the liblist.gam file ...\n\ngamedll "sturmbot\\dlls\\STURM_bot.dll"\n\n\n\nThis file keeps getting overridden when we launch dod in steam.\n\n\n\nWorkaround #1) One solution was to force this file as "READ ONLY".\n\n\n\nThis only works up until the time when DOD gets an update.\n\nThe next time DOD is launched, and the liblist.gam file is still READ ONLY, dod crashes.\n\n\n\nWorkaround #2) Turn off READ ONLY.\n\nWatch DOD replace the liblist.gam file.\n\nExit DOD, update liblits.gam file and turn READ ONLY back on.\n\n\n\nThis is one pain we would like eliminated (still allowing us to play DOD  of course).\n\n\n\nIf anyone can shed some light on us 56kers that still play DOD because of bots, please give us hope.\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\nGooofy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346541, 53327, 1005, 102678, 1072936800, '', 'It should be said that making it read-only doesn\'t do jack squat if your HDD is FAT32.\n\n\n\nAnd gamestartup.mp3 has the same problem. If it is replaced DOD ALWAYS overwrites it with the original.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346605, 53327, 1005, 102405, 1072936800, '', 'thats weird i have mine to read only and my Sturmbot and DoD work fine [] ive had it set on that for like a month or two and ive had no probs []\n\n\n\nand im useing Win ME and all works fine [] and i use Sturmbot allot bigtime with your waypoints Gooofy and allso with Gotchas []\n\n\n\ni even have my Config file set to Read-Only and have had no probs with that too []\n\n\n\nbut there is alot that Steam and DoD Dev need to fix in here [] im still waiting on a dam DoD update or a nice Steam update [] they seem to update dam CS alot more then DoD :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346727, 53327, 1005, 100452, 1072936800, '', 'back it up.\n\n\n\nmake a copy called liblist.bak, and after dod updates, delete the new one, and change the name of the old one to liblist.gam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(367562, 53327, 1005, 102677, 1072936800, 'LIBLIST.GAM file cure is here (steam only)', 'Jowo just pointed this out to me:\n\n\n\nSteam News February 9, 2004, 6:26 pm (/?area=news) ....\n\n"Greg Coomer"\n\nquote:\n\nENGINE (all games)\n\nAdded new command line option "-dll"; Syntax is -dll [game_dll_to_load]\n\n\n\n\n\nWhich means that the LIBLIST.GAM file does NOT need to be touched at all.\n\nInstead just add -dll sturmbot\\dlls\\STURM_bot.dll to the Day of Defeat launch options.\n\n\n\nInstructions:\n\n\n\n1. Steam -> Games\n\n2. Click on Day of Defeat with the right mouse button\n\n3. Select Properties\n\n3. Click on Launch Options\n\n4. Enter: -dll sturmbot\\dlls\\STURM_bot.dll\n\n5. Click OK\n\n6. Click CLOSE\n\n7. Double click on Day of Defeat\n\n\n\nThat\'s it.\n\n\n\nNote: If you have LIBLIST.GAM file as READ ONLY, I recommend that you take READ ONLY off, as it (used to) prevents patches for Day of Defeat from installing properly.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346430, 53350, 1013, 102679, 1072936800, 'Favorite Servers- Wierd, Annoying Bug', 'I know it\'s kind of minor but if I try to delete a server from my favorites list, the next time I go on Steam the server is back or there is a blank name but a "0" by the ping.  It\'s not a big problem but it is kind of annoying when I want to remove a favorite and it keeps reappearing.  I already tried to reinstall Steam but the problem continued.  Any idea how to fix the problem?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346871, 53350, 1013, 102679, 1072936800, '', 'No one has any clue how to solve this? =(', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346878, 53350, 1013, 100602, 1072936800, '', 'i also have it but only when i open servers directly from the main menu in counterstrike it works fine', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346890, 53350, 1013, 102680, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same problem.  If I delete a server from favorites list it comes back next time no matter what I do.  I have 2 blank servers that show a ping.  If i click on view server details it shows an ip but no map or anything.  Very annoying.  It happens in the game server list, counter strike server list....anywhere same thing happens.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(346983, 53350, 1013, 102681, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same issue as well.  In addition if I delete them from favorites they start duplicating next time I look.  So instead of the deleted server not only still showing up, there are 2 (or more) of them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(347172, 53350, 1013, 102682, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah it\'s an annoying one.\n\n\n\n\n\nPersonally I delete the serverbrowser.vdf file from my C:\\Program Files\\Steam\\config folder. That clears the whole thing so I can start afresh [], (the file is replaced automatically the next time you close Steam).\n\n\n\n\n\nPain in the arse I know but it\'s better than having a favs list full of turd servers.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(347207, 53350, 1013, 102683, 1072936800, '', 'yeah this has been bothering me too.. its why i came on these forums.. rather small, but annoying as hell bug.. especially when u add diff servers here and there and intend to delete them soon because of scrims, diff. times when ur playing etc....  kinda sucks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
