(356975, 54471, 1005, 102695, 1072936800, '', 'It sounds like you was playing O on the defending team which is why you was switched teams.\n\n\n\n\n\nI dont know the server or how its setup but if its a Clanstyle server then fair enough, if its a public play server then maybe a bit harsh that you got booted off.  IM not really in the position to comment on that.\n\n\n\n\n\nEither way just find a server that plays the game how you like it.\n\n__________________\n\nAmigaOasis\n\n\nHead TFC Admin\n\n\nhttp://www.tfc.jolt.co.uk\n\n\n\n\n\n213.208.119.132:27025 - TFC Classic\n\n\n213.208.119.131:27055 - DM Pit\n\n\nCheck webby for more servers', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(358036, 54471, 1005, 102696, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by FourStroke \n\n\nServers like [burstfire.net] CTFCL Public Corpse are more or less for "advanced players". They demand you to know how to play clan-style-like and if you dont they just kick you out.\n\n\n\n\n\nFor people not used to play clanwars it can be hard to understand the "rules" and my advice is to play elsewhere if you dont know them or learn them before joining.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFourstroke is right.  burstfire.net is a euro server company, and CTFCL I believe is a euro league server, which has more clan oriented people playing on it and they expect clan like play on it.  So basically, if you\'re not up to their standards, they don\'t want you to play there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
