(378768, 57514, 1013, 102709, 1072936800, 'about the silencer on the M4....', 'I hear that the silencer for the M4 makes the gun less powerful, but more accurate... then I hear that it makes the gun more powerful and more accurate... so how effective is the silencer and what does it exactly do?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(378778, 57514, 1013, 102671, 1072936800, '', 'silencers lower the speed of the bullet to subsonic levels whereby dropping the sound of the exit from the muzzle.  this intern would make the gun have less kick reducing some recoil. (allowing you to spray better). allso the gun is slightly less accurate from a distance. in cs your rate of fire is slightly lower (about that of the ak).  it also reduces some of the damage delt (1-3 points).\n\n\n\nwhat all this means is that you could be shooting your enemy in the back and it would take 4 hits to kill instead of 3. the good news is, is that he will have no idea where you are.\n\n\n\ni use the silencer for medium distances and flanking situations.  i try not to use it while sniping unless i am behind the enemy.  but thats just in scrims. when playing around i like to slap the silencers on my usp and m4, and play like a ninja.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(379432, 57514, 1013, 102710, 1072936800, 'Question about the silencer on the M4....', 'quote:Originally posted by MomSaysImCooL \n\nI hear that the silencer for the M4 makes the gun less powerful, but more accurate... then I hear that it makes the gun more powerful and more accurate... so how effective is the silencer and what does it exactly do?  \n\n\n\nWORNG! It\'s actually thew other way around, I\'ve tested it myself. The silencer makes it alittle less accurate but a tiny, virtually insignificantly, bit more powerful', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(382986, 57514, 1013, 102711, 1072936800, '', 'i never shoot without the silencer.\n\nsomehow i can shoot a lot more acurate that way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(384135, 57514, 1013, 100078, 1072936800, 'Re: Question about the silencer on the M4....', 'quote:Originally posted by J.D. Givaphuk \n\nWORNG! It\'s actually thew other way around, I\'ve tested it myself. The silencer makes it alittle less accurate but a tiny, virtually insignificantly, bit more powerful  \n\n\n\nWow your an idiot..\n\n\n\nWithout the silensor it has more damage and is a bit accurate than the silenced.\n\n\n\nWith the silensor it has less recoil and the sound of the gun is silenced a bit.\n\n\n\nBoth of them have a different recoil pattern,Put on a silensor and spray a bit. Now take it off and spray a bit. See how they shoot different spots?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(385211, 57514, 1013, 102712, 1072936800, '', 'actually the silencer makes the gun lesspower full and makes it more like an ak (crosshairs expand quiker).  I like the silencer i can use it jsut as well as i can without the silencer sometimes i jsut dont want a loud sound.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(385226, 57514, 1013, 102713, 1072936800, '', 'Yea, most of you guys are retarded.  Silencer makes gun LESS accurate (watch your mp_dynamiccrosshairs, when you put silencer on, they expand a little bit.)...also, it does make your crosshairs expand a little quicker (more spray)\n\n\n\nMany people say they put silencer on because it increases their HS count, which would explain it pretty well...most people have a tendancy to hit the left arm hitbox.\n\n\n\nAlso, adding silencer doesn\'t make the gun more/less powerful.\n\n\n\nIf you want proof of this, look it up in the leaked CS:CZ code.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(385891, 57514, 1013, 102714, 1072936800, '', 'What the silencer does depends on if you\'re talking about a real M4(A1) or CS\'s M4A1. A real gun gets more accurate with a silencer. As well as slowing down bullets to subsonic levels (or so I\'ve heard), it effectively adds another few inches to your barrel. Normally, a longer barrel would also mean bigger recoil, but I\'d guess a silencer lessens recoil instead, due to it slowing down the bullets and all.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(386002, 57514, 1013, 102347, 1072936800, '', 'In CS the silencer reduces damage and accuracy. But the damage is only 1-2 shots less than unsilenced, so there is little difference. \n\n\n\nHowever I\'ve noticed that a silenced M4 won\'t kill a player with kevlar helmet in 1 headshot, but unsilenced usually will.\n\n\n\nThe accuracy difference is not all that big, and can only be seen by the dynamic crosshair expanding.\n\n\n\nAlso some people have a psychological reaction to the silenced M4 sound that makes them think the gun is more accurate because it\'s not noisy and distracting.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(386741, 57514, 1013, 102713, 1072936800, '', 'on a REAL m4 silencer doesn\'t add accuracy, its actually a larger bore than the inner barrel, and is basically like the muffler on your car. (Ever see a straight cherry-bomb muffler?...its the same thing but a little smaller)\n\n\n\nBtw, I took a looked at code again, and yes it does decrease dmg by just a LITTLE...not much to matter.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(386859, 57514, 1013, 102715, 1072936800, '', 'I generally find that people aim better and kill more with the silencer on. Just sounds cooler [].', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(387289, 57514, 1013, 100011, 1072936800, '', 'In CS the sound suppressor is seemingly slightly less accurate (looser crosshairs with the sound suppressor on) and typically does less damage but in turn reduces the distance that the full noise can be heard and also has the quieter noise that can be replaced to a louder noise IIRC.\n\n\n\nStrangely enough in 1.3 it seemed that the sound suppressor against an armoured chest actually did more damage strangely enough but either way not enough to make a difference in the number of shots to kill.\n\n\n\nThe M4A1 either way kills in about 4-5 (haven\'t tested in a while, damage is affected by range as well) shots to an armoured chest suppressed or unsuppressed and 2 shots to an armoured helmet (unsuppressed does about 92, suppressed is in the 80\'s range) regardless of distance.\n\n\n\nIn addition, the ROF is unaffected from what I can tell.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn real life a sound suppressor typically doesn\'t affect accuracy in any real tangible way at short ranges (generally CS\'s ranges which are about 100-150m at most) but at longer ranges the loss of speed begins to dramatically affect the bullets trajectory.\n\n\n\nOn the other hand it does typically lower recoil and pressure reduction sound suppressors can lower it by 20-30% or more depending on the weapon and the type of suppressor.\n\n\n\nAt the same time the damage done by the round due to its slower speed is lower.\n\n\n\nIIRC a sound suppressor either bleeds off the gasses, uses wipes or the like to actually slow down the bullet or a combonation of both.\n\n\n\nThe biggest sources of noise made by the bullet are the super sonic crack of it breaking the sound barrier and the noise of the gasses rushing out after the bullet as it leaves the barrel (the latter being the main issue).\n\n\n\nWhat most sound suppressors do is delay the release of the gas and allow more room for expansion so the pressure is lower and thus the sound of the gasses rushing out behind the bullet are lower. This in turn typically reduces the speed of the bullet but not by all that much. Things like washers and wipes are what reduce a bullets speed down sufficiently to lower it below supersonic speeds and in turn can affect the accuracy of the weapon a fair bit.\n\n\n\nThe reduction of pressure system can significantly reduce the sound of the muzzle blast and thus the main source of noise that gives away a shooters position and this can be used with Super Sonic ammunition fine.\n\n\n\nCombined with subonic ammunition the reduction of pressure system can lower the noise of the weapon down to a very quite noise that in some cases is no longer than opening a can of coke or the noise of a hammer clicking.\n\n\n\nThe M4A1 in CS as far as I can tell uses just a pressure reduction system as you can still hear the crack of the shot as it flies by you when they are a good distance away but you cannot tell the direction easily.\n\n\n\nIt should have the same accuracy if not slightly lower, it should do slightly less damage and have lower recoil.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn reply to Mortal Monkey:\n\nA sound suppressor typically does not add to the barrel length and thus doesn\'t make it more accurate and the longer the barrel the lower the recoil and greater the accuracy. Why on earth would a longer (and thus heavier) barrel allowing for the bullet to spin even more increase the recoil?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(387367, 57514, 1013, 102716, 1072936800, '', 'im not een goint to get into the silencer+noise+ accuracy thing but just to inform all u guys who may not know: a silencer is also supposed to supress ligth(or so im told) yet when u put a silencer on in cs you still see the same burst that u woudl form an unsilenced one... i knwo alot of you are saying "yea but i see its is smaller on my screen when i put the silencer on".. yes that is true the first person point of view shows a smaller muzzle flash but the THIRD PERSON pov shows a normal one ..ie YOUR ENEMIES SEE A FULL MUZZLE FLASH ... so keep that in mind when u think u are a complete ninja!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(387381, 57514, 1013, 100011, 1072936800, '', 'The suppressor often includes a flash hider and the game engine is so old that things like that have been overlooked.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(387386, 57514, 1013, 102716, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Wudge \n\nThe suppressor often includes a flash hider and the game engine is so old that things like that have been overlooked.  + what i said and i now have a complete thought!!! lol', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(379635, 57623, 1013, 102717, 1072936800, 'Steam Folder doesnt have email file in steam apps', 'ummm i dunno where to put mods since my steam folder is missing the email file in steam apps. help me out?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
