(391857, 59058, 1013, 102720, 1072936800, 'Downloading Mods on steam?', 'I\'m out to get a copy of HL this weekend (EB has some on sale!).  However, I don\'t want to use Steam with it.  I want to know if I can still download the mods Steam hosts (ie CS, DOD, etc) to use in a non-steam enviroment.  Fileplanet doesn\'t have the downloads (not that i\'ve seen) and counter-strike.net doesn\'t have any downloads (just a link to steam).\n\n\n\n\n\nThe only copy of some of these I have is back in 2000.  Any seperate updates? \n\n\n\n\n\nI don\'t give a darn about the latest versions or cheating.  It will be used for LAN\'s not on the net with friends).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(391981, 59058, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'Why do you not want to use Steam?  If you need to have the older versions try these:\n\n\n\n\n\nCS 1.5: http://www.counter-strike.net/mod_full.html (http://www.counter-strike.net/mod_full.html)\n\n\nDoD: http://www.fileplanet.com/files/80000/84650.shtml (http://www.fileplanet.com/files/80000/84650.shtml)\n\n__________________\n\n"I\'m pretty sure at least here a lot more people could be helped if we dnd\'t have to deal with cheat posters, "OMG VALVE SUCKS" posters, not to mention the people that PM us with clearly keygen\'ed keys that "don\'t work". Not everyone\'s doing that, but so many do it makes it pretty hard to help the people who have legit issues and legit problems." \n\n\n---Waldo', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(392071, 59058, 1013, 102720, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t want to use steam for 3 reasons actuatly:\n\n\n\n\n\n1) when I get together with friends we have no net connection\n\n\n2) i like to burn my dl\'d stuff to CD (i erase/install games as i want to play them, plus when friends show up we hand around burned cd\'s of mods/levels/skins for others to use, or ftp)\n\n\n3) i live in the middle of nowhere and can only connect to the net at 28.8 (with a 56k modem) so I do most of my downloading overnight via a download mngr (took me 3 nights [8 hr\'s a night] to download farcry demo).  []\n\n\n\n\n\nIf Steam games could be used offline (no online necessary) & backed up (and i don\'t mean just burning the cache folder to CD, I mean regular ZIP/RAR/EXE files being downloaded) then I\'d use it because it would be easier then searching for dl\'s and waiting in line at fileplanet. []  But, until DSL/Cable is offered where I live, steam isn\'t as useful as it could be for me.\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks for the info too, it\'s what I was looking for!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(392626, 59058, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'You can find the majority of HL mods here:\n\n\n� http://www.half-lifefiles.com/ (http://www.half-lifefiles.com/)\n\n\n� http://www.halflife-mods.com/ (http://www.halflife-mods.com/)\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(392662, 59058, 1013, 102720, 1072936800, '', 'sweat.  Thanks!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(402139, 60214, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, 'Solution for the CD-KEY problem', 'Believe it or not but a possible solution for this may not be valve but sierra.\n\n\n\nI called sierra wondering about this.\n\n\n\nTell Sierra that you bought the game and your CD-KEY Doesn\'t work on the WON version of HL.\n\n\n\nThey wont ask for your CD-KEY, but they will give you a address to arrange some things.\n\n\n\nYou send in your original CD-KEY and your CASE. You pay for the shipping and in about 3 weeks, they\'ll send it back with your same CD and a new KEY.\n\n\n\nThis might make it work.\n\n\n\nBut remember, the\'ll take your own CD-KEY out of the database. Tell them someone must have generated your cd-key.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(402152, 60214, 1013, 102721, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve called Sierra too but they said to me that  they aren\'t responsible for this problem. Maybe it\'s because i\'m from Germany.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
