(402400, 60214, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by mavimaus \n\nThe guy on the phone said that I have to write an e-mail to support@steampowered.com (mailto:support@steampowered.com) and that they can\'t help me.\n\nI wrote the mail last week and now I have to wait. []  \n\n\n\n\n\nDid you mention the STEAM at all?\n\n\n\nDont', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(402418, 60214, 1013, 102723, 1072936800, '', 'like an idiot i did.  i wonder if i could call and try again doing it the way that you suggested? i found your post too late.\n\n\n\nmed', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(402474, 60214, 1013, 102721, 1072936800, '', 'You mean that I better leave the steam thing out?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(403331, 60214, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'Yes.\n\n\n\n\n\nSierra officaly doesn\'t support STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\nBut tell them you bought the game recently and went and clicked on multiplay and it said your CD-key is in use.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(403498, 60214, 1013, 102722, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Catch_ME \n\nYes.\n\n\n\n\n\nSierra officaly doesn\'t support STEAM.\n\n\n\n\n\nBut tell them you bought the game recently and went and clicked on multiplay and it said your CD-key is in use.  \n\n\n\nSo you are telling us that we with out CD-Key error problems should go through the headache of contacting Sierra everytime this happens?  Think about it before answering again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(403792, 60214, 1013, 102721, 1072936800, '', 'I think you don\'t know what we are talking about.\n\nDid he said that you have to call them if you don\'t have the cd-key problem? \n\nI have it and he advises me to call Sierra.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(403942, 60214, 1013, 100513, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Typhon \n\nSo you are telling us that we with out CD-Key error problems should go through the headache of contacting Sierra everytime this happens?  Think about it before answering again.  \n\n\n\nNO,\n\n\n\nRead the orignal post dude.\n\n\n\nIf you have a CD-Key problem, it might be fixed by getting another CD-KEY from Sierra.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405105, 60554, 1026, 100027, 1072936800, 'March 3rd Update', 'The update release tomorrow will include a new HldsUpdateTool version. It will have a number of improvements. The tool should update itself automatically when you run it (after the update is released).\n\n\n\nThe changes are:\n\n\n\n* New command-line syntax *\n\n\n\nThe old "-update game dir username..." syntax will still work, so don\'t worry. \n\n\n\nHowever, a more powerful syntax was necessary for some new features, and to prevent common mistakes. With the new syntax, each parameter is explicitly listed (instead of assuming they are all in the correct order). For instance:\n\n\n\nhldsupdatetool -command update -game cstrike -password mypassword -username user ... etc\n\n\n\nYou can run "hldsupdatetool -?" to get the full syntax list.\n\n\n\n* New "-verify_all" flag *\n\n\n\nIf you run an "update" command with "-verify_all", it will check that each file in the install matches the latest Steam version. If, somehow, your installation gets corrupted and will not run properly, this should bring it back to working order.\n\n\n\n* "Resume" download feature*\n\n\n\nPreviously, if the tool lost connection to the Steam servers in the middle of an update, the next time you ran it, it would re-download some of the files it got the last time. This should be fixed now, it will pick up where it left off.\n\n__________________\n\nSteam Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405147, 60554, 1026, 102617, 1072936800, 'LAGG=', 'Can you fix the lagging problem that steam has had the last couple of months\n\n\n\nthanks\n\n\n\nregards\n\nmarkus\n\n__________________\n\nComputer Specs\n\nCPU: AMD XP +2100 1,74 Ghz\n\nRam: 1024 MB DDR 3300 PCI Slot\n\nVideo Card: nVIDIA GeForce 3 Ti 200\n\nSound Card: Sound Blaster 5.1 Live!\n\nInternet Connection: High Speed Internet 512 DSL\n\n\n\n.:.MaMaMia.:.Vancouver.:.\n\n208.170.202.59:27015\n\nWe are recruiting!\n\n|CS|Headshot \n\nMarkus', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405194, 60554, 1026, 102724, 1072936800, '', 'Nice work guys, I like how you guys fixed pramater stuff.\n\n\n\n* "Resume" download feature* hopefully people well be running servers on good connections to avoide this problem []\n\n__________________\n\n:: Need HELP for anything? - http://www.r5a.org/forum/ :: Post there!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(406192, 60554, 1026, 102725, 1072936800, '', 'ABOUT THE NEW HLTV UPDATE\n\n\n\nThe new windows update include Hltv.cfg which is VERY IRRITATING. You guys erased my old customized hltv.cfg and wrote a new one, which by the way has NOTHING new.\n\n\n\nDamn you Valve!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(407183, 60554, 1026, 102726, 1072936800, '', 'MOTD doesn\'t work in offline mode []\n\n\n\nIn fact I have to delete the motd.txt file otherwise the offline steam clients hang for about 30 seconds when joining the server and then doesn\'t display the motd.  I\'m just using the default motd.txt so it\'s not like it\'s looking for web links....\n\n\n\nA major pain when you\'ve just spent a day desiging a motd web page for a lan!! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
