(500411, 60556, 1026, 102735, 1072936800, '', 'Yeee, why are the bots gone?????? (again)\n\n\n\nOr is it an attack on the Linux users again??\n\nHow much money do you get from MS, for destroying the unix distro\'s???\n\n\n\nValve tsk. tsk. tsk.\n\n\n\nElectronic Arts is eating you. \n\nCome on, you can do better than this.\n\n__________________\n\nOriginal Games Do Not fade!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(517204, 60556, 1026, 102734, 1072936800, 'No answer', 'Still no answer from Valve, It\'s sad that they don\'t answer our questions. It\'s not a very professionel way to tread customers.\n\n\n\nI would be more patient if I know that the bot\'s will come again and they are working on it.\n\n\n\nAs for now I\'ll like to get my money back, because I allready have payed for one Counter strike..\n\n__________________\n\nBest regards\n\n[SnB]Sarge', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405666, 60611, 1013, 100076, 1072936800, 'Can I leave Steam running for update today?', 'I\'m getting ready to leave and want to be able to play when I get home. Can I just leave Steam running while I\'m gone, let it update, and expect it to work and be up-to-date when I return. Especially since this is expected to take 3 hours to complete (per Steam News page). Or is this one that requires you to "login" again before it will update?\n\n\n\nIt\'s now 6am EST. Estimated time for update is 6am PST (~12pm EST?) That means that it should be finished when I get home at about 5pm EST and I should be able to play. Right?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405668, 60611, 1013, 102397, 1072936800, '', 'You have to restart steam for it to download the update.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(405671, 60611, 1013, 100076, 1072936800, '', 'That sucks, but ok.\n\n\n\nThanks for the quick and thoughtful response. It is much appreciated.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(408959, 61166, 1013, 102736, 1072936800, 'Laggy server connections after update', 'If your lag has significantly increased after the update then do the following.\n\n\n\nRight click on the steam icon in the system tray and choose the "settings" option. Then click on the "Internet" tab and verify the speed that is selected is correct. If it is not then choose the correct speed and then hit the "OK" button. \n\n\n\n\n\nThere was a bug causing it to be reset to modem speed when we release the update for some people, which would in turn cause extra lag.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409273, 61166, 1013, 102736, 1072936800, '', 'Just an update to this. Anytime you view the "Settings" screen this value will be reset. For now you will have to use a tool like regedit to set the value in:\n\n\n\nHKEY_CURRENT_USER\\\\Software\\\\Valve\\\\Steam\\\\Rate\n\n\n\nto the value you want (5000 for 256kbps DSL, 7500 for 512kbps and above DSL, 20000 for LAN).\n\n\n\nWe will be releasing a fix early next week for this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409562, 61264, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'Creating New Accounts w/ same CD-KEY', 'Hi,\n\n\n\nA lot of people have recently created new accounts and tried to re-use their cd-keys. This will not work - even if you use the same email address that as your old account name.\n\n\n\nThe confusing part (sorry) is that before Wednesday\'s update, your account name and email address were the same thing In Steam. All old accounts are still that way, unless you go in and change the email address field (via "Change Contact Email" in the Settings page). \n\n\n\nIf you make a new account now, and set the "email address" field to your same email, it is still a different account.\n\n\n\nSo, here is an example.\n\n\n\n- Long ago, Joe created an account "Joe@email.com" on Steam, and registered his cd-key with it\n\n\n\n- Yesterday, Joe created an account "JoeRulz", on Steam, and set it to use his "Joe@email.com" email address. He verified the key, then tried to play. It asked him for his cd-key, but then told him it was already in use.\n\n\n\nJoe will need to login to his old account. This means typing "Joe@email.com" in the Steam Login dialog where it says "Account Name". This account will still have his cd-key registered, his Friends list, etc. \n\n\n\n\n\nthanks,\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409767, 61264, 1013, 102737, 1072936800, 'Ummm Okay.. but...', 'What if Joe forgets his old login information because he was away from the scene for so long because they took away the bots in CS, and now he wants to try it out again?\n\n\n\nI cannot remember my old login info, and everything I try now says it\'s incorrect. It\'s been almost 7 months since I deleted Steam and it\'s contents, and now it says my cdkey is already in their database.. Heck, I don\'t even remember giving them my key. But I must have. \n\n\n\nHow can you get the information Steam has with the cd-key instead of nick and password. So if i say this is my cdkey, then that person who is registered with it is mailed their login and password??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409830, 61264, 1013, 102738, 1072936800, 'yeah i forgot my password :(', 'my login information is the same as my new accept for the password how can i delete my old account or something.\n\ni did pm mr. Sherman, but i can understand that he has about a thousand of these things a day but is there any way i can cs again without having to buy another hl-generation. can anyone from steam handle this?\n\n\n\nim kinda having stress not being able to cs :S\n\nwolfenstein ET isnt fun with a geforce 2 :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409943, 61264, 1013, 102739, 1072936800, '', 'i have a slitly different problem...i made an account long ago on my bros comp...well he just moved out and i have a new computer...well i tryed what i thought was my first account but it said it wasnt there so i just created a new account...now if its possible i think i made it the same name as the first account...if you can at least tell me its impossible to create 2 accounts with the same name then i know its still out there somewhere...and if i did some how use the same account name and e-mail, then how do i use my cd-key', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409953, 61264, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'ArcAngel -\n\n\n\nCheck your PM. Actually, it looks like you\'ve done exactly what I\'m talking about in this thread. You have an old account where the account name is your current email address, and then you\'ve made a new account recently with your nickname as the account name, and it is trying to use the same cd-key. []\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409967, 61264, 1013, 102740, 1072936800, '', 'I think I did the same thing, as "JOE"... How can I reset my key??\n\n\n\nCuz I cant remember my old pass..\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=61331 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=61331)\n\n\n\n(my threat)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(409968, 61264, 1013, 102741, 1072936800, 'account', 'hi, I have similar problem. Once upon a time, I created account. I had to reinstall steam and now- After I login to my [old]account, It updates c-strike and ask me for retype my CD-key, but its already in my account, so its already in use. Please help, or how to delete my account?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410004, 61264, 1013, 102742, 1072936800, '', 'well what if your email was one your school fixed too you.... this happend for me and now i got to no they are going to delete it once i start highschool.. can i then change the emailadress i once typed in', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410017, 61264, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'YES\n\n\n\nYou can change the email. [] \n\n\n\nSteam -> Settings -> Change Contact Email.\n\n\n\nThis will change the email address on your Steam account. It will not change the account name - you will type the same thing you used to to log in.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410192, 61264, 1013, 102743, 1072936800, 'Cd-Key', 'Hello,\n\n\n\nSad to that Valve only can answer questions aboute emails, but not help people with their CD-key problems.\n\n\n\nThanks alot /kind regards\n\nClaus Teglman', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410233, 61264, 1013, 100106, 1072936800, '', 'just a quick question:\n\ntaylor, will it be possible in the (near) future to change the account name as well?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410363, 61264, 1013, 102744, 1072936800, 'Taylor is awesome', 'Thank you thank you thank you!\n\nThis solved my problem completely!!\n\n\n\n\n\n-Melissa', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410390, 61264, 1013, 102745, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, i have a similar problem to GTAZ, i created an account, and forgot all my login information, but it automaticly logged me in when i started it up.  But then i was having trouble with the Wednesday update, it was saying it was smaller than expected or something, and so i uninstalled it and reinstalled it.  I then created a new account, and it wont let me run any games, until i enter my CD key, and then it says its already in use.  If there was a way, like GTAZ said, to just email the account information of a certain CD key, to the email on the account, then that would be great, and ill PM whoever i need to to get that done.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410471, 61264, 1013, 102746, 1072936800, 'Backfired', 'well...it looks like this little cd-key plan of steam backfired on them. \n\nIm having the same problem...and i know for a fact that i did NOT give steam my cd-key becouse the cd-key that is on the cd-case is upstairs in the attic, and has been since after i installed it back in 98 or 99. so, is steam spyware too? and if so why are you blaming it on us if we cant remember what our login name and password is? why dont ya just reset that file and let us all start anew...\n\nalso, I noticed when i was choosing the game halflife to be on my system that tfc was offered in the free 30 day subscription, I though tfc came with halflife? i dont remember ever seeing the disk in any of the packs. are we going to have to pay for it now?.after playing it for so long? I realy dont expect to get a reply here, but it would be nice to have these questions answered. But i hope I have brought these to your and others attention.    if ya want to chat...pm me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(410900, 61264, 1013, 102747, 1072936800, 'I have a big problem', 'Hi,\n\nafter the new update, i had to login, but i forgot my account name.\n\nSo i made a new.\n\naccount name: cepo\n\nE-Mail: slipknot_13@gmx.de (mailto:slipknot_13@gmx.de) (I changed to slipknot_12@gmx.de (mailto:slipknot_12@gmx.de))\n\n\n\nAnd now, i can�t use my key!\n\nI don�t know, which nick i had\n\ni think it was like "nothing" (maybe cepo-eins, too)\n\nCan u check it please??\n\nI don�t want to buy a new HL version.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(414732, 61264, 1013, 102748, 1072936800, 'CD Key', 'This is very frustrating.  Its been a while since I have played HL. bought the game several years ago, and loved it.  The CD became so scratched, I went out and bought the Platinum Edition, I think. It came with all 4 games. Well its an older version so I needed to update it to play online. I spent forever looking for the update and then when I tried to use gamespy get the updated files, I had to sit and wait for 2 hours for the download to start. I dont understand why Valve cant have the updates on their own site. If they do, I sure can\'t find them. Well, after 10 hours of downloading I was able to update. I set up my steam account and tried to play. I was bummed when it made my machine crash over and over. I gave up. \n\n\n\nNow I have a new machine, and loaded HL, waited 2 hours to download update from Gamespy again. Luckily , i have cable now so it only took an hour to get the update this time. \n\n\n\nSo, now i have a new machine, cable connection, new account, and my cd key is invalid. Son of a *&*(^. \n\n\n\nThen it took me 2 days to be able to post here. Do you want my business or not?\n\n\n\nIt seems so easy to fix the cd key issue, My question is... ARE YOU GOING TO FIX IT? A little feedback from the powers to be would be nice.  Even if you just lie to us, its better than not answering the issue of " the cd Key"  I would think the easier it is to use Steam, the more players you would have, and the more software you would sell.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(414734, 61264, 1013, 102749, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by corp_krazy \n\nsome peoples account names are ISP email accounts that arent accessible anymore like mine, and when we tried to create a new account it say cd key already in use \n\nOK, we\'re going to try once more. It doesn\'t matter if the e-mail address isn\'t accessible anymore. The e-mail address linked to your account can be changed. The account name, however, remains your old e-mail address. Simple.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(414774, 61264, 1013, 102750, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by goweb \n\nOK, we\'re going to try once more. It doesn\'t matter if the e-mail address isn\'t accessible anymore. The e-mail address linked to your account can be changed. The account name, however, remains your old e-mail address. Simple.  \n\n\n\nare u saying they cant help anyone out with there cd keys\n\nbecuase/if its on a different account?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(414802, 61264, 1013, 102751, 1072936800, 'goweb heres the problem', 'Goweb\n\n this is directed at you, although i am not experiencing this problem, it seems to me that to change your mailing address you would have to be logged into steam and change it in your steam options folder, however if you do not have the information to log into your account you can not  change the mailing address. this is just my own hypothesis i may have missed a shortcut that would allow you to change your mailing address without being logged in.once again sorry if i have over looked any option that would allow you to overlook this minor issue', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(414836, 61264, 1013, 102749, 1072936800, 'goweb heres the problem', 'quote:Originally posted by arc arsenal \n\nGoweb\n\n this is directed at you, although i am not experiencing this problem, it seems to me that to change your mailing address you would have to be logged into steam and change it in your steam options folder, however if you do not have the information to log into your account you can not  change the mailing address. this is just my own hypothesis i may have missed a shortcut that would allow you to change your mailing address without being logged in.once again sorry if i have over looked any option that would allow you to overlook this minor issue  \n\nDo you know the e-mail address you used?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
