(410966, 61312, 1005, 102756, 1072936800, '', 'So, I should set my rate to 73728? no I dont think so.\n\n\n\nFlawed []\n\n\n\nWhile you are spot on with your calculations and what they mean - at least in calculating theoretical max download speeds, Thats not quite how it works.\n\n\n\nI would advise you that rates do not pertain so directly to your download speeds since CS rarely goes higher than 6kb/s even on 2MB Cable/DSL.\n\n\n\nNow, I haven\'t really thought this all through cos im trying to Watch 24 on DVD (Gotta love it), but a rate of 6000 on 56k will more than likely clog your connection up. try 4500 on 56k, 6000 on ISDN, 10000 on 256cable/dsl, 15000-25000 on 512/576/600kb adsl cable and so on.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
