(432862, 64680, 1013, 102776, 1072936800, 'Clear things up!', 'Im really confused by all the suggestions that peoples are coming with now :S \n\n\n\nIf you Teal buddy could post one post here and type the exactly thing that we have to do to get steam to work that would be great! I know that you are a busy man here.. \n\n\n\nTell us how we can fix it if we have a Steam.dll. problem and how to fix it if we have that win32 problem.. \n\n\n\nI know that you guys are normal ppls like us, so please take your time! \n\n\n\nThank you', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(432920, 64680, 1013, 102777, 1072936800, '', 'Heh, Thanks I\'ve never been called on specifically.\n\n\n\nThe Steam.DLL problem is the one I have actually had, and acutally solved for Steam. (well solved the way to fix it quickest)\n\n\n\nSo I\'ll start with it.\n\n\n\nFirst, you have to go to your Steam Folder, then click on the program \'UNWISE\' (it slightly resembles the recycle bin) \n\nNext, let it uninstall using the "automatic" mode.\n\n\n\nAfter this has happened you no longer have steam on your computer :\'( but heres how to get it back and fixed. []\n\n\n\nFirst get the latest installer from /download/SteamInstall.exe (/download/SteamInstall.exe) \n\nThis link is the straight DL from steam, how nice of them to be considerate and not make you sit through two hour lines on Fileplanet or Fileshack eh?\n\n\n\nOk once you have the installer, its simple! Install steam! And it will work, everyone who has had this problem, and followed my guidelines for fixing it are now playing on steam once again.\n\n\n\nThe Win32 Problem has been touched on by steam in the red "Read First" Threads. Next time I see waldo or Sherman online, i will also ask them for updated information on this problem to give to you all.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(p.S. Thanks for the thank you. [] When you get your Steam//Cs working would you like to play? Aim me: xPiXoNx   --- No hate mail on that please only here people [] )', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(432936, 64680, 1013, 102776, 1072936800, '', 'Thx man, i really apperciate what you are doing for us n00bs out here! I sure wanna play.. This all started when i was installing DoD... Silly DoD ruind my computer :P hehe', '127.0.0.1', 1),
