(438308, 65356, 1013, 102781, 1072936800, 'IMPORTANT: For Those With Input Lag Problems', 'Since the last update there have been more and more people complaining about input lag. This is NOT connection loss or choke nor is it an FPS problem, it is problem *ONLY* with the last 2 Steam updates.\n\n\n\nThe symptoms are:\n\n\n\nA significant (0.5-3second) delay from mouse movement or keyboard input to them taking effect ingame. This is usually intermittant rather than constant.\n\nNo lag whatsoever when specating, ie. Other people ingame appear to move/shoot perfectly normally. I say again: THIS IS NOT A CONNECTION BUG.\n\nNo FPS drop lower than the previous updates have caused.\n\n\n\n\n\nSo far no members of Staff have commented on any of this, those of us suffering with this problem have been flamed for not reading the Sticky threads concerning ATI FPS Drops or Laggy Server Connections.\n\n\n\nOnce again THIS IS NOT A PROBLEM WITH RATES OR FPS. I have not changed any of my settings, either Steam or Hardware related, since the update before this happened. All my other games work perfectly well, as did Steam before the Offline Mode update.\n\n\n\nThis is a very real a serious problem affecting all Steam games, and I\'ll keep bumping this until someone from Valve responds with a valid answer.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you need to know, I\'m running:\n\n\n\nWinXP Home SP1\n\nAthlon XP 2400+\n\n512Meg Ram\n\n256Meg Radeon 9600Pro\n\nMicrosoft Optial Mouse with Standard Keyboard\n\n\n\nIf you have the same problem (*That is, input Lag NOT connection or FPS problems*) please post here with your system spec.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438341, 65356, 1013, 102782, 1072936800, '', 'amd athlon xp 2600+\n\n2.09 ghz\n\nnvidia geforce fx 5200\n\n1.oo gb of ram\n\n164 gb of rom\n\n__________________\n\nFor Every Action There Is An Opposite Or Equal Reaction', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438400, 65356, 1013, 102783, 1072936800, '', 'For me, this problem has ocurred only when using my keyboard.\n\nWhat happens is, my mouse freezes and I keep moving after I release the key.\n\n\n\nWorse on heavy maps, like de_aztec.\n\n\n\nI mostly play CS but the problem is even worse in NS.\n\n\n\nDO NOT tell me to update my keyboard and/or mouse drivers as I\'ve had the problem on both my computers with wildly differrent specs and I\'ve switched between several differrent keyboards and mice. (no cordless crap)\n\n__________________\n\nSpecs:\n\nWindows XP Pro. English SP1\n\nMotherboard: MSI K7N2 Delta\n\nCPU: AMD Athlon XP3000+\n\nMemory:2x DDR 512MB  PC3200 \n\nVideo: ATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128MB /w Catalyst 4.2 drivers - \n\n"High Performance" settings\n\nSound: Integrated nvidia nForce2\n\n---- input ----\n\nMouse: Intellimouse Explorer 3.0 (usb)\n\nKeyboard: Logitech internet navigator SE (usb /w PS/2 adapter)\n\n----  Steam: CS 1.6 ----\n\n800x600 - 16bit\n\nofficial CPL-GUI.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438403, 65356, 1013, 102784, 1072936800, '', 'I used to have this problem. My system specs are in my signature.\n\n\n\nTo add to what phluid said: Please post when the problem began, what steps you have taken to try and resolve the problem, what programs you have set to run on startup, and what system services you have active.\n\n\n\nPlease also try the following steps:\n\n1. Ensure that your problem is actually an independent control lag problem, not one brought on by a ping of 5000. That is, you have keyboard or mouse lag even when you only have 10-40 ping.\n\n2. Ensure your PC is free of viruses, adware, and spyware.\n\n3. Try the DirectSound "emulation only" workaround: go to Start->Run->dxdiag->DirectSound->drag the slider at "sound acceleration" to the far left.\n\n4. Right-click Counter-Strike in the Games menu, go to Properties, and add -noforcemparms -noforcemaccel -noforcemspeed under launch options.\n\n5. Uninstall any third-party mouse and keyboard drivers (ones that did not come with Windows itself.)\n\n6. Roll back your sound card\'s drivers if possible.\n\n7. Open Task Manager and end any extraneous processes (programs not needed for your PC or Counter-Strike to operate.)\n\n8. Use BlackViper\'s Services 411 (http://www.blackviper.com/ (http://www.blackviper.com/)) to tweak your system services if you are using Windows 2000 or XP.\n\n9. Try setting the theme to "Windows Classic" (if running Windows XP) and uninstalling any third-party theming programs (WindowBlinds, etc.)\n\n__________________\n\nNeoflame\n\n\n\nCS-Relevant System Specs:\n\nP4 1.8 gHz\n\n512MB PC2100 DDRRAM\n\nATI Radeon 9600 Pro OC\'d to 480/320\n\n1024x768 85Hz FSAA=2x AF=4x\n\nATI Catalyst 4.3\n\nCrappy Avance AC\'97 Soundcard\n\nWindows XP Home Edition SP1/Mandrake Linux 10.0 Community\n\n256/1024Kbps Cable\n\n\n\nIf pro is the opposite of con, what is the opposite of progress?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438427, 65356, 1013, 102783, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve had this problem for at least 4-5 updates back. But it\'s always been worse in NS, and my current system is very high end, so I\'m not usually affected by the symptoms unless I\'m running a virus scan, winamp, and some extra background processes.\n\n__________________\n\nSpecs:\n\nWindows XP Pro. English SP1\n\nMotherboard: MSI K7N2 Delta\n\nCPU: AMD Athlon XP3000+\n\nMemory:2x DDR 512MB  PC3200 \n\nVideo: ATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128MB /w Catalyst 4.2 drivers - \n\n"High Performance" settings\n\nSound: Integrated nvidia nForce2\n\n---- input ----\n\nMouse: Intellimouse Explorer 3.0 (usb)\n\nKeyboard: Logitech internet navigator SE (usb /w PS/2 adapter)\n\n----  Steam: CS 1.6 ----\n\n800x600 - 16bit\n\nofficial CPL-GUI.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438430, 65356, 1013, 102785, 1072936800, '', 'hi guys, this problem you are having sucks. i am posting some really old info here in the outside chance it may help somebody. it has to do with direct 3d flip for input problems.\n\nwww.tweak3d.net/autoexec/halflife/ (http://www.tweak3d.net/autoexec/halflife/)\n\n I dont have the input problem myself, however im including this link for those who want to try the autoexec maker for performance boost. there is the 3d flip info 1/2 way down the page.\n\nive heard it has helped others with the problem. but plz dont yell at me if it doesnt work for you. yes the info is old, but it still is a great link to put in favs and use as needed.\n\na lil bit of copy and paste is all you need to do. good instructions at bottom of page. just have a blank notepad open for the info.\n\nhope it helps somebody out there.\n\n__________________\n\nmy pc stuff:\n\namd 2500 barton\n\ngigabyte mobo 7n400l\n\n1024 mb ddr400 (pc3200) ram dual channel\n\nPlantronics dsp 500 headset with\n\nbuilt in soundcard and speech\n\nrecognition.\n\nati 9600xt 128 mb\n\nmaxtor 80 gb with xp\n\n2nd drive 30 gb maxtor\n\ndsl 768/256 - creative 7410 external modem\n\n\n\nTFC nutaholic...oh my gawd.. dont touch that! thats my flag! \n\n[dont flame all the noObs...you werent born playing half life!!!]\n\nplayin da TFC  since demos had 4 mirvs! I lub de demo spammo!\n\nMember of [TNT] THE NAMELESSTEAM\n\nCopper Div. Champs 3-15-04 YaY !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(438473, 65356, 1013, 102783, 1072936800, '', 'Rocky,  I bet that\'s a good page for tweaking fps, but like you said yourself, it\'s probably not the solution.\n\n\n\nI think it could decrease the severity of the symptoms for some without removing the problem completely.\n\n__________________\n\nSpecs:\n\nWindows XP Pro. English SP1\n\nMotherboard: MSI K7N2 Delta\n\nCPU: AMD Athlon XP3000+\n\nMemory:2x DDR 512MB  PC3200 \n\nVideo: ATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128MB /w Catalyst 4.2 drivers - \n\n"High Performance" settings\n\nSound: Integrated nvidia nForce2\n\n---- input ----\n\nMouse: Intellimouse Explorer 3.0 (usb)\n\nKeyboard: Logitech internet navigator SE (usb /w PS/2 adapter)\n\n----  Steam: CS 1.6 ----\n\n800x600 - 16bit\n\nofficial CPL-GUI.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
