(439283, 65356, 1013, 102787, 1072936800, '', 'i had this same problem\n\n\n\nall i do is play in Offline Mode.. just go into offline mode BEFORE u connect to the internet and its fine, u only get the servers that u have in ur fav\'s tho, no internet games or friends list.\n\n\n\nand atm im running:\n\n\n\nRedeon 9000 Graphic Card ( Probably 64MB )\n\n\n\n3.06Ghz\n\n\n\n1GB DDR RAM ( getting another 1GB stick very soon :P )\n\n\n\nOnly 30GB hard drive []\n\n\n\nBut my Laptop is flying []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(439727, 65356, 1013, 102788, 1072936800, '', 'For me the problem has pretty much always been here.  I only play ns but I can say that it\'s significantly annoying.  My computer is:\n\nPentium 4 2.66ghz\n\n768 mb of ddr 2700 Ram\n\nGeforce MX 420\n\nLogitech wireless Mouse & Keyboard\n\n(The problem still happens with wired keyboards & mouses)\n\nOther games run perfectly fine for me, but when I open steam and play ns I get at least .5ms lag from my mouse and up to 3 or 4 seconds of lag sometimes.  Windows 98 compatability mode used to fix this problem for me, but now I can\'t use that "quick fix" so I\'m basically screwed out of playing any ns games.  I tried cs and dod long enough to experience problems and I dont even wanna bother now because never being able to aim directly sucks.  For now I\'m just gonna play Unreal Tournament 2004 where my mouse doesn\'t glitch up AT ALL!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
