(441143, 65626, 1013, 100118, 1072936800, '', 'http://enriched.zidev.com/software.php (http://enriched.zidev.com/software.php)\n\nlook for TCP optimizer at the bottom.\n\n\n\n\n\nin counterstrike:\n\npress "~"\n\ntype rate 20000\n\nsee if game gets better..\n\n\n\nrate 20000 works good for me.. try some other rates..\n\n\n\n\n\nClose the console press "~"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(442506, 65858, 1005, 102791, 1072936800, 'Possible Fix for lock up on exit', 'Im not going to say this will work for everyone but it did for me and why I dont know. I went into my C:\\Program Files\\Steam folder and deleted my ClientRegistry BLOB FILE then I restarted STEAM Since I did this no more lock ups on Exit. There Error I was getting was an offset file error. Dont be afraid to do this it will not damage your game in anyway. You will have to relog after update though so make sure you have your Password handy. Good Luck.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(447080, 66400, 1013, 102792, 1072936800, 'Cs:cz', 'I have a question about Condition Zero. Will CS:CZ and Cs 1.6 be compatible with each other, or will will CZ players only be to play with other CZ players. Also, when HL2 comes out, will there be a...CS2? If so, will that be compatible with CS and CZ? Please explain how this will work.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(447087, 66400, 1013, 102793, 1072936800, '', 'CZ players can play with CS1.6 players on CS 1.6 servers. However they can also play on CZ-only servers not available to CS 1.6 players.\n\n\n\n\n\nHL2 is the sequel to HL which is written using Valves new Engine - the Source Engine.\n\n\n\nCS2 will *probably* be a retail game based on the Source Engine. But we dont know this for sure.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(447092, 66400, 1013, 102792, 1072936800, '', 'Oh ok, thnx. So CZ is backwards compatible with 1.6, but 1.6 isn\'t compatible with CZ servers. Got it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(460876, 68076, 1005, 102801, 1072936800, 'Steam Does It Again', 'Ok, I really haven\'t had any problems with steam before up until the last update. I couldn\'t understand why everyone was hating on steam in the past. BUT HOW CAN YOU **** UP THIS BAD THIS MANY TIMES!?!?!\n\n\n\nThe crash bug in the last update was bad enough, but now after this last update when I alt+tab out of Day of Defeat (not sure if it does this for other games) MY ******* COUMPUTER REBOOTS. I get an error report saying there was a serious error in my NVIDIA drivers. \n\n\n\nDO YOU NOT EVEN TEST THESE THINGS BEFORE YOU SEND THEM OUT?? WE PAYED MONEY FOR THESE GAMES AND WE EXPECT THEM TO WORK. WE ARE HAVING THIS BS "BETA TEST" SHOVED DOWN OUR THROATS AND YOU DON\'T EVEN TAKE THE TIME TO PLAYTEST THE UPDATES. GET YOUR ACT TOGETHER DAMNIT WERE NOT YOUR BITCHES', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(461198, 68076, 1005, 102378, 1072936800, '', '*BUMP* \n\n\n\nbumping will get the devteam to notice this thread easier .\n\n\n\ni havent played dod since the update , i\'ll try it later .\n\ni hope i don\'t get this problem .', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(464887, 68076, 1005, 102802, 1072936800, '', 'I agree with you Steam and alot of other companys seem to think more of trying to make money and geting ppl to dl stuff so they can Muck up our computer or just straight up use us for trial and error...If you think I am going to dl anymore steam stuff you are crazy....Bye Bye Steam I would rather poke my eyes out with flaming sticks than play steam anymore....If you are tired of the bugs , Lag and just overall poor quality of Steam just uninstall it like I have...Now I see why some clans have returned from the BS and I am sure more will follow.....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
