(469230, 68076, 1005, 102804, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bballr4567 \n\nGuys you have to be patient. They dont have too many people working for them. They have to fix this bug in every game.  \n\n\n\nIn think in two weeks at least an acknoledgement of "Ok guys there\'s a problem and we are working on it" isn\'t asking too much.  Like I said CZ hasn\'t been out long at all and theres already two updates for it. Plain and simple DOD is not a priority', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(469329, 68076, 1005, 102805, 1072936800, '', 'I agree and rest assured they can kiss a TON of money good bye if they don\'t treat their present fan base better. In the retail business, the saying goes it\'s harder to attract new customers than to keep the ones you have..... Seems no one at VALVe/STEAM/Sierra has heard of this motto....or these\n\n\n\nOnce bitten, twice shy\n\n\n\nFool me once, shame on you. Fool me twice, shame on me.\n\n\n\nand others....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(470142, 68076, 1005, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Yea but look at the updates that it has gotten. Its the same updates that every single game had got like 4 weeks ago. They havent done anything to the game itself. Give it time they dont have very many people working inside the place. And its not like you cant get out of the game. Sure you have to do a couple extra steps but so what.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(470433, 68076, 1005, 102804, 1072936800, 'not just one bug', 'Aside from the fact that it has been two weeks since there "update" has reaked havoc on systems everywhere...\n\n[rant] Strikes me as ood as when virii do this we call it a crime... when software companies do it it\'s called a bug. Bug... Virus... hmmm [/rant]\n\n\n\nI\'m not having just the crash bug.. I have posted this in another thread and others agreed they are having a hard time with it as well...\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Targeted \n\nI don\'t know if anyone else has this problem as well but it is related to the ones mentioned above.  Please be constructive in your comments.\n\n\n\nI notice usually when I start out playing DOD that I get really good on targeted kills. By targeted I mean my crosshairs are narrowed and I get a what you see is what you get type shooting soloutions. After some time of playiing it seems that the stability of my shooting soloution weakens. That is to say I shoot but do not hit my targets in the crooshair field. While I tend to use a semi automatic soloution I can really feel this difference. If I use an automatic it\'s alot less evident but can tell it to some extent. I have checked to make sure its not lag. Typically i can play in the 45-60ish pings and thats what I\'m used too. After this starts happening..it is only a matter of time before DOD will crash. Sometimes its not long after sometimes its way after\n\n\n\n Any ideas anyone?  \n\n\n\nOthers backed me up on this. So it\'s not just one bug we are talking about. Not to mention that it\'s thier update that messed it up. Obviously it doesn\'t take a genius to figure this..back out the "update" since so many people are having problems untill they fix it(which would require them using people to beta test OTHER than US!!!) I\'m starting to picture the standard attire at Valve\\Steam is white lab coats. Gues what we get... mouse ears and whiskers..and guess what we ain\'t the Mousekateers people!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(478650, 68076, 1005, 102806, 1072936800, 'not enough employees', 'not enough employees is not a good excuse. they give themselves the work so why are they short handed? overextending themselves is foolish and annoying. hire more people or cut back on the projects until they are finished. truly nuff said', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(479238, 68076, 1005, 102807, 1072936800, 'Bugs and Such', 'Another point that was mentioned but not really discussed is that the game worked better before their last major update (March 10?), So why not just undo the last update until they have these bugs worked out?\n\n\n\nI also agree that someone from Steam at least acknowledging the problem and letting us know they are working on it would be a common courtesey.\n\n\n\n ---This lack of intrest on Steam\'s part makes me think that, indeed, they have no plans to fix this problem.--- (sad)\n\n\n\nAlso -  Saying that it isn\'t really that big of a deal is kinda avoiding the issue, yeah compared to alot of other problems in the world this is not a big deal, but for the people that have an hour or two of free time here and there to play dod, having to reboot the game every 20 minutes or so is a pain in the ****[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(461407, 68171, 1005, 101429, 1072936800, 'What $30.00 is worth!! Read Now!!', 'Okay Valve seriously screwed up on this one, this is worse than the Blue Shift release since that actually had a single player game that was half-way entertaining.  They are charging $30.00 for CZ, they won\'t let you use the new Ritual models, they updated some maps, and included Bot support, wow POD bot is free.  They have had 3 years to make this game and well they put out a pack that is worth maybe 10 bucks for the "new" contnent.\n\n\n\nOn retrospect lets look at what some other game companies are releasing for $39.00 now a days?  Well DICE recently released Battlefield Vietnam.  A completely new game with new vehicles, upgraded graphics engine, awesome soundtrack, killer huge maps, changed variations in play styles and tactics.  That seems like a worthy $39.99 these days.\n\n\n\nOkay since that may be a sole exception lets try another one.  Hmm what else just got released, oh yeah Epic Games Unreal Tournament 2004.  Well if you have read any reviews they say this is "the" game to have.  What did they offer to players?  An upgraded graphics engine that is gorgeous, new game play modes "onslaught is a blast!", new models, they brought the assault mode back, over 100 maps (Yes 119 total), and the fastest shooter in the world.\n\n\n\nOkay lets take Valve, they charge $30.00 for it over Steam and $39.99 in stores.  Okay I have faith in Valve, they won\'t screw the community.  For my $30.00 I get bots (that don\'t work all that well and cannot jump or climb ladders), I get some redone maps (only 3-4 are new), no upgraded graphics engine same old **** models, no new game modes, no new sounds.  \n\n\n\nI used to believe that Valve was concerned about their community, at one point they were, but that time was long ago and now all if about money and making a profit.  They really screwed us on this release in hoping the CS name would sell another product.  This is not the first time they screwed people, what they charged people for CS 1.5 and DoD although it was a free download.  \n\n\n\nEpic and DICE seem to have gotten the idea that they need to listen to their community, Valve has forgotten us, it is a very say day indeed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
