(470714, 69450, 1005, 102846, 1072936800, '', 'um read bud im not talking about getting banned for hacking im talking about CZ not what it was advertised to be, meaning that the 32(think thats what it was) new weapons,new models, screens on the box and everything else isnt in the game is false advertising, O and FYI the XBOX version has everything the game should be I.E. new modles weapons etc.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(470747, 69450, 1005, 102627, 1072936800, '', 'Wow ... Devlin ... your CS|RU FE has to be THE best CS pack ever created ... GJ ... I stopped playing CS for good and gave away my Steam account, but seeing the screenshots makes me wish I hadn\'t ...\n\n__________________\n\n12 Year Old AOLer Forum Moderator Nominees:\n\n\nbigun, eck| A L ! E N, {X][S}MILF, alen284, AK47FOOL, Aim@Me, ThE4cE, steamuser, \n\n\nn!ce, Cereph, NEED HELP21, 0101.pimp();', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(470775, 69450, 1005, 100065, 1072936800, 'Sloppy work, just very sloppy', 'quote:Originally posted by Devlin \n\n\nI\'m wondering if you guys are lacking resources. Logically, you haven\'t published in 5 years and did a lot of development. That\'s a hellof a bill to pay. That about sums it up in a nutshell. Valve isn\'t a big company, everybody tends to confuse it with a large (sometimes international) company. They don\'t have a lot of people to work on every single bug fix you want, but it\'s on their to-do list (eventually).\n\n\n\n\n\nValve put all the money they got from HL + a bit more and put it into the development of HL2. THis was said numerous times from Gabe Newell in interviews I have seen over the internet. That\'s not a whole lot of money left to hire new support reps or a bug development team. Just be patient.\n\n__________________\n\nGet your official Killer Koala postings right here at steampowered.com. Now with over 1800+ posts to my name, that shows dedication!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(473137, 69450, 1005, 102844, 1072936800, '', 'You have a point, but I would do it.. for FREE!\n\n\n\n\n\nI work as a software developer for multiple companies and I don\'t get paid much either, but I DO deliver my software (as good as)bug-free, and so is expected of me before I get paid.\n\n\n\n\n\nWell, maybe I missed some economic classes.. ow well\n\n__________________\n\nDevlin\n\n\nCS|RU Developer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(473183, 69450, 1005, 100204, 1072936800, 'Re: Sloppy work, just very sloppy', 'quote:Originally posted by Killer Koala \n\n\nThat about sums it up in a nutshell. Valve isn\'t a big company, everybody tends to confuse it with a large (sometimes international) company. They don\'t have a lot of people to work on every single bug fix you want, but it\'s on their to-do list (eventually).\n\n\n\n\n\nValve put all the money they got from HL + a bit more and put it into the development of HL2. THis was said numerous times from Gabe Newell in interviews I have seen over the internet. That\'s not a whole lot of money left to hire new support reps or a bug development team. Just be patient.  \n\n\nThank God, Half Life 2 will own everything out there! [] That way they\'ll get money for people! No more excuses Valve! []\n\n__________________\n\n*Poke*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(474534, 69450, 1005, 101178, 1072936800, '', '"Valve put all the money they got from HL + a bit more and put it into the development of HL2. THis was said numerous times from Gabe Newell in interviews I have seen over the internet."\n\n\n\n\n\nI think thats exactly Devlins point. Why release the game when its so buggy? I don\'t see any point in releasing half-arsed games that just causes more people to complain. More stress. Valve definately have no excuses for HL2.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf they are that tight on resources etc, they should focus on one thing at a time. At the moment, that would be HL2. Its just a pity they can\'t afford to get more staff. :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(475375, 69450, 1005, 102486, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Devlin \n\n\nYou have a point, but I would do it.. for FREE!\n\n\n\n\n\nI work as a software developer for multiple companies and I don\'t get paid much either, but I DO deliver my software (as good as)bug-free, and so is expected of me before I get paid.\n\n\n\n\n\nWell, maybe I missed some economic classes.. ow well  Donations people []\n\n__________________\n\n--- Getting computer ON FRIDAY, 4/9\n\n\n\n\n\nAMD Athlon XP 2800+ 32bit, 512mb Corsair Dual-Channel \'Low Latency\' DDR PC3200 RAM, ATi Radeon 9700 Pro 128mb 8x AGP, 280GB 7200RPM HDD, Windows XP Professional\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope now my CS won\'t run like assmonkey :D\n\n\n\n\n\nMe and The-Moose are the founders of www.steamingpileof****.com\n\n\nIt\'s funny how this link ACTUALLY works! Ironic, isn\'t it? URL redirection is teh shiz :)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(471851, 69671, 1005, 102847, 1072936800, 'request for statement from valve', 'This is a request for some kind of statement regarding the future of the counterstrike: condition zero title from a valve employee.\n\n\n\nI know you are aware that many of your customers were left a bit confiused regarding the condition of the released title and its content.  Some of your customers have shown great frustration at what they ended up buying.\n\n\n\nAlthough some users are completely happy and may not agree with those that are showing such frustration.\n\n\n\nIt\'s my hopes that you can release some kind of statement regarding its future.  Even something simple like "Don\'t worry cs fans, were working hard on new content and patches and they will be coming in the future.  Sorry can\'t commit to a date, but its coming." would do us all wonders.\n\n\n\nThank you for taking the time to read my thread.\n\n\n\n-Me\n\n\n\nP.S.\n\n\n\nGuys lets please keep this one flame free.  It\'s in everyones best interest here.  Just keep it bumped =)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(471890, 69671, 1005, 102848, 1072936800, '', 'well thought out cerebix... i could not agree with you more.  After WASTING my 30 bucks on CZ i would like to here somthing from valve. There are many more VERY strong feelings i would like to express but for the sake of somthing happening and to keep this flame free i will keep my mouth shut.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(471899, 69671, 1005, 100829, 1072936800, '', 'n1 cerebrix', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(471930, 69671, 1005, 102849, 1072936800, '', 'here here, please lets hear something, even "sorry, what you bought is what you get" would be better than nothing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(471968, 69671, 1005, 102848, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jackals \n\nhere here, please lets hear something, even "sorry, what you bought is what you get" would be better than nothing.  \n\n\n\ni agree but i would rather have them say:\n\n\n\n"ummm errr we did use false advertizing to get you all to buy our bot err i mean game and we have no intentions to give new skins or add any new features to an already complete game"\n\n\n\nmy faith in valve would be restored if they said anything but i think the other responce would be so thruthfull[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472002, 69671, 1005, 101444, 1072936800, '', 'Here\'s somthing for you: what you saw as "advertised" was really "previously advertised".  Let me explain for those who don\' know.  Origionally VALVe outsourced the development of Condition Zero to a software develop company called Ritualistic Entertainment.  That game had new weapons, models, maps - and a single-player mission campaign accross the world, and is now known as the deleted scenes.\n\n\n\nWhat happened to that about 2/3 of the way through the development process was that VALVe rejected what Ritual was developing for unknown reasons and transfered the project to Turtle Rock Studios.  What Turtle Rock produced is what we now know as Condition Zero: bots, some new maps and textures, and a Tony Hawk-esque single-player game.\n\n\n\nNow the confusion is 2-fold; one, that many retailers (and the publisher SIERRA) continued to advertise the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game, which was no longer being developed.  Two, that the game was boxed in a Ritual boxed which was designed to point out the features of the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game.\n\n\n\nHonestly, I understand the frustration - but if you\'d read the latest CS Nation review you\'d have known all that.  You cannot blame VALVe for your inability to keep up with current data reguarding their projects - you can however blame SIERRA, and your local retailer.  What you can blame VALVe for is switching developers.  That was most likely an upper management decision, and they\'ll have to live with that for a while - for as we all know, the deleted scenes kick ass.\n\n\n\nAs for the models, 1 of 3 things is occuring.  One, VALVe does not have sufficient permission or rights to use the Ritual material (new skins, models, maps, etc) on the Turtle Rock game.  If this is the case, the possibility remains that they will be released as an update.  Two, Turtle Rock refused to incorporate Ritual\'s work in their game - wanting to keep the game true to their namesake.  VALVe may be bound by their decision to do so.  If this is the case, it still lends to the idea that the Ritual material may be released officially.  The last possibility is the VALVe is holding them out of sheer spite, that they think that because its in the Deleted Scenes that they do not need to include it in the actual game.\n\n\n\nI hope this has explained many of the questions being asked in this thread.  As a reminder I am not an employee of VALVe and do not speak on their behalf - I consider myself and informed observer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472071, 69671, 1005, 102849, 1072936800, '', 'As i understand, and please p-wolf, correct me if I am wrong, the retail box has the ritual logo on, thus is an error.  However I went into my local retailer (EBGAMES), and looked at the stragtegy guide which has the turtle rock logo on it (not ritual), in this stragtegy guide it has the training from deleted scenes, the new weapons, new maps, but with the rest of the guide is all based on how the "official release" is.  So to summerize, the stragey guide covers a mix between rituals and turtle rock, but wit the turtle rock logo on it.  I suggest you go look in your retailer for it and then post a reply.\n\n\n\nAs a reminder, I like valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472086, 69671, 1005, 101444, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jackals \n\nAs i understand, and please p-wolf, correct me if I am wrong, the retail box has the ritual logo on, thus is an error.  However I went into my local retailer (EBGAMES), and looked at the stragtegy guide which has the turtle rock logo on it (not ritual), in this stragtegy guide it has the training from deleted scenes, the new weapons, new maps, but with the rest of the guide is all based on how the "official release" is.  So to summerize, the stragey guide covers a mix between rituals and turtle rock, but wit the turtle rock logo on it.  I suggest you go look in your retailer for it and then post a reply.\n\n\n\nActually if you read my post I did mention the Ritual box still being used.  You are correct, and the strategy guide includes the Ritual-like walkthrough because you still get the Deleted Scenes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472090, 69671, 1005, 102850, 1072936800, 'I AGREE', 'I NEED SOME SORT OF INFROMATION ON SOME NEW STUFF', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472095, 69671, 1005, 101444, 1072936800, 'I AGREE', 'quote:Originally posted by PerZin \n\nI NEED SOME SORT OF INFROMATION ON SOME NEW STUFF \n\n\n\nDid you READ what I posted?  Please consider it, and don\'t use caps you 12 year-old AOL user you.  Next thing you know, you\'ll be saying "OMG WTF H@X!" - and you don\'t want that, do you?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472118, 69671, 1005, 102851, 1072936800, '', 'This is all for nothing guys,\n\nValve will never respond to our questions, they never have, so why now.\n\nThere must be a law against what they did. All a got is new maps for $59 Australian.\n\nValve and Nvidia must have the same screwedup managment who release products on lie\'s and fauls advertising.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472163, 69671, 1005, 102847, 1072936800, '', 'guys please move the chit chat to another thread, theres plenty of them you can debate things in.\n\n\n\nthanks for the bumps tho', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472198, 69671, 1005, 102852, 1072936800, 'Warning - completely un-informed opinion', 'Gentlemen:\n\n\n\nAs a non-CS / CS:CZ player I make the following observations:\n\n\n\n1. Fine thread you have started here. Nice to see that there are CS players with more than the ability to twitch and shoot.\n\n\n\n2. cerebrix: I have yet to see any responsible statement from any Steam - Valve employee of any degree of authority or knowledge on this web site, in any forum or in any thread. With all due respect to the other Steam - Valve employees who have posted, I am talking about SENIOR Steam - Valve employees or decision makers.\n\n\n\n3. P-Wolf: [ this is where the un-informed opinion comes in... I know nothing of CS / CS:CZ other than it exists ... I\'m a DoDer and would be playing, but for the latest round of Steam bugs ]\n\n\n\n\n\nP-Wolf said: Now the confusion is 2-fold; one, that many retailers (and the publisher SIERRA) continued to advertise the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game, which was no longer being developed. Two, that the game was boxed in a Ritual boxed which was designed to point out the features of the Ritualistic Entertainment version of the game. \n\n\n\nZot says: What? You have *got* to be kidding me? That must be on the very edge, if not over the line, of false advertizing. I\'m sure these things are checked by lawyers for Valve - Sierra - Ritualistic, but if not illegal that is right at the top of the list of mis-leading practices.\n\n\n\nP-Wolf said: if you\'d read the latest CS Nation review you\'d have known all that. You cannot blame VALVe for your inability to keep up with current data reguarding their projects - you can however blame SIERRA, and your local retailer. \n\n\n\n\n\nZot says: Huh? All due respect P-Wolf, getting solid regular information out of Valve is anything BUT easy and certainly finding anything realiable about Valve projects on the internet is like looking for a needle in a hay stack. There is ten times as much ....er...make that 1 million times more bs and speculation about Steam - Valve and their projects than any solid information provided by those who could/should be providing that information.\n\n\n\nBlame Sierra? Ya, ok. I\'ll go along with that.\n\n\n\nBlame your local retailer? For what? Selling product? Not warning you that you may not like what you are buying? Not ripping the packaging off and wrapping it in plain brown paper? I don\'t see the retailers role in this deception. Likely the retailers are even more in the dark than buyers of pc games when it comes to these issues.\n\n\n\nZot final comment:\n\n\n\nIt is nice to see a well presented thread. It is also pathetic to see that Steam - Valve et al have abandon the floor, so to speak, and left it for their customers and "the community" to try and figure out what Steam - Valve might say to explain these types of issues, if it were not for the fact that Steam-Valve et al have the hear-no-evil, see-no-evil, speak-no-evil policy of dealing with customers, complaints and the community in general.\n\n\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nZot', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472204, 69671, 1005, 101444, 1072936800, '', 'I\'d hardly consider my opinion uninformed.  I\'ve played CS for 4 years, and beaten this game already - and yet I SOMEHOW managed to keep up with the developer change unlike apparently: you.  What I said is what happened.  As for the release information - did you try CZ\'s official site?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(472210, 69671, 1005, 102848, 1072936800, '', 'p-wolf... thanks for summing it up for us.  From what you have said and what I already know I think it is safe to say that cz advertizing and selling was not completly true and understood by all who bought it. I have played some more and enjoy it somewhat, but I really do feel sorry for all the people who preordered it along time ago hoping for all the knew stuff.\n\n\n\nI am still quite worried and somewhat mad about the amazon description about the product because it baces the information about the old game. also the OFFICIAL cz site still uses the old skins and guns for their picture.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(474947, 70127, 1005, 100349, 1072936800, 'Snagging CZero stuff and linking to it is a big "NO" on here', 'No.  No no no no no.  NO\n\n\n\nOK guys.   We want to make it really clear that posting links to, or information on how to extract or get CZero stuff is a big "NO".  No links to extracted files, stuff you "found" that got leaked, etc.\n\n\n\nI know it\'s "easy" to do, and I\'m sure some of you think Valve "owes" you this.  But the bottom line is it\'s not exactly legal at all.  Go talk about it somewhere else all you want, but not on Valve\'s own forums.\n\n\n\nYou\'ll find threads on this subject will be closed, and the posters banned depending on how obvious (ie, stupid given this warning) the poster is.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(483985, 71458, 1013, 102946, 1072936800, 'Legal CS Centers', 'I saw somewhere that Valve says there are 800 - 1,000 or so game centers paying for the Cyber Cafe License.  (/?area=cybercafes (/?area=cybercafes)).  I am going to visit California in a few weeks and would like to visit a game center while I am out there.  Is there a list of legal game centers somewhere so I can visit a center that is actually paying for Valve products?  Is the info posted somewhere for gamers to find?\n\n\n\nI would hate to visit a center that is not paying, when I can support the centers who are supporting Valve.\n\n\n\nI would think that if there are 800 - 1,000 centers out there paying for the license, the least Valve could do is post the names and addresses of the centers that are participating in the program.\n\n\n\nIf Valve won\'t at least publicize the centers, why would any new center join the program?  And how are customers like me supposed to find them?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(484956, 71458, 1013, 103435, 1072936800, 'Yeah Yeah', 'I totally agree with you, we (who support the valve cyber cafe program and operate LEGALLY) should get some credit for it......\n\n\n\nThanx Valve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(487332, 71458, 1013, 100136, 1072936800, 'Legal CS Centers', 'quote:Originally posted by Crucifingers \n\nI saw somewhere that Valve says there are 800 - 1,000 or so game centers paying for the Cyber Cafe License.  (/?area=cybercafes (/?area=cybercafes)).  I am going to visit California in a few weeks and would like to visit a game center while I am out there.  Is there a list of legal game centers somewhere so I can visit a center that is actually paying for Valve products?  Is the info posted somewhere for gamers to find?\n\n\n\nI would hate to visit a center that is not paying, when I can support the centers who are supporting Valve.\n\n\n\nI would think that if there are 800 - 1,000 centers out there paying for the license, the least Valve could do is post the names and addresses of the centers that are participating in the program.\n\n\n\nIf Valve won\'t at least publicize the centers, why would any new center join the program?  And how are customers like me supposed to find them?  \n\n\n\nyesss good idea. they should contact them and ask if they want to be included on...the website i suppose. i would love to know what ones are around in my area, too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(506559, 71458, 1013, 100587, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, that\'s the Nvidia is doing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(508021, 71458, 1013, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'Yep Nvidia\'s site u can find "The Way is Nvidia, Meant to be played" Cyber Cafes there.\n\n\n\nMaybe VALVe can do that too? I mean I can see the Cyber Cafe\'s Title on the STEAM site now, but its for "Please sign up to our program"\n\n\n\nAdd a few words like \n\n\n\n"Visit one of our Cyber Cafes for all the latest STEAM ENABLED games!"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(536647, 71458, 1013, 100030, 1072936800, '', 'We have begun work on this.\n\n\n\nMike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(587713, 71458, 1013, 100262, 1072936800, '', 'If you\'re looking for a place to play in Southern California, the cafe I represent is legally licensed by Valve.\n\n\n\neCyberDeck\n\n4249 Campus Dr #b144\n\nIrvine, CA 92612\n\n\n\nIn the University center right across the street from UC Irvine. We\'re right next to the 24 hour fitness.\n\n\n\nAnd yes, I agree, these Cafes should be posted up just like how other companies put up their licensed cafes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(618913, 71458, 1013, 103436, 1072936800, '', 'looking for a good LAN center who has paid for STEAM in Northern California Visit:\n\n\n\nDefcon 1 Network Center\n\n1451 Southwest Blvd.\n\nRohnert Park, CA\n\n94928', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(620981, 71458, 1013, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'Maybe I should do that too?\n\n\n\nWe\'re probably the only one around this WHOLE Chinatown/Cityhall area with a Legal STEAM licenese. and probably the only place with Fiber Optic (yep, an OC-3) installed at our Cafe. \n\n\n\nSome of our computers are using Athlon64 and Radeon 9800 Pro, we\'re going to put more Athlon64 Comps with Radeon X800 XT video cards in the 2-3 months.\n\n\n\nWe have STEAM on all computers, but of course we have WAY more games than that :-) , stop by for more details!\n\n\n\nAddress is : \n\nGame Players Station\n\n28 Elizabeth ST 2nd FL\n\nNew York NY 10013\n\n\n\nLooking forward to see ya :-)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
