(646898, 71458, 1013, 102946, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Mike Dunkle \n\nWe have begun work on this.\n\n\n\nMike  \n\n\n\nHow long before we have a list of "Centers actually paying Valve"?  Or is the list now complete with the five centers who posted their own information in this thread?\n\n\n\nValve used to spout that they had 1,000 centers participating in the cybercafe program, then they dropped the number to 800.  To date, I have only seen proof of five self-proclaimers in this thread.\n\n\n\nIt\'s been about 6 weeks since Mike said they were working on posting a list.  How hard could it be to upload a list of centers to a webpage?  Is Valve totally embarrassed at the lack of participation from game centers that they are afraid to actually list them for all to see?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(646973, 71458, 1013, 100030, 1072936800, '', 'The project is a background task while we focus on more valuable features/releases like HL2, CS-Source, and a cafe update/license server.  The feedback I get from the cafes in the program is that they would like to have these things ASAP.\n\n\n\nMike\n\n\n\nP.S. We are doing our best to protect cafes in the program.  C & D letters are being sent as we discover cafes not in the program using our software.  Cafes in the program should send us information about cafes in their area that are not in the program to protect their investment.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(650582, 71458, 1013, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'Sounds cool.\n\n\n\nIt will be cool if the Cafe Content server gonna be out soon [] so All my cafe\'s computer can just "download" the updates from the server instead of lagging the whole internet connection.\n\n\n\n(because its still a pain to copy the files to every single computer I have every time STEAM having some big updates)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(489477, 72135, 1013, 102854, 1072936800, 'Pay to play on Steam. Now official? (see Screenshots)', 'Hi, I just read that there will be a online fee to play via steam.\n\n\nIs it now official? I read that payment software will come out within one of the next updates.\n\n\nhttp://www.counter-strike.de/newspics/counter-strike.de/200404/news-1-1080774604.jpg (http://www.counter-strike.de/newspics/counter-strike.de/200404/news-1-1080774604.jpg)\n\n\nhttp://www.counter-strike.de/newspics/counter-strike.de/200404/news-2-1080774604.jpg (http://www.counter-strike.de/newspics/counter-strike.de/200404/news-2-1080774604.jpg)\n\n\nLook at the screenshots.\n\n\nI guess we all knew, that this will happen sooner or later.\n\n\nDamn, I will not pay to play via this crapy steam s h i t.\n\n\nEven if it will just cost 1 $ a year.\n\n\nIs there any way to play CS 1.6 and DOD without steam?\n\n\nWhat will you do?\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is pretty obvious that this is fake. Valve is a US company and in the US we use \'.\' not \',\' to seperate dollars and cents. Not only is the creator obviously European but he needs to try harder and do his homework. Also, IC Wiener I would like to see you edit this out now. Now your thread will die a slow painful death cause you made me lock it. \n\n\n\n\n\nLove\n\n\nIntrepid00', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(489507, 72135, 1013, 101711, 1072936800, '', 'It is possible, but I know they will lose a TON of players from that, because the majority do not have access to a credit card.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso, I checked the Steam support section to see if any changes were made and I saw this:\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:The billing policies for Steam can be found here [coming soon].\n\n\n\n\n\nSomething is sure to happen very very soon.\n\n\n\n\n\nEDIT: Why in those screenshots are the money and cents seperated by commas, when it should be periods?\n\n\n\n\n\nExample: Counter-Strike Monthly Fee: $4,99\n\n\n\n\n\nIt should be: Counter-Strike Monthly Fee: $4.99\n\n__________________\n\nComputer Specs:\n\n\n\n\n\n2.6 GHz Pentium 4 800mhz Processor w/ Hyper-Threading Technology\n\n\nRadeon 9800 Pro 128mb Graphics Card\n\n\n80Gb 7200RPM Maxtor Hard Drive\n\n\n512mb DDR Dual Channel Memory w/ 400mhz FSB\n\n\nWindows XP Home Edition\n\n\nSoundBlaster Live! 5.1 Digital\n\n\n3mbps Broadband (Adelphia)\n\n\n\n\n\nComputer and CS Tweaked to perfection\n\n\nAverage 200-300 FPS in Counter-Strike (even during shoot outs)\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------------------------------------\n\n\nIgnorant morons on the forums (ignor them at all times):\n\n\neck| A L ! E N, General Ivan, cloudstrife79, newjack4200, GP1183, shuda, Ran321.\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------------------------------------\n\n\nSmart/Non-ignorant people:\n\n\nTKL, Goatblower, g@z, me™,  Chimp, Mr. Chris, Somedude212.\n\n\n\n\n\n最明智不问问题, 因此, 没人是明智的。', '127.0.0.1', 1),
