(490394, 72236, 1026, 101757, 1072936800, 'what linux distro is your server on?', 'just wondering what people use... as im planning on switching to linux. if that has been asked before.. at least one person reply telling me, and then the rest of you just ignore this post.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(490478, 72236, 1026, 102857, 1072936800, '', 'debian woody ! what else ??? ;-)))', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(490866, 72236, 1026, 102858, 1072936800, '', 'You can use almost any distro that you want, Debian is a good one, I personally use Gentoo.  Check out Distrowatch to compare different distros.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.distrowatch.com (http://www.distrowatch.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(490909, 72236, 1026, 102859, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m currently using a Debian Woody/Sarge hybrid.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(491537, 72236, 1026, 102860, 1072936800, '', 'I use gentoo for my x86-64\'s and the performance is horrible compared to fedora.\n\n\n\nhondaman\n\nwww.hardgaming.com (http://www.hardgaming.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(492259, 72236, 1026, 102858, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m assuming you\'ve compiled the sources properly for the AMD64 arch.  I\'ve always have had equal or better preformance with Gentoo compared to other distros.  \n\n\n\nIn the end it really just comes down to the distro you prefer the most, personally I\'d try a couple.  Especially if you are trying to learn here too.  If you aren\'t trying to learn and just want to get a server up, I would not recommend Gentoo because of it\'s more involved setup.  If you just want to get a system up and running Fedora (basically RedHat\'s development distro) wouldn\'t be a bad choice.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.distrowatch.com (http://www.distrowatch.com)\n\nhttp://www.gentoo.org (http://www.gentoo.org)\n\nhttp://www.debian.org (http://www.debian.org)\n\nhttp://fedora.redhat.com (http://fedora.redhat.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(493179, 72236, 1026, 102861, 1072936800, '', 'SuSE.\n\nBecause people in the industry dont have an entire day to compile Gentoo! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(493325, 72236, 1026, 102858, 1072936800, '', 'Well, that completely depends on the industry.\n\n\n\nIf you are doing webhosting, *BSD would be the way to go. []\n\n\n\nBSD based servers consistently come up with the longest uptime and lowest failed requests of any OS.  Besides if you really want you can get precompiled Gentoo optimized for most architectures.\n\n\n\nI haven\'t used SuSe in quite some time, but I\'m interested in the changes Novell will bring to them.  I think the addition of suse to the discussion just leaves Mandrake and Slackware out for the major distros.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.distrowatch.com (http://www.distrowatch.com) \n\nhttp://www.gentoo.org (http://www.gentoo.org) \n\nhttp://www.debian.org (http://www.debian.org) \n\nhttp://fedora.redhat.com (http://fedora.redhat.com)\n\nhttp://www.suse.com (http://www.suse.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(495263, 72236, 1026, 102533, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Master Ruthless \n\nSuSE.\n\nBecause people in the industry dont have an entire day to compile Gentoo! []  \n\nDid you ever hear about stage tarballs? Or do you really want X running on your gameserver to waste a few more resources ...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(497454, 72236, 1026, 101757, 1072936800, '', 'after somer reading (thanks for the links Scorpian_Sting) i think im ganna give slackware a try... any comments on my decision (such as, reasons not to)?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(497541, 72236, 1026, 100270, 1072936800, '', 'Hi\n\n\n\ndoes the cpu usage really drops with debian or slackware? i use suse 9.0 and for 16 slot cs 1.6 in need 20-50% of a XP2500+ !!\n\nits a little to much :-(', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(497927, 72236, 1026, 102858, 1072936800, '', 'Slackware is the oldest continually developed distro out there.  I know several people who really like it though I\'ve never actually used it.  It may be a bit more complex than something like SuSe or Fedora, but probably is a good choice.\n\n\n\nCPU usage will be dependent on the plugins running on the server, people on the server, map of the server etc.  It will also depend on the other services running on the machine and can also be affected by different compiling optimizations.\n\n\n\nIf you are running a i686 compiled software (assuming that is right for your cpu) and have already eliminated unneeded services you are unlikely to find much of a difference between distros.  Though each one does have a slightly different kernel which may give you a percentage point of difference here and there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498770, 72236, 1026, 102861, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LaMersSs \n\nDid you ever hear about stage tarballs? Or do you really want X running on your gameserver to waste a few more resources ...  \n\n\n\nHum\n\nIt is not that hard to install any distro minus X...\n\nGentoo isn\'t the only distro you can strip X from.\n\n\n\nAlso have you ever heard of init3???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499318, 72236, 1026, 101757, 1072936800, '', 'whats this "X" that is referred to many times in this thread?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499444, 72236, 1026, 102861, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by white_rabbit \n\nwhats this "X" that is referred to many times in this thread?  \n\n\n\nI hope your joking but just in case your not heres an explaination...\n\n\n\nIt is the MS Windows like GUI interface that make Linux or UNIX look kinda like Windows instead od DOS.\n\n\n\nPeople feel including myself that to run X on a server drains resources that can be put to better use. Kinda like DOS doesn\'t use up near as much in the way of memory and processor power as Windows does.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(491595, 72373, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, 'Did you get VAC banned today?', 'About 2500 accounts got banned by mistake today, but the bans have been rolled back.  Those banned should be able to play now, and won\'t get re-banned.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(492580, 72494, 1013, 102862, 1072936800, 'High ms', 'My ms is always spiking when I get in a group of people or start shooting. FPS is always at 60 and my ping is around 20-30. I don\'t have any choke or loss, but the ms keeps spiking. Sometimes it will jump to like 150. Anyone know what I can do to stop this? Thanks!\n\n\n\n~ Dr Pepper', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(492590, 72494, 1013, 102785, 1072936800, '', 'great ping, no bitches there. try typing in console fps_max 100 or more. it tops out at 100 anyways. do you have net graph running or something else to figure your connect specs?\n\nnet_graph 3 is the one i use. with no choke or loss, you are really doing good. there are many other things to enter for your tweaks. try this lil program to maybe get a lil more out of what you have.\n\nwww.hltoolz.com (http://www.hltoolz.com)\n\n__________________\n\nmy pc stuff:\n\namd 2500 barton\n\ngigabyte mobo 7n400l\n\n1024 mb ddr400 (pc3200) ram dual channel\n\nPlantronics dsp 500 headset with\n\nbuilt in soundcard and speech\n\nrecognition.\n\nati 9500 128 mb\n\nmaxtor 80 gb with xp\n\n2nd drive 30 gb maxtor\n\ndsl 768/256 - creative 7410 external modem\n\n\n\nTFC nutaholic...oh my gawd.. dont touch that! thats my flag! \n\n[dont flame all the noObs...you werent born playing half life!!!]\n\nplayin da TFC  since demos had 4 mirvs! I lub de demo spammo!\n\nMember of [TNT] THE NAMELESSTEAM\n\nCopper Div. Champs 3-15-04 YaY !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(492607, 72494, 1013, 102863, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same problem; my ping will jump up and cause a pause in the game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(492611, 72494, 1013, 102862, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah I use net_graph 3.  Thanks I\'ll try that download.\n\n\n\n~ Dr Pepper', '127.0.0.1', 1),
