(492604, 72499, 1013, 102863, 1072936800, 'Ping Spikes', 'My ping spikes from ~70 to 200 (sometimes up to 1000) on all servers; causing a pause in the game. I first noticed it when the "offline" patch came out. This problem has pushed me away from Counter-Strike and often frustrates me when I try to play the game because it has become unbarable. This problem only seems to occur when playing games on Steam. Some days I will be fine, the next I will lag. I can play for hours without this lag, leave, and come back at a later time and be lagging. I usually notice the spikes when a sound goes off, but thats not the only time I spike, its always happening. I dont know what to do anymore because I have tried everything. I recently saw a post about error logs and I went to check mine. I have error logs for everyday as it seems. The following are the two errors that I am getting in the logs: \n\n\n\nError:Failed to load dialog file Resource/UI/CareerBackgroundMenu.res\n\n\n\n\n\nFunction trace:\n\nCGameUI::Start\n\nCGameUI::Initialize\n\nCBaseUI::Start\n\nCBaseUI::Initialize\n\nHost_Init\n\nCFileSystem_Steam::Mount()\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd...\n\n\n\n\n\nError:Failed to load dialog file Resource/UI/ClassMenu.res\n\n\n\n\n\nFunction trace:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMy system is not all that great, but it has run Counter-Strike lag-free in the past.\n\n\n\nAMD Athlon 750 mhz\n\n512 Ram\n\nGeForce 4 - 64mb\n\n\n\nI have hardly any programs running in the background and turning them off seems to do nothing. I have searched for all any adware, spyware, and viruses. I have played with my rates and still nothing. So, any help would be great.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(494365, 72499, 1013, 102863, 1072936800, '', 'I see many other posts with the similiar problem, but no one can seem to come up with an answer?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(494434, 72499, 1013, 102864, 1072936800, '', 'I have the exact same problem with a good pc and cable connection, its very, very odd\n\n__________________\n\nIf you can\'t amaze people with your intelligence, confuse them with your stupidity', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(495355, 72499, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, '', 'i also have the same prob ... ping jumps to bull**** []\n\n\n\nBut no real answer anyway !\n\n\n\nGreetz Space', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(495855, 72499, 1013, 102866, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same problem since the last update.  HELP!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(496556, 72499, 1013, 102863, 1072936800, '', 'I may of found a solution, at least I think it works for me. What I have done, is turned off my "System Scan" on my virus scanner and it seems to do much better. System Scan scans almost every file at the second that it is used. It also expains the lag when sounds go off in Counter-Strike because it is scanning that file; and of course using system resources. \n\n\n\nI hope this helps to anyone else with this problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498769, 72499, 1013, 102863, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, I have tested it many times and the problem is my "System Scan" function on my Virus Scanner. So, if this is the same problem you have while playing Counter-Strike, you may want to check out your scanner.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(502129, 72499, 1013, 102864, 1072936800, '', 'nope it\'s not that\n\n__________________\n\nIf you can\'t amaze people with your intelligence, confuse them with your stupidity', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(502942, 72499, 1013, 102867, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, I have entirely disabled my McAfee programs (all of them- firewall, virus scanner, and privacy service) and the problem still persists. My ping doesn\'t spike or anything, but everybody (including me) stops moving. After a second or two, everybody warps to wherever they were moving to when I was frozen, including me. This happens once every half-minute or so, although it can happen more or less depending on how many people are in the server.\n\n\n\nThis hasn\'t happened before the April 2nd update.\n\n\n\nMy specs are...\n\n\n\nP4 2.66 GHz\n\n512mb RAM (Not sure on the type)\n\nGeForce FX 5900 128mb video card\n\n768kb DSL connection', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(503047, 72499, 1013, 102868, 1072936800, '', 'has anyone tried completely reinstalling and/or deleting all configuration files?\n\n\n\njust a suggestion, (i don\'t have the problem).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
