(505103, 72499, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Mr.Nike \n\nit wont help , deleting clientregistry.blob makes your steam thing that it isn\'t up-to-date so it will update again, but it doesnt fix anything neither does a re�nstall of steam nor a format of your pc\n\n\n\n(believe me i\'ve been that far, it just doesnt help the lag is still there ) \n\nI googled for the fix and that was the exact fix that came up in numerous other posts. It may not work but its worth a shot.\n\n__________________\n\n"He was a wise man who invented beer".\n\n-Plato\n\nw00ters cxxx|;;;:::::: 60 Second Rule\n\nPowered by w00ter Bot v 1.0', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(493634, 72662, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, 'When i see more than 4 people ..... then ping jumps to 500', 'Hi ... i have a big serious problem !\n\n\n\nWhen many peoples stay closly around me and the "traffic" is very high my ping jumps always from 80 to 300-1000 !\n\n\n\nIn great maps like Aztec or in the mid of Dust ...... the ping is always to 1000 !!!!!!\n\n\n\nBut the Fps are still k ...... like 60-70 ..... !\n\n\n\n\n\nMy connection is t-online DSL 768 !!!! So it should really be enough ! I have no other programs online when i play cs..... i have shut down everything ! Also my rate and settings are really k !\n\n\n\nI typed them all manual !  Its also the same if i get to to the internet with router or without router ! I have no firewall !!!\n\n\n\nMy PC is really good enough for cs *lol*\n\n\n\n2.4 P4\n\nAti Radeon 9700 128 mb ram\n\n1 gig ram \n\n80 gig drive (only 5 gigs free)\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat can it be that always my ping jumps to such a high value !!!!!!!! \n\n\n\nI hope you can help me ... very thanks to all my replys!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
