(493703, 72662, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, '', 'i tried 7500 9000 10000  always the same ....\n\n\n\ni tried serveral updaterate, cmdrate settings ......... \n\n\n\nThe reason is that my ping is k when i fight against 1-2 enemys !! But when there are more or when i play maps with large rooms etc, then my ping explode suddenly !!!\n\n\n\nGreetz Space', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(493740, 72662, 1013, 102878, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, I had the same problem as you. Any server more than like 3-4 people I lag!!!!!! WOW big time. So, I was asking around and I got this.\n\n\n\n\n\nrate 10000; cl_cmdrate 70; cl_updaterate 70\n\n\n\nand I set my CS to that and I get Faster dl\'s up to 7kbs a second and my ping is at its best never jumps!\n\n\n\nI suggest you try that, and tell us if it made a difference.\n\n__________________\n\ndont at teh baby!\n\n---------------------\n\nP4 AMD Athlon 2.2Ghz\n\n512 DDR \n\nG Force 2 MX 440', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(493771, 72662, 1013, 102879, 1072936800, '', 'Need similar fix for Natural Selection! Please?!\n\nIt started after the last update, suddenly\n\nall freezes but check your taskmanager\n\nyou will see the cpu usage sky rocket\n\nwhen running steam game. I use an\n\nold 750 AMD but never had any problems\n\nbefore the update. At the same time network\n\nusage stays at 0,25-0,5%.\n\nWhat I\'m saying is that it\'s not you, your\n\nnetwork or your comp... it\'s the code...\n\n\n\nIs valve aware people have this problem?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(494062, 72662, 1013, 102880, 1072936800, '', 'Well lets see what is your cl_cmdrate? cl_updaterate? If you can let us (everyone trying to help.) what all of the rates are. not just the rate area. maybe all of the cls? that would let us know where your problem lies.\n\n__________________\n\nWin XP Pro\n\nPent. M (Centrino) 1.4\n\nRaedon Mobility 9000 64 Mb Vid.\n\n512 DDR\n\n60 Gig Hard drive.\n\nDirect X 9.0b (4.09.0000.0902)\n\nUSB Logitech Premium 300 Headset\n\nWireless Microsoft Optical Intellimouse\n\nCable Modem Motorola Surf Board\n\nPing in Steam w/ anygame 40.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
