(497922, 73282, 1013, 102887, 1072936800, 'Horrible Ping!!!', 'I really need some help with this one guys.  Nobody on mIRC knows what the deal is and I\'m getting tired of hearing "contact your isp", so please don\'t tell me to do that.  My clan has a server, which I ping just fine it, but when we run the cal/server.cfg files, my lag in the SAME EXACT server with LESS people than when it\'s a pub just plain skyrockets.  My latency doesn\'t drop below 300, so basically, I can\'t scrim, period.  Could you go without scrimming?  Neither can I, so PLEEEASE help me guys!  I would be sooo grateful if somebody can look into this for me []\n\n__________________\n\nLoNDoNbo! pwns!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(497954, 73282, 1013, 101035, 1072936800, '', 'Turn on Firewall, I had lag two day\'s ago and was pissed, my firned told me to turn it on and it calm down.\n\n\n\nStart > Connection > (your connection > click on your properties, then go to the ADVANCED TAB and check on the first box, if you still lag I don\'t know man.\n\n\n\nIf you are running a router search for a firewall option somewhere.\n\n__________________\n\nSignature Here:', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498178, 73282, 1013, 102866, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve got the same problem except it\'ll be fine for awhile and then it\'ll jump to 1000 and then go back down.\n\n\n\nBump.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498183, 73282, 1013, 102864, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by The Holy Molar \n\nI\'ve got the same problem except it\'ll be fine for awhile and then it\'ll jump to 1000 and then go back down.\n\n\n\nBump.  \n\n\n\nalot of people have this problem, a lot of topics have started regarding this problem but it\'s stil not fixed, i have it 2 btw\n\n__________________\n\nIf you can\'t amaze people with your intelligence, confuse them with your stupidity', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498211, 73282, 1013, 102785, 1072936800, '', 'what did the server owner do in the cal configs that are diff from the others? i would look there and ask what settings are different. mostly it would be settings that effect clientside connect speed or bandwidth caps maybe?\n\n__________________\n\nmy pc stuff:\n\namd 2500 barton\n\ngigabyte mobo 7n400l\n\n1024 mb ddr400 (pc3200) ram dual channel\n\nPlantronics dsp 500 headset with\n\nbuilt in soundcard and speech\n\nrecognition.\n\nati 9500 128 mb\n\nmaxtor 80 gb with xp\n\n2nd drive 30 gb maxtor\n\ndsl 768/256 - creative 7410 external modem\n\n\n\nTFC nutaholic...oh my gawd.. dont touch that! thats my flag! \n\n[dont flame all the noObs...you werent born playing half life!!!]\n\nplayin da TFC  since demos had 4 mirvs! I lub de demo spammo!\n\nMember of [TNT] THE NAMELESSTEAM\n\nCopper Div. Champs 3-15-04 YaY !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(513430, 73282, 1013, 102887, 1072936800, '', 'thank you for the help guys!  but i just found out my prob like 2 hours ago, i got into a scrim, and my ping didn\'t jump over 60.  now... i\'m a CS n00b and i probably should have known that, but i was talking to somebody in #team3d on mIRC and they were talking about values, so i got into the conversation, and told them i only play online, what are the perfect values?  they told me this, and i suggest you guys do this too....\n\n\n\nin your console, type the following..(without <> )\n\n\n\n<rate> - if this is at 1, which mine was, that\'s EXACTLY why you\'re having probs.. change this by typing rate 25000 (most server will cap it at 9999, but some servers now allow 25000)\n\n\n\nin addition to this very important value, there are 2 others that have to do with how much information your internet allows CS to send info to and from the server which you\'re playing on (so i\'m told)..\n\n\n\n<cl_cmdrate 101>\n\n<cl_updaterate 101>\n\n\n\nwell,  i hope this works for you guys, and thank you for the help []  adios!\n\n__________________\n\nLoNDoNbo! pwns!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498792, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, 'Strange Lag Spikes (DoD)', 'Hello fellow Steamers,\n\n\n\nI think I may be experiencing a problem similar to this thread:\n\n\n\n/forums/show...ghlight=bizarre (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=64421&highlight=bizarre)\n\n\n\nWhen playing Day of Defeat, every minute or so my game freezes/stutters/stalls for a few seconds - you know that old lag symptom: when all the players around you seem to freeze in their tracks, and then 1 to 3 seconds later they\'re half-way across the hall, indicating that they\'ve actually been moving while you\'ve been stuck. \n\n\n\nHas anyone else been experiencing this lately?\n\n\n\nI recently switched my motherboard and cpu (upgraded) and performed a standard hard drive format, and reinstall of Windows XP. Everything runs beautifully, except this strange succession of freezes/lags in Day of Defeat. These symptoms occur on all servers, and usually aren\'t accompanied by an increase in Ping. My ping usually hovers between 30 and 60. \n\n\n\nMy specs are as follows:\n\n\n\nPentium 4 3.0c\n\n1gb DDR 3200 RAM\n\nNvidia Geforce FX 5600\n\nAsus PC4800-E Deluxe Mobo\n\n\n\n\n\nI guess the first thing i\'m trying to determine is whether this is a Steam issue or something wrong with my PC. \n\n\n\nIf there are any other threads I may have missed, I\'d appreciate a link to them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(498924, 73404, 1013, 102568, 1072936800, '', 'Mine does this on CS, have reinstalled video drivers, reinstalled steam. Doesn\'t help. Started this after the last update. Although mine does it about every 20-30 sec. Any fixes out there yet? Please let us know=)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499155, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m glad to hear that i\'m not the only one experiencing this difficulty. It\'s really detrimental to gameplay.\n\n\n\nA little more info: i\'ve been monitoring my own lag spikes, and they seem to occur more often than just every minute, especially during large amounts of in-game activity, i.e. explosions, bullets firing etc. I\'ve noticed that complaints about this lag-spike issue have been coming from all quarters of the Steam world: CS, DoD, NS et al. \n\n\n\nCould it be the recent update that caused this? Perhaps the implementation of offline mode?\n\n\n\nHere\'s another thread which is kinda similar... they seem to be experiencing the same \'lag spikes\' as we are.\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=72499 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=72499)\n\n\n\nThe gist of it is that Norton Anti-Virus may be hampering online play by running in the background. You may want to experiment with different settings. I\'m using Norton Anti-Virus 2004, that\'s about it, and don\'t see too many settings to tweak, but its worth a shot. \n\n\n\nI hope more people post here with suggestions or comments. \n\n\n\nThanks,\n\n\n\nKoala', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499162, 73404, 1013, 102888, 1072936800, '', 'At least you can play a game.  Steam reports that all of my games require an update and I cannot launch any game.  The last time I launched Cstrike, it told me that the game would be available for play in like 115 minutes.\n\n\n\nBy the way, I noticed that I have been getting Steam updates in dribs and drabs... every 20-30 seconds.  This may account for your laggy situation.  Take a look at your monitor and see if you have been getting these annoying updates in small pieces.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499178, 73404, 1013, 102888, 1072936800, '', 'Also of note, I\'m sitting on a 768k DSL and Steam is only updating every 20-30 seconds for about 3 or 4 seconds at a rate of 41kb. Anyone else seeing this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499179, 73404, 1013, 102888, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, every update is at 41.5kb.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499231, 73404, 1013, 102889, 1072936800, '', 'yea, i didnt get to play steam for about 4 mothes from teh prior update..............the people at steam arnt good at updating (on offense) but they keep to test more, and yes ive had that problem...................just gotta sit it out till they fix it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499505, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for those thoughts. I\'m sorry to hear that you can\'t even play Steam games right now. I\'m sure a lot of people are in the same boat right now, and I can definitely sympathize: I too have had to perform endless reboots of my pc, uninstalls of steam, reinstall\'s of steam, and have spent a great deal of time combing the forum for help.\n\n\n\nHang in there!\n\n\n\nI checked my monitor. I doesn\'t look like anything is updating at the moment. Good suggestion though, it may definitly help some others. Everyone having this problem should at least check to see if Steam if trying to download stuff while they\'re playing.\n\n\n\nOk, now: per my last post above, I tried to tweak my Norton Anti-Virus settings to see if that cleared up the lag-spikes I am experiencing. It didn\'t make any differance. The other two threads I linked above make referance to Norton settings that I don\'t have and "refreshing" activities that I don\'t think my Norton Anti-Virus \'04 performs. In either case, it didn\'t seem to help much.\n\n\n\nI don\'t think its an issue with my hardware, although I haven\'t ruled it completly out yet. My younger brother often plays DoD online with me. He is on the same network as I am, but using a much less powerful computer (AMD 750mz Duron. 512 mb SD-Ram. Elsa Gladiac Geforce 3; [too bad about that company by the way]) and isnt\' having any trouble at all with lag spikes. I\'m actually jealous.  :-) \n\n\n\nHe did tell me however, that there are times when from his point of view i\'ll appear to freeze in the middle of whatever i\'m doing during the game. This helped to confirm that i\'m definitely experiencing a lag-related issue when in-game.  \n\n\n\nThe next thing i\'m going to try is some LAN activity with Sturm-Bots to see if I experience any lag spikes on a local game.\n\n\n\nAny other thoughts or comments are appreciated!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499511, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, '', 'Here\'s another thread that appears to be talking about the same problem, a "stuttering" and "choking" resembling lag spikes.\n\n\n\n/forums/show...;threadid=56353 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=56353)\n\n\n\nHere\'s a quote from one of the last posts in that thread:\n\n\n\n"Lately (after the April 2nd update, supposedly only modifying Steam and not CS) I\'ve been stuttering like Zaren has been. I\'ll be in a game and all of a sudden everything will stop... a few seconds later, everybody pops up wherever they moved to while I was stuttering, and I usually wind up dead on the ground. It\'s a bit harder to keep up with my team if I have to stop moving every 5 seconds to wait for my game to start again."\n\n\n\nThere is some talk about Spyware eating up resources. I\'ll run a test with ad-aware on my pc and check it out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499799, 73404, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, '', 'I have also the same problem !!!\n\n\n\n\n\nhere my thread /forums/show...;threadid=72662 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=72662)\n\n\n\nIt must be something with the relation of my hardware and Steam .... or the code of steam perhaps !!\n\n\n\nI couldnt guess anything ..... but my problem is more that my ping gets into high value 500 + und so i am lagging around ! MY Fps are still good 50++\n\n\n\nI have also a very good PC ..... and i have ATI RADEON 9700 graphics card .... so it cannot be a problem with graphic company ... i guessed that !\n\n\n\nWe must wait to for Steam to fix this probelm ..... i payed for Fastpath and i hope this will help me !\n\nI also getting into lag when much activity is on my inet connection ...... much shots,bulletts or in great rooms like in Aztec !\n\n\n\nI also shut down my virus detection software ... always the same !\n\n\n\n\n\nDont know anything ... its reallly really strange !\n\n\n\n\n\ngreetz Space', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499818, 73404, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, '', 'Another question ! By net_graph 3 you can see In and Out kb by your connection !\n\n\n\nHow i can make this value higher so my client receive more kb/s !!\n\nI think this is perhaps the prob ..... always when i must get more than 100 k/s my ping gets higher and higher .... this would also include the prob why i lag in great rooms and in big fights only !!\n\n\n\nWith what things i can affect this value?=????\n\n\n\ngreetz Space', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(499951, 73404, 1013, 102890, 1072936800, '', 'hey guys, i\'ve been having this problem for months on end now..\n\n\n\n/forums/...ghlight=bizarre (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=64421&highlight=bizarre)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(500156, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for posting those threads guys. Of course, I wish none of us had these problems, but its nice to know that i\'m not the only Steam user with these issues.\n\n\n\nSpacejunkie - could you explain a bit more about net_graph?  I seem to remember something about this in the old days of Half-Life and Ping tweaking when most people still had 56k modems. You might be on to something. I\'ve noticed that I tend to get more "stuttering" during moments of intense activity - people running around, shooting rifles, throwing grenades etc.\n\n\n\nMeesh - thanks for chiming in. when it comes to your network config, you really seem to know your stuff!  I\'m glad to see that disabling Norton Anti-Virus auto-protect has helped solve the issue for some people. Do you have any idea what other posters mean when they refer to Norton\'s "90 sec refresh?". I\'ve been rummaging around my Norton 2004 Anti-Virus and haven\'t seen any option relating to a consistent refresh. \n\nAlso - you\'ve been experiencing this for months?? Yikes. So this didn\'t become noticeable with the last steam update? How have you dealt with this over time? Have you received any assistance from official Steam/Valve staff? I do appreciate these forums, I think they\'re an invaluable resource, but sometimes it feels like we are participating in a very large, unwieldy beta-test. :-)\n\n\n\nA little bit more from my own testing as well:\n\n\n\nBOTS\n\nThank god for Sturmbot. I played some LAN matches on my PC with bots and didn\'t experience any "lag spikes".  I went ahead and increased the load by adding some custom sounds, models, skins and sprites. Even with 16 bots running around causing havoc on Anzio I didn\'t get the same freezing or stalling. So local area network play isn\'t being affected.\n\n\n\nONLINE\n\nStrange. When I experience a lag spike, i\'ll usually hit TAB quickly to see if my ping rises in conjunction. Sometimes it does, sometimes it doesn\'t. At certain times it will jump a 100+ more than it should be, like from 30 to 400. Other times it\'ll merely jump between 40 and 50, seemingly normal ping variation whilst online. Occasionally too, other players will start "disappearing and reappearing" in and out of sight while running.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(500309, 73404, 1013, 102865, 1072936800, '', 'New Info : I have tried to play online at my freinds inet connection !!! I also have the same lag spikes ... but he doesnt have any problems !!\n\n\n\nSO IT CANNOT BE THE INET CONNECTION  ... i guessed so ! Its something with my computer ... but what`??? i have turned off all Anti Vir or firewalls ...... i think that i have no trojans or such things on PC !!!\n\n\n\nWhat causes this hard lag ???? .... anyone have some ideas ???\n\nI dont know .... really ........ any other inet games or any other games without steam run very well on my comp !\n\n\n\nThe campain of cz also works fine .... its must be something with the steam program or code or any inet program at behind ... or the relation to this programs !!!!!\n\n\n\nAny mod can answer some solution or make of course a command that they recognisted this problem ???!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nIts really bad to play cs so ..... of course you can play only a few maps .... at the others the lag is really too high to play !!!!\n\n\n\nI have spend 30 Euro and so i want a game that i can play ... not that **** !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(501722, 73404, 1013, 102869, 1072936800, '', 'Are you experiencing any dramatic and sudden increases in your ping rate when this happens?\n\n\n\nI have been observing my online sessions more closely, and more and more frequently there does appear to be a large increase in ping whenever I get temporarily frozen or stuttered.\n\n\n\nAlso, I\'ve noticed more and more threads talking about ping and lag issues lately. More people may be experiencing the same problems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(500930, 73708, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, 'For experienced 56k users in need of help', '56k Tweaks For All OS\'s \n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nI\'ve seen a number of people asking for some 56k tweaks lately and thought this might help out.\n\n\n\nFor 98 & ME:\n\n\n\n1. First and most important make sure you have the latest drivers for your modem, from the manufacturer.\n\n\n\n2. Open modem properties in Control Panel and under advanced port settings slide both all the way to the right.\n\n\n\n3. Set maximum port speed to 115,2000.\n\n\n\n4. Open Internet Options in IE and under temp internet files - settings select - Automatically.\n\n\n\n5. Under extra settings (where init strings go) put in s11=55 to make your modem dial faster or s10=60 if you have frequent disconnects.\n\n\n\n6. Make sure you have a good "clean" phone line, the #1 reason 56K modems don\'t connect at a good transfer rate is static on your phone line, and remember your throughput is more important than what your connection says it is connected at. If you are connected between 44,000 - 50,000 that is as good as it gets (you are limited to 53,333 by the FCC)\n\n\n\n7. Download TCPOptimizer and put in the following settings:\n\n\n\nUnder the "settings" tab select "dial up" and "custom settings", in "network adapter selection" choose "dial up adapter". Then use the following settings:\n\n\n\nMaxMTU - 1500\n\nTCP Receive Window - 8760\n\nMTU Discovery - Yes\n\nBlack Hole Detect - No\n\nSelective ACKs - Yes\n\nMax Dup ACKs - 2\n\nTime to Live (TTL) - 128\n\nTCP 1323 Options - uncheck both boxes\n\n\n\n"Other settings" tab:\n\nMax Connections per Server - 4\n\nMax Connections per 1.0 Server - 8\n\n\n\nThen select "Apply changes" and reboot to take effect.\n\n\n\n8. Open your registry (start - run - type regedit) and change the following registry entries:\n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\Class\\Net\\000X (where X is a number between 1 and 9)there is a value named SLOWNET, change it from 01 to 00.\n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\VxD\\COMBUFF it has a value called Start, change its value from 00 to 01.\n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\VxD\\VCACHE, it has a value named Start, change it from 00 to 01.\n\n\n\n9. Open your sys.ini file (start - run -sysedit - ME type system.ini) close the boxes until you are at the one with the title C:\\WINDOWS\\SYSTEM.INI, under [386enh] add the line ComXXIrqXXbuffer=4096, XX=Com port your modem is on and Irq assigned to your modem, it should look like Com03Irq07buffer=4096. Then select file - save and reboot to take effect.\n\n\n\n\n\nFor 2K & XP:\n\n\n\nFor 2K & XP users I suggest using Cablenut to tweak your settings due to the fact it installs the AFD parameters and allows you to tweak them. These values utilize memory for buffers that help speed up and stabilize your connection and latency. The following ae my suggestions for settings to use in Cablenut:\n\n\n\nDefaultReceiveWindow = 8192 \n\nDefaultSendWindow = 4096 \n\nDisableAddressSharing = 1 \n\nInitialLargeBufferCount = 10 \n\nInitialMediumBufferCount = 24 \n\nInitialSmallBufferCount = 32 \n\nLargeBufferSize = 4096 \n\nMaxFastTransmit = 6400 \n\nMediumBufferSize = 1504 \n\nPriorityBoost = 0 \n\nSmallBufferSize = 128 \n\nTransmitWorker = 32 \n\nFastSendDatagramThreshold = 1024 \n\nEnableFastRouteLookup = 1 \n\nEnablePMTUDiscovery = 1 \n\nIgnorePushBitOnReceives = 0 \n\nGlobalMaxTcpWindowSize = 8760 \n\nMaxFreeTcbs = 2000 \n\nMaxHashTableSize = 4096 \n\nMaxNormLookupMemory = 5000000 \n\nSackOpts = 1 \n\nSynAttackProtect = 1 \n\nTcp1323Opts = 0 \n\nTcpLogLevel = 1 \n\nMaxDupAcks = 2 \n\nTcpMaxHalfOpen = 100 \n\nTcpMaxHalfOpenRetried = 80 \n\nTcpRecvSegmentSize = 1460 \n\nTcpSendSegmentSize = 1460 \n\nTcpTimedWaitDelay = 30 \n\nTcpUseRFC1122UrgentPointer = 0 \n\nTcpWindowSize = 8760 \n\nMaxConnectionsPer1_0Server = 8 \n\nMaxConnectionsPerServer = 4 \n\nDefaultTTL = 128 \n\nDisableUserTOSSetting = 0 \n\nTcpMaxDataRetransmissions = 6 \n\nDefaultTOSValue = 92\n\n\n\nAlso add the following entry to your registry:\n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\AFD\\Parameters \n\n\n\nAdd the parameter BufferMultiplier and give it a value of 400 hexidecimal which will make it 1024.\n\n\n\n\n\n1. First and most important make sure you have the latest drivers for your modem, not Microsoft\'s, but the one\'s from the manufacturer.\n\n\n\n2. Open modem properties in Control Panel and under advanced port settings slide both all the way to the right.\n\n\n\n3. Set maximum port speed to 115,2000.\n\n\n\n4. Under extra settings (where init strings go) put in s11=55.\n\n\n\n5. Make sure you have a good "clean" phone line, the #1 reason 56K modems don\'t connect at a good transfer rate is static on your phone line, and remember your throughput is more important than what your connection says it is connected at. If you are connected between 44,000 - 50,000 that is as good as it gets (you are limited to 53,333 by the FCC)\n\n\n\n6. Download TCPOptimizer and put in the following settings:\n\n\n\nUnder the "settings" tab select "dial up" and "custom settings", in "network adapter selection" choose "dial up adapter". Then use the following settings:\n\n\n\nMaxMTU - 1500\n\nTCP Receive Window - 8760\n\nMTU Discovery - Yes\n\nBlack Hole Detect - No\n\nSelective ACKs - Yes\n\nMax Dup ACKs - 2\n\nTime to Live (TTL) - 128\n\nTCP 1323 Options - uncheck both boxes\n\n\n\n"Other settings" tab:\n\nMax Connections per Server - 4\n\nMax Connections per 1.0 Server - 8\n\n\n\nThen select "Apply changes" and reboot to take effect.\n\nLeave all other boxes blank, select save to registry and reboot.\n\n\n\n7. Open Internet Options (IE)and under temp internet files - settings select - Every visit to page.\n\n\n\n8. Open your Network Connections from the Control Panel � right click on your Cable connection and select properties, if you have the �QoS Packet Scheduler� installed highlight it and select uninstall. \n\n\n\n9. Open up regedit, navigate to HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE/Software/Microsoft/Windows/Current Version/Explorer/RemoteComputer/NameSpace, find the key named {D6277990-4C6A-11CF-8D87-00AA0060F5BF}. Right click on it and delete it. \n\n\n\nAlso add the following entry:\n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Contro\n\nl\\PriorityControl (if PriorityControl is not there, make the value) - on the right hand side right click and select new DWORD value, name it IrqXPriority (X = Irq assigned to your modem), then right click it and select modify and give it a decimal value of 1. \n\n\n\n\n\nFor ALL OS\'s:\n\n\n\nThe most important thing to remember about dial up is that the maximum you can download ANYTHING under absolute perfect conditions is 6.7kb/s, so don\'t be frustrated with your speed, remember it is only 56K (actually 53333). To understand a little better, most dial up connections have a connect speed of somewhere in the mid 40K range, which is very good, so say you connect at 48000, to find your maximum throughput divide that by 8 which gives you 6kb/s, which actually very good for dial up. The tweaks I have provided will help you maximize that throughput as best possible, don\'t expect super speeds by tweaking your dial up, be happy if you are getting 6kb/s. \n\n\n\nFOR FASTER WEB PAGE LOADING: \n\n\n\nThis tweak will help web pages load faster, it has no real effect on download speeds, just helps your pc look up websites faster thereby speeding up how fast the page loads and making websurfing more enjoyable. \n\n\n\nNavigate to this registry entry and change the following settings: \n\n\n\nFor XP & 2K \n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\Tcpip\\ServiceProv ider \n\n\n\nFor 98, 98SE & ME \n\n\n\n HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Servic\n\nes\\VxD\\MSTCP\\Service Provider \n\n\n\n\n\nOn the right for ALL OS\'s change these entries: (ALL values are HEXIDECIMAL) \n\n\n\nClass - 1\n\nDnsPriority - 1 \n\nHostsPriority - 1 \n\nLocalPriority - 1 \n\nNetbtPriority - 1 \n\n\n\nWrite down the current values PRIOR to changing them in case it doesn\'t work so you can revert back. To change the value right mouse click on the value and select modify and enter the values above once you have done all of them reboot to take effect and see how fast your pages load. \n\n\n\n\n\nP.S. If you have a dial up connection I HIGHLY recommend using a download manager, it will help maximize your download speed, resume downloads if you are disconnected and you can even schedule downloads for the middle of the night (it will automatically dial up and download the desired file and hang up when done) when you aren\'t using your pc.\n\n\n\ncredit: http://forums.speedguide.net/showthread.php?t=68127 (http://forums.speedguide.net/showthread.php?t=68127)\n\n\n\nyou can get the programs mentioned [cablenut, tcpoptimizer] @ www.speedguide.net (http://www.speedguide.net)\n\nor type the names into www.google.com (http://www.google.com) first link is correct one', '127.0.0.1', 1),
