(503354, 73756, 1013, 102852, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Ritchey007 \n\nsimple answer...\n\n/index.php?area=cheat_form (/index.php?area=cheat_form)  \n\n\n\nDear Sir:\n\n\n\nIt appears you did not understand either of the questions that introduced this thread or the thread\'s topic, based on your above quoted response.\n\n\n\nI did not ask, nor in fact has any poster in this thread to date asked, how to request a ban removal from Steam-Valve-VAC et al.\n\n\n\nThanks for your contribution to the discussion.\n\n\n\nBased on the public statements recently made about VAC "errors" and "ban removals" for 2500 users your response and the whole wording of the Steam "Been Caught Cheating?" web page is insulting. Clearly VAC is **not** perfect, yet you have already judged those "caught" by VAC guilty.\n\n\n\nIf you happen to have some constructive input with regard to the questions posed, please do contribute further.\n\n\n\nNext time I would like a completely irrelivant opinion I\'ll be sure to seek out a moderator.\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nZot', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(503363, 73756, 1013, 100136, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Zot IamCND! \n\nDear Sir:\n\n\n\nIt appears you did not understand either of the questions that introduced this thread or the thread\'s topic, based on your above quoted response.\n\n\n\nI did not ask, nor in fact has any poster in this thread to date asked, how to request a ban removal from Steam-Valve-VAC et al.\n\n\n\nThanks for your contribution to the discussion.\n\n\n\nBased on the public statements recently made about VAC "errors" and "ban removals" for 2500 users your response and the whole wording of the Steam "Been Caught Cheating?" web page is insulting. Clearly VAC is **not** perfect, yet you have already judged those "caught" by VAC guilty.\n\n\n\nIf you happen to have some constructive input with regard to the questions posed, please do contribute further.\n\n\n\nNext time I would like a completely irrelivant opinion I\'ll be sure to seek out a moderator.\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\n\n\nZot  \n\n\n\nwow\n\n__________________\n\n<!--\n\n\n\nLearn to incorporate what your thread is about INTO THE TITLE of the thread before posting!!!11\n\n\n\n-->', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(503368, 73756, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, '', 'Does anyone have  ANY official info as to why EXACTLY the VAC update caused 2500 ppl to get banned?\n\n\n\nWhat exactly did VAC PU on that was in just 2500 pplz game?\n\n\n\nWTH??\n\n\n\ni know it was a "false positive" but what triggered the positives?\n\n__________________\n\n"He was a wise man who invented beer".\n\n-Plato\n\nKiller Koala Killer\n\nw00ters cxxx|;;;:::::: 60 Second Rule\n\nPowered by w00ter Bot v 1.0', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(516697, 73756, 1013, 102899, 1072936800, 'Why not just un-ban everyone from this week?', 'I will not subject you all to the full bulk of my wrath, if you want to read my entire rant....\n\n/forums/...;threadid=75784 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=75784) \n\nthere you go. In terms of numbers, I went through the forums (before they started removing people for complaining that is) and counted all of the people that I felt were probably legitimately banned due to a bug, myself being one of them. I did not count the numerous "my lil Bro DL\'d h4x" complaints, but only people (from April 1st and on) that were banned and had no idea why. I counted a total of 218 different users..... wow. 218 that actually have accounts to post on these boards (I made one as a result.)  218 that were actually home, or had enough time to post... Im guessing that the actual number is into the thousands. Why would it be so hard to simply unban everyone banned since April 1st? Sure, a few hackers would get off, but they would either get caught again, or be scared enough by there temporary banning that they would quit cheating. I just dont see why we have to go through the wait (and the insult) of the "Im sorry for being a dirty cheater" form. I paid for this game. I want to play it. Im sorry if that is unreasonable. Straighten your crap out Valve, you arent making any friends with the customers.\n\nDavid Thompson', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(516782, 73756, 1013, 102900, 1072936800, '', 'Well, I\'ve never cheated and I\'ll tell you right now: If I ever get banned by VAC, Valve has just lost another faithful customer. I\'m not filling out their form. There are plenty of other good games on my hard drive. Deleting Steam will just make more room for them in addition to freeing up memory. I must say, however, that it has been nice to play on other people\'s servers and actually have a fair chance for once.\n\n__________________\n\nAMD Athlon XP 2400+ @ 2600+ (2.1GHz/280MHz)\n\nPNY Optima PC2700 1GB\n\nSOYO SY-KT333 DRAGON Ultra (Platinum Edition)\n\nATI Radeon 9800 XT @ 450MHz/780MHz\n\nCreative Sound Blaster Audigy 2 Platinum\n\nhp dvd writer dvd200i\n\nSeagate Barracuda ATA V 80GB\n\nRoad Runner Cable (2773kbps/373kbps)\n\nMicrosoft Windows XP Professional SP2 (v.2096)\n\n3DMark03 Score: 6313\n\nAquaMark3 Score: 34101', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(516815, 73756, 1013, 102901, 1072936800, '', 'I was banned by vac in the past month... this was becuase of cheating...now this means 2 things to me:\n\n1)It shows valve are improving vac and reducing cheats as the hack i was using was only a few months old.\n\n2)I have a reason to buy cs:cz\n\n\n\nSo now im happily playing cs again without cheats.\n\n\n\nIf only more people bought cz then we could all have sexy map textures(except the new aztec).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(516820, 73756, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'One of my friends was one of the false bans and he has no clue what he had that was picked up on. He sent in the form and he was unbanned and still to this day he has no clue why it happened to him. \n\n\n\nThere is always going to be people that come in here to complain about being banned because they werent hacking etc. but 99% of them are right bans.\n\n__________________\n\nTo all the people that are saying why wont VALVe work on this or that, they have only 60 people in their company. Cliffe told me so it must be true. \n\n\n\nPlus they are working on all this: CS, CS:CZ, DoD, Source (the engine itself), CS:S (and other Source ports?), HL2, CS2, TFC2 and DoD2 (?)!!!!\n\n\n\n{-DB-} Custom Maps Server: 69.93.116.250:27015 Great pings even for the Euro guys, 32 person and most of the time admins are present. Drop on in for a great time.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(518984, 73756, 1013, 102902, 1072936800, '', 'those initial 2500 bans may have been lifted, but there were many other wrongful bans after april 1st, as i noticed while going through the forums... in fact, nearly all of those people who said they were innocent reported being banned after april 1st.  I think valve really needs to look into this, because the sudden spike in "i was wrongfully banned threads" (ESPECIALLY AFTER april 1) really does say something.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(519343, 73756, 1013, 100136, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by DavidT316 \n\n\nExactly. If Valve does have a true list of all the known cheats and stuff, why dont they even make an un-installer and put it up for free on their page? Hey, it would even give them the excuse to make a new insulting form! You have to fill out the "I used to be a dirty cheater, but I have decided to give up my wicked life of cheating" to get the "cheat-cleaner" program....\n\n\nSo many suggestions, so many deaf ears.\n\n\n\n\n\nFor the record, I really didnt even mean to suggest that I might have once cheated, I just threw that out there as a combination of sarcasm and example.\n\n\n\n\n\nCome on Valve, you know you are sick of me, you must have seen some of these suggestions by now.\n\n\n\n\n\nDavid Thompson  \n\n\n\n\n\nLOL\n\n\n\n\n\nnot sure if hackers can take advantage of them actually having a "cheater uninstaller", unless it just comprises an update tool that verifies the files, and then redownloads and copies over those files. but you see i\'m so ignorant on cheats it\'s not even funny.\n\n\n\n\n\ndavid you\'ve filled out the form already, right?\n\n__________________\n\nWindows ME\n\n\nquad opteron 846\n\n\n16GB pc3200 ECC\n\n\n12x147GB ultra320 wide scsi in raid 50\n\n\nredundant 1500watt psu\'s', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(519349, 73756, 1013, 102899, 1072936800, '', 'Yup, filled it out on April 10th... still waiting. I have received a copy of my own complaint in the email, and nothing more. Does that mean that it was reviewed and ignored? Im not familiar with the system.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(519353, 73756, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by DavidT316 \n\n\nMost of us arent complaining that our little brother got us banned, in fact, I make fun of the people that submit that to the form (it is cloggin up the process, and making this take longer for me to get unbanned). There seems to be a great increase in the number of complaints, and I just wish that Valve would adress the possibility that they missed a few (hundred) in the unbannings. Or if nothing more, at least tell US what we were banned for.\n\n\n\n\n\nIf these posts bother you, you dont have to read them, but dont tell us to not complain because the bug didnt effect you. Thanks\n\n\nDavid Thompson  \n\n\n\n\n\nActually most of the people that make a post say something like my borther cheated, someone esle used my comp and I had CD running. All of these are horrible excuses. It clearly states in the EULA that YOU are responsible to who uses your computer and what goes on it. If you where caught cheating and were not cheating the appeal process works if you are civil with it. If you get a reply email then you werent cheating and you are unbanned, if you where cheating you dont get a reply and are banned for a year. \n\n\n\n\n\nYes I dont have to read the post but these people are stupid enough to make them. There is nothing that these boards can do for you if you are caught. Use the form and try to get the ban overturned. Simple as that. \n\n\n\n\n\nBTW When where you caught??\n\n__________________\n\nIf you dont like Steam stop b*tchin and uninstall and play on WON, its still there.\n\n\n\n\n\nTo all the people that are saying why wont VALVe work on this or that, they have only 47 people in their company.\n\n\n\n\n\nAnybody here ever hear of Dublin Dr. Pepper??? Man its the best!!\n\n\n\n\n\nThe N00b Awards for 2004 go to......(SOD) NIghthawk, CanadianSoldier and Killseeker!!! Who would of thought this???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
