(519428, 73756, 1013, 102904, 1072936800, '', 'quote:waldo = slow or you = liar :P \n\n\nnah you sound like valve person but why didn\'t waldo change it sooner?\n\n\n\n\n\nProbably because I didn\'t ask him to at the time.  Damn Waldo for not being psychic!\n\n\n\n\n\nAs far as some of the suggestions here, the idea of a cheat uninstaller is one we\'ve had for while.  However, it\'s technically difficult to safely uninstall hundreds of different cheats, many of which had bugs in their own installation and implementation.   \n\n\n\n\n\nThis being said, I\'ll definantly re-examine this.\n\n\n\n\n\n                        Nick\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\n\nNick Shaffner\n\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(519434, 73756, 1013, 100136, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Nick Shaffner \n\n\nProbably because I didn\'t ask him to at the time.  Damn Waldo for not being psychic!\n\n\n\n\n\nAs far as some of the suggestions here, the idea of a cheat uninstaller is one we\'ve had for while.  However, it\'s technically difficult to safely uninstall hundreds of different cheats, many of which had bugs in their own installation and implementation.   \n\n\n\n\n\nThis being said, I\'ll definantly re-examine this.\n\n\n\n\n\n                        Nick\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\n\nNick Shaffner\n\n\nValve  \n\n\n\n\n\nthanks! also can you tell me if you all are re-considering the bans for vac, i.e., a server cvar allowing a text menu popup to agree you are on a secure server and where to go to read steam\'s subscriber agreement, or...first time caught warning (or 1 month) and 2nd time a year, etc...\n\n\n\n\n\nmany have posted recently as to well,the fact they\'re sorry they cheated []\n\n\nsure i can believe that. i\'m sure they hate they fact vac caught them, and hopefully now they respect how great VAC has and is becoming now, and will NEVER cheat again. with this being said, a less lengthy of a ban might suit these cases well.\n\n\n\n\n\nalso a FAQ on how to do a clean install of steam again, including backing up gcf files as a reminder, might be good for those that cheat, buy another cd key, and get banned again for not remembering to remove the cheats, OR DIDN\'T KNOW HOW TO and didn\'t do it correctly.\n\n\n\n\n\nthanks!\n\n__________________\n\nWindows ME\n\n\nquad opteron 846\n\n\n16GB pc3200 ECC\n\n\n12x147GB ultra320 wide scsi in raid 50\n\n\nredundant 1500watt psu\'s', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(519443, 73756, 1013, 102904, 1072936800, '', 'quote:also a FAQ on how to do a clean install of steam again... \n\n\n\n\n\nGood suggestion.  We used to have something like this, but I think it got eaten at some point.\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:thanks! also can you tell me if you all are re-considering the bans for vac. \n\n\n\n\n\nWe aren\'t re-considering VAC\'s ban duration at this time.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAnyways, off to catch some sleep.\n\n\n\n\n\n                               Nick\n\n\n\n\n\n--\n\n\nNick Shaffner\n\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(518577, 76055, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '"Could not connect to Steam"', 'If you are having the problem of not being able to connect to the Steam network try this, it has helped a few people already:\n\n\n\n1) Locate and move platform.gcf to the desktop (if it works you can delete the copy on the desktop)\n\n2) restart Steam and let a new platform.gcf download\n\n3) Try to play.\n\n\n\nThanks to w00ters for this possible fix.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
