(521870, 76462, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, 'What to Do About SpyWare & Virus Problems!', 'For any of you with Spyware, Virus or Trojan infections\n\nhere are solutions and help!\n\n\n\nFirst, you can try and fix it yourself.\n\nHere is a collection of mostly free tools to de-infest your computer:\n\n\n\nFirst Line of Defense Tools:\n\nMicrosoft Update for all Operating Systems (http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/en/default.asp)\n\nSpybot Search & Destroy (http://www.security.kolla.de/)\n\nLavasoft Adaware (http://www.lavasoftusa.com/)\n\nBazooka Spyware Scanner (http://www.kephyr.com/spywarescanner/index.html)\n\nMcAfee AVERT Stinger (http://vil.nai.com/vil/stinger)\n\n\n\nNOTE: If you are having problems updating your O/S you may also have problems Installing/updating Steam! If you are unable to update your Windows, go here and troubleshoot your update problem (which might fix Steam as well): http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/troubleshoot/ (http://v4.windowsupdate.microsoft.com/troubleshoot/)\n\n\n\nAs an additional step to check your systems, \n\nMicrosoft has provided a "Baseline Security Analyzer"\n\nthat will check for many security-risk related problems.\n\n\n\nSpecial Diagnostic and Repair Tools used only with\n\nInstruction from qUiCkSiLvEr and Computer Cops\n\nHijackThis and CWShredder (http://www.spywareinfo.com/~merijn/downloads.html)\n\nHijackThis Tutorial for Inquiring Minds (http://home.covad.net/~k25125/SteamyThings/HijackThis_Tutorial.htm)\n\nWARNING: USE HIJACKTHIS ONLY IF YOU ARE INSTRUCTED TO DO SO\n\n\n\nInformation about Spyware and Virus and Trojans:\n\nComputer Safety Online (http://www.cjwd.demon.co.uk/compsafetyonline.html)\n\nSARC Symantec Security Response (http://www.sarc.com/)\n\nDoug Muth\'s Anti-Virus Resources (http://www.claws-and-paws.com/virus/)\n\nChristian Wagner\'s Excellent Spyware/AdWare/Malware FAQ and Removal Guide (http://www.io.com/~cwagner/spyware.html)\n\nDSL Reports Spyware and Adware F.A.Q. (http://www.dslreports.com/faq/spyware)\n\nWhat is Spyware (http://www.spychecker.com/spyware.html)\n\nGibson Research OptOut! Internet Connection Misuse & Abuse (http://grc.com/optout.htm)\n\nGibson Research Shields Up! (http://grc.com/default.htm)\n\nCounterExploitation! [cexx.org] (http://cexx.org)\n\nAdware, Badware & Spyware Profiles (http://www.accs-net.com/smallfish/advw.htm)\n\n\n\nReputable Online Virus and Trojan Scanners:\n\nPanda ActiveScan (http://www.pandasoftware.com/activescan/com/activescan_principal.htm)\n\nTrend Micro Housecall (http://housecall.trendmicro.com/housecall/start_corp.asp)\n\n\n\nFull Virus and Trojan Scanner packages\n\nsome are free all have trial downloads:\n\nNorton/Symantec (http://www.symantec.com/nav/nav_9xnt/)\n\nTrend PC-Cillin (http://www.trendmicro.com/en/products/desktop/pc-cillin/evaluate/overview.htm)\n\nPanda Anti-Virus (http://www.pandasoftware.com/com/nprod2002/platinum_home.asp)\n\nAVG Anti-Vrius from Grisoft (http://www.grisoft.com/)\n\nKapersky Labs Anti-Virus (http://www.kaspersky.com/trials.html)\n\nMcAfee Security ViruScan (http://download.mcafee.com/us/eval/evaluate2.asp?cid=9445)\n\nNorman Virus Control (http://www.norman.com/Download/Trial_versions/en-us)\n\nF-Secure Internet Security 2004 (http://www.f-secure.com/download-purchase/list.shtml)\n\nVexira Antivirus for Windows (http://www.centralcommand.com/downloads.html)\n\n\n\nand here is a list of more free spyware removal tools:\n\n\n\nSpyware/Adware removal tools:\n\nPestPatrol! (http://www.pestpatrol.com/)   <-- will detect and clean many resistant problems but $$\n\nWebroot Spysweeper (http://www.webroot.com/php/tryme.php?bjpc=64000&vcode=DT02)\n\nTrojan Remover (http://www.simplysup.com)\n\nKL-Detector (http://dewasoft.com/privacy/kldetector.htm)\n\nX-Cleaner Free (http://www.xblock.com/download-freeware.shtml)\n\nSpyware Blaster (http://www.javacoolsoftware.com/spywareblaster.html)   <-- doesn\'t scan or clean spyware but it blocks it\n\nSpyware Guard (http://www.wilderssecurity.net/spywareguard.html)   <-- scans, removes and blocks spyware\n\nSpySites Plus (http://camtech2000.net/Pages/SpySites_Program.html)\n\nTrojanHunter (http://www.misec.net/)\n\nBHODemon (http://www.spywareinfo.com/downloads/bhod/)\n\nGoodbye Spy (http://www.topshareware.com/GoodBye-Spy-download-2012.htm)\n\nOther spyware removal instructions (http://www.pchell.com/)\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you need help to disinfect and secure your computer, \n\nI\'ve made arrangements with one of the best delousing and\n\nSpyware Help Forums online today.\n\n\n\ngo here:CastleCops (http://www.computercops.biz/index.php)\n\n\n\nAnd be sure to tell them qUiCkSiLvEr sent you!\n\n\n\nPlease note that they have one forum now\n\nfor both spyware problems (http://www.computercops.biz/forum67.html) and virus/trojan (http://www.computercops.biz/forum67.html) problems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
