(522682, 76551, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, 'Mouse Input Delay Guide', '-=+Mouse Lag Guide+=- for all OS v 1.1 4/20/04\n\n\n\nTools for the Job:\n\n\n\n+ Winrar (http://www.rarlab.com/download.htm)\n\n+ Logitech Mouseware (http://www.majorgeeks.com/download2785.html) / Microsoft Intellipoint (http://www.microsoft.com/hardware/mouseandkeyboard/Download.mspx)\n\n+ DirectX 9.0c (http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/details.aspx?FamilyID=a6dee0db-dcce-43ea-87bb-7c7e1fd1eaa2&displaylang=en)\n\n\n\nThe Guide:\n\n\n\n\n\nInstall Winrar [use any decompressor capable of decompressing .exe files].\n\nInstall DirectX 9.0c (http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/details.aspx?FamilyId=0A9B6820-BFBB-4799-9908-D418CDEAC197&displaylang=en) [if not done already] as the latest DX contains input improvements. Reboot as necessary.\n\nLocate the mouseware/intellipoint software package. Right-click -> select extract files... extract driver portion to a folder [eg tmp].\n\nUninstall mouseware/intellipoint software/mouse drivers currently installed. Reboot as necessary.\n\nOpen up device manager [by default: Right-click My Computer -> Properties -> Device Manager or control panel -> mouse], locate Mouse from list [if uninstalled old driver, unplug/replug mouse and let the device wizard guide you through process for next step].\n\nChoose update driver option. Search for files, point to tmp [location driver portion exacted to].\n\nLet it update your driver. Reboot as necessary.\n\nOpen up Steam -> Right-click Steam in Taskbar -> Open up Games -> Right-click desired game -> Choose \'Properties\' -> Choose \'Launch Options\' -> Add: -noforcemaccel string to box, ok.\n\nLaunch favorite MOD and play. All mouse issues should be fixed.\n\n\n\nOther Suggestions:\n\n\n\n+ Use a generic 2 button PS/2 mouse to isolate mouse as problem.\n\n+ Lower directsound acceleration level or turn it off completeley [start menu -> run -> dxdiag -> Sound Tab -> Turn the slider down incrimentaly until it works.\n\n+ Add -noforcemparms string to launch options box.\n\n+ Uninstall current mouse drivers, let windows detect and install \'default\' mouse drivers [the ones that come pre-installed into xp/2k].\n\n+ [In game] Bring down the console [~] and type in m_filter. Should report "0", if not change to m_filter "0" or vice-versa.\n\n+ If optical mouse, use non reflective surface, avoid real wood surfaces.\n\n+ Experiment w/ video modes OGL/D3D.\n\n+ Turn off num lock key.\n\n+ Click on "Start" and select "Control Panel" \n\nClick on Accessibility Options \n\nOn the Keyboard tab, ensure that "Use StickyKeys", "Use FilterKeys" and "Use ToggleKeys" are disabled \n\nAlso, you need to click on the "settings" button for all three options: StickyKeys, FilterKeys and ToggleKeys and ensure that the "Use shortcut" is unchecked on the dialog that opens.\n\n+ If OS is WinXP and powertoys is installed, uninstall it.\n\n+ Add vgui_emulatemouse "1" to config or type in console.\n\n+ Click Start, Control Panel. \n\nIf necessary, click Switch to Category View. \n\nClick Performance and Maintenance. \n\nUnder Control Panel Icon, click the System icon. \n\nThe System Properties window displays.\n\nClick the Hardware tab. \n\nClick Device Manager. The Device Manager window displays. \n\nSelect Universal Serial Bus controllers. \n\nRight-click USB Root Hub. \n\nClick Properties. The USB Root Hub Properties window displays. \n\nClick the Power Management tab. \n\nClear the check box next to Allow the computer to turn off this device to save power box. (This will prevent a power loss to the USB port.) \n\nClick OK to close the USB Root Hub Properties window.\n\n\n\nif you have any questions about a specific suggestion, feel free to ask: carlandomagic[AIM] (http://www.aim.com/get_aim/express/aim_expr.adp?aolp=)\n\n\n\nMore fixes are on the way so sit tight if nothing here works []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
