(530508, 77478, 1013, 102937, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SesameSticks \n\nPerhaps the fact that he paid for them?  The servers?  You mean Mr.T here paid for all secure servers out there?  Because that is what he is talking about.  He isnt banning somebody from his own servers, he is tricking people into banning themselves from all VAC secure servers - and he certainly didnt pay for them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(530528, 77478, 1013, 102941, 1072936800, 'Free Cheats', 'quote:Originally posted by KHALIK \n\nI am running 3 CS servers \n\n\n\nI am also running 1 VAC Secure server.\n\n\n\nTotal= 4 CS SERVERS\n\n\n\nI have 3 servers falsely dedicated as a cheat server [NON-SECURE], all redirecting to a VAC secure server!\n\n\n\nThe reasults:\n\n\n\nWhen re-directed to the VAC secure server, I keep seeing players getting banned, in console via HLSW for violations.\n\n\n\nHehe...That will teach em not to cheat!\n\n\n\nI planned to expend more servers!  \n\n\n\nur ***. if you hate cheaters play VAC ur ALMOST as bad as the cheaters themselves\n\n\n\nbtw i dont cheat but more peeps will make vac cheats so they can just keep playong on insecure ones with hidden vac so ur making hackers that have settles in one stop migrate.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(532416, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, 'Allowing Steam: Response from Dunkle requested', 'At the last E3 Mike Dunkle told me that cafe\'s that did not buy into the program could still have the Steam client downloaded as well as all the modules so that individual could use their own Steam accounts at the cafes.  Now it is my understanding that Valve has changed their stance on this matter.\n\n\n\nValve has now been quoted as saying, "you would be required to erase the copy of the Valve products after that user logged off the system".\n\n\n\nThis makes little sense to me as those products are un-useable without the password, and forcing someone to re-download all of the software each time is a bit rediculous.  It would be like saying that a CyberCafe couldn\'t keep Everquest installed even though the gamer would need to have purchased the game and be paying Sony every month to play it.  Without the account info, the game is useless.\n\n\n\nIt was my understanding that a person\'s Steam account was portable but could only be played from one PC at a time.  Why does it matter if the person plays their own game at home or in a cybercafe?  You would punish the user because perhaps their home computer or connection is not so hot or because they want to play face to face with their buddies?\n\n\n\nOr is it that not enough of these cafe licenses are being sold in the states and you are now deciding to change the rules?\n\n\n\nI hate to end in such a strong worded manner, but it has to be said. \n\n\n\nMike, we need an answer on this.   Are people allowed to use their accounts wherever they want?  Do you expect them to download the client each time they go to a cafe?  Are you trying to punish the cafe or the gamer who owns the account?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(533200, 77674, 1013, 102082, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s a waste of money and bandwidth, better off trying the new games that don\'t have Steam.\n\n__________________\n\nDon\'t vote for Bush/Cheney 2004!\n\nLeet speak and shortened English (U, UR, Y, etc) is stupid, don\'t use it\n\nWhy Pro gaming is stupid - http://www.gamespy.com/articles/489/489731p1.html?fromint=1', '127.0.0.1', 1),
