(545783, 77674, 1013, 102946, 1072936800, '', 'Mike Dunkle posted something on the 23rd (in this same forum section), so he has been cruising the forums.  He is obviously just ignoring this thread for now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(561578, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'Two and a half days since my last post and still waiting.  Ten days since the original post and still waiting.\n\n\n\nMike, it is important to have an answer here because it looks like via e-mail people are getting a completely difference answer than you have given face to face or over conference calls.  Please clarify your stance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(562171, 77674, 1013, 101052, 1072936800, '', '2 emails sent to Mike dunkle 1 week ago on clarification on licences also no response...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(564812, 77674, 1013, 102947, 1072936800, '', 'I have sent many emails and started a post about this but haven\'t heard jack. Im sure there are cafe groups out there that help each other, but wich ones would be the best. Im sure the only way to fight back is to get together on this and many other issues.\n\n\n\nIm in San Jose and Im going to be starting a Cafe. If you already have one or are very very very intrested in starting your own please respond to this post... \n\n/forums/...;threadid=71926 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=71926)\n\n\n\nSorry to piss of the starter of this thread, just tired of waiting to hear from valve. They are slowing me down.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(576171, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', '13 days and still waiting for a response from Mike Dunkle.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(576393, 77674, 1013, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'two weeks here and still awaiting response, I will try and phone him again tonight and see if i get any further, but it  seems no one is answering any phones at steam, i keep getting the same voice mail box when i press for recpeption.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(580041, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'I will give a few days for E3.  Mike is probably there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(598036, 77674, 1013, 102948, 1072936800, '', 'umm I don\'t think you are going to get an answer. \n\n\n\nYou probably couldn\'t shame me into giving one so I doubt you will be able to do it to him. \n\n\n\nGive it up bud.  Clearly Valve changed their minds.  It happens.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(598844, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'There is a lot going on behind the scenes here Raul.  On a recent conference call with iGames, Valve (Mike Dunkle) said that having Steam available for people who have their own accounts was OK.  He then turned around and e-mailed an iGames member center saying the exact opposite.  What we need now is a public clarification.  This forum is where centers, iGames members or not, go for answers.  So it is here that Mr. Dunkle should clarify.  Especially since many are reporting that Valve is not responding to licensing requests.\n\n\n\nWe all know he reads these boards, and this is not an unusual request.  We simply cannot have different rules depending on who Mike is talking to.  Perhaps there was a mis-communication.  Perhaps within that month Valve changed their mind and didn\'t tell anybody.  We won\'t know until Mike chimes in.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(599371, 77674, 1013, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t believe there is any miscommunication, its just the case that "Steam" choose not to answer because its not in their best interests to.\n\n\n\nTo Whit, the older copies of HL Generations for Cyber cafes are "LEGAL" and are ok to be used with Steam.\n\n\n\nHowever, once you buy a copy from Vivendi universal publishing, the licence key has now been deleted by Steam, although according to the paperwork, we are entitled to use it.\n\n\n\nI have been speaking to so many people now, its beyond a joke, both my Solicitors and the legal Dept. of vivendi Universal publishing both say my licences are Valid, even Mr Dunkle admitted they were, (if they were not, I can assure you he would have sued me faster than you can say Steam).\n\n\n\nHowever, only Steam can issue new licences, hence the reason they are so quiet, So quiet in fact that after some 20 plus emails from me in 6 weeks, over a years worth of chasing by my local Cyber supplier and ten months of chasing by Vivendi universal Publishing, NO ONE HAS HAD A REPLY.\n\n\n\nThe question..? are the licences Valid..? If so what is the new Key? If not, what am I being charged yearly for?\n\n\n\nThis question has gone unanswered for so long its ridiculous, I am personally waiting for a reply to this question, and I have a feeling hell will freeze over before it is answered, the only thing I have no doubt on is that I SHALL be receiving yet another email from M dunkle stating using CS in a shop is illegal unless licences are for cibers, again I will provide all he asks for, and again once he has his proof, he will ignore me and hope I go away, like you.\n\n\n\nWell , I am waiting for a reply, I keep emailing weekly, and phoning 3 to 5 times a week, and always no reply, ALWAYS.\n\n\n\nBut, soon the yearly charge for my CS licences will arrive, which is kinda funny, I have 37 legal licences, and only 12 work.. yet I am charged for 37, yet Steam refuse to acknowledge I have a claim, yet I am paying for the game, and accoriding to the paperwork supplied by Vivendi I am entitiled to use this software in a Cyber Shop. but the licence was issued by Sierra, but Steam refuse to honour that contract, choosing to ignore it.\n\n\n\nWell, let me put it this way, the clock is ticking, when the next bill arrives for my 37 copies, if I still have no reply, then my reply will be, to permanently remove Steam from my shop.\n\n\n\nI have just completely lost all faith in Steam, in Mike Dunkle and in their Customer Support, all I get is "Nothing", all I ever get as a reply is "Nothing" and all Steam seem to think of their clients both and and new is "Nothing".\n\n\n\nSteam.. so well named, a company so bloated in its own self worth, it is just full of hot air, vaporware to be blunt.\n\n\n\nMr. Dunkle, if you are reading this.. please answer the question.. Are the Sierra issued licences for Cybers valid..? If not why are we being charged yearly for them..? and if they are valid.. why have you disabled the Vivendi Universal Publishing CD keys for Cybers and not re-issued new ones?\n\n\n\nSteam as a company have renaged on the licences as granted by Sierra, and simply hoping we will go away will have far more repercussions than you can imagine, for we will go, and not return.\n\n\n\nAs Always, waiting for a reply.\n\n\n\nSigned on behalf of 1000\'s of Cibers Everywhere.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(603614, 77674, 1013, 102949, 1072936800, '', 'guys...\n\nwe are talking business here! they are on business... but what any company around the world knows is to make their earning being fair.\n\nAs I am in Brazil, my monthly fee is cheaper, but, dont thing it will be expensive, it will! my price per hour, in us$ is 1 dollar per hour... \n\nif the charge, in your case, was cheaper no one, as far as I see, would conplain. Everyone here knows about being legal and apreciate others work, but come on... 10 per month is almost a robery!\n\nas I said in other topic, I tried to move away from cs as soon as I notice that I was going to have another thing to pay monthly. did not work... people move away from my lan house (as cyber cafés as known here) they went to other cafés just to play CS... \n\n\n\nimagine 1 US per station per month!\n\nmine has 30 pcs... how many 30 pcs cybers around the world?\n\n1000?\n\n1000*30= 30000 per month\n\n\n\n10000?\n\n300000 per month\n\n\n\n100k?\n\n3.000.000 per month!\n\nonly on the cyber café program!\n\n\n\nin any case, they can pay a few servers to validade accounts... site, support, and so on!\n\n\n\ni am not being greedy, i dont mind paying somtheing that I feel that is fair! i have pleasure to pay to someones work that makes mine easier!\n\n\n\nenough complaining guys!\n\ncompany policies!\n\nsooner or later another game will come!\n\never saw battlefield II?\n\ncool game!\n\ntry some DC (Desert combat)!\n\nlol!\n\n__________________\n\nSorry.. CS is business... BF is fun!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(603756, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'This thread technically is not a debate as to wether or not the Steam program is a good deal.  This thread is to allow Mike Dunkle to say wether or not Steam can be installed at centers that are not on the program so that people who have their own Steam accounts can use them there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(606425, 77674, 1013, 102946, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by RevH \n\nThis thread is to allow Mike Dunkle to say wether or not Steam can be installed at centers that are not on the program so that people who have their own Steam accounts can use them there.  \n\n\n\nI just don\'t see Valve telling centers they can go ahead and install the software without paying for the priveledge.\n\n\n\nIn March 2004, they claimed (on their cybercafe page) that they had 800-1000 centers (/forums/...;threadid=71458 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=71458)) signed up and paying $10 per month per machine with a minimum of 10 machines.  They are making a minimum of $100 a month from 800 centers.  That adds up to a million dollars a year in revenue from those game centers alone.\n\n\n\nNow, imagine if they told centers they could install the game for free for customers who already have accounts.  What idiot game center owner would continue to pay the $100 a month.  All the owner would have to do is tell their customers that they can play Counter Strike at their centers, but they have to buy their own personal accounts now before they can play.  Unfortunately, I (along with most people) wouldn\'t run out and purchase an account just so we could play CS at the center we frequent.  We would just play the games that do not require that we have our own accounts.\n\n\n\nOn the other hand, if customers can play CS at the 800-1000 centers that are paying the cybercafe fees, think of how many of those customers do not have their own accounts, but decide to run out and buy a copy so they can play at home.  I know I have run out and bought several games for home after I have played it at the center I go to.  If only 4 or 5 customers a month at each of the 800-1000 centers buys a copy for home, that\'s about 50,000 game copies sold because of the influence of game centers.  Valve needs to figure out how to get 10,000 or 100,000 game centers to go with their cybercafe program.\n\n\n\nHey Valve, imagine if you had 100,000 centers paying $100 a month.  Over $100 Million!  What if you made it $20 per month per machine...that would be $200 Million.  Yeah, that\'s the way to go....just be patient.  With 800-1000 centers today and more joining everyday, it won\'t take that long to get to that 100,000 game center mark.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(608310, 77674, 1013, 102950, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Crucifingers \n\n\n\nIn March 2004, they claimed (on their cybercafe page) that they had 800-1000 centers (/forums/...;threadid=71458 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=71458)) signed up and paying $10 per month per machine with a minimum of 10 machines.  They are making a minimum of $100 a month from 800 centers.  That adds up to a million dollars a year in revenue from those game centers alone.\n\n \n\n\n\nJust to clarify...\n\n\n\n10 machines @ $10 a machine @ 800 centers is $960,000.00\n\n\n\nBut thats close to a Million. \n\n\n\nThe fact of the matter is they are bringing in somewhere between:\n\n $960,000.00 to $1,200,000.00 a year off of thier current cyber client base and thats only if each location has 10 mcahines. I\'ve only been to two and they both had 50 plus machines.\n\n\n\n800 locations with 50 machines = $4,800,000.00\n\nThats over 4 million a year.\n\n\n\nCha-Ching!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(609420, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'I am not attempting to debate how much money Valve can rake in by forcing centers to give them money or how sucky the game is or how Valve could make more money from people who run home and buy the game after playing at a center.  While all those topics are valid, they have been discussed in other threads.  This thread is really for one purpose, for Mike Dunkle to publicly say once and for all what Valve\'s stance is on making Steam available in a center to people who already have accounts.\n\n\n\nMike has stated in person and on the phone that the Steam client can be installed so that people can use their own accounts.  Recently he e-mailed a center the exact opposite response.  I just want to know from Mike what Valve\'s current stance is.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(612404, 77674, 1013, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'Dont mean to hijack your thread, but I think one Issue that is just blazing a light here, is that Mike Dunkle / Steam, just are NOT responding.\n\n\n\nThat is pretty much the case in point, see the thread date, any one of us got a response yet? I know I haven\'t.\n\n\n\nI think the thread topic confused matters with the "response from Dunkle" requested, we are all beyond exasperation at waiting for a response.\n\n\n\nWhat gets me though is how the heck can Steam go to E3 and wax lyrical about their super this and superb that.. when they cant even manage to reply to a thread on their own forums, which is without doubt both clear as water, not full of profanities and asking some very straightforward and understandable questions.\n\n\n\nNext time I am asked for my views on Steam, I\'ll point the reporters to this website, and in particular to this thread, and use this as a perfect example of Steam customer care.\n\n\n\nNow I mention this, I am kicking myself as I had a newspaper guy here the other day, hmm, ill see if I can find his card, see if he is interested in the dark side of support.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(624124, 77674, 1013, 102950, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by RevH \n\nI am not attempting to debate how much money Valve can rake in by forcing centers to give them money or how sucky the game is or how Valve could make more money from people who run home and buy the game after playing at a center.  While all those topics are valid, they have been discussed in other threads.  This thread is really for one purpose, for Mike Dunkle to publicly say once and for all what Valve\'s stance is on making Steam available in a center to people who already have accounts.\n\n\n\nMike has stated in person and on the phone that the Steam client can be installed so that people can use their own accounts.  Recently he e-mailed a center the exact opposite response.  I just want to know from Mike what Valve\'s current stance is.  \n\n\n\nUnderstood... my point being with that kind of income they could invest in some quality support/customer service...\n\n\n\nStill no reply from MD?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(627078, 77674, 1013, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'NO. []\n\n\n\nlike I said, hell wil freeze over first.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(628903, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'MIKE!\n\n\n\n(I imagined myself yelling it like Kirk did for Khan in Wrath of Khan...man, am I a nerd)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(633301, 77674, 1013, 102950, 1072936800, '', 'Khaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaan!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\'er, I mean Mike.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nold nerd here', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(633320, 77674, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'Give it up guys, he won\'t answer. If he wanted to then an answer would\'ve been posted by now . . .\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(633442, 77674, 1013, 102950, 1072936800, '', 'I gave up long ago on getting a quality reply on any level from valve on any subject... I quit kidding myself 3 months into steam. Not to mention the pre-steam years.\n\n\n\n\n\nWhy do I keep posting.\n\n\n\nTo further the proof that valve has no excuse.. They are getting a bad rap by their own hand.. not because people just want to Bi*ch, or have it in for them.\n\n\n\nThere are a multitude of post requesting official assistance on any number of levels, they request this help in a polite manor. \n\n\n\nThey are blatantly ignored... and there is NO EXCUSE!\n\n\n\nVALVE/STEAM you are alienating your customer/market share.\n\n\n\nThe leather interior and silk underwear doesn\'t grow on trees..\n\n\n\nCan you say disruption of revenue flow!\n\nMD or someone official... answer the question. You folks(sales/support) are loosing respect here.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(659418, 77674, 1013, 102944, 1072936800, '', 'Well Mr. Dunkle, you are back posting on the forums and still no response, yet sadly I don\'t seem to be going away.  I don\'t see why this one is so difficult to answer.  You\'ve answered this question many times in the past.\n\n\n\nI am guessing now that the e-mail the CyberCafe received was pure intimidation.  A desperate move from a company that made a lot of promises about this program and kept very little, and now is growing concerned why more cafe\'s aren\'t immediately jumping on the band wagon.  My guess is that you know that it is OK to allow people to use their own accounts in a center, and you know you don\'t have much legal ground to stand on concerning this issue.\n\n\n\nWith no response from Mr. Dunkle, this is all I have to assume.  I will not ask for an answer here again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(662282, 77674, 1013, 100030, 1072936800, 'Reply', 'In general, users can use their Steam accounts for personal use (non-commercial) at multiple locations (e.g. logging in at a cybercafé they may occasionally use or using it on their work computer and home computer).  In short, the portability of a user\'s Steam account does not mean that commercial establishments like cybercafés can exploit our games without a license whether it be a tournament or pay for play.  If indeed a user installs Steam on a cybercafé computer to access their account, you could allow an activity like this, but you would be required to erase the copy of the Valve products after that user logged off the system (through a program like DeepFreeze or the like) just like any other software that is installed by a customer that you do not have a license for.\n\n\n\nMike\n\n__________________\n\nBusiness Development and Cafe Operations', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(533806, 77874, 1026, 102904, 1072936800, '4/20/04 VAC Updated', 'VAC Updated Yesterday, more of the same:\n\n\n\n* New detections.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(533858, 77874, 1026, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'Weee\n\n\n\nYes, I have found that the level of competition has dropped remarkably in recent weeks, and I am ruling the pub servers again now that its appears I am only competing against honest players. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
