(542573, 78614, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by FrozenHalo \n\nSome Taylor dude told me to reinstall. its the only way to fix that.  \n\nYou mean Taylor Sherman who works at VALVe?  Show some respect!\n\n__________________\n\n"I\'m pretty sure at least here a lot more people could be helped if we dnd\'t have to deal with cheat posters, "OMG VALVE SUCKS" posters, not to mention the people that PM us with clearly keygen\'ed keys that "don\'t work". Not everyone\'s doing that, but so many do it makes it pretty hard to help the people who have legit issues and legit problems." \n\n- Waldo', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(542609, 78614, 1013, 100042, 1072936800, '', '*hails Mr. Taylor*\n\n__________________\n\nNo one sees the Hampster w/Radioactive Bananas... unless he\'s the bait.  o.O', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(544310, 78948, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, 'Backward facing players', 'Whos seen this bug in CS/CZ where you are looking at a player and it appears they are looking away from you when they are in fact facing you?  It sems to have appeared more frequently over the past 4-6 weeks.\n\n\n\nQuestions:\n\n---------------\n\n1) how often have you seen it?\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\nAny other info you can provide?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(544329, 78948, 1013, 102974, 1072936800, '', 'Ive seen it a couple of times in the past week.\n\n1) on the overpass in avalanche  i was coming out of axis house to go across to church, though i had a nife kill...but no\n\n2) under the bridge on kalt.  \n\nI dont know if i can re-create it, i try not to, but ill see.\n\n\n\nNo i was not running custom skins,\n\nand it was DoD, for those who dont know the maps.\n\nboth kills were with the Thompson, i dont know if that matters.\n\nIf i think of anything else, ill give it a try.  Ill also go opn a 24-7 Ava/Kalt server and run of demo.  Nothin better to do with the hd space []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(544353, 78948, 1013, 100435, 1072936800, '', 'ocarD, from what I have been able to determine this problem is prevalent in all official mods at the moment, at varying degrees in each. However, I have yet to observe the phenomena on any unofficial Steam mod.\n\n\n\nIt is quite common in Counter-Strike/Condition Zero, and not nearly as much in the others, but a problem nonetheless. While I\'m not sure of the exact timeframe it appeared over, it may have been introduced with the 2.09 update [Someone else please confirm this].\n\n\n\nI\'m still attempting to determine the situation that seems to be the cause, will report back later.\n\n\n\nBTW, it does not have anything to do with the use of custom models, as this has been observed by me on full default games of CS and DoD.\n\n\n\n\n\n---Working on getting a good demo, will email.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(544374, 78948, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for the replies so far, please keep them coming.  If anyone can get me a demo that would be helpful as well.  2/9/04 seems about right for the bug.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(544569, 78948, 1013, 102072, 1072936800, '', 'i play deathmatch on cs alot.  since its nonstop play and people are constantly spawning in, i get this bug and sux cuz i think theyre lookin one way, i pull out knife and i get shot [] by them.\n\nsince we\'re on the topic of bugs, i also noticed that the appenddemo command doesnt add to the file specified.  unless its supposed to be different from 1.5\n\ni type the following and it works in 1.5\n\nrecord blah\n\nstop\n\nappenddemo blah 3\n\nstop\n\nplaydemo blah\n\n\n\nand it only plays the first part. it be different for 1.6?\n\n\n\nalso... []\n\nanyone notice how now you can literally fly when youre in the air and get shot up?  i was in a server where i started off with 255 life and jumped towards a CT who was spraying me with his colt, his bullets kept pushing me back quite a distance and i was in the air.  i know it had nothin to do with the server cuz its happened to me on normal match servers that have no mods.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545083, 78948, 1013, 100417, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by |CC|Animal \n\n100MB HDD \n\n\n\nLOL', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545138, 78948, 1013, 102975, 1072936800, 'Backward facing players', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\nNo that often, maybe four or five times over the last six weeks or so. Each time it was confined to a particular session, if I shut down CS and played later in the day the problem was not evident.\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\nAbout 6 weeks ago I think.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\nNot purposefully - it seems random.\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\nNo, only running the official skins.\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nCS 1.6', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545217, 78948, 1013, 102976, 1072936800, '', '1) How often have you seen it?\n\nVery frequently in the last 2 weeks. It happens in almost every server I play on at least once.\n\n\n\n2) When did you first see it?\n\nAbout six weeks ago, but it only became a serious problem about 2 weeks ago.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\nNot intentionally, but it happens very frequently for me in servers.\n\n\n\n4) Were you running custom skins?\n\nYes - Wolf Recon (updated for 1.6) (http://www.csnation.net/skins/view_skin.php?id=3620) for CT\'s and Killage People (http://www.csnation.net/skins/view_skin.php?id=3894) for the Terrorists. However I have experienced it in CZ (less frequently) with the default models.\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nMost frequent in CS 1.6, yet still happens in CZ.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545245, 78948, 1013, 100565, 1072936800, 'This happens all the time', '1. All the time.\n\n\n\n2. Playing Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\n3. Um it just happens while playing Counter-Strike or Counter-Strike: Condition Zero.\n\n\n\n4. No.\n\n\n\n5. I\'ve only seen it in Counter-Strike and Counter-Strike: Condition Zero.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545262, 78948, 1013, 102202, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n\n\nOn an evening playing for 3-4 hours it appears one time at a minimum\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n\n\nmaybe about 2 months ago\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\nNo. But maybe it only appears, when an opponent is behind a wall firing/looking in another direction and then comes to my sight und he still looks in the "wrong" direction but killing me...\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n\n\nNo. My CS is standard\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\nCS. Don\'t playing other Mods []\n\n\n\n--\n\n\n\nI think I haven\'t seen this bug on Cheating-Death servers, only on VAC servers... (but I want bet on this [])', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545353, 78948, 1013, 100220, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n     ...as often as a grenade kill? \n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n     Yesterday, actually.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n     I saw this in two instances where players had shot instantly after reloading. They seem to be shooting at me while facing another direction. I\'m not sure that this is the cause, but I\'ll try to recreate it.\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n     No.\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n     Counter-Strike.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545355, 78948, 1013, 102977, 1072936800, '', 'My problem is, every player is looking sidewards (is this spelled correctly), no matter what they are doing. \n\n1. I see it all the time\n\n\n\n2. About 2 months ago\n\n\n\n3. It happens all the time, no matter what they are doing\n\n\n\n4. Nope\n\n\n\n5. It was Day of Defeat', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545443, 78948, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'Thank again everyone, please keep the reports coming.   If you can get a demo of it happening, that would be great.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545444, 78948, 1013, 102515, 1072936800, '', '1: Quite Often\n\n2: Release of steam modified games (They appear to have used new models)\n\n3: Yes\n\n4: No\n\n5: CS and CZ', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545650, 78948, 1013, 102919, 1072936800, '', 'OcarD\n\n\n\nThis happens to me VERY VERY FREQUENTLY, Mainly the models are Sideways (RIGHT) facing but still shooting me.\n\n\n\nIt happens to me probably 5 times in a 30 minute round.\n\n\n\nI am at work now, when I get home, I\'ll record a demo and if you let me know where to send it, I will, if not, I\'ll find somewhere to host it.\n\n\n\n\n\nEDIT:  Oh yeah,\n\n\n\nHappens On Counterstrike 1.6, No Custom ANYTHING (Cept some binds)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(545655, 78948, 1013, 102978, 1072936800, 'Backward facing players', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n\n\n- All the time\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n\n\n- Some time ago, after some updates\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\n- I don\'t know..\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n\n\n- No\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\n- Only Counter-Strike\n\n\n\nAs for the demo, I\'ll give it a try []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546312, 78948, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'Questions:\n\n---------------\n\n1) how often have you seen it?\n\nAll the time\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\nAlmost from the beginning of CS 1.6 Official Release, It is my suspicion that most of the problems that stem from the shield are caused by the same bug. Also the reload animations I see of other live players also appears to be way out of sync at the same time. i.e. They appear to me that that are halfway through a reload animation and then they are shooting me the next instant, even though they told me that they have effected a complete reload.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\nAfraid not, although Im nearly always getting shot by that person.\n\nI know it happens a lot on dust2 and Aztec\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\nI never run custom skins, I hate them!\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nIt was Counter-Strike via the Full Steam Cache Download Method.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546315, 78948, 1013, 102979, 1072936800, '', 'i get the models look like they are looking at a bridge so i think i have time to stop and aim, and without turning they shoot me in the face.  i get this at least once a time every time i play.  i dunno if ive gotten the backwards model thing.  ill look into it.  any fix coming up to take care of it???', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546319, 78948, 1013, 102980, 1072936800, '', 'In my experience a person cannot activly re-create this bug.  The players who will be facing the wrong way can be easially identified in my experience when the round restarts and the players spawn.  When the players spawn the people facing backwards from everyone else (or when you spawn and you spawn backswards) seem to be the ones that during the round will have the animation bug.\n\n\n\nThis is just my experience however', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546396, 78948, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by evilcheese \n\ni get the models look like they are looking at a bridge so i think i have time to stop and aim, and without turning they shoot me in the face.  i get this at least once a time every time i play.  i dunno if ive gotten the backwards model thing.  ill look into it.  any fix coming up to take care of it???  \n\n\n\nThats the exact problem we are talking about.\n\n\n\nAlthough I don\'t know why they called it the "Backward facing players bug" since they arent necessarily facing backwards, just not facing you, and we all do exactly what you\'re saying, thinking we have that extra split second to aim all the more carefully, but in reality do not.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546469, 78948, 1013, 101444, 1072936800, 'Backward facing players', '1) Off and on; more in pubs than in scrims (all the scrim servers have no mods).\n\n\n\n2) The Knee Deep in Blood pub about a month and a half ago.\n\n\n\n3) Not at will.\n\n\n\n4) No.\n\n\n\n5) CS, but I\'ve seen it in CZ pubs as well.\n\n\n\nOn a side note, it doesn\'t really bother mean - because I never go for knives; if I see someone I shoot them reguardless of what way they\'re facing, but I do see how this could be a problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546478, 78948, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, '', 'It happens randomly [cant reproduce it] w/ a stock Steam/CS install [not custom anything].', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(546806, 78948, 1013, 101580, 1072936800, '', 'I have only seen this happen when the player facing the wrong way is close to a wall or entity.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(547610, 78948, 1013, 102981, 1072936800, '', 'I too have seen some of these bugs, and with a friend helping testing this out, I\'ve found out why this happens.\n\n\n\nHe stood still looking at me, and I turned my back on him and ran away and then stopped. Without moving, I turned towards him and he only saw me pointing to his right when actually I was pointing to him.\n\n\n\nThen we tried again, but when I stopped I crouched and then turned around. This time I was pointing in the opposite direction to which I was facing him.\n\n\n\nSo, lately, I\'ve tried using this bug online to fool people and it works. They come running with the knife in their hands.\n\nAnyway, I stopped using this cuz it\'s filthy and it\'s not fair.\n\nI hope I helped out, and hopefully this will be corrected sometime soon.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(547926, 78948, 1013, 102982, 1072936800, '', 'the only place ive seen this happen frequently and without fail is on de_dust2_cz. everytime i see it, same place. always. id get u a demo but my steam aint workin and i cant get ne1 to reply to my post. on dust2_cz, if u r t or ct, come out of/go through tunnel to b site. if ur going through, it will be on ur left coming out on ur right. the stack of boxes on the left of t/right of ct. when someone is hiding/camping behind that box, they will be faceing the wall, but they r shooting at me or someone else. i do not suspect hax. it just seems to be a glitch. it also seems to only happen on cz maps. not the original maps but the newer maps with cz skins(understand????). ive seen it othe times but that is the only place it always happens.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(549725, 78948, 1013, 102983, 1072936800, '', 'Seen this many times in CS, happens alot. I\'ve read and began to observe this for confirm it. It\'s when you turn a certain way, cant remember if it\'s left or right, as i read it long ago, and i\'m always seeing this in 3rd person view obviously.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(550919, 78948, 1013, 102984, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve had this happen to me on Counter-Strike with no custom anything, all the defaults.  Happens all the time, any map, anytime, and I cannot re-create it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(551383, 78948, 1013, 102985, 1072936800, '', '1) i see it atleast once or twice every map.\n\n\n\n2) i believe the first time i saw this was right around the release time of CZ.\n\n\n\n3) im sure i could, but i dont know what causes it.\n\n\n\n4) no custom skins or anything, except my scripts\n\n\n\n5) CS', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(552708, 78948, 1013, 102982, 1072936800, '', 'im not an expert but from what ive seen this glitch usually occurs next to walls. when a player is right up against the wall. the player is aiming at u but it looks like hes looking away and aiming over his shoulderif u look closely(if u have time before u die) the head is also turned backward. i see it all the time and know how to recreate it on one map for sure. ive tried on other maps with little success. i thought i was the only one seein this glitch until i read a few of the posts and forums here. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n**NOTE** all this happened before my cz/steam took a crap and died on me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(553181, 78948, 1013, 102986, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it? - quite often !\n\n2) When did you see it first? - when starting to play cs 1.6 and dod 1.1\n\n3) Can you re-create it? - model looking in a different way but shooting me\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins? - no !\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod? - cs, dod', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(553299, 78948, 1013, 102987, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n\n\nOften enough for it to be noticeable, meaning a few times a session (session, for me, being about 2 1/2 hours of play)\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n\n\nSame as most...right about the time CZ was being released.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\nI\'ve tried and I haven\'t been able to.\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n\n\nNo.  I do run custom sounds and a few custom flag mdl\'s, but everything else is default.\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\nI only play Day of Defeat so that\'s all I\'ve seen it in.\n\n\n\n\n\nI have noticed that I see it more on custom maps than on the defaults.  \n\n\n\nAs others have stated everytime I\'ve seen it the person has been next to a wall or object, like a bunker.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(553620, 78948, 1013, 102988, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n\n\nSeveral times a night. Also see the reload animation glitch.\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n\n\nAbout the time CZ was being released.\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\nHave not tried yet.\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n\n\nNo. I play leagues like CAL, UGS, STA, PCGN that require default models\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nCS', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(554191, 78948, 1013, 102989, 1072936800, '', 'This bug happens often in the start of the round when you spawn, especially when you\'re reloading a gun.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(554593, 78948, 1013, 102990, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve only seen this in one instance, but It happens to my friends often as well..\n\n\n\nit was on de_dust2\n\n\n\nI was standing in B site looking out the double doors, and there was a player standing right behind those 3 green boxes, who was appeared to be looking at CT spawn... suddenly his gun just started unloading, and I got HS\'ed :-\\', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(554703, 78948, 1013, 102991, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by retribution \n\nocarD, from what I have been able to determine this problem is prevalent in all official mods at the moment, at varying degrees in each. However, I have yet to observe the phenomena on any unofficial Steam mod.\n\n\n\nIt is quite common in Counter-Strike/Condition Zero, and not nearly as much in the others, but a problem nonetheless. While I\'m not sure of the exact timeframe it appeared over, it may have been introduced with the 2.09 update [Someone else please confirm this].\n\n\n\nI\'m still attempting to determine the situation that seems to be the cause, will report back later.\n\n\n\nBTW, it does not have anything to do with the use of custom models, as this has been observed by me on full default games of CS and DoD.\n\n\n\n\n\n---Working on getting a good demo, will email.  \n\n\n\nIt hapens in cs to, and alot. Last night i played on assult as T, I was the last one on the T team, and one CT left. I was standing behind him, and i he was standing whit his back to me. I zoomed in whit AWP and his still standing whit his back to. Just as i was going to shot him i got a bullet in my head.\n\nI know he wasent cheating couse we was on a LAN and someone did watch his screen as it happend......... SO.......its not just MODS that has this problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(554904, 78948, 1013, 102992, 1072936800, '', 'maby its when a player is turning fast and you dont register it because you get choke or loss then your computer dont know were hes aiming...\n\n\n\nwhen hes not moving forward or something', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(555124, 78948, 1013, 102993, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s easy to recreate.  stand in one place and turn your mouse to the side.  Completely glitches out your upper torso.  If you turn 90 degrees, your model will cease to keep turning even though your crosshair is still going.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(555152, 78948, 1013, 102982, 1072936800, '', 'its just a glitch in the game get over it and let it go. yes it is easy to recreate and thx to vixro, we all can do it now!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(555153, 78948, 1013, 102994, 1072936800, '', 'I noticed it 1st about 2 months ago...really pissed me off too.  I was going to knife someone as it appeared they were looking away, them they shot me even though they were not looking at me.  \n\n\n\nI see it almost everytime I play, on either one of the servers I go to.  Other people have been seeing it too.  No skins are allowed on our servers and we run AMX for admin commands.\n\n\n\nWe just play CS no DOD or anything so I only see it in CS, I also never noticed it before until like I said about 2 months ago...never saw it in 1.5 or previous versions, or even in 1.6 until a while ago.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(555393, 78948, 1013, 102995, 1072936800, '', 'i personally see it all the time (i am playing cs most of the time as i dont have a full time job)\n\n\n\njust last night i was going to knife some one, thought they were watching shot a and get blasted in the face.\n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(556372, 78948, 1013, 102996, 1072936800, 'Buggy Buggy :)', 'Questions:\n\n---------------\n\n1) how often have you seen it?\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\nAny other info you can provide?\n\n\n\n\n\nA1) Daily, I play anywhere of 6-11hrs a day, so yes I see this allot\n\n\n\nA2) hard to say....I recently started playin allot 3 weeks ago\n\n\n\nA3) It seems to happen everytime to the same player that I view.  A regular of a server that I admin on. So I would say yes I could recreate it\n\n\n\nA4) No, I don\'t use any custom skins, only a custom spray image\n\n\n\nA5)  I first noticed it on CZ.  The server I play on runs the AMX-Mod\n\n\n\nOther:  At first I had isolated it to a certain player because I get it with this player everytime they are on, I at first thought it was  a hack but then I saw it on a couple more players.  I\'m begining to wonder if it has something to do with a Mod or Plugin that the servers are using.  Could possibly be messing up a certain section of coding.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(556666, 78948, 1013, 102997, 1072936800, '', 'yeah, i notice it on cs, but the character does seem to be facing forward, but  turningat a 90 degre angle, then still shot me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(557187, 78948, 1013, 102998, 1072936800, '', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\n\n\n     At least every other round.\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\n     \n\n     A month or two ago\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\n     Basically an enemy will be looking either way to the right or backwards and still be shooting me...\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\n\n\n     I was (not player skins though if that\'s what you mean... only weapons), I uninstalled them but still found the same problem.\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\n\n\n     Counter-Strike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(565603, 78948, 1013, 102999, 1072936800, '', '1. A fair bit\n\n2. Couple of weeks ago\n\n3. No []\n\n4. Default skins\n\n5. CS1.6\n\n\n\nI\'ve only seen this happen when they\'re ducking', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(566014, 78948, 1013, 103000, 1072936800, '', 'I have seen this in cs 1.6 often i do not run custom skins and it has occured on default maps like de_dust.bsp this has been going on for 3 months its crazy to see the players facing away from you whaen they kill you and no this in not a freek moment in cs this is going on everyday. it happens to me every day i play cs its a netcode issue where the models are facing one direction and not being told to refresh to anothers pc anotherwords its also like when a person shoots you at the same time you shoot at them the signal just seems to vanish from both players like its being cancled out. no loss shows at these places and no blood shows up and no choke. This is a net code issue and is getting on my nerves because this game was not tested with qualified developers...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567276, 78948, 1013, 103001, 1072936800, '', 'Questions:\n\n---------------\n\n1) how often have you seen it? often.\n\n2) When did you see it first? I think it was around the time CZ was put on.\n\n3) Can you re-create it? no\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins? no\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod? CS 1.6\n\n\n\nI was gonig to knifesome 1, and they were facing the other way. but shot and killed me.  + many more examples simiar to this. Lining some1 up and they shoot me ect ect', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(568524, 78948, 1013, 103002, 1072936800, '', 'Samething happened to me.\n\nI was playing on italy and someone was ducking in one of the corner in the house.\n\nThe guy looked like he was looking about 90 degrees off from where I was, and when he fired his shots hit me. Its anoying but its rare.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569157, 78948, 1013, 103003, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ocarD \n\nThank again everyone, please keep the reports coming.   If you can get a demo of it happening, that would be great. \n\n\n\nBasically same answers as everybody else for me, but I\'ll try my best to get a demo [].', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569333, 78948, 1013, 102305, 1072936800, '', '1. At least once per playing period on a server\n\n2. At least the last month.\n\n3. It\'s too random to try to catch, I\'d have tons of long demos, and it\'s not always easy to tell.\n\n4. No.\n\n5. I\'ve only really seen it in DOD, but I don\'t really play CS or CZ as often or for as long.  It\'s really bad in DOD...check the forums at dayofdefeat.net, there are at least a few posts referencing this somehow.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569981, 78948, 1013, 103004, 1072936800, '', 'i was playing chateau and i had a shield....i ran into 3 terrorist (bots)  and watched as 2 of them aimed at me... the 3rd one was turned around with a deagle and when i opened the shield i could here the deagle shots firing at me and just to make sure i checked that there were no teamates around and i took a screen shot..... enjoy    i dont know how to show you all the screenshot though!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(571398, 78948, 1013, 102376, 1072936800, '', 'i dunno if this will be of any help but it seems to happen every time i play cs. There seems to be no pattern to it at all. i am running custom skins for guns and players. It seems to have been happening for about 5 weeks now though im not sure when i first saw it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(571809, 78948, 1013, 103005, 1072936800, '', 'how often? everyday, everyscrim.. not in cs:cz but 1.6', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(573589, 78948, 1013, 102432, 1072936800, '', 'Happens ~2 times per map for the past month+\n\n\n\nThe player seems like they\'re looking sideways, usually crouched...then they start firing at me and i die...note that during the entire sequence it always looks like they\'re facing another direction, until they get up and move, then it looks correct again.  also, it seems to happen randomly.  i have seen it out in the open, near walls, crouched, uncrouched...it is very annoying when trying to get a knife kill, or when faced with multiple enemies, trying to shoot the guy that is looking at you (ignoring the one that isn\'t) and then getting killed by the one you thought wasn\'t looking, but turned out just to be a glitch\n\n\n\nthis occurs in CS and DoD both\n\n\n\ni have only default models in DoD, but i run custom models in CS (combination of PAF and Insane skin paks)\n\n\n\ni doubt i could get a demo of it, but i guess i could try :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(574855, 78948, 1013, 103006, 1072936800, '', 'T spawn on d2 about to TK before lo3 and got shot in the head trying to knife him ^-^', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(575162, 78948, 1013, 103007, 1072936800, 'yes', '1) It happens to me often (Makes me die, most of the time)\n\n2) A good while ago\n\n3) not that I know of\n\n4) No I do not, but I did at a time and it did it too. Still does it now.\n\n5) It does it on CS for sure not sure about CZ...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(575901, 78948, 1013, 103008, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by chair_jacker \n\ni was playing chateau and i had a shield....i ran into 3 terrorist (bots)  and watched as 2 of them aimed at me... the 3rd one was turned around with a deagle and when i opened the shield i could here the deagle shots firing at me and just to make sure i checked that there were no teamates around and i took a screen shot..... enjoy    i dont know how to show you all the screenshot though!!!  \n\n\n\nI get it occasionally, but with bots on aim_awp it happens everytime.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(576530, 78948, 1013, 103009, 1072936800, '', '1. I see it daily\n\n\n\n2. Don\'t remember\n\n\n\n3. about 80% of the times it happens it is when someone is crouching with a "seconday weapon" and of those times it involves a gun (that i have seen it) ot mostly happens when he is holding a USP\n\n\n\n4. official\n\n\n\n5. Counter-Strike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(576848, 78948, 1013, 103010, 1072936800, '', 'OK I have seen it a few times, but I found this demo which re-vreates it and also shows how messed up some hitmoxes are\n\n\n\nhttp://www.mymtw.de/community/users...p;user_id=14907 (http://www.mymtw.de/community/users/getfile.aspx?type=demo&user_id=14907)\n\n\n\nThe first part shows the looking-the-wrong-way glitch and the second shows the messed up hitboxes. VALVE should definately take a look at it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(580840, 78948, 1013, 102989, 1072936800, '', 'The demo can also be found here:\n\n\n\nhttp://www.gg-movies.de/downloads/cs-model-hitboxes.rar (http://www.gg-movies.de/downloads/cs-model-hitboxes.rar)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(582126, 78948, 1013, 103003, 1072936800, '', 'And here [] http://home.arcor.de/nexius0r/demo.rar (http://home.arcor.de/nexius0r/demo.rar)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(583803, 78948, 1013, 103008, 1072936800, '', 'Good demo.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(584347, 78948, 1013, 103011, 1072936800, '', 'yes, as a matter of fact, i see it EVERY day. every time i play iceworld, and the round starts, if i\'ve spawned behind the 2 guns that most people go for (ak47 or m4a1) and somebody spawns in front of it, and we both just hold the foward key to get it, it seems like the other persons legs are facing one way, but their top half of their body is like lol...180\'d to face me, and looks REALLY retarded  lol. but anyway, i have no custom skins or anything, but it happens pretty much every time i cs (always fy_iceworld [])', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(585308, 78948, 1013, 103012, 1072936800, 'Answer', '1) how often have you seen it?\n\nAbout everytime I play the game fo more than 10 minutes\n\n\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\nAround early Mars I think\n\n\n\n\n\n3) Can you re-create it?\n\nYes, it\'s easy, just turn 89 degrees and people watching you thinks you look sideways, possbile glitch is that you now can turn the torso, and the legs does\'nt rotate until a 90 degree turn. Remember that the hitboxes are made for an unturnable torso (my guess) and thats why it\'s harder to hit someone with the modelbug.\n\n\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\nNo, all default.\n\n\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nBoth mods, but less frequent in CZ (or I perhaps play it less)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(585674, 78948, 1013, 103013, 1072936800, '', 'It usually happens to me when the other player is near a wall and crouching', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(590194, 78948, 1013, 100289, 1072936800, '', '3) Can you re-create it?\n\n\n\nmay be this screen showing server side data (http://home.arcor.de/matrixstorm/files/cstrike/msmod0001.jpg) can help you.\n\n\n\nIt shows data from a custom metamod plugin (i posted this one on the hlcoders list a while ago).\n\n\n\nAs you can read in the text there is an headhitbox on the server but the client sees s.th. different.\n\n\n\nYou can test this very simply for your self, just code an smal metamod plugin, that does an traceline from the players aim and shows the hitgroup etc..\n\n\n\nIn fact this bug occurs very often but in the most cases the difference is only like on the pic.\n\n\n\nThis bug seems to be related to the following player movement: turning around (rotation) (when you\'re moving your mouse too look around). Also when starting on maps like aim_map players are sometimes not updated \n\n\n\nPlease don\'t apologize about the doted lines, this was another feature of the plugin that has nothing to do with the traceline one. The height is not draw correctly, but the other coordinates are correct.\n\n\n\nIf i can help with some thing else let me  know (i.e. a demo with plugin running).\n\n\n\n\n\n1) how often have you seen it?\n\nusing the plugin you can see this bug in every round.\n\nwithout plugin you would only recoginize the difference 2 times a week (when there are huge ones, player facing the wall, fraggin you).\n\nthis may be not the case on non DSL connections, because on modem this bug may often feel like lag or latency!\n\n\n\n2) When did you see it first?\n\nsry, don\'t know but must have been before 2004-03-12 (YMD)\n\nHowever, I have not seen this bug again yet on the new 05.03.04 and 04.28.04 updates!\n\n\n\n4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\nno, never!\n\n\n\n5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nCS', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(590236, 78948, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'ripieces: Can you post a link to the demo with plugin enabled please?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(590299, 78948, 1013, 100289, 1072936800, '', '20040507_hitboxbug.zip (~477 KByte) (http://home.arcor.de/matrixstorm/files/cstrike/20040507_hitboxbug.zip)\n\n\n\nhere it comes, plz tell me if it the demo works (recorded on de_dust just ~8 minutes before this post).\n\n\n\nplz don\'t download to often cause of traffic, thx.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(590773, 78948, 1013, 100047, 1072936800, 'Backward facing players', 'Questions:\n\n---------------\n\n 1) how often have you seen it?\n\nseen it a couple of times\n\n 2) When did you see it first?\n\n+month ago\n\n 3) Can you re-create it?\n\ndunno what u mean\n\n 4) Were you runnning custom skins?\n\nno.\n\n 5) Was it CS or CZ or another mod?\n\nCS / DOD\n\n\n\nAny other info you can provide? \n\nim using my own script pack i created over time since cs1.5, but im sure it has got notting to do with the models', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(591673, 78948, 1013, 103014, 1072936800, '', 'Don\'t know if this has been posted elsewhere, but here\'s a good demo of the\n\n\n\n1) Torso-directional bug\n\n\n\n2) Hitbox outside the model bug\n\n\n\nhttp://www.fakelabs.net/cs-model-hitboxes.rar (http://www.fakelabs.net/cs-model-hitboxes.rar) (1.42MB)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592145, 78948, 1013, 100289, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Guoguodi \n\nDon\'t know if this has been posted elsewhere, but here\'s a good demo of the\n\n\n\n1) Torso-directional bug\n\n\n\n2) Hitbox outside the model bug\n\n\n\nhttp://www.fakelabs.net/cs-model-hitboxes.rar (http://www.fakelabs.net/cs-model-hitboxes.rar) (1.42MB)  \n\n\n\n\n\nvery good demo!\n\n\n\nlooks like the hitboxes are rotated the full 180 degrees on the server while the model on the client is not (only torso is  rotated to a maximum of 90 degrees).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592169, 78948, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ripieces \n\n20040507_hitboxbug.zip (~477 KByte) (http://home.arcor.de/matrixstorm/files/cstrike/20040507_hitboxbug.zip)\n\n\n\nhere it comes, plz tell me if it the demo works (recorded on de_dust just ~8 minutes before this post).\n\n\n\nplz don\'t download to often cause of traffic, thx.  \n\n\n\nI got yr demo ripieces\n\n\n\nI have my own here:\n\n\n\nhttp://whisper.ausgamers.com/downloads/hitboxe.dem (http://whisper.ausgamers.com/downloads/hitboxe.dem)\n\n\n\nSo far, I have not seen any response from Valve reagarding the whole hitbox issue. If they have can they post the link here?\n\n\n\nAnother idea would be top create a demo with hitbox sized models, that are just the polygons that make up the hitboxes so you can see precisely how far out of whack the hitboxes are.\n\n\n\nThanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592178, 78948, 1013, 102406, 1072936800, '', 'It stated when 9 way blending came into play', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592271, 78948, 1013, 100289, 1072936800, '', '@Whisper\n\n\n\nThx 4 your demo (-e), but I am sorry: I guess your demo does not show the bug. [i]You\'re hitting the other player in his arm-hitbox, because of the recoil of your usp, so it is not a bug.[/u]\n\nThe other player should have turned around a little, then you would get better results.\n\n\n\n\n\nYou can draw the clientside hitboxes when recording for comparision:\n\n\n\n1. sv_cheats must be turned on on server and client.\n\n2. proceed to a new level (cvar shall not be overwritten).\n\n3. now type on your client r_drawentities 3 in console (1= normal; 2= bones; 3= hitboxes; 4= model + hitboxes transparent)\n\n4. start the recording.\n\n\n\nDrawing serverside hitboxes with an plugin is not that easy, because it causes traffic for each line drawn and also the only correct angle you can get is the one for the headhitbox (I didn\'t manage to get the correct other angles in the plugin (4 metamod) for CS).\n\n\n\nI guess VAVLE will first try to look into their code before they say anything.\n\nMay be they don\'t answer right here, but a fix (steam update) would be also a good answer, wouldn\'t it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592374, 78948, 1013, 100289, 1072936800, '', 'S.o. did a very good description of the problem (/forums/showthread.php?s=&postid=587384#post587384)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592389, 78948, 1013, 103015, 1072936800, '', '1) i see it about 6 times a day.\n\n2)1 month ago\n\n3) yes tell my friend to walk into the wall and look at me and hes still facing backward but aiming at me.\n\n4)no.\n\n5)CS / CZ.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(592862, 78948, 1013, 103016, 1072936800, '', 'i only read your first post.. and heres what i have to say.\n\n\n\nthis has been a glitch in cs since 1.6 was released. ive had this problem since the first time i played 1.6 and im not the only one. i see it on various maps: aztec, dust2, assault, and many many more. i didnt think anything of it until other people started complaining about the same thing. like i said, ive had this problem in CS since the 1.6 update. no lie. and ive reinstalled steam several times and the glitch is still there, and its there after every update you guys release too. =/ its been like 7 months that ive had this problem, and i know im definitely not the only one.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(597487, 78948, 1013, 103017, 1072936800, '', 'We\'ve found and fixed this problem.  We\'ll be releasing the fix soon.  Thanks, everyone, for your efforts to help find clues about the problem.\n\n\n\nEric Smith\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
