(567504, 81835, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, 'Cryout to VALVe, please fix these ~50 bugs!!', 'projectile has posted a VERY interesting thread over at gotfrag. The thread gives us 50 rather important bugs that should be fixed in the game. (This is actually projectile writing with this account [] ) \n\n\n\nAnyways, VALVe, Please fix these things\n\nAnd for the players, give this thread some attention.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/)\n\n\n\nAlso post ALL your views and other stuff in !THIS! Thread in the suggestion forum: /forums/...;threadid=82139 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=82139)\n\n\n\nCut out of the thread(CLICK THE LINK TO SEE THE WHOLE LIST):\n\n\n\n................................................\n\n- Flying boxes. \n\nComment: Why not fix both of the flying boxes instead of one? (de_nuke) \n\n\n\n- Forbidden areas. \n\nComment: Forbidden areas such as the sky on de_dust should be removed beacause \n\nof the exploit in cups and so on. \n\n\n\n- Invisible walls. \n\nComment: Invisible walls such as the one above the famous ledge in \'bombspot A\' \n\non de_dust2 should be fixed. (If you are sitting on the ledge you can jump up \n\nand down and \'look over the wall\' and see opponents on the long yard or in the stairs.) \n\n\n\n- Boost thorugh ceilings/roofs. \n\nComment: You can boost through thin ceilings and roofs if there is just enough space \n\nfor two ducking players. Eg. the yellow house on de_nuke. The area over the catwalk ladder on de_nuke. \n\n\n\n- Weapons being seen through walls \n\nComment: Sometimes if the wall is thin enough and your weapon is long enough the opponent \n\non the other side can see your weapon through the door/wall. (This is if you are close enough to the door) \n\n\n\n- Models being seen through walls \n\nComment: The same thing as with the weapons but with models instead of them. \n\nA well known example is the one where you are sitting down(ducking) in \n\nthe yellow house with your [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] hanging out through the wall. \n\n(The yellow house in the main bombspot on de_nuke) \n\n\n\n//Misc \n\n- Cl_righthand gets the opposite value. \n\nSituation: When tabbing out to Windows and tabbing back again \n\nComment: If you are using cl_righthand 0 it switches to cl_righthand 1 as you tab through windows. \n\n\n\n- Models being rendered the wrong way. \n\nSituation: Various, from time to time, when you are unlucky. (THIS IS THE MOST \n\nANNOYING BUG IN THE WHOLE GAME, \n\nIT MESSES UP YOUR BRAIN AND HAUNTS YOU WHEN YOU SLEEP, DAMMIT FIX THIS ONE) \n\nComment: The models are being rendered sideways or something. \n\nWhen you are watching the model (from another computer of course) it looks as \n\nif it is looking towards the side when it in fact is looking directly at you. \n\nThis can be VERY devastating in a situation when you are sneaking up behind a \n\nlot of people. \n\n\n\n- Reload. \n\nSituation: Various \n\nComment: The model sometimes acts as if it reloads, it doesn\'t really reload, \n\nit just looks as if it does. Very annoying, can be solved by either shooting \n\nor dropping and picking up the weapon or reloading it. \n\n\n\n- Glock. \n\nSituation: Various \n\nComment: Sometimes the glock starts shaking as if it was having a seizure. \n\nDrop/pickup usually solves it. \n\n\n\n- Silentplant. \n\nSituation: When planting one half of the bomb inside a box and the other side outside the box. \n\nComment: This bug has been around since the creation of de_ maps. \n\n\n\n.........................\n\nThanks. \n\n\n\nNavid "projectile" Christensen \n\nprojectile \n\n#dot.spot @ se.quakenet.org \n\nprojectile@tuol.org (mailto:projectile@tuol.org) \n\n\n\nGive this thread some attention, get the ball rolling.\n\n\n\n\n\nLinks to sites that have highlighted this issue:\n\n\n\nSWE: http://www.fragbite.com/?newsID=5186 (http://www.fragbite.com/?newsID=5186)\n\nSWE: http://cs.nordicgamers.se/?news=0&a...f23593de128d5ac (http://cs.nordicgamers.se/?news=0&action=more&id=7603&PHPSESSID=a120e831cf1dbe2d2f23593de128d5ac)\n\nInt: http://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments (http://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments)\n\nInt: http://www.sogamed.com/?s=community...amp;news_id=447 (http://www.sogamed.com/?s=communitynews&sub=viewnews&news_id=447)\n\nInt: http://www.schroet.com/scenenews.php?id=4227#353607 (http://www.schroet.com/scenenews.php?id=4227#353607)\n\nInt: http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188 (http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567623, 81835, 1013, 103012, 1072936800, 'Nice work projectile!', 'The 3 MOST irritaing bugs are...\n\n\n\n1\n\nThe most irritating bug is the model bug for sure. The models seems too look sideways when he is aiming right at you...\n\nThis bug came somwhere late in cs1.6 and I cant remember it from 1.5\n\n\n\n2\n\nThe same for the switching weapon exploit, you can hear an emtpy wav file beeing played (I think thats why you here a "-eeehfrss-" sound when switshing between HE/Flash/smoke and prim/sec weapon. Some teams use this exploit to the fullest throwing 5 HEs at the location when a switching sound is activated.\n\n\n\n3\n\nSee enemies through walls when switching fast between teammates. This bug has been around for some time. Cant be THAT hard to force a mp_fadetoblack thing 10ms that it takes to switch between teammates.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567630, 81835, 1013, 102939, 1072936800, '', 'A lot of your bugs are flaws in the HL engine, not CS.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567634, 81835, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, '', 'I have updated the gotfrag post with different numbers. Please write the ones that annoy you the most.\n\n\n\n2, 11, 19, 21, 27, 33 ARE VERY IMPORTANT IMO\n\n\n\n//projectile', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567637, 81835, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Its my thinking that they have fixed many of the demo bugs. I havent tried it but I have heard that it works.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567639, 81835, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SesameSticks \n\nA lot of your bugs are flaws in the HL engine, not CS.  \n\n\n\nOkay, but they can probably still be fixed. My bad. [] \n\n\n\nGet the ball rolling!!\n\n\n\n//projectile', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567657, 81835, 1013, 102975, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah, many of the \'models/guns being seen through objects/walls\' problems are a limitation of the HL1 engine - they\'ve been arounf from day one and I\'m not sure we\'ll ever be seeing these kind of things fixed.\n\n\n\nAnyhow, good post Bzr, I\'d definitely like to see the following three bugs sorted asap....\n\n\n\n15 - Models being rendered the wrong way.\n\n\n\n38 - Ladders\n\n\n\n43 - The hitbox is crazy when it comes to shooting someone from behind. \n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567663, 81835, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, '', 'Bzr has nothing to do with this, he was just kind enough to lend me (projectile) his account. :PP', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567770, 81835, 1013, 103063, 1072936800, 'yay', 'cmon vALVE fix these stuff and counter-strike will be LOADS more fun, and probably more people will start playing it, cause i got like 10 friends that think CS is a ****ing BUG game and if u fix it then u guys gonna get more publicity !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567795, 81835, 1013, 103064, 1072936800, '', 'Ouch, That bug, the one when you see someone shooting at you, but he\'s not even facing you... i hate that one... \n\n\n\nSilent plant is no big deal but yea. let\'s keep valve busy by making them fix bug, this way they won\'t change stuff on our beloved guns lol jk', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567805, 81835, 1013, 103065, 1072936800, 'yay', 'quote:Originally posted by ocxigen \n\ncmon vALVE fix these stuff and counter-strike will be LOADS more fun, and probably more people will start playing it, cause i got like 10 friends that think CS is a ****ing BUG game and if u fix it then u guys gonna get more publicity !  \n\n\n\n\n\nYeah, and don\'t "fix" something that no person is disagree with it (like Crosshair, awp an headshot symbol)!!!!! Speak more with the community, find out, what is better for the players ...\n\nIf you won\'t be without work, u should fix the Crosshair, awp and headshot symbol, many peoples are angry of u! In my class, they say: Valve suxx .... (sry 4 the word, but it is so ...). And don\'t change something at awp or another gun, because after an update, we have to learn the weapon to use, and that is very difficult, if an update is once in the week .... !!!! And I find 1.5 was good, because you have a game and no so money updates and so many changes ...\n\nMy idea is, you change the Crosshair, AWP and headshot symbol an then nothing. You work on a update, which updatet all the bugs in one update... so, the gamer haven\'t to learn the "new" gun very often ..!!! But find out, if the update get new bugs, then fix it before Steam the update updatet!\n\n\n\n\n\nPlease tell me, what is your oppenion/what you say abot my oppenion?\n\n\n\nCu, your Dfler ^^', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567905, 81835, 1013, 103066, 1072936800, '', 'change awp, crosshair, hs icon back []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567943, 81835, 1013, 103067, 1072936800, '', 'YES PLEASE FIX ALL THAT, I\'VE NOTICED SOME OF THOSE BUGS MYSELF they are very annoying, specially the alt+tab one.\n\n\n\nAlso, please give us the option of increase/decrease crosshair size.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567947, 81835, 1013, 100738, 1072936800, '', 'gj projectile', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(567974, 81835, 1013, 103065, 1072936800, 'yeah ...', 'quote:Originally posted by [-Viper-][-NL-] \n\nchange awp, crosshair, hs icon back []  \n\n\n\nYeah, that is I mean ^^ []. And what is with the upate?\n\nI think, you have to add a new order. E.g.: cl_crosshairtype "0" or ..."1" ...!!!!!!!!111', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(568601, 81987, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, 'Balancing the M3', 'The so called "noob cannon" as of after this update is somewhat still unbalanced.  I\'d like to see a slightly lower reload rate.  I\'m not sure if you guys have ever been shotgun shooting, but I can\'t imagine ANYONE reloading the shotgun that fast.  I know I fumble around a bit with the shells when throwing them in the gun.  I don\'t think it should be slowed down too much; just very slightly.\n\n\n\nImprovement Suggestion:\n\n\n\n--  Slow down reload for M3\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber\n\n\n\n\n\n(Also: All the new updates are great.  They really balance the game.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569025, 81987, 1013, 103068, 1072936800, '', 'Dude the M3 is not called a noob cannon and i still dont think the auto shotgun should be called the noob cannon either. For a long time the AWP has been called the Noob Cannon thats why they make plugins to limit the use of the NOOB Gun.\n\n\n\nSee awpers want a gun that can shoot clear across the map with one shot and kill someone with almost hitting any body part but thats called SKILL right. \n\n\n\nBut if a guy sneaks up close with a M3 or Auto shotgun they get called why are you using the noob cannon for. I think that is lame.\n\n\n\nThey need to lower the price of auto shotgun and also make the spray on the m3 shells stay closer together for farther distances to allow the gun to compete.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(574049, 81987, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, '', 'Bah i meant the auto shotty.  Sorry', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(574115, 81987, 1013, 103069, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Fiber-Optics \n\nDude the M3 is not called a noob cannon and i still dont think the auto shotgun should be called the noob cannon either. For a long time the AWP has been called the Noob Cannon thats why they make plugins to limit the use of the NOOB Gun.\n\n\n\nSee awpers want a gun that can shoot clear across the map with one shot and kill someone with almost hitting any body part but thats called SKILL right. \n\n\n\nBut if a guy sneaks up close with a M3 or Auto shotgun they get called why are you using the noob cannon for. I think that is lame.\n\n\n\nThey need to lower the price of auto shotgun and also make the spray on the m3 shells stay closer together for farther distances to allow the gun to compete.  \n\n\n\nThis person has never played a competetive match in his life...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(574343, 81987, 1013, 100698, 1072936800, '', 'the autoshotgun only becomes a noob cannon at close range. long range, and the autoshotgunner is most likey not going to do anything at all. if you play maps like fy_iceworld, thats where the autoshotty becomes the noob cannon. find a server that doesnt allow it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(574462, 81987, 1013, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'Eh, it\'s a decent suggestion. I\'m sure that someone who practices every day might be able to reload that fast.\n\n\n\nAnd get it right, people. It\'s the n00b st1ck.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(577485, 81987, 1013, 100698, 1072936800, '', 'or noob toob.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(577556, 81987, 1013, 103070, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s noob stick [] There is a clan called n00b-stick you know :-p', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(577587, 81987, 1013, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by nomex45 \n\nor noob toob.  \'Noob Toob\' is another way of saying it. \'n00b st1ck\' was meant to rhyme with \'boom stick\' (a type of shotgun) rather than have each word rhyme with the opposite.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(577617, 81987, 1013, 103071, 1072936800, '', 'It also isnt nearly as good as a p90 in every situation its supposedly \'good\' in.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(577632, 81987, 1013, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Vek \n\nIt also isnt nearly as good as a p90 in every situation its supposedly \'good\' in.  If you play some close-range maps like cs/de_747 and such, you\'ll enjoy using the auto-shotgun a lot.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(578398, 81987, 1013, 103072, 1072936800, '', 'just to let u know the "noob cannon" is the mp5', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569436, 82086, 1005, 100989, 1072936800, 'Valve, How can a message of over 20000 players be ignored?', 'Just look at this petition, and tell me that it can be completely ignored. Please, as a loyal customer and supporter of Valve and their products, I only want the best of Counter-strike and Steam, and this latest update does not fit what is anywhere near best. \n\n\n\nClick here (http://www.petitiononline.com/giveawp/petition.html) to view the petition of over 20000 people who are upset about this update. Whether or not their maturity is there or not, it CANNOT be ignored.\n\n\n\nFor the sake of your own product please rollback the AWP update at least in Counter-strike for this can seriously damage your (Valve\'s) reputation!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569454, 82086, 1005, 100871, 1072936800, '', 'online petitions mean nothing!\n\nsweet tapdancing moses when will you figure that out?!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569463, 82086, 1005, 103073, 1072936800, '', 'I was curious to know how valve felt about the reaction.. if they cared or not. Personally, I am enjoying it more so now. I am having to relearn the game, and frankly its more fun. Dont know if it was supposed to be like this or what. Why havent they said anything in their news? \n\n\n\nAnyway, keep up the hard work valve, remember, you cant satisfy everyone [].', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569485, 82086, 1005, 103074, 1072936800, '', 'Personally i have a question.  If we email Steam Support about these updates, would they pay attention to that more than us posting here on the forums?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569492, 82086, 1005, 100717, 1072936800, '', 'Wow its impossible to make everyone happy with this game, can\'t you see that? 20,000 people? steamids are in their millions arent they? technically thats only a fraction of users, and even a smaller fraction even care\n\n\n\nPetition huh... countless people have signed that petition for a chance to put their clan channel, website or their "important" name across a popular counterstrike petition, some idea of selfimportance and the chance to be seen by someone they know gets their signature but not for its true cause\n\n\n\nwith that in mind, how many of those people that signed it actually care about the awp? or have not double voted?\n\n\n\nIn my opinion the delay should be lowered very slightly but if it isnt, so be it, its not like everyone who signed the petition hit every quickscope and no scope or even tried doing it and now the update gave them a permanent scar in their gameplay, people say awp is more defensive and thats not a terrible thing for it to be.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569495, 82086, 1005, 101002, 1072936800, '', 'does that petition site only allow people to sign once btw?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569765, 82086, 1005, 100989, 1072936800, '', 'I got an email confirmation for it so im assuming yes', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569791, 82086, 1005, 101002, 1072936800, '', 'i have 3 e-mails, not only do i doubt its accuracy but 20000 is not a very impressive number in the largest game community. not that valve care for rants either.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569796, 82086, 1005, 100142, 1072936800, '', 'I wonder how many people signed it several times using fake emails? Factor that in it\'s less than 20000. 1,000,000/20,000 = 2%....such a large percentage of peoples want their awp back. And don\'t forget that there is more than 1,000,000 people on steam and more than likely less than 20,000 DIFFERENT people on that petition.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569808, 82086, 1005, 103075, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Praestantia \n\nI wonder how many people signed it several times using fake emails? Factor that in it\'s less than 20000. 1,000,000/20,000 = 2%....such a large percentage of peoples want their awp back. And don\'t forget that there is more than 1,000,000 people on steam and more than likely less than 20,000 DIFFERENT people on that petition.  \n\n\n\n1,000,000 ppl dont play cs. the 1,000,000 is for HL+CS+DOD+TFC ect. ect. ect.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569814, 82086, 1005, 103076, 1072936800, '', 'Well...I cannot speak for every CS player out there...but I can speak for myself...my clan...and everyone I have played with or against since the update. \n\n\n\nEveryone I asked, or everyone who has made a comment has made negative comments about it. Just because you only have 22,000 signatures does not mean that there are  not 1,000,000 people who don\'t like it. I wouldn\'t have even known about these forums if one of my clan memebers didn\'t tell me about it...and I have been playing CS long before steam.\n\n\n\nDo some testing... \n\n\n\nGo to a random server and start asking people what they think about the changes to the awp/scout?\n\n\n\nI guarantee you that you will get an overwhelming response to change it back.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569824, 82086, 1005, 100142, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by shr3k \n\n1,000,000 ppl dont play cs. the 1,000,000 is for HL+CS+DOD+TFC ect. ect. ect.  \n\n\n\n1.3 million people play all the mods. Considering how CS has more than all the other mods put together i would assume that is pretty close.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569879, 82086, 1005, 103077, 1072936800, '', 'i started an upside-down petition, for people who like the update, NO ONE signed it, compared to 20,000 people that signed that one, what does that mean?\n\nPlease people, there\'s many many cs players that have NO IDEA that these forums exist, so you can\'t do the math if you\'re missing numbers, hence my upside-down petition.\n\n\n\nhave a nice day\n\n\n\nGG STEAM!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569976, 82086, 1005, 103078, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Praestantia \n\nI wonder how many people signed it several times using fake emails? Factor that in it\'s less than 20000. 1,000,000/20,000 = 2%....such a large percentage of peoples want their awp back. And don\'t forget that there is more than 1,000,000 people on steam and more than likely less than 20,000 DIFFERENT people on that petition.  \n\n\n\nWhere is everyone getting this number from?  Is it related to steam ID\'s?  If so, it\'s a totally useless number due to these little things called lan centres that have several thousand (atleast..) copies of HL, where people that more than likely already own it are playing it, hence doubles.\n\n\n\nThen, factor in the fact that there is no feasable way that every single playing person has seen it.\n\n\n\nI\'ve seen two people from notable clans say that they liked the update, and many, MANY more from notable clans say they hated it.  The leagues are getting screwed over, you know the people that actually care about this game and spend hours playing it, for the Pub Stars that walk into a server and play an hour a week.  How is that fair?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569990, 82086, 1005, 101002, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by k.l0wr3z \n\ni started an upside-down petition, for people who like the update, NO ONE signed it, compared to 20,000 people that signed that one, what does that mean?\n\nPlease people, there\'s many many cs players that have NO IDEA that these forums exist, so you can\'t do the math if you\'re missing numbers, hence my upside-down petition.\n\n\n\nhave a nice day\n\n\n\nGG STEAM!  unlike the anti-update petitions you posted it once on one forum and gave it a name which dosent mention anything to do with what its about in the topic, im on these forums and would be happy to sign one if it was posted clearly.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569819, 82139, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, 'Cryout to VALVe, please fix these ~50 bugs!!', 'Posted the same thing in another part of this forum:\n\nThe other thread (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=81835)\n\n\n\nHoping that CLIFFE or someone else involved with valve takes a look at it. (This is projectile typing).\n\n\n\nHere it Goes:\n\n\n\nprojectile has posted a VERY interesting thread over at gotfrag. The thread gives us 50 rather important bugs that should be fixed in the game. (This is actually projectile writing with this account  ) \n\n\n\nAnyways, VALVe, Please fix these things\n\nAnd for the players, give this thread some attention.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/)\n\n\n\nCut out of the thread(CLICK THE LINK TO SEE THE WHOLE LIST):\n\n\n\n................................................\n\n- Flying boxes. \n\nComment: Why not fix both of the flying boxes instead of one? (de_nuke) \n\n\n\n- Forbidden areas. \n\nComment: Forbidden areas such as the sky on de_dust should be removed beacause \n\nof the exploit in cups and so on. \n\n\n\n- Invisible walls. \n\nComment: Invisible walls such as the one above the famous ledge in \'bombspot A\' \n\non de_dust2 should be fixed. (If you are sitting on the ledge you can jump up \n\nand down and \'look over the wall\' and see opponents on the long yard or in the stairs.) \n\n\n\n- Boost thorugh ceilings/roofs. \n\nComment: You can boost through thin ceilings and roofs if there is just enough space \n\nfor two ducking players. Eg. the yellow house on de_nuke. The area over the catwalk ladder on de_nuke. \n\n\n\n- Weapons being seen through walls \n\nComment: Sometimes if the wall is thin enough and your weapon is long enough the opponent \n\non the other side can see your weapon through the door/wall. (This is if you are close enough to the door) \n\n\n\n- Models being seen through walls \n\nComment: The same thing as with the weapons but with models instead of them. \n\nA well known example is the one where you are sitting down(ducking) in \n\nthe yellow house with your [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] hanging out through the wall. \n\n(The yellow house in the main bombspot on de_nuke) \n\n\n\n//Misc \n\n- Cl_righthand gets the opposite value. \n\nSituation: When tabbing out to Windows and tabbing back again \n\nComment: If you are using cl_righthand 0 it switches to cl_righthand 1 as you tab through windows. \n\n\n\n- Models being rendered the wrong way. \n\nSituation: Various, from time to time, when you are unlucky. (THIS IS THE MOST \n\nANNOYING BUG IN THE WHOLE GAME, \n\nIT MESSES UP YOUR BRAIN AND HAUNTS YOU WHEN YOU SLEEP, DAMMIT FIX THIS ONE) \n\nComment: The models are being rendered sideways or something. \n\nWhen you are watching the model (from another computer of course) it looks as \n\nif it is looking towards the side when it in fact is looking directly at you. \n\nThis can be VERY devastating in a situation when you are sneaking up behind a \n\nlot of people. \n\n\n\n- Reload. \n\nSituation: Various \n\nComment: The model sometimes acts as if it reloads, it doesn\'t really reload, \n\nit just looks as if it does. Very annoying, can be solved by either shooting \n\nor dropping and picking up the weapon or reloading it. \n\n\n\n- Glock. \n\nSituation: Various \n\nComment: Sometimes the glock starts shaking as if it was having a seizure. \n\nDrop/pickup usually solves it. \n\n\n\n- Silentplant. \n\nSituation: When planting one half of the bomb inside a box and the other side outside the box. \n\nComment: This bug has been around since the creation of de_ maps. \n\n\n\n.........................\n\nThanks. \n\n\n\nNavid "projectile" Christensen \n\nprojectile \n\n#dot.spot @ se.quakenet.org \n\nprojectile@tuol.org (mailto:projectile@tuol.org) \n\n\n\nGive this thread some attention, get the ball rolling.\n\n\n\n\n\nLinks to sites that have highlighted this issue:\n\n\n\nSWE: http://www.fragbite.com/?newsID=5186 (http://www.fragbite.com/?newsID=5186)\n\nSWE: http://cs.nordicgamers.se/?news=0&a...f23593de128d5ac (http://cs.nordicgamers.se/?news=0&a...f23593de128d5ac)\n\nInt: http://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments (http://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments)\n\nInt: http://www.sogamed.com/?s=community...amp;news_id=447 (http://www.sogamed.com/?s=community...amp;news_id=447)\n\nInt: http://www.schroet.com/scenenews.php?id=4227#353607 (http://www.schroet.com/scenenews.php?id=4227#353607)\n\nInt: http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188 (http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(569948, 82139, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, '', 'My mail to cliffe:\n\n\n\nHello Cliffe, \n\n\n\nI\'ve made up my mind about getting your minds set to fix these bugs instead of updating counter-strike with what you call \'various improvements\'.\n\n\n\nThis list that I have created has been recevieved very well all over the world. It is time for you to start listening to the counter-strike community. Read the comments regarding the threads. You will understand for sure.\n\n\n\nThanks a lot.\n\n\n\nHere is the root link: \n\nhttp://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/threads/82318/)\n\nThis is the main steam link:\n\n/forums/...mp;pagenumber=1 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=81835&perpage=15&pagenumber=1)\n\nThis is the second steam link:\n\n/forums/...;threadid=82139 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=82139)\n\nOther links from various large international community sites:\n\nhttp://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188 (http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=26188)\n\nhttp://www.sogamed.com/?s=community...amp;news_id=447 (http://www.sogamed.com/?s=communitynews&sub=viewnews&news_id=447)\n\nhttp://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments (http://www.gamers.nu/?p=news&n=1382#comments)\n\nhttp://www.schroet.com/scenenews.ph...27#353590353602 (http://www.schroet.com/scenenews.php?id=4227#353590353602)\n\n\n\nPlease answer this mail. It is a very important issue that deserves attention from everyone at VALVe and STEAM. \n\n\n\n\n\nNavid "projectile" Christensen\n\nprojectile@tuol.org (mailto:projectile@tuol.org)\n\n#dot.spot @ se.quakenet.org', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(570132, 82139, 1013, 103079, 1072936800, '', 'The "silent plant" and jumping through ceilings are the things that make this game so cool. Taking that away just make\'s it another game. Bugs or not, these things have been part of CS for a long time and should not be changed. The first time you found out how to silent plant, didn\'t you feel like you immediately wanted to show off your new knowledge to your friends or (if you don\'t have any) other people on the server? I know I did when i found out i could silent plant, jump through celeings, and walk in the sky. Changing these things just makes the game worse and you and many others fail to realize that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(571315, 82139, 1013, 103062, 1072936800, '', 'Maybe those things that you describe should be kept. But things like models looking the wrong way doesn\'t make a better game. K?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(572658, 82139, 1013, 103080, 1072936800, '', 'stop dreaming, \n\n\n\nlike they\'re ever gonna fix those.\n\n\n\nthey\'ll only make new "features" they can put on the \'box\' to sell more copies....\n\n\n\nvalve = company, not some charity organisation', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(572765, 82139, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'i suggest posting cs suggestions in the official cs suggestions forum (http://www.forumplanet.com/counterstrike/forum.asp?fid=6695). I doubt cliffe comes to the steam forums as much as the official forums (if he even comes here at all). I believe the steam suggestions forum is meant for suggestions directed steam and not the games that run off of it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(572766, 82139, 1013, 103079, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by roeb \n\nstop dreaming, \n\n\n\nlike they\'re ever gonna fix those.\n\n\n\nthey\'ll only make new "features" they can put on the \'box\' to sell more copies....\n\n\n\nvalve = company, not some charity organisation  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nwell put', '127.0.0.1', 1),
