(587384, 82802, 1005, 103456, 1072936800, '', 'Hi there, I\'m the creator of this demo.\n\n\n\n-- my bug analysis --\n\n\n\nvisual model bug: What\'s interesting is, that it doesn\'t work when turning left. Only right and from 90� to < 180�. I have no reason for that.\n\n\n\nhitbox displacement: I think the only problem is, that every hitbox just turns like the old way, what\'s bad, because for example the legs now don\'t move visually when turning, but the hitboxes still do. I bet if the models would turn like the old way too, the whole hitboxskeletal would fit the model perfectly.\n\n\n\nIf I can help in any way, just let me know, I\'ll try to.\n\n__________________\n\n[ Addicted to funmaps? | www.planet-zYk.de ]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(587408, 82802, 1005, 101002, 1072936800, '', 'thats worse then i thought it was. the last part with awm and the invincable head was insane. i believe the right person to show this to would be Taylor\n\n__________________\n\nEpox 8RDA3+ nForce2 Ultra 400\n\nAthlon XP 2500+ @ 3200+ 400fsb\n\n1024mb dual channel DDR400 CL2.5 3-3-3\n\n128mb ATi 9800 Pro @ XT (Omega 2.5.44)\n\n120GB 7200rpm Western Digital Caviar 8mb cache IDE\n\nBelkin 54g Wireless Desktop Network Card\n\nADSL 512D/L - 128U/P\n\nCreative Soundblaster Audigy2\n\nLogitec mx900\n\nZalman 5.1 headphones\n\n3DMark03 v.3.4.0 - 6059 (default settings, looped 3 times)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(587451, 82802, 1005, 101372, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s very important, so fix this huge bug please. \n\nAnd btw many german ppl have got problems with the circumflex (^)  in the console. If they open the console and type something in there, they have to remove the first character which is the ^. And this every timer after they have open the console. So please fix this that the circumflex not appear after the console will open.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(587467, 82802, 1005, 103456, 1072936800, '', 'I still see no need for this \'realistic\' playermodels. Where is the realism when you shoot 20 bullets on your enemy and he survives?\n\nEven talking about realism in CS is so stupid and that\'s the point.\n\nWe don\'t want a realistic game. We want a working game that is fun and could be used for official esports, tournaments and LANs. It was really fun and it still is more fun than other games, but if you keep this way (making the game more realistic and newbie friendly) you\'ll lose many players with every update. The best thing would be, asking the community, what they wanna have changed or at least let a choice of what being changed (like at cl_dynamiccrosshair/cl_radartype). You can use use Condition Zero or whatever for earning money.\n\nDon\'t ruin a mod, which had grown so big, because it was non-commercial.\n\n\n\nJust think about it VALVe.\n\n__________________\n\n[ Addicted to funmaps? | www.planet-zYk.de ]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(588082, 82802, 1005, 100163, 1072936800, '', 'bump\n\n__________________\n\nIt\'s pass September 30, 2003 no HL2 \n\nIt\'s pass December 18, 1998 no TF2\n\nCZ went gold 2 times? (10/7/03,11/23/03) out March 23, 2004\n\nWhy should I pay $40 for a patch to a game?\n\n\n\nA Note About WON and Counter-Strike 1.5\n\nSeptember 17, 2003, 11:35 am � Chris Bokitch \n\n There seems to be a lot of confusion over the proposed plan to pull the plug on WON. WON will be available until the Steam service is working the way it was intended to. We will not simply pull the plug. If you wish to, you can reinstall Half-Life (if necessary) and play Counter-Strike 1.5 the way you always have.\n\n\n\nCS servers 29,220- DOD Servers 1,646- CZ Servers 1,085- TFC Servers 848 Now which one should I play? GG valvE!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(588237, 82802, 1005, 103094, 1072936800, '', 'yes planet-zYk.de don\'t realism only fun! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(589208, 82802, 1005, 100163, 1072936800, '', 'I just want a game where if you have your gun in the guys face, he dies. With the hitbox in front of the model you have to go 6" over.\n\n__________________\n\nIt\'s pass September 30, 2003 no HL2 \n\nIt\'s pass December 18, 1998 no TF2\n\nCZ went gold 2 times? (10/7/03,11/23/03) out March 23, 2004\n\nWhy should I pay $40 for a patch to a game?\n\n\n\nA Note About WON and Counter-Strike 1.5\n\nSeptember 17, 2003, 11:35 am � Chris Bokitch \n\n There seems to be a lot of confusion over the proposed plan to pull the plug on WON. WON will be available until the Steam service is working the way it was intended to. We will not simply pull the plug. If you wish to, you can reinstall Half-Life (if necessary) and play Counter-Strike 1.5 the way you always have.\n\n\n\nCS servers 29,220- DOD Servers 1,646- CZ Servers 1,085- TFC Servers 848 Now which one should I play? GG valvE!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
