(579519, 83281, 1005, 103092, 1072936800, 'FYI: SK say no to latest crosshair changes', 'One or two of the players from the biggest, most successful and well known clan in the history of CS have talked about the new changes to the crosshairs in CS. As you will no doubt all be aware that 3 of SK\'s players all use 640x480 and have done for some time. The recent changes have meant that the crosshair now resembles this in 640x480, using the 1024x768 crosshair in all resolutions:-\n\n\n\nhttp://www.btinternet.com/~sarah.m.gibbs/xhair3.JPG (http://www.btinternet.com/~sarah.m.gibbs/xhair3.JPG)\n\n\n\nSurely the fact that arguably the best clan in the World have talked about  how they don\'t agree with or like it means something to VALVe. Please, stop pushing these changes on us. We don\'t all want a small crosshair.\n\n\n\nIf you\'re going to change the crosshairs at least give people the option of using a crosshair from any resolution in the resolution of their choice (i.e. using 640x480 crosshair in 800x600, 1024x768 crosshair in 640x480, 800x600 crosshair in 1152x864 etc)\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ll leave you with this from Potti. More comments can be found on regular SK forums and the Insider forums.\n\n\n\n#39 By  SK|Potti    / 2004-05-04 13:20:32   \n\nwhat the f*ck are they crazy, not many ppl out there got top of the line computers that can handel 1024 in res, and no point in playing any other res if the crosshair is based on 1024', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579526, 83281, 1005, 100282, 1072936800, '', 'Not all of us have top of the line computers that can run 1024*768? Well, I played cs for a good bit at that resolution on a k6-2 450/128mb/16mb TNT just fine until they decided to quadruple the min specs on halflife a couple of years ago. The game used to run awesome on a system like that at almost any res (within reason.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579538, 83281, 1005, 103092, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s not the way the game runs, it\'s the fact we don\'t want the changes to our resolution. All the people that kicked up a fuss about 1024 being changed didn\'t like it either. Just put the crosshairs back to resolution specific sizes, not one crosshair for all. We don\'t want it!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579552, 83281, 1005, 103093, 1072936800, '', 'either that or make it a clients side option. Nobody would complain then.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579559, 83281, 1005, 103094, 1072936800, '', 'yes it\'s a good idea ..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579568, 83281, 1005, 101002, 1072936800, '', 'well unless sk have controling shares in valve there opinions are as influencial as anyone elses.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579573, 83281, 1005, 103092, 1072936800, '', 'So then the people that whined about the changes because they were in 1024x768 or higher resolutions didn\'t have any right to get the crosshairs changed to suit them did they?\n\n\n\nYou can\'t cater for just one section of the games players VALVe. This affects everyone that doesn\'t already use 1024x768. Why was the change brought about? No one has actually explained it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579576, 83281, 1005, 100282, 1072936800, '', 'Don\'t fix what isn\'t broken. \n\nCrosshairs were fine, if you wanted to use 800*600 cross hair...you used that resolution...if they saw this as a "problem" maybe they could have added a crosshair menu so users can select the cross hairs they want regardless of resolution. Right now they are just changing things for the sake of changing things, and enough people made a stink about the large cross hair so they changed it back. Completely missing the point in the proccess.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579586, 83281, 1005, 103092, 1072936800, '', 'They didn\'t even change it back, they adjusted it so all the people in 1024x768 didn\'t have a problem anymore! Thanks VALVe! Now you just have to cater for the people that liked the 800x600 crosshair, the 640x480 crosshair, the 1152x864 crosshair, the 1280x1024 crosshair etc etc etc.\n\n\n\n1. Undo the changes\n\n2. Implement a menu system that allows for users to select their prefered crosshair for their prefered resolution\n\n3. Have happy end-users again\n\n\n\nIt\'s quite simple guys.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579588, 83281, 1005, 103095, 1072936800, '', 'Carbonite\'s idea with the chooseable CH is great ! I could get my 800*600 ch back (i also use that resolution ingame) and players who prefer to play with bigger ch in higher reso. would be pleased too ! An update with this feature would be really great !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579613, 83281, 1005, 103096, 1072936800, '', 'make 2 version of this game\n\n1.for kid\n\n2.for profs', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579620, 83281, 1005, 103097, 1072936800, '', 'What the **** is valve thinking?\n\nProgrammer #1: Dude, im bored. Lets ruin cs!\n\nProgrammer #2: Yeah, lets destroy this 5+ year old game just for fun []\n\ni need my fattass crosshair, its part of my playing style. valve should add som\n\n\n\nSERIUSLY VALVE, YOU NEED TO START LISTENING TO PROGAMERS, THEY ARE ROLLEMODDELS FOR THE WHOLE COMMUNITY!\n\n\n\nits not all about how you want it, you cant change stuff just coz you want to. You got a big responsability you know :|\n\n\n\nmake a list and pass it around to the most respected clans like 3d, noa, sk, and other us\\german clans on wether to keep the new updates or remove them. this has gone far enough, seriusly. you need to clean up your mess', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579641, 83281, 1005, 103098, 1072936800, 'xhairs', 'ok valve... read this thread, no one here likes the crosshairs. \n\n\n\nyou need to stop making random changes that you know nothing about.\n\n\n\nyes you made the game, but no you don\'t play it like we do. and in fact.. i was playing the game before valve even got their greedy little hands on it and started making it suck.\n\n\n\nhow about you get some feedback from the real cs community before you do something so stupid. \n\n\n\nthere\'s about 5 complete nublets in this forum that said the crosshair and awp changes were good ideas. NEWS FLASH! THEY\'RE NEW TO THE GAME! GET ADVICE FROM VETERAN PLAYERS FFS!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579650, 83281, 1005, 103092, 1072936800, '', 'That\'s what I have been saying all along. These are the same people that spark up "where do I change my rates?" in servers when someone talks about rates and settings.\n\n\n\nVALVe have got to learn to consult the pro players more. It was nice that they asked about the gun price changes and then took our resounding NO as the answer and didn\'t bring in their proposed changes. Where was the consultation on this because I don\'t remember anyone saying "Would you object to playing with a ludicrously small crosshair in the resolution you have been using for over 4.5 years?"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579682, 83281, 1005, 103096, 1072936800, '', 'everything Value should do from now on just can be concluded in one sentence:\n\n\n\nDo Not Change Anything Does Not Need To Be Changed !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579599, 83292, 1013, 101432, 1072936800, '"HLTV-Client" for everyone / for free', 'Hello and thanks for reading my post!\n\n\n\nI\'ve been getting to the following idea because I was talking to a friend without knowledge of Computer games and clan matches and thelike.\n\n\n\nWhat would you think of a completely free Steam client (i.e. without necessity to enter a valid CD-key) with the only ability to watch matches through HLTV?\n\nThis way you could be able to get a lot more publicity, because people who are interested in one or more of your games could watch some matches and thus experience them from a third person point of view.\n\nOn the other hand it would be great for the gaming community to be able to show their exciting matches to people who aren\'t from the community itself (yet).\n\n\n\nAny constructive criticism is appreciated, flaming may stay out of this thread, thanks []\n\n__________________\n\nSvenCoop.net - The Sven Co-op fansite', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(579710, 83292, 1013, 103458, 1072936800, '', 'I think this is a great idea.  It would promote the games and certainly steam could put a "buy now" link all over it.  Far too many times I have tried to describe to non gamers what these games are like and without a working install the description turns into something they just don\'t understand.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(580233, 83292, 1013, 103459, 1072936800, '', 'nice idea.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(583353, 83292, 1013, 101432, 1072936800, '', 'JohnCub: Yes, that\'s exactly what I was experiencing, too. Trying to explain TFC to someone and she just said some times "I will have to see it to understand it..."\n\nWould be great to hear something about this from the Valve staff. Is this anything possible to implement? Do you even like the idea?\n\n__________________\n\nSvenCoop.net - The Sven Co-op fansite', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(587493, 83292, 1013, 103460, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, this is a good idea, and yes, it is something we will do.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
