(584892, 83955, 1005, 103100, 1072936800, '', 'exploit:\n\ntr.v. ex�ploit�ed, ex�ploit�ing, ex�ploits (k-sploit, ksploit)\n\nTo employ to the greatest possible advantage.  (dictionary.com)\n\n\n\nwhen you quickswitch after awping, and it\'s "magically" reloaded, the game still registers the reloading, meaning you don\'t get any extra time (as krokko said).  this eliminates all advantages that quickswitching would bring, other than to unscope the awp and to get your pistol out.  how is this an advantage?  learn what a word means before you go throwing it around like a moron.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(584893, 83955, 1005, 100620, 1072936800, '', 'You cannot state that my argument isn\'t valid.\n\nIf you wish to do so, prove it to me.\n\n\n\nIt seems to me you\'re avoiding my points.\n\nWhat I wanted was someone to prove me wrong on all my points and no just the moronic "you\'re wrong"\n\n\n\nTell me then:\n\nIf it were an exploit, why was only one weapon fixed? Makes no sense to me\n\nAnd if it were an exploit, why wasn\'t it changed until a whorde of noobs who couldn\'t cope with the skill in it started whining on 50 pages in these forums?\n\nPlease TELL ME THAT', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(584903, 83955, 1005, 100620, 1072936800, '', 'Bunnyjumping was a herritage from the quake engine. It was not an exploit, since:\n\nHalf-life was not based 100% on the Quake 1 engine.\n\nThe Quake 1 engine is the only Quake engine to date that had bunnyjumping that wasn\'t intended.\n\n\n\nIn Quake 2, rocketjumping and strafejumping (bunny if you so please) was a know feature and Part of the game.\n\n\n\nCounter Strike was based on a game where bunnyjumping WASN\'T an exploit.\n\nRemoveing it from the game was a Design decition!\n\n\n\nGet you facts right next time...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(584904, 83955, 1005, 102784, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by krokko \n\nYou cannot state that my argument isn\'t valid.\n\nIf you wish to do so, prove it to me.\n\n\n\nIt seems to me you\'re avoiding my points.\n\nWhat I wanted was someone to prove me wrong on all my points and no just the moronic "you\'re wrong"\n\n\n\nTell me then:\n\nIf it were an exploit, why was only one weapon fixed? Makes no sense to me\n\nAnd if it were an exploit, why wasn\'t it changed until a whorde of noobs who couldn\'t cope with the skill in it started whining on 50 pages in these forums?\n\nPlease TELL ME THAT  \n\nWow, you\'re dense. 3-4 people just proved your argument invalid through comparing it to absurdity. Reread the page.\n\n\n\nThe noscope exploit only applies to very slow ROF weapons with no zoomed crosshair. Only the AWP and Scout fall under that category. And you\'ve got it backward; it wasn\'t until after the change that noobs who couldn\'t cope with the real skill involved in using the AWP started whining.\n\n\n\nIt was an exploit, because it took advantage of something that was not intended to be possible in the game. So was bunnyhopping.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
