(584926, 83955, 1005, 100620, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by neoflame \n\nWow, you\'re dense. 3-4 people just proved your argument invalid through comparing it to absurdity. Reread the page.\n\n\n\nThe noscope exploit only applies to very slow ROF weapons with no zoomed crosshair. Only the AWP and Scout fall under that category. And you\'ve got it backward; it wasn\'t until after the change that noobs who couldn\'t cope with the real skill involved in using the AWP started whining.\n\n\n\nIt was an exploit, because it took advantage of something that was not intended to be possible in the game. So was bunnyhopping.  \n\n\n\n\n\nThe only thing that supposedly "proved me wrong" was this (nothing else with any content was posted before my post "3-4 people"  lol :/   get your math straight man): \n\n\n\n"how is stopping the gun from reloading then having it magically reloaded not a exploit? and the annoying thing is you instantly can sprint away and jump back to fire that magical bullet right where the cross hair is the instant you land. this wont end till the morons stop sharing the same single braincell and realise that is an exploit because it is one and valve officially noticies it as one by fixing it. i\'ll say this once more kids, cal does not decide whats allowed in cs they only have power over the matchs using cs."\n\n\n\nand I answerd that right below, so I won\'t repost it\n\n\n\nyou do nothing but flame and say that I am wrong\n\nor perhaps that it is lame', '127.0.0.1', 1),
