(589398, 84247, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by D-Monkey \n\nHeres the new grandaddy of them all:\n\nftp://public:content@65.39.204.184/...Y/shadowops.zip (ftp://public:content@65.39.204.184/COURTESY/GAME_RELATED/CZERO/MISSION_PACKS/D_MONKEY/shadowops.zip)\n\nEdit: U can add this to the top list if u like. Id appreciate it.  \n\n\n\nI think there are (OR SHOULD BE) a large number of us who are wary of clicking a link with an @ in it.  D, can\'t you put this pack on the same site as your first one ?\n\n\n\nAlso, this links to a how-to Zip file for setting up balanced T campaigns.  By design I did not make it into a campaign.  But I did do a great deal to get the CT opponent bots just about right, and to even out the T teammate bot skills for great play.\n\n\n\n/forums/...;threadid=83180 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=83180)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(589858, 84247, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, 'Ratings for above Packs', '---\n\n--- Edit - BigDaddyK\'s Ranking\n\n--- \n\n\n\nHere\'s what I think of the above Mission Packs, with a rating of 1 to 5.\n\n-  My rating is based on playing the Easy Level and looking at the other 3 VDFs (scouring for typos, etc.).\n\n-  The rev number of the release is the author\'s rev, or absent that, the latest file date.\n\n-  Updated by BigDaddyK 05-20-2004\n\n\n\nHavok\'s Terrorist Mission Pack, rev. 5/1/04\n\nplayable mirror of the TurtleRock campaign, but needs 2 things:\n\n-   more T based objectives\n\n-   uses default bot profile and names are not reversed, mainly creates weapons problems early.\n\nthis is a 2, but a quick refresher mod can make it a 3 (cannot get a higher rating as a mirror).- \n\n\n\n\n\nThe Terrorist Mission Pack, rev. 0.2, by Anders Konradsen\n\n-  very bland name, I renamed folder to cz\\MP\\KonradsenTerrorist\n\n-  same bot problem as havok\'s\n\n-  PLUS \'stoprescue\' on 4th map seems unachievable (bug?) - until fixed, a 0.\n\n\n\n\n\nNational Insecurity Mission Pack, rev. 5/5/04\n\n-  second rev. on this pack, mostly for naming rules after Cliffe put out the dox.\n\n-  CT tasks are a little weak on defusal/prevent plant.  \n\n-  this mission is a rearrange of the 18 CZ maps to form a basic regional background story.  Reasonable low-cal attempt to do so.\n\n-  this is probably a 2.5 mission, if you play the Turtle Rocks Mission 4 times and then try this one you\'ll find it repetitive, 2.5.\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\nSJ\'s Original CS Mission Pack, v02\n\n- Note the typo list on bottom half of page 3 of this thread, \'rescure\'.\n\n-This Mission Pack is chock full of tasks to challenge the player, many of them innovative or at least interesting (steal mac10 from a T and kill with it on 747), but some of them are too much.  (kill 3 with knife on easy level, kill 7 on survivor BUT kill 8 with mp5 [what is that?]).\n\n- If you want tasks and challenges that take time to complete, this one is it.  BUT you may find yourself setting it aside and playing other faster MPs.  Keep this around to munch on now and then, but also for inspiration, a 3.\n\n- I did not complete the Easy level before writing this review, CZ crashing snafu and last 4 maps very annoying challenges.\n\n\n\n- The Balancing Guide for Terrorist Bots, rev. 1.1, by BigDaddyK\n\nI wrote this and it\'s not a mission pack, good start for my later packs, 0.\n\n(If you drop this into Havok\'s folder and put the DB file in czero, you will see how it changes the play)\n\n\n\n\n\nWorst Case Scenario, rev. 5/5/04\n\n-  T-side mission, each triplets has a different theme location.\n\n-  new T bot teammates created for this MP.\n\n-  2 zip files to install.\n\n-  Eddy ? a new typo.\n\nfix the eddie typo yourself and try it out, 3.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Shadow Ops Mission Pack,rev. 5/6/04 [?]\n\nHave not played this one.\n\n\n\n\n\nKidd Egg\'s Mission Pack, rev. 5/8/04 [?]\n\nHave not played this one.\n\n\n\n\n\n- BlackSun T Mission Pack , rev. 1.3b\n\nHave not played this one.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
