(588690, 84358, 1005, 100748, 1072936800, '', 'Brief thoughts on Assault_CZ:\n\n\n\n-The sewers definitely add a new element of gameplay.\n\n\n\nI like how they are actually DARK and you have to use your flashlight and/or buy NVG. This forces you to take care when going into them and is another threat area that an enemy (on either side you are opposite) can come from.\n\n\n\nExcellent addition to the map.\n\n\n\n-I like the overall look and feel. It\'s bright, clean, has good FPS (r_speeds), but is still the same basic map.\n\n\n\n\n\nConstructive Suggestions:\n\n\n\n-Complete the catwalk under the billboard against the wall. Extend it to the warehouse front wall and the underpass column.\n\nThis would give Ts and CTs a new path to go across, cover and snipe from outside.\n\n\n\n-For Bot (and Human) Play: \n\n\n\nStraighten the gates. Have one forward (left one leading to warehouse), one backward (right side). This may look strange, but it allows the bots to run through the entrance freely without getting snagged (because bots can\'t see the fence meshes).\n\n\n\nMake sure there is either a flat, concrete wall behind the ladders, or an invislbe barrier (can\'t remember what they are called) that acts like a wall so the bots have NO CHOICE but to go up one side.\n\n\n\n-Maybe make the sewers like Militia with working lights?\n\n\n\nI know I said I like them the way they are... And I do... But this is just something to consider that would really "finish" this map and make it official worthy.\n\n\n\nJust my two cents.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
