(590655, 84655, 1013, 103119, 1072936800, '', 'Just out of curiosity, Can an Intel (R) Application accelerator cause a problem with the new updates? After looking at the code it makes several enhancements to an application that load into memory. I would appreciate an answer from Nick and Nick only if possible,\n\n\n\nThanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(590660, 84655, 1013, 102904, 1072936800, '', 'The Intel Application Accelerator can cause memory corruption errors with VAC due to the way it interacts with the Counter Strike process.  If you are getting these, I\'d recommend disabling it before running Counter Strike.\n\n\n\nPlease note that memory corruption errors won\'t get you banned.\n\n\n\n                            Nick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
