(609982, 86929, 1013, 103151, 1072936800, 'Codename Gordon Help!!', 'I preloaded this game while in Steam onto my computer, and now it says I pre-ordered it. If this game costs any money, please un-order me or un-load it from my Steam.\n\n\n\nI do not wish to be charged to play this game.\n\n\n\nOnly take my name off the pre-order list if I have to pay to play this game. If its free for Steam users, please tell me, also.\n\n\n\nThanks!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(610002, 86929, 1013, 102758, 1072936800, '', 'its free', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(610074, 86929, 1013, 100158, 1072936800, '', 'lol.... If it didn\'t ask for your credit card ITS FREE', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(610106, 86929, 1013, 103152, 1072936800, '', 'you might want to hide yoru steam id too', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(610191, 86929, 1013, 103151, 1072936800, '', 'Thank god its free!\n\n\n\nAlso, I\'ll edit and take out the stuff.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(610243, 86929, 1013, 100250, 1072936800, '', 'I think it says pre-order complete because it having permission to access a free game is the same as having pre-ordered a game in Steam\'s eyes.\n\n\n\nPre-load Complete + Allowed to play game = Pre-Order Complete.\n\n\n\nO\' course, this makes perfect sense for CZ, but not for something free like Codename Gordon. It\'s just a UI inconsistency.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611760, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, 'Mission Pack: Black Sun', 'Here is a mission pack, as high quality (or higher) than the default CT one, only for terrorists.\n\n\n\nThis is a mission from the terrorist perspective. No more trying to rescue pesky hostages, and other annoying tasks. On hard mode this will be pretty challenging, and on expert it will be extremely difficult, so I suggest starting it on easy or normal. Enjoy, and let me know what you think or if you find any bugs.\n\n\n\nVisit www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun (http://www.sandwiregames.com/blacksun) for the newest version and version history.\n\n\n\nCurrent version available: 1.4\n\n\n\nNewest changes\n\n\n\nCustom bots have been added.\n\n\n\nAdded new tasks for normal, hard and expert mode.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611766, 87104, 1005, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'did u play your own missions all the way yet? ive made a few packs and belive me there are bugs . some things just crash cz like injure with a HE  on dust crashes,are loads more i cant remember them right now\n\n\n\nalso with your download zip, maybe make a czero folder with the maps wide ,mission pack folder etc. so u can just unzip in czero..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611780, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by eram \n\ndid u play your own missions all the way yet? ive made a few packs and belive me there are bugs . some things just crash cz like injure with a HE  on dust crashes,are loads more i cant remember them right now\n\n\n\nalso with your download zip, maybe make a czero folder with the maps wide ,mission pack folder etc. so u can just unzip in czero..  \n\n\n\nI will redo the zip like that once I am told it works for everyone (no missing files or anything).\n\n\n\n\n\nI played it all the way through on one mode while making it, and there were several bugs, and then I fixed it and made sure, in the other modes, there were no bugs (I\'ve identified all possible bugs).\n\n\n\nSo, I am almost 100% sure there are no bugs like that. Just not sure if all necessary files are there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611806, 87104, 1005, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'nice pack, 1 thing ive found tho is the oilrig_wide.tga does not show up in game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611829, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by eram \n\nnice pack, 1 thing ive found tho is the oilrig_wide.tga does not show up in game.  \n\n\n\nI think it says in the readme, but you have to rename it to as_Oilrig.tga (remove the _wide part of the name). I just did that since there were two of those oilrig tgas, each belonging in a different folder.\n\n\n\nAnyway, it will be eaiser in the next version with different folders already in the zip, you will only have to extract it to czero.\n\n\n\nDoes everything seem to work so far? What do you think about specific challenges etc?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611846, 87104, 1005, 100341, 1072936800, '', 'just from looking at the zip:\n\n\n\nmissionpackinfo.vdf\n\n-not needed\n\n\n\nBotProfile.db not included\n\n-this causes an error for me since I\'ve changed the names of my bots in that default file\n\n-this can be included in your pack folder\n\n\n\nthe map oilrig should be renamed as_oilrig.bsp\n\n\n\nnot related to your pack:\n\nI don\'t think they included a mission description for as maps.  Can anyone confirm this?  Mine come up as Hostage/Rescue.  I could be using an old file...  dunno...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(611850, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by pepe7373 \n\njust from looking at the zip:\n\n\n\nmissionpackinfo.vdf\n\n-not needed\n\n\n\nBotProfile.db not included\n\n-this causes an error for me since I\'ve changed the names of my bots in that default file\n\n-this can be included in your pack folder\n\n\n\nthe map oilrig should be renamed as_oilrig.bsp\n\n\n\nnot related to your pack:\n\nI don\'t think they included a mission description for as maps.  Can anyone confirm this?  Mine come up as Hostage/Rescue.  I could be using an old file...  dunno...  \n\n\n\nWhere should my BotProfile.db go? In the czero folder? in czero/missionpacks/ where?\n\n\n\nIs oilrig included in default in cz? Do I need to include that map?\n\n\n\nThanks.\n\n\n\nedit:\n\n\n\nOk, I made those changes. I am pretty sure it will all work, but someone let me know please.\n\n\n\nIf anyone has any suggestions for gameplay changes (make it easier / harder, add a certain type of challenge, switch out some maps for others, etc.,) feel free to post them.\n\n\n\nIf you find any other bugs, please let me know.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(612374, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'Can anyone tell me if 1.1 works without any bugs? Thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613132, 87104, 1005, 100341, 1072936800, '', 'No time to test, but the contents look ok.\n\nTry coming up with some custom bots (skill/name) for the next one.\n\nas_oilrig is included with CS and the nav file is included with CZ, so everyone should have it.  I don\'t see any harm in including them in your pack, just in case.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613232, 87104, 1005, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'oilrig main pic still not show up and the bots names are the wrong way round.other than that all good', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613530, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by eram \n\noilrig main pic still not show up and the bots names are the wrong way round.other than that all good  \n\n\n\nWhat do you mean wrong way around?\n\n\n\nThe picture shows up for me.. can anyone else confirm that it does or doesn\'t show up?\n\n\n\nAlso, does oilrig come standard on CZ? Should it not be included? Or only standard on CS?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613553, 87104, 1005, 103154, 1072936800, '', 'i installed the blacksun 1.0 pack, and it works fine. i played for about 20-40 minutes and i\'m halfway through the normal.\n\n\n\none thing i liked is "try to injure an enemy with..." whatever.  i laughed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613881, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ching0 \n\ni installed the blacksun 1.0 pack, and it works fine. i played for about 20-40 minutes and i\'m halfway through the normal.\n\n\n\none thing i liked is "try to injure an enemy with..." whatever.  i laughed. \n\n\n\nYeah, that one is for glock only! On expert mode (and I think hard also) you actually have to *kill* people with the glock, but I thought it might be too much of a challenge on easy/normal modes.\n\n\n\n\n\nTo people who reported errors with the as_oilrig preview images:\n\nPlease try installing version 1.1 and tell me if the problem still persists.\n\n\n\nRegarding the inclusion of as_oilrig.bsp and .nav:\n\nCan someone please tell me for certain that as_oilrig is included in CZ so I can stop including it in this pack? I thought that only the _cz maps were included, but maybe I was wrong.\n\n\n\nRegarding bot names being mixed up:\n\nWhat exactly is the problem here, I wasn\'t sure what you meant.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNew version coming soon:\n\nThe next version will fix any bugs mentioned above, as well as  add custom bot names (i.e. terrorist names for the terrorists, names like Cpt. Scott, etc., for the counter terrorists , based on their skins).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(613897, 87104, 1005, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'quote New version coming soon:\n\nThe next version will fix any bugs mentioned above, as well as add custom bot names (i.e. terrorist names for the terrorists, names like Cpt. Scott, etc., for the counter terrorists , based on their skins).\n\n\n\n\n\n__________________\n\n\n\n\n\nyes that was what i was on about, the CT\'s have all the T names.. its not so hard to change them around, or u can get the T-balance that someone made and posted on this forum', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(614118, 87104, 1005, 103153, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by eram \n\nquote New version coming soon:\n\nThe next version will fix any bugs mentioned above, as well as add custom bot names (i.e. terrorist names for the terrorists, names like Cpt. Scott, etc., for the counter terrorists , based on their skins).\n\n\n\n\n\n__________________\n\n\n\n\n\nyes that was what i was on about, the CT\'s have all the T names.. its not so hard to change them around, or u can get the T-balance that someone made and posted on this forum  \n\n\n\nWhat\'s the T-Balance?\n\n\n\n\n\nI see how I change the team names easily, but for the enemy names.. can I just change them in the .vdf files?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(616540, 87665, 1013, 103158, 1072936800, 'Valve, you\'ve won my respect.', 'About 6-8 months ago, people focused (sp) all their attention on one thing in these forums: How much they thought steam sucked. There were some people that would calm the flamers down with a "relax, it\'s something good in the making." \n\n\n\nNow, Steam seriously is one of the best gaming tools I have ever used. It\'s a GREAT Idea, it runs smoothly now (I havent gotten a steam error in about 6 months of use), and it\'s extremely useful.\n\nThanks. You not only work your asses off to get us some new half life mods, (Source) but we have been getting consistant (sp)updates and new extras. \n\n\n\n\n\nWe all appreciate it.\n\n__________________\n\n-squaK', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(616558, 87665, 1013, 103159, 1072936800, '', 'Lucky you. For some of us it\'s just as buggy and unplayable as it was when it was first released (actually, it\'s more buggy and unplayable than it was in the first beta).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
