(642349, 88617, 1005, 100507, 1072936800, '', 'I bought a 9600XT and got Gordon on it, whoever said the different versions thing on it....they better give me the whole damn game (sp +multi) or I\'ll be mighty pissed....or they could at least give us a huge discount (like if we take the coupons to buy the special editions we get like 20-30 bucks off or something)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642753, 88617, 1005, 103171, 1072936800, '', 'my cupon does not mention single player only, it just mentions a "free* copy of Valve\'s full version game - Half-Life 2"\n\n\n\nthe * is attributed to this: "Plus shipping & handling and applicable taxes."\n\n\n\nso wtf ? what am i getting here ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642784, 88617, 1005, 103180, 1072936800, '', 'Just for you guys, my ATI radeon 9800 xt box says right on the back, "Full version includes single and multiplayer modes."  On the card it says, "With your purchase you are eligible to receive a free* copy of Valve\'s full version game - Half Life 2."  The asterisk pertains to shipping.  In other words you pay for shipping.  Hope this helps all.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642917, 88617, 1005, 103171, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jagermeister311 \n\nJust for you guys, my ATI radeon 9800 xt box says right on the back, "Full version includes single and multiplayer modes."  On the card it says, "With your purchase you are eligible to receive a free* copy of Valve\'s full version game - Half Life 2."  The asterisk pertains to shipping.  In other words you pay for shipping.  Hope this helps all. \n\n\n\nI\'d still like some sort of official confirmation from somebody who knows what they\'re talking about.\n\n\n\nI guess i\'ll have to email valve when i get home then...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(643881, 88617, 1005, 101419, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by [dave^]Cannon \n\nhl2\'s mp will be css (counter strike source) and i think that will be fun. \n\ngrsdfjghl\n\n\n\nNO ITS NOT OMG\n\nCSS is a PORT of counterstrike to HL2, but HL2 will have it\'s own multiplayer, like HL2DM or something, they have yet to reveal it.\n\n\n\nGetting decidedly annoyed with having to tell this to people over and over.\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/sho...mp;pagenumber=1 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?threadid=1298&perpage=15&pagenumber=1) <== Look near the end(like page 35 and later) and you should see one of the emails regarding exactly this. And how gabe or whoever it is responds that No, CSS is not "the" multiplayer mode of HL2, it\'s just a port.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(645332, 88617, 1005, 103181, 1072936800, '', '*GAH*!\n\nFinally, after I registed a week ago, I can post.\n\n\n\nAnyway, on the back of my Radeon 9600xt card that I got from NewEgg around christmas, it says "Full Version Includes *BOTH* Single Player and Multiplayer"\n\n\n\n,... Of course there\'s a disclaimer stating that "product may vary from version shown"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(645786, 88617, 1005, 101715, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m pretty worried considering that I do have the voucher and it doesnt work.\n\n\n\nThe are al least two completely Indistinguishable numbers/letters that i cant do anything about.\n\n\n\nATI wants a reciept, a UPC code, and pictures of the voucher to send the box copy (i dont have the reciept).\n\n\n\nIt looks like im really screwed there, so i advise you to hold onto your stufff!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(633921, 89580, 1013, 103182, 1072936800, 'Steam after update failure.', 'Evening I\'ve been a dedicated player for years now, but since the release of Steam I\'ve had quite a few problems with the program. Till a few days ago deleting Clientregistry.blob solved the very most of my problems until now.\n\n\n\nHere\'s what happens, I run the Steam update program fine no problems, but there it stops. As the program *should* show me the login window where I have to type password etc I instead get an error. (Windows has made an illegale action we apologize the inconvienence but you\'re screwed and we don\'t give a sh*t) \n\n\n\nI have reinstalled Steam several times and tried out several different client installation programs with no luck. I\'m pretty clueless of what else I should do and appreciate *any* feedback that I yet haven\'t tried out. Could this be a bug in my copy of windows itself? hell I ran out of ideas.\n\n\n\nThanks in advance, Philippe.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634006, 89580, 1013, 100134, 1072936800, '', 'virus / adaware scan? did you try to delete clientregistry.blob + steamui.dll + steam.dll? Check your hd for errors (scandisk) and run a mem test. get all new drivers for your hardware. And make sure that you took a look into the steam troubleshooter and quicksilvers FAQs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634056, 89580, 1013, 103182, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah been there done that, guess i\'ll spend my night scanning disks and what not, thanks for your support.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634144, 89603, 1013, 100962, 1072936800, 'Where is Gooseman?', 'Hey, where\'s Gooseman?\n\n\n\nAll the news and interviews regarding CS are coming from Cliffe only.\n\n\n\nFor those of you who don\'t know Gooseman and Cliffe created Counter-Strike together and I want to know why we only hear from Cliffe?\n\n\n\nIs Gooseman still working at Valve? And if he does, what exactly does he do? Does he create skins? maps? does he program?\n\n\n\nThanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634236, 89603, 1013, 100133, 1072936800, '', 'they locked gooseman in the basement, then boiled him to death, because people act like [color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color] hats when they play cs\n\n\n\nso valve\'s goose is realy cooked now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634243, 89603, 1013, 102895, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by veal_calf \n\nthey locked gooseman in the basement, then boiled him to death, because people act like [color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color] hats when they play cs\n\n\n\nso valve\'s goose is realy cooked now.  \n\n\n\nDid they made this up to make people buy HL2 because will be based in Gabe Newell\'s basement? :lol:', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(634267, 89603, 1013, 100133, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by paulius \n\nDid they made this up to make people buy HL2 because will be based in Gabe Newell\'s basement? :lol:  wtf????? i guess english is not your first language, i cant figure out what you were trying to say, take a semester of english and then come back.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
