(636054, 89821, 1013, 103186, 1072936800, 'Give shield a lifespan and improve animations...', 'Here a novel idea that might please quite a lot of people... \n\n\n\nGive the shield a life span of 250 armour points and improve the animations, so:\n\n\n\n1.  The shield can sustain damage and eventually become useless, much like regular armour.\n\n\n\nAt the moment the shield is the only inprenitrible object in the game. We can shoot through almost any map wall (wood, brick, concrete and even steel), boxes of all types and sizes. But, we can\'t shoot through a shield?!?\n\n\n\nIt\'s also the only piece of equipment in the whole game with infinite durability under fire, even after several nades had been thrown at the previous barer or it being hit with fire from 5 AWM\'s (by far the most powerful gun in the game).\n\n\n\n2. We can properly tell, without a doubt, when the shielder is covered or uncovered.\n\n\n\nAt the moment, nobody can trust the animations. For example (based on what I have witnessed): You shoot at a shielder that appears uncovered and hit nothing but shield, and later you shoot a shielder that appears covered and get a headshot.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636429, 89821, 1013, 103187, 1072936800, '', 'i think they should make the shield clear, like a some police forces have so you can see throught it. Maybe it should be a bit blury.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636443, 89821, 1013, 103188, 1072936800, '', 'nah, leave the shield the way it is, it\'s fine.\n\n__________________\n\nT\'was in the darkest depths of Mordor\n\nI met a girl so fair,\n\nBut Gollum, and the evil one crept up\n\nAnd slipped away with her.\n\nHer, her....yea.\n\nAin\'t nothing I can do, no.\n\n- Led Zeppelin\n\nROFL j00z n00b!!11!!1!\n\nRemember, every time you camp, GOD KILLS A BABY! Please, think of the babies.\n\nhttp://www.clanlw.net/\n\nIs da intrnet, I\'m alowd 2 spel rong!\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n12 Year Old AOLer Forum Moderator Nominees: \n\nbigun, eck| A L ! E N, {X][S}MILF, alen284, AK47FOOL, Aim@Me, ThE4cE, steamuser, \n\nn!ce, Cereph, NEED HELP21, 0101.pimp(); hlidskjalf', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636450, 89821, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'The shield at its current state is fine. It\'s just annoying when the entire CT team decides to buy it for five straight rounds.\n\n__________________\n\n-=[ASUS P4GE-V]=-\n\n-=[Sound Blaster Audigy 2]=-\n\n-=[Intel Pentium 4 (2.8 @ 3.2)]=-\n\n-=[Hitachi 80 GB HDD 7200 RPM]=-\n\n-=[Xpert Vision Radeon 9600XT 128MB]=-\n\n-=[512MB Samsung 64x64 3PC2700 DDR RAM]=-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636457, 89821, 1013, 103189, 1072936800, '', 'hey how about shield has life points! like an armor\n\n\n\nit goes down everyshot then breaks\n\n\n\nthen dropp out of hand n u can\'t use it anymore like an empty pistal', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636490, 89821, 1013, 103186, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by disgraceful1 \n\nhey how about shield has life points! like an armor\n\n\n\nit goes down everyshot then breaks\n\n\n\nthen dropp out of hand n u can\'t use it anymore like an empty pistal Thats pretty much what I was proposing in fewer shorter sentance. []\n\n__________________\n\nX-51 ::.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636499, 89821, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, '', 'This is a terrible idea.  Anyone with a shield is extremely easy to kill.  Suck it up and learn to play with it.  It\'s part of the game and it\'s here to stay.  If you don\'t like it go to no shield servers.  It doesn\'t make sense for the shield to have "health" points.  It would become useless.  Also: shooting threw walls and other objects depends on the thickness.  Once a wall reaches a certain thickness you can\'t shoot through it.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636523, 89821, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'You\'re lucky that nades even do any damage to shielders. If you think about it, the shield should protect against high explosives grenades, too.\n\n__________________\n\n-=[ASUS P4GE-V]=-\n\n-=[Sound Blaster Audigy 2]=-\n\n-=[Intel Pentium 4 (2.8 @ 3.2)]=-\n\n-=[Hitachi 80 GB HDD 7200 RPM]=-\n\n-=[Xpert Vision Radeon 9600XT 128MB]=-\n\n-=[512MB Samsung 64x64 3PC2700 DDR RAM]=-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636529, 89821, 1013, 100121, 1072936800, '', 'not entirely true for above post.  I, along with most of the cs population can easily kill a shield holder at its current state. \n\nthe hit points for the shield will make the game more exciting and yet challenging. \n\n\n\nNegative:\n\nct can no longer sit in corner and camp\n\nct may get hurt more easily\n\n\n\nPositive:\n\nmakes ct use pistol\n\nmakes ct move\n\n\n\nBenefits:\n\nif you use pistol you get good with it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636560, 89821, 1013, 103186, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SteveTauber \n\n...Your entitled to your opinion and I respect that.\n\n\n\nI am not against the shield being in CS1.6, but I feel that the current shield is buggy, unbalanced and in desperate need of an overhaul. I have posted observations to back this up in my first post.\n\n\n\nBTW, some twit recently found a way around most server side equipment restrictions, including the shield restrictions on "no shield" servers.\n\n\n\nI am hoping that with the proposed changes mentioned in my first post, there wont be a need for any shield restricted servers.\n\n__________________\n\nX-51 ::.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636571, 89821, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by X-51 \n\nYour entitled to your opinion and I respect that.\n\n\n\nI am not against the shield being in CS1.6, but I feel that the current shield is buggy, unbalanced and in desperate need of an overhaul. I have posted observations to back this up in my first post.\n\n\n\nBTW, some twit recently found a way around most server side equipment restrictions, including the shield restrictions on "no shield" servers.\n\n\n\nI am hoping that with the proposed changes mentioned in my first post, there wont be a need for any shield restricted servers.  \n\n\n\nI agree they should fix the bugs, but doing what you say is just dumb.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636572, 89821, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by I2o[G]uE TacT-X \n\nYou\'re lucky that nades even do any damage to shielders. If you think about it, the shield should protect against high explosives grenades, too.  \n\n\n\nObviosly a riot shield protects against high heat.\n\n\n\nGive me a break.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(636928, 89821, 1013, 103188, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SteveTauber \n\nObviosly a riot shield protects against high heat.\n\n\n\nGive me a break.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber  \n\n\n\n+1\n\n__________________\n\nT\'was in the darkest depths of Mordor\n\nI met a girl so fair,\n\nBut Gollum, and the evil one crept up\n\nAnd slipped away with her.\n\nHer, her....yea.\n\nAin\'t nothing I can do, no.\n\n- Led Zeppelin\n\nROFL j00z n00b!!11!!1!\n\nRemember, every time you camp, GOD KILLS A BABY! Please, think of the babies.\n\nhttp://www.clanlw.net/\n\nIs da intrnet, I\'m alowd 2 spel rong!\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n12 Year Old AOLer Forum Moderator Nominees: \n\nbigun, eck| A L ! E N, {X][S}MILF, alen284, AK47FOOL, Aim@Me, ThE4cE, steamuser, \n\nn!ce, Cereph, NEED HELP21, 0101.pimp(); hlidskjalf', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(637091, 89821, 1013, 103190, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Premo_Maggot \n\nnah, leave the shield the way it is, it\'s fine.  \n\nwow you must be crazy. inifinite lifespan is just G@Y, plus it really G@Ys up the game.\n\nI\'D rather play a game with NO shield at all than play wit shields with no lifepoints or armorpoints.\n\nIt\'s just ret4rded.\n\nI kinda have a good idea... The Shield is transparent to enemies but not transparent to allies. OR make a little sympon or triangle like HALO(kinda like esp) to indicate that it is your allie, but it doesn\'t show up against an enemy.\n\nSO shields should have armor points and/or add transparent or esp (like HALO) to improve sighting.\n\nP.S., if steam DOES decide to do this, they should add animation of a *beat-up* or just *bought* to indicate if it still can be used.\n\n__________________\n\nP4 10.8 ghz \n\n356 mb ddr ram \n\nSony 9000\n\n20" Inch Flat Square Panel Screen \n\n(100 fps at 1020x860 256 bit color) \n\nMy Future room comp (building it) \n\n----------------------- \n\nthermaltake III case \n\np4 2.8c ghz with HT \n\nasus p4c1200-deluxe mobo \n\n2064 mb 3900 ddr ram \n\nGeforce 9400 ultra 654mb ddrII ram \n\n628 of Video Card Memory', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(637096, 89821, 1013, 103186, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SteveTauber \n\nI agree they should fix the bugs, but doing what you say is just dumb.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber It\'s all good and fine to say an idea is dumb. But, can you post why you think it is dumb?\n\n\n\nI am not criticizing what your saying or ignoring you, but I really don\'t like it when people say an idea is stupid without atleast stating a valid reason (a valid reason is not the same as an excuse) as to why or why not they think an idea is stupid.\n\n__________________\n\nX-51 ::.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(641872, 90465, 1013, 100115, 1072936800, 'VALVe, HL2 and CS source comp specification?', 'I was wondering if AMD 64 bit 3200 with 512 mb ram, ATI 9800 XT 256 mb be good enough for HL2 at a consistent 100 fps?\n\n\n\nI\'ve had people showing me screenshot on IRC of their FPS in Hl2, somehow they got the leaked version and test it.\n\n\n\nThe comp for that was something like ATI 9800 XT 256 MB, 3.2 ghz intel ht 1 gb ram, RAID hd, etc...\n\n\n\nand it would drop to 30 fps in open areas.\n\n\n\nI\'m hoping thats only due to the non retail version they got and hoping the retail version will be optimized.\n\n\n\nI mean 9800 XT 256 mb intel 3.2 ghz is pretty much top of the line, and if it won\'t run the game smoothly at a consistent rate, then how will people move onto that game for competition in leagues and tournaments?\n\n\n\nPerhaps you guys can fill us in on the specification required to run HL2 and cs source smoothly at a consistent 100 fps rate in all areas? \n\n\n\nSome information would be kindly appreciated. Thank you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(641891, 90465, 1013, 100131, 1072936800, '', 'that wont run at 100fps - thats really unlikely. do you need it at 100? won\'t 60 do?\n\n__________________\n\n"Wake up Mr Freeman, wake up and smell the ashes" - Gman', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(641934, 90465, 1013, 103184, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s hard to predict, mainly because most of the final graphics engine optimizations are probably still in progress. Your guess is as good as anyone\'s.\n\n\n\nAnd remember FPS depends on how high the settings for detail are. 9800\'s are decent cards though.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(641936, 90465, 1013, 100020, 1072936800, '', 'It won\'t get 100fps with full detail, but my X800 series card will []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642174, 90465, 1013, 100063, 1072936800, '', 'Even if we all had a super uber computers that run all games  at 5000 FPS with all settings at insane, we are still limited to the refresh rate of our screens.\n\n\n\nIf you have a PC that runs HL2 at steady 100 FPS at 1024 x 768, but a screen that only supports 75 Hz at that resolution, then you\'re screwed, because 35 FPS get wasted.\n\n__________________\n\n/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=90249\n\n^ Worst. Thread. Ever. ^', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642284, 90465, 1013, 101970, 1072936800, '', 'Unlikely to get constant 100fps, but dont expect to be in trouble with those specs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642325, 90465, 1013, 100507, 1072936800, '', 'Are you kidding me?  I\'ve seen some people\'s computers (not mine of course, no no) get 100fps with like a 9600xt and a 3200 baton...with 512mb of ddr400 ram, and a normal 7200rpm hard drive.  \n\n\n\nYou\'ll be fine and then some.\n\n__________________\n\nChieftec Server Chassis w/ side window, Silver\n\nAbit NF7-S *Nvidia and Abit split up..:(*\n\nAMD Athlon XP 2500+ Overclocked to 3200+ (about 2.2Ghz)\n\n512MB of PC3200 DDR RAM\n\nATi Radeon 9600XT\n\n120GB 7200rpm 8mb cache Maxtor HDD', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642331, 90465, 1013, 100507, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Maxey \n\nEven if we all had a super uber computers that run all games  at 5000 FPS with all settings at insane, we are still limited to the refresh rate of our screens.\n\n\n\nIf you have a PC that runs HL2 at steady 100 FPS at 1024 x 768, but a screen that only supports 75 Hz at that resolution, then you\'re screwed, because 35 FPS get wasted.  \n\n\n\ncl_showfps 1 with developer 1 on and fps_max set to 2000 shows that I have around 200-300fps in CS and I only have a monitor with a refresh rate of 75.\n\n\n\nThe correct thing to say would be "You wouldn\'t see the difference between 100 and 75 unless you turned v-sync off, when then it probably wouldn\'t matter because above 60 you really can\'t tell the difference"\n\n__________________\n\nChieftec Server Chassis w/ side window, Silver\n\nAbit NF7-S *Nvidia and Abit split up..:(*\n\nAMD Athlon XP 2500+ Overclocked to 3200+ (about 2.2Ghz)\n\n512MB of PC3200 DDR RAM\n\nATi Radeon 9600XT\n\n120GB 7200rpm 8mb cache Maxtor HDD', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642442, 90465, 1013, 103197, 1072936800, '', 'u really should worry about getting anything +60 FPS. unless u have really good eyes, u cant tell the difference.\n\n__________________\n\nPentium 4 HT 3 ghz\n\n512 mb ram\n\n120 gb hard drive\n\nNvidia geforce fx 5200\n\nSB Audigy 2\n\nwin xp sp1\n\n15 inch LCD 75 hertz', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642059, 90495, 1013, 103198, 1072936800, 'Aiming HELP!', 'Wow guys.  Today when I got on Cs the aim is really messed up.  When I shot the bullet would go 10 feet up.  Now I have to shoot at the ground to actually kill someone.  Does anyone know how to fix this???  Also.  This morning, There has been a thick black line on the bottom on the screen while in a game covering up health and ammo.  Does anyone know how to fix this to?  If you do please help.  Thank you!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642285, 90495, 1013, 101970, 1072936800, '', 'well thats a damned weird one.\n\n\n\nbackup your config files and re-install CS\n\n\n\nif its still broke, your gfx card might be on its way to a better life []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642343, 90495, 1013, 100655, 1072936800, '', 'uh.... I would change resolutions first. Go back and forth\n\n__________________\n\nDescribe a color', '127.0.0.1', 1),
