(642268, 90513, 1013, 102895, 1072936800, 'Question about screenshots.', 'quote:Originally posted by squirrelbait007 \n\nOk I think im taking them F5 right. Now my question is where are they I go looking in my steam games folders and cant fine them nowhere Id like to see the picture I took.  \n\n\n\nWeren\'t you banned yesterday?\n\n\n\nAre you sure that key in binded to do screenshots?\n\n__________________\n\n---> www.hlds101.tk <--- The best documentation about the Steam Dedicated Server!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642271, 90513, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'They should be in your counter-strike\\cstrike folder in .bmp format. If they are not there, check if your F5-key is bound to the screenshot command.\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642317, 90513, 1013, 102856, 1072936800, '', 'Ok I can now find my screenshots for counterstrike, but how do I find them for a third party mod.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642318, 90513, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by squirrelbait007 \n\nOk I can now find my screenshots for counterstrike, but how do I find them for a third party mod.  half-life\\<mod folder>\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642330, 90513, 1013, 102856, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Apprentice \n\nhalf-life\\<mod folder>  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSon of a ***** I cant find cause I didnt take them I didnt take them cause the key wasnt set. I lose my images now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642346, 90513, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by squirrelbait007 \n\nSon of a ***** I cant find cause I didnt take them I didnt take them cause the key wasnt set. I lose my images now.  Ouch!\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642385, 90513, 1013, 102856, 1072936800, '', 'Ok now how would I go about uploading them onto the internet.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642393, 90513, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by squirrelbait007 \n\nOk now how would I go about uploading them onto the internet.  Convert them to .jpg files and store them on some free hosting services like Lycos.\n\n__________________\n\nIt seems totally incredible to me now that everyone spent that evening as though it were just like any other. From the railway station came the sound of shunting trains, ringing and rumbling, softened almost into melody by the distance.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642406, 90513, 1013, 101060, 1072936800, '', 'Did you notice those suckers are enormous?  First change them to .gif format.  Use paint if you have no other graphics program.  Or go to http://www.jasc.com/ (http://www.jasc.com/) and download an evaluation copy of Paint Shop Pro (PSP).\n\n__________________\n\nIt\'s gotta be the puppy chow.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642286, 90517, 1013, 103199, 1072936800, 'IMPORTANT: For Those With Input Lag Problems  **Fixed Update**', 'I was having problem with my CS and CZ with some strange mouse -key board lag...    The user phluid started a post about it... \n\n\n\n  /forums/...;threadid=65356 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=65356)\n\n\n\nI was about to trash my cs and somone had said that all they did to fix the problem was ..    \n\n\n\n--- This setup is for Windows XP --- \n\n\n\n   Hit    CTRL-ALT-DELET keys  go to Processes Tab .   You will see a long list of programs that are running..  Look for Steam.exe    Right click on it and go to SET PRIORITY ....  Set it to LOW and your game will work great,  back too my 4:1 ratio like the old days!! \n\n\n\n\n\n  Just want to say thanks to phluid and all the people that replayed to his post as I joined here just to say THANK!!!!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nToo bad  steam customers are doing all the work!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642728, 90517, 1013, 103200, 1072936800, '', 'WOW!! Thanks for starting a new thread and posting the fix.  I had read about this fix previously in the forums, but it seemed to have random cases of it working so I ignored it, but it works great for me.  Now I won\'t have to turn DirectSound on and off.  Thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642742, 90517, 1013, 100469, 1072936800, '', 'Strange fix. Low priority? Input devices typically are running on real-time I do believe, sooo... []\n\n\n\nOh well. A fix is a fix!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(645713, 90517, 1013, 100029, 1072936800, '', 'Indeed it works!!!!\n\n\n\nATTN: There really needs to be an option to set this, judging from the previous threads there are many many people with this problem and having to ctrl-alt-del to change the priority of of hl.exe is a pain in the [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color]!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(645748, 90517, 1013, 103200, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, well here\'s what I\'ve found as a problem with this solution.  When I set the priority of Steam.exe to low, I find that I will get occassional lags while I\'m playing which is not due to lags(pretty sure about this b/c it\'s periodic but consistent).  This isn\'t that big of a problem b/c when it lags, if I\'m moving my mouse during the lag, when the lag is over, the mouse ends up where I expect it, so I have not that big of a problem with this, it\'s just like online lag.  Another problem I\'m having is that if I alt+tab out of steam, one of the best features about steam, then go back to CS, the sound gets REALLY bad.  As in it\'s barely audible, the sound quality is down, and there\'s crackles alll the time.  I didn\'t have that much of a problem with the DXDiag fix, so I think I will go back to that for now.  Although that is a bit more tedious, it\'s not much more than the priority fix since you have to set the priority each time you reboot and there was no problems at all with gameplay.  \n\nI really hope Valve gets off their asses and figure out what the hell the problem is.  I mean, I understand the game is over 5 yrs old and they got more pressing matters at hand *cough*Half Life 2*cough* but whatever development team that has been working on Steam up until now has decided to implement Steam when the old version was working fine(despite all the hacking) and "fix" it.  Well, it wasn\'t broke, and now it is, so please fix it Valve.  Does Valve even moderate these forums?  \n\nI still say we need to all get together and plan a time to have a crapload of people submit problem tickets of this exact problem and see if we can emit a response.  I suggested this before but there didnt\' seem to be much interest.  Pleasem PM me if you are interested.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(645761, 90517, 1013, 102160, 1072936800, '', 'hmmm thats strange... no matter whats runing input should be getting the higest priority. maybe its somehting wrong with windows xp.\n\n\n\nalso since theres a new thread i would also post a warning of a powertoy that can cause some sorta input lag.\n\n\n\nits installer is taskswitch.exe and what it does is replace your task menu (alt-tab) with one that has screneshots of the tasks.\n\nit also seems to cause input problems and lag. to fix it uninstall the task menu modifier and reboot.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(646644, 90517, 1013, 102785, 1072936800, '', 'I mentioned this fix to some of my team so we went and tested it and they were pleasently surprised. some were apprehensive or sceptical, but they did notice a change on a lower ping server. guess we will be doing this each time we start steam, yes it goes back to default normal priority when you close steam out.\n\n\n\nI close steam as a normal thing to allow my other stuff to work like email surfing etc. I ran a test and left it open to see how my normal tasks would operate tho. I did notice that on low settings steam didnt stop web pages from loading as before.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(646769, 90517, 1013, 103201, 1072936800, '', 'so:\n\n\n\n1. This is NOT a Steam problem it has been around since cs 1.5 so is a Valve problem (i always hated the HL engine, the Unreal engine was a lot better then and even now ...1998)\n\n\n\n2. Is more related to DirectX, because in OpenGL this input lag doesn\'t happen, or at least no1 says this is related to opengl. So first change to OpenGL this can solve ur problem if it doens\'t affect your fps.\n\n\n\n\n\nHow to fix it ?\n\n\n\n\n\n1st. Temporal Fix: go to the Hardware Manager / Mouse / Properties / Advance Settings (I hope u understand i have and spanish version of WinXP), then change the 1st and 3rd options to its highest (sample and buffer �?, the second option is the wheel mouse detection), in my case they are 200 and 300 respectively.\n\n\n\nMaybe even if this doesn\'t fix your problem u may want to leave these settings to its highest, because u can improve the resolution/precision of your mouse.\n\n\n\n2nd. Workaround: lower the priority of steam.exe to Below Normal, and u can also set the priority of explorer.exe to High (Task Manager / Processes Tab). Do it every time before you play.\n\n\n\n3rd. Workaround: run Dxdiag (Win+R) and in the Sound Tab disable Hardward Acceleration (remember to restart your pc). If this works then start moving the slider to the right to the best setting, cause u can mess the sound in the game if u disable the HA).\n\n\n\n4th. Workaround: Unistall Alt+Tab Powertoy or end the Taskswitch.exe process before playing on Steam.\n\n\n\n5th. Workaround: Disable your Antivirus before playing on Steam.\n\n\n\n\n\nNote: sometimes one of these options can help u with the input lag, if not try them all! or\n\n\n\n\n\n6th. Stop playing on Steam and try UT2004, Far Cry, CoD, or whatever u like []\n\n\n\n\n\nREAL FIX:\n\n\n\nIts up to Steam to really solve this problem, why? because it seems that only the valve games are affected by this input lag and if u have read the systems specs of the others users THIS IS NOT A HARDWARE PROBLEM\n\n\n\nAt least it would be nice if they post a new about that this is really an issue and that they are working on that, WE ARE YOUR CUSTOMERS, WE PUT THOSE FKING DOLLARS ON YOUR POCKETS!...or maybe they can\'t handle this problem and they are afraid of saying that valve/steam suk \n\n\n\nnote: i still think that cs and dod (haven\'t played ns) are excellent games, the problem was that the modders just chose a bad engine for those games.\n\n\n\nsorry for my incipient english', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(649249, 90517, 1013, 100029, 1072936800, '', 'I really dont think you actually have any idea what we are talking about Loki. If you experienced this lag you would know that it is not some constant thing, and nearly everyone who is subject to it are adament that the problem is only recent.\n\n\n\nAnd the fix is not to lower steam.exe\'s priority but that of hl.exe, to demonstrate this people experiencing the problem of intermittent mouse/keyboard lockups where the mouse wont respond and the keyboard will become stuck for between 0.5 and 2 seconds raise your hl.exe\'s priority to High and you will see that the problem increases drastically, lowering the priority stops it occuring. The other fix for this is too lower Direct Sounds acceleration in dxdiag, this reduces the mouse/keyboard lockups but adds a short delay on all sounds.\n\n\n\nIt is not the sort of mouse delay experienced under direct x, it is a non-constant and sometimes infrequent one caused under opengl which is not reproduceable (u cant simply point at a specific place for it to occur, the occurances are more or less random).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(650369, 90517, 1013, 103201, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by minus_human \n\nI really dont think you actually have any idea what we are talking about Loki. If you experienced this lag you would know that it is not some constant thing, and nearly everyone who is subject to it are adament that the problem is only recent.\n\n \n\n\n\n"Recent"???  well you are wrong, i don\'t know since when u r playing valve\'s games but for me it\'s been years.\n\n\n\nand if I said that is not only from a personal experience, friends of mine did have this problem years before too. you can read the original thread where a lot of users confirm this\n\n\n\non that time the only solution for my friends and I was to switch to OpenGL. In OpenGL mode none of us got an input lag anymore; "but" as u can read on my previous post I didn\'t said that this only can happen on DirectX I just said that this seems to be "more related to DirectX" .. can u notice the difference?\n\n\n\nOn the other side:\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by minus_human \n\nAnd the fix is not to lower steam.exe\'s priority but that of hl.exe, to demonstrate this people experiencing the problem of intermittent mouse/keyboard lockups where the mouse wont respond and the keyboard will become stuck for between 0.5 and 2 seconds raise your hl.exe\'s priority to High and you will see that the problem increases drastically, lowering the priority stops it occuring. The other fix for this is too lower Direct Sounds acceleration in dxdiag, this reduces the mouse/keyboard lockups but adds a short delay on all sounds. \n\n\n\n\n\nIf you read again I said "Workaround" and a workaround IS NOT A FIX...why would I want to disable my Sound Hardware acceleration???!!! ... when everything works better (except steam) with it?\n\n\n\nAND, lines below...(well now, up) I said: Note: sometimes one of these options can help u with the input lag, if not try them all\n\n\n\nthose workarounds "can" help you but I didn\'t tell anybody that any of them are a REAL SOLUTION!.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe only thing I agree with you is that this seem to be random, but I notice that when you strafe and move the mouse a lot (and at the same time) its more probably that you will get an input lag, even if there is no other player in your field of view.\n\n\n\n\n\nCome on  minus_human, I\'m only trying to resume the original thread, because when [OG]Menacer open this new one, he left some useful info that other users wrote.\n\n\n\nwe are here to help each other not to fight against us without even read what someone\'s post', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(652309, 90517, 1013, 103202, 1072936800, '', 'Disagree its related to open gl, wtf would any1 want to paly in direct x is beyond me anyway, even tho i know ppl do.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(652397, 90517, 1013, 100029, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by .[oni].Loki \n\n"Recent"???  well you are wrong, i don\'t know since when u r playing valve\'s games but for me it\'s been years ... In OpenGL mode none of us got an input lag anymore; "but" as u can read on my previous post I didn\'t said that this only can happen on DirectX I just said that this seems to be "more related to DirectX" .. can u notice the difference? \n\n\n\nOk i\'m still just not sure exactly what you are talking about. For a long time now anyone i know using direct 3d (way before steam) has been subject to a delay between moving the mouse and it moving on screen. What we are talking about here is something entirely different which *only* occurs within opengl.\n\n\n\nThe direct 3d lag is old school and unimportant as its as simple as changing to opengl to fix. The lag people have been experiencing in the recent past occurs within opengl and is not really a *lag* as the name implies but rather *lockups* which occur with mouse movement and keyboard movement (movement become stuck strafing) periodically. It is more detremental in counterstrike and day of defeat because of the need for precise aiming but it occurs much more frequently in natural selection.\n\n\n\nJust so we have this clear, the *input lag* we have been refering to is not that experienced under direct 3d, it is different, much different infact and i would hope that valve even as a quick fix would implement a command line trigger to lower hl.exe\'s priority because this is rediculous and rendering the game unenjoyable for many.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(663709, 90517, 1013, 103203, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks Guys piority thing did the trick', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(663970, 90517, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'Whats the command Line Switch so STEAM will always start in Low Priority?\n\n\n\nI don\'t see any reason or harm as to why it couldn\'t always run this way?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(664191, 90517, 1013, 103204, 1072936800, '', 'Setting Steam.exe to low priority used to work for me.  Since then my computer broke, and I replaced the motherboard and harddrive.  Setting its priority to low no longer works for me.  I will try setting hl.exe to low priority instead.  But for those that work by setting the Steam.exe priority to low, you can open Notepad, type in\n\n\n\nstart /low Steam.exe\n\n\n\nSave it as a .bat file in your steam folder where Steam.exe is located, then make a shortcut to that instead of Steam.exe.  I\'m using Windows XP Pro, don\'t know what OS\'s this works for.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642755, 90573, 1013, 103205, 1072936800, 'LAN servers are restricted to local clients (class C)', 'i just start a server using steam hlds software everything works but my friend can\'t join my server or any class A  server he has cs:cz\n\n\n\ni try putting sv_lan 0  but it don\'t work', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(642797, 90573, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'Draco posted this once:\n\n\n\nquote:You need to do many things for your friends to connect:\n\n\n\n1) Go to www.showmyip.com (http://www.showmyip.com) and get your external IP.  This is the IP you will give your friend.\n\n\n\n2) Set up you router to forward the Half Life ports to your game server.  For the ports you need to open look at this FAQ: /index.p...859448,31415800 (/index.php?area=faq&id=1050915505,27362300,1071859448,31415800)\n\nThen go here to learn how to do the actual port forwarding on your specific router: http://www.portforward.com/routers.htm (http://www.portforward.com/routers.htm)\n\n\n\n3) Start your server and in the console type sv_lan 0 (this will fix the error message you are seeing)\n\n\n\nIf you follow the directions in the links above then your server will work just fine.  This assumes you arent using a dedicated server.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
