(643962, 90573, 1013, 103205, 1072936800, '', 'r u sure that will solve my problem? cause i did try that \n\n\n\n1) Go to www.showmyip.com (http://www.showmyip.com) and get your external IP. This is the IP you will give your friend.  gave ip to him server show on list.\n\n\n\n2) Set up you router to forward the Half Life ports to your game server. For the ports you need to open look at this FAQ: /index.p...859448,31415800 (/index.p...859448,31415800)\n\nThen go here to learn how to do the actual port forwarding on your specific router: http://www.portforward.com/routers.htm (http://www.portforward.com/routers.htm)\n\n\n\n#2 is confusing because he has a dlink 604 router and on the link u gave me it ask me to do the following go to virtual server \n\n\n\n1. Put in the name of the sevice i\'m trying to forward ports. i put cstrike\n\n\n\n2. Enter privite ip address. i didn\'t what to put so i put his ip\n\n\n\n3. select Protocol type, enter Private \n\nPort and public port. The link u gave me  for steam ports said:  The following ports must be "open":\n\nUDP 1200\n\nUDP 27000 to 27015 inclusive\n\nTCP 27030 to 27039 inclusive\n\n\n\ni could only put 1 Private and public port at a time and it\'s limited to how many virtual server i could put. so, i can\'t open all those ports. i put in  udp 27015 for Private Port and public port.\n\n\n\n3) Start your server and in the console type sv_lan 0 (this will fix the error message you are seeing) Now, i don\'t get this error my friend is getting this error and i\'m hosting the game not him.\n\n  \n\ni open his cs:condition zero type in sv_lan 0 in his console, connect to my server and he still get the error. sv_lan is 0 on my server  by default\n\n\n\nIf you follow the directions in the links above then your server will work just fine. This assumes you arent using a dedicated server.\n\n\n\nBut,i am using a dedicated server.\n\n\n\ni\'ll be wait for your reply', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(643980, 90573, 1013, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'Did you read this ??\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Apprentice \n\nAppearantly, I spoke to soon. I can see your server in Steam and I\'m able to play on it with a latency of around 100, but that\'s to be expected from a server on the other side of the world. At least your end works.\n\n\n\nMake sure that your friend followed the 3 steps I\'ve quoted earlier.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
