(647850, 91062, 1005, 100323, 1072936800, 'CS:CZ 1.2 Released --->', 'The official 1.2 update for CS:CZ has been released, and all other Steam games have been updated. Steam will update itself automatically when you restart. Here is a list of the changes:\n\n\n\n\n\nCOUNTER-STRIKE: CONDITION ZERO ADDITIONS:\n\n\n\nAdded new hostage models and animations\n\n\n\nAdded new hostage behaviors and dialogue\n\n\n\nAdded SPETSNAZ and Militia player models\n\n\n\nAdded crosshair customization (color, size, opacity)\n\n\n\nAdded player location system\n\n\n\nAdded exponential fog in OpenGL\n\n\n\nAdded in-game vgui progress bar for nav mesh analysis\n\n\n\nAdded de_sienna_cz\n\n\n\nAdded de_vostok_cz\n\n\n\nCOUNTER-STRIKE: CONDITION ZERO CHANGES:\n\n\n\nUpgraded de_inferno_cz\n\n\n\nUpgraded deagle view texture\n\n\n\nUpdated cs_italy_cz with 32 spawns\n\n\n\nUpgraded weapon UI images\n\n\n\nTweaked glock and USP sounds\n\n\n\nTweaked snow walking sound\n\n\n\nCorpses fade out with cl_corpse_stay\n\n\n\nGrenades are dropped on death\n\n\n\nImproved player turning right hitbox behavior\n\n\n\nImproved shield behavior\n\n\n\nImproved brass ejection behavior\n\n\n\nBots can use silencer on m4a1\n\n\n\nImproved bot_auto_vacate behavior with spectators\n\n\n\nCareer tasks are reset on mp_restartround\n\n\n\nImproved tutor behavior\n\n\n\nhud_draw 0 doesn\'t remove blackout\n\n\n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\n\n\nFlashlight sound no longer masks weapon firing sounds\n\n\n\nImproved text behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\n\n\nRound timer doesn\'t re-appear until the round restarts when the bomb is defused or explodes\n\n\n\nImproved player model hands\n\n\n\nALL STEAM GAMES:\n\n\n\nAdded refresh login dialogue for invalid login sessions (Invalid UserID ticket message)\n\n\n\nHistory area in game console no longer gets key focus', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(647853, 91062, 1005, 100344, 1072936800, '', 'I love you', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(647854, 91062, 1005, 100323, 1072936800, '', 'More information on the new hostages:\n\n\n\n-------\n\n\n\nMovement and Navigation\n\nHostages can now crouch, use ladders, and break windows as well as walk, run, and jump, allowing them to go just about anywhere a player can.\n\n\n\nRescue from Far Away\n\nThe �use� range of Hostages has been greatly increased, allowing CT�s to rescue Hostages from across the room.  If the Hostage is waving at you, you can �use� him!\n\n\n\nEmotions\n\nHostages can be quite emotional.  They will fidget if bored, watch other players moving near them, and show fear and terror when gunfire erupts.\n\n\n\nEscaping\n\nIf the Hostages find themselves alone and unguarded after about one minute into the round, they will sneak off and attempt to escape on their own.  Hostages will not try to escape if they have seen a Terrorist recently, or a Terrorist is anywhere in the nearby area (visible to them or not).\n\n\n\nWaving to CTs\n\nUn-rescued Hostages will wave at far away CTs they happen to see, unless that Hostage also sees a Terrorist at the same time.  If a nearby Terrorist is looking at a Hostage, the Hostage will not wave to a CT.  If a Hostage sees a CT and simultaneously sees nearby Terrorists who are not looking at him, he will shake his head "no" to the CT to warn him.\n\n\n\nWarning CT�s about Terrorists\n\nWhen a Hostage is rescued by a CT and there are Terrorists in the area, the Hostage will warn the CT of their presence.\n\n\n\nFear and Fleeing\n\nHostages can become afraid and even terrified.  A terrified Hostage will sometimes flee to a nearby hiding spot.  Hostages are afraid of gunfire, people being killed, and loud noises such as breaking windows.  They become terrified if they witness someone die, or are shot.  A Hostage will usually not flee if there is a Terrorist in the vicinity.\n\n\n\nHostages and "Home" Spots\n\nThe location of a Hostage at the beginning of a round is considered to be its "home" spot.  Hostages tend to stay in their home spots, and Terrorists can return Hostages to their home spots if they are caught while escaping or fleeing.  A Hostage will only leave its home spot if it is rescued by a CT, is injured, sees another Hostage die, or is left alone long enough to try to escape.\n\n\n\nReturning Hostages to their "Home" Spots\n\nTerrorists can return escaping or fleeing Hostages to their home spots by moving close to them while pointing their weapon towards them.  This intimidates the Hostage, who will turn around and walk back to his home spot � even if it is all the way across the map.  Hostages that are returning home will stop if they spot a CT, however.\n\n\n\nTechnical Notes:\n\n\n\nNav Files\n\nThe new Hostage behaviors use data from the CS Bot .nav files.  If a map does not have an associated .nav file, the Hostages will revert to their legacy behavior system.\n\n\n\nModels\n\nThe new hostage system uses models HostageA.mdl, HostageB.mdl, HostageC.mdl, and HostageD.mdl. These models are assigned via code, and override whatever hostage models were placed in the actual map.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
