(651615, 91539, 1013, 103224, 1072936800, '', 'HL.exe isnt running, but if i go into steamapps folder and delete all my games and try to re-download them, it just says like:\n\n\n\nCACHE FAILED, CRC CHECK FAILED (all the stuff fails) and it wont re-download,\n\n\n\nSo for some reason, i just cant get into any of my games, i have logged out and in many times. I am not the only person with this problem, i know about 5 other people in #steam-cs , is there any thing else i can do? i want to be able to play!\n\n__________________\n\n- RIFK', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(651638, 91539, 1013, 103224, 1072936800, '', 'OH! I just right-clicked counter-strike and went to PROPERTIES, and selected DO NOT UPDATE GAME AUTOMATICALLY, then reselected UPDATE GAME AUOTMATICALLY and as soon as i clicked on update automatically, it said:\n\n\n\n SteamProcessCall(StartLoadingCache)(0xab0013,0x16b\n\nfc04,0x16bfd0c) Failed - Failed to get content ticket\n\n__________________\n\n- RIFK', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(651717, 91539, 1013, 103226, 1072936800, '', 'This is the reason.\n\n\n\nI also get the same error now and did some searching.\n\n\n\nWhen i get the error i do a  netstat which gives me this.\n\n\n\nsteam13.steampowered.com:27038\n\n\n\nThis is the steam content server which its trying to download this new update? or whatever, it needs to contact this server. \n\n\n\nThis can be supported by the errorlog - \n\n\n\nError:CJoinGameDialog::OnSteamError() : launch game failed, with steam error:\n\n  SteamProcessCall(WaitForAppReadyToLaunch)(0xab0014\n\n,0x160fc04,0x160fd0c) failed with error 1: Failed to get valid content ticket\n\n\n\nWhich means that it connot connect to a content server.\n\n\n\nHowever when you ping this server.\n\n\n\nPinging steam13.steampowered.com [207.173.177.130] with 32 bytes of data:\n\n\n\nRequest timed out.\n\nRequest timed out.\n\nRequest timed out.\n\nRequest timed out.\n\n\n\nPing statistics for 207.173.177.130:\n\n    Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 0, Lost = 4 (100% loss),\n\n\n\nSo why dosent it try to contact another content server?\n\nWho knows.....Valve coded it...thats probably your answer.\n\n\n\nMy conlusion is that, whoever didnt update their cs from when his server WAS working, is now screwed because the server has gone down or somthing arather.\n\n\n\nIt would be great if this was in the FAQ or somthing, because their are no explainations for it (other then the hl.exe already running, which isnt the case here)\n\n\n\nThe other solution to this was to log off and on to change content servers, however this dosent work as i get the same content server every time. \n\n\n\nBtw the only game that does launch is Codename Gordan\n\n\n\nMaybe if valve spent their time fixing their bad coding and software instead of creating sh*t like Codename Gordan, we wouldnt have this problem.\n\n\n\nPlease Valve, fix it for crying out loud.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(651913, 91539, 1013, 103226, 1072936800, '', 'THanks to BLooH\n\n\n\nHe posted a fix-\n\n\n\nGame currently down fix \n\nEveryone with the new problem "game is currently down. try again at another time" Just change the system clock. Mine was at 2003 and when i changed it to 2004 the games worked.\n\n\n\n\n\nMine was set at 2002 for other reasons. \n\n\n\nSEt it to 2004 and it worked.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(651942, 91539, 1013, 103227, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by mrbucket \n\nHL.exe isnt running, but if i go into steamapps folder and delete all my games and try to re-download them, it just says like:\n\n\n\nCACHE FAILED, CRC CHECK FAILED (all the stuff fails) and it wont re-download,\n\n\n\nSo for some reason, i just cant get into any of my games, i have logged out and in many times. I am not the only person with this problem, i know about 5 other people in #steam-cs , is there any thing else i can do? i want to be able to play!  \n\n\n\ni also cannot get into counter-strike, i can play it at first and then after a day , i don\'t know why, i cannot get into the game, so i remove steam and try to reinstall it. after i reinstall Steam and i cannot download ANY GAME except codename gordon and dedicated sever. and at the errorlogs , it said "Failed to get valid content ticket" i don\'t know why , my cdkey had been registered and cannot use again. i don\'t know what to do now~', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(651958, 91539, 1013, 103228, 1072936800, '', 'Cheers 311 - worked a treat\n\nAlthough couldn\'t Stream create a easily accessible FAQ to deal with any client side problems like this \n\nAt the FAQ only says "Check your net connection / check open ports / check the steam server status" - maybe Steam could add a link on this FAQ answer to less common problems which could be the cause?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
