(662008, 92542, 1013, 102449, 1072936800, '', 'You by any chance receiving memory errors such as those mentioned in this thread: /forums/...threadid=92462. (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=92462.)\n\n\n\nIt seems to be the same problem I\'m receiving, but I\'m rather oblivious as to what I can do to rectify the issue.  If I do find anything, I\'ll let you know.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667876, 93320, 1005, 103231, 1072936800, 'Valve!! Are You Reading This?', 'http://www.esportsea.com/index.php?...tent&id=940 (http://www.esportsea.com/index.php?s=esports&d=content&id=940)\n\n\n\nProbably THE BEST article on how CS has changed.  I seriously think Valve should read this and see what they have done.  Don\'t you see valve?  It\'s not just the people who whine in the Steam forums, it\'s the PEOPLE (CAL-I) who made YOUR game WHAT IT IS TODAY.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667888, 93320, 1005, 103232, 1072936800, '', 'I saw it at gotfrag.  Read it, good article. Everyone read it right now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667897, 93320, 1005, 103231, 1072936800, '', 'This is the last paragraph of the article, and I think the most important at which Valve should at least skim through, which they wont.  Because my idea is that all they care about now is money, "screw the eSports" they say....\n\n\n\n"That\'s also why NiP-X3 will remain the best competitive game in CS of all time, it used a more skilled game version and had the two undisputed best teams of each continent facing off in one of the closest matches ever witnessed. Don\'t expect to see another NiP-X3 worthy faceoff, don\'t expect to see HeatoN ace another top 12 team on an eco and don\'t expect to see extreme long term roster stability in the face of an ever reduced skill gap. It\'s not longer a question of evolution but instead of adaption. "', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667900, 93320, 1005, 103233, 1072936800, '', 'CAL-I ? wth ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667915, 93320, 1005, 103231, 1072936800, '', 'yes roach, see, it goes like this, most of the people who attend CPL, are CAL-I, or at equivalent skill.  Those are the people who are playing this game 5 hours a day.  The ones that got people like Frank Nuccio to create a CS division of CPL and bring in a hell of a lot more people and publicity into the game.  And all the CAL-I players made it famous back when it was good (cs 1.3)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
