(667938, 93320, 1005, 103233, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by PubIz0rs \n\nyes roach, see, it goes like this, most of the people who attend CPL, are CAL-I, or at equivalent skill.  Those are the people who are playing this game 5 hours a day.  The ones that got people like Frank Nuccio to create a CS division of CPL and bring in a hell of a lot more people and publicity into the game.  And all the CAL-I players made it famous back when it was good (cs 1.3)  \n\n\n\n\n\nOke cool [] thanks for explaining []\n\n\n\nCpl is a kinda lan right ? =/  \n\n\n\ni play cs for 4 years orso now and i dont know what cpl is :P i hear all pro players go play there or something.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(667940, 93320, 1005, 103235, 1072936800, '', 'LOL, valve read??? check this shiznat out\n\n\n\nhttp://www.forumplanet.com/counters...amp;tid=1336055 (http://www.forumplanet.com/counterstrike/topic.asp?fid=4954&tid=1336055)\n\n\n\nnow i see where cliffe does polls rofl', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668209, 93320, 1005, 101793, 1072936800, '', 'The best of the best attend at the CPL. The winners make BIG $$$.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668224, 93320, 1005, 103124, 1072936800, 'Valve!! Are You Reading This?', 'quote:Originally posted by PubIz0rs \n\nit\'s the PEOPLE (CAL-I) who made YOUR game WHAT IT IS TODAY.  Could somebody please explain to me what that means?  Do you somehow seriously have the delusional belief that this game wouldn\'t exist if it wasn\'t for "pros?"  Get real.\n\n\n\nAs for the article, it seems to be saying the game is too easy.quote:it used a more skilled game version and had the two undisputed best teams of each continent facing off in one of the closest matches ever witnessed.Is that the argument that you guys are trying to make?\n\n\n\nAnd now, to provide a link of my own: http://www.gamespy.com/articles/489....html?fromint=1 (http://www.gamespy.com/articles/489/489731p3.html?fromint=1)\n\n\n\nNumber 2 is the one that\'s most relevant in this case.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668268, 93320, 1005, 100065, 1072936800, '', 'Leagues do have that choice to revert back to 1.3. It has been released for Steam. They at any time can put that in as standard and you can all go back to when the game needed "skill."\n\n\n\nIf I\'m not mistaken, I didn\'t really read through the whole thing as it was just boring league team talk but they didn\'t really specify what decreased the skill gap except for that small mention of fixing bunny hopping.\n\n\n\nFrom what I read, people took their tactics from league demos so the teams got screwed on that. So all that was left was individual fighting. There\'s nothing there for Valve to read on what needs fixing. Quote something out if I missed it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668620, 93320, 1005, 103236, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve played CS for several years, and I never heard of CAL or whatever until I joined this forum...\n\n\n\nThis game wasn\'t made for the pro\'s it was made for players...that someone turned it into a matchevent also, is okay and all, but that is not why the game exist....\n\n\n\nActually you would have to blame the "pros" and "leet" players for the game being fixed...\n\n\n\nIf it wasn\'t for all those leet players who used bunyyjumping, bunnyjumping would not need to be fixed and the lame delay that happens when you land after jumping would not exist today.\n\n\n\nIf "leet" players had not abused the quickswitch and AWM, there would not have been made a fix for it..\n\n\n\netc etc....from my personal experience, I would say that if anything, leet players ruined the game...not Valve....\n\n\n\nBut that\'s just me...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668659, 93320, 1005, 103237, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Last Soul Reape \n\nI\'ve played CS for several years, and I never heard of CAL or whatever until I joined this forum...\n\n\n\nThis game wasn\'t made for the pro\'s it was made for players...that someone turned it into a matchevent also, is okay and all, but that is not why the game exist....\n\n\n\nActually you would have to blame the "pros" and "leet" players for the game being fixed...\n\n\n\nIf it wasn\'t for all those leet players who used bunyyjumping, bunnyjumping would not need to be fixed and the lame delay that happens when you land after jumping would not exist today.\n\n\n\nIf "leet" players had not abused the quickswitch and AWM, there would not have been made a fix for it..\n\n\n\netc etc....from my personal experience, I would say that if anything, leet players ruined the game...not Valve....\n\n\n\nBut that\'s just me...  \n\n\n\nWOW is all I can say, you are very ignorant for this reason: it\'s not an exploit, or cheating or abuse IF THE GAME ALLOWS IT, it is called being smart, and using everything you can do (without downloading hacks) to your advantage.  WOW', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668668, 93320, 1005, 103235, 1072936800, '', 'wow you must live under a rock lol.\n\n\n\nIt\'s not the pros who have ruined the game.  Look at some of the stuff that is taking place before thin summers CPL.  Players are getting signed for $40,000 a year.  Esports is becoming a viable career and a possibility for some.  Players are getting annoyed because the game is becoming slower and slower.  I don\'t have a problem with the recent fixes, and I think the pro gamers are dealing with it as well.  Your so called "leet" players didnt ruin the game.  Cause if I\'m not mistaken I\'ve yet to see a "leet" player run around with a shield.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(668686, 93320, 1005, 103238, 1072936800, '', '"As I said before basically CS is going to be interesting now since the skill gap is reduced and yet that is arguably the most important factor followed by teamplay issues. The future isn\'t super organised teamplay from hours of practice combined with meticulously thought out tactics, instead it\'s roster changing until you have the best 5 skill players available to you, working with them to establish some sembelence of teamplay and then applying some of the myriad of tactics available for you to download. Rinse and repeat until CS is dead. Not only did competitive CS devolve but there is nowhere for it to evolve to. Thanks once again Valve software for the software equivalent of inbreeding the CS family tree until future generations lacked thumbs and higher brain functions."\n\n\n\n"The skill gap is shrinking with every update"\n\n\n\nAnd that is what MANY of us have been claiming for a long time.  April 28th update was just another of these de-evoloving updates.\n\n\n\nin the article they point out that the skill gap has been shrinking since the jump to 1.4.  yet another point i have stuck by since its release.\n\n\n\nnice one valve..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(671748, 93743, 1013, 103239, 1072936800, 'Host_Error: UserMsg: Not Present on Client XXX', 'Hrmmmm lets see here, connect to a server, play for like 30 seconds, get disconnected, look in my console for the reason and i get a statement like this\n\n\n\nHost_Error: UserMsg: Not Present on Client XXX\n\n     xxx being different numbers all the time. \n\n\n\n\n\ni\'ve tried opening all the tcp and udp ports need for cs, even though its pointless im not runnign a server.\n\n\n\nwow i really hate steam, gg random HS factor, lets go back to 1.1 where things worked...\n\n\n\nplz and thx can some one help ? have a match this week.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(671855, 93743, 1013, 103239, 1072936800, '', 'please help upupup', '127.0.0.1', 1),
