(672793, 93743, 1013, 103239, 1072936800, '', 'new one \n\n\n\nHost_Error: CL_Parse_Version: Server is protocol -1996361121 instead of 4\n\n\n\n\n\nHost_Error: DispatchUserMsg:  User Msg CZCareer/130 sent too much data (195 bytes), 192 bytes max', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673496, 93743, 1013, 103240, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve been getting these same errors. I can\'t figure out why all of a sudden when i\'ve been able to play just fine for the past  6 months and now i get these damn errors. I tried reinstalling counter-strike and steam to find that the error still existed. WTF valve?!? I think that if you can tell us what the problem is you should be able to tell us how to fix it. I mean cmon damnit get on the ball.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674081, 93743, 1013, 100745, 1072936800, '', 'I just started getting these errors tonight. I\'ve never had them before, in three years of playing CS. Can anyone explain how to fix this?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBAD:   13:svc_bad\n\nWrote erroneous message to buffer.dat\n\nHost_Error: UserMsg: Not Present on Client 194', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674098, 93743, 1013, 100745, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, I figured out how to fix this error. Apparently it has to do with recently upgrading my Linksys firmware. Weather this is Steams fault, or Linksys\'s is debatable. I\'m sure there won\'t be a fix anytime soon, so just roll back your Linksys firmware if you\'re getting this error.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
