(722789, 93743, 1013, 103245, 1072936800, '', 'Heres the Dec 13th 2002 firmware for the BEFSR41 version 1 & 2. It also supports some other ones that are in the release notes. Use at your own risk.\n\n\n\nhttp://mrpips.shackspace.com/befsr-fw-1442z.zip (http://mrpips.shackspace.com/befsr-fw-1442z.zip)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(727054, 93743, 1013, 103246, 1072936800, '', 'can you give me the old firmware for the BEFSR81 version 3?  plz thanks if u do', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(729389, 93743, 1013, 103247, 1072936800, '', 'Hey, thanks for that old firmware, but i wanted to ask people using the Linksys BEFSR41 if they\'ve ever had problems with the router dropping the internet connection? my router was fine until a couple of months ago when it began to just randomly drop the internet connection...and i\'d have to reset the router atleast 3 times a day..and sometimes i\'d even have to reset the modem itself. I\'ve asked linksys numerous times about this problem and all they have been able to tell me is that upgrading the firmware will fix the problem....even though i have always kept my firmware up to date.\n\n\n\nanywho if anyone knows anything about this problem or experiences somewhat of the same thing....lemme know if theres a fix or something before i take a baseball bat to my router and purchase a new one []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673495, 93752, 1013, 100279, 1072936800, '', 'quote:12 - Weapons being seen through walls \n\nComment: Sometimes if the wall is thin enough and your weapon is long enough the opponent on the other side can see your weapon through the door/wall. (This is if you are close enough to the door) \n\n\n\n13 - Models being seen through walls \n\nComment: The same thing as with the weapons but with models instead of them. A well known example is the one where you are sitting down(ducking) in the yellow house with your [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] hanging out through the wall. (The yellow house in the main bombspot on de_nuke) \n\n\n\nThese are basically unfixable right now.  They occur because models are clipping through the walls because collusion hulls don\'t actually cover the entire model + gun.  And if they did, it would make movement very awkward and difficult because you\'d get caught on everything, not be able to get very close to walls, etc.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673691, 93752, 1013, 100117, 1072936800, '', 'Maybe they were kidnapped! Buh Bum Buuuuuhm... \n\n\n\nor not', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673765, 93752, 1013, 100323, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by tricksta189 \n\ncan you be more specific  \n\n\n\nSure.\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n\n\ncrosshair customization\n\ncl_corpse_stay\n\nplayer turning right hitbox behavior\n\nbrass ejection behavior\n\nhud_draw 0 \n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\nFlashlight sound \n\ntext behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\nRound timer behavior\n\nOther hitbox improvements', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673789, 93752, 1013, 103248, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nSure.\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n\n\ncrosshair customization\n\ncl_corpse_stay\n\nplayer turning right hitbox behavior\n\nbrass ejection behavior\n\nhud_draw 0 \n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\nFlashlight sound \n\ntext behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\nRound timer behavior\n\nOther hitbox improvements  \n\n\n\ncliffe, will we ever get the drop grenades on death modification to cs as well?  It would be very useful in matches and scrims.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673796, 93752, 1013, 102793, 1072936800, '', 'cliffe i think you know all the bugs there are that need to be fixed, to be honest.\n\n\n\ni mean, the guy who wrote that excellent bug list and you gave him some free goodies - those are pretty much all the bugs that exist in CS right now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(673969, 93752, 1013, 103249, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nSure.\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n\n\ncrosshair customization\n\ncl_corpse_stay\n\nplayer turning right hitbox behavior\n\nbrass ejection behavior\n\nhud_draw 0 \n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\nFlashlight sound \n\ntext behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\nRound timer behavior\n\nOther hitbox improvements  \n\n\n\nyay!!!!ty cliffe, any idea on when it will come out?this week,next week?also what is brass ejection behavior', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674037, 93752, 1013, 103250, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nSure.\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n\n\ncrosshair customization\n\ncl_corpse_stay\n\nplayer turning right hitbox behavior\n\nbrass ejection behavior\n\nhud_draw 0 \n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\nFlashlight sound \n\ntext behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\nRound timer behavior\n\nOther hitbox improvements  \n\n\n\n\n\nIt\'s great to see you posting, will there be any fixes on the suddon fps issues that several people have seemed to have lately? (ME being one of them)\n\n\n\nIt is NOT my fault because i can run warcraft3 just fine, thanks if you reply[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674043, 93752, 1013, 100186, 1072936800, '', 'brass ejection behavior update means:\n\nthey are going to make the awp/scout casings eject from the right side, or they are going to get rid of casing ejection all together, a la condtion zero', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674058, 93752, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'The sad thing is: Valve might actually fix all these bugs and all we will be left to complain about is the AWP & Shield and at which time we will all probably get moved to the Source Engine anyway and have to start the bug hunt / removal process from scratch all over again! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674103, 93752, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nSure.\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n\n\ncrosshair customization\n\ncl_corpse_stay\n\nplayer turning right hitbox behavior\n\nbrass ejection behavior\n\nhud_draw 0 \n\nScope blackout drawn in software mode\n\nFlashlight sound \n\ntext behavior in top-right corner of observer mode\n\nRound timer behavior\n\nOther hitbox improvements\n\nThe thing about the brass ejection is that it should be part of the weapon model (v_model). If you use custom skins, you\'ll notice some of the better replacements have a shell casing. This would allow for perfect brass ejection. You would never see the brass come out from the wrong side. The shell casing gets mirrored along with the model.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674112, 93752, 1013, 102573, 1072936800, '', 'quote:8 - Flying boxes.\n\nComment: Why not fix both of the flying boxes instead of one? (de_nuke). And what about the flying box on de_cbble? See: http://teamgt.mystic.net.nz/~cease/bug.jpg (http://teamgt.mystic.net.nz/~cease/bug.jpg) \n\nthat\'s a mapping issue, if every box were touching the ground then the r_speeds would be higher. so everything isn\'t completely connected', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674129, 93752, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'Todays computers should be more than capable of handling high r_speeds. The maximum r_speeds that are enforced for and official CS map are (now) relatively low.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674139, 93752, 1013, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by I2o[G]uE TacT-X \n\nTodays computers should be more than capable of handling high r_speeds. The maximum r_speeds that are enforced for and official CS map are (now) relatively low.  \n\n\n\nYou would think that, but look at the massive amounts of complaints about the latest version of Aztec!\n\n\n\nIt ran fine on my computer too!\n\n\n\nThat didn\'t stop the complaints flooding in though did it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(674243, 93752, 1013, 100962, 1072936800, '', 'SILENCE! \n\n\n\n\n\nNOT SCILENCE', '127.0.0.1', 1),
