(676991, 94346, 1005, 102576, 1072936800, '', 'wowowow u beat me to it.. i was just about to post this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(679637, 94732, 1026, 103261, 1072936800, 'Server getting bad spikes after Update', 'Okay so I have three servers (2 CS and 1 CZ) running on my box.  I updated all the servers last night once the udpate came out.  Since then only one of the servers is experiencing issues where it will play fine for a while then all of a sudden everyone will freeze for about 5-10 seconds then it will go back to being okay but a minute or so later it will do that again.  \n\n\n\nI have disabled all the plugins (like metamod and amxx) but the issue still happens.  Funny thing is how the other two servers will fun just fine.  I even tried coping the entire directory structure from one of the working servers to the non working one but that didn\'t fix anything.\n\n\n\nAnyone else seeing issues like this?\n\n\n\n\n\n(Server specs Dual Xeon 2.6ghz, 2 gigs PC2700, SATA 10000RPM Hard drive, T3 connections)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680003, 94732, 1026, 100469, 1072936800, '', 'That just doesn\'t make sense to me :\\ How are you making sure the other 2 server instances are spike free when the other one spikes? Also, can you tell me the memory usage for each one, and the amount it uses upon starting up, i.e. 60MB. Disabled plugins, meaning using mp.dll for gamedll file? Really from what you say, the only thing different would either be the server ip\'s, or the port it is running on. Which one is piking, one of the cs or the cz? If it is CZ...........then it is CZ. I think atleast, lots of said about CZ servers and people getting booted out of nowhere. Not sure if this happens with CS though, haven\'t played that game since cz came out []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680029, 94732, 1026, 103261, 1072936800, '', 'How am I checking....well I got people on each of the servers and they aren\'t spiking when I am spiking on the other.\n\n\n\nYes using mp.dll for the server when I disabled everything (but that didn\'t help so I went back to metamod)\n\n\n\nMemory usage depends on how many people on in there but typical is about 60 like you said maybe a lil more\n\n\n\nEach server runs on a different port\n\n\n\nTrouble server is on 27015  the other two are one 27016 and 27017.\n\n\n\nIts a CS 1.6 server that is having issues.\n\n\n\nDidn\'t start till the recent update.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680047, 94732, 1026, 103262, 1072936800, '', 'Hey we have the same problem with our 2 servers, and i have noticed it happens when more than 1 player connects the server and u can see them in specmode .... it�s not lag it closes the connection ...\n\n\n\nWe have never had problems before .... with the servers\n\n\n\nEach server is :\n\n\n\nBarton 2500 \n\n512 PC 3200 Ram\n\nConnection 30 mbit each way ...\n\n\n\nAll happenened after updating ... \n\n\n\nSoultaker', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680059, 94732, 1026, 103261, 1072936800, '', 'yeh a friend of mine that has a couple servers is noticing it too.  He disabled all his plugins as well but still had the issue.  You are right that there has to be more than 1 in the server...if I went in my server alone and just ran around there was no lag spikes at all but once someone connected...BAM lag spike...its more of a freeze than a lag spike though as everyone is jsut frozen like the game locked up or something.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680069, 94732, 1026, 103263, 1072936800, '', 'we are suffering the same problem as are a number of other servers.  The HLDS mailing list has a number of complaints on it too.\n\n\n\nFine before the steam update.  Afterwards, you get lag spikes lasting upto 5 seconds periodically. Bandwidth isnt a problem and cpu  use is not an issue.\n\n\n\nAgain, we see them all in spec mode too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680092, 94732, 1026, 103261, 1072936800, '', 'DoubleDoom can you keep this thread updated from what is said on the hlds mailing list for us []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680121, 94732, 1026, 103263, 1072936800, '', 'will do.  At the moment it is just server admins complaining of this exact problem.  No feedback or solutions.  Not much info offered.\n\n\n\nHowever, it does appear to be effecting custom maps rather than defaults and 32 player servers mostly.\n\n\n\nedit. although just as i say that, ours does another 5 second spike on dust2 and read another post from someone that says their server only runs default maps.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680131, 94732, 1026, 103261, 1072936800, '', 'I just got reports that our 2nd cs server is having issues now too.  We run default maps only and 21 max people (1 reserved slot)\n\n\n\nI hope there is a fix soon', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680166, 94732, 1026, 103263, 1072936800, '', 'here is a sample of posts in the last 30 minutes\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:  >> many of our servers are showing problems with a big lag spike every\n\n>> 10min or\n\n>> so\n\n>> this spike has a few smaller spikes then one lasting for approx 5 sec\n\n>> where\n\n>> everything freezes.\n\n>>\n\n>> the server then returns to normal, it isn\'t cpu causing it because it is\n\n>> fine\n\n>\n\n>\n\n> Yeah I am seeing this too.\n\n \n\n\n\nquote: Same here... this isn\'t good. []\n\n \n\n\n\nquote:Im trying to find out if anyone else is having issues since the last patch,\n\n\n\nmany of our servers are showing problems with a big lag spike every 10min or\n\nso\n\nthis spike has a few smaller spikes then one lasting for approx 5 sec where\n\neverything freezes.\n\n\n\nthe server then returns to normal, it isn\'t cpu causing it because it is\n\nfine\n\n\n\nit is happing more on our larger servers.\n\n\n\n\n\nKingsley\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nquote:Same here. Terrible CPU spiking for about 1 minute. And the server almost\n\nirresponsive.\n\n\n\nVery bad.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nquote: Hi,\n\n\n\nI have this problem too, on some map, official, I have freeze of 5/15\n\nseconds.\n\n\n\nPls help us Valve, or recall this update :-/\n\n\n\nFinger', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680428, 94732, 1026, 103264, 1072936800, '', 'same problem for me but after removing metamod and everything the spike seem to disapear :|', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681319, 94732, 1026, 103265, 1072936800, '', 'Same thing here although I\'m on linux not windows dedicated.  No mods. Server is healthy but each CS instance lags like hell now and again. Smokeping, process load and traffic graphs all good.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681390, 94732, 1026, 100469, 1072936800, '', 'I would say while testing this to ensure mp.dll is being used on all servers. There have been reports of memory leaks directly with metamod, and who knows what the new versions of metamod can do now. Also, are you using the same server.cfg settings, excluding the obvious different things i.e. name, rcon pw, etc...Basically, the settings relating to the maxrate, updaterate, etc...they are they same on all 3 server instances? This situation is very hard to troubleshoot since it is on the same box with same bandwidth connection. Instead of copying another folder of a non-spiking server, try making a new folder, updating directly with hldsupdatetool, and make new configs, change port, and start up and see. I\'ve had some strange problems before and that was the only way to fix them - copying another server\'s folder, redoing configs, etc, didn\'t work for some things.\n\n\n\nAlso, can you have a pingplotter running in the background while servers are up, from www.pingplotter.com (http://www.pingplotter.com) ? Get that, run it for a long time, a day straight or something, have a few running and pingplotting to different locations. See what yields.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681431, 94732, 1026, 103266, 1072936800, '', 'Same problems here, running a complete plugin free windows dedicated.\n\n\n\nThank god I had a backup of the DLL\'s (from before the last update) \n\n\n\nValve, now it\'s your turn, i guess', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681627, 94732, 1026, 103263, 1072936800, '', 'the linux hlds have had posts that suggest that reverting to the previous binary fixes it.\n\n\n\nHas anyone got a copy of the previous version mp.dll? We could try that out and see if it acts as a temporary fix until valve fix the problem\n\n\n\nedit.  Should have read the above post.   Can you make that dll available for us to download somewhere please?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(679945, 94773, 1026, 100195, 1072936800, 'CPU usage goes to 99% since last update', 'Ever since I updated our server last night, the cpu usage shoots up to over 90% and the game becomes unplayable.\n\n\n\nPlease tell me that Valve is working on this and will have it resolved within the next 12 hours. I\'m running one 20 player game on a p4 3.0 with a gig of dual channel ram and it can\'t handle 14 people right now\n\n\n\nOnly a couple of maps are playing with dust2 being one of them.\n\n\n\nI do not see how people running multiple servers will be able to keep their machines up for much longer.\n\n\n\n\n\nCliffe? Any word on this issue?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681265, 94773, 1026, 103267, 1072936800, '', 'Im experiencing the same thing on my NS 3.0 server.  Since the last update it went from handling 28 players with a 70-80% load to holding MAYBE 14-16 players with 99-100% load.  Its horrible.\n\n\n\nMind you this box is:\n\n\n\nDual Xeon 2.4 w/ Hyperthreading\n\n2 GB DDR RAM', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681336, 94773, 1026, 102533, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ViolentKoRn \n\nIm experiencing the same thing on my NS 3.0 server.  Since the last update it went from handling 28 players with a 70-80% load to holding MAYBE 14-16 players with 99-100% load.  Its horrible.\n\n\n\nMind you this box is:\n\n\n\nDual Xeon 2.4 w/ Hyperthreading\n\n2 GB DDR RAM  \n\n\n\nThe problem with that statement is that the engine files werent even touched.\n\n\n\nBack to the CS topic, we are experiencing these lag issues as well and so are many more on the Linux mailing list.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681450, 94773, 1026, 103263, 1072936800, '', 'and it effects windows servers as well.  There are similar threads in the windows server forum as well', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681493, 94773, 1026, 103267, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LaMersSs \n\nThe problem with that statement is that the engine files werent even touched.\n\n\n\nBack to the CS topic, we are experiencing these lag issues as well and so are many more on the Linux mailing list. \n\n\n\nIm not sure what changed to cause this issue.  I know its affected that NS server and one of my other CS servers.  Suddenly they go from working flawless to barely being able to run.  Nothing changed in their configuration.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681515, 94773, 1026, 102533, 1072936800, '', 'Wondering how you managed to squeeze on a 28 man on a xeon 2.4 :\\\n\nLast attempts with a MP 2.4 failed at 14-16 players (and yes this was before the update).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681526, 94773, 1026, 103267, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve run quite a few 28 player servers on a 2.4 Xeon.  Our community runs 3 28 player servers on two dual 2.4 xeon boxes and 1 p4 2.8 box.  Up until the last patch it ran fine.  I know for a fact a 2.4 Xeon should run a NS 3.0 server past 16 players.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(684533, 94773, 1026, 103268, 1072936800, '', 'I also have this problem on a Debian server. Until the last update, everything went smoothly with 24 players.  Since the last update, we experience terrible slow downs (generally at the beginning of maps), even with less than 10 connected players. It seems to be more map-related than player number-related.\n\n\n\nAlso, as said in another thread, HLTV does not work anymore.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(685759, 94773, 1026, 103269, 1072936800, '', 'Yup, same problem here.  Fedora Core 2, 2.8ghz P4, 1 Gig of RAM.\n\n\n\nI\'m running 2 18 player CS 1.6 servers, and they randomly spike the CPU up to 99%.  \n\n\n\nHorrible.  \n\n\n\nI take it there is no fix to this, other than quit hosting servers?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687118, 94773, 1026, 103270, 1072936800, '', 'I too am a Linux server operator. Since the patch our server is non playable. I have shut it down because it is like seeing a horse who has broken its ankle hobble around. Please STEAM DEV TEAM, fix this issue. \n\n\n\nOut of curiosity what is everyones current versions, I am at\n\n\n\nCounter-Strike Base Content and Linux Server Engine version 11 \n\n\n\nand\n\n\n\n\'Half-Life Base Content\' version 7\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJarvis.\n\n\n\n\n\nPS- Are all linux server seeing this?? I can\'t believe we the only ones.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687183, 94773, 1026, 103271, 1072936800, '', 'RH 7.3\n\n2.4 kernel\n\nAthlon 2200+\n\n\n\nSame problem.  I saw it happen on de_inferno and cs_siege.  Other maps have been played since and I haven\'t seen the problem for a couple hours.\n\n\n\nI did disable my bot plugin AND statsme.  The bot plugin didn\'t have anything to do with it.  Statsme MAY have.  Im not really sure.  Is anyone else with these problems using statsme 2.8.0.15?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687185, 94773, 1026, 103270, 1072936800, '', 'I see the windows lads have a work around for this, does anyone have any pre patch files for us Linux folks??\n\n\n\nDon\'t let these workarounds excuse your duties STEAM DEV TEAM haha []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687196, 94773, 1026, 103271, 1072936800, '', 'The workaround would probably be to go back to the previous binaries.\n\n\n\nI have a backup server that hasnt been updated.  If people knew what files were required, I would be willing to share.\n\n\n\nThe only negative is its all a big waste of time if Steam issues another update that fixes the problem.\n\n\n\nI tried to update my servers to see if there was another update released, but of course it\'s having problems and telling me all of my accounts are invalid or connection reset.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687215, 94773, 1026, 103270, 1072936800, '', 'Windows folks call it mp_dll not sure what ours would be. But Mug please don\'t update your other server haha you may be our only hope [] I will see if I cannot locate the files we need. Hopefully others will too.\n\n\n\nJarvis\n\n\n\nPS- I got ladies that will soon be hot if we don\'t get this resolved haha', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687552, 94773, 1026, 101507, 1072936800, '', 'Same problem here only it\'s very spuratic.  I\'m only having a problem on my 3000+ box 64 bit with a 32 bit Fedora core 1 loaded.  Dunno what the issue is.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680732, 94880, 1005, 103272, 1072936800, 'Original CS Weapon Names', 'A while ago I got my hand on a patch that would revert the CS weapon names back to what they used to be before Steam. Does anyone know where I could get this again?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680745, 94880, 1005, 103273, 1072936800, '', 'http://files.filefront.com/1896333;..._and_Utilities/ (http://files.filefront.com/1896333;/pub2/Counter_Strike/Tools_and_Utilities/)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680902, 94880, 1005, 103272, 1072936800, '', 'hmm, before I had an .exe file this is just a .txt file. Where does it go? I searched for another copy to overwrite but there isn\'t one.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680931, 94880, 1005, 103273, 1072936800, '', 'Place the file in this folder \n\nC:Program FilesSteamSteamAppsyouremailcounter-strikecstrike esource', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680949, 94880, 1005, 103274, 1072936800, '', 'where is esources????', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680964, 94880, 1005, 103273, 1072936800, '', '**they mean RESOURCE folder', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680970, 94880, 1005, 103274, 1072936800, '', 'ok so then where do i put it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680971, 94880, 1005, 103275, 1072936800, '', 'you can get it from http://www.bobsbunker.net (http://www.bobsbunker.net)\n\nThe file is called titles.txt and inside this file are all the names for diffrent stuff in CS as the weapons names you can eiter make this file yourself or download it and since it seems you have no skill in this department I suggest you just download it..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681134, 94880, 1005, 103003, 1072936800, '', 'www.saiyanhighlife.com/rtg/?rtg=fixes (http://www.saiyanhighlife.com/rtg/?rtg=fixes) (yes that is my site and yes I made those fixes using old CS 1.5 files [].)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681135, 94880, 1005, 103272, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by CLOWN_staples \n\nPlace the file in this folder \n\nC:Program FilesSteamSteamAppsyouremailcounter-strikecstrike esource  \n\n\n\nI\'m not seeing that folder... \n\n\n\n\n\nquote:you can get it from http://www.bobsbunker.net (http://www.bobsbunker.net)\n\nThe file is called titles.txt and inside this file are all the names for diffrent stuff in CS as the weapons names you can eiter make this file yourself or download it and since it seems you have no skill in this department I suggest you just download it..\n\nWhere abouts on that site? I can\'t access the downloads page, do I have to become a member to get this little .txt file?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681169, 94880, 1005, 103272, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by DiZzyBonne \n\nwww.saiyanhighlife.com/rtg/?rtg=fixes (http://www.saiyanhighlife.com/rtg/?rtg=fixes) (yes that is my site and yes I made those fixes using old CS 1.5 files [].)  \n\n\n\nCool, that\'ll work.. although those aren\'t exactly the weapon names I was looking for there better then CS1.6 weapon names.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681257, 94880, 1005, 103276, 1072936800, '', 'I have a custom titles.txt on my site in the scripts section, URL is in my sig.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681781, 94880, 1005, 103277, 1072936800, '', 'the titles.txt only fixes the old style text menus.\n\nif you prefer to use the vgui menu style, you need a custom cstrike_english.txt (cstrike\\resource), wich needs a 1.6 titles.txt (that contais these # _ placeholders). custom 1.5 titles.txt causes some weird messages ingame, like "%s dropped the bomb"...\n\n\n\nso better extract the titles.txt and cstrike_english.txt from your 1.6 cache files and change the weapon names manually in these extracted files...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681860, 94880, 1005, 103276, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by -3dg3- \n\nthe titles.txt only fixes the old style text menus.\n\nif you prefer to use the vgui menu style, you need a custom cstrike_english.txt (cstrike\\resource), wich needs a 1.6 titles.txt (that contais these # _ placeholders). custom 1.5 titles.txt causes some weird messages ingame, like "%s dropped the bomb"...\n\n\n\nso better extract the titles.txt and cstrike_english.txt from your 1.6 cache files and change the weapon names manually in these extracted files...  \n\n\n\nMy titles.txt addresses the "%s dropped the bomb" issue.\n\n\n\nIt is highly customized, and I think experienced players will like it more than the conventional text. Read all about my customizations and see screenshots here:\n\n\n\nhttp://members.cox.net/noshelter/tutorials.htm#three (http://members.cox.net/noshelter/tutorials.htm#three)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(681869, 94880, 1005, 100579, 1072936800, '', 'I have a fixed titles.txt, so that when a player drops the bomb, the players name is shown and not \'% dropped the bomb\'.\n\n\n\nThis is the best titles.txt right now\n\nhttp://home.online.no/~ovassend/titles.txt (http://home.online.no/~ovassend/titles.txt)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680915, 94910, 1005, 103278, 1072936800, 'ds updates... are there any?', 'have there EVER been ne ds updates?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680950, 94910, 1005, 100418, 1072936800, 'DS', 'Just a small fix for a few bugs on 1.1 I think...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(680968, 94910, 1005, 100418, 1072936800, 'DS', 'I mean when CZ updated to 1.1, I think they fixed a few issues causing DS to crash, other than that, just the standard HL.exe updates apply.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(684066, 94910, 1005, 100323, 1072936800, '', 'We\'ll be releasing some of the "lost" DS maps over time.\n\n\n\nCliffe\n\nVALVe', '127.0.0.1', 1),
