(684056, 95222, 1013, 100357, 1072936800, 'Scheduled Maintenance Downtime Tonight -->', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nScheduled Maintenance Downtime\n\n \n\nTonight at approximately 6:00 pm PST Steam will be down for scheduled server maintenance. Steam games will not be available for a short time thereafter (probably about half an hour). News will be posted here as soon as the maintenance work is complete. Thanks for your patience. \n\n\n\nCool stuff.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(684412, 95222, 1013, 103289, 1072936800, '?', 'not cool stuff i mean everything works fine till this update man everything. steam u better help me fix this b/c like every other day I am trying 2 get steam 2 work. its a complete joke. i already tried deleting files and etc. help me i can\'t connect', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(684462, 95222, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Daniel you have to wait a while. If it says that steam cant connect it cant. Just be patient man. I live in TX too and Im not having a problem at all. \n\n\n\nAnd yea this has to be the least contraversial update in a long long time. (other than DoD, where the people are happy about every update, unlike some other communities.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683756, 95261, 1013, 100323, 1072936800, 'Steam Client, HLDS Update Released', 'An update to the Steam client and HLDS update tool has just been released. Steam will update itself automatically when you restart. Here is a list of the changes:\n\n\n\n\n\nSTEAM CLIENT CHANGES / ADDITIONS:\n\n\n\nSteam will now generate a recipt when you purchase a product, instead of sending it via e-mail \n\nRemoved email verification \n\nAll Steam error messages are now localized \n\nImproved offline behavior if no SteamUI.dll or Steam.dll present \n\nImproved content server responsiveness \n\nDisabled background preloaders when any game is running \n\nPreloader checks to see if an item will fit in the cache (improves going offline) \n\nImproved behavior of content "tickets" (thrown out if system clock more than 4 weeks off) \n\nImproved loading progress bar time calculation \n\nImproved startup speed of Steam \n\nImproved responsiveness of user cancel \n\nChanged legal characters in new account names to only be \'a\'-\'z\', \'A\'-\'Z\', \'0\'-\'9\', and \'_\' \n\n\n\nHLDS UPDATE TOOL CHANGES / ADDITIONS:\n\n\n\n\n\nAdded "-retry" flag -- auto-retry to get content every 30 seconds', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683759, 95261, 1013, 103291, 1072936800, '', 'awesome, but it appears that the forums dont utalize html', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683778, 95261, 1013, 100279, 1072936800, '', 'Could you explain what any of these will do?  A lot of them sound like they will affect users, but it\'s all in techspeak.  []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683782, 95261, 1013, 100414, 1072936800, '', 'You stole my words Apos :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683795, 95261, 1013, 100250, 1072936800, '', 'Very cool techspeak. \n\n\n\nFrom the sound of it, they made Steam a whole bunch better in its very complicated sounding innards.\n\n\n\nKeeping checksums of the main files is a very, very bright idea. Means Steam will actually recognise if those are corrupted now. Hooray. \n\n\n\nBig change I noticed: When you try and purchase a game, it actually tells you what games you\'ll get with that purchase. \n\n\n\nAnd you can buy Half-Life and co. over Steam with credit card now! No need to go to a shop! That said, the cost seems to be $34.95, which seems a tad steep, really.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683805, 95261, 1013, 100414, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Epsilon \n\nBig change I noticed: When you try and purchase a game, it actually tells you what games you\'ll get with that purchase. \n\n\n\nWonder why they didn\'t include that change.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683813, 95261, 1013, 100323, 1072936800, '', 'Edited.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683814, 95261, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Yea that is kinda steep but oh well. Some places dont even sell the game anymore.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683823, 95261, 1013, 100063, 1072936800, '', 'This is going to be the smoothest (sp?) Steam update ever.\n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683846, 95261, 1013, 100347, 1072936800, '', 'Impressive list.  Not sure how it all impacts us but sounds like speed and efficiency updates - much appreciated.\n\n\n\nA little bummed I still don\'t have the save password thing working when you first fire up Steam - it\'s checked but not saving.  I\'ve killed the ClientRegistry.blob file as suggested.  I\'ll hold hope for the next update for my particular issue.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683852, 95261, 1013, 100279, 1072936800, '', 'Sweet cliffe, thanks!    \n\n\n\nquote:And you can buy Half-Life and co. over Steam with credit card now! No need to go to a shop! That said, the cost seems to be $34.95, which seems a tad steep, really.\n\n\n\nDoes seem a bit steep: at least compared to what the HL pack goes for in my area, seems like there\'s no discount for the fact that you don\'t get a box or materials.  I would have thought that selling it online would be a lot cheaper than creating/shipping retail boxes.  But maybe:\n\n\n\n1) since the price has to be global, it has to be averaged out from all the sale locations (i.e. can\'t be cheaper in North Dakota than it is in New York the way it is in stores)\n\n2) Vivendi owns a cut of every sale of games it was liscenced to distribute, so Valve can\'t cut prices because it has to pay Vivendi as if it was using them to sell a retail box\n\n3) the cost for download bandwidth is roughly the same for contracting out the production of retail boxes, so there isn\'t really any money saved \n\n4) Don\'t want cheaters to be able to buy up tons and tons of accounts.\n\n5) I\'m no business guy, so what do I know?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683858, 95261, 1013, 103183, 1072936800, '', 'Great! \n\nTime to connect and update!!!\n\n<pleadingly looks at crappy modem> []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683937, 95261, 1013, 100279, 1072936800, '', 'Does "error messages localized" mean that they display in different languages?  Not that it does much for me, but that\'s pretty darn cool.  []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683993, 95261, 1013, 103292, 1072936800, '', 'That seems to be the going rate for $19.99 games thru steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(684017, 95261, 1013, 103293, 1072936800, '', 'Oh wow, now I\'m confused.\n\n\n\nNow when you register a Half-Life key on Steam, you no longer get Counter-Strike? A CZ or CS key will open up CZ and CS, while any other key will open up Half-Life, TFC, OpFor, etc. is how I understand it. So in that case, when you get around to resetting a CS CDkey I sent in, will that account have access to CS and CZ only? In that case I\'ll have to go buy a Half-Life CDkey. At a store. $35 is highway robbery on such an old game, mods or not.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(683836, 95274, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, 'Actiontec Product Users.', 'Hello, are you using an Actiontec Product and recieving errors? There are a few ways to fix this.\n\n\n\nSome of the Errors that you might be seeing are:\n\n\n\n"Bad Command Character in Client Mod."\n\n\n\n"Bad Parse in Client Command."\n\n\n\n"CMD_MAXBACKUP HIT."\n\n\n\nYou may also notice that you might be getting Disconnected more often if you are using your mic a lot.\n\n\n\nThings that we have tried in order to get these Problems resolved are:\n\n\n\nContacting Actiontec to put out a FirmWare Upgrade. From what I know the last one was I think in 2002. But I guess that they said that they are not going to do it.\n\n\n\nTrying to put the Modems into DMZ Mode.\n\n\n\nTrying to put the Modems into Transparent Bridging Mode.\n\n\n\nTrying a few other things and they did not resolve these Problems.\n\n\n\n1. Get a new ISP<----This is what I did, I now have Charter Internet.\n\n\n\n2. If your ISP is Qwest Call them and tell them that your Modem is giving you Errors while your playing online<----I did call them but instead we just got Charter Internet. However they did say that they were sending me a new Modem for free, but mine was Broke. How I think it Broke was by setting it into Transparent Bridging Mode (my Internet just went out). If they say that they wont send you a new one because of the Error go set it in Transparent Bridging Mode. If you have a day or so you might want to try this.\n\n\n\nWhat Transparent Bridging Mode is, is I guess like a Super DMZ Mode.\n\n\n\n3. If your ISP is not Qwest Call your current ISP and ask them about the Error and see if they send you a new Modem for free, if not set it in Transparent Bridging Mode.\n\n\n\n4. Buy a new Modem<----Check out your Local Computer Store(s).\n\n\n\n-ShUtY.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(689668, 95274, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, '', 'Also, to add to this Thread. If you have an Actiontec Product and are receiving errors or other Problems other then the ones I described Please let me know and I will try to see what is going on with that and try to give a Detailed Solution in this Thread.\n\n\n\nSome other things to be Aware of. If you go to www.Qwest.com (http://www.Qwest.com) and are going to try to get ahold of Actiontec make sure that you dont click on the Actiontec Phone Number. Call you ISP because Actiontec has a $29.99 Fee for calling for help.\n\n\n\nAnd when you do reach a number with someone that can help you with either getting a new Modem or trying to resolve this make sure you are very detailed. And make sure that they understand what you are trying to do or resolve.\n\n\n\n-------------------------------\n\n\n\nIf anyone else has anything to add to this thread with a Fix, a new Firmware Upgrade from Actiontec, or anything it may be Please be sure to post.\n\n\n\n-Thanks, ShUtY.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(689766, 95274, 1013, 100210, 1072936800, '', 'does the 640kb steaminstall.exe need the internet for completion. mainly to get the steam.dll file it needs and crashes on when it can\'t find it?\n\n\n\ni have a \n\nActiontec dsl/gateway modem. GT701-WG\n\nMy Isp is qwest.\n\n\n\nwed. this whole thing started with a "cannot connect to steam network".\n\nafter waiting and trying it again for about 5hrs, I uninstalled steam. \n\n\n\nNow I can\'t reinstall steam. get a \n\n"Steam.exe (main exception): unable to load library steam.dll" error.\n\n\n\nagain I do have a actiontec GT701-WG modem, however never(and I do mean never) had problems to this extent before.\n\n\n\n1CSer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(689843, 95274, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, so I\'m now thinking that the different Models of the Actiontec bring up different Errors. 1CSeroutofmany I would suggest that you call Qwest Today and then there will be a Computer telling you to Press 1 to lead you to this place and Press 2 to go to this place, (kind of like an Answering Maching on a Telephone) go to talk to someone from the Internet Service and make sure its the right place that you are talking to, I do know that when we called Qwest we got Transferd I think 2-5 times trying to get to the right place.\n\n\n\nThen tell them that you Play an Online game and you are recieving Errors because of your Actiontec. Then they will most likely help you solve it or send you a new Modem that should work just fine. If they dont just tell them your thinking about switching ISP\'s if it doesnt get resolved.\n\n\n\nThen if you need to Read off the stuff that I have posted in this Thread to them, and if they ask for a link give it to them and tell them to read the First Post in it.\n\n\n\nThat should help and hopefully you can get a new Modem Overnighted to you. Make sure you tell them your Address to send it to before they go off on their own and send it to an Address they think your at. I know that mine ended up getting sent to a Different Address so we just Switched ISP\'s because they kept sending stuff to that Address even after telling them that we dont live at that Address and giving them our correct Address.\n\n\n\n-ShUtY.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(689973, 95274, 1013, 100210, 1072936800, '', 'Well seems simple enough however. I feel a little bad calling them and requesting action, when my setup worked before the wed update. U know what I mean? the only change was steam. not my modem.\n\n\n\nnot trying to start anything here. just need to see your logic. I am thinking about calling them and asking if they made any changes in their network strucure, like updated any firmware on their end.. Multiple things could have happened (at once) on wed..  lol\n\n\n\ndo you see my logic.. ?\n\n\n\n\n\n1CSer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690974, 95274, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, '', 'It probably isnt the CS, its just that Actiontec\'s dont exept the Packet Data correctly.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(691288, 95274, 1013, 102927, 1072936800, '', 'A post from 1CSeroutofmany.\n\n\n\nquote: Figured out why I could\'nt connect to steam network!!!!!! \n\nTurns out (somehow) my DSL/router firewall settings had been changed from basic to Low!!!!!!!! have no clue how, Have in the past put in on low and tried steam, and saw it did\'nt work that way. I doubt my isp did it. \n\n\n\nI\'m concluding that my modem for some reason found that setting to be needed, and set it that way on weds upon boot up. \n\n\n\nSo if you have a Actiontec dsl/gateway modem. model GT701-WG, or any router/modem for that matter. For GT701-WG, goto (in internet browser) 192.168.0.1 and go to advanced setup, then see if your firewall is set to low or not. if so, put it to basic..\n\n\n\nam updating everything in steam, and cs now. I hope everything goes o.k.\n\n\n\nI wish I did\'nt have to put in new hdd and install xp just find this information out. but O well, whatever means to an end huh? lol\n\n\n\nthanks to any and all for help or suggestions during my time in need.. I will be sure to come back and help reinforce the idea that something(besides steam) is probably at fault.\n\n\n\nLike I said I did\'nt change my firewall setting, that just reminded me, you don\'t have to change something for something to change. lol\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n1CSer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(695796, 95274, 1013, 100210, 1072936800, '', 'hey shuty.. thanks for posting that for me man..  I did\'nt get a chance. I have so many threads open lately.. hard to keep up..  \n\n\n\nI\'ve been posting that everywhere to shed some light on other peoples problems and to give some hope for people that still can\'t connect. \n\n\n\nagain thanks for helping me out.. your a bro.. =)\n\n\n\n1CSer', '127.0.0.1', 1),
