(687213, 95654, 1013, 100117, 1072936800, 'AWP (not compaining) >unique idea<', 'I really hope that I am the first person to suggest this. If it has already been suggested then please don\'t flame me.\n\n\n\nI\'m sure all of us have seen the threads complaining about the AWP. There are atleast 30 of them, and even a petition people are signing. We come to a problem when trying to satisfy everyone. Without the delay, the beginners complain that the awp is too easy to use and people are too good with it. With the delay, skilled players complain that Steam and Valve took away their awp. \n\n\n\nIt would be very hard to satisfy both groups of people. (I\'m not taking sides here, although I do have an opinion, which I do not want to state, becuase it is irrelevent in this thread). I do, however, have an idea. It came to me about 10 minutes ago when I was on the toilet. (Sorry, I\'m gross).\n\n\n\nMy idea is this: Make the delay a server command. \n\n\n\nWhat I mean is, the person who runs/owns the server can choose whether or not they want the delay on their server. If they do, they simply do a command like "mp_awpdelay 1" or something. If they don\'t they set it to "0". Now this would solve virtually all future conflict about the awp. The beginners could play on servers with the delay, and the awp buffs could play on servers without it. I feel that everyone would get what they wanted. Plus, it is alot politer than just saying to change it back.\n\n\n\nAny constructive criticism is wanted. Feel free to brainstorm this and think of any ideas to make it better. Please post alot, becuase I want this thread to get alot of posts and stay alive so Steam or Valve will notice it. \n\n\n\nThanks, Bunze.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687255, 95654, 1013, 103232, 1072936800, '', 'I think it\'s been said to make it a command.  Also, there is a server side patch out to have the awp pre-update.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687287, 95654, 1013, 100115, 1072936800, '', 'Good idea!\n\n\n\nI hope Valve would implement this change instead, so competitive players and league has the option to keep it like the old way.\n\nI mean it\'s more pleasure to watch the old awp than the new ones...\n\n\n\nNot much action in the new awp update.\n\n\n\nI think Valve really needs to consider the players that made CS successful..\n\n\n\nThe old players that spread the word about the game.\n\n\n\nOtherwise CS wouldn\'t be what it is today..\n\n\n\nI hate to see them backstabbing the very people that made CS successful and popular.\n\n\n\n\n\nWe set the goals for the beginners, thats why they play day and night to improve, hoping to reach that level.\n\n\n\nThen you have more beginner turning into advance/good players, thus insipiring more people to dedicate the time into this game to become good.\n\n\n\nIt saddens me to a great extent that Valve no longer cares for those people.\n\n\n\nJust one update without even listing the changes, such as a big change of this is beyond breach of trust.\n\n\n\nIn previous updates, Back in beta days, Valve always list all the changes they made to the game in counter-strike.net\n\n\n\nNow they\'re too big and they don\'t want to because they don\'t need to... Just messed up the game of the people that made their game successful without a word.\n\n\n\nThis is a very good solution to fix and address the problem.\n\n\n\nAnd if Valve specifically Cliffe sees this and takes no regard...\n\n\n\nThen that tells us he doesn\'t care about the community and the players that made his game popular.\n\nJust think about it, if he doesn\'t care about the very people that made his game successful and big, then why would he care about the new people?\n\n\n\nHE DOESNT\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope gooseman was in control, because things seem a lot better when he was in control...\n\n\n\n\n\nIf they can change the awp without even listing the change, then they can constantly changes the hitbox, mess with your recoil. aim. reflexes without you even knowing..\n\nIn that case WHAT IS THE PURPOSE TO PLAY?\n\n\n\nNONE.\n\n\n\nIt\'s not fun, no goal because goals are being scrape goat by them...\n\n\n\nI hate to continue CS, my friends are the only reason I am putting up with this madness.\n\n\n\nFor those people who is going to flame my head off, understand this, one day you too will see this, I hope by then you will be able to understand people like me.\n\n\n\nWe put our valuable time into a game to get to the top, then getting messed up by Valve\'s employees and random changes without words is not a very good experience.\n\n\n\nBelieve me, one day when you reach the top of your performances, and when valve continues this stuff on you, you too will see things very clearly.\n\n\n\n\n\nValve, it\'s time to fix your game.\n\n\n\n\n\nOr you can say good bye to thousands, even millions of people who made your game what it is today.\n\nThe very own people who help tested bugs, who made CS what it is today from a low quality beta game with loads of glitches.\n\n\n\n\n\nCan you say it wasn\'t the old players of the community that made CS what it is today?\n\n\n\nI don\'t think so.\n\n\n\nA friend of mine who is basically a top awper was on his way to becoming a pro sniper with big sponsorship deal coming in..\n\n\n\nThis unotified change basically ruins the entire need and purpose of him being in the team. Thus his dream of becoming a professional CS player is over. He sacrificed many things, education, got into fights with girl friends and family just to get to the top in the game. He was specialized in AWP, he doesn\'t use other weapons much, hes not a newb in those guns, just not what makes him a special player. He was a special pro awper. Sure he could adapt, but it would hardly make him special..\n\nFor example, in Nuke RAMP. Back then he could hold against the ramp rush of 4-5 people no problem with the awp. RIght now, assuming he doesn\'t miss... He can take ONE the MOST with the awp before hes gone... That basically ruins his purpose, AWP is extremely expensive to purchase in team-game where money is critical to victory.\n\n\n\nThat is only one example. All those hours he put in goes into nothing. He retired, gone and done for good with CS. He basically cried, and it\'s not funny. Coming from a big man, seeing him all upset, angry yet helpless at the same time is not something that deserves laughing.\n\n\n\nHe sacrifice a lot to get to where he was, he ALMOST fulfilled his dream, yet one simple change ends his career, and everything he went through goes into nothing.\n\n\n\nJust nothing... How can Valve expect people to trust them and take them seriously?\n\n\n\nSimply put, awp is now weak in team-game of competitive cs.\n\n\n\nThis command suggestion will give competitive player what they want.\n\n\n\nWhy not leave the option available?\n\n\n\nI hate to see Valve becoming a weak company just because of a weak awp...\n\n\n\nI see MANY people who would be good indication of valve becoming weak, at least in the respect of those people.\n\n\n\nPeace.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(687309, 95654, 1013, 100117, 1072936800, '', 'Well, CAL would have to consider using the new/old awp. I think they would use the one without the delay but you never know. Thanks guys, and I hope more people post.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
