(690839, 95751, 1013, 103307, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by GokuSongoku \n\nYou know how many games they are working on?\n\n\n\nCS:CZ\n\nCS\n\nHL\n\nDOD\n\nCZ[]S(maybe)\n\nTFC\n\nDMC\n\nOF\n\nRicochet\n\nHL2\n\n\n\nand thats alot of games.. no wonder they are stressed and makes mistakes  \n\n\n\nWell,  Scuse me Sir,\n\n\n\nBut if you are not able to do one Thing,  Then you do not.\n\n\n\nIf they are not able to do all those things,  Well no problem, just don\'t do it.\n\n\n\nBut don\'t drive Millions people on your Own problem just because you are not able to resolve Things you  Undertook.\n\n\n\nPlayers never asked to Change to Steam Platform.\n\n\n\nI repeat:  Players Never Asked to change to Steam Platform.\n\n\n\nThey Decided it Themself.\n\n\n\nWell, now Assume.\n\n\n\nBest Regards.\n\n\n\nJuhWork.\n\n__________________\n\nStones From my Ennemies, Roses From my Friends.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690880, 95751, 1013, 103308, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by JeffM \n\nYou could burn in hell for all I care. lol.\n\n\n\nNobody in this forum has half the talent the Steam developers have. If you did, you wouldn\'t be here. These guys are talented programmers. Plain and simple. They have created a system that with time will prove to be "the" way to deliver games. Software stores will soon become obsolete.\n\n\n\nEverybody here bashes Steam. Nobody here can do a damn bit better.\n\n\n\nWhine Whine Whine...  \n\nOf course we cant, were not game programmers. This is their JOB. Im not going to thank them because they do a job. Just remember, the customer is always right. We payed money to use steam. so we expect to be able to use steam. We also expect help when we have problems. Not to be told that we should thank them for doing such a great job. When we are sitting here with a broken steam and no one to our knowledge doing a f***ing thing about it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(691181, 95751, 1013, 101003, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by JeffM \n\nYou could burn in hell for all I care. lol.\n\n\n\nNobody in this forum has half the talent the Steam developers have. If you did, you wouldn\'t be here. These guys are talented programmers. Plain and simple. They have created a system that with time will prove to be "the" way to deliver games. Software stores will soon become obsolete.\n\n\n\nEverybody here bashes Steam. Nobody here can do a damn bit better.\n\n\n\nWhine Whine Whine...  \n\n\n\nYes they are indeed talented. Unfortunately not enough. If you cannot handle what you have created either give it to someone more talented, or you if you are the top, then destroy what you have made, as the world cannot yet handle it.\n\n__________________\n\nYep', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(691250, 95751, 1013, 103309, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Divine_Enigma \n\nthey can burn in hell far as i care. lol  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nyou suck   valve may not be perfect but their doing their best to let us play!  go valve    these games are my life!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(691265, 95751, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'You people that dont like steam dont have to play on it. WON is still there. Go have fun and leave the people that appericiate what Steam is and whats its done.\n\n__________________\n\nTo all the people that are saying why wont VALVe work on this or that, they have only 60 people in their company. Cliffe told me so it must be true. \n\n\n\nPlus they are working on all this: CS, CS:CZ, DoD, Source (the engine itself), CS:S (and other Source ports?), HL2, CS2, TFC2 and DoD2 (?)!!!!\n\n\n\n{-DB-} Custom Maps Server: 69.93.116.250:27015 Great pings even for the Euro guys, 30 person and most of the time admins are present. Drop on in for a great time.\n\n\n\nPosted by Silicon Vampire: \n\nAll the pointless arguements trying to justify cheating are rendered moot for one simple reason. As soon as a cheat is written/run with the intention of avoiding anti-cheat measures and gaining an unfair advantage against other players, there is no justification possible. It is what defines a cheat and it is wrong.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692296, 95751, 1013, 103307, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bballr4567 \n\nYou people that dont like steam dont have to play on it. WON is still there. Go have fun and leave the people that appericiate what Steam is and whats its done.  \n\n\n\nSorry,  But too Easy to say this.\n\n\n\nYou does not assume the problem.\n\n\n\nDon\'t forget that people who paid this game are on their own right to assert a minimum of Stability.\n\n\n\nAnd unfortunatly it isn\'t.\n\n\n\nYou cannot say to costumer "Don\'t use it, go away".\n\n\n\nSince i get Steam I had a new problem about every Month.\n\n\n\nEvery Month a new bug appears, sometimes many in the same time.\n\n\n\nAnd when we finished to Fixed it,   another comes...\n\n\n\nNow i had the crash memory read problem.\n\n\n\nWhen they will fix it, what new bug will release ?\n\n\n\nThats why people who post in this forum always seems Upset.\n\n\n\nSure they are,   before steam they played  Cs (or another game) without any problem.\n\n\n\nNow they have constantly a problem with it...\n\n\n\nYou should understant them,  and not talk as a king who don\'t care about it.\n\n\n\nAnd stop saying "They are best programmer than you,    they are doing the best."  Cause it\'s really idiot to say this.\n\n\n\nSure they are better then us on program.  That\'s their job.\n\n\n\nBut it appears that they cannot handle things they create.\n\n\n\n\n\nLet\'s have an example:\n\n\n\nYou are a builder.  you build a house.\n\n\n\nBut you make many hole on the wall,  and also  pipe of water are perforated,  and the heating doesnt work.\n\n\n\nAre you goind to say:  "Well, just leave the house,  and  don\'t ask me anymore, its the best that i can do"\n\n\n\nNo sir.  You will repair the pipe, stop the hole,  and anything else.\n\n\n\nDo not reverse the problem.\n\n\n\nThat\'s their job to fix it.\n\n\n\nThey probably do their best to fix it.\n\n\n\nBut it appears thats its quite not enough.\n\n\n\nSo get your apologies to your costumer  and try to do more than your best.\n\n\n\nThat\'s what they will do.\n\n\n\nBut of course  people who post:\n\n\n\n " they are the best "  " Steam is wonderful "  " don\'t use it anymore "  " shut up steam is very good "  " u suck  steam is good are your an idiot "\n\n\n\nare not members of the Steam Staff.\n\n\n\nSo we don\'t care about it.\n\n\n\nTry to read one more times this post.\n\n\n\nAnd think about them.\n\n\n\n\n\nBest Regards.\n\n\n\nJuhWork.\n\n__________________\n\nStones From my Ennemies, Roses From my Friends.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692368, 95751, 1013, 103310, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by JuhWork \n\nSorry,  But too Easy to say this.\n\n\n\nYou does not assume the problem.\n\n\n\nDon\'t forget that people who paid this game are on their own right to assert a minimum of Stability.\n\n\n\nAnd unfortunatly it isn\'t.\n\n\n\nYou cannot say to costumer "Don\'t use it, go away".\n\n\n\nSince i get Steam I had a new problem about every Month.\n\n\n\nEvery Month a new bug appears, sometimes many in the same time.\n\n\n\nAnd when we finished to Fixed it,   another comes...\n\n\n\nNow i had the crash memory read problem.\n\n\n\nWhen they will fix it, what new bug will release ?\n\n\n\nThats why people who post in this forum always seems Upset.\n\n\n\nSure they are,   before steam they played  Cs (or another game) without any problem.\n\n\n\nNow they have constantly a problem with it...\n\n\n\nYou should understant them,  and not talk as a king who don\'t care about it.\n\n\n\nAnd stop saying "They are best programmer than you,    they are doing the best."  Cause it\'s really idiot to say this.\n\n\n\nSure they are better then us on program.  That\'s their job.\n\n\n\nBut it appears that they cannot handle things they create.\n\n\n\n\n\nLet\'s have an example:\n\n\n\nYou are a builder.  you build a house.\n\n\n\nBut you make many hole on the wall,  and also  pipe of water are perforated,  and the heating doesnt work.\n\n\n\nAre you goind to say:  "Well, just leave the house,  and  don\'t ask me anymore, its the best that i can do"\n\n\n\nNo sir.  You will repair the pipe, stop the hole,  and anything else.\n\n\n\nDo not reverse the problem.\n\n\n\nThat\'s their job to fix it.\n\n\n\nThey probably do their best to fix it.\n\n\n\nBut it appears thats its quite not enough.\n\n\n\nSo get your apologies to your costumer  and try to do more than your best.\n\n\n\nThat\'s what they will do.\n\n\n\nBut of course  people who post:\n\n\n\n " they are the best "  " Steam is wonderful "  " don\'t use it anymore "  " shut up steam is very good "  " u suck  steam is good are your an idiot "\n\n\n\nare not members of the Steam Staff.\n\n\n\nSo we don\'t care about it.\n\n\n\nTry to read one more times this post.\n\n\n\nAnd think about them.\n\n\n\n\n\nBest Regards.\n\n\n\nJuhWork.  \n\n\n\nGod damn almost cried reading that, its so fuc,king true  *takes hat off to Juhwork*  \n\n\n\nalso the thing about us not asking for steam is so true, we didnt ask for this cr.ap they made us d-load it along with 1.6, from there on we\'ve had nothing but troubles, maybe if they\'d stop constantly updating the bloody thing we wouldnt complain, but the fact that they keep doing this all the time almost every fuc.king month just brings about the same amount of problems. Why cant steam just update once the program is completely as they want it to be with every single thing they want in it, and then and only then release an update not every fuc.king month!!! \n\n\n\nGod, i wish all of us lot could play the "steam team" on CS, and just fu.ck them up and embarass them, they\'re prolly a bunch of n00bs.\n\n__________________\n\nTHERES THIS COUNTER STRIKE AND HALF LIFE SERVER APPLICATION THINGY THAT SUCKS - WONDER WHAT IT IS?!!....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692406, 95751, 1013, 102793, 1072936800, '', 'your mum is a noob agt CS, but i bet she still kicks your ass in real life.\n\n\n\n\n\nanother day in the life of a 12 year old steampowered.com forum member...\n\n__________________\n\nThere is NO such thing as a Keygen which creates valid online keys for use with Steam.\n\n\n\nYou can get so-called \'Keygens\' which simply contain a list of PREVIOUSLY stolen keys, but these are likely to have been banned already since so many people have access to them.\n\n\n\nThe mathematical probability of guessing a working, valid key of the form XXXX-XXXXX-XXXX is infintesimally small. \n\n\n\nKEYGENS FOR ONLINE CD-KEYS ARE A MYTH!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692412, 95751, 1013, 103311, 1072936800, '', 'I feel that Steam is very good...when it\'s working. I mean, I know there will be bugs now and then, and I know that Steam is working very hard to fix them. So, Id\' like to thank Steam for their hard work, and I guess I\'ll just have to play for 1.5 now until the problem is fixed...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692458, 95751, 1013, 100658, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m going to put down a lot of the arguments right here... You can still play your game without steam... You can install Half-Life out of the box and play single-player and LAN games all you want... You don\'t have to install the upgrades and you don\'t have to run Steam.  You paid for HL, and you can play HL\n\n\n\nAnd for all the people who are saying "I want to take a mallet and bash the Steam servers," Steam isn\'t centralized at Valve HQ... And to the people who said "I want to pour hot water on the Steam developers," I suppose you are going to come to my house and beat me up for writing this post as well... And to both, I hope you can hang on to that soap in jail, because Big Bubba is watching\n\n\n\nSomeone said to use a win32 interface... Steam is\n\n\n\n"The Players never asked to change" - The players never asked Valve to make the best FPS game to date, but look where we ended up... If Valve waits for the players to decide everything that should happen then nothing will get done.  And Valve is doing a pretty good job of handling all of those games\n\n\n\nAnd someone talked about making you download 1.6... Again, you don\'t have to download it... Go look up an old beta installer and play LAN games... Nobody forced you to use it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692502, 95751, 1013, 102517, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by JeffM \n\nYou could burn in hell for all I care. lol.\n\n\n\nNobody in this forum has half the talent the Steam developers have. If you did, you wouldn\'t be here. These guys are talented programmers. Plain and simple. They have created a system that with time will prove to be "the" way to deliver games. Software stores will soon become obsolete.\n\n\n\nEverybody here bashes Steam. Nobody here can do a damn bit better.\n\n\n\nWhine Whine Whine...  \n\n\n\nword.\n\n\n\nBTW you don\'t pay money for STEAM to use it. STFU. \n\nThe customer is NOT always right, only some companys use that motto.\n\n__________________\n\nWell now it seems more than silence has been broken\n\nAnd I think I\'ve figured out the the dying lie\n\nYes the truth is that your dialect is half truth\n\nAnother conversation died alone', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692580, 95751, 1013, 103312, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Tevinhead \n\nOf course we cant, were not game programmers. This is their JOB. Im not going to thank them because they do a job. Just remember, the customer is always right. We payed money to use steam. so we expect to be able to use steam. We also expect help when we have problems. Not to be told that we should thank them for doing such a great job. When we are sitting here with a broken steam and no one to our knowledge doing a f***ing thing about it.  \n\n\n\n*Groan* No you didnt pay to use steam ffs. stop f**** complaining WON is there, go use it.\n\n__________________\n\nAMD Athlon"Thoroughbred"2000mhz+\n\n1gig DDR pc2700\n\nAsus Gforce FX5200 256Mb\n\nDolby Digital 5.1 encoder \n\nTechnics Surround sound  [6 spker]\n\nWindows XP Pro @ sp1\n\n\n\nA Quote on Steam:-\n\n\n\n"I do enjoy steam, its a great idea, but if I bought a car I wouldnt expect to need to get it updated every Wednesday and then have to deal with a whole new set of problems"\n\n\n\nA quote on CZ :-\n\n\n\n"Why the **** should I pay 30 bucks to beta test a game that looks & plays the same as the one I already have?"\n\n\n\n[img]http://ileet.net/images/jebus.jpg[/img]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692599, 95751, 1013, 103310, 1072936800, '', 'just because steam works for u doesnt make our complaints wrong and yours right u stupid wa.nker, dont diss my mum or call me a 12 yr old im probbly older than u u c.unt. \n\n\n\ni bought CS years ago and have since lost the CD, cant help that, but whats worse is that my 1.5 was overwritten during what the 15th odd reinstall, cant be blamed for that mistake what with all the frustrtation having to reinstall over and over, mistakes are bound to happen and as a result lost 1.5 and my old HL, shud i   d-load it again? no, whats the point, the servers ive gotten used to playing now are 1.6 and that is where all my friends are, why play the older version with a bunch of strangers. im not mad at the games, valve games are all great in my honest opinion - i wouldnt be playing them if i didnt like them, i am mad at steam not the games, when u have had this many problems EVERY month then u will begin to understand the level of frustration that ppl are having with this and why we dont want it anymore.\n\n__________________\n\nTHERES THIS COUNTER STRIKE AND HALF LIFE SERVER APPLICATION THINGY THAT SUCKS - WONDER WHAT IT IS?!!....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692781, 95751, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Many and I mean many of the Steam problems are with the user and not Steam itself. Ive seen probably thousands of cases solved by Quicksilver because the person didnt have thier computer configured right. Remember Steam is still in beta. WON is final. It is more stable. If you dont like how steam is working for its not like its the only option. \n\n\n\nThe people that get me are the ones that have one small problem think that Steam blows and they unistall and install to fix it. The ever looping update is the first time Ive ever had a really serious problem with Steam. Many people just give up and dont try anything. Its sad but I dont care for people who do that.\n\n__________________\n\nTo all the people that are saying why wont VALVe work on this or that, they have only 60 people in their company. Cliffe told me so it must be true. \n\n\n\nPlus they are working on all this: CS, CS:CZ, DoD, Source (the engine itself), CS:S (and other Source ports?), HL2, CS2, TFC2 and DoD2 (?)!!!!\n\n\n\n{-DB-} Custom Maps Server: 69.93.116.250:27015 Great pings even for the Euro guys, 30 person and most of the time admins are present. Drop on in for a great time.\n\n\n\nPosted by Silicon Vampire: \n\nAll the pointless arguements trying to justify cheating are rendered moot for one simple reason. As soon as a cheat is written/run with the intention of avoiding anti-cheat measures and gaining an unfair advantage against other players, there is no justification possible. It is what defines a cheat and it is wrong.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
