(691998, 96003, 1005, 103276, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cliffe \n\nWe are looking into the shield issues.  \n\n\n\nThank you Cliffe, That is all I wanted.\n\n\n\nAs you probably know, I am an ardent supporter of Valve. I just wanted some sort of sign from you guys that this problem is being addressed.\n\n\n\nThank you for your continued support of this wonderful game, and thank you for taking the time to answer me.\n\n\n\nBecause of your response, you have restored my faith in Valve.\n\n\n\nP.S. This thread should be locked and stickied right now, just to let folks know that you guys are on the job.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692024, 96003, 1005, 103313, 1072936800, '', 'Its always nice when Cliffe arises and responds. I am loyal you you cliffard. LOYAL!\n\n\n\nAs for the shield in the meantime, \n\n\n\nAll I do with it is go into some pubs and piss people off []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692040, 96003, 1005, 100565, 1072936800, '3 game play changing exploits', 'http://csczcs2ideas.csbanana.com/ (http://csczcs2ideas.csbanana.com/)\n\n\n\n#25 and #26 under weapon related glitches section\n\n\n\n#27 under other glitches section', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(692054, 96003, 1005, 103313, 1072936800, '', 'Good reply Opo, good info here.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(697699, 96003, 1005, 101408, 1072936800, '', 'Thank you Cliff for responding.  I seem to be the only one complaining about the shield crashing server problem.  I enabled the shield over the weekend on my two pubs and I believe they crashed no less then 10 times each before I disabled them again.  \n\n\n\nAs always there does not seem to be pattern, it just happens.\n\n\n\nThanks again Cliff, for at least acknowledging there are problems.  If anyone at Valve wants to see it happen, let me know as it doesn\'t take long for the server to crash after shields are enabled.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690350, 96028, 1026, 103314, 1072936800, 'File links for fixing server spiking.', 'Well, yet again it appears valve has outsourced it\'s coding to a bunch of kindergarden children.\n\n\n\nIs there a fix (From Valve) for the cpu spikes that have occured after the last update or do we all just have to piss off as usual and wait weeks for you guys to come up with a fix. It really makes gaming suck.\n\n\n\nThanks again for making me abhor administrating hlds based servers.\n\n\n\nProps to the community for picking up the slack and offering a temporary solution. Using the old mp.dll\n\n\n\n\n\nThis link courtesy of XGS-Barry\n\nhttp://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll (http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll)\n\n\n\nA link from us here at Dick\n\nhttp://files.dickathon.com/mp.dll (http://files.dickathon.com/mp.dll)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690359, 96028, 1026, 103315, 1072936800, 'temp fix', 'Here is my post to the other email thats just like this one.\n\n\n\n"\n\nWell I read thru everyones post and I must say that there is no certain reason why the servers are spiking. We have everything from 8 player privates to 32 player publics out of all four locations and there is no set reason why the problems are being caused. Its not a actual CPU problems itself as I noticed when it does do the random lockup the cpu spikes some but on our Dual Opterons the cpu was not going over 20% cpu usage with the spike but the players in the server we feeling the lockup. I updated all our servers and just used the old mp.dll for now to fix the problem. Make sure to use the mp.dll that is 1.25mb in size and the only problem you should see is the countdown clock will not showup. Its a burden yes but its better then the lockups every 10 seconds or so. I would have to say 90% of my servers were having problems and the others were not. Some were on the same box so out of expierence I know this is defiantly not a overloaded problems which some were trying to suggest. I have been running servers since 1999 and this is just one of these updates. Lets just hope that they come out with a fix soon to remove this problem.\n\n\n\nDownload the 1.25mb mp.dll below.\n\nhttp://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll (http://xgamingservers.com/mp.dll) \n\n"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690457, 96028, 1026, 103316, 1072936800, '', 'Another reason why keeping a history of DLLs is a good idea. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690461, 96028, 1026, 103315, 1072936800, '', 'exactly we have kept every update since beta 3 series lol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(696817, 96028, 1026, 103314, 1072936800, 'bump', 'Hey Valve guys what\'s the word?\n\nWe going to get the round timer back anytime soon?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(703444, 96028, 1026, 103314, 1072936800, 'bump', 'Can I get a fix?\n\n\n\nPatience is a virtue.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(703451, 96028, 1026, 100136, 1072936800, '', 'Barry, I assume you didn\'t update the gamedll file for servers such as clans using them for CAL matches, right [] Especially more concerned about public servers that are locked to have the match and then they get in trouble for old gamedll file []\n\n\n\nDid you email everyone and everyone that responded back you updated? I bet you guys have a sophisticated system though for updating all servers from a control panel []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(705951, 96028, 1026, 100016, 1072936800, '', 'Well all I have to say is this:\n\n\n\nOn Intel CPU\'s running Windows 2000 the problem is always exhibited by huge increases in CPU usage at exactly the same time the lag is occuring. The CPU usage will spike to 100% and sit there for a while then come back.\n\n\n\nMoreover, we have been able to alleviate the problem almost entirely by serverely cutting back the numbers of HLDS processes on each box and the numbers of players per process.\n\n\n\nMost of our servers are dual P4 Xeons mixed in with a few dual P3\'s for the smaller servers.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(711119, 96028, 1026, 103314, 1072936800, 'Time marches on.', 'Where is the Valve fix?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(711221, 96028, 1026, 103317, 1072936800, '', 'is none, probably won\'t be one and this is bull**** because i can\'t play in CAL b/c im an easy target when i freeze up thnx to updates!  way to improve CS for the community!  thanks, valve!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(690203, 96483, 1013, 103321, 1072936800, '', 'I get this error also.. it says:\n\n\n\n[ The instruction at "0x0ed35969" referenced memory at "0x0efc5800". The memory could not be "read".  Click on OK to terminate the program ]\n\n\n\nI can\'t play CS for more than a few minutes at a time... I notice that the error ocurrs most frequently when things are actually happening in CS such as guns being shot, lots of people joining servers... lo3 restarts/CAL.cfg being activated.  I know it\'s not a problem with my computer because i just built it and i had the same problem on my last computer which was a compaq.  I am needed on my team, and this error happens when we scrim all of the time.  I tell my team NOT to start me because It\'s useless.  There is no reason for me to play if whenever something happens "The instruction at blah blah" comes up.  Someone needs to address this, it seems to be a major problem effecting mostly the CS community.\n\n\n\nI am currently running:\n\nAMD Athlon 2600+ 2.08 Ghz\n\n512 mb PC2700 Ram (It\'s not bad ram so dont even try to tell me)\n\nATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128 mb\n\nASUS a7n8x-x Mobo\n\nMaxtor 60 gig 8mb\n\n\n\nIts not a problem with my system, its a problem with steam, it needs to be fixed...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(691222, 96483, 1013, 103321, 1072936800, '', 'Im clicking Counter-Strike... when it says "Install" I click it and im getting mad because instead of installing CS it just sits there... It won\'t reinstall...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
