(703706, 96483, 1013, 101719, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Jsink \n\nSir, quicksilver, sir...  This error is not caused by any hardware/BIOS setting...  It is an error with steam.  \n\n\n\nDon\'t you just love comments driven by a cursory glance at the thread, without reading and comprehending what\'s actually taking place?\n\n\n\n\n\nJeebs board or OS is SCREWED.  Maybe both.  Until these issues are square, ain\'t nothin\' else good going to happen. The OS install can be done without spending any money.  I would suggest starting there, see if the same results are reported.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(704038, 96483, 1013, 103321, 1072936800, '', 'I not only am subscribed to this thread, and have been following it since the beginning... but i too have the problem:\n\n\n\nThe instruction at "0x0ed35969" referenced memory at "0x0efc5800". The memory could not be "read".  Click on OK to terminate the program\n\n\n\nWhich, i might add is what this post is about.. I thought quicksilver was trying to tell jeebus that this problem could be solved with hardware changes etc... Don\'t say that i just posted after a "glance" when the reality is that ive been here since the beginning.  I need help too, and steam is causing me this problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(704152, 96483, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'Ok, so all I know really from your posts is you are getting this error: quote:The instruction at "0x0ed35969" referenced memory at "0x0efc5800". The memory could not be "readI see you also posted your system specs: quote:AMD Athlon 2600+ 2.08 Ghz\n\n512 mb PC2700 Ram\n\nATI Radeon 9700 Pro 128 mb\n\nASUS a7n8x-x Mobo\n\nMaxtor 60 gig 8mb What I need to know is:\n\n1. what Operating System\n\n2. what have you tried to fix the problem\n\n3. have you been able to use steam and play games before\n\n4. which games do you play\n\n5. What other programs do you have installed on your system,\n\nespecially firewall, anti-virus, security software, script and pop-up blocking, netlimiter, cybersitter, things like that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(695650, 96680, 1013, 103330, 1072936800, 'Friends steam problem...', 'I\'m posting this for a friend, as his account here hasn\'t been validated by an admin yet...anyway, here\'s his problem.\n\n\n\n\n\nok why am i keep getting this everytime i click steam first it updates to 26% which doesnt need done because ive checked after i was just playing steam and it didnt mention updates... this is the thing am getting.. any ideas? \n\n\n\nhttp://img44.photobucket.com/albums...11/untitled.jpg (http://img44.photobucket.com/albums/v134/storm1811/untitled.jpg) \n\n\n\niove uninstalled and reinstalled serveral times still no hope', '127.0.0.1', 1),
