(707241, 98034, 1005, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Det` \n\nIf there is going to be a CZ Source all I can say is how pefetic is that going to be. What would be the point in that? Condition Zero should just be left alone now. It was Valve\'s attempt at making CS a single player game and now all it is Counter-Strike with new skins, maps and 1 or 2 new additional features. Please Valve, don\'t waste your time with a CZ Source. I doubt there will be one anyway.  \n\n\n\nDont you get it yet? CS-S with its content and CZ-S with all its updates []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(707728, 98238, 1013, 100235, 1072936800, 'ATTN: Server ADMINS!!! LAG ISSUE FIX!!!', 'Our good friends at VALVe have come through. They have just sent this via the HLDS announce list....\n\n\n\nquote:We have identified the cause of the lag and have created a fix for it.\n\nUpdated game dlls will be released via Steam next week.\n\n\n\nIn the meantime we have a hotfix available, the updated game dlls can be\n\ndownloaded from:\n\n/drop/06...ke_gamedlls.zip (/drop/06232004_cstrike_gamedlls.zip)\n\n\n\nUnzip this file into the cstrike/dlls directory.\n\n\n\nThe md5 sums of the updated game dlls are:\n\n10f2dcdbacc50e9fe198fa05b85e5ca8  mp.dll\n\n1c4d3d4d073be72829e8d81dce59a4c7  cs_amd64.so\n\n6a57b0d1817cfc659059694e6e281d33  cs_i386.so\n\n\n\n\n\n- Alfred\n\n\n\n_______________________________________________\n\nhlds_announce mailing list\n\nhlds_announce@list.valvesoftware.com (mailto:hlds_announce@list.valvesoftware.com)\n\nhttp://list.valvesoftware.com/mailm...o/hlds_announce (http://list.valvesoftware.com/mailman/listinfo/hlds_announce)\n\n\n\nHope Alfred doesn\'t mind.\n\n__________________\n\nRepresentin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere...\n\n\n\n-=LoT=- StealthMode\n\n\n\nLegion of Terror\n\nhttp://legion.nuclearfallout.net\n\nhttp://www.teamlot.net\n\n\n\nVALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there!\n\n\n\nSTOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!!\n\n\n\nWHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
