(709023, 98238, 1013, 100235, 1072936800, '', 'OMG, I am not going to debate the legitimacy of this file. Number one its hosted here on the steam website. Number two, no virus author EVER has released an md5 checksum with their virii. Number three, email alfred yourself. Geez, some people are just ignorant when it comes to people trying to help.\n\n__________________\n\nRepresentin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere...\n\n\n\n-=LoT=- StealthMode\n\n\n\nLegion of Terror\n\nhttp://legion.nuclearfallout.net\n\nhttp://www.teamlot.net\n\n\n\nVALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there!\n\n\n\nSTOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!!\n\n\n\nWHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709026, 98238, 1013, 100002, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by StealthMode \n\nOMG, I am not going to debate the legitimacy of this file. Number one its hosted here on the steam website. Number two, no virus author EVER has released an md5 checksum with their virii. Number three, email alfred yourself. Geez, some people are just ignorant when it comes to people trying to help.  \n\n\n\nHey I\'m just screwing around.  I would like to point out virii authors have released md5 sums for their programs.  I know one that was pgp signed even.  Ok have fun now.\n\n\n\n-- Steve Tauber', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709036, 98238, 1013, 100235, 1072936800, '', 'Sry Steve, I just had a long night I guess. Came back and read the guys post above about some unfounded rumor somewhere and rebutted it. Then you came back with your reply and I guess I jumped the post a lil harsh.\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ll just speel it out for them I guess....\n\n\n\nquote:THIS FILE IS NOT A VIRII, IT IS HOSTED ON A VALVe OWNED WEBSITE! IF YOU DO NOT BELIEVE IT IS LEGITIMATE, WRITE ALFRED REYNOLDS YOURSELF AND BELIEVE HIM! I WAS JUST TRYING TO DO ALL ADMINS A FAVOR BY POSTING IT, JUST IN CASE THEY DO NOT GET THE ANNOUNCE EMAILS! TO WHOMEVER STARTED THE RUMOR THAT ITS A VIRII, YOU SHOULD BE PUBLICLY FLOGGED!\n\n__________________\n\nRepresentin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere...\n\n\n\n-=LoT=- StealthMode\n\n\n\nLegion of Terror\n\nhttp://legion.nuclearfallout.net\n\nhttp://www.teamlot.net\n\n\n\nVALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there!\n\n\n\nSTOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!!\n\n\n\nWHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709057, 98238, 1013, 103336, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by StealthMode \n\nHmmm, this is not why servers are lagging. Think about it, if the mp.dll were causing the lag, then ANY metamod server wouldn\'t lag. There is a deeper issue at work here.  \n\n\n\nI\'m not familiar with CS so much, but all Metamod does is allow multiple DLLs to be loaded - the core game DLL still must be launched through it. Check your Metamod configs and you will see that it is there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709069, 98238, 1013, 100235, 1072936800, '', 'Plugins.ini (for metamod) lists the dlls metamod calls upon/loads. Nowhere in that file does it say mp.dll. Thats the only "config" metamod uses other then its own native .dll\n\n\n\nAnd when you install metamod, you have to rem (remark) out (//) the stock dll in order to add the line to run the metamod.dll. So I think that I was correct in saying metamod doesn\'t use the mp.dll.\n\n\n\nThis is easily proven, by DELETING the mp.dll and starting a server running the gamedll /addons/metamod/dll/metamod.dll in the liblist.gam file. If metamod needed mp.dll it would have crashed the server when it tried to load without it. 8)\n\n__________________\n\nRepresentin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere...\n\n\n\n-=LoT=- StealthMode\n\n\n\nLegion of Terror\n\nhttp://legion.nuclearfallout.net\n\nhttp://www.teamlot.net\n\n\n\nVALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there!\n\n\n\nSTOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!!\n\n\n\nWHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709074, 98238, 1013, 103336, 1072936800, '', '...so then where exactly does it get the game code from? I\'m sorry, I\'m really unclear on how CS works (I\'m a TFC guy). Metamod can\'t simply recreate CS on its own...\n\n\n\nI don\'t have the HLDS version of CS installed so I can\'t check.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709346, 98238, 1013, 100235, 1072936800, '', 'Good question. Honestly I think it gets all its code from the gcf file. OR in the case of servers, from the servers cache file. Metamod is just an alternate dll to use instead of the mp.dll.\n\n\n\nI will test this since I started it. 8)\n\n\n\nEDIT: Ok I tested it. Looks like I am mistaken and metamod DOES call to the mp.dll (or the server still wants it loaded outside of metamod). I removed the mp.dll and tried to start the server, it crashed saying it could not find mp.dll (even with mp.dll remmed out of the liblist.gam file, and metamod.dll listed as the dll for the mod). /EDIT\n\n__________________\n\nRepresentin\' 1337 }-{ax0r }-{unterz everywhere...\n\n\n\n-=LoT=- StealthMode\n\n\n\nLegion of Terror\n\nhttp://legion.nuclearfallout.net\n\nhttp://www.teamlot.net\n\n\n\nVALVes remix of DMX Ruff Ryders anthem...for the hack distributors out there!\n\n\n\nSTOP, DROP, SHUT EM DOWN, OPEN UP SHOP!!!\n\n\n\nWHOA, NO, THIS IS HOW VALVES GONNA ROLL!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709564, 98238, 1013, 102713, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, your all wrong.\n\n\n\nMetamod is a WRAPPER to the mp.dll...all it does is intercept and pass calls to the .dll\n\n\n\nSo basically...metamod.dll is just a second dll attached TO mp.dll\n\n\n\nmp.dll is still being used.\n\n\n\nMetamod does this for all mods...thats why sometimes "special support" has to be added because not everyone calls their dll mp.dll\n\n\n\nIf you used +localinfo game_dll [path to a new dll]...then it would actually use whatever new DLL you listed.  Thats how you get things like non-mm bots working.\n\n__________________\n\nwww.TKWired.com', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(707887, 98261, 1026, 103337, 1072936800, 'Steam Hot Fix', 'Message: 4\n\nDate: Wed, 23 Jun 2004 17:04:39 -0700\n\nFrom: "Alfred Reynolds" <alfred@valvesoftware.com>\n\nTo: <hlds@list.valvesoftware.com>,\n\n	<hlds_linux@list.valvesoftware.com>,\n\n	<hlds_announce@list.valvesoftware.com>\n\nSubject: [hlds] CS lag fix\n\nReply-To: hlds@list.valvesoftware.com (mailto:hlds@list.valvesoftware.com)\n\n\n\nWe have identified the cause of the lag and have created a fix for it.\n\nUpdated game dlls will be released via Steam next week.\n\n\n\nIn the meantime we have a hotfix available, the updated game dlls can be\n\ndownloaded from:\n\n/drop/06...ke_gamedlls.zip (/drop/06232004_cstrike_gamedlls.zip)\n\n\n\nUnzip this file into the cstrike/dlls directory.\n\n\n\nThe md5 sums of the updated game dlls are:\n\n10f2dcdbacc50e9fe198fa05b85e5ca8  mp.dll\n\n1c4d3d4d073be72829e8d81dce59a4c7  cs_amd64.so\n\n6a57b0d1817cfc659059694e6e281d33  cs_i386.so\n\n\n\n\n\n- Alfred\n\n\n\n\n\n--__--__--', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(709123, 98261, 1026, 103338, 1072936800, 'Error Message after Fix', 'After instaling this Fix, a Error Message appears :\n\n\n\nDisconectet from the Server Reason :\n\nbad file server consistency is enforcing file scope_arc_sw.tga.\n\n\n\nWhats this ? Never heard of this file in CS....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
