(738430, 101329, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'Killer Koala is bent on the idea that the shield is a defensive weapon. That\'s basically blaspheme. Is the USP alone a defensive weapon? I say not. It\'s when you add a impenetrable shield; then it becomes an offensive item. I like this idea, but the hitboxes need to be either the same size as the shield or slightly smaller. I hate aiming at the person, but only hearing a "dink." VALVe also needs to fix the multi-weapon glitch, too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(739408, 101329, 1013, 100011, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Whisper \n\nI think Wudge pinched my idea from the way Ive got my servers setup! []  \n\n\n\nLol...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(740716, 101329, 1013, 100017, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah I agree with pretty much all of this post.\n\n\n\nThe only time I ever shield is on CS maps like militia and definately assault.\n\n\n\nOnly thing is, I don\'t see how you have a problem with the hitboxes, for me they\'re fine, I never have a problem taking a shielder\'s dome off, I just wait for them to look out and take a pot-shot at me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(738680, 101650, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'CD KEY issues', 'If you are having trouble registering a cd-key with Steam, please use the Steam Troubleshooter. Please read everything it says carefully, and try the methods it recommends to find any account of yours that may be using the key already. If that doesn\'t work, the Troubleshooter tells you everything else you need to know. Posting a thread here won\'t do you any good, and I\'m going to start closing all of the new threads about cd-keys I see.\n\n\n\n/support.php/ (/support.php)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(739214, 101650, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'Note:\n\n\n\nThere is currently a bug in Steam that may tell you your cd-key is invalid if you enter it when trying to join a game server (double=clicked on a server in the Servers window). You\'ll need to go to the Steam Games window, double-click the game you want to play, and enter the key there. Thanks,\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(752409, 101650, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'There has been a change in procedure for people that are having trouble with cd-keys they just purchased. Instead of emailing Hien, please follow these instructions (this only applies to troubles with cd-keys from freshly opened boxes):\n\n\n\nquote:\n\nFrom this point on, all such inquiries should now be emailed only to halflifekeys@vugames.com and no longer to Hien Nguyen.\n\n\n\nThe customer must include the following within the message in .jpeg format: \n\n\n\n1.      A copy of the actual game CD. \n\n\n\n2.      A copy of the HL/CS packaging which clearly displays the CD key number. \n\n\n\n3.      A  copy of the sales receipt.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(811510, 101650, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, 'Duplicate CD-keys -- Valve, Sierra, etc', 'There seems to be some confusion over this item from the Troubleshooter.\n\n\n\nOn the page about newly-purchased cd-keys, it suggests you email pictures of the keys to "halflifekeys@vugames.com". VU Games is the parent company of Sierra - the publishers of the games, and printers of the keys. They are a different company from us (Valve). They provided us with this email address as a place to send customers who were having difficulty using keys from newly-purchased games -- specifically, keys that they might have accidentally printed more than once. They know which keys this happened to (we don\'t), and so can properly attend to their needs.\n\n\n\nTo the best of our knowledge, they are checking that email address and helping out customers in this condition. But we can\'t check on the status of your request, you\'ll have to contact them for that.\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\n\n\nTaylor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(811516, 101650, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'Note:\n\n\n\nAs I mentioned in this other thread (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=108755), VU Games is not the same company as Valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(883797, 101650, 1013, 100028, 1072936800, '', 'This is just a summary of Steam Accounts and CDKeys, in a litle more detail then the FAQ which is here:\n\n/index.php?a...009373,58908500 (/index.php?area=faq&id=1050915492,63276400,1080009373,58908500)\n\n\n\nSteam is Free\n\nPlayers do not have to pay for Steam itself.\n\n\n\nDedicated Server is Free\n\nPlayers do not have to pay for Dedicated Servers. Stand-alone Dedicated Servers need a valid Steam Account but do not require a CDKey.  Client Dedicated Servers use the Steam Account that is currently logged in.\n\n\n\nYou should not use the same Steam account for your stand-alone Dedicated Server that you use for your Client.\n\n\n\nCodename Gordon is Free\n\nPlayers do not have to pay for Codename Gordon.\n\n\n\nCyberCafe Accounts\n\nCyberCafe Accounts are totally different from individual player accounts and are supported differently.\n\n\n\nNo Subscription Accounts for Players\n\nAt this time there are no subscription-type accounts offered for players. Maybe sometime in the future, but not now.\n\n\n\nPlayers Must Own a Unique and Valid CDKey\n\nPlayers have to purchase a suitable CDKey to play HL and any of the regular games.\n\n\n\nThere are several types of CDKeys out there.\n\n\n\nThe WON CDKey: xxxx-xxxxx-xxxx (4 X 5 X 4)\n\n\n\nWON CDKeys are single-game Retail CDKeys that get upgraded to a full Platinum pack CDKeys (in Steam) which give you CS, HL (single-player and multiplayer HLDM), OP4 (single-player and multi-player), DoD, Ricochet, DMC and TFC.\n\n\n\nBlue Shift is not available under Steam but works as a single-player mission if you have the physical CD. \n\n\n\nThe Blue-Shift CDKey does give you a full Platinum Pack set of games when you use it for a Steam Account.\n\n\n\nOpposing Force CDKeys are not valid for use with your Steam Account, OP4 required HL (It\'s an add-on pack only).\n\n\n\nOP4 CDKeys are in this format: xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx (5 X 4)\n\n\n\nHigh Definition Packs\n\nHigh-Definition Packs do not work directly with Steam (they might with some manual installation work).\n\n\n\nOnline Purchases\n\nIf you purchase CZ Retail or Online through Steam, you get CS, CZ and CZ: DS (Deleted Scenes).\n\n\n\nRetail CZ purchases have a CDKey in the format: xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx (5 X 5)\n\n\n\nOnline CZ purchases do not give you a CDKey number, the CDKey is automatically bound to your Steam account.  You don\'t need to know the CDKey number, only your Steam Account. (Don\'t ask for the CDKey from Valve, it\'s never disclosed.).\n\n\n\nIf you have a retail CZ CDKey, when you install Steam, you must select either CS or CZ Games, and when prompted enter your CZ CDKey. If you select any other Games they will not accept the CZ CDKey as valid.\n\n\n\nIf you purchase HL online you get the "Premium Pack" which includes everything but CZ and CS. Again, this purchase does not give you a numerical CDKey, it gets bound to your Steam Account.\n\n\n\nATI HL2 CDKey\n\nATI HL2 CDKeys were part of a Radeon Graphic Card Purchase and give you access to HL2 when it is released. Until then, that ATI HL2 CDKey will also give you access to the Platinum Pack selection (all the HL1 games except CZ and CZ: DS).\n\n\n\nThe ATI HL2 CDKey is on a small scratch-off card that is included in your Graphics card box.\n\n\n\nThe CDKey has the format: xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx (5 X 5).\n\n\n\nAt one time, if you got the ATI HL2 CDKey, you were also able to order a physical CD of most of the Steam Platinum-Pack Games from ATI via their web-page (this was Steam only, and required you to be online to Validate the installation through Steam).\n\n\n\nI don\'t know if this physical CD is available any longer from ATI.\n\n\n\nThe ATI physical CD did not ship with a CDKey but have a SKU number something like "180-G3D056-100" that players often try to use as a CDKey, needless to say it won\'t work.\n\n\n\nATI Scratch Off - BE CAREFUL\n\nYou need to be very careful when you scratch off the covering on the ATI HL2 CDKey or you could scratch off the numbers as well. If you damage the card and can\'t read the CDKey, ATI might help but I don\'t believe there is anything more you can do about it.\n\n\n\nATI CDKey Useage\n\nIf you already have a Steam Account with a Premium or Platinum pack CDKey attached to it, you won\'t be able to add the HL2 CDKey to that Steam account right now.  However, when HL2 becomes available, you will be prompted for a valid HL2 CDKey so you can enter it at that time.\n\n\n\nOnly One Type of CDKey\n\nLast but not least, you can only add one CDKey of each type to your Steam Account.   \n\n\n\nOne WON CDKey plus one CZ CDKey plus one HL2 CDKey.\n\n\n\nTrying to add a 2nd CDKey of the same type to your Steam Account will prove to be a disappointing experience.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
