(759092, 103739, 1013, 103466, 1072936800, '', 'Sorry if I\'m repeating myself over the forums (I\'ve already posted part of this twice in other topics) but I have a little insight on to what is probably going on and how you can get your friends working as well as it can right now.\n\n\n\nFirst off, in order to CONNECT to your friends list, here are a few things you can try.\n\nIf you\'ve already attempted these methods, I\'m sorry.\n\n\n\nThe apparent cause of the problem is some file that stores your friends information. I\'m assuming that a recent patch created a new file that seems to be confusing the client-side friends system. There is a process that is supposed to fix these files and supposedly this is what you do:\n\n\n\n1) Turn steam off to be safe.\n\n\n\n2) Go to your steam/config folder - you should have a friendsdata.vdf and hopefully two userdata_####.vdf files. (If you have only one, I suggest the other possible fix. If you have more than two, that means that you have multiple users on your computer and it will be much harder finding the right files to alter - it may only fix one login anyway.)\n\n\n\n3) By right clicking on the userdata_#### files and viewing the properties, find the older of the two (it will probably be bigger). Replace the friendsdata.vdf with the older file. (Make a backup if you want to be safe.)\n\n\n\n4) Try login in. If it doesn\'t work, then try the second method.\n\n\n\nThe second method is much simpler, but more of a hassle. All I did was a clean reinstall. Uninstall steam, delete any remaining latent files, and reinstall it. The network seems to be rather slow right now and it will take a while to get it all updated again, but this fixed friends for me. (To the point where you can log on, anyway.)\n\n\n\nNote: If you login and find the list filled with the [A-K-S]WARRIOR names, do not delete them, as these are actually your friends. Read on to learn why...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNow onto speculation about the recent friends problems...\n\n\n\nOnce I reinstalled steam (a hassle for dialup people, perhaps, but it works) my friends list came back to life. Unfortunately, as with others, it seemed like some of my friends were missing and I had all these [A-K-S]WARRIOR entries. \n\n\n\nUnfortunately, I decided to do a clean wipe of my list and readd everyone. Unfortunately because the AKS WARRIOR\'s are your friends, with a different name. If you didn\'t already pick this up, their last name remains unchanged if you go to view their .. profile. \n\n\n\nI realised when I went to readd them that all the friends on my list who had not had their names changed could be added, but all of my friends who were renamed could NOT be found.\n\n\n\nIn my opinion, I think this has something to do with when you first logged into steam. All the people whos\' names were unchanged were people who installed steam as soon as it came out whereas my friends who took much longer were not found.\n\n\n\nIf my guess is right, whatever they\'ve done to the database has temporarily deleted players and either the unchanged players are from an earlier backup or they\'re being added back to the database slowly.\n\n\n\nThe final solution is just to let Valve get the database full again. Just let them fix it. My note for all the flamers: It\'s not easy to work when you have people yelling at you. You are more likely to rush and mess something else up in the process of fixing it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
