(783114, 106013, 1013, 100177, 1072936800, '', 'YOU might be smart enough not to use aim , but all my friends aren\'t', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783147, 106013, 1013, 100065, 1072936800, 'Proof aim has spyware', 'quote:Originally posted by noobinatorV2.0 \n\nhttp://img7.exs.cx/my.php?loc=img7&...aimspyware1.jpg (http://img7.exs.cx/my.php?loc=img7&image=aimspyware1.jpg) Heheh You know after looking this up for awhile, you know what cnetwait.odl does? It launches AIM on Windows startup.\n\n\n\nHere\'s a way to test that:\n\nOpen AIM, go to My AIM, Edit Options, Edit Preferences.\\\n\nChoose Sign on Category, Choose Start AIM when Windows Starts and hit OK.\n\n\n\nNext, go to Start, Run, type in msconfig.exe\n\nGo to your Startup tab\n\nScroll down till you see the startup item AIM, and to the right you\'ll see the cnetwait.odl beside the aim.exe launch command.\n\n\n\nThat\'s all it does. That\'s why you don\'t trust some Anti-spyware programs. Some programmers just guess at what MIGHT be spyware and disable it anyways cause they didn\'t find a privacy policy or whatever. This is completely legit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783175, 106013, 1013, 100178, 1072936800, 'Re: Proof aim has spyware', 'quote:Originally posted by Killer Koala \n\nHeheh You know after looking this up for awhile, you know what cnetwait.odl does? It launches AIM on Windows startup.\n\n\n\nHere\'s a way to test that:\n\nOpen AIM, go to My AIM, Edit Options, Edit Preferences.\\\n\nChoose Sign on Category, Choose Start AIM when Windows Starts and hit OK.\n\n\n\nNext, go to Start, Run, type in msconfig.exe\n\nGo to your Startup tab\n\nScroll down till you see the startup item AIM, and to the right you\'ll see the cnetwait.odl beside the aim.exe launch command.\n\n\n\nThat\'s all it does. That\'s why you don\'t trust some Anti-spyware programs. Some programmers just guess at what MIGHT be spyware and disable it anyways cause they didn\'t find a privacy policy or whatever. This is completely legit.  \n\nLol nice catch man.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
