(782823, 106063, 1005, 100181, 1072936800, 'CS:Source beta ...only one map', 'A2597 got an email response from Gabe Newell regarding the forthcoming CS:source beta and posted it at www.halflife2.net (http://www.halflife2.net) forums:-\n\n\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/sho...4214#post574214 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?p=574214#post574214)\n\n\n\n\n\nIt looks like there will only be the one map, and that map will most likely be De_Dust. It\'s a beta so for testing purposes one map makes sense...but De_Dust....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(782840, 106063, 1005, 100182, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah I agree. de_dust is gettting kinda"old", but hell, I still love that map. The beta will be more than outstanding anyway , I know it will. Have fun.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(782845, 106063, 1005, 100183, 1072936800, '', 'Aww...I was expecting to shoot the the watermelons off the tables in the market in Italy, or climb up those pyramids in Aztec.\n\n\n\nBut oh well, at least we actually got some official news, and we are getting to test it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(782866, 106063, 1005, 100181, 1072936800, '', 'I\'d rather it was De_Dust2 tbh. I think it\'s a better map all round compared to De_Dust. As a T you can Rush left, Sneak down the middle or battle your way through the doors on the right. De_Dust isn\'t anywhere as versatile.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
