(783014, 106063, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, 'Anyone want to be a victim?', 'quote:Originally posted by eram \n\ncan 1 map be considered a beta test?  \n\n\n\nWell, someone be brave and download it when it\'s released and let the rest of us know if it is indeed only one map. I don\'t see any point in downloading GBs of the new source code just for some new eye-candy which will likely run poorly in it\'s beta state and kill my system resources. \n\n\n\nThe short of it is they can either put me on the payroll to play a single map over and over again, change the beta to make it worth the hassle with additional maps or at least different gameplay or promise the beta testers the full version when it comes out. Otherwise I\'ll stick with CZ thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783037, 106063, 1005, 100189, 1072936800, '', 'What? Did you guys think there was going to be a full list of maps to choose from? de_dust fits as it has been the show map for counter strike since its release. It is just a test of the engine not the maps.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783047, 106063, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, 'CS:Source beta ...only one map', 'quote:Originally posted by Kadayipolokov \n\nA2597 got an email response from Gabe Newell regarding the forthcoming CS:source beta and posted it at www.halflife2.net (http://www.halflife2.net) forums:-\n\n\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/sho...4214#post574214 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?p=574214#post574214)\n\n\n\n\n\nIt looks like there will only be the one map, and that map will most likely be De_Dust. It\'s a beta so for testing purposes one map makes sense...but De_Dust.... \n\n\n\nThanks for the link, at least it answered one question for me...\n\n\n\nquote:CS:Source is in great shape, and I don\'t see it impacting the RC date. It is the plan to include it in the regular and collectors edition boxes.\n\n\n\nI\'ve heard the rumours about CS:Source but it was unclear if I would have to shell out more money e.g. if CS:Source was only included with the collector\'s edition. Well now that that\'s addressed, does anyone have any idea what the difference is between the versions? Will the collector\'s edition include DoD or something else? Or is it going to be something useless like a T-shirt and poster?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783063, 106063, 1005, 100190, 1072936800, 'wtf are you talking about? do you know what "Beta"s even are?', 'I think that you guys are forgetting what a "beta test" is really about.\n\n\n\nThey\'re not released so that the players get to have fun. They\'re released so that the players can help find bugs, and the payoff for them is free gametime.\n\n\n\nWhile a lot of you will just get the game, and just play it, there is a majority of the people out there that will take the beta the way they should. They will look around for bugs, and expirement: IE: What happens when I throw this nade in this map problem area. What visual defects do I get on XXX video card.\n\n\n\nThe reason they would only release one map? Again, this is a beta test, not a free "play b4 u pay" thing. And, you saw what happened with CS:CZ, so don\'t you think you\'ll expect to see someone trying to package up CS:S and trying to give it out to their friends with some bypass? Most likly. \n\n\n\nSo, 1 map, because that\'s all you need to be in the enviroment of the game. 1 map because it\'s just a beta to see how it works on everyones computer. Because VALVe doesn\'t have a replica of all our computers at their building.\n\n\n\nHavn\'t you guys ever beta\'d before? They\'re will be problems, we WILL find them, That\'s why we beta, to fix, not to play(well, also to play, but the other thing more). But you guys that are crying are just gonna say "WTF!! WHY DOES IT CRASH? I\'M NOT GONNA SWEAR!!", When you should be saying, "When I do this \'xxx\' while standing at \'xxx\' I get \'errors/visual defects/unexplained major lag/crash\', and this is how you replicate the error so you can text/fix it yourself \'xxx\' "', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783069, 106063, 1005, 100190, 1072936800, 'Re: CS:Source beta ...only one map', 'quote:Originally posted by gregrout \n\nThanks for the link, at least it answered one question for me...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI\'ve heard the rumours about CS:Source but it was unclear if I would have to shell out more money e.g. if CS:Source was only included with the collector\'s edition. Well now that that\'s addressed, does anyone have any idea what the difference is between the versions? Will the collector\'s edition include DoD or something else? Or is it going to be something useless like a T-shirt and poster?  \n\n\n\nGabe Newell said that even he is totally not sure of what all they\'re will be, but that he does know that their will be a few little things packaged in, and as far as the game, their will be some sort of extra content to play. Maybe extra levels, maybe extra who knows.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783202, 106105, 1013, 100191, 1072936800, 'stop external voice programs from working', 'The main problem as I see it with the game is people being able to utilise external programs which go against the game principles. For example once you have died you can\'t talk to your team mates that are still in the game. Programs like Teamspeak , Roga Wilko etc. make everyones lives a misery in my opinion. Need to find some way to prevent the programs from working whilst CS/CZ is operative.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783235, 106105, 1013, 100192, 1072936800, '', 'Thats not for everyone...And it\'s probly just certain settings you have on your soundcard that do so. I\'ve been able to run teamspeak, ventrilo, and CS at the same time(don\'t ask why). But, it has happend to where i lose voice in one program or the other. You may want to go look for some fixes or read up on the vidcard you have and settings that may do that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783251, 106105, 1013, 100193, 1072936800, '', 'yeah. Why stop there? You know, when my friends come over and we play CS, I think it\'s really unfair that we can talk to each other after one of us have died. Valve should make people wear an electronic muzzle.\n\n\n\nWhat about lan parties? Yep, unfair to talk to each other. Maybe Valve should remove the lan option. Wouldn\'t want anyone talking to each other after they died, would we?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783281, 106105, 1013, 100192, 1072936800, '', 'oops lol...i just skimmed through it and read it wrong...my bad.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783412, 106105, 1013, 100194, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Xaleth \n\nyeah. Why stop there? You know, when my friends come over and we play CS, I think it\'s really unfair that we can talk to each other after one of us have died. Valve should make people wear an electronic muzzle.\n\n\n\nWhat about lan parties? Yep, unfair to talk to each other. Maybe Valve should remove the lan option. Wouldn\'t want anyone talking to each other after they died, would we?  \n\n\n\nI recently went to ECL about a week ago, and my friend\'s clan were using ventrillo. The catch was that ECL had a server setting that made the screen turn black when they die. So they wouldn\'t be able to view the game anymore. I think that works well to stop \'voice(lan) hacking\'.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783579, 106105, 1013, 100195, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by an80sbboy \n\nI recently went to ECL about a week ago, and my friend\'s clan were using ventrillo. The catch was that ECL had a server setting that made the screen turn black when they die. So they wouldn\'t be able to view the game anymore. I think that works well to stop \'voice(lan) hacking\'.  \n\n\n\nThats a setting called mp_fadetoblack but its not the greatest option to use in a pub server.\n\n\n\nI think the first poster has a valid point. CAL and other leagues started allowing the use of 3rd party chat programs like ventrilo and teamspeak to be used in matches for the soul reason that they could not control it. The thing about a match is that once u die, your screen goes black so you really can\'t see anyway but you can still communicate your position and who killed you. And also, your voice comm is not recorded in the demo\'s that you have to record while playing matches.\n\n\n\nThe thing is that now most people are going into pubs using the same chat programs and after they die, they lead they friends are clan mates around telling them where each member of the other team is at. Its actually easier than if you were lanning with someone cause you never have to take your eyes off of the screen. Its starting to get abused and everyone can laugh now but when someone else does it to you over and over, you won\'t laugh any more.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783582, 106105, 1013, 100192, 1072936800, '', 'you can still use the friends network...there is still a phone...different messengers...Your not going to stop it, if a server deosn\'t want to allow it they\'ll put forcecam on. There isn\'t a lot you can do about it so its not going to happen', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783601, 106105, 1013, 100195, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by MrHamolka \n\nyou can still use the friends network...there is still a phone...different messengers...Your not going to stop it, if a server deosn\'t want to allow it they\'ll put forcecam on. There isn\'t a lot you can do about it so its not going to happen  \n\n\n\nI said he had a valid point, not that valve was going to do anything about it.\n\n\n\nAlso, since you mentioned them. \n\n\n\nYou have to drop console to get to the friends network and message someone on your friends list\n\nYou have to alt tab out of game to use various other messengers\n\nHow many people actually sit on the phone and tell each other where the other team is? That leaves them playing with one hand or a crocked neck.\n\nIf there was a plugin for any of the admin controls that are out there that would allow admins to be void of the forcecam, I would have that option enabled.\n\n\n\n\n\nBut you are right, I doubt Valve would have control over such programs so in that light, they will probably never move to do anything about it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783653, 106105, 1013, 100194, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by MrHamolka \n\n...there is still a phone...   OMG would ppl really go that far to raise their score 1 point, to go from rank 3 to 1.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by i||ega|-op\n\nThats a setting called mp_fadetoblack but its not the greatest option to use in a pub server.\n\n\n\nThis is probably the best way to prevent this chat cheating. But even if they do report to their other teammates on their last position, the enemy that killed them is more than likely to move to a new location, or find a hiding spot for more kills.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(783778, 106105, 1013, 100192, 1072936800, '', 'Actually yes people have, I\'ve heard people in CS type out "hey call me now" So yeah, they do. And I have a friend that, when he plays cs, he calls up his friend (when friends network is down) and over the phone calls him and talks to him while playing. So its not something thats crossing the line.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(784378, 106105, 1013, 100196, 1072936800, '', 'thats a very bad idea.\n\nok some kiddies might go on public servers or somthing and tell their mate where ppl are but just think of the cs, dod or whatever clans.\n\nthe voice program in cs is not that good that clanmembers use that in a war.\n\n\n\nyou cant solve this problem, if people use this opiton that you can spectate whoever you want (only on servers where that is allowed) than you cant do anything against that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(784536, 106105, 1013, 100194, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by MrHamolka \n\nActually yes people have, I\'ve heard people in CS type out "hey call me now" So yeah, they do. And I have a friend that, when he plays cs, he calls up his friend (when friends network is down)and over the phone calls him and talks to him while playing. \n\n\n\n\n\nI thought you meant that person A would call person B that is playing on the same server as person A. So then person A would tell person B where all the enemy are.\n\n\n\nquote:(when friends network is down)\n\n\n\nWhat!?\n\n\n\nWhen friends network is down?.....If his network is down then hes definitely not playing CS!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(784566, 106105, 1013, 100004, 1072936800, '', 'Download a wallhack. That way, you\'ll be on the same level as those hackers with external voice programs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*disclaimer* Don\'t actually do what I said. I was being sarcastic.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785147, 106105, 1013, 100139, 1072936800, '', 'there\'s nothing you can really do about ppl using externel programs such as skype/msn/aim/yahoo blah blah and whatever else. its one of those things [] ones gotta deal with..sad eh? ;/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785530, 106105, 1013, 100012, 1072936800, '', 'an80sboy. . I hope that was sarcasam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785421, 106328, 1013, 100197, 1072936800, 'i hate "pwned"', 'It\'s spelled with an "o",not a "p"...just bc people can\'t type and hit "p" instead of "o" doesnt mean it should become some fad\n\n\n\n\n\nmy 2 cents\n\n\n\n\n\nthey are good pennies too, the shiny kind with 2004 on them, becuase they were made this year.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nyay\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\npwned this thread good!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785523, 106328, 1013, 100012, 1072936800, '', 'yeah, I hate jokes as well. DOWN WITH HUMOR!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785547, 106328, 1013, 100197, 1072936800, '', 'no, but pwned really does get me all red in the face\n\n\n\nmy suggestion is to rid of the use of this nonsense', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785787, 106328, 1013, 100042, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Darius \n\nyeah, I hate jokes as well. DOWN WITH HUMOR!!!  \n\nPWNEDi', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(785829, 106328, 1013, 100198, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by nikefido \n\nno, but pwned really does get me all red in the face\n\n\n\nmy suggestion is to rid of the use of this nonsense  \n\nmy suggestion is to stop playing video games', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(786277, 106328, 1013, 100127, 1072936800, '', 'pwned... you\'ll never get rid of it, dont even try, its useless.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(786618, 106328, 1013, 100141, 1072936800, '', 'It is a crap word though, When I see players say it I immediately picture the stereotypical online player, wearing his \'Haxor\' t-shirt, listening to blink 182.\n\n\n\nHey, maybe they can add a \'nerd\' filter option so us normal people don\'t need to be subjected to nerd words like \'pwned\' and \'ownage\' and those ridiculous chat binds where they use upper case and lower case letters alternately and replace \'A\'s with \'4\'s. Afterall 1t l0ok5 ****3.\n\n\n\nI\'m sure I\'ll be getting some replies from the nerds saying \'dude, you suck\' and other teen american sayings. But oh well....Flame away.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(786649, 106328, 1013, 100197, 1072936800, '', 'no Obewansabogie i have much more respect for you\n\nnot to say i had any for you before, becuase I didnt know you existed\n\n\n\nbut thanks\n\n\n\n\n\nblink 182......lol....it fits so well', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(786681, 106328, 1013, 100199, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Obewansabogie \n\nIt is a crap word though, When I see players say it I immediately picture the stereotypical online player, wearing his \'Haxor\' t-shirt, listening to blink 182.\n\n\n\nHey, maybe they can add a \'nerd\' filter option so us normal people don\'t need to be subjected to nerd words like \'pwned\' and \'ownage\' and those ridiculous chat binds where they use upper case and lower case letters alternately and replace \'A\'s with \'4\'s. Afterall 1t l0ok5 ****3.\n\n\n\nI\'m sure I\'ll be getting some replies from the nerds saying \'dude, you suck\' and other teen american sayings. But oh well....Flame away.  \n\n\n\nWhy would you call the people using them nerds? I would have called them dip****s.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(786811, 106328, 1013, 100200, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Pooty \n\nmy suggestion is to stop playing video games  \n\n\n\nHahahahaha.\n\nHe just got PWNED....Yes, PWNED.\n\n\n\nWhy cant you let us have our fun? Let us say PWNED because its\n\nall us 12 year olds have left.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
