(790513, 106627, 1005, 100237, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m 28\n\n\n\nI think the average age depends on the country you are from.\n\n\n\nIn countries where Internet access, especially broadband is very expensive, players tend to be at least in their twenties because they have jobs and can pay for access that kids cannot extort from their parents.\n\n\n\nIn countries where Internet access is cheap and most households have broadband the average age drops because kids have more time on their hands.\n\n\n\nThe real question though, should be, what is the average age of users on this forum because almost every thread turns into a juvenile flame war.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(790526, 106627, 1005, 100238, 1072936800, '', '20 here and i\'ve been playing since beta 6 wohooo', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(790527, 106627, 1005, 100239, 1072936800, '', 'Well, I am 26 and have been playing for about 3 weeks lol - so I guess since 1.6. You never know one day I might be able to say that and sound good!\n\n\n\nI have to admit though I have found the CS hype a little over rated (braces for a flaming). After hearing about it time after time after time I purchased Half Life and downloaded all the juicy Steam extras. After playing CS for a few weeks I just dont think it is up to its own reputation, well not any more anyhow.\n\n\n\nI think Counter Strike : Source is desperatly needed - for me anyhow - for the game to be worth taking time out from other games to play.\n\n\n\nDaniel', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(790542, 106627, 1005, 100240, 1072936800, '', '14, been playing since cs 1.1', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(790555, 106627, 1005, 100202, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Druidwitch \n\nWell, I am 26 and have been playing for about 3 weeks lol - so I guess since 1.6. You never know one day I might be able to say that and sound good!\n\n\n\nI have to admit though I have found the CS hype a little over rated (braces for a flaming). After hearing about it time after time after time I purchased Half Life and downloaded all the juicy Steam extras. After playing CS for a few weeks I just dont think it is up to its own reputation, well not any more anyhow.\n\n\n\nI think Counter Strike : Source is desperatly needed - for me anyhow - for the game to be worth taking time out from other games to play.\n\n\n\nDaniel  \n\n\n\n\n\n1.5 was better...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(790577, 106627, 1005, 100237, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Druidwitch \n\nI have to admit though I have found the CS hype a little over rated (braces for a flaming). After hearing about it time after time after time I purchased Half Life and downloaded all the juicy Steam extras. After playing CS for a few weeks I just dont think it is up to its own reputation, well not any more anyhow. \n\n\n\nI think you have started playing at the wrong time. CS has been in a kind of transition phase for a year or more now. Before 1.4 it was a spectacular game with a brilliant community but recently has been plagued by cheats and horrible mods. The basic premise of the game though is timeless and I think CS:S will for a time return the CS community to the good old days.\n\n\n\nStick with it, CS is a keeper, I look forward to hearing my kids whinge that CS4 is no where near as good as CS3.8 was.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
