(797759, 107476, 1013, 100245, 1072936800, 'Vigil for HL2\'s ongoing product development...', 'While this thread is in direct response to the announcement of the leaked version of CS: Source, it is not designed to provide any information to the persons responsible for the incident.\n\n\n\nI\'ll make this as simple as I can, because this has gone on long enough.\n\n\n\n6 years ago when Valve Software first released Half-Life, they came under a lot of scrutiny when the sourcecode for that game was hacked by someone who wanted to undermine their company.  I can\'t exactly remember whether anyone was caught, but it did cause a serious blow to gaming as a whole.  Then, after five years of development put into its sequal, the company was again attacked last year, when HL2\'s sourcecode and videos from E3 2003 were hacked straight from their own servers.\n\n\n\nThis also followed with several anonymous postings on the Net from the supposed hacker about how Valve had been lying to us about the status of the Source Engine.  Proceedings followed with several arrests worldwide of people in possesion of hacking materials that were needed to breach Valve-security.\n\n\n\nFinally today, HL2Central reported a leaked copy of CS: Source on a warez site, further spreading rumours about Valve\'s disloyalty.\n\n\n\nI don\'t know who is doing any of this, but if this is the same person who started this little drama, let me say this... maybe you\'re doing this to prove how good a hacker you are, maybe you\'re being paid for it from a competitor, I don\'t know, and frankly I don\'t really care.  If this is an attempt to make a name for yourself in the community, at best you are only making the rest of us wait longer for Half-Life 2 because they have to keep changing the encryptions on their servers.\n\n\n\nI call for all at Valve Software and in the community to rise up with me and rid ourselves of this continuing threat, whose desire is only to get their kicks from hacking games developers because they have nothign better to do with their time... like get a job.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(797774, 107476, 1013, 100009, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m doing my part, as I am pushing Microsoft to install an e-slap button on my computer as well as some backups for after I wear it out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(797783, 107476, 1013, 100246, 1072936800, '', 'thanks I had no idea you could download it.\n\n\n\nwell now I\'m going to.\n\n\n\nidiot.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(797786, 107476, 1013, 100174, 1072936800, '', 'Don\'t worry.\n\n\n\nThe "recently" leaked version of "CS Source" is actually part of the HL1Ports that leaked together with the HL2 beta in October 2003. It\'s nowhere as complete as the CS Source beta that\'s coming out soon.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(797796, 107476, 1013, 100246, 1072936800, '', 'lol ya I just looked.\n\n\n\nit\'s worth nothing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(797822, 107476, 1013, 100009, 1072936800, '', 'Ya basically anything from that alpha leak is jay you in kay junk, except for that amusement park ride video that was funny.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798393, 107546, 1013, 100252, 1072936800, 'Faulty Bans ?', 'I\'m hoping I\'m not the only case, but here it goes :x\n\n\n\nThe point of this so you don\'t get edgey is that I was banned from a server, with no indication why, and no admin banned me, strictly server.  I have never hacked in my entire life, nor use any scripts or modified any skins for CS.  It\'s the basic install with my own custom modifications (crosshair, sensitivity, nofrocem stuff, video/audio, et cetera).\n\n\n\nHere\'s what happened:  I joined a server, was playing de_prodigy, stays on that for 10 or so minutes, then changes to some aim map no one likes on a pub >.<  I do bad, but I stick it out, shooting up with some friends, not really trying as much as I am talking.  Then the map changes again to de_inferno.  Somehow, I do really well (that or the opposing team just really sucked, but it sounds better the other way :x), and I am able to kill 5 people in the first 30 seconds of the first round with all headshots, and as I\'m running to go kill another, I get a message that says that I\'m on the banned list.  \n\n\n\nIs there some type of detection that anti-cheat programs use that might have caused it to think my randomness could have been the sign of hacking ?\n\n\n\nI can still connect to VAC servers, but I can\'t connect to this particular server.  \n\n\n\nAny ideas on why I\'d get banned from a server ?  O_o\n\n\n\nAtre.\n\n\n\nPS  I suck at cs :x  and new nvidia driver is out, go go reforce !', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798401, 107546, 1013, 100253, 1072936800, '', 'An admin mayb thought it was suspicious.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798461, 107546, 1013, 100254, 1072936800, '', 'I heard hl guard monitors headshots and that many so qiuck might have triggered it to think aimbot and it ban cause of that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798603, 107546, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'So does CD.  Just dont go back to that server, there are 20k+ other servers.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798671, 107546, 1013, 100256, 1072936800, '', 'Uk2 servers have this for when you do really well.\n\n\n\nyou\'ll get warned and then banned for being to good.\n\nIt stops good players from owning the new starters.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798746, 107546, 1013, 100257, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ocarD \n\nSo does CD.  Just dont go back to that server, there are 20k+ other servers.  \n\n\n\nI thought CD blocked the cheat i didn\'t know it has a bit of hl guard in it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798761, 107546, 1013, 100258, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by zerostone \n\nI heard hl guard monitors headshots and that many so qiuck might have triggered it to think aimbot and it ban cause of that.  \n\n\n\nIf there\'s any truth to this statement (which I doubt) then that\'s the lamest detection method ever!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798804, 107546, 1013, 100255, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by interspaced \n\nI thought CD blocked the cheat i didn\'t know it has a bit of hl guard in it  \n\nI believe you can set a threshold in CD for headshots and once reached it kicks/bans you based on what the admin has set to penalty to be.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798816, 107546, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by psycho_thrasher \n\nIf there\'s any truth to this statement (which I doubt) then that\'s the lamest detection method ever!  Yup thats true. HLGuard detections blow. They are horrible. Ive been kicked from prolly 10 or so for an aimbot because I moved to the enemy too fast. Ummm no got a 14 sensitivity.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799060, 107546, 1013, 100259, 1072936800, '', 'HLguard aimbot detection is awesome.\n\n\n\nWe have tested it by downloading aimbots on non-vac servers and it did not take long for hlguard aimbot detection to catch us.\n\n\n\nWe use hlguard on our servers, and obvious hackers got caught again and again.\n\n\n\nHlguard not only catches aimbots, it also catches cheat scripts.\n\n\n\nGO HLGUARD........\n\n\n\n\n\nHlguard gave LIFE to Half-life Mods and CS.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799067, 107546, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Cheat scripts is a myth. \n\n\n\nHLGuard is horrible. Not only is the aimbot detection horrible but if you switch to your pistol too much itll detect that as a fast switch script. It also zaps power from the server and makes pings skyrocket. \n\n\n\nHLGuard is horrible. It detects me as having an aimbot and I suck.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799113, 107546, 1013, 100259, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bballr4567 \n\nCheat scripts is a myth. \n\n\n\nHLGuard is horrible. Not only is the aimbot detection horrible but if you switch to your pistol too much itll detect that as a fast switch script. It also zaps power from the server and makes pings skyrocket. \n\n\n\nHLGuard is horrible. It detects me as having an aimbot and I suck.  \n\n\n\n\n\nHlguard is the BEST Aimbot detection tool out there.\n\nIt is possible that n00b admins set it up poorly. But, with standard settings, Hlguard cannot go wrong (99% of the time).\n\n\n\nOn our server, we do give 2nd chance to those who gets caught+banned by hlguard just to take care of the 1% posibility of a false ban.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799283, 107546, 1013, 100260, 1072936800, '', 'Uhm I didn\'t think HLGuard detected aimbot at all, what it does is measure reaction time / speed and accuracy of shots and when it deems a shot too accurate and the reaction time too fast it logs it on a text called "aimwarn", the server admin decides what the aimwarn is set to normally being around 5/30 (5 flags on the list in 30 mins) but often admin who don\'t understand that seeing isn\'t all and that some players use sound :/ drop this setting to 3/30 or less, making the likelyhood of an honest player being banned much more likely. \n\n\n\nAlso whilst UA deny it, HLGuard does make mistakes with aimwarn, use it on a laggy under resourced server (and we all know how common they are) and you\'ll find it flags just about everyone as an aimbotter.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799302, 107546, 1013, 100261, 1072936800, '', 'That has got to be the worst way of detecting cheats I have ever heard. I always thought they had some sophisticated system to check the running processes and see if they were cheats, but now I am told it just checks if you are, in it\'s opinion, too good to be playing fairly..\n\n\n\nI pity the people who are so good at cs they get banned everywhere they go..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(800772, 107546, 1013, 100259, 1072936800, '', 'HLGUARD aimbot detection is pretty good, since we have tested it ourselves and have been using on all our  servers for over 1 year now:\n\n\n\n\n\nFrom United Admins, how hlguard works:\n\nquote:\n\nHLGuard\'s aimwarn works kind of like: Each frame (some frames skipped to reduce cpu usage) HLG draws a line from each player to each other (enemy) player. If there is a wall between then nothing is done except noting down the "time". As soon as 2 players can see eachother (enemies to eachother) HLGuard records time untill damage/kill, angle of crosshair movement, speed of crosshair movement and such things. Combined players will get aimwarns according to hlg_aimbotlevel.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798558, 107563, 1042, 100262, 1072936800, 'HLDS CS:Source Beta', 'When the beta comes out, will there be an opportunity to run hlds source too? I\'d like to run a CS source server at my cafe during beta.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(798820, 107563, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'I asked that a while ago, but no one seems to be able to answer ....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799459, 107563, 1042, 100030, 1072936800, '', 'Yes, we will also beta the HLDS:S when we start CS:S beta.  You will be able to host a server.\n\n\n\nMike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799842, 107563, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'Excellent :-D', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(802740, 107563, 1042, 100264, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Mike Dunkle \n\nYes, we will also beta the HLDS:S when we start CS:S beta.  You will be able to host a server.\n\n\n\nMike  \n\n\n\nwil it be win32 hlds:s only? or will we also be (pleasantly  ) suprised with a linux hlds:s []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807437, 107563, 1042, 100265, 1072936800, '', 'knock, knock... will it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(813846, 107563, 1042, 100266, 1072936800, '', 'what is HLDS?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(813909, 107563, 1042, 100030, 1072936800, '', '"Half-Life Dedicated Server"\n\n\n\nYes.  A linux version of the server will be made available during the beta.\n\n\n\nMike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(820445, 107563, 1042, 100267, 1072936800, '', 'Thatks for replying irs always good to see a post from a Valve member.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(833142, 107563, 1042, 100268, 1072936800, '', 'Will the resource requirements for linux servers vary greatly from HLDS:Source to normal HLDS?\n\n\n\nLewis', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(833336, 107563, 1042, 100119, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SaintsServers \n\nWill the resource requirements for linux servers vary greatly from HLDS:Source to normal HLDS?\n\n\n\nLewis  \n\n\n\nLinux Binary > Windows', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(833531, 107563, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'No way ! :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(833583, 107563, 1042, 100268, 1072936800, '', 'Ok - but what about CPU/memory usuage, for running a CS:Source server on linux, in comparison to running a CS 1.6 server on linux?\n\n\n\nLewis\n\nSaintsServers.com', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(834740, 107563, 1042, 100269, 1072936800, '', 'This would be great to know.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(836391, 107563, 1042, 100270, 1072936800, '', 'hi,\n\n\n\ncan "normaly" people also host a cs:source Linux Beta Server? Because we have no Cyber Cafe !\n\n\n\nWill the CPU Usage drops a little bit on the Linux Servers? :-))\n\nI think it will drop 100% []\n\n\n\nthx', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(799816, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, 'TFC keeps crashing - even after a format!', 'Ok, for a few days now Team Fortress Classic has been making my PC crash. What happens:\n\n\n\n_______________________________\n\n\n\n\n\nFine for a minite or two..\n\n\n\nOh-er a bit of lag, maybe my brother is downloading?\n\n\n\nBut he\'s sleeping! WTF...\n\n\n\nIt\'s lagging again, oh, this is local lag, not connection lag.\n\n\n\nAhhh this is annoying, oh it\'s moving again.\n\n\n\nFS it\'s stopped again........still not doing anything..........hello??..............bah PC Crashed totally!\n\n\n\nCRTL + ALT + DEL!!!!! Bahh who stole task manager??\n\n\n\nPC Froze, pressing reset - again. Lost all IRC and MSN connections, etc, all messages awaiting gone but oh well. And hey, lets not save any changed Windows settings either.\n\n\n\n_______________________________\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd before you ask, these are NOT the problem:\n\n\n\n> The server I\'m on, I\'ve tried many, and I get a ping of 20ms to them too!\n\n> My TFC Files, I formatted my hard disk and this STILL happens. Also, the team fortress classic.gcf file was not backed up so that is totally fresh.\n\n\n\n_______________________________\n\n\n\n\n\nWhat\'s up Steam? Fix this please, TFC happens to be my favourite all-time game and I\'d happily buy Team Fortress 2 (when it finally comes out), but not with this problem. It\'s putting me off the whole game.\n\n\n\nThanks in advance for supporting,\n\n\n\nAdam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(800216, 107680, 1005, 100272, 1072936800, 'Specs?', 'Can we see some system specs?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(800731, 107680, 1005, 100042, 1072936800, '', 'Also, try running TFC without any other programs running (i.e.: msn, irc, kazaa, bittorrent).\n\n\n\nSpecs are needed though...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(800928, 107680, 1005, 100273, 1072936800, '', 'Doubt its steam.  Is your connection active when your PC is idle?  I took my PC out of my firewall and stuck it in a DMZ to download some stuff over bittorrent.  After sticking it back in my connection was always active.  Looking around I had files I never heard of in task manager.  Closing them and deleting stopped the problem and didnt cause any nasty system crashes looking for files that were deleted.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.thebanlist.com/forums/sh...highlight=files (http://www.thebanlist.com/forums/showthread.php?t=512&highlight=files)\n\n\n\nIve also had another one on someone elses PC not too long ago that I had to fix\n\n\n\nhttp://forums.freddyshouse.com/showthread.php?t=22357 (http://forums.freddyshouse.com/showthread.php?t=22357)\n\n\n\nAt the time google didnt show up anything for netclna.exe.  Now however it brings up spyware and trojan websites.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801708, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, 'Specs?', 'quote:Originally posted by Blackcrisis \n\nCan we see some system specs? \n\nRead my sig []\n\n\n\n\n\nIt\'s highly odd how this has only happened for the last one or two days :/ it\'s been fine for over a year before.\n\n\n\nI\'ll try it without msn and irc.\n\n\n\nMy router is UPnP, so forwarding shouldn\'t be needed, besides I have 27015 TCP/UDP open for when I run small games for friends.\n\n\n\n\n\nI forgot to mention, TFC is the ONLY game doing this. Counter-Strike, Day of Defeat, etc are all working in perfect condition.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801736, 107680, 1005, 100274, 1072936800, '', 'Tried a surface scan of your hard disk, and/or checked your RAM?\n\n\n\nMade sure your video card (and other hardware) drivers are up to date?\n\n\n\nTried changing settings, particularly video settings?  Try TFC on 640x480, or try D3D instead of OpenGL.\n\n\n\nChecked through your active processes to see if there is something unknown or otherwise suspect?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801762, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Fester \n\nTried a surface scan of your hard disk, and/or checked your RAM?\n\n\n\nMade sure your video card (and other hardware) drivers are up to date?\n\n\n\nTried changing settings, particularly video settings?  Try TFC on 640x480, or try D3D instead of OpenGL.\n\n\n\nChecked through your active processes to see if there is something unknown or otherwise suspect? \n\nDone defrag, RAM is fine (1280 MB).\n\n\n\nDrivers all up to date.\n\n\n\nCurrently using 1024x768 windowed in OpenGL but I\'ll try D3D.\n\n\n\nNo dodgey processes running (spyware, virus, etc).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801770, 107680, 1005, 100040, 1072936800, '', 'TFC eventually freezes then and you have to reboot?  Does it freeze at the same screen each time?\n\n\n\nIs TFC up to date?  If you right click on TFC in the games list does it show 100% and ready to play?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801810, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'TFC is perfectly up to date, and no not at a particular screen. Just within 3-5 minites of play.\n\n\n\n\n\nEDIT: Tried Direct 3D, still crashed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(801928, 107680, 1005, 100273, 1072936800, '', '/me points to fdisk', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(802013, 107680, 1005, 100272, 1072936800, '', 'Try directly connecting to your internet if you use a router...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(802019, 107680, 1005, 100042, 1072936800, '', 'If you haven\'t tried yet, try deleting the local game content and start over again.  (Go to Steam icon -> Games -> right-click on TFC -> "Delete local game content")... but make sure you back your config/sprites/maps before you do.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(802151, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'i formatted the hard disk and redownloaded the content lol', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(813744, 107680, 1005, 100041, 1072936800, '', 'If you are experiencing freezing lag, etc... that can sometimes cause the game to crash, try these commands:\n\n\n\nrate 999999\n\ncl_cmdrate 100\n\ncl_updaterate 100\n\n\n\nSometimes steam just completely resets these to the default values which are.. well... crap.\n\n\n\nDefault Values:\n\n\n\nrate 7500\n\ncl_cmdrate 30\n\ncl_updaterate 30\n\n\n\nUsually setting these commands to 999999, 100, and 100 respectively takes away most, if not all of my lag. Check these settings often if you are experiencing lag, for they will reset very often.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(814326, 107680, 1005, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'i have an autoexec.cfg that sets these values when i start the game though :/\n\n\n\n________________\n\nMy AUTOEXEC.CFG\n\n\n\n\n\n// <email hidden> Half-Life Configuration\n\n// Autoexec.cfg\n\n\n\nECHO Setting configuration from Autoexec.cfg...\n\n\n\ncl_lw "1"\n\ncl_lc "1"\n\ncl_download_ingame "1"\n\ncl_allowupload "1"\n\ncl_updaterate "45"\n\ncl_rate "20000"\n\ncl_cmdrate "100"\n\ncl_cmdbackup "2"\n\ncl_showfps "1"\n\nfps_max "100"\n\nfps_modem "0"\n\nhud_fastswitch "1"\n\nmp_decals "300"\n\nrate "20000"\n\n\n\nbind 1 slot1\n\nbind 2 slot2\n\nbind 3 slot3\n\nbind 4 slot4\n\nbind 5 slot5\n\nbind 6 slot6\n\nbind 7 slot7\n\nbind 8 slot8\n\nbind 9 slot9\n\nbind 0 slot10\n\n\n\n// End of File', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806206, 108229, 1013, 103479, 1072936800, 'Another rant.', 'Now, I am normally a steam enthusiast. I always have defended VALVe in the whole crowd of hating Steam. But, I am tired of this lag. It is affecting my score and my server. Also, the friends network is always down. Wtf is with that? Kinda BS if you ask me. I need it because my friends use multiple IM programs (F*ck trillian), and I use friends to contact them. When will it be resolved? No, I don\'t think I was ripped off like another thread. I paid only $20 for my CD key. But I do feel like we could be getting a little more. But, I do appriciate all the work VALVe is doing. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806233, 108229, 1013, 100271, 1072936800, 'Another rant.', 'quote:Originally posted by Spazztastic \n\nAlso, the friends network is always down. Wtf is with that? Kinda BS if you ask me. I need it because my friends use multiple IM programs (F*ck trillian), and I use friends to contact them. When will it be resolved? No, I don\'t think I was ripped off like another thread. I paid only $20 for my CD key. \n\n\n\nYes, you paid.\n\nYou paid for a video game - not a friends network.\n\n\n\nI don\'t recall us getting a friends network originaly, and nobody is paying any extra to have one.\n\n\n\ntbh, for $20, or around �8 in UK, you get Half-Life, Counter-Strike, Day of Defeat, Team Fortress Classic, Deathmatch Classic, Ricochet, and all the third party mods you can eat. You can\'t really expect anything more for so little.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806237, 108229, 1013, 103479, 1072936800, '', 'I run a CS server (and I make money off it), so its important I have a way to contact my admins though.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806248, 108229, 1013, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'yes but there are many instant messengers for that, internet relay chat, forums, email.\n\n\n\n\n\nsteam friends is a lucky bonus. nobody is paying for it apart from valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806250, 108229, 1013, 100134, 1072936800, '', 'you were able to communicate with your clanmates before steam was released - so why bothering about friends?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806253, 108229, 1013, 103479, 1072936800, '', 'I never played HL/CS/Anything before Steam. I only play 1.5 at LAN parties.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806271, 108229, 1013, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'i play nearly every mod [] Valve offer so much for a little price.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806299, 108229, 1013, 101571, 1072936800, '', 'Friend\'s working, at least for me.\n\n\n\nAbout lag... Try to adjust some settings. Beginning in your steam-settings, connection-tab.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806364, 108229, 1013, 100246, 1072936800, '', 'DONT INTRDUCE THINGS THAT DONT WORK FOR ANYONE\n\n\n\nSO what if we didn\'t pay for the friends network, STOP sticking up for VALVE your not gona become a mod or something.\n\n\n\nThey MADE us download FRIENDS so it\'s SHOULD work bottom line.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806491, 108229, 1013, 103479, 1072936800, '', 'Both sides make strong points. But I go with stanley. If your going to put it in there, make it work. Or take the PoS out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(806638, 108229, 1013, 100538, 1072936800, '', 'Why dont you give them time to take it out?  Are they not working on enough already?  Do you think they have an army of a million workers ready to fix your every personal problem?  \n\n\n\n\n\nStanley M. --\n\nValve did not make you download anything.  Friends came inside of STEAM which you downloaded, by yourself.  And Stanely, you post "dont introduce things [Friends] that dont work for anyone" right after someone that posts that Friends is working for them.  Tell me how that makes sense?\n\n\n\nCG1 -- You say the same things I said in other posts, and these people are acting the same towards you as others towards me where I posted.  It\'s pretty draining to try to explain to people they\'re expectations are to high.  I think its futile to try to stop their ulcers from forming. However its nice to see someone that is defending common sense.  Even though we seem like we\'re sucking up to Valve for it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807711, 108229, 1013, 100069, 1072936800, '', 'I can see valve are busy anyone can see that..but if your going to include something make it work or get rid. \n\n\n\nOn the other hand having a friends network there doesnt harm the user in anyway.. its a nice bonus especially when it works', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807735, 108229, 1013, 103480, 1072936800, '', 'No, but the whole point of steam was to eliminate hassles like having to use 3rd party apps like messengers and the likes, and yet people pretty much have to, plus these lag and performance issues don\'t give me tons of confidence in the system.  \n\n\n\nYou\'ll notice the fanbois have pretty much given up on defending steam besides saying "shut up whiney n00b," or "oh god, heres another one."\n\n\n\nBut honestly, what is the point of steam now?  It was touted as an all in one, sever browser, updater, launcher, buddy list/IMing.  Updating seems to be a joke, with valve updating at some of the worst possible times, not seeming to consult with clans and league organizers.  The afformentioned friends list seems to be a failure at the moment, and having a performance issues with hardware that there is really no excuse to have them (and then the fanbois saying "well you just don\'t know anything about computers," or something similar).\n\n\n\nSo really?  Why is steam so great?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807747, 108229, 1013, 100538, 1072936800, '', '"oh god heres another one","shut up you whiney n00b"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807817, 108229, 1013, 100271, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Stanley M \n\nDONT INTRDUCE THINGS THAT DONT WORK FOR ANYONE\n\n\n\nSO what if we didn\'t pay for the friends network, STOP sticking up for VALVE your not gona become a mod or something.\n\n\n\nThey MADE us download FRIENDS so it\'s SHOULD work bottom line.  \n\nYes, they made you download friends. It\'s part of steam. Try reading the valve subscriber agreement.\n\n\n\nand yes, I was sticking up for valve for this reason, because we DIDN\'T pay for a friends network. We paid for a video game. Running steam isn\'t cheap you know.\n\n\n\nAnd you should think about what you type because what you said there makes you look like a right idiot.\n\n\n\nquote:Originaly posted by undeniable\n\nWhy dont you give them time to take it out? Are they not working on enough already? Do you think they have an army of a million workers ready to fix your every personal problem?\n\n\n\n\n\nStanley M. --\n\nValve did not make you download anything. Friends came inside of STEAM which you downloaded, by yourself. And Stanely, you post "dont introduce things [Friends] that dont work for anyone" right after someone that posts that Friends is working for them. Tell me how that makes sense?\n\n\n\nCG1 -- You say the same things I said in other posts, and these people are acting the same towards you as others towards me where I posted. It\'s pretty draining to try to explain to people they\'re expectations are to high. I think its futile to try to stop their ulcers from forming. However its nice to see someone that is defending common sense. Even though we seem like we\'re sucking up to Valve for it.\n\nBoth good points yes but there are alot of kids around whining things aren\'t working, when they don\'t even contribute to them. Nobody pays for steam friends network apart from Valve. They are a business and are suppost to be making money, not losing. tbh the sensible people here are getting damn fed up of people complaining constantly about steam, friends, etc when they don\'t know how hard it is to impliment and maintain a network like Steam.\n\n\n\nSteam is one of a kind, no other company has done anything like it. Of couse there are going to be problems fs.\n\n\n\nquote:Originaly posted by Dauvin\n\nNo, but the whole point of steam was to eliminate hassles like having to use 3rd party apps like messengers and the likes, and yet people pretty much have to, plus these lag and performance issues don\'t give me tons of confidence in the system.\n\n\n\nYou\'ll notice the fanbois have pretty much given up on defending steam besides saying "shut up whiney n00b," or "oh god, heres another one."\n\n\n\nBut honestly, what is the point of steam now? It was touted as an all in one, sever browser, updater, launcher, buddy list/IMing. Updating seems to be a joke, with valve updating at some of the worst possible times, not seeming to consult with clans and league organizers. The afformentioned friends list seems to be a failure at the moment, and having a performance issues with hardware that there is really no excuse to have them (and then the fanbois saying "well you just don\'t know anything about computers," or something similar).\n\n\n\nSo really? Why is steam so great?\n\nAs I just said - Steam is one of a kind, nobody has ever made an automated content system like this on such a massive scale. It can\'t be perfect first time. I mean, look at Windows 95. **** loads of bugs, but that was one of a kind at it\'s time, and now we\'re on XP/2003 things are improving. Give steam time.\n\n\n\nAbout performance issues, over 90% of people complaining about performance and lag with steam is because of their own computer. Alot of people seem to be forgetting the point that technology moves forward. It doesn\'t stand still and it most certainly doesn\'t go backwards (apart from with Windows ME but I won\'t go into that). If people use old computers, they are going to get poor performance. Steam does not need changing to improve performance, users computers do. Have you seen the half life 2 hardware survey page? There are people with 16 MHz computers using steam, which is absolutely crap and yet I bet they all complain.\n\n\n\nYou mentioned about "shut up whiney noob, etc". Well the only reason people here say that is because there are far to many ungreatful spoilt brats around constantly whining about steam when 9 times out of 10 it\'s their own fault. Steam was made for the majority, not the minority.\n\n\n\nNow your mentioning valve updating at worse times? m8 shut up. How the hell can valve know when it\'s a good time to update or not for people? "Oh hey, dauvin doesn\'t want steam updated now lets wait a whole month to release this important bug fix and piss loads of people off just to suit him". And about consulting with clans and leages, now your really losing it tbh, what the hell? It\'s not up to valve to inform every clan and league orginiser about an update or whatever happens, why should have change their busy enough schedule just to suit the minority, it\'s not as if we pay much towards steam.\n\n\n\nand yes we all seem to know by now that friends has failed but you are missing the point that we paid for a video game, not a friends network, or board games. We pay so little for a half life cd key that grants us so many games.\n\n\n\nWhy is steam so great? Well, ok steam has some bugs, it\'s not perfect but why dont you try implimenting such an automated network yourself? Can you do that? Didn\'t think so. Almost as stupid as when a whole croud boo at someones football shot, when most of them can\'t even kick the ball.\n\n\n\n\n\n________\n\n\n\nOk that\'s the end of this long post [] Thanks for reading.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807773, 108354, 1013, 103476, 1072936800, 'Hack detection built into steam', 'Well, I know this is a big task yet if completed it would be beneficial to all, especially server owners who want rock sloid proof if someone hacks or not. \n\n\n\nI play and am admin on the [RAW] server and we catch quite a few aimbotters. Many contest the ban incurred by HLGaurd, yet we stay firm with the ban. Even though we have full trust in the system it would further help us and thousands others to be able to determine someone with hacks or not by using a trusted software program and what\'s better than steam?\n\n\n\nThis is the reason why I decided to suggest this, a player recently who is scared he will get banned due to recieving several HLG flags said this:\n\n\n\nquote:im getting really freaked out. i got aimbot warning #2. so im wondering if theres a program to find any hax downloads or something. this stuff is really freaking me out again.\n\n\n\nMany people, at least people who don\'t live alone, have others using their computers and hence have access to CS and the internet and can potentially download hacks onto one\'s system without letting the owner know. This was the case for one or two palyers on our server and we set them straight, keeping our trust in them. Maybe something like this won\'t be able to be handled effectively by vavle, yet it\'s  a place to start.\n\n\n\nBTW, I have posted this issue on UA forums as well, take a look and see the replies: http://forums.unitedadmins.com/inde...t=0#entry234090 (http://forums.unitedadmins.com/index.php?act=ST&f=185&t=40513&st=0#entry234090)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807788, 108354, 1013, 100063, 1072936800, '', 'You never heard of VAC (Valve Anti Cheat)?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807806, 108354, 1013, 103477, 1072936800, '', 'Unfortunatly, thats a major flaw in steams design, one of the only ones. There is no way to tell for an absolute certainty that a player did not place a hack themselves. It is the responsibility of the user to safegaurd his/her own computer against roomies/siblings/hobos not steam\'s. Someone once suggested a more secure email disclosure, when his password was easily guessable. How does HLG work for you? does it work better than VAC?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(807858, 108354, 1013, 103476, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, HLG is doing a great job, and in my opinion is far more effective than VAC. Then again, I have not had a chance to play with the code, yet with experience I believe that HLG is superior to VAC. Just my humble opinion.\n\n\n\nAnd I understand that there is a level of one\'s own responsibility involved in maintaining a cheat free computer, but being able to scan for unknown hacks on one\'s hard drive is a nice thing to have.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(808639, 108354, 1013, 100180, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Dizzman786 \n\nActually, HLG is doing a great job, and in my opinion is far more effective than VAC. Then again, I have not had a chance to play with the code, yet with experience I believe that HLG is superior to VAC. Just my humble opinion.\n\n\n\nAnd I understand that there is a level of one\'s own responsibility involved in maintaining a cheat free computer, but being able to scan for unknown hacks on one\'s hard drive is a nice thing to have.  \n\n\n\nHave I read right? HLG superior to VAC? \n\n\n\nHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA.\n\n\n\nCome on bud, you cannot be that ignorant. You have no clue about VAC or it\'s capabilities. You have no idea how it works or just how effective it is. Have you played on a VAC enabled server? I have played on many HLG servers and have seen way too many cheaters. \n\n\n\nVAC > HLG\n\n\n\nVAC > Anything.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809301, 108354, 1013, 100203, 1072936800, '', 'screw the hacks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809534, 108354, 1013, 100012, 1072936800, '', 'uh, sorry Jeff, but last time someone told me VAC was omnipotent I told them to give me his server\'s IP (it was a nice coincidence he had a server that ran VAC) and I downloaded some hack. booted them up, went to his server, and he never got a single warning about me. ever.\n\n\n\nthere\'s no system that can 100% tell you someone\'s hacking and be right all of the time.\n\n\n\nCheating Death SOUNDS like it could, but I don\'t know enough about it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810289, 108354, 1013, 103476, 1072936800, '', 'And Jeff, another thing.\n\n\n\nIf you read my first post then you would know that we run a WARCRAFT server. VAC software would catch everyone that IS NOT a hacker, why? Because VAC is not fully compatible with WAR3 gameplay, however, HLG can be made compatible to a WAR3 server. It won\'t be perfect, but it will still do a better job than VAC. Which is why I said that in my opinion HLG owns VAC. And thank you Darius for further proof of VAC\'s incompitence. And I know HLG is not perfect either, nothing is except God.\n\n\n\nAnd please don\'t post unnecessary posts and waste others\' time, I don\'t care for posts that say "screw the hacks" that is plain ignorant.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810545, 108354, 1013, 103478, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Maxey \n\nYou never heard of VAC (Valve Anti Cheat)?  sorry but that still doesn\'t work...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810604, 108354, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'HLG\'s aimbot detection is horrible. All it is is an educated guess. Someone moves the xhair to thier enemy a little too fast and OMG you are an aimbotter. \n\n\n\nAlso VAC does not warn any admins if a hacker has been playing on thier server. It will never do so. \n\n\n\nMany people like HLG because you get to know which players are supposedly cheating but do you care that much that you believe in a system that guesses??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809556, 108539, 1005, 100282, 1072936800, 'New CS Idea', 'Please introduce an invisible clown with two TMP\'s and a flashbang cannon on his shoulder. This can be done before game unavailable and constant cs crashes are addressed, those are not important. Also the chicken graphics need to be updated, HE grenades should leave a rainbow arch, there should be a midget CT like OddJob in Golden eye and the p90 still needs that scope....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809560, 108539, 1005, 100283, 1072936800, '', 'for real though, p90 should penetrate....\n\n\n\n\n\nback tot he updates valve will put in... cts should get dogs, stinkbombs......hmmc ant think of anythign stupid , i\'ll leave it to you valve., oh wait i know, disable the game for hundred of users with unspecific and unneded warnings and eror boxes, oh wait you already did that too....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809609, 108539, 1005, 100284, 1072936800, '', 'I think that CT\'s should have prisoners that they can undress and put bags on and then they should be equpped with $10 Kodak disposable cameras.\n\n\n\nCT\'s should also get letters that explode and T\'s should get helicopters that turn into bats and stuff like that.\n\n\n\nAll kills and explosions should be turned into large animations like in the classic Batman show where it just says BAM! or KABOOM! or AK-47!\n\n\n\nFinally, there should be a new class called "Valve" since we all know they are the most destructive group of all.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(809935, 108539, 1005, 100285, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by federal \n\nI think that CT\'s should have prisoners that they can undress and put bags on and then they should be equpped with $10 Kodak disposable cameras.\n\n\n\nCT\'s should also get letters that explode and T\'s should get helicopters that turn into bats and stuff like that.\n\n\n\nAll kills and explosions should be turned into large animations like in the classic Batman show where it just says BAM! or KABOOM! or AK-47!\n\n\n\nFinally, there should be a new class called "Valve" since we all know they are the most destructive group of all.  \n\n\n\n\n\nlmfao...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810039, 108539, 1005, 100206, 1072936800, '', 'I think we should we should get fully functional Gundams / AGWS / Mechs, but only for the Terrorists, as a counter for the shield. CTs should get a Metal Gear RAY (Ala MGS2: Sons of Liberty)  and both dust maps should be deleted from the installer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810378, 108539, 1005, 100286, 1072936800, '', 'Holy ****, you people don\'t know that those sarcastic CS suggestions are old?\n\n\n\nGuys, that joke died out a LOOOONG time ago. Try to come up with something new.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(810386, 108539, 1005, 100283, 1072936800, '', 'it\'s still satisfying to do after each complete **** up on valve\'s part.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(811964, 108539, 1005, 100282, 1072936800, '', 'Well, when they take something that\'s working fine and consistantly break it people get upset. When they try to fix things no one cares about while ignoring serious bugs and issues that have been brought up to them repeatedly people get upset. When the game no longer works because of an update no one wants anyway people get upset. When pretty much the entire community goes from stable cs to crashing cs and are told to check their OS people get upset. I\'m just a sarcastic person, I\'m not going to create  a real thread to explain the existing problems because they\'ve all been brought up before and if there\'s one thing I know it\'s the developers just don\'t care. They couldn\'t have tested this patch before they released it to steam users. Why do I say this? Because it crashes cs all over the place, how do you not notice this?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(811974, 108539, 1005, 100287, 1072936800, '', 'i have new idea for steam, which effects cs. no more updates!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(814525, 108539, 1005, 100284, 1072936800, '', 'I have an idea, give us 1.5 back!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1043076, 108540, 1005, 100288, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m amazed that any elf-respecting company would release a game as buggy as this. \n\n\n\nWhat amazes me more was the bug I came across the day where the Headshots don\'t kill. I recorded a demo of me putting I believe 6-8 awp shots into an AFKs face double zoomed in, he wasn\'t lagged out,a nd if he was he still would have been shootable. None of these shots registered or killed, and as an awp, the bullet entered the front of his head and the back, failing to trigger and hit boxes. I can send the demo to any Valve people.\n\n\n\nIts still really good comedy, so maybe you shouldn\'t fix it.\n\n\n\n\n\nI hope CS:S is a hell of alot better, bug wise, then this release of 1.6.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1043547, 108540, 1005, 100289, 1072936800, '', 'happens to me with 1% of my shots in clanwars (I got used to to where the boxes are :)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1043733, 108540, 1005, 100290, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t know if it is a "bug" but it is really annoying.... In normal play if your running and you get shot you move slower, well if you get shot while on a ladder but don\'t die and then get off the ladder no matter how long ago you where shot you will walk slow like you just got shot', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050214, 108540, 1005, 100288, 1072936800, 'Another Bug', 'lolol. not sure if this one has been around alot or not.\n\n\n\nbut, yesterday I was chillin with a clanmat in assault using pumps only, and he was comng in the back door, and he threw a smoke grenade at the door, so the door opened, he ran in, let it close then ran out. (not sure why). He then, put his character against the door. THe part that would touch the Door FRAME when it closes, not like the body of it, but the end, He then became ATTACHED to the door and his character would follow the path of that door.\n\n\n\nI went and I saw it, so I wa slike, ok let me try it. So Ir estarted round and went back, smoked the door and same thing happened, execpt I was land sharking, and then he jumped on my head and we were swinging with the door together.\n\n\n\nI have that on Demo too. lol\n\n\n\nIt was pretty funny. But I also think its the same thing that gets me killed with doors, where the door closes and yoiur dragged in with it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1055561, 108540, 1005, 100291, 1072936800, '', 'i record a demo when i play... once a time i my little brother buried in the ground........ lol..it wasn\'t punishment for  tk and  he can move.... [] muahahaha very funny...was he digging?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1082229, 108540, 1005, 100292, 1072936800, '', 'My CS completely shuts down if I alt + tab out to any other program.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1083541, 108540, 1005, 100036, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Apex \n\nMy CS completely shuts down if I alt + tab out to any other program.  \n\n\n\nThat isnt a bug. I only know of one other person who has that problem, and i think it has to do with the RAM. He only has 256MB on WINXP.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1087704, 108540, 1005, 100293, 1072936800, '', 'Hey I have noticed Hitboxbuggs in the head and i think stomac or chest ! \n\ni started to play bad after the update .. i thought: well there\'s nothing wrong with cs (what i noticed) until yesterday i shot a person and i heard 5 Hits i heard them i was like 5 meters close to him but he killed me and a text came up where it showed that i made 2 hits! \n\n\n\nand also i played aim_aztec and i was left alone with the last CT who was AFK i had awp and i aimed with dubble zoom for his head it was right in the middle of the head i shot 3 times and  two of those missed until the third made a hit sry i dont have anny demo on this but i think someone in this thread had one with the awp thingy.\n\n\n\nplz release an update with this bugg as soon as possible it should be released soon in like a day or two.. because the last update were a month ago\n\n\n\nsry for bad english *swedish* :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1088123, 108540, 1005, 100292, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by GerMaN eLiTe \n\nThat isnt a bug. I only know of one other person who has that problem, and i think it has to do with the RAM. He only has 256MB on WINXP.  \n\n\n\n\n\nThing is, it never did it before until about a week ago.  It\'s a fresh install of Steam, too.  I have 512mb DDR.  I noticed I can alt-tab out while I\'m in the menu but in CS (not playing) but when I alt-tab back, it shuts it down quickly.  Oh well, I guess I\'ll try re-installing it...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1096125, 108540, 1005, 100036, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by secure \n\nHey I have noticed Hitboxbuggs in the head and i think stomac or chest ! \n\ni started to play bad after the update .. i thought: well there\'s nothing wrong with cs (what i noticed) until yesterday i shot a person and i heard 5 Hits i heard them i was like 5 meters close to him but he killed me and a text came up where it showed that i made 2 hits! \n\n\n\nand also i played aim_aztec and i was left alone with the last CT who was AFK i had awp and i aimed with dubble zoom for his head it was right in the middle of the head i shot 3 times and  two of those missed until the third made a hit sry i dont have anny demo on this but i think someone in this thread had one with the awp thingy.\n\n\n\nplz release an update with this bugg as soon as possible it should be released soon in like a day or two.. because the last update were a month ago\n\n\n\nsry for bad english *swedish* :P  \n\n\n\nAbout the first thing, it may be that your cl_updaterate is of low value. I would prefer to have at least 45 set to that cvar.\n\n\n\nThe hit boxes on AFKs are quite often very screwy/weird. If they are afk, expect some hitboxes to be unbalanced.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1099261, 108540, 1005, 100293, 1072936800, '', 'i live in sweden with 8mbit dsl i have a ping due 25-30\n\nand my cl_updaterate is on 70 and my cl_cmdrate is at 70 too and they are not to hight we often use 101 101 here but i have a better ping with 70 70', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1106391, 108540, 1005, 100294, 1072936800, '', 'When I\'m in Counterstrike, and I try to press alt+tab, it goes into a black screen, and after about 10 seconds it restarts my computer.  Does anyone know how to fix this or what\'s wrong??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1110169, 108540, 1005, 100295, 1072936800, '', 'When spamming with guns (spraying) i\'ve found that the gun wont automatically reload , and i have to press slot2;slot1 , or use last inv 2 times to be able to use my gun. this bug exists for me in counter strike and condition zero', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1111500, 108540, 1005, 100289, 1072936800, '', 'there are two bugs with the deagle (that might be related)\n\n\n\nyou can shoot very fast with the deagle and after that nor reload animation/sound will be played (and reloading seems to take longer  than usual).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1112457, 108540, 1005, 100296, 1072936800, '', 'when shooting with any gun, for a second the model will stop firing, the sound for the first person guns will stop, but the bullets will still register in the server.\n\n\n\na minor bug, but annoying at times', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(812531, 108860, 1013, 103481, 1072936800, 'Continuous Game Crashes - Memory Errors', 'Howdy all,\n\n\n\nI\'ve been hopping from server to server trying to see wether or not it\'s just been me that has been seeing consistant crashes of CS, but I\'ve talked to many people and this is not the case.\n\n\n\nEveryone seems to be getting a certain memory error:\n\n\n\n"The Instruction at "0x0f3a5969" referenced memory at "0x0f635808". The memory coule not be "read".\n\n\n\nClick on OK to terminate the program."\n\n\n\nAnywho, I\'ve noticed that it only happens when there is a kill or a hit from the Auto Sniper Rifles, the Scout, and the AWP (we all know which weapons)... If there is a way to fix this cool, I would try the Linksys Firmware crap if I felt like it, but I\'m in a bad mood already, and I don\'t believe that I should have to change the settings of my router in order to be compatible with the new CS update... \n\n\n\nWhy not rollback to the last update? I thought it had been working beautifully ever since the Friends list had been updated. I don\'t want servers to ban the weapons because of the update. I like my scout... []\n\n\n\nWell anywho, that\'s all I got... By the way, I like this guy:\n\n\n\n"steam gave us the update with the error \n\nsteam will give us the error fix\n\ni will not change a thing in my pc \n\n\n\n\n\nsteam is ****ed up fix it or lose a lot of customers"\n\n\n\nMaybe a tad harsh but... I think we all just want to play some CS.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(812540, 108860, 1013, 100901, 1072936800, '', 'Valve will fix it, just give thme time!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(812549, 108860, 1013, 100342, 1072936800, '', 'i agree\n\n\n\njsut go back a couple of days to the last update and leave it for a while!\n\n\n\nNo need for a update every F###en month!\n\n\n\nI just wish it would go back the way it was when it first started otut!!\n\n\n\n-Petrides, Dam u Steam', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(812558, 108860, 1013, 103481, 1072936800, '', 'I know they will, \n\n\n\nbut why not rollback while they try and fix it, rather than have a buggy version of CS up and running for several days??\n\n\n\nQuote: "Dam you Steam"\n\n\n\nNone of that []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(812668, 108860, 1013, 103482, 1072936800, 'Dammit', 'Well dammit! Its happening to me too. I dont know what the problem is but its happening to me and it sux. Some one help us that is smarter than me. My favorite map is scoutzknivez...this is dumb i wanna play that map. Stoopid, steam...Get Rid of this Bug!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
