(1051512, 110442, 1013, 100376, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by indpndnt \n\nwhen i pre-loaded Hl2...in whitch folder does it downloads ? In the SteamApps folder in your Steam folder... you\'ll just see a file called base source shared materials.gcf. It\'s mainly textures and stuff, and encrypted so it\'s basically useless data until you activate it by buying off Steam or entering the CD-key from a box copy or coupon. This is all after it\'s released, of course.\n\n\n\nYou can\'t play Half Life 2 using a Condition Zero key.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1051577, 110442, 1013, 100376, 1072936800, '', 'About registering the coupon to play CS:Source beta and get the premiere pack... I know you can enter it by trying to run HL and then you get a prompt for the key. But what if you already have Half Life? That won\'t ask for a CD key. So where do you get Steam to ask for a key, to use CS:S?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
