(834972, 111208, 1005, 100386, 1072936800, 'Video Evidence: Quickswitching was not an exploit', 'Now that the awp delay has been in the game for a while and the arguing has diminished a bit, i\'d like to show actual proof that quickswitching was not an exploit.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi (http://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi)\n\n\n\nCreated by Drax (previously of zEx). zEx was one of the top American clans in case you didnt know.\n\n\n\nI\'m not complaining or trying to get CS back to the good ol days, i\'m just stating some simple facts here people.\n\n\n\nJeff Cliffe says this was a "quickswitch exploit".  \n\n\n\nDraw your own conclusions.\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nedit #1: there is another video made by sacko\n\n\n\nhttp://home.online.no/~ovassend/awp.avi (http://home.online.no/~ovassend/awp.avi)\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nedit #2: Also, if you wish to discuss the use of Quickshots, at least know what they are first.  Here are 3 demos of it, all by different top players.  This is more evidence that i wish to show of why the delay was added, i think everyone should watch at least one of these demos.\n\n\n\nKsharp: http://www.team3d.net/index.php?s=demos&id=115 (http://www.team3d.net/index.php?s=demos&id=115)\n\n\n\n* this demo is in 1.6 before the awp delay was implemented. You also have to register(it\'s free) on Team3D\'s website to d/l this. Deathmatch server, alot of nice awp and deagle action.\n\n\n\nPag.Xero: http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/546/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/546/)\n\n\n\n*this is a 1.3 demo(you can run it in 1.5, it will work) and probably the best example of what i\'m talking about. This d/l also requires a free registration. He goes 38-0 in a pub before they kick him.\n\n\n\nDrax (he created the first video): http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/3763/ (http://www.gotfrag.com/cs/demos/3763/)\n\n\n\n*this is a 1.5 demo, really nice shots in this one, it\'s in a pub and they all think he\'s cheating.\n\n\n\nMy quick guide to playing demos. \n\n\n\nJust d/l, extract into your /cstrike folder. For 1.5 this would be Sierra/Counter-Strike/cstrike. For steam it\'s /Steam/Steamapps/your-email/Counter-Strike/cstrike\n\n\n\nThen start up CS, go into console type playdemo "nameofdemo" -WITHOUT the quotes.\n\n\n\nOr you can d/l SKplayer or Geekplay.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(834998, 111208, 1005, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'I love you...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835002, 111208, 1005, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'Just because a clan did it doesn\'t make it right.\n\n\n\nIt was still an exploit, as it wasn\'t something that was meant to be done. You were supposed to have to wait for the animations (that\'s why they\'re there).\n\n\n\nI could really go either way and wouldn\'t mind it being back, but it was an exploit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835008, 111208, 1005, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'Well an \'animation exploit\' is  silly...  If it is a concern that affects gameplay then it should be changed, not because you screw up the animations.\n\n\n\n/EDIT:  But I\'m happy with how CS is so I don\'t care too much.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835022, 111208, 1005, 100387, 1072936800, 'Video Evidence: Quickswitching was not an exploit', 'quote:Originally posted by n3vin \n\nNow that the awp delay has been in the game for a while and the arguing has diminished a bit, i\'d like to show actual proof that quickswitching was not an exploit.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi (http://www.planetawesome.com/kilo/awp_quickswitch.avi)\n\n\n\nCreated by Drax(previously of zEx). zEx was one of the top American clans in case you didnt know.\n\n\n\nI\'m not complaining or trying to get CS back to the good ol days, i\'m just stating some simple facts here people.\n\n\n\nJeff Cliffe says this was a "quickswich exploit".  \n\n\n\nDraw your own conclusions.  \n\n\n\nwhat codec do I need to view this video?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835026, 111208, 1005, 100388, 1072936800, '', 'People used the quickswitch primarily to get out of the zoom mode, skipping animations only gave them an advantage if they actually wanted to use their pistol instead of switch back to awp. The video actually shows you it\'s slower to quickswitch then to just wait.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835027, 111208, 1005, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'Looks like DivX to me.\n\n\n\n/EDIT:  Rofl and why do you point this out to \'Senior Members\'?  I see the little juniors saying quickswitch is an exploit...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835029, 111208, 1005, 100386, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by kekekeke2101 \n\nJust because a clan did it doesn\'t make it right.\n\n\n\nIt was still an exploit, as it wasn\'t something that was meant to be done. You were supposed to have to wait for the animations (that\'s why they\'re there).\n\n\n\nI could really go either way and wouldn\'t mind it being back, but it was an exploit.  \n\n\n\nThat explanation is a copp out.  Just think about it, why of all things in counter-strike to change would be to make people watch the bolt animation?  It sounds trivial until you see it in action.  We all know why it was "fixed".  I\'d rather valve just admit it than use that as an excuse.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835040, 111208, 1005, 100386, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by garfong \n\nPeople used the quickswitch primarily to get out of the zoom mode, skipping animations only gave them an advantage if they actually wanted to use their pistol instead of switch back to awp. The video actually shows you it\'s slower to quickswitch then to just wait.  \n\n\n\nYour partly correct.  You can STILL swtich back to your pistol and fire just as fast with or without the delay.  Which leaves only one type of thing affected: Quickshots.  And who were the only people able to use quickshots to it\'s full effectiveness? You see what im getting at?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835042, 111208, 1005, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by n3vin \n\nThat explanation is a copp out.  Just think about it, why of all things in counter-strike to change would be to make people watch the bolt animation?  It sounds trivial until you see it in action.  We all know why it was "fixed".  I\'d rather valve just admit it than use that as an excuse.  It\'s not for the animation itself, the animation is so that you see how long of a delay you have until you can use it - you aren\'t supposed to skip the delay, so you aren\'t supposed to skip the animation.\n\n\n\nThey were put there so you could see when you were actually allowed to use the gun rather than watch the \'pretty effects.\' It was put there to show the delay. VALVE wanted the delay, so they fixed the exploit.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by n3vin \n\nYour partly correct.  You can STILL swtich back to your pistol and fire just as fast with or without the delay.  Which leaves only one type of thing affected: Quickshots.  And they didn\'t want these \'quickshots\' there, so they put in a delay.\n\n\n\nI\'d really hope that they at least add the animation delay to the pistols, too, as it makes little sense not to.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835054, 111208, 1005, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'You can still skip the animation...  All they did was put a delay after the quickswitch.\n\n\n\n/EDIT:  Maybe the delay was a punishment for people who didn\'t wait for the bolt action?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835056, 111208, 1005, 100386, 1072936800, '', 'quote: And they didn\'t want these \'quickshots\' there, so they put in a delay.\n\n\n\nI\'d really hope that they at least add the animation delay to the pistols, too, as it makes little sense not to. \n\n\n\n\n\nYou got to my point.  Valve just doesnt admit this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835061, 111208, 1005, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'Personally, I didn\'t really care, though I can\'t say I care much about the shield expolit either. I\'m sure you could have a rifle ready while you still have your pistol out, and I\'m sure you could fire from behind a shield (just poke your hand out a bit).\n\n\n\nPeople didn\'t like either, so now one\'s delayed and the other\'s gone.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by n3vin \n\nYou got to my point.  Valve just doesnt admit this.  That they wanted the delay?\n\n\n\nWhy wouldn\'t they? People kept complaining about it, and they got what they want.\n\n\n\nAdapt or go to a different game - hell, go back to 1.5. It\'ll be out for Steam soon and a lot of people will be playing it. I\'ll probably play it for a while, too. It was fun.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835068, 111208, 1005, 100388, 1072936800, '', 'It would be kinda kool if they just made it so the animation reloaded the awp as it raised it in one smooth motion.\n\n\n\nThen you could see the animation and the delay wouldn\'t be there...But Valve wanted to nerf the awp and like you said it was a cop out excuse.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(835122, 111208, 1005, 100147, 1072936800, '', 'Would you have preferred "We nerf\'ed the AWP" to "Fixed/removed quick-switch exploit?"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(836615, 111388, 1013, 100389, 1072936800, 'Dzenis\'s - Counter-strike 1.6 Tweaking Guide', 'Ok, First off I been hearing from alot of different ppl that they "lag" or get very "low fps" in Counter-Strike 1.6 So this guide should boost your FPS (Frames Per Second) and lower your ping a bit. To view your FPS / Loss / Choke just type "net_graph 3" in game in the console.\n\n\n\nVideo Card Drivers & Settings\n\n\n\n1, First you want to check to see if you have your latest video card drivers installed. Go to your video card website and make sure to check. \n\n\n\nATi Video Card Drivers\n\n\n\nNVidia Video Card Drivers\n\n\n\n2, Once you have downloaded and installed your latest video card drivers you will want to do a few minor changes to the video card settings. \n\n\n\nVertical Vsync - This makes your game look better but can suck down your FPS really bad. Vertical Vsync will need to be turned off. Below shows how.\n\n\n\nRight Click Desktop > Propertise > Settings > Advanced > Your Video Card > Performance & Quality Settings. Your Vsync should be in there. Just simply set it to "off" and apply settings.\n\n\n\nAntialiasing - This also makes your game look better but it\'s not needed and by turning it off your game play will be much smoother and you will gain some FPS. This setting is in the same place as your "Vysync" setting so turn it "off".\n\n\n\n16 Bit Color - Counter-Strike was meant to be played in 16 bit color and if you want to reach your max FPS (Frames Per Second) then be sure to set it to 16 bit color. 32 bit color may make your Counter-Strike graphics a bit nicer but you wont tell a difference setting it to 16 bit color. Below is how to set it to 16 bit color.\n\n\n\nRight Click Desktop > Propertise > Settings (Find Color Quality)\n\n\n\nMonitor Refresh Rates - This setting REALLY helps you reach your max FPS (Frams Per Second) and should be set as high as your monitor can handle. Most people have there\'s set to 60 Hertz which is NOT good. Try to set this to atleast 85 Hertz. How to change refresh rates below.\n\n\n\nRight Click Desktop > Propertise > Settings > Advanced > Monitor \n\n\n\nOpen GL Mode - Be sure to run Counter-Strike in OpenGL mode. DONT ever run Counter-Strike in Software mode or Direct3D mode. It can be changed ingame options.\n\n\n\nConfig Tweaks & Tricks\n\n\n\nConfig Commands\n\n\n\nBelow is a list of useful config tweaks. Your config is located STEAM/SteamApps/username/Counter-Strike/cstrike/config.cfg NOTE: Be sure to back up your old config.\n\n\n\nmp_decals "20" \n\ngl_affinemodels "0" \n\ngl_alphamin "0.25" \n\ngl_clear "0" \n\ngl_dither "1" \n\ngl_flipmatrix "0" \n\ngl_flashblend "0" \n\ngl_lightholes "0"\n\nprecache "1" \n\ndeveloper "1"\n\ncl_weather "0"\n\nfps_max 150\n\ncl_download_ingame "0"\n\ncl_himodels "0"\n\nhpk_maxsize "0.5"\n\n\n\nFPS Booster Trick\n\n\n\nGo to the Windows\\System32 directory and look for your opengl.dll \n\nIf you\'re using a nvidia card the nvoglnt.dll is the right one. For Ati cards it\'s the atioglxx.dll. And for the rest the opengl32.dll. \n\n- copy that file to your ..\\SteamApps\\user@user.de\\counter-strike\\gldrv directory. \n\n- open the drvmap.txt in that directory and change the text to the following: \n\nDefault Default gldrv/YOURFILENAME.dll OpenGL Driver\n\n\n\nHigh FPS Player Models - If your computer is really bad and your still cant seem to get better FPS (Frames Per Second) you might want to try an replace your player models. If your playing in big servers lanywhere from 18 players to 32 players you will get a FPS (Frames Per Second) drop due to all the player models your Counter-Strike has to load. I myself downloaded these and they have helped my Counter-Strike alot. Below is the program I used to download the High FPS Models. It gives you instructions on how to install your models and it also has good FPS tweaks / Ping Tweaks.\n\n\n\nhttp://www.frag-wire.com/downloads/hltsetup.zip (http://www.frag-wire.com/downloads/hltsetup.zip)\n\n\n\nWell hope every liked this guide and hope it helps you as much as it helped me. If admin/mod could pin this it would be great.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840365, 111388, 1013, 100389, 1072936800, '', 'If you are having Timed Out problems with steam this sould help you too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840440, 111388, 1013, 100390, 1072936800, '', 'nice faq, but some of the things im missing there\n\neg, antialiasing option, monitor refresh rates\n\nas for the vsync, I had to scroll to the "HL3" option (I\'ve had HL installed multiple times in multiple directories) and change my vertical sync for that specific program\n\n\n\nI also need to question why to never use Direct3D, for me, it seems that Direct3D gives me a higher FPS, or at least last I used OpenGL, it seemed choppy and unstable.\n\n\n\nOne more thing, perhaps you can have a faq that includes everything for not only CS, but for all HL? It\'d be a big help, thanks. I\'ll be sure to try some of it.\n\n\n\n-SnakeBite', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840602, 111388, 1013, 100391, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SnakeBite34 \n\n... why to never use Direct3D, for me, it seems that Direct3D gives me a higher FPS, or at least last I used OpenGL, it seemed choppy and unstable...\n\n \n\n\n\nI have the same problem, started when i got me 9600xt. Was fixed when i tried omega drivers for radeon, i use the multires when playing any games with openGL (starting from quake1). \n\n\n\nOfcourse, those dricers are all unofficial and unsupported, but since  the official drivers didnt work on my system ...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840816, 111388, 1013, 100389, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Dzenis \n\nIf you are having Timed Out problems with steam this sould help you too.  \n\n\n\nThanks ill try to get everything for HL to but i only play 1.6 and the derections helped me out good.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(847149, 111388, 1013, 100389, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Dzenis \n\nThanks ill try to get everything for HL to but i only play 1.6 and the derections helped me out good.  \n\n\n\nHave fun with it you guys', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(847448, 111388, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, '', 'quote:cl_download_ingame "0"\n\nthis cvar does nothing now. cl_allowdownload "1/0" is the only option.\n\n\n\ncs 1.6 broke alot of cvars :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(838783, 111576, 1013, 100393, 1072936800, 'Host_Error: UserMsg: Not Present on Client 232', '**EDIT: I was just informed that the error code 52 (as well as 232) was also reported to some clients.\n\n\n\nI and many clients who conect to my server experience this error on a regular basis.\n\n\n\nServer:\n\nAthlon XP 2200+\n\n512MB RAM\n\n80GB hdd\n\nup to date all around\n\nGentoo Linux, kernel 2.6.7 w/pax/grsec patches\n\nMetaMod 1.17.1\n\nAMXModX 0.16\n\n\n\nSome simple scripts like AWP-Punish, some extra basic unrelated admin tools installed (ie, to allow amx_alltalk <0 | 1> to be a command), etc.   I had WC3 2.5.0 installed, but unloaded it to see if it fixed the errors -- the errors still happen.  I basically tried that with all of the AMXX plugins, but the errors happen, regardless.\n\n\n\nI\'ve searched for this error on this forum, AMXX\'s forums, googled for it, and searched on other forums, with no luck.  I found an abundance of similiar errors, but all with completely different error codes (19 instead of 232, for example).  Anyone know the problem?  THanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(839746, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, 'I\'ll take a shot at explaining ;)', 'Well I\'ll take a quick guess that you have a Linksys router?\n\nAnd I\'ll also guess you\'ve updated it with the new firmware?\n\nIf that is the case your stuck in the same place as alot of people.\n\nIt seems that something in the new firmware conflicts with steam and allows only a few seconds of gameplay (I\'ve managed to gain 30 seconds.)\n\nThe only solution is if you can find the old firmware here:\n\nftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub (ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub)\n\n\n\nI unfortunately have the Linksys BEFSR81 v3 - It seems apparent they haven\'t placed the old firmware on their site/ftp like they have for every other bloody router :/ that really doesn\'t help.\n\nI hope Valve or Linksys come up with a solution in the very near future as I am missing Half-life. []\n\n\n\nHope this has helped you in anyway possible even if it\'s just stating why it is happening.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(839747, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, '', 'ADD - Also search in this directory:\n\nftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub/befsr41/ (ftp://ftp.linksys.com/pub/befsr41/)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(839825, 111576, 1013, 100393, 1072936800, '', 'Actually, personally, there are no routers between me and my server.  My HLDS server also acts as a router for my windows box.  My switch is Linksys, but it\'s a switch only, no router.  My router was provided by my ISP -- I don\'t know the make and model of it, they claim they build it themselves.  The SSL cert for the router was issued by Linksys, however, and all available information from the router and the router\'s cert seems to imply a WRT54G model router (which is a wireless router), so my guess is that it\'s got the innerparts of a WRT54G, but built up with other parts than the standards.\n\n\n\nRegardless... I have no control over its current firmware version, and even if I did, it can\'t possibly be the problem -- the packets from my windows box to the server box never see the Linksys router.  And yet it happens to me, as well as my clients (my clients most likely do use Linksys routers -- two that I talk with regularly do for sure, not sure about the rest.)\n\n\n\nAny ideas on why I might be disconnected?  Checking my firewall logs shows that nothing related to hlds and my windows box was blocked...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840050, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, '', 'Hmmm ok I just thought I\'d put that information incase it was any help and because its a common problem at the moment.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(840850, 111576, 1013, 100395, 1072936800, '', 'It seems like a lot of users (mainly linksys routers) are having this problem.  And from everything I can gather, it started happening after the last Steam update. \n\n\n\nI am bumping this in hopes of getting it acknowledged by someone that can look into a possible solution to the problem.\n\n\n\nThe router I use is a Linksys, and it is currently working 100% fine with every app I use:\n\n\n\nInternet browsing (IE, Mozilla Firefox)\n\nQuake 3\n\nWolfenstein Enemy Territory\n\nUnreal Tournament 2004\n\nDiablo II\n\nUsenet applications\n\nPeer to peer applications\n\nnetwork samba sharing\n\nYou name it!\n\n\n\nEven Half Life/CS/TFC/DOD before the move-over to Steam.\n\n\n\nThis is a real problem.  I don\'t think the router is at fault because everything else I do works with it.  \n\n\n\nI\'ve read one thread in this forum where someone said it works as long as you downgrade your router\'s firmware to a version from 2002.  That is unacceptable, because the current firmware fixes many security flaws within the router, and has not caused problems with any other app I use.\n\n\n\nI am going to really press this issue, because I am anticipating Half LIfe 2, and it would be a shame to not be able to play online.\n\n\n\nI\'m not trying to be inflammitory at all.  If anyone from Valve reads this, I thank you for your time.  \n\n\n\nMy main intent is to get a response from somone to see if it\'s something Valve is aware of, and working on, and if they have contacted Linksys about a possible fix.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(842286, 111576, 1013, 100395, 1072936800, '', 'BUMP', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(844015, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, '', 'I am currently trying to get the previous firmware for my Linksys Router Model (BEFSR81 V3) to see if that will help. I have sent Linksys Support a message and have quickly recieved a reply that an e-mail will follow with the firmware. Hopefully that works for my part of the problems []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(845156, 111576, 1013, 100396, 1072936800, '', 'i gather that this problem hasn\'t been fixed yet []\n\n\n\nsigh, i wonder if i should get the old router firmware...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(845212, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, '', 'I\'d have already got it, if it wasn\'t for the fact that they\'ve put every single previous firmware on their site except the ONE I need.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(845232, 111576, 1013, 100396, 1072936800, '', 'which one is the one we need?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(845250, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, '', 'The one I need (Linksys Model: BEFSR81 v3) I think it is 2.45.5 or some number similar.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(845338, 111576, 1013, 100396, 1072936800, '', 'i\'d rather not fiddle with my routers firmware\n\n\n\ni wonder when this will be fixed', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(849475, 111576, 1013, 100394, 1072936800, 'BUMP', '- bump -\n\nI\'d like the answer to that too, since even though downgrading my firmware may be the answer (I say "may be the answer" because I\'ve not yet recieved my promised email containing the previous firmware and therefore can not say it will work), downgrading my firmware takes away the fixes that were involved my security in the firmware update. It\'s obviously something on Steams part as every other piece of software I use has no problem keeping a steady connection.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(849569, 111576, 1013, 100396, 1072936800, '', 'bleh, im suprised more people aren\'t having this problem', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(847732, 112456, 1005, 100397, 1072936800, 'The Official Hackers In CZ', 'Some people don\'t think there are hacks for Counter-Strike Condition Zero.  But they are wrong.  Tonight I have witnessed someone hack and admit it and even tell us where he got his hacks.  His name is KyA | hyper-knuckles {Le@DE|2}, STEAM ID:\n\n\n\nSTEAM_0:1:3288574 17 13:35 56 0\n\n\n\nIf you would kindly report him to steam and help me out and all the rest that were in the server it would be greatly appreciated.  I know that may only be one of thousands that hack but at least it will help.  This guy that was hacking said that he found his hacks on www.**********.com (http://www.**********.com) and he said that he is using a cd key that thousands of other people have got.  It is a cd key that has been hacked by someone and now posted on a web site somewhere that anyone can use.  He also said he got free games such as CS:CZ and Blue Shift from this site.  Just by downloading him.  I believe he did and whoever thinks that can not happen should back away from their computer now and never go on it again.  \n\n\n\nSteams anti-cheating system(VAC) seems to not be working very well because there are still many hackers that haven\'t been caught and probably many that never will be caught.  But I think steam should improve there anti cheat system.  A good recomendation for servers to have is HL Guard.  Also known as Half-Life guard.  It is a very good anti-cheating software program that can catch hackers on your server and ban them and unlike cheating death the other person does not need to download it on there computer in order to play.  I think all servers should have this because it is a great idea for a server.\n\n\n\nIf any of you could report this hacker than maybe he will be gone.  He plays on my favourite sevrer and always comes in hacking.  When people hack it\'s just not fun to play Counter-Strike and many people are quitting Counter-Strike becasue of it.  I believe that if steam came down harder on these hackers the game would be more enjoyable for you and everyone else and more people would play Counter-Strike.  Please reply and tell me what you think.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(847762, 112456, 1005, 100203, 1072936800, '', 'u know ur not suppose to put their steam id in these forums\n\n\n\nhackers usually get banned later on\n\n\n\ni always c hackers on for a week only\n\n\n\nafter that they dissapeared\n\n\n\nBANNNED', '127.0.0.1', 1),
