(864879, 113886, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s fine.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(864892, 113886, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, 'Somethings messed...', 'I\'m dying to play it... I\'ve downloaded it, loaded it, but for some reason, when I start the mission, there\'s no bots. It\'s just me running around.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(864919, 113886, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, 'Somethings messed...', 'quote:Originally posted by gregrout \n\nI\'m dying to play it... I\'ve downloaded it, loaded it, but for some reason, when I start the mission, there\'s no bots. It\'s just me running around.  \n\n\n\nRename the folder from \'Extended Duty\' to \'ExtendedDuty\' and restart CZ.\n\n\n\nFix will be in with no rev name change in five minutes.\n\n\n\nEdit\n\n\n\nZip is fixed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(865008, 113886, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, 'Re: Somethings messed...', 'quote:Originally posted by BigDaddyK \n\nRename the folder from \'Extended Duty\' to \'ExtendedDuty\' and restart CZ.\n\n\n\nFix will be in with no rev name change in five minutes.\n\n\n\nEdit\n\n\n\nZip is fixed.  \n\n\n\nThanks, that fixed it... so far so good. Great mission pack... I like it. I noticed that the map selection screen is a bit messed. The tga or bmp files for the maps seem to be missing (temporarily) for the maps ... de_airstrip, de_storm and Train. These maps are named differently. My guess is that there is a delay as the game searches for these files. But then I\'m not sure. If I scroll the map selection screen it tends to find the pictures for the maps. I like it a lot though... a great job. It would be great if they put together a tutorial on how to make your own missions. The rtf file they include is a bit too much. It would be even better if Valve threw together a mission editor that would let people put together their own missions with ease.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(865509, 113886, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, '... Mission Pack intention...', 'I ran into a problem with the third mission, namely the MAC-10 quota. I\'m not a gun expert, so I use the F1 key if the gun model doesn\'t register with me. That said as a CT I don\'t believe I have access to the MAC-10. I\'ve assumed the closest to that is the low-end submachine gun, but I thought the MAC-10 was a terrorist weapon. So I guess the question is, do I have to kill a terrorist and snag his weapon hoping it\'s a MAC-10 or should this weapon be available via the F1 key? I was just wondering.... that\'s all. I just haven\'t been lucky enough to kill a T carrying one.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(865600, 113886, 1005, 100417, 1072936800, '', 'mac10 is a t only weapon the tmp is the ct equivalent', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(865642, 113886, 1005, 100188, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Cool_Al \n\nmac10 is a t only weapon the tmp is the ct equivalent  \n\n\n\nThat\'s what I thought. I mention it because in the earlier missions in this mission pack you had to use other T weapons as a CT, but these weapons were always available to purchase using the F1 key, even though they are not available in buy screen for CTs. I don\'t know if it\'s a scripting bug, or intentional. If it\'s intentional, then it makes that level a lot harder, because you have to kill a lot of T\'s to find that one weapon and live long enough to keep it. So based on the eariler versions, it seems like it could be a bug; but, that said the mission is theoretically still possible to complete.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(866332, 113886, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, '', 'You have to kill T to get the weapon.  This has been done before in mission packs.\n\n\n\nMAC-10 Madman or Inmate423\n\nGalil      ScaR or Scratch\n\nKrieg    EddiT\n\nAK-47  Many\n\ng3sg1  Rhino', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(866864, 113886, 1005, 100418, 1072936800, '', 'The link still doesn\'t work for me...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(868325, 113886, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by BigDaddyK \n\nYou have to kill T to get the weapon.  This has been done before in mission packs.\n\n\n\nMAC-10 Madman or Inmate423\n\nGalil      ScaR or Scratch\n\nKrieg    EddiT\n\nAK-47  Many\n\ng3sg1  Rhino  \n\n\n\nLooks like the Hard and Expert Missions were done a little sloppy and need to be fixed to access the Mac-10 and Kreig, maybe the Galil.  I\'ll probably release rev. of pack by Thursday.  Want to figure out how likely it is for a \'Spray\' bot to choose the Mac-10.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(868563, 113886, 1005, 100418, 1072936800, '', 'why no reply??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(868737, 113886, 1005, 100415, 1072936800, '', 'Note the lack of Mac-10/Kreig in Hard/Expert level has been fixed in rev. 1.1.\n\n\n\nhttp://mysite.verizon.net/res1g4li/ExtendedDuty-1-1.zip (http://mysite.verizon.net/res1g4li/ExtendedDuty-1-1.zip)\n\n\n\nthanks greg\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by NinjaGaijin \n\nwhy no reply??  \n\n\n\nwhy no t-bone ?\n\n\n\nWhat\'s your question ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873909, 114784, 1040, 101107, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bballr4567 \n\nAhh you really dont understand how Valve schedules things do you?? Go search the DoD forums and look at some of Waldos posts about it. \n\n\n\nAnyways if you all seriously think this is such bad bad news its delayed go ahead. The game is obviously ready to be played and its just a mtter of time.  \n\n\n\nWe/I never said its was totally "bad bad news",  the lack of telling us why the release of the game did not happen is unfair to the community and like I said a few posts before, we will just have to deal with it im afraid [] .', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873929, 114784, 1040, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Well I mean its a beta too. They didnt even have to tell us about it and allow us to play it. I mean I just watched all the vids again today and I seriously cant wait for this game but I know that Valve wouldnt hold onto if there wasnt a good reason to. \n\n\n\nYou gotta trust a company that on thier first even game it made Game of the Year at 40+ different publications.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873934, 114784, 1040, 101107, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Willdo \n\nim starting a petition!  \n\n\n\nlol It wont get you anywhere, if I was in your shoes, I would go to other forums and judge their reaction to the delay, and bring back the feedback to this forum, at least then if VALVe reps read this thread they can see that making no response is worse than delaying a game- or something along that lines. \n\n\n\nNighty Night.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873937, 114784, 1040, 103494, 1072936800, '', 'Well they really got lucky with that one.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873948, 114784, 1040, 103495, 1072936800, '', 'yeah thats true but what did they do after that for the next 5 years and more? release the same game over and over, sorry but i agree with you that valve specifies genius but thats only judging them on something that happened a long time ago, times and games nowdays are far more different then back then and becuase of more choice were more critical, so you cant praise them on a game that by todays standerds is poor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873962, 114784, 1040, 103496, 1072936800, '', 'yeah im still pissed though and you should understand that. And trust me valve is gonna see one hell of a long e-mail tommrow =D.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873965, 114784, 1040, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Well you also got to think that this game is nothing like anything out. They HAVE to do it right.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(873968, 114784, 1040, 100420, 1072936800, '', 'CS:S delayed? No.... What a surprise! [/end sarcasm]\n\n\n\nI mean come on, we\'ve all seen this coming. I find this completely unprofessional coming from a company such as Valve.\n\n\n\nSome people have pre-ordered this game almost a year ago. You can\'t go around telling everyone that product is ready for shipping when you know you won\'t make the deadline.\n\n\n\nThey know what they\'re doing though. Creating all this hype, getting more people to buy Condition Zero only to get access to CS:S, that\'s some pretty basic marketing strategy, especially when we consider the fact they already have a working beta, as we\'ve seen in Korea.\n\n\n\nI would be willing to bet 10$ right now that they have a working beta, and that they could easily release it at this very second. Internal playtesting is probably even finished, maybe a long time ago.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874002, 114784, 1040, 103495, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bballr4567 \n\nWell you also got to think that this game is nothing like anything out. They HAVE to do it right.  \n\n\n\nthey do have to do it right as itl be chaos on here otherwise wont it haha, but when you say its not like anything out your partcially right as it is indeed a unique game becuase its from the already created half life world etc.. but in game concept terms id say its quite old as guy killing monsters was done so long ago with doom being one of the 1st and half life poaching the idea but changing it enough into there own, also today wise id say halo and halo 2 were very similar also as its roughly the same idea just told differently, but its because of these games that valve know they have to really make the best game ever because lets be honest its what were all expecting isnt it? So if they pull it off (fingers crossed) then all faith in valve will be restored, until then im not saying there great nor saying there bad just saying HURRY UP AND GIVE ME MY GAME lol', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874008, 114784, 1040, 103497, 1072936800, 'Pretty sure this is marketing ploy...', 'Pretty sure this is marketing ploy...I\'m going to try and prove that this is. I took a pic of all currently playing players of CZ. Roughly 10,000. That tells us about atleast 10,000 people play CZ. \n\n\n\nNow if that number doubles triples then that would prove that the delay was a scheme thought up by some guy in the marketing department. \n\n\n\nWith this scheme you could get more people buying CZ to play CS:S,because they know they have more time. Haveing 20,000 or 30,000 people testing beta is a lot better for the company, because these people are potential buyers. \n\n\n\nHaving 15,000 players buying CS:S at the end of the beta phase is better than 5,000 dont you think so? Also, there is or may also be another reason.Having more people testing the beta will get more people finding bugs faster(if thats the case). \n\n\n\nNow why dont they just give it to, and let the CS community test it...I\'m sure they\'ll find all the bugs in a matter of minutes/hours/days whatever.\n\n\n\nThe point is they wouldnt be making any money from the CS owners. That is why! \n\n\n\n\n\nLets do some math say 1 copy of CZ is $30, and $10,000 people buy the game, how much do you get?$300,000.\n\n\n\nNow lets delay the beta...and wait till we get another $10,0000 people from the CS community to buy CZ.Dont you get more money?Now this would make up for poor sales and maybe some other things. \n\n\n\nNow you have 20,000 people testing the beta,I garuntee atleast half those people would buy CS:S or HL2. See this is a simple strat used by Valve to make some money.\n\n\n\nAlthough I dont like this strat, I think its a good Idea...but aleast give an indepth explanation for delaying a game. Thats all I have to say,and I\'m sure a few would be agreeing with me on this.\n\n\n\n-Cole3000', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874016, 114784, 1040, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'I like the HL games because you can cause mayhem but you also have to think about what you are doing. How many games are like that these days?? \n\n\n\nI hate shoot em up games because they get boring. Like Ive heard so many people talking about Doom 3 is that it gets repetive so fast. Ive even read that one guy can tell when and where enemies will spawn because of the elements in the game. A really dark room=4 enemies in front of you and two in back. BORING!!!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874017, 114784, 1040, 102828, 1072936800, '', 'like I said, it\'s all business and marketing', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874022, 114784, 1040, 100322, 1072936800, '', 'Honestly, when does bballr not defend Valve? Part of debating is understand the other side and he defends Valve for every little mistake they make. It\'s to the point where everything he says is invalid, because he doesn\'t seem to understand why large amounts of people are complaining. Perhaps he\'s half right in the fact that how people express their frustaration with Valve is all too often immature. But if large amounts of people are complaining on a company\'s forums, I\'d say they have some problems to deal with, whether or not the consumers may be right or wrong. It\'s the consumers who buy the game, and who make a company what it is. Valve\'s actions have lead them to their reputation now, which is nothing new with business. Valve is capable of making awesome content, but they just need to let us play it already..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874030, 114784, 1040, 102828, 1072936800, '', 'obviously a valve Hammer Legion Member, nth wrong with that tho. Just stating the fact', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(874052, 114784, 1040, 100518, 1072936800, '', 'True, Valve is just another profit-making corporation not really listening to their customers and always letting them down and making false hopes by saying all sorts of release dates and delay. They sure do have a beta waiting to be released but they probably think now that they could make more money if they wait. Now maybe they will even release a CZ update so people will want to buy it even more and then when they have a lot more money they will make preload available for a couple of days just to have time to make more money and then they might let us play a few days later just for a short time so we all want to play it more later and we will buy it. \n\n\n\nI truly hope that CS: Source beta and the real game will get cracked a lot and that people will eventually release it on the internet so everyone gets to test it without paying. I paid for CZ and might pay CS: Source if I think it\'s worth it but I\'m still happy to know people playing your games for free because they don\'t feel like supporting a money making coropration.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(882380, 114808, 1013, 103498, 1072936800, '', 'I posted this in the old thread but it died:\n\n\n\nMy solution to this problem:\n\n\n\n1) Back up your SteamApps and skins folders if you so desire.\n\n\n\n2) Uninstall Steam.\n\n\n\n3) Delete everything in your Steam folder.\n\n\n\n4) If you cannot delete steam.exe, this solution is for you. Otherwise just re-install steam.\n\n\n\n5) Restart your computer. After it shuts down, hold down the F8 key until you come up with a menu.\n\n\n\n6) Select "Run in Safe Mode."\n\n\n\n7) Once the computer has booted into safe mode, go to My Computer and navigate to your Steam folder.\n\n\n\n8) Delete steam.exe\n\n\n\n9) Restart the computer normally.\n\n\n\n10) Reinstall steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(882396, 114808, 1013, 103499, 1072936800, '', 'I can delete it. But that error comes up when I reinstall and try to load it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(882981, 114808, 1013, 103500, 1072936800, '', 'Woohoo my steam is updating now...\n\n\n\nWould be really nice to know whats causing this since i get this error almost every single #�%#  day !!\n\n\n\nIt is really annoying especially when you have to download 3-400mb each time []\n\n\n\nI have no spyware no virusses (clean xp install etc..)\n\n\n\nCan daemon-tools or other virtual drives cause this ?\n\n\n\nI run norton 2004 and tiny personal fw, bla bla bla ...\n\n\n\nHEELP ? []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(883110, 114808, 1013, 103500, 1072936800, '', 'well that joy was short lived.....\n\n\n\nI went to safemode and deleted steam and ran all sort of anti spyware gadgets and full system virus scans bla bla...\n\n\n\ncleaned out the run section of the windows registry except for norton etc..\n\n\n\ndisabled norton script blocking (said in the steam forums this could cause problems)\n\n\n\nran scandisk and norton utilities and reg cleaner and ..... eek i got tonz of toolz []\n\n\n\nBut nothing helps even tried reinstalling xp....\n\n\n\nIm really close to giving up on steam, i played cs1.5 for 2 years without 1 error, and i had steam for a month and prob reinstalled it 10 times by now...\n\n\n\nWHAT IS LOCKING UP THE DAMN FILE !!! it aint in processes...  *pulling out the rest of my hair*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(884257, 114808, 1013, 103500, 1072936800, '', 'uninstalled steam and borrowed a condition zero cd from a friend, and installed steam from there now it works fine .. lol\n\n\n\nI made a note about it in my own clans forum aparently many others have the same problem [] lol good work,  steam is a really stable program *cough*..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(884706, 114808, 1013, 103499, 1072936800, '', 'http://whore.gotdns.org/slax/steam_is_retarded.jpg (http://whore.gotdns.org/slax/steam_is_retarded.jpg)\n\n\n\nthats what comes up. HELP ME FOR THE LOVE OF CS!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(884985, 114808, 1013, 103500, 1072936800, '', 'Do what i did ..\n\n1: Install steam on another pc on your LAN or get a friend with a working install to send all of c:\\valve\\steam (except clientreg.blob & counterstrike.gcf & and his account folder, in steamapps dir)\n\n\n\n2: Goto safe mode and copy the new acquired steam over your own install (say yes to all)\n\n\n\n3: Reboot and run your new steam.exe and it should make a quick update and woohoo []\n\n\n\nThis worked for me after 1 month of bs problems, hope its helpfull...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(885167, 114808, 1013, 103499, 1072936800, '', 'AWESOME! I went upstairs, installed steam, then i put the folder on the network, came down here and opened it and it worked! YESH!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
