(892336, 116880, 1013, 103508, 1072936800, 'individuals being blamed for lag', 'i\'ve noticed a lot of players blaming other people for the high ping on a server, or servers going so far as to auto-kick players with a ping higher than some set number (usually 150).\n\n\n\nthe prevalent idea here seems to be that a player with a high ping is going to lag the rest of the server. for example, i just joined a server where everyone was pinging at 400ms, except one guy who had 800. they kicked the 800ms player, presuming that he was causing the server problems. kicking him didn\'t improve anything.\n\n\n\nping is simply a measure of the rate at which the server can communicate with an individual player. why do people think one player\'s ping is going to effect everyone else\'s? is there any merit at all to this idea? do the game servers do something to try to compensate for a player\'s high ping?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892345, 116880, 1013, 103509, 1072936800, '', 'i thought that if some one had bad lag he would lag teh server. adn thus, every one in it', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892352, 116880, 1013, 100046, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Batz \n\ni thought that if some one had bad lag he would lag teh server. adn thus, every one in it  Fortunately not.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892353, 116880, 1013, 100448, 1072936800, '', 'dude get off the forums you\'re lagging them!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892382, 116880, 1013, 100658, 1072936800, '', 'Well if their ping is so high(800) that they aren\'t able to play, they are only increasing the load on the server and taking up a spot... I agree that if it\'s less than 250~300, then they should still be allowed on', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892385, 116880, 1013, 101035, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by domomike \n\ndude get off the forums you\'re lagging them!!!  \n\n\n\ngood example.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892485, 116880, 1013, 103508, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by WrG|IceMouse \n\nWell if their ping is so high(800) that they aren\'t able to play, they are only increasing the load on the server and taking up a spot... I agree that if it\'s less than 250~300, then they should still be allowed on \n\nyeah, i understand that there\'s other reasons to boot them; i was just wondering why the idea exists that one player can completely lag everyone to the point of unplayability. it seemed pretty strange to me. if everyone is pinging >400, then the issue is likely with the server, not some player on it.\n\n\n\nbut i wanted to make sure there wasn\'t something in the server code itself that i wasn\'t aware of that would actually give credence to the idea.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892754, 116880, 1013, 100392, 1072936800, '', 'nah, nobody is going to lag a server.\n\n\n\nthe server should have net settings capped properly to limit bandwidth overusage, other than that no lagger will lag a server.\n\n\n\ni think ppl set that autokick on b/c laggers are damn hard to hit and they get lots of random kills thx to lag compensation.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892817, 116880, 1013, 103510, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by w00ters \n\nnah, nobody is going to lag a server.\n\n\n\nthe server should have net settings capped properly to limit bandwidth overusage, other than that no lagger will lag a server.\n\n\n\ni think ppl set that autokick on b/c laggers are damn hard to hit and they get lots of random kills thx to lag compensation.  \n\n\n\n\n\nYou kinda contradicted yourself there.\n\n\n\nWith lag compensation enabled, this does\n\ntend to create a sensation of the server lagging\n\nwhen ping ranges varry so much, but more shots seems to\n\nregister (low ping vs high ping).\n\n\n\nWithout lag compensation, the low pinger tends to either walk\n\nthrough a high-pinger,  half the bullets dont seem to register, or\n\nthey look like they are teleporting instead of running .\n\n\n\nEither way it does effect the game, just gotta decide how ya want\n\nyour server to play.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892883, 116880, 1013, 103511, 1072936800, '', 'trust me, if evry1 is pinging at 40-50 and some geezer comes on with 300 ping he will lag the WHOLE server out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892911, 116880, 1013, 103512, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SoNofSaTaN \n\ntrust me, if evry1 is pinging at 40-50 and some geezer comes on with 300 ping he will lag the WHOLE server out.  That\'s simply not true, and not how the Half-Life client/server architecture works.  The main reason people with higher pings are kicked from servers is because they tend to lag so badly that they appear to "warp" through the level and are much harder to hit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892920, 116880, 1013, 103513, 1072936800, '', 'Players with lower pings actually lag the server out...\n\n\n\nTheir broadband demands higher download/upload rates and puts a strain on the server (ever wonder why servers have their clients limited to a "rate" of 9999. Higher rate means better pings for clients but more strain on the server.\n\n\n\nLPB\'s are hogging all the bandwidth and blaming it on dial-up users who actually use the least bandwidth from the server...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892944, 116880, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'Last time I asked the people that worked on the netcode for Valve games, the word is that high ping people have ZERO effect (lag) on servers.  It\'s just an urban myth worthy of snopes (http://www.snopes.com)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(892963, 116880, 1013, 100448, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Waldo \n\nLast time I asked the people that worked on the netcode for Valve games, the word is that high ping people have ZERO effect (lag) on servers.  It\'s just an urban myth worthy of snopes (http://www.snopes.com)  \n\n\n\nWhao! Thanks for clearing that up! I never knew that...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(893061, 116880, 1013, 100085, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by domomike \n\ndude get off the forums you\'re lagging them!!!  \n\n\n\nhahaha', '127.0.0.1', 1),
