(908980, 118409, 1013, 100511, 1072936800, '[LunchTimeDigest] Should you preload HL2 if you\'re buying the box?', 'The LunchTime Digest\n\nAugust 10, 2004\n\n\n\nI\'m doing a polka-dance to Stinky Wizzleteats\' "Happy Happy Joy Joy." (http://www.bitstorm.org/happyjoy/)\n\n"Why ever are you doing that, Lunchtimemama?"  you ask?\n\n"Because Half-Life 2 starts preloading TODAY, you eediot!" I reply.  Yes sirs and madams, THAT \'Half-Life 2!\'  It\'s really gonna happen.  Right now.  FOR REAL!\n\n\n\nWhile you probably aren\'t getting jiggy with your "You Eediot" CD (http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/B000008JY8/qid=1092197757/sr=8-4/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i4_xgl15/002-5368362-9720859?v=glance&s=music&n=507846), I\'m sure everyone is as excited as I at this step toward RELEASE.  I\'ve been following a lot of the "Will you buy HL2 retail or through Steam?" threads and it seems that a majority of gamers still like to have a box they can ogle.  This puts quit a few people in an odd situation.  If you plan to buy the box, should you preload?  The answer is an unyielding yes!\n\n\n\nIf you were to purchase the boxed game without preloading, you would be spending a good 3-5 minuets waiting for the game to copy from your 24-52x CD ROM.  And if HL2 is anything like CZ, you will need to wait 3-5 minuets to convert the installation to the Steam cache (if you want multiplayer).  That\'s a good 6-10 minuets which could have been spent playing Half-Life 2!!!\n\n\n\nOn the other hand, if you preload the game, you need only spend the 10-20 seconds inputting the CD key before you\'re ready to go!  The only reason not to preload is if you don\'t plan to register your copy with Steam, which in turn makes me wonder why you are reading the Steam forums.\n\n\n\nSo my friends, you see, even if you are planning to buy the retail version of HL2, you should still preload Half-Life 2.  There\'s no good reason not to!  Now, if you\'ll excuse me, there\'s a song about a whale� NO� a song about being happy with my name on it.  Until next time friends!\n\n\n\n\n\n-Lunchtimemama\n\nStaff Writer for the LuchTimeDigest\n\n\n\n� 2004 Lunchtimemama\'s Homemade Rotisserie Pork Rines Inc.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(909014, 118409, 1013, 100512, 1072936800, '', 'OK!\n\n\n\nThat\'s it I\'m going for a walk.\n\n\n\nSee you all in an hour.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
