(1029426, 121263, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by kekekeke2101 \n\nYeah, but I didn\'t know they tracked your computer to match it with your Steam account. That one\'s new information to me.\n\n\n\nStill amusing that that guy tried to use an invalid credit card eleven times.\n\n\n\n Yeah, I know. I was just wondering if you could match my computer to my Steam account and Forum account as well.  \n\n\n\nYou give this forum and Steam 2 pieces of info when you sign up - an account name, and a legit email address.  Every time you use Steam and this forum, your IP address is available.  If you see the same name, the same email, and the same IP address tied to somone\'s forum activities, and then the same name, email address and IP address on Steam that tried 7 times to use stolen or fake cd-key and 11 invalid credit-card number tries...  you can probably make a well founded assumption.\n\n\n\nSome people aren\'t very clever.  Every website in the world tracks IP addresses and such information.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
