(955712, 122099, 1005, 100686, 1072936800, '', 'There\'s still the fact that it\'s client-side rendering of a server-side function.  Nobody here can tell what would happen to the Phoenix Conn. player, had somebody shot him in the head there, because you\'re not even supposed to be able to see yourself in CS, let alone see your own model, let alone hitboxes.\n\n\n\nIf it happens frequently, and it\'s obviously not lag, or an otherwise taxed server, we\'ll hear about it enough, tomorrow, and for the next few weeks.  Nobody will be able to shoot one another, and my kill score will be much the same as it always has, because I always manage to shoot straight past the boxes in all of the other games - headshots don\'t count as headshots, when it\'s in certain spots, etc...  It doesn\'t matter who\'s right, right now.  Frankly, if it was somebody else\'s hitboxes I was looking at, and somebody proved to me that they were off, and that they were breaking the game, I\'d worry, and hope for a patch.  ...you\'ve just proven that p_models and the player camera work differently than world models, especially between servers and different clients.\n\n\n\nWoo.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
