(973378, 124589, 1040, 100751, 1072936800, '', 'You do understand they went with CZ and ATI owners because they do not want the "WHOLE" community "beta testing" it.\n\n\n\nIts like doing a survey, your not going to ask every person in the world what their favorite ice cream flavor is. They take a sample of the community.\n\n\n\nUsing CZ and ATI as the sample was the easiest way of doing so.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(973381, 124589, 1040, 100750, 1072936800, '', 'quote:As for who is deserving of it, some kiddy goes out and buys cz and they are deserving, i on the other hand have been a supporter of cs ever since it was made and would never leave it for another game am not deserving.\n\n\n\n\n\nCS was free, no one supported it....because no one payed for it you dumb [color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color][color=pink][font=symbol]©[/font][/color].\n\n\n\nits not about who deserves it, its about if you can buy it, then ****ing buy it. if you cant, go play cs 1.6.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(973388, 124589, 1040, 100752, 1072936800, 'For the dedicated community', 'quote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nI dont know about a lot of other cs players but me and my friends were appauled wen we heard we werent able to get the source beta, ur basically forcing all the dedicated players who want to play the beta to buy a new vid card or buy a copy of one of the easiest/crappest games i have ever played. nothing would plz u guys more than to kill cs by the looks of it.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nIf it is such a crappy game why are you worried about the beta?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(973389, 124589, 1040, 100753, 1072936800, '', 'Benny I don\'t understand your complainign about not being able to get source, but than also not being able to afford a card to run source? \n\n\n\nSo why not kill  2 birds with one stone, and keep playing cs1.6? Since you can\'t get a card to run it? (considering it runs on some really low end cards) I mean if they gave it to you and you couldnt run it, you\'d have to upgrade anyways?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(973446, 124589, 1040, 100754, 1072936800, '', 'you don\'t  HAVE to get the BETA.\n\n\n\nthe FINAL will come out and not require you to have cs:cz or something else.\n\n\n\nMANY betas are for specially chosen groups.\n\n\n\ncompanies do this for a reason, probably the simple fact that they don\'t want many people using it. or whatever their reason is.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(973478, 124589, 1040, 100755, 1072936800, 'For the dedicated community', 'quote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nur basically forcing all the dedicated players who want to play the beta to buy a new vid card or buy a copy of one of the easiest/crappest games i have ever played.\n\n\n\nwrong. they are rewarding those who have shown continued MONETARY support. the ATI bundle is in essence monetary support, since Valve made a deal with ATI wnich lured people to buy that product, and the CZ owners (like myself) actually bought that game, rather than illegally downloading the skins online and smirking at how they basically "got CZ for free, uhuhuhuh", then flaming Valve employees on these forums about how crappy CZ is. \n\n\n\nthis beta test is Valve saying "dear loyal and valued customer, please enjoy this beta test, and please report any bugs. your reports help us perfect the game for everyone else, and you get a little preview taste of the game for your trouble"\n\n\n\nthe Valve servers literally came to a screeching halt to do this. now you imply they should do it for everyone else as well? that would cost an unimaginable mount of money for bandwidth, just so demonstrably unsupportive "customers" could beta test.\n\n\n\nyou are not being forced to buy anything extra to get CS:S - you will be able to buy the game when it is released, like everyone else. however, if you already HAD PURCHASED one of those items, you would have been able to partake in this little thank you gift from Valve. otherwise, the damn game ain\'t out yet, so chill and pretend you don\'t know about this beta test. []\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nnothing would plz u guys more than to kill cs by the looks of it.\n\n\n\nin fact, it would seem they are going to milk the CS cow until it is good and dry, hence another version of the game []\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nAs for who is deserving of it, some kiddy goes out and buys cz and they are deserving, i on the other hand have been a supporter of cs ever since it was made and would never leave it for another game am not deserving.\n\n\n\nthat is correct. you are NOT deserving of this beta test. in fact, i beg to differ with your portrayal of yourself as a supporter of cs. since the only purchase required to play cs could have in theory been made in 1998 (halflife), while being able to play cs for free ever since then, and you saying you\'ve played since the beginning, i would rather classify you as a moocher of the cs community. \n\n\n\nsimply playing a free game for 6 years does not make you a supporter of it\'s developers. laying down the bucks when new product is released is the surest way to show your support. (ok, whether or not cz is "new" is debatable, i admit - my point still stands however)\n\n\n\nthe only new cs game since the original has been cz, and you call it crappy and refuse to buy it. this makes you anything BUT a supporter of cs.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nI will "NOT" submit to your cruel torture and money hungry ways\n\n\n\nthen i must assume you stole your copy of windows, along with most of your software, and you also drive away from the gas pump and the drive through window without paying, rather than submit to the cruel torture of microsoft, exxon and mcdonalds.\n\n\n\nValve is a business, and business is about making money. if you can find a way to make a living doing something you love, you are very fortunate. i suspect this would apply to the Valve team.\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Benny T \n\nPS SIF NOT GIVE THE REAL PLAYERS SOURCE!!!!  \n\n\n\nbut my dear child, the real players ARE being given source. as i\'ve clearly illustrated, while you may be "leet" at cs, Valve doesn\'t care about that. they define "real players" as "real customers". you may be the greatest player in the world, but if you dont buy their products, you will get no "thank you\'s"\n\n\n\nin short: you don\'t matter as much as we do, and Valve likes us better than you []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
