(1007528, 128407, 1040, 100748, 1072936800, '#1 Priority: FIX THE NETCODE', 'Sorry for the capitals... \n\n\n\nBut after about 15 hours playing the Beta, the main thing that is killing the "CS Feel" is the netcode more than any in-game tweaks or "realism" additions.\n\n\n\nI was on a sub-30 ping server and was about three (game) feet from an enemy, aimed directly at his head and he didn\'t die. This is after emptying half a magazine of an MP5 on him as well.\n\n\n\nAnd before all the 12-year olds invade this thread with pointless, "You just suxors, dude!", or "Learn to aim, F*got Biatch!" posts...\n\n\n\nThe problem was experienced by every other person on the 14 player server -- Meaning, this wasn\'t some uber 20 vs. 20 game where pings were spiking all over the place.\n\n\n\nIn addition, I had these cvars set in my config as follows:\n\n\n\ncl_smooth 0\n\ncl_smoothtime 0.1\n\ncl_interp 0.1\n\ncl_predict 1\n\ncl_lagcompensation 0\n\n\n\nThe in-game movement is indeed smooth... \n\n\n\nBut again, actual shots registering was a common occurance and the main reason people started dropping from the game because they felt it was "no fun" to just "spray and pray" in the hopes that the server (finally) registered their shots.\n\n\n\nI know that Source is not the HL-1 engine and that Server Admins really need to upgrade a lot of their hardware to run it...\n\n\n\nBut I can tell you, this is the root cause for half of the complaints and comments about this game on this forum that go like:\n\n\n\n1) "My uber X800XT PE/6800 Ultra gets sh*tty frames per second. WTF? Source Suxxors!"\n\n\n\nand...\n\n\n\n2) "Quit ruining CS you Valve Nubs! It\'s too random and has no skillz!"\n\n\n\nTruly.\n\n\n\nThe hit detection (and object collision) needs to be of a much better quality when the final game ships, or you will have more flaming and upset CS players that actually don\'t know WHY they are saying the things they are (or will).\n\n\n\nDon\'t make the mistake UBISoft did with the Raven Shield netcode -- which is actually about at the same, subpar level as the CSS Beta -- And just leave it like this because there are much better games with better netcode that register hits and misses as they should be.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1007535, 128407, 1040, 100843, 1072936800, '', 'well said... experienced similar stuff in the past few days - netcode defiantly needs working on.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1007538, 128407, 1040, 100836, 1072936800, '', 'That isn\'t necissarily due to the net code.\n\n\n\nUsually mistakes like that are due to the users computer. Eg- you shoot the guy just as , as he is getting lag it just doesn\'t seem as obvious like in 1.6 when models looked liek they were having siezers.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1007541, 128407, 1040, 100566, 1072936800, '', 'Nicely said. The hit detection is... cringing at times.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049814, 128407, 1040, 100844, 1072936800, '', 'No it is not because of the users computer.\n\n\n\nI\'m getting 100fps no choke or loss and pinging under thirty on servers.\n\n\n\nI\'ve lost count of how many times I\'ve ran up behind someone with autoshotty, plugged them in the back/head with all 7 shots, and had only one or no shots register.\n\n\n\nWhen you flank someone and have 7 easy pointblank shotgun shots the result shouldn\'t be that you have to switch to your pistol to finish them off.\n\n\n\nThe netcode/hitdetection is way off at times. And yes it has a lot of that same crap feeling you get from raven shield where what the server decides hits hardly ever matches up with what you see.\n\n\n\nThis has to be fixed or it will kill the FEEL of CS. If physics objects have to be reduced to get the netcode back to at least 1.6 quality then they should do that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049885, 128407, 1040, 100845, 1072936800, '', 'quote:This has to be fixed or it will kill the FEEL of CS\n\n\n\nIt will not kill the FEEL of CS, it will kill the game completely, same with any other game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050057, 128407, 1040, 100846, 1072936800, '', 'Yeah i have been getting this quite a lot, very frustrating, its not on my side either, some servers seem better then others depending upon time and load, but really it seems like there is really poor shot registering.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050380, 128407, 1040, 100847, 1072936800, '', 'yeah. the other day I had tmp and a terrorist ran past me. I unloaded the full clip, He was aiming at ct sniper area so he didnt move.  He was probably about 2 to 3 game feet away.  Another terrorist comes out and kills me just as I finished the clip off. I checked the life of the guy I fired upon......87 health!!!! 1 or 2 bullets hit him out of 30, 2 to 3 feet away....very frusterating!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050426, 128407, 1040, 100848, 1072936800, '', 'is there any chance that you ARE hitting them but you just "think" you are not, making your spray wildly trying to register that hit .. in turn making your miss.\n\n\n\nJust a suggestion as so far I have foudn the netcode seems good and the responses are good, it just doesnt feed that info back to you..\n\n\n\ncheck that out and just look at the glock mpgs for both cz and source.\n\n\n\n/forums/...threadid=132223 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=132223)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050516, 128407, 1040, 100849, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LittleFo0t \n\nIt will not kill the FEEL of CS, it will kill the game completely, same with any other game.  \n\n\n\nI dont care how you say it. Its all the same. \n\n(/m3 n0 l1kz1n\' un1337 n3tc0d3, d0d3!)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050648, 128407, 1040, 100844, 1072936800, '', 'IF the choice was between having barrels and trash to kick and shoot around or having the SOLID netcode/hit detection of 1.5 or 1.6, then I\'m sorry to say the barrels and trash HAVE TO GO.\n\n\n\nThe gameplay would be much better without the objects and have solid hit detection than it is now with iffy fudgy lazy hit detection and some trash, tires, and barrels to kick/shoot around.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050719, 128407, 1040, 100850, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by mediaxs \n\nIF the choice was between having barrels and trash to kick and shoot around or having the SOLID netcode/hit detection of 1.5 or 1.6, then I\'m sorry to say the barrels and trash HAVE TO GO.\n\n\n\nThe gameplay would be much better without the objects and have solid hit detection than it is now with iffy fudgy lazy hit detection and some trash, tires, and barrels to kick/shoot around. \n\n\n\nToo true , they are of no use whatsoever at this point in time.\n\n\n\nGive us back the FEEL of the game , ditch the player animations while youre at it.\n\n\n\nIt is trully lifeless and laggy tbh []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050732, 128407, 1040, 100851, 1072936800, '', 'the netcode is realy funny []\n\n\n\nhope it will be fixed in a later beta, but for this beta i just hope to get my old buy menus back []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050794, 128407, 1040, 100852, 1072936800, '', 'i got no problems with the netcode, but let me tell you what i saw the other night. I was spectating a guy on the other team and i watched his pitiful aim, first off to the left and then to the right and then finally on him. The only problem was that the other guy had enough time to turn around and shoot him in a few shots. Well, instantly the guy I am spectating begins by saying \'omfg\', so I chirped up before he could go further and said, \'you missed him, so be quiet". Well dude begins losing it on me and I tell him I was spectating him. So he continued to tell me off etc.\n\n\n\nNow what I ask is, how many of you are the same when you go on about emptying a mp5. If I have noticed anything it was rare and at times even I will (to myself) fly off the hook when I am playing. Let\'s face it, it\'s a new game, it has bugs but the hit prediction is not as bad as everyone has made it out to be. I have put in about 75 hours if not more into this game and though there are some things that need improving, I have had zero problems with netcode(packetloss is server) and the hitboxes have been fine.\n\n\n\nAnyhow a lot of what the original poster has said is great, but for the tweaking, I\'ve done nothing on my CS:S and it runs perfectly fine and smooth as CS 1.6. Could be because of some of my XP tweaks.. I don\'t know.\n\n\n\nI\'m looking forward to some CS:S Update news.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1050832, 128407, 1040, 100853, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by mediaxs \n\nIF the choice was between having barrels and trash to kick and shoot around or having the SOLID netcode/hit detection of 1.5 or 1.6, then I\'m sorry to say the barrels and trash HAVE TO GO.\n\n\n\nThe gameplay would be much better without the objects and have solid hit detection than it is now with iffy fudgy lazy hit detection and some trash, tires, and barrels to kick/shoot around.  \n\n\n\n\n\nhey, we need that new buggy stuff to make css a new better game, just let them fix it..if you dont want those trash and barrels, you HAVE TO GO back to cs 1.6', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1007846, 128442, 1040, 100854, 1072936800, 'How to convert you old 1.6 buyscript', 'This post was made to explain to players of Counter-strike source how to\n\nconvert their old buy script from CS 1.6. Its painfully easy realy, what you \n\nhave to do it edit old script and add "buy" infront of the weapon your are buying.\n\n\n\nHere is a example:\n\nquote:The Old 1.6 way\n\nalias buyteamheavy "sg552;primammo"\n\n \n\nquote:How to do it in CS S\n\nalias buyteamheavy "buy aug;buy sg552;buy primammo"\n\n \n\n\n\nHere is a list of all the commands the buy command supports:\n\nquote:\n\nusage: buy <item>\n\n  primammo\n\n  secammo\n\n  vest\n\n  vesthelm\n\n  defuser\n\n  nvgs\n\n  flashbang\n\n  hegrenade\n\n  smokegrenade\n\n  galil\n\n  ak47\n\n  scout\n\n  sg552\n\n  awp\n\n  g3sg1\n\n  famas\n\n  m4a1\n\n  aug\n\n  sg550\n\n  glock\n\n  usp\n\n  p228\n\n  deagle\n\n  elite\n\n  fiveseven\n\n  m3\n\n  xm1014\n\n  mac10\n\n  tmp\n\n  mp5navy\n\n  ump45\n\n  p90\n\n  m249\n\n\n\n\n\nHow to install your newly made buy script\n\nFirst off find your steam folder, then got to: Valve Steam\\SteamApps\\Your@MailAddy.com\\counter-strike source beta\\cstrike\\cfg\n\nplace your buyscript in this folder ( or the one you can download from the bottom off the post).\n\nThen edit your config.cfg and add quote:exec buyscript.cfg ( Notice that you dont have to add exec cfg/buyscript.cfg, it assumes your running a config inside the cfg folder)\n\n\n\nDownload example buyscript (http://eks.wtfux.com/buyscript.cfg) ( Hosted by: www.clanhq.com (http://www.clanhq.com) )\n\n\n\nEDIT:\n\nAlso note that the source engine will not allow you to load as big "scripts" as HL1 did. You will get a error message "\n\nCbuf_AddText: buffer overflow", this means in my xp that the file you executed is to big. Just cut you script into several files (HL1 allowed me to exec files around 15kb but source only allows about 7kb)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
