(1019817, 129638, 1005, 100876, 1072936800, '', 'This is taken from hl2world.com message boards post by Macex\n\n\n\nquote:The animation is not called avoiddance, it\'s called menu_pose (3). There is another animation called speaker_testpose (255), which shows the ct lounging around on the speaker test map. \n\n\n\nIf you want to do the animation in the test_speakers map you do this command. \n\n\n\n"ent_fire ct use" <- activates the entity \n\n"ent_fire ct setsequence menu_pose" or "ent_fire ct setsequence 3" \n\n\n\nYou can also hack the map to add a cycler entity and set the sequence to 3 like the thread starter did. Also the menu_pose animation puts the entity about 50 units higher than where it should be, so it\'s like he\'s dancing in the air.  \n\n\n\nHave fun, because I am!\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance1.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance1.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance2.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance2.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance3.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance3.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance4.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance4.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance5.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance5.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance6.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance6.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance7.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance7.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance8.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance8.jpg)\n\nhttp://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance9.jpg (http://www.wtfhost.com/userfiles/mace/dance9.jpg)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
