(1030290, 130622, 1040, 101389, 1072936800, 'Let\'s discuss the flashbangs', 'I\'m surprised nobody\'s been talking about this yet (can\'t find any threads with a search, anyway).\n\n\n\nThe flashbangs: Yes they look really pretty, and the audio muffling is a nice addition, but it seems the old face-the-other-way FB dodge no longer works. I\'m guessing this is an intentional change to the game, but I think it\'s a bad one.\n\n\n\nI have two beefs with this:\n\n\n\n1) It\'s difficult to get close enough to your own exploding flashbang to take advantage of it when it goes off. Lobbing one around a nearby corner, intending to charge in after it detonates, will often get you blinded.\n\n\n\n2) Flashbanging your own team is too likely, because even if you throw it beyond their line of sight, they could still be in the radius. It\'s very difficult to judge and makes them dangerous to use unless you\'re right at the front of the rush (in which case, you\'re probably team-flash fodder yourself).\n\n\n\nSo: I\'d like to see the flash effect reduced according to line-of-sight, like it was in CS. I do concede that the new "bang" effect should mess up your hearing whether you\'re looking at the explosion or not.\n\n\n\nIn pre-emptive response to one obvious argument: I appreciate that the fuzzy-vision could be attributed to a general symptom of concussion, rather than just staring at the flash itself, but at the same time I think an avoidable flash effect - as used in CS - makes for more well-rounded gameplay.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030295, 130622, 1040, 100221, 1072936800, '', 'nothing to discuss. they are the ****.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030358, 130622, 1040, 101003, 1072936800, 'Let\'s discuss the flashbangs', 'quote:Originally posted by thisnameistaken \n\nLet\'s discuss the flashbangs  \n\n\n\nLet\'s not', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030363, 130622, 1040, 103365, 1072936800, '', 'I agree that they shouldnt BLIND you if you arent facing the same direction.. they should still make you deaf.  I don\'t have any experience with real flashbangs, but I would find it hard to believe if looking away from one before it was thrown would still make you blind (but once again I have no idea how powerful the blast of light would be)...  Anybody know?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030366, 130622, 1040, 103366, 1072936800, '', 'Actualy,when you turn your back to the flash,it does dumb the effect down a bit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030386, 130622, 1040, 100527, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by strobe32 \n\nI agree that they shouldnt BLIND you if you arent facing the same direction.. they should still make you deaf.  I don\'t have any experience with real flashbangs, but I would find it hard to believe if looking away from one before it was thrown would still make you blind (but once again I have no idea how powerful the blast of light would be)...  Anybody know?  \n\n\n\nif you were in range of a real flashbang it would probly knock you on your [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color]. regardless of wich way you were standing.\n\n\n\nanyone see that video on real TV when that swat officer put that flashbang in his pocket thinkin it wasnt live.....BANG!!!!!\n\n\n\nhe was walking around without a pantleg dazed as could be, then he fell to the ground...later rushed to a medical center.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030405, 130622, 1040, 101089, 1072936800, '', 'valve did go to a militry shooting range so maybe they got to see what flashbangs are really like. who knows, i like that its harder to avoid now...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030418, 130622, 1040, 100537, 1072936800, 'Let\'s discuss the flashbangs', 'quote:Originally posted by thisnameistaken \n\nI\'m surprised nobody\'s been talking about this yet (can\'t find any threads with a search, anyway).\n\n\n\nThe flashbangs: Yes they look really pretty, and the audio muffling is a nice addition, but it seems the old face-the-other-way FB dodge no longer works. I\'m guessing this is an intentional change to the game, but I think it\'s a bad one.\n\n\n\nI have two beefs with this:\n\n\n\n1) It\'s difficult to get close enough to your own exploding flashbang to take advantage of it when it goes off. Lobbing one around a nearby corner, intending to charge in after it detonates, will often get you blinded.\n\n\n\n2) Flashbanging your own team is too likely, because even if you throw it beyond their line of sight, they could still be in the radius. It\'s very difficult to judge and makes them dangerous to use unless you\'re right at the front of the rush (in which case, you\'re probably team-flash fodder yourself).\n\n\n\nSo: I\'d like to see the flash effect reduced according to line-of-sight, like it was in CS. I do concede that the new "bang" effect should mess up your hearing whether you\'re looking at the explosion or not.\n\n\n\nIn pre-emptive response to one obvious argument: I appreciate that the fuzzy-vision could be attributed to a general symptom of concussion, rather than just staring at the flash itself, but at the same time I think an avoidable flash effect - as used in CS - makes for more well-rounded gameplay.  \n\n\n\nIts a awesome change, your just dumb. End of thread.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030545, 130622, 1040, 100880, 1072936800, '', 'IRL, I thought FB\'s gave of a very high ringing sound.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030575, 130622, 1040, 100527, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by nbk5 \n\nIRL, I thought FB\'s gave of a very high ringing sound.  \n\n\n\nmainly a flashbang is desighned to disorient you making it easier for swat/police to raid the hell outa you while your semi-concious', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030586, 130622, 1040, 103367, 1072936800, '', 'i think the flashes are sweet and should stay how they are now!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030588, 130622, 1040, 100276, 1072936800, '', 'You can dumb down the FB effect by quiet a bit when turning away from them, but you will still be affected which is good.. \n\n\n\nBecause finally they are a bit more usefull now together with the smokegrenade.. What use is a FB anyway if people can just turn away from it fast and not be affected a single bit, completly useless..\n\n\n\nConclusion: I like The FB in CS:S, leave it the way it is, thxs..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030788, 130622, 1040, 101927, 1072936800, 'Let\'s discuss the flashbangs', 'quote:Originally posted by thisnameistaken \n\n1) It\'s difficult to get close enough to your own exploding flashbang to take advantage of it when it goes off. Lobbing one around a nearby corner, intending to charge in after it detonates, will often get you blinded. \n\n\n\nYeah, it\'s called having skills.  I for one think the flashbangs are just perfect the way they are.  I\'m a *very* average CS player and yet I\'ve been able to defend myself very well against stronger opponents, often snipers, just be using a well placed flashbang.  And when I get flashed myself, I bow down to the opponent and admit defeat.  Because it was good sport.\n\n\n\nFinally a gameplay mechanic that rewards thinking and outsmarting your opponent rather than just godlike aiming and lightning reflexes.\n\n\n\nThe flashbang is just fine.  It\'s like the AWP.  People [color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color][color=orange][font=wingdings]û[/font][/color] because they don\'t know how to use it, or play against it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030839, 130622, 1040, 100562, 1072936800, '', 'Howsa everyonesa dooins  i say dat duh flashbangs ir kool!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1030919, 130622, 1040, 100323, 1072936800, 'Let\'s discuss the flashbangs', 'quote:Originally posted by thisnameistaken \n\n\n\n\n\nThe flashbangs: Yes they look really pretty, and the audio muffling is a nice addition, but it seems the old face-the-other-way FB dodge no longer works. I\'m guessing this is an intentional change to the game, but I think it\'s a bad one.\n\n\n\n.  \n\n\n\nThis will be fixed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
