(1048180, 132230, 1005, 100900, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Fool\'s Gold \n\nAfter a close scrutiny of Gabe Newell�s account history on the forums, we\'ve come to the conclusion that the gold post is a fake. While we can\'t be 100% certain at this stage, all indicators point towards someone hacking the forum account. That said, all Gabe\'s previous posts on these forums are quite legitimate.\n\n\n\nWe apologize for the confusion and will be investigating further. Theoretically, an IPB forum account should be very difficult to hack. Well, that was the theory at least. We\'ll keep you updated. \n\n \n\n\n\nWell there u have it []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048181, 132230, 1005, 100905, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by eAi \n\nIts not a hoax. Gabe often posts on hl2fallout (see the original post at http://www.hl2fallout.com/forums/in...amp;#entry76575 (http://www.hl2fallout.com/forums/index.php?showtopic=4221&st=0&#entry76575)) Do you have evidence to support that that CSNation, HL2fallout and other sites don\'t have ??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048199, 132230, 1005, 100904, 1072936800, '', 'No, thats true... it probably is.\n\n\n\neAi', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048361, 132230, 1005, 100906, 1072936800, '', 'If onyly valve could step up and give us some damn info.. We\'ve been wainting for a year? just a official true for false statement would do fine.. I think we deserve that for patiently waiting.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048404, 132230, 1005, 100199, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by phased \n\nIf onyly valve could step up and give us some damn info.. We\'ve been wainting for a year? just a official true for false statement would do fine.. I think we deserve that for patiently waiting.  \n\n\n\nIt\'s Valve. They\'ll keep obscenely quiet for 1 week only, then they will go and post a 2 sentence thread on a choice either A. HL2Fallout.com B. HL2.net or C. HL2World, in which they will explain in vague detail what happened and will announce a A. One Month B. Six Month C. Eight Month delay. After which they will go into hiding for A. Two Months B. Until E32005, in which they will release the game A. Then B. One Month from then.\n\n\n\nIt\'s the Valve way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048944, 132230, 1005, 100907, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by phased \n\nIf onyly valve could step up and give us some damn info.. We\'ve been wainting for a year? just a official true for false statement would do fine.. I think we deserve that for patiently waiting.  \n\n\n\nI agree.  Valve can just as quickly stomp it down if it\'s a hoax.  Considering how many threads popped up last night on tho forums about the rumored gold status, you\'d think that the enforcers on these forums could just as easily say something to refute that rumor.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1048969, 132230, 1005, 100908, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Silverback1138 \n\nI agree.  Valve can just as quickly stomp it down if it\'s a hoax.  Considering how many threads popped up last night on tho forums about the rumored gold status, you\'d think that the enforcers on these forums could just as easily say something to refute that rumor.  \n\nYou have to remember that up until about now I suspect the entire Valve team was probably asleep, that would explain the long silence.  As for why they havn\'t posted anything now?  Well its saturday, and if it is true and the game will be going gold then I can certainly understand them sleeping in.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049290, 132230, 1005, 100045, 1072936800, '', 'false.\n\n\n\nDo you really think the gold announcement will be made with a 4 word forum post?  OMFG will count as four words by itself! :-]\n\n\n\nAlso, patient is not a word I would use to describe people\'s manner of waiting. []  Understandable -- I\'m pretty excited about it myself.\n\n\n\nAt any rate, it\'s 9:18am ... sorry I slept in or I would have stomped sooner.  At any other rate, it looks like hl2fallout.com cleared things up a while ago (relatively) with their Fool\'s Gold post.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049046, 132324, 1013, 100909, 1072936800, 'can not stay in games', 'i can fully access steam games and log on to the servers but i get sent back to the mane menu every 30 sec to 1 min. and in that time i can play the games im lag free. also when i was on my frends server the same thing happend and he told my that his server log  shoed "client sent drop" would this be of any help??. furthermore this just started to happen about 2 months a go i was able to play steam games with no problm thakyou for any help.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049305, 132324, 1013, 100910, 1072936800, '', 'you should check your console to see hwat error message yuou get.  then you should use the search feature on the forum to see if anyoen else has the same problem.\n\n\n\nHeres the post in response to these problems (IF its the one you have):\n\n/forums/show...threadid=101151 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=101151)\n\n\n\nmostl likely, its your firmware.  this happened to a lot of poeple abouyt a month back, and they said that you should downgrade your firmware.  I didnt want to do that, so I took the alternative.\n\n\n\nIt says it in the post, but Ill tell you.  You go to Play Games on Steam.  You right click the game(s) you want to do this with.  Then you click Create Desktop Shortcut.  On the desktop shortcut, right click it and go to Properties.  In the directory, add a space at the end and type this in:\n\n\n\n+clientport 26007\n\n\n\nThen you hsould be able to play A-OK, is your problem.  First you should check your console to see the error message/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1049413, 132324, 1013, 100909, 1072936800, '', 'there is 1 problm tho i do have the BEFSR81 router with the latest firware 2.50.2 is there a way i can down grade the firm ware??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1059731, 132324, 1013, 100911, 1072936800, '', 'I have posted the firmware for the BEFSR81 v3 to downgrade to a version that works with Steam games and stopped the constant disconnecting.\n\n\n\nhttp://miketaggart.com/files/Linksy...1_0915_code.bin (http://miketaggart.com/files/Linksys%20BEFSR81v3%20Firmware/CN81_v2.45.5_001_0915_code.bin)\n\n\n\nThe downgrade worked perfectly for me, but I was quite upset that Linksys could not provide it for me when I called them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1061362, 132324, 1013, 100909, 1072936800, '', 'ty for the post i also found a nother fix for this problme on the form Aeroplane told me to go the other fix is at the vary bottem of the page and agen ty for all the help', '127.0.0.1', 1),
