(1141260, 141033, 1005, 100971, 1072936800, '', 'there really isn\'t a "significant" one.  60 FPS looks damn smooth, and 100 doesn\'t look a whole lot better.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1142825, 141033, 1005, 100967, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by The Package \n\nthere really isn\'t a "significant" one.  60 FPS looks damn smooth, and 100 doesn\'t look a whole lot better.  \n\n\n\nActually, with my refresh-rate locked at 120 Hz, there\'s a world of difference between 60 and 100 fps []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1143134, 141033, 1005, 100964, 1072936800, 'Thanks', 'Who ever posted about v sync. Thanks. I can run at my 100 fps now. That was too easy. Just turn vertical sync off.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1143157, 141033, 1005, 100972, 1072936800, 'Thanks', 'quote:Originally posted by CROOOOW \n\nWho ever posted about v sync. Thanks. I can run at my 100 fps now. That was too easy. Just turn vertical sync off. \n\nPersonally, I wouldn\'t turn v-sync off as many people on the forums have said, v-sync  on prevents screen tearing. Still, many people do turn it off and they get away with it so if you want and it works, that\'s cool', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1143204, 141033, 1005, 100973, 1072936800, '', '...bit of useless info to make 60 fps seem not so bad.....\n\n\n\na standard television runs at between 25 fps and 30 fps\n\n\n\nthe default fps for cs is 72 fps\n\n\n\nyour monitor at 72 hz is considered "flicker free" ... it stops eye strain\n\n\n\nCROOOOW ... just remember that if you`re monitor cannot run at 100Mhz, without deselecting the "hide modes that this monitor cannot display" box in your display properties (monitor tab), your setting your monitor above its rated capacity...you may shorten its component life', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1144433, 141033, 1005, 100974, 1072936800, '', '85fps with vsync on is much smoother than 100fps with vsync off\n\nheck i bet 60fps with vsync on is better than 100fps with vsync off', '127.0.0.1', 1),
