(1176973, 144060, 1013, 101051, 1072936800, '', 'well muffin..... as far as the what you said\n\n\n\n[quote]edit: the answer to you\'re question I thought was obvious? people are using model/sprite cheats..... I think it was a step in the right direction but it created more issues.... at least their heart was in the right place.... haha[quote/]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI agree on the right direction thing.....but, every single map / sprint i have has come from cs/nation etc.... or the game itself....they still in my opinion screwed up big time with this update.... BEYOND>>>>>  they could have at least tested it out a little longer before throwing it out there...this is Retarted all the way...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179610, 144440, 1042, 100030, 1072936800, 'Cafe Administration Release - Version 1.2', 'A new version (V1.2) of the Caf� Administration Server is now available.  We have added a number of new features and improve overall system performance.\n\n\n\nCAServer:\n\n* Fixed CAS taking anything but ESCAPE to quit\n\n* Added SPACE key to emit current number of consumed licenses on CAServer\n\n* Improved LAN copy speed\n\n* Added MAC address for master server verification for cafes with dynamic IPs\n\n* Added timed update mode -- can be enabled/disabled, and times for update can be set by cafe owner.\n\n* Fixed issue with corrupted caches stopping loading and giving warning about "skipping app"\n\n* Fixed "Cannot logout of Steam" error when another Steam instance is running.  This will no longer cause the CAServer to throw the error on a dialog box thereby stopping its execution. Instead, the error is logged in the log file (it did previously as well).\n\n* Fixed requirement (bug) for having cr/lf at end of passwords.txt file.\n\n* Added timestamp to CAServer to show when updates are processed\n\n\n\nLSClient:\n\n* New configuration parameters for lsclient\n\n* Added ability to force Steam to logout after game is shut down (cafe request)\n\n* Added save/restore capability -- Caf� customers can create local accounts "cafe login" with passwords and have their game settings restored each time they visit the caf�.\n\n* Added ability for client to accept user login thereby allowing cafe customers to log into Steam using their own Steam accounts\n\n\n\nMisc\n\n* Created a utility for customers to retrieve all MAC addresses for a particular pc\n\n* Created utility UI for CAServer configuration and cafe account creation\n\n	* Edit CAServer configuration parameters\n\n	* Add/Edit/Remove cafe users for saving saved games and user configuration files\n\n\n\nWe will continue to support CAS version 1.1 until the caf� customer base has moved to the new MAC address base master server.  In order to use the new CAS software, you\'ll need to download the new CASPackage.zip file from Valve\'s FTP:\n\n\n\nftp.valvesoftware.com\n\nUser: CAServer\n\nPass: ValveCAS2112\n\n\n\nInstructions (word doc) are included in the zip for proper installation of the CAS and client software.  If you haven\'t already, please make sure you email casmaster@valvesoftware.com (mailto:casmaster@valvesoftware.com) and include the following information:\n\n\n\n1) Contact email address\n\n2) External static IP address or MAC addresses reported using the MACUtil found in the CASPackage.zip file\n\n3) Caf� ID #\n\n\n\nIf you have any problems, please contact support@valvesoftware.com (mailto:support@valvesoftware.com).  Be sure to include any error or warning messages you are seeing and a full description of the problem and your caf� ID number.\n\n\n\nMike', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179687, 144440, 1042, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks Mike.\n\n\n\nJust one question though, and Ill take a peek now in the Doc to see if its covered..\n\n\n\nYou mentioned added a function to close the steam account when game is closed/cyber cafe close.\n\n\n\nCan you be more specific how this works, and how I can go about making use of this feature..\n\n\n\nMy cyber cafe software is a bit basic t.b.h. and if I can see how others are closing the steam account when finsihed with, I will try and see if I can find a way to intergrate it into my cafe software..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179700, 144440, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'For question on the new features, leave them here I\'ll answer them all as much as I can []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179729, 144440, 1042, 101052, 1072936800, '', 'Just did :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179894, 144440, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'I left the answer on your MSN :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1179959, 144440, 1042, 101053, 1072936800, '', 'The 1.2 server won\'t let any of our clients log in.\n\nWhen I try running an old lsclient, it shows connecting to server for about a minute, then just dissapears.\n\nIf I manually copy the 1.2 client files to a client, then it says the server is getting updates.\n\nThe server is not updating though, it shows waiting for connections.\n\n\n\nAlso, the macutil program does not run on my server.  It crashes with a missing dll error "MFC42D.dll" (windows 2000 server)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180021, 144440, 1042, 101054, 1072936800, '', 'Anthem,\n\n\n\nSend me your config files (ricke@valvesoftware.com).\n\n\n\nAs for the MACUtil let me check on that I must be using something that requires the dll (which is on my dev machine obviously).\n\n\n\nRick\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180078, 144440, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by anthemgamer \n\nThe 1.2 server won\'t let any of our clients log in.\n\nWhen I try running an old lsclient, it shows connecting to server for about a minute, then just dissapears.\n\nIf I manually copy the 1.2 client files to a client, then it says the server is getting updates.\n\nThe server is not updating though, it shows waiting for connections.\n\n\n\nAlso, the macutil program does not run on my server.  It crashes with a missing dll error "MFC42D.dll" (windows 2000 server)  \n\n\n\nIf you\'re using CAS before version 1.2 , you have to manually copy the file over to your clients, because older version cannot get the new files "correctly" from the new CAS.\n\n\n\nRick, I forgot to tell ya about this [] (smack me for this one)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180102, 144440, 1042, 101054, 1072936800, '', 'Oh yes good point Albert222.  You have to re-install the new files.  I made a large number of changes to the networking code (protocols and performance) so we have to ask you to do a fresh install of the files.  Sorry I didn\'t mention that in the release notes.\n\n\n\nRick\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180602, 144440, 1042, 101055, 1072936800, 'Help !', 'Hello,\n\n\n\njust installed CAS 1.2 on the clients (Win XP SP1). When starting the lsclient.exe up, the login window is displayed for approx. half a second and then the program simply terminates!\n\n\n\nI�ve copied the files over to the clients manually in the /Valve/Steam directory.\n\n\n\ns there something missing? The config file is correct...\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\nMartin', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180611, 144440, 1042, 101054, 1072936800, '', 'Ok there\'s a few people with this (although Albert and I never saw this) so for now if you get this problem, keep using the previous version of CAS until I have a solution.\n\n\n\nRick\n\nValve', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180681, 144440, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'Even the best tester like *cough*me*cough* cannot detect everything []\n\n\n\nIf you have this problem, please use the older version first. Until Rick have a solution.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1180988, 144440, 1042, 101053, 1072936800, '', 'I can\'t run the new server, so I don\'t know how well that user config feature works, but I have a few concerns.\n\nMy cafe management software has the feature built in as most do, and I don\'t really want to mess with another product trying to do the same thing.  Also, I have a huge array set up to hold all of our user files, but that is on a different server.  I\'m not going to run CAS on that server, or anything else  (stability).  This means I have to make sure I have enough disk space on the CAS server now too.  I\'ve no idea how large the HL2 save files will be, but I know some of the other games can get pretty large.\n\n\n\nWouldn\'t it just be easier for the developers to make the saves and configs go to a static path and let us worry about transfering files.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1181055, 144440, 1042, 101056, 1072936800, 'Help !', 'I have the same problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nquote:Originally posted by Atreju \n\nHello,\n\n\n\njust installed CAS 1.2 on the clients (Win XP SP1). When starting the lsclient.exe up, the login window is displayed for approx. half a second and then the program simply terminates!\n\n\n\nI�ve copied the files over to the clients manually in the /Valve/Steam directory.\n\n\n\ns there something missing? The config file is correct...\n\n\n\nRegards,\n\nMartin', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1181060, 144440, 1042, 100263, 1072936800, '', 'you can always disable the config/save games feature on the LSClient options.\n\n\n\nJust let CAS handle the licesening manganment for you, and let your Cafe software (I assume is SmartLaunch) to do the others.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1181034, 144577, 1013, 101057, 1072936800, 'Temp Fix to <Not Responding>', 'If you are having trouble connecting or pinging a server, then download xfire (a program like steam friends that can be used with like 100 games) and install it. Make a new user, add your server ip to the favorites and double click it to join. Viola.\n\n\n\nXfire: http://www.xfire.com/xf/index.php (http://www.xfire.com/xf/index.php)\n\n\n\nUrl Fixed, god i hate steam forums. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
