(1247590, 150789, 1005, 101090, 1072936800, 'CONFIRMED: HL2 RETAIL uses Steam and Internet', 'Just in case you weren\'t sure, this from Valve today...\n\n\n\nQUOTE\n\nResponse (PatrickMc) - 10/06/2004 09:32 AM \n\nHello, \n\n\n\nHL2 can only be played through Steam and will require an Internet connection, but you will be able to play in Offline mode once you have registered your cd key. \n\nUNQUOTE\n\n\n\nIt\'s going to be fun convincing the RETAIL crowd that this is really a good idea.\n\n\n\n--\n\nGrumps', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247622, 150789, 1005, 101091, 1072936800, '', 'So, to "verify" your purchase, it requires an internet connection.\n\n\n\nAfter "verification", the single player game can be played with Steam in "Offline" mode, which doesn\'t require an internet connection.\n\n\n\nFor many people, this will not be a problem.\n\n\n\nFor those that it is a problem, they probably hadn\'t  read the system requirements when they bought it.\n\n\n\nGentle', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247637, 150789, 1005, 100462, 1072936800, 'CONFIRMED: HL2 RETAIL uses Steam and Internet', 'quote:Originally posted by grumpycrab \n\nJust in case you weren\'t sure, this from Valve today...\n\n\n\nQUOTE\n\nResponse (PatrickMc) - 10/06/2004 09:32 AM \n\nHello, \n\n\n\nHL2 can only be played through Steam and will require an Internet connection, but you will be able to play in Offline mode once you have registered your cd key. \n\nUNQUOTE\n\n\n\nIt\'s going to be fun convincing the RETAIL crowd that this is really a good idea.\n\n\n\n--\n\nGrumps  \n\n\n\n\n\nHAHAHA, warez suckers are gonna get served humble pie.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247713, 150789, 1005, 101092, 1072936800, 'Re: CONFIRMED: HL2 RETAIL uses Steam and Internet', 'quote:Originally posted by DarkWasp \n\nHAHAHA, warez suckers are gonna get served humble pie.  \n\n\n\n\n\nI think thats the main reason steam is required to run the game. I knew something would happen like this after they got h4x0rd. Its VALVes way of saying FU to h4xorz. Its a smart move in my opinion, like come on, who doesnt have an internet connection that is into PC gaming? Ive read a few stories about people that are in college and steam wont punch a hole in the campus firewall but a handful of people are not going to sway a decision to remove a major function of the developers platform. I feel for those people but s41t happens sometimes and there is nothing you can do about it. Dial up through a cell phone or something to registetr and be done with it. Ive done it before!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247736, 150789, 1005, 101093, 1072936800, 'Re: CONFIRMED: HL2 RETAIL uses Steam and Internet', 'quote:Originally posted by DarkWasp \n\nHAHAHA, warez suckers are gonna get served humble pie.  \n\n\n\ni hope ur not trying to say that this game wont be illegally copied, cuz it will. im getting mine through steam, but i will prob still d/l the HL2 on DVD from a warez site so i can have the game on disc and not just on steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247741, 150789, 1005, 101094, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s a brilliant idea, but it won\'t stop Warez.  Someone will crack it just like they always do.  Whether they crack the executable and remove the necesseity for Steam, write some kind of "no Internet" crack, or simply design some sort of local Steam server emulator with a hacked client... it\'ll just fuel the cracker community and then Valve will have to start all over.\n\n\n\nBut I don\'t know what I\'m talking about really.  I don\'t have any knowledge on the subject beyond supposition.  I guess we\'ll see, this COULD be the end of warez, or it might just delay the warez until a few weeks after release, which will fuel sales on it\'s own.  Doom 3 and Sims 2 were both available illegally on the internet before they even hit store shelves... but they\'ve both sold extremely well anyway.\n\n\n\nWhatever, I think it\'s a great idea, and I don\'t care about it because I have an internet connection, I have Steam, and i am going to buy Half Life 2.\n\n\n\nSteam is free, the internet is cheaper than it\'s ever been (Bellsouth is offering DSL for $9.95 a month) and the only people who lose are the dumb little kids who go to Wal-Mart and convince their illiterate parents buy games without even considering the limitations of their ancient PC.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247771, 150789, 1005, 101092, 1072936800, '', 'I agree with you on that one. I also have steam, cable connection(balls fast), and a locked copy of HL2 on my PC. I think it will definitely cut down on the amount of people using a cracked copy of the game. Developers are smart but so are h4x0rz and there is no way to stop them, they will eventually find a way to crack anything. I kinda liked the battle between h4x0rz and cd protection myself, CD protection would be knocked down and then they would just develop a different one, I think they are up to Safedisc 3.3 or some crap now. LOL.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247774, 150789, 1005, 101095, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Thater \n\nIt\'s a brilliant idea, but it won\'t stop Warez.  Someone will crack it just like they always do.  Whether they crack the executable and remove the necesseity for Steam, write some kind of "no Internet" crack, or simply design some sort of local Steam server emulator with a hacked client... it\'ll just fuel the cracker community and then Valve will have to start all over.\n\n\n\nBut I don\'t know what I\'m talking about really.  I don\'t have any knowledge on the subject beyond supposition.  I guess we\'ll see, this COULD be the end of warez, or it might just delay the warez until a few weeks after release, which will fuel sales on it\'s own.  Doom 3 and Sims 2 were both available illegally on the internet before they even hit store shelves... but they\'ve both sold extremely well anyway.\n\n\n\nWhatever, I think it\'s a great idea, and I don\'t care about it because I have an internet connection, I have Steam, and i am going to buy Half Life 2.\n\n\n\nSteam is free, the internet is cheaper than it\'s ever been (Bellsouth is offering DSL for $9.95 a month) and the only people who lose are the dumb little kids who go to Wal-Mart and convince their illiterate parents buy games without even considering the limitations of their ancient PC.  \n\nuhh their system has already been cracked, they won\'t be preventing much, incase you didn\'t know, css was out way before they released it because someone got a hold of a cyber-cafe account, and found a way to play without steam. amazing huh?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247782, 150789, 1005, 101092, 1072936800, '', 'Also.....\n\n\n\nDoom 3 and Sims 2 were both available illegally on the internet before they even hit store shelves...\n\n\n\nWonder if that will happen to HL2?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247807, 150789, 1005, 101096, 1072936800, '', 'one of the greatest gifts of all:  if you put your mind to it, it will happen.\n\n\n\nunfortunatly, some use it for unproductive means, ie: hackers.\n\n\n\nthis game will be hacked.  it is that simple, if a lock is made and it it meant to be opened by a key, that key can be recreated in many, many ways.  \n\n\n\nit is sad, because i know that some of the $$ i shell out for games is set aside to offset the cost of hackers/warez.\n\n\n\nif this setup, by VALVe, delays or removes some of the initial impact, good for them.\n\n\n\n- Keep.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247820, 150789, 1005, 101097, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by meekmaster \n\nAlso.....\n\n\n\nDoom 3 and Sims 2 were both available illegally on the internet before they even hit store shelves...\n\n\n\nWonder if that will happen to HL2?  \n\n\n\nAlways live by this general rule:\n\n\n\nAnything made by man can be destroyed by man.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247840, 150789, 1005, 101096, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by CSTactics \n\nAlways live by this general rule:\n\n\n\nAnything made by man can be destroyed by man.  \n\n\n\nkinda funny wording your used:\n\n\n\n"always" an absulute  "live by this general" not absolute "rule".\n\n\n\njust made me smile.\n\n\n\nI would think ideas made by humankind, can\'t be destroyed.\n\n\n\n- Keep.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247849, 150789, 1005, 101092, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by CSTactics \n\nAlways live by this general rule:\n\n\n\nAnything made by man can be destroyed by man.  \n\n\n\nHAHA, I hope the same too about delaying the hackers, I bet that will anger them like a pack of hemerhoids, lol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247905, 150789, 1005, 101098, 1072936800, '', 'Does everyonr think this is simply to hinder hackers?\n\n\n\nI\'m not so sure..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1247907, 150789, 1005, 101099, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m just worried that keygens will take away valid CD Keys from people who actually purchase it.\n\n\n\nEdit: DOOM 3 was the most pirated game ever (it only required a key for multiplayer, or something like that) and iD still profited massively. Deep down I really, really hope that the amount of money Valve poured into anti-piracy technology will not be made up by people decide against pirating it and get it from the store. Most people are honest, and these measures hurt the people who buy it more than the pirates.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1248733, 150883, 1013, 100323, 1072936800, 'Tomorrow', 'Half-Life 2 Steam Offers Ready Thursday\n\n \n\nTomorrow at 11 am PST, the Half-Life 2 Steam offers will be ready for purchase. Details and pricing for these offers are pasted below. Those who purchase via Steam, will receive the final version of Counter-Strike: Source immediately. Half-Life 2 and other games in the Steam offerings will be made available to purchasers upon their release.\n\n\n\nATI/Half-Life 2 bundle owners may redeem their product key for the Bronze offer or apply their key toward the purchase of either the Silver or Gold offers, receiving a credit equal to the price of the Bronze offer.\n\n\n\nAlso tomorrow, the Counter-Strike: Source beta will close. Valve would like to thank the thousands of gamers who participated in the beta and helped make it a success. \n\n\n\nFor more detailed information, please visit www.steampowered.com (http://www.steampowered.com)\n\n\n\n\n\nHalf-Life 2 Steam Offers\n\n\n\nSTEAM OFFERINGS\n\n\n\n1. "Bronze" -- $49.95\n\n-- Half-Life 2*\n\n-- Counter-Strike: Source\n\n*(To be made available upon product\'s release.)\n\n\n\n\n\n2. "Silver" -- $59.95\n\n-- Half-Life 2*\n\n-- Counter-Strike: Source\n\n-- Half-Life 1: Source*\n\n-- Day of Defeat: Source*\n\n-- Valve\'s back catalog currently available on Steam *(To be made available upon products\' release.)\n\n\n\n\n\n3. "Gold" -- $89.95\n\n-- Half-Life 2*\n\n-- Counter-Strike: Source\n\n-- Half-Life 1: Source*\n\n-- Day of Defeat: Source*\n\n-- Valve\'s back catalog currently available on Steam\n\n-- Complete Half-Life 2 Strategy Guide from Prima Games\n\n-- 3 different Half-Life 2 posters\n\n-- Half-Life Collector\'s box\n\n-- Half-Life 2 hat\n\n-- Half-Life 2 postcard\n\n-- Half-Life 2 stickers\n\n-- Half-Life 2 Soundtrack CD\n\n-- Chance to win a trip to Valve! (1 trip offered for every 5000 Gold packages purchased).\n\n*(To be made available upon products\' release.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
