(1254486, 151333, 1005, 101137, 1072936800, '', 'The best thing to do which has already been mentioned on here. Partition your hard drive and install on a different partition to your windows installation. Then you can format every day and steam will not be affected.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1261947, 151333, 1005, 101133, 1072936800, '', 'ok dw i cbf orderin cds no more i need a week b4 i can get silver and 2weeks for gold but i\'m gonna go silver', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1261986, 151333, 1005, 101138, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by BakeSnake \n\nnot everyone has a dvd burner, so our only option would be to rar the gcf files and split them into cd sized parts. totally bogus. im irate at valve. i should be able to buy hl2 retail and THEN download EVERYTHING ELSE, just like i can do now with hl1.\n\n\n\nlame.  or you could wait awhile until Vivendi puts out the games on disk.\n\n\n\n\n\nValve doesnt make CDs or DVDs .. theyre developers not a distribution company.... instead of being irate with Valve you should be extremely happy with the fact that you can get CS:Source now instead of waiting however long to get it through Vivendi.plus youre going to get DOD:Source as well for the price you would pay for the disk version in store.\n\n\n\noh and the reason you were able to get those games for free when you had HL1 was they were developed by a third person that chose to do them for free ...they then were sorta bought out so that Valve could sell a retail version of the mod.\n\nnow that there is a fan base for those said mods.. Valve has gone to work and created a DOD and CS for source ..they have all the right in the world to decide to charge you for them..because they themselves put work into them.\n\n\n\nor are you somebody that thinks you shouldnt have to pay for products', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1262284, 151333, 1005, 101133, 1072936800, '', 'so whos the distruputerperthing?\n\ncant i pay for cds from them like cz? 15-20bux?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1262457, 151333, 1005, 101138, 1072936800, '', 'Vivendi is the company that is contractually obligated to bring HL2 on dvd/cd... they will release it as such once they find that HL2 is ready.when that is?... no one really knows', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253384, 151353, 1013, 101139, 1072936800, 'HL2 Packs and Tax ..', 'One of the main reasons to buy the game on steam for me (Israeli user), is the fact that a retail box here would have 18% VAT, aswell as 40-50% customs tax when imported in. That results in a very, very high price for a single game.\n\n\n\nSo naturally, im wondering, do i have to pay any taxes while buying the game from steam ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253388, 151353, 1013, 101140, 1072936800, '', 'yes, you will have to pay taxes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253391, 151353, 1013, 100043, 1072936800, '', 'the prices quoted already include TAX', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253394, 151353, 1013, 100708, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t have a clue about Israel, man. In the United States if the product ships from another state you do not have to pay sales tax.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253398, 151353, 1013, 101139, 1072936800, '', 'Im aware of the fact ill have to pay taxes, yes, but which ones is the matter.\n\n\n\nIm hoping the country doesnt have anything to do with the purchase, since im not getting any physical material shipped in .. im only charging my credit card with the deal.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253408, 151353, 1013, 100043, 1072936800, '', 'u will pay Valves TAX', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253463, 151353, 1013, 101139, 1072936800, '', 'If thats the case, id prefer to get it on steam indeed, instead of paying lots of taxes on a retail box.\n\n\n\nCould any VALVe staff confirm this ? im not asking taylor or gabe to respond, they have more then their fair share of work to do these days, but if a moderator could confirm this it would be great.\n\n\n\nThanks in advance, R.Sagy.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253654, 151353, 1013, 100658, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m not sure if this answers your question because I found it in a rush and didn\'t get to read it\n\nhttp://www.cato.org/tech/tk/011017-tk.html (http://www.cato.org/tech/tk/011017-tk.html)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253688, 151353, 1013, 101141, 1072936800, '', 'You do not have to pay any tax at all. \n\n\n\nWith those high Israeli taxes, I reccommend you buy it from steam.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253704, 151353, 1013, 100185, 1072936800, '', 'when i got CZ via steam i was charged $5.24 TAX from VALVe on-top of the normal charge.\n\nThat was USA to England for a steam game with no CD etc.\n\ni think we will be charged tax on top of what the price says.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253726, 151353, 1013, 101142, 1072936800, '', 'When I got CS:CZ via Steam I paid no taxes according to the e-mail receipt from Steam - I\'m in New Zealand   where retail will have taxes ... it seems that different countries have different rules when it comes to downloading ...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253733, 151353, 1013, 101143, 1072936800, '', 'I wasn\'t charged any tax when i bought CZ from Canada. So i expect it will be the same with HL2.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253751, 151353, 1013, 100185, 1072936800, 'My CZ sale.', 'Thank you for your recent purchase. Condition Zero is now available in your\n\nSteam "Games" window. To play, just double-click on the name of a game in this\n\nlist.\n\n\n\nYour credit card has been charged as detailed below. This email serves as your\n\nreceipt.\n\n\n\nProduct				Cost\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nCondition Zero                $  29.95\n\n\n\nTax (United Kingdom)          $   5.24\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nTotal                         $  35.19\n\n\n\nCurrency:                     U.S. Dollars\n\nCredit card type:             Visa\n\n\n\nENGLAND SUX! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253783, 151353, 1013, 101139, 1072936800, '', 'Hm.. $5 Tax, does that fit with the VAT taxes in the UK, or is it simply a taxing on the download valve drives or something ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1253791, 151353, 1013, 101141, 1072936800, '', 'That is like 16%, man.\n\n\n\nOutrageous.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
