(1258098, 151953, 1005, 101136, 1072936800, '**How To.. Backup Your Steam Folder and Games onto CD or DVD**', 'Steam MUST be closed before beginning!\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n*Using WinRAR to backup your games in Steam*\n\n\n\nFollow the first set of instructions, in order to compress the Steam folder and make them ready to burn []\n\n\n\n1a) Find the Steam folder, by going through the folders on the harddrive >>>\n\nFound here; "My Computer" >>> "x:\\" >>> "Program Files" >>> "Valve" >>> "Steam" >>> \n\n\n\nOR\n\n\n\n1b) Open WinRAR and click the "Browse" button to search for the SteamApps folder >>>\n\n(This might be easier if you have used WinRAR before and/or familiar with file tree structures)\n\nHere is an  Example (http://212.112.186.18/steam/pickweretosave.gif)\n\n\n\n2) Right-click on the folder and select "add to archive" from the popup shell >>>\n\n(This is the menu that appears when you right click)\n\n\n\n3) Select a RAR NOT ZIP >>>\n\n(This is an important step)\n\nHere is an Example (http://212.112.186.18/steam/4rarnotzip.gif)\n\n\n\n4) Select the "Store" compression method >>> \n\n(You can select best etc but using "store" will ensure that nothing gets corrupt during compression\n\nHere is an Example (http://212.112.186.18/steam/5selectstore.gif)\n\n\n\n5) Split in to bytes >>>\n\n(This is where you input 4500000000 bytes for dvd)\n\nHere is an Example (http://212.112.186.18/steam/7splitintobytes.gif) \n\n\n\n\n\n6) Select ok >>>\n\n(This may take a while, depending on the compression levels)\n\n\n\n7) The created SteamApps.rar will be created here;\n\n\n\n"My Computer" >>> "x:\\" >>> "Program Files" >>> "Valve" >>> "Steam" >>> \n\n(Where x is the primary installation partition. C:\\ is the default for most users!)\n\n\n\n------------------------------------------------\n\n*Burning Games to CD or DVD*\n\n\n\nOpen up Nero and burn all the backed up RAR files on to CD\'s or a DVD by following the next set of instructions []\n\n\n\n1) Start Menu >>> Program Files >>> Nero Burning ROM \n\n(Some users might want to use NeroExpress?)\n\n\n\n2) Select "CD ROM (ISO)" and type a name suitable >>>\n\n(Preferrably use sequential name like SteamBackup1 , 2 etc)\n\n\n\n3) Click New >>>\n\n\n\n4) Find location of saved "SteamApps1, SteamApps2.rar etc, then drag and drop the files on to the cd >>>\n\n\n\n5) Select Burn Icon and confirm!\n\n(You can backup and burn the barebones files for Cs: Source , and HL2, instead of the whole SteamApps folder.. However; This involves ONLY backing up the relevant .gcf files! Do this at your own risk!)\n\n\n\n=============================================\n\n\n\n*Re-Installing files back into Steam folder*\n\n\n\nFollow this final set of instructions in order to re-install your games in to Steam []\n\n\n\n1) Re-Install Steam >>>\n\n(Log-Out and Exit after installation)\n\n\n\n2) Find SteamApps1.rar, SteamApps2.rar etc >>>\n\n (These will be on your CD\'s or DVD that you burned earlier)\n\n\n\n3) Right click and select "Extract to" >>>\n\n(This is where Steam is installed) e.g "My Computer" >>> "x:\\" >>> "Program Files" >>> "Valve" >>> "Steam"\n\n\n\n4) WinRAR will ask for next archive >>> \n\n(Just select the next archive or disc (as WinRAR calls it) when it asks i.e The SteamApps2.rar would be the next "disc" or "archive" in this case)\n\n\n\n5) Thats it! You\'re Done!\n\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nThese are the application installers, you will need;\n\nClick to open and, select "Save As"\n\n\n\n1) WinRAR Installer\n\n\n\n\n\n2) Steam Installer\n\n\n\n\n\n3) Nero Burning ROM Installer\n\n\n\n\n\n=============================================\n\nClick Here (/forums/showthread.php?s=&postid=1447527#post1447527) to learn about creating a self extracting (.exe) file to unpack Half Life 2 for you []\n\n----------------------------------------------', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1258203, 151953, 1005, 101158, 1072936800, 'How To.. Backup Your Games', 'quote:Originally posted by EVH \n\nThis is EVH\'s easy way to back-up your Steam folder and protect your Steam games for ever \n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n"My Computer" >>> "C:\\" >>> "Program Files" >>> "Valve" >>> "Steam" >>> \n\n\n\n*Then just burn whole "Steamapps folder" onto DVD/CD*.. \n\n\n\n==NOTE=======================\n\n\n\nYou might need to RAR the whole thing and seperate into 4.7GB parts (Using WinRAR) to fit on more than 1 dvd... or seperate 700mb parts (cd people)... depends on how many games you have...\n\n\n\nOR you can just burn each of the individual .gcf files on to as many dvds/cd\'s as you can fit them on and slip them in to the "steamapps" folder, when you re-install steam\n\n\n\n=============================\n\n\n\nWinRAR can be found here http://www.downloads.com (http://www.downloads.com)\n\n\n\nSteam can be found here http://www.steampowered.com (http://www.steampowered.com)\n\n\n\n**MAKE THIS A STICKY SO PEOPLE DONT REPEAT ANY THREADS ASKING HOW TO BACKUP GAMES []**  \n\n\n\nGood post []\n\n\n\nquote:**MAKE THIS A STICKY SO PEOPLE DONT REPEAT ANY THREADS ASKING HOW TO BACKUP GAMES []** \n\n\n\nOnly if it were that easy LOL', '127.0.0.1', 1),
