(1264313, 151953, 1005, 101162, 1072936800, 'Disk Spanning', 'Hi there\n\n\n\nYou can use winrar (www.rarlab.com (http://www.rarlab.com)) to span your files across smaller disks.  Comes in handy when you can only write to CD\'s and not DVD\'s.\n\n\n\nMy approach to backups was to create a partition on my drive dedicated to games installs.  Not only do the games load faster, all of the files are retained whenever I feel like reinstalling windows.\n\n\n\nNahema', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264319, 151953, 1005, 101163, 1072936800, 'Split Files...', 'You install WinRar, rightclick your Steamfolder , chose "Add to archive" . In the window which now appears you choose "split into parts" (or sth. like that , since i have the german Version-its a dropdown menu) , choose the length of the parts and off you go ....\n\nEDIT:You also must choose to compress to .rar as format since zips don\'t support splitting files.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
