(1263048, 152528, 1040, 101181, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by [dave^]Cannon \n\nITS NOT BETA ANYMORE, this is the final game, of course there will be ongoing update for ages, maps, models, possible gameplay improvement, etc etc.\n\n \n\n\n\nThis is Beta V.2!! Ask a mod or a VAlve employee if you dont believe me.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1263049, 152528, 1040, 101176, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cleanbluesky \n\nThe big new disadvantage of Steam... VALVe would not have had teh balls to put out this \'final product\' in a box as it is still a B3ta...\n\n \n\n\n\nYou are right. Valve got what they want with steam: many people buys software that is 10 percent finished. After all, they can say: you will get the other 90 percent in some months with update, stay happy.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1263061, 152528, 1040, 100623, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by S|N|ST4 \n\nSo basically VALVe released an unfinished product. Typical.  \n\nagree !\n\nas usual :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1263895, 152642, 1040, 101182, 1072936800, 'Anyone managed to actually GET solid 99fps?', 'If so what spec/tweaks do you use?\n\n\n\nThanks', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264008, 152642, 1040, 101182, 1072936800, '', 'no then []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264022, 152642, 1040, 101128, 1072936800, '', 'People who do probably all have fairly new cards. I mean you need a new card just to keep up with this stuff!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264044, 152642, 1040, 101182, 1072936800, '', 'im on 9800pro, 1gb Duel RAM, 2ghz... im averaging 55fps :/ I know the CPU isnt the best but how good do our machines need to be to get 99fps!?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264214, 152642, 1040, 101183, 1072936800, '99', 'I\'m using a max fps of 101 but it acutally locks it at 99 sooo...\n\n\n\nI have Amd64 3500+, 1.5gb dual channel PC3200 XMS, neo2 platinum, 9800Pro\n\n\n\nI run dxlevel 80, 800x600, no AA or AF, low shader, low shadows, high on the other 2, no vsync.\n\n\n\nI don\'t get 99 constant like CS but I\'m working on it, thats my goal anyway.. if I findout the perfect settings I\'ll share.\n\n\n\n99 fps constant is a must for me, i\'m just goign to keep turning thinks off/low until I can get some nice FPS....\n\n\n\nhave fun tweaking', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264223, 152642, 1040, 101184, 1072936800, '', 'I have a Athlon 64 3000 (2.0GHz), 9600Pro stock, 512MB DDR333 and I\'m getting:\n\n\n\n1024x768, no AA, med textures:  60 fps (avg)\n\n1024x768, 2xAA, med textures:  50 fps (avg)\n\n\n\nThat\'s in CS games.  Stresstest for some reason rate much better.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264226, 152642, 1040, 100566, 1072936800, '', 'I get 99 fps most of the time when running around by myself.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264241, 152642, 1040, 101174, 1072936800, '', 'With a half decent system and some tweaking it shouldnt be too hard, trouble is then u end up with a rather washed out, plain looking game.\n\n\n\nId rather just have the eye candy for a while []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264279, 152642, 1040, 101185, 1072936800, '', 'I get 100 + fps on my own on most maps with little action, around players say 8 with no fire i get 80 - 90, then in battles i can get as low as 30 fps!!.\n\n\n\n3.2 p4 800fsb\n\n1024 duel kingsmax ddr 400\n\nsapphire x800xt\n\n\n\nim not used to droping fps in games, so trying to get a solid 99 fps is a must for me.\n\n\n\nSomething really wierd is, if i use everything on high AA + AF on max and all on high, i get same fps with everything on Low, well there is like 5 fps diffrence between high and low ?\n\n\n\ncan anyone explain this....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264322, 152642, 1040, 101186, 1072936800, '', 'Strangly even if firefights mine never drops below 40 fps \n\n\n\nAthlon 2800+ \n\n512mb Single\n\nRadeon 9800pro Stock\n\nNForce2\n\nDX9\n\n\n\nAnd I looks great!\n\n\n\nAndy', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264422, 152642, 1040, 101187, 1072936800, '', 'you guys are too worried about fps.  This isn\'t the same engine as regular CS.  Getting 99 fps doesn\'t matter towards jack crap right now.  Anything over about 40 constant is good enough to have a smooth feeling game.  Turn off your net_graph or cl_showfps and you won\'t even be able to tell when your fps is 45 or 95.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264480, 152642, 1040, 101188, 1072936800, '', 'with everything on high settings my fps usually stays around 100-120 sometimes dropping to 70 or 80', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264484, 152642, 1040, 101189, 1072936800, '', 'Man human eyes cant tell difference anything above 30 fps, why need 99 fps. Most games comes out this year, you wouldn\'t get 99 fps unless you are a big freak about fps than you turn all things down than you have 99 fps.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264485, 152642, 1040, 101015, 1072936800, '99', 'quote:Originally posted by x6-rbt \n\n\n\n\n\nI don\'t get 99 constant like CS but I\'m working on it, thats my goal anyway.. if I findout the perfect settings I\'ll share.\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nYou realise the human eye is incapable of seeing anything faster than 72 fps, right? Anything above that is a waste of your machine power.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1264513, 152642, 1040, 101190, 1072936800, '', '^ That\'s (30 fps) a myth.  If we couldn\'t tell the difference between 30 fps and 100 fps very few people would complain about having crappy fps.  A good monitor will refresh @ 100 hz.  I\'m also positive that  I can tell the difference between 50, 60, 70, 80, 90 and 100 fps.  Anything below 100 is not perfectly smooth for me because of the high refresh rate -- particularly when my view is changing (such as turning the mouse and turning around ingame).  Otherwise, it looks fairly smooth with 60 fps and a static camera.  FPS games are very different to watching TV or playing strategy games etc.\n\n\n\nAlso, TV / Cinema has motion blur to fool our brain, computer games do not.\n\n\n\n*edit - http://www.100fps.com/how_many_fram..._humans_see.htm (http://www.100fps.com/how_many_frames_can_humans_see.htm)\n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1265302, 152796, 1040, 101191, 1072936800, 'Erm... give me my money back.', 'Excuse me but there is no way im paying �40 for this pile of absolute cr*p. This has to be the worst netcode ive experienced in my entire life of gaming. I get into the game and a nanosecond later it crashes my computer. YES, i know 70% of people are experiencing this, YES i know valve will fix this, YES i know this is flamebait, NO i don\'t give a sh*t.\n\n\n\nGet it fixed NOW, or give me my money back, this sort of stuff gets trading standards involved.\n\n\n\nGet it sorted!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1265316, 152796, 1040, 101192, 1072936800, '', 'What I\'ll do is make them give me $40 for my HL2 voucher that cost me $20 []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1265325, 152796, 1040, 101193, 1072936800, 'Erm... give me my money back.', 'quote:Originally posted by ogradyc1984 \n\n\n\nGet it fixed NOW, or give me my money back, this sort of stuff gets trading standards involved.\n\n\n\nGet it sorted!  \n\n\n\nOooh you gotta laugh when idiots talk about stuff they don\'t understand!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
