(1267083, 152981, 1040, 101205, 1072936800, 'soundstorm 5.1 still broken in final build', 'well ive been submitting bug reports from the first beta, hoping theyd resolve this. nope. broken on final. was this even looked at? was it too low on their list of bugs? is it something thats going to be looked into now that this game is "shipped"? i hope so.\n\n\n\nin case you dont know. soundstorm audio doesnt have front/rear separation in the game. its basicly 2 channel stereo, the front and rear speakers are just cloned.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1267101, 152981, 1040, 101206, 1072936800, '', 'I get that two...but the directional sound still works...ie I can distinguish what is behind and what is in front.\n\n\n\nQuestion is, could this be a DX9c issue?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1274978, 152981, 1040, 101205, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by BIOHaZard \n\nI get that two...but the directional sound still works...ie I can distinguish what is behind and what is in front.\n\n\n\nQuestion is, could this be a DX9c issue?  \n\n\n\nyouve got a good imagination. what you hear in front is exactly the same as what you hear in back. about it being a directx issue, no idea, but it works fine in every other game ive tried..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275008, 152981, 1040, 101207, 1072936800, '', 'try updating your nforce drivers', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275030, 152981, 1040, 100931, 1072936800, '', '5.1 NF2 issues as stated on Beta and on release.\n\n\n\nAnd the surround psuedo effect is just cloning of the front speakers.\n\n\n\nI have a friend who is using drivers that are around the 2.17 version (very old) and he says he is getting surround (well quad) and the sound test picks out his speakers correctly.\n\n\n\nI will not be downgrading my drivers for one game.\n\n\n\nValve please fix this.\n\n\n\nAnd I have the latest drivers installed btw.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275189, 152981, 1040, 101208, 1072936800, '', 'i dont think valve cares, i have been reporting the dell soundblaster bug (scratchy sound) since day one of the beta too, and they have not said one word about it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1287657, 152981, 1040, 100049, 1072936800, '', 'This is a bug in the current nforce driver.\n\n\n\nThe next driver release from Nvidia should address this problem.\n\n\n\nErik', '127.0.0.1', 1),
