(1269742, 153257, 1013, 100511, 1072936800, '', 'As I understand it, cards are restricted to one purchase per game.  This is to prevent fraud.  There is, of course, the slight possibility that a situation such as your\'s will arrive (as it apparently has), but it is acceptably nominal.  The obvious work-around is to use someone else\'s credit card.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1269765, 153257, 1013, 101218, 1072936800, '', 'Well i understand to limit it becuse of fraud, but why limit it to one? Also the wording they use to tell you this makes you think that you can use it more than once before that message should come up.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt says\n\n"This transaction was not prossessed becuse the Cedit Card below has been used too many time in Steam."\n\n\n\nIt should say, Has already been used in steam, within <time frame> (as i am sure you would eventualy be able to use it agian)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1270541, 153257, 1013, 101220, 1072936800, 'Let me see if I have this correct', 'quote:Originally posted by Lunchtimemama \n\nAs I understand it, cards are restricted to one purchase per game.  This is to prevent fraud.  There is, of course, the slight possibility that a situation such as your\'s will arrive (as it apparently has), but it is acceptably nominal.  The obvious work-around is to use someone else\'s credit card.  \n\n\n\n1. Steam requires a CC to buy a game via Steam.\n\n\n\n2. VALVe will not accept cash, a check, or a money order for Steam purchases.\n\n\n\n3. Only one purchase per card per game is allowed.\n\n\n\nAssuming all of the above is correct, I\'d say this poster has a VERY legit complaint. I personally would be royally pi$$ed off if this happened to me- enough so that I would refuse to spend my own money on the game (i.e., beg for it as a gift if I want it badly enough).\n\n\n\nMy bank issued my card to *me*. Who are YOU people to tell me how often I can use it? I think I may have to give a call to the CC vendors your system supports and see if they know about this. After all, they make a percentage of every sale here, too, just by virtue of their cards being used.\n\n\n\nI wonder what Mastercard or Visa would have to say to a vendor that only allows a customer to use the cards they issued once per customer (I already know the answer to that, I just want YOU to think about it for a bit). I bet they\'d have some reservations about renewing their various service contracts with VALVe. If I stressed it enough, I bet they would even make a call or two to the Interested Parties and have a little chat.\n\n\n\n"...use someone else\'s credit card." Beg pardon? Are you *asking* this guy to commit CC fraud, or are you merely asking him to trade on connections with friends or relatiives to get VALVe\'s software? Both really, really suck as a business plan, VALVe people. You should know this.\n\n\n\nI think is a VERY dumb thing to do, for a number of reasons. How would you feel if a grocer did this? A power company? "I\'m sorry, sir, but you are not allowed to use your card to pay the surcharges on your bill, because you already used the card to pay the bill itself. No, sorry, we don\'t take cash, checks, or money orders. I guess you\'re just SOL..."\n\n\n\nWould *you* do business with a company like that?\n\n\n\nHad I known about this policy when I got my ATI card (one with a voucher) I likely would have bought the lower-priced non-HL2 Nvidia card instead, and just waited to get the game off the shelf when it came out.\n\n\n\nTo protect against fraud? Have you never heard the phrase, "never try to bull$hit a bull$hitter"? With all the fraud protections on accounts these days, I very, very strongly doubt this is the real reason. It may be the reason you were given, but I really doubt it\'s the real reason... it\'s just a ridiculous explanation. Even Enron made better excuses than that!\n\n\n\nCome on, VALVe, you can do better than this. And yes, I would consider this one a Steam "dealbreaker" if I didn\'t already have a voucher.\n\n\n\nUntil you drop this policy, VALVe, I think I\'ll err on the side of caution for my friends and tell them to just get it off the shelf and not bother with the Steam-download thing. \n\n\n\nI want to protect *them* against fraud, too. See? That door swings both ways!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1270625, 153257, 1013, 101221, 1072936800, '', 'It came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1270653, 153257, 1013, 101220, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Sitro \n\nIt came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database?  \n\n\n\nI doubt that would matter much to the card issuers if they don\'t already know about this policy. If you *really* don\'t like it, that\'s the way to go. \n\n\n\nThey would be ones who are actually in a position to force a change in VALVe\'s policy regarding this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1270676, 153257, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Sitro \n\nIt came to my attention that; to say your card has been used, you have to store the card info. In registration process, anywhere is it said that it will be saved in Valve\'s database?  \n\n\n\nWe store what is called a "one-way hash" of the number. It can never be used to find out the original number, but we can hash an incoming number and compare the result to the list of hashes in the database. There is an incredibly small possibility (eg, it\'ll never happen) that two card numbers result in the same hash value.\n\n\n\nIncidentally, passwords work the same way. Your Steam password never leaves your computer. A one-way-hash is calculated of it, and that is what is actually sent to our servers and stored in / compared to the database. It\'s a very common technique - Windows domain passwords are the same.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1270696, 153257, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'As far as the original topic goes - we\'re looking into some things that may allow us to loosen the restriction.\n\n\n\nFor now though, we have enough fraud w/ stolen credit cards that we really need the restriction. There are some places in the world right now where such fraud is very common, and every time it happens it costs us money (more than just the purchase price). If it happens too much, it can jeopardize our relationship with the bank. It\'s really lame, in other words. Even something as simple as raising the limit to two purchases per package per card, would not be good: it would basically double the fraud rate.\n\n\n\nBelieve me, it\'s no fun rejecting people\'s attempts to give us money! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1271185, 153257, 1013, 101222, 1072936800, '', 'I trust you in this fact but for example in germany aren\'t many CCs in use. So my father agreed to by the games for my friends with his own card. Is there a way to reactivate the card?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1271191, 153257, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Maddin \n\nI trust you in this fact but for example in germany aren\'t many CCs in use. So my father agreed to by the games for my friends with his own card. Is there a way to reactivate the card?  \n\n\n\nCreate a Support request using the link at the top of the page. You have to view one FAQ before submitting a request, fyi. Then click "ask a question".', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1274970, 153890, 1005, 101223, 1072936800, 'CS:Source - Walling needs to return [and other aspects]', 'I belive that dealing moderate damage to an enemy through a wall and knowing certain spam spots to get an edge on the map was something unique to counter-strike. The ability to \'wall\' someone was nicely implemented into the game. It adds a different aspect to the game, especially in competative lan tournaments. Getting walled is part of the game. It was part of the game to shoot at someone while they were running behind a wall. That is Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\nI dont think that an excuse like, "Oh, it was removed to help protect against cheating" is a good excuse, because that is what VAC is there for. Valve should be working on VAC to the point that where players could have a high trust in it that other players wouldnt be cheating.\n\n\n\nSource has completely removed traditional walling and made shooting thru doors and thin walls nearly useless. I think we need to bring back part of Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\n\n\n[edit]\n\nI was going to add this to a different post in the future, but I decided to do it now after seeing the first reply.\n\n\n\nSome other things that valve needs to think about to increase gameplay. I\'ve always belived that gameplay should come before beauty and realism.\n\n\n\nWhen spraying or at farther ranges it is nearly impossible to see where your bullets are landing, so you cannot efficiently control your spray. These should be visible.\n\n\n\nIt is nearly impossible to tell when you\'ve hit someone in the head. In traditional CS if they werent equipped with a helmet you could see a trail of blood exit the enemies head. In Source it looks more like if a small can of spray paint was heated and it happened to burst. In traditional CS there was always a loud and rewarding sound to a headshot, the \'dink\'.\n\n\n\nIf this game wants to replace Counter-Strike in league play and online play, I think it needs to live up to it\'s ancestors gameplay value.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1274982, 153890, 1005, 101124, 1072936800, '', 'No more dinking too  :/', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1274984, 153890, 1005, 100832, 1072936800, '', 'oh really so i guess an ak bullet should in real life got thru a concrete wall that is about 2 foot thick. stop crying about this plz\n\n\n\nit still does go thru certain things like boxes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1274985, 153890, 1005, 101224, 1072936800, '', '100% Agreed. Gameplay should never be watered down for the sake of hindering cheats, ever.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275000, 153890, 1005, 101225, 1072936800, '', 'you will find that you can still shoot through certain objects, just not 2ft thick walls anymore []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275014, 153890, 1005, 101224, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by sosleapy \n\noh really so i guess an ak bullet should in real life got thru a concrete wall that is about 2 foot thick. stop crying about this plz  \n\n\n\nYou realize how silly you look when you arbitrarily decide what should and shouldn\'t be realistic in a game ultimately created for the sake of fun? Yes, an AK47 bullet isn\'t going to penetrate through a thick concrete wall, but last time I checked it also doesn\'t merely wound someone when they are shot in the chest by it at point-blank range with no body armor.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275022, 153890, 1005, 101226, 1072936800, '', 'OH NOS! Its more realistic!! QUIK!! EVERYONE WHINE!!!!\n\n\n\n\n\nHonestly im glad HE\'s dont hurt you through 2 foot walls anymore and that AK bullets dont penetrate 2 foot thick titanium-alloy reinforced concrete with quarter inch thick steel plating anymore. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275060, 153890, 1005, 101223, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by sosleapy \n\noh really so i guess an ak bullet should in real life got thru a concrete wall that is about 2 foot thick. stop crying about this plz\n\n\n\nit still does go thru certain things like boxes.  \n\n\n\nI\'m sorry that I edited the post. But, as it reads now I stated that I think they should sacrifice realism for gameplay in some cases.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275071, 153890, 1005, 100845, 1072936800, '', 'eww walling! WTF who shoots through walls ? This was suppose to be a tactical game, not a loney toon shoot-out game.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275089, 153890, 1005, 100832, 1072936800, '', 'i am glad they took it out even though i never got killed thru these walls. and yes i agree any gun that shoots someone in the head with one shot should kill them too', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275094, 153890, 1005, 101227, 1072936800, '', 'a certain amount of realism is good, I agree.  However, gameplay of cs should not get watered down because someone doesn\'t think an ak bullet can peirce a 6 inch solid wood door (which it could anyway.)  \n\n\n\nCS has done so well, because the gameplay value of it is phenominal compared to other team based FPS games.  I agree w/ the creator of this post that it should be easier to track your bullets in CS:S so that you can control your spray better.  []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
