(1275111, 153890, 1005, 100845, 1072936800, 'CS:Source - Walling needs to return [and other aspects]', 'quote:Originally posted by at0m \n\nI belive that dealing moderate damage to an enemy through a wall and knowing certain spam spots to get an edge on the map was something unique to counter-strike. The ability to \'wall\' someone was nicely implemented into the game. It adds a different aspect to the game, especially in competative lan tournaments. Getting walled is part of the game. It was part of the game to shoot at someone while they were running behind a wall. That is Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\nI dont think that an excuse like, "Oh, it was removed to help protect against cheating" is a good excuse, because that is what VAC is there for. Valve should be working on VAC to the point that where players could have a high trust in it that other players wouldnt be cheating.\n\n\n\nSource has completely removed traditional walling and made shooting thru doors and thin walls nearly useless. I think we need to bring back part of Counter-Strike.\n\n\n\n\n\n[edit]\n\nI was going to add this to a different post in the future, but I decided to do it now after seeing the first reply.\n\n\n\nSome other things that valve needs to think about to increase gameplay. I\'ve always belived that gameplay should come before beauty and realism.\n\n\n\nWhen spraying or at farther ranges it is nearly impossible to see where your bullets are landing, so you cannot efficiently control your spray. These should be visible.\n\n\n\nIt is nearly impossible to tell when you\'ve hit someone in the head. In traditional CS if they werent equipped with a helmet you could see a trail of blood exit the enemies head. In Source it looks more like if a small can of spray paint was heated and it happened to burst. In traditional CS there was always a loud and rewarding sound to a headshot, the \'dink\'.\n\n\n\nIf this game wants to replace Counter-Strike in league play and online play, I think it needs to live up to it\'s ancestors gameplay value.  \n\n\n\nI think, no i mean i know your wrong, lol. No one likes change around here, but everyone still deals with it anyways.   With cs being ported to source, it just put many more years into counter-strikes life. Whether they add and/or take away something SOME people dont like.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275116, 153890, 1005, 101228, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LittleFo0t \n\neww walling! WTF who shoots through walls ? This was suppose to be a tactical game, not a loney toon shoot-out game.  \n\n\n\nyoure an idiot.\n\n\n\nagree w original post, learning where you can wall is a veteran move...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1275132, 153890, 1005, 101223, 1072936800, 'Re: CS:Source - Walling needs to return [and other aspects]', 'quote:Originally posted by LittleFo0t \n\nI think, no i mean i know your wrong, lol. No one likes change around here, but everyone still deals with it anyways.   With cs being ported to source, it just put many more years into counter-strikes life. Whether they add and/or take away something SOME people dont like.  \n\n\n\nYes, everyone will most likely just adapt and play the game anyways. Except something may change in league play, where this game is trying to become a sport. In an event such as CPL, another game might take the throne because of the lack of gameplay here. I for one don\'t want that to happen, and am offering my advice to valve thru these forums.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
