(1293852, 155776, 1026, 101257, 1072936800, 'Steam keeps downloading old HLDS_RUN insted of SRCDS_RUN', 'And I don\'t know why. I have it update -game "counter-strike source".\n\n\n\nAlso, when I try to update anygames on my linux server with my account that payed for HL2 preorder I get this message:\n\n\n\n"Unknown field in CAccountPaymentCardInfoRecord"\n\n\n\nCan anybody clear this up. Maybe it will only download the srcds_run on the account that payed for HL2 preorder, but I get that error above and it wont update any games, not even the original cstrike. I have also tried from doing a fresh install. Any insight on this would be great. Thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1293884, 155776, 1026, 101258, 1072936800, '', 'Have you tried using a new steam account? Create it using the "./steam" file with the correct parameters (can\'t remember off the top of my head)\n\n\n\nI run 3 servers and have different steam accounts for all of them.\n\n\n\nHTH\n\n\n\nIcon', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1295058, 155776, 1026, 101259, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m getting the same problem with not downloading the srcds_run file.  I\'m following the directions on the top of this forum and from http://server.counter-strike.net/fo...;threadid=33952 (http://server.counter-strike.net/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=33952)\n\n\n\nI have a thread on Counter-Server forums asking for help at http://server.counter-strike.net/fo...;threadid=33999 (http://server.counter-strike.net/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=33999)\n\n\n\nI tried a Windows dedicated server install and I get the srcds.exe fine but no srcds_run in Linux.  Anyone else seeing this?  Everything else seems to be working; I get the CS:S and HL2 files and it says "HLDS installation up to date" when it is done.  I run Fedora Core 2 and the 2.6 kernel.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1295915, 155776, 1026, 101260, 1072936800, '', 'I had the same problem as described above. Be very sure to remove ~/.steam/Clientregistry.Blob\n\n\n\nIt seems to install correctly now I did, can\'t be sure yet, as it\'s not fully installed yet.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1296861, 155776, 1026, 101259, 1072936800, 'I believe I found a solution', 'Follow these steps to get a fresh CS:S dedicated Linux server if you have problems downloading srcds_run:\n\n\n\n# is the linux command prompt and I make comments in ()\n\n\n\n1. Make sure you have no previous .blob files\n\n# find / -name "*.blob"\n\n/root/.steam/ClientRegistry.blob\n\n\n\n(I ran steam as root before so this file is in root\'s home directory)\n\n\n\n/usr/steam/srcds_l/InstallRecord.blob\n\n\n\n2. If you find any, rm them\n\n# rm -rf /root/.steam/ClientRegistry.blob\n\n# rm -rf /usr/steam/srcds_l/InstallRecord.blob\n\n\n\n3. If you ran steam before, let\'s start fresh. Delete the /usr/steam directory\n\n# rm -rf /usr/steam\n\n\n\n4. Then remake it and a srcds_l subdirectory and go there\n\n# mkdir /usr/steam\n\n# mkdir /usr/steam/srcds_l\n\n# cd /usr/steam/srcds_l\n\n\n\n5. Now download the steam linux client from here\n\n# wget http://acm.cs.umn.edu/~cleric/steam.tar.gz (http://acm.cs.umn.edu/~cleric/steam.tar.gz)\n\n\n\n6. Uncompress it\n\n# tar zxvf steam.tar.gz\n\n\n\n7. Make sure it\'s executable\n\n# chmod +x steam\n\n\n\n8. I also made sure that root owned the file\n\n# chown root:root steam\n\n\n\n9. If you have not made a DEDICATED steam account to run this dedicated server you should do that now.\n\n# ./steam -command create -username <uname> -email <real email address> -password <passwd>\n\n\n\n(If you have created this account anytime before, go to the next step)\n\n\n\n10. Now run the command to install CS:S and al the necessary files with it including srcds_run\n\n# ./steam -command update -game "counter-strike source" -dir . -username <uname> -password <passwd> -remember_password\n\n\n\n(make sure to use a uname and passwd that is NOT the one you used to purchase HL2 or the one you use to run your steam client to play. Use the uname and passwd you created just to run the dedicated server)\n\n\n\n(also make sure that there are no hlds* files in this directory. If you started fresh, you should have any)\n\n\n\n11. The download will take some time so go eat something or take a nap or go play CS:S on your client box in the meantime.\n\n\n\n(If everything is working you\'ll see:\n\n\n\nChecking/Installing \'Counter-Strike Source Shared Content\' version 13\n\n...\n\nChecking/Installing \'Linux Source HLDS\' version 11\n\n...\n\nThe above line means you will get the srcds_run file)\n\n\n\n12. Once everthing is downloaded you\'ll get "HLDS installation up to date"\n\n\n\n13. Now you should be able to run the server\n\n# ./srcds_run +ip <your host ip> +maxplayers 16 +map cs_office +log on -autoupdate &', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297022, 155776, 1026, 101260, 1072936800, '', 'Please make a new user to run stuff like this.\n\n\n\nNo need to run the server as root, that\'s just asking for problems.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1334898, 155776, 1026, 101261, 1072936800, '', 'I made exactly what u wrote, but I only get some hlds-files anyway. Steam downloads all the CS:S-files but no srcds_run.\n\n\n\nAnyone has any idea?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(have an SuSE 9.1 Rootserver)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297106, 156086, 1040, 101262, 1072936800, 'Message to Valve', 'I\'d like to aim this directly at VALVe, hoping that when Cliffe, or whoever browses the forum they find it. Please take note of these points and actually implement it into CS:S, as obviously, with all the flame threads you understand that currently there is something wrong with what you\'re doing.\n\n\n\nRecently I really have contemplated you\'re mistakes. The episode of when you released a small crosshair, were given huge negative feedback from the community, so decided to force everyone to use large crosshairs? You have to have an IQ of less than 30 if you thought this would have been an efficient fix. You have replicated this type of so called \'fix\', or \'update\', and your reasoning (i\'d prefer the term "excuse) is pathetic. Hopefully you will see sense.\n\n\n\nTo the point:\n\n\n\nMovement:\n\nFirstly, there is a huge problem with the movement. For anyone that has a clue about FPS games, you should know that movement is a key factor for your play and style, more noticeable in DM games like Quake, but still. \n\n\n\nI don\'t know if the physics engine is the cause of this, but there is a bug where if you\'re next to a wall, crouched and try moving forward it jolts/lags. Whilst jumping, you can no longer bunny hop (without accelerating), like you could in 1.6, to any gamer that incorporates jumping into their style (fisker for one), this is very irritating; being a direct port of 1.6, this is obsolete and should be removed. \n\n\n\nThe removal of \'peeping tom\', or whatever you want to call it - when you tap crouch you get a small jump to see over crates etc - this should be reinstated to CS:S. \n\n\n\nThe last major issue with movement is the lagginess of it. With 1.6 we had smooth, direct response to your input movement, now it seems delayed and, like someone on another thread put: "You\'re skating on an ice-rink".\n\n\n\nWeapon Handling/Behaviour:\n\nNo matter what you say, or whatever graphs you produce, the weapon behaviour is not the same. It feels more like pre 1.3, where you could hold the trigger down and create a constant stream of spray, which is easily contollable. In CS, recoil control was a huge asset of a player\'s skill, this has been taken away and thus depleting the feel of CS.\n\n\n\nShooting through walls, commonly known as \'wall banging\' was a huge element of skill for CS, it really did make this a key part of CS. You have taken out one of the few skilled elements left in CS, its like removing rocket jumping from Quake.. unthinkable.\n\n\n\nThe AWP has been recently debated many times, and was clearly ruined by adding a delay to it\'s zoom. If you return the fast switch of the AWP, you will be returning a very valuable skill to CS.\n\n\n\nGameplay/Misc\n\nThe gameplay has slightly increased in speed, which is about the only good thing you have added, or theoretically, returned, to CS. Obviously you will have to work on making CS:S a skilled game thats suited to competetive, and professional play. You honestly cannot continue to make the game easier, so the younger and less talented public players will stop whining. In the long run, it really is better to make a skilled game, that new players can learn to respect better players, like CS used to be.\n\n\n\nPlease take note, before you totally destroy CS. You have a very good platform to base a potentially excellent next generation game, which those who play on UK2 publics can enjoy, as well as those competing at tournaments for a �30,000 prize.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297136, 156086, 1040, 101181, 1072936800, '', 'That was probably the best post i have ever read on this forum.\n\n\n\nHere\'s to you []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297175, 156086, 1040, 101263, 1072936800, '', 'I like this post! []. Valve please take note!\n\n\n\nCS benifited so much when you listened to Shaguar and implemented an improve money system. To your credit when you released the small crosshair/then big you made it sorted so everyone is happy. \n\n\n\nMy personal opnion is cs is still a good game, although you\'ve started removing some key elements which made it better for competitive players. The awp delay has now made the game less skilled than before, slower as well (people have to be cautious when using the awp). Competitive play has suffered, why? - because you decided to listen to some people that play public all day and got fed up of being \'owned\' by better players with the awp.\n\n\n\nPlease seriously think about the competitive side of cs as well as the public. CS:S could be soo much better with just a few things added like mentioned in this topic.\n\n\n\nMany thanks\n\n\n\nPeter', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297183, 156086, 1040, 101264, 1072936800, '', 'It seems like what you want is cs:s to be just like 1.6.  well , I have a solution for you, PLAY 1.6.  cs:s is what it is source, not 1.6.  Sure it\'s a port but look at the changes from 1.3 -> 1.4 -> 1.5 -> 1.6.  They were all ports but the game still changed, it will change and will continue to change.  If you happen to like the play of 1.6 better than source then more power to ya, play that.  But dont think that valve will change their game for you.  or that the universe revolves around you, sorry.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
