(1297248, 156086, 1040, 101269, 1072936800, 'kmdam', 'OK now I will not drag this out.\n\n\n\n-Try constructive criticism without the antagonizing remarks if you want a positive response from Valve.  Otherwise you are on the right track.\n\n\n\n-The way I see it, if they cater to the likings of the younger less talented genre in order to stop their whining, it will inevitably make folks such as yourself whine.  A \'catch 22\' for Valve?!\n\n \n\n-This is not Quake, stop making comparisons.  Oh and it is different than \'Contra\' too []\n\n\n\n-Bottom line, you have valid points/suggestions, but hey, Valve employs professional gamers to help with the designs so lets be grateful for their continued efforts to better online gaming that did not exist several years ago.  Do you remember the "Attari"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1297252, 156086, 1040, 101263, 1072936800, '', 'lol, i struggled to understand that, and this really isn\'t a thread like most of the others.\n\n\n\n"OMG I GET A BAD SCORE ON PUBLIC"\n\n\n\n"I KEEP DYING AND GETTING KILLED"\n\n\n\n"I\'M NO LONGER GOOD AT CS"\n\n\n\n\n\nI guarantee that the more \'skilled\' players will agree to this rather than the less skilled. Its not about public, its about competitive cs.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1298439, 156209, 1040, 100565, 1072936800, 'List of Commands to Make Counter-Strike: Source Look Even Better!!!!', 'First off, this thread is to list commands that make Counter-Strike: Source look even better, by increasing the looks of it or other simple tweaks.\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n\nIf you want to make use of these commands the easy way then download my generic autoexec.cfg at this link\n\n\n\nmountaincable.net/~jameslin/autoexec.cfg (http://mountaincable.net/~jameslin/autoexec.cfg)\n\n\n\nand place it in the directory stated below.\n\n\n\nIf you\'d rather put the commands directly into your config.cfg then read on.\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n\nThese commands go into your config.cfg, which is found in this directory.\n\n\n\nX:\\Program Files\\Valve\\Steam\\SteamApps\\YOUR_EMAIL@WHATEVER.COM\\counter-strike source\\cstrike\\cfg\n\n\n\nOpen the config.cfg using notepad. When typing the commands in, make sure you type them in below where it says unbindall, which is at the top of the config.cfg Once you put them you will have to save the changes, and it would be a good idea to make the config.cfg a read-only file, so the game doesn\'t change the settings on you. You can make it a read-only file by right clicking on it and hitting proporties, then checking the box that says read-only.\n\n\n\nPlease note that some of these commands may lower your FPS, I personally use the first nine of them and notice no difference in my FPS at all. But the effect is there, obviously more noticeable with the weaker machines.\n\n\n\nNow onto the list of commands!\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #1\n\n\n\nmp_decals "4096" \n\n\n\nThis determines the maximum number of decals visible at one time, 4096 is the max number for this command, it prevents decals just suddenly disappearing, like when to much blood gets on one wall.\n\n\n\nDefault: mp_decals "300"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #2\n\n\n\ncl_ragdoll_collide "1"          \n\n\n\nThis one makes the ragdolls collide with each other, so they don\'t clip inside of each other. Makes body pileups look a lot better.\n\n\n\nDefault: cl_ragdoll_collide "0"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #3\n\n\n\ncl_c4dynamiclight "1"          \n\n\n\nThis one gives the C4 bomb ticking light, dynamic lighting, it makes the light on the C4 look much better.\n\n\n\nDefault: cl_c4dynamiclight "0"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #4\n\n\n\nr_lod "-5"          \n\n\n\nThis one makes it so that the models always look their best from any distance, so when you get closer they don\'t suddenly switch to a different mesh.\n\n\n\nDefault: r_lod "-1"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #5\n\n\n\nr_decal_cullsize "0"          \n\n\n\nThis one makes it so that decals don\'t just appear when you get close, it makes it so you can see them from any distance. For this command you need to put it in your config and you also need to edit the valve.rc file with notepad and change the setting in there too and save it. The valve.rc file is in the same folder.\n\n\n\nDefault: r_decal_cullsize "1"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #6\n\n\n\nr_propsmaxdist "5000"         \n\n\n\nThis command sets the maximum visible distance for props, it prevents props from fading in/out as you get closer/further away from them. I don\'t know if 5000 is the actual max number for this command, the default is 1200, so 5000 just seemed like a good number to choose to me.\n\n\n\nDefault: r_propsmaxdist "1200"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #7\n\n\n\nr_rainradius "2500"\n\n\n\nThis command makes the radius of rain fall around you larger, so you can see the rain from further away.\n\n\n\nDefault: r_rainradius "1500"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #8\n\n\n\nr_rainsplashpercentage "100"\n\n\n\nThis command sets the percentage that the rain makes a splash in the water.\n\n\n\nDefault: r_rainsplashpercentage "20"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #9\n\n\n\njpeg_quality "100"         \n\n\n\nThis command works with the jpeg command, with jpeg_quality set to 100, it makes the screenshots you take 100% quality, so they look really good.\n\n\n\nDefault: jpeg_quality "90"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nCommand #10\n\n\n\nmat_mipmaptextures "0"\n\n\n\nThis command makes textures look their best from any distance. This command makes the game look really grainy, I don\'t use it myself but there are a select few that like this look. This command has quite a big impact on FPS.\n\n\n\nDefault: mat_mipmaptextures "1"\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nTheres the ten commands I know of so far to make CS:S look even better! If you find any that aren\'t already on the list please reply to this topic and add them to the list in a similar way as I have done here.\n\n\n\nEnjoy!! []\n\n\n\n-Opo\n\nmountaincable.net/~jameslin (http://mountaincable.net/~jameslin)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1298450, 156209, 1040, 101270, 1072936800, '', 'Any commands have effect on lag?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1298458, 156209, 1040, 100565, 1072936800, 'Slightly', 'I personally use all five of these commands, I\'m not to sure about how much they affect FPS, but I haven\'t noticed any difference. The only ones that may hurt your FPS is the mp_decals and r_lod commands.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1298534, 156209, 1040, 101271, 1072936800, 'Slightly', 'quote:Originally posted by Opo \n\nI personally use all five of these commands, I\'m not to sure about how much they affect FPS, but I haven\'t noticed any difference. The only ones that may hurt your FPS is the mp_decals and r_lod commands.  \n\n\n\n\n\nDo you really notice a big difference in image quality or do you have view side by side screenshots to really see it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1298572, 156209, 1040, 100565, 1072936800, 'Uhhh', 'The commands change just what my descriptions say.\n\n\n\nThe mp_decals on max makes the game look better because you won\'t be playing and then suddenly see a bunch of bullet holes just dissappear off the wall.\n\n\n\nThe cl_ragdoll_collide is nice because you don\'t see anymore ragdolls clipping through each other.\n\n\n\nThe cl_c4dynamiclight looks good because you can see the ticking light on the C4 bounce off walls and objects around where it is planted.\n\n\n\nThe r_lod command is really nice because, well if you go on de_dust or de_dust2 you know those weird seed baskets things, if you\'re far away from them, you\'ll notice they have a huge black mark at the bottom of them its like a tear in the basket then when you get closer it suddenly disappears into nowhere. This command set to r_lod "-5" prevents such things from happening.\n\n\n\nThe r_decal_cullsize command is nice because it allows you to see decals from any distance. So when you get close to them they don\'t suddenly appear out of nowhere, you can see them from no matter how far away your are if you set this command to 0.\n\n\n\nThe commands in the list so far don\'t affect image quality, they make effects and various things in the game look better. But who knows there might be some commands that improve image quality, just haven\'t found them yet []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
