(1335371, 159172, 1026, 100796, 1072936800, '', '*bump*', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335940, 159172, 1026, 101318, 1072936800, '', 'one thing since I\'ve received a PM about this - DO NOT use the above if someone is cheating. Cheating is a whole different world. You have zero legal recource if someone is cheating. You do not own the software and there isn\'t anything illegal about cheating. Cheating falls within Valve\'s realm. It is up to Valve to do something about cheating. \n\n\n\nbut if someone takes down your server (or in this case service and disconnects the users attached to said service), that is a Denial of Service. DoS can be considered "harrassment" by some states and counties. While you\'ll NEVER get a judgement against someone for the above type of hacking, they can technically be charged with a crime under the National Information Infrastructure Protection Act of 1996. Educate yourself by reading the following: http://www.usdoj.gov/criminal/cyber...rime.html#VIIIa (http://www.usdoj.gov/criminal/cybercrime/compcrime.html#VIIIa)\n\n\n\nAnyways, I\'m hoping someone else is taking the time to shut these kids down. To be honest, it\'s kinda fun in a sick way because you know someone\'s getting in serious trouble on the other end. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336130, 159172, 1026, 101270, 1072936800, '', '*bumpin*\n\nI run a source clan server and lo and behold a member of the clan tried this - with a full server nonetheless. I am tryin to seem impartial because this is going in my forums as well.\n\nSuggestions?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336184, 159172, 1026, 101318, 1072936800, '', 'I\'ve run a CS server in one form or another for 5 years (since 1.0 so however long that is). If someone who has been playing on my server that long pulled this stunt, I wouldn\'t hesitate to notify his ISP. You can say that I\'m passionate about this but this is also my job (cyber-security). If someone who you call a teammate/friend doesn\'t have enough respect of your server (your $$$, your bandwidth, your time) then he doesn\'t deserve you not calling BS on him and reporting him. But that\'s my $.02.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336281, 159172, 1026, 101319, 1072936800, 'New server crash exploit - what you can do', 'quote:Originally posted by MMAzrael \n\nIn a post 9/11 world, this activity is very sensitive and quite illegal. Is it as bad as crashing a bank\'s system or DDoS\'ing Yahoo/Google? No but the legal line between the two is extremely thin.\n\n\n\nEnjoy.  Oh so this is how the police state is going to creep over this country? Incremental doeses that have the support of people like you becasue of minor justifications for unjust laws? Having poeples BROADBAND  \n\n SHUT OFF for using a video game software exploit? Do you even understand what your promoting?\n\n\n\nyea in this post 9/11 world you should be watching out for the looming police state not trying to get revenge on people who crash your server.\n\n\n\n(by the way it would not hold up in court as a DoS "attack" unless you can proove you incurred monetary damage)quote:Originally posted by MMAzrael \n\nI\'ve done this 17 times in the past 36 hours. I\'ve had 12 replies stating that the offenders internet access has been disabled. Most of are kids I\'m sure and they\'ll have to explain to their parents why the cable + internet was turned off. I have also been on the phone w/ 5 of the ISPs. I\'m real proud of you.\n\n\n\nI don\'t use the crash exploit and I don\'t hack but If I ever met you I would knock you the f*ck out.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336374, 159172, 1026, 101320, 1072936800, '', 'VGS, its just the ****ing internet they can live without it and i would rather they didn\'t have it seeing as how they are crashing people off of servers. They most likely also use hacks,cheats, or scripts.  Also if your going to pull a "I have two stars and I have been here longer than you", don\'t even try, i have been around since 2000. I just made a new account for steam. One more thing thing, learn some grammar.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336448, 159172, 1026, 101318, 1072936800, '', 'VGS, I\'m not really understanding where you are coming from. You are saying that it\'s ok for a script kiddie to do something as innoculous as DoSing a game server. What do you think some of these people become? The future for *some*, and I grant you a very small minority, will be doing bigger and worse things (like EBay, ETrade and Yahoo attacks). What about those who DDoS the Steam service? Is that ok because it\'s "just a game"?\n\n\n\nYou don\'t need monetary loss to prove DoS. And I\'m not a fan of conspiracy theories so the whole Ashcroft is a Nazi/Police State thing doesn\'t spur me on. Cybercrime is cybercrime. If you start trying to justify the fact that some is "ok" just because it\'s on a game, you begin to whittle down the entire system.\n\n\n\nAnyways, talking tough over the internet proves how childish you are. I\'m done. Act like an adult and talk rationally and maybe we can discuss this like responsible people.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1336484, 159172, 1026, 101270, 1072936800, 'Re: New server crash exploit - what you can do', 'quote:Originally posted by VGS \n\n\n\nI don\'t use the crash exploit and I don\'t hack but If I ever met you I would knock you the f*ck out.  \n\n\n\nIt does not crash servers - it disconnects clients.\n\n\n\nKeep your flamin in the kiddies section.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
