(1331744, 159185, 1040, 101270, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by trogg \n\nThe bug dosn\'t crash the server, it forces all clients to crash to desktop, the server remains unaffected.\n\nTherefore i find it hard to believe isp\'s are banning accounts over it.\n\nI have reported plenty of users who have attacked my ip, to my knowledge none have been banned, its just not that easy.\n\nServer logs can be forged quite easily.\n\nIn short, dont make this a sticky as its completely pointless.  \n\n\n\n\n\nThe recently discovered exploit that can cause all connected users to crash back to their desktop is nothing short of a Denial of Service. In some cases, this can force you to restart your srcds service. If you live in the United States and the attack originates within the US, this is illegal. Is it a major cybercrime? Obviously not however it\'s against every AUP published by every ISP.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1331748, 159185, 1040, 101322, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by trogg \n\nThe bug dosn\'t crash the server, it forces all clients to crash to desktop, the server remains unaffected.\n\n\n\nTherefore i find it hard to believe isp\'s are banning accounts over it.\n\n\n\nI have reported plenty of users who have attacked my ip, to my knowledge none have been banned, its just not that easy.\n\n\n\nServer logs can be forged quite easily.\n\n\n\nIn short, dont make this a sticky as its completely pointless.  \n\n\n\nAgain nobody will get banned.\n\n\n\nwishful thinkin on a pissed off players part.\n\n\n\npure fantasy\n\n\n\nThis thread is on a par with the one about people using warez gettin fined $10,000, it just aint gonna happen ladies.\n\n\n\nJust so u know, i have retail, and i dont use the crash bug []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1331800, 159185, 1040, 101325, 1072936800, '', 'with the correctly worded email, many things can be done []\n\n\n\nmate of mine managed to shut down the biggest cheat provider for my old mmo by getting on contact with the isp and sorting them out. also managed to shut down a further 30 sites offering cheats for said mmo.\n\n\n\nwouldnt suprise me if this was totaly genuine. would love to see the look on some of the kids faces when teir dad reads out an emial from the isp saying they were cut off for being tossers lol', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1331825, 159185, 1040, 101322, 1072936800, '', 'how would they recieve said email???? :P', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335905, 159542, 1040, 101326, 1072936800, 'Friend\'s ISP terminated his connection.', 'On saturday my friend got fed up at a server he was playing at and decided to be cute and use the crashing method on it,   he did crash it but the admin traced his IP and got ahold of RR.  RR called his dad earlier today to explain the deal, and apparently crashing clients and servers is considered a denial of service attack...... which I think ain\'t right since it doesn\'t cause damage to anyone.  \n\n\n\nThis whole thing could of gotten ugly if the server\'s owner decided to get legal, but he didn\'t (what dumbass would go as far as lawyers for this?).  It\'s pretty stupid how people get worked up over this though.... it restarts a server and crashes people to desktop and they need to call ISP\'s over this........  I\'m not saying crashing is cool or anything, but disconnecting someone\'s line because of this is retarded.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335918, 159542, 1040, 101327, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s the only way people will learn. You wouldn\'t let a criminal go unpunished for any crime would you? I sure hope not. They will reinstate his connection in a little while, and if they don\'t, he can always get a new ISP.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335947, 159542, 1040, 101328, 1072936800, '', 'I wish it was legal for the government to take your friend and hold him for a couple of years untill his dumbass learns not to F other people\'s **** up. Why are people pissed? Maybe you wouldn\'t mind if I came to your house broke your windows and spray painted your car would you? Its not like anyone is going to get hurt! We are pissed because there are a bunch of retards messing up our property (yes servers are property and their services are property). So just tell us where you live and we will show you and your friend why it is no big deal.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335964, 159542, 1040, 101329, 1072936800, '', 'EDIT: I hardly think physical threats (which are 99.9% useless over TCP/IP) are neccessary. Especially since the poster had nothing to do with it. \n\n\n\nIt IS a DoS attack, and the Server Admin did the right thing. Read Road Runner\'s ( I\'m assuming thats the ISP you meant by RR)  Acceptable Use Policy. It\'s against thier rules to use a computer using their service to perform any illegal activity, such as a DoS attack. \n\n\n\nYou\'re right it\'s not funny, cool, cute, or "l337" to crash a server, but since he violated the AUP Road Runner has every right to disconnect him.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1335965, 159542, 1040, 101327, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Deluxe Edition \n\nI wish it was legal for the government to take your friend and hold him for a couple of years untill his dumbass learns not to F other people\'s **** up. Why are people pissed? Maybe you wouldn\'t mind if I came to your house broke your windows and spray painted your car would you? Its not like anyone is going to get hurt! We are pissed because there are a bunch of retards messing up our property (yes servers are property and their services are property). So just tell us where you live and we will show you and your friend why it is no big deal.  \n\n\n\nNo reason to get cranky man, this is how flame wars start. Just explain to him in a kinder manner, i\'m sure he\'ll still get the point! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
