(1338208, 159721, 1005, 101336, 1072936800, 'Things DoD could learn from Rome: Total War?', 'Lately I\'ve been playing lots of RTW and little of DoD. I believe the reason has something to do with the fact that RTW is fun, and DoD feels more and more like work. But I believe that DoD could take some things from RTW and become a good game again. For example, in RTW there is no proning in corners, and there are actual tactical decisions to be make. In addition, in RTW weapons hurt people.\n\n\n\nI believe DoD could become good by adopting some of these ideas.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
