(1342303, 160037, 1040, 101367, 1072936800, '<< Weapon Movement Speed Guide >>', 'Since I was curious about how fast you actually run with each weapon I decided to create a chart detailing the movement speed, both crouched and running, with each weapon.  Many would call this a waste of time, but in the middle of a boring class lecture, nothing is a waste of time []\n\n\n\nSo here it is:\n\n\n\nMovement Speed Graphical Chart (http://www.bakednet.com/images/games/movspeed.JPG)\n\n\n\nUpdate: Added Knife to chart...heh. =)\n\nUpdate: Added zoomed movement speeds for Scout, Aug, Commando, AWP, 552 Sniper, G3/SG-1.\n\nUpdate: Fixed typo with x/y labels.\n\n\n\n\n\nA few points of interest:\n\n\n\n The Scout does help you run faster! You run at about 250 with a  knife, and 260 with a Scout!\n\n All pistols are the same running speed as the knife, you rather then running defenseless with a knife, run with your pistol!\n\n With the FAMAS you\'ll run at the same speed as an AWP, even though it\'s half it\'s weight!\n\n Other guns as slow as the AWP: Galil, FAMAS, G3/SG-1.\n\n You run at *almost* the same speed with a Para then you do with an Aug!\n\n The only SMG which makes you run slower then the knife is the P90.\n\n You can run faster with the automatic shotgun then with the pump-action version.\n\n\n\nNew points since update:\n\n\n\n The G3/SG-1 and Aug have NO movement penalty when zoomed in!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNote: No equipment (armor, grenades) affect running speed.\n\n\n\nThanks for your interest!\n\n\n\nEDIT: Sorry, I should have meantioned how I got this.  If you type cl_showanimstate 1 in console it\'ll show your movement speed, amongst other things.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
