(1342554, 160037, 1040, 100253, 1072936800, '<< Weapon Movement Speed Guide >>', 'quote:Originally posted by BakedGoods \n\nSince I was curious about how fast you actually run with each weapon I decided to create a chart detailing the movement speed, both crouched and running, with each weapon.  Many would call this a waste of time, but in the middle of a boring class lecture, nothing is a waste of time []\n\n\n\nSo here it is:\n\n\n\nMovement Speed Graphical Chart (http://www.bakednet.com/images/games/movspeed.JPG)\n\n\n\n\n\nA few points of interest:\n\n\n\n The Scout does help you run faster! You run at about 250 with a  knife, and 260 with a Scout!\n\n All pistols are the same running speed as the knife, you rather then running defenseless with a knife, run with your pistol!\n\n With the FAMAS you\'ll run at the same speed as an AWP, even though it\'s half it\'s weight!\n\n Other guns as slow as the AWP: Galil, FAMAS, G3/SG-1.\n\n You run at *almost* the same speed with a Para then you do with an Aug!\n\n The only SMG which makes you run slower then the knife is the P90.\n\n You can run faster with the automatic shotgun then with the pump-action version.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNote: No equipment (armor, grenades) affect running speed.\n\n\n\nThanks for your interest!  Thanks a bundle!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1342583, 160037, 1040, 101367, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by SpYd3r \n\nWhere\'s the knife?\n\nWhat are the units?\n\nAnd how did you calculate it?\n\n\n\n\n\nApart from that... well done.  \n\n\n\n- Added the knife, sorry =S\n\n- Not sure, using the cl_showanimstate 1 command it\'ll give you a number for your velocity, 0-260.\n\n- ^^^ check above\n\n\n\nThanks for the acknowledgment guys!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1342584, 160037, 1040, 101372, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by ~LiquidMetal~ \n\nyea how shuld i know if it trow if the scout if faster then the nife..\n\n\n\nYea i can crate a game and test(dumass)  \n\n\n\nRofl []\n\nWhat drugs did he take ? \n\nIn comparison to him is my english much better []\n\n\n\n\n\nBut nice work BakedGoods !\n\nHow did you calculate it ? [Thx found the answer above this msg]\n\n\n\n-edit-', '127.0.0.1', 1),
