(1443179, 168451, 1013, 101450, 1072936800, 'Concern over keyGen', 'Im going to assume the same thing that happened with CS:S will happen with HL2, my question is that  if someone uses a keygen or a hacked copy of HL2 and it uses my cd key or it takes my steam ID, is there a way I can prove my purchase of this game to get my account reset. I payed enough money that I would hate to lose it all and Im hearing plently of stories of people who have lost their accounts and are not getting any replies. I love valve and steam but if this situation does not get cleaned up then steam has 0 advantage over any other software.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443186, 168451, 1013, 100511, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s bound to your email address, is it not?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443208, 168451, 1013, 101450, 1072936800, '', 'thats true but if someone gains access to your account it can be easily changed. And if you cant login cause someone else is using your account how can you reset it?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443233, 168451, 1013, 101451, 1072936800, '', 'contact valve and they should be able to sort it out for you\n\n\n\nthe easiest way i knw of doing this right now is to PM taylor Sherman or to e-mail him but do not abuse this or he might not answer anything anymore\n\n\n\nSherman you rock', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443273, 168451, 1013, 101452, 1072936800, '', 'No one can steal your STEAMID, its a myth (unless ofcourse they steal your account). The pirated version must be bound to an account which has its own STEAMID, its not randomly generated.\n\n\n\nSome people will get the "SteamID in use" error in certain servers because they are cracked servers, just ignore those servers as they usually suck anyway.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443300, 168451, 1013, 101340, 1072936800, '', 'its your own fault if someone gets ahold of your password whether it be from you telling them or a key logger or some other way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443444, 168451, 1013, 101453, 1072936800, '', 'In the near future you will be able to make a CD Backup of your games.\n\n\n\nKeyGens as a rule don\'t work and we have never had an instance of a KeyGen\'d CD-Key getting registered on a Steam account. \n\n\n\nMost often people lose accounts because they don\'t use strong passwords. Having your Account name and password the same is one of the most common ways to get your account stolen by another user...so don\'t do it.\n\n\n\nAlso keep in mind that you shouldn\'t share your login information / e-mail account password / or *ANY* other account information with anyone...including (especially) your brother / sister / kids / mates / buddies / pals / pets / etc. If you use Steam at a cafe or friends\' house make sure you log out completely.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443599, 168451, 1013, 101454, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by DougV \n\nIn the near future you will be able to make a CD Backup of your games.Is this feature being added directly into Steam to back up the files?\n\n\n\nquote:KeyGens as a rule don\'t work and we have never had an instance of a KeyGen\'d CD-Key getting registered on a Steam account. Unfortunately, there have been a few occasions where I used to play (when the old WON system was in place) and it said my key was already in use.  Now if that person had my key (which they must have got from a keygen) - there is nothing stopping them registering that key with that account on Steam [exception being that I got registered first]  -  The same could be said for HL2 keys.  How can you be sure that a year down the line someone who buys HL2 legit in the shop cant get online because someone keygenned the key thats been in a sealed box for a year?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443670, 168451, 1013, 101453, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Spooky \n\nIs this feature being added directly into Steam to back up the files?\n\n\n\n>Yes\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, there have been a few occasions where I used to play (when the old WON system was in place) and it said my key was already in use.  Now if that person had my key (which they must have got from a keygen) - there is nothing stopping them registering that key with that account on Steam [exception being that I got registered first]  -  The same could be said for HL2 keys.  How can you be sure that a year down the line someone who buys HL2 legit in the shop cant get online because someone keygenned the key thats been in a sealed box for a year?  \n\n\n\n> We have not had that happen in Steam with someone using a KeyGen. More likely someone has opened the box in the store and taken a picture of the CD-Key and used that to register in Steam. As a rule, whoever has the physical CD-Key from a retail box is the owner of the key. We will disable any account containing a duplicate key. You can\'t imagine the stories that people come up with. Also, never purchase an account from someone on EBay or IRC...chances are they have obtained the account through less than honest means and there is a great liklihood that account will be disabled and you will be out your purchase price.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443698, 168451, 1013, 101454, 1072936800, '', 'Cool, thats good to know anyway.  Its a bit of an inconvenience for anyone unlucky to get a key in use already though, but I suppose there isn\'t much people can do with that.\n\n\n\nOn the backup idea, would that also include DVD backup?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443748, 168451, 1013, 101455, 1072936800, '', 'When you make a backup of your game, do you still have to have steam in order to play HL2? Do you need steam to re-install HL2 from the backups?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443750, 168451, 1013, 101453, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Spooky \n\nCool, thats good to know anyway.  Its a bit of an inconvenience for anyone unlucky to get a key in use already though, but I suppose there isn\'t much people can do with that.\n\n\n\nYes...people suck when they steal...\n\n\n\nOn the backup idea, would that also include DVD backup?  \n\n\n\nNot sure...I\'ll try to find out and post if I do.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443758, 168451, 1013, 101456, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Inu \n\nWhen you make a backup of your game, do you still have to have steam in order to play HL2? Do you need steam to re-install HL2 from the backups?  At the moment yes.  Probably will never change unless VALVe abondons Steam.\n\n\n\nNice to see a VALVe guy here Doug!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443816, 168451, 1013, 101453, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Inu \n\nWhen you make a backup of your game, do you still have to have steam in order to play HL2? Do you need steam to re-install HL2 from the backups?  \n\n\n\nYes. Steam is a requirement...even to play in "offline" Mode.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1443836, 168451, 1013, 101455, 1072936800, '', 'So this going to be a built in option like in the steam ui I click make backups then it starts burning off cd\'s. Then when I put back in the CD I go to steam and I click install from backup?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
