(1532026, 176237, 1040, 101598, 1072936800, 'Audio Stuttering', 'There is bound to be more threads on this as its becoming apparent a lot of people are experiencing this issue in HL2. I suggest making a sticky on it.\n\n\n\nBasically, whenever the game loads sounds on the fly, the game takes a performance hit, stuttering the sound and causing the game to judder.\n\n\n\nI and others have tried numerous solutions to fix it and so far, nothing as worked sucessfully. I have even ran the game in a window with an MP3 running over the top. The game stuttered, the MP3 did not suggesting this isn\'t a soundcard issue.\n\n\n\nPlease post here if you have this problem so it can be highlighted as its ruining a bloody fine game.\n\n\n\nI have contacted Valve via their support system but lets make them aware of it here too....and keep it clean. We want the problem sorted, not blown up.\n\n\n\nCheers\n\nSie', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532054, 176237, 1040, 101275, 1072936800, '', 'I have the exact same problem []  Thought my system was bad ©©© enough to run it, but it still stuTters with the audio issues.\n\n\n\nSpecs;\n\n\n\nAthlon64 3500+\n\nMSI K8n Neo2\n\n1gb memory\n\nATI X800Pro\n\nAudigy XGamer\n\nWD 10,000rpm HD\n\n\n\nThis should be a fast enough rig to run the game at these settings ?\n\n\n\n1280res 4xAA/8xAF, all details Highest', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532062, 176237, 1040, 101557, 1072936800, '', 'Its not the sound I understand from other forums that the problem is actually the AUTOSAVE... Im awaiting a post on how to disable Autosave and hopefully that cures it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532065, 176237, 1040, 101599, 1072936800, '', 'P4 3.02\n\n1 gig DDR\n\nGigaByte mobo\n\ngeforce FX 5900 Ultra\n\nAudigy 2 ZS Gamer\n\n\n\nI had the same problem with it stuttering with sounds and such. All I did was go into options and set the "sound quality" from "high" to a lower setting and it went away. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532067, 176237, 1040, 101600, 1072936800, 'Me too...', 'I\'ve been experienciing this  too, and the reason I\'m in the forum now is the game actually crashed during one of those stuttering episodes, I was on the beach, having just been given a rocket launcher by an english major, the flyer attacked, the stuttering started, the game crashed.\n\n\n\nMind you, its the first time its crashed all day and I\'ve been playing it solid since 8.55 am this morning !\n\n\n\nSo, why\'s the game stuttering? I\'m sure a patch will mend it.......', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532078, 176237, 1040, 101495, 1072936800, '', 'same issue, it\'s annoying but not game stopping by any means. does it now and again.\n\n\n\nspecs:\n\n\n\nAthlon XP3000+\n\nRadeon X800 Pro\n\n1 GB Corsair Ram\n\nAudigy 2 ZS', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532100, 176237, 1040, 101557, 1072936800, '', 'Hmm if you set sound to medium you give the game less to "load" but doesn\'t the medium sound quality suck? Or is it barely noticeable (maybe it just cuts the number of simultaneous audio sounds allowed?)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532101, 176237, 1040, 101598, 1072936800, '', 'On the contrary, it does appear to be triggered by sound. Maybe its both Sound and Autosave but my money is on sound.\n\n\n\nFor instance, the stuttering does not coincide with the autosaves appearing in the load menu.\n\n\n\nAdditionally, stuttering occurs in G-Man\'s speech at the beginning of the game when no autosaving is occuring.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532105, 176237, 1040, 101601, 1072936800, 'Darn', 'Same here. \n\n\n\nHad the same issue with Doom 3 when opening doors, some tweaks in the console and cache optimization eventually got it all sorted, so lets hope to get some fast results here.\n\n\n\n\n\nAthlon XP 2500+ @2.2\n\n512 Crucial DDR333 in Dual Channel\n\nTurtle Beach Santa Cruz\n\nEVGA 6800\n\nMaxtor 80gb  (OS/Storage)\n\nMaxtor 160gb  (Games/Partition for Steam/Storage)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532129, 176237, 1040, 101598, 1072936800, '', 'A lot of people seem to think this is specifically an Audigy2 Sound Crad problem. With this in mind I also ran the game through my M-Audio Audiophile 2496 Soundcard.\n\n\n\nThe problem was still there.\n\n\n\nThe problem does seem to go away somewhat when reducing various game performance settings but its still there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532144, 176237, 1040, 101602, 1072936800, '', 'I think its an Audigy 2 DRIVER problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532161, 176237, 1040, 101603, 1072936800, '', 'While I haven\'t had any sound issues in Half Life 2 to speak of yet, I have horrid sound issures in Counter Strike Source.  Are these games related closely enough to where it\'s the same problem?\n\n\n\nPentium 4 3.4 Northwood\n\n2 Gigabytes DDR3200 Corsair XMS Memory\n\nIntel 875 Motherboard\n\nSapphire X800Pro\n\nAudigy LS Sound Card\n\nAntec True Power True 550', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532163, 176237, 1040, 101604, 1072936800, '', 'Same thing happens to me, and it is ruining the game as it is very frequent. Since the release is new I don\'t expect a fast answer/solution, but some kind of acknowledgement would be fine.\n\n\n\nI don\'t have an audigy, I am using my Nforce2 onboard sound device.\n\n\n\nWhat I have tried:\n\nAll sound quality settings - same result.\n\nDirectSound Hardware acceleration on and off(and in-between) - same result.\n\nReinstalling drivers - same result.\n\n\n\nAny other ideas??', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532165, 176237, 1040, 101598, 1072936800, '', 'Indeed they are tjr1973. I also have this problem in CS: Source.\n\n\n\nI\'m about to remove my Audigy2 from my pc to completely eliminate that possiblity that its related to that card and/or its drivers.\n\n\n\nSome people have even said they got this problem when they updated their Ati drivers but its obviously not that as people here are running on Nvidia cards too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1532167, 176237, 1040, 101605, 1072936800, 'Same', 'same problem.\n\n\n\nathlon xp 1900\n\naudigy gamer\n\nradeon 9600 pro\n\n1 gig o ram', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533571, 176640, 1040, 101606, 1072936800, 'BAD ERROR! NEED TO FIX IT! Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit', '"Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit"\n\n\n\nI get that error when I try to start Half-Life 2 under "My Games" in steam. I bought the game for over 30 hours ago and I\'ve tried to fix this problem ever since (well I slept a little too). I\'ve tried all tips and tricks, workarounds etc etc.\n\n\n\nSomeone says it\'s my DVD-drive. I doubt, then it\'s 20 more DVD-drives out there wrong. Because that\'s the amount of people I have spoken to who also encountered this problem. Imagin all other people with this problem world wide -- I can\'t even think about it. This is really really bad.\n\n\n\nAnd for you who wonders:\n\n\n\nYes, I have installed Steam, Half-Life 2, entered my CD-key, authenticated with Steam, downloaded all updates etc etc. Steam even said to me this morning that everything was okey and I was ready to play the game. But ACK, NO. I still get "Unable to authenticate orginal disc within time limit".\n\n\n\nWhy the HECK must Steam use my CD when I\'ve installed the game and even get a green light from Steam servers? This is really bad.\n\n\n\nAnd to extra clear. I\'ve updated my list firmware (hardware) and software for my DVD-drive/burner (which is a Plextor one I bought yesterday, JUST (I repeate, JUST) to install, play and ENJOY Half-Life 2.\n\n\n\nAny fixes for this? Will fixes be released? If it is, when? As I wrote, I\'m not the only one with this problem.\n\n\n\nWhen I buy a game, I would AT LEAST expect to play it whenever I want.\n\n\n\nAnd finally, just to say my opinion. Valve, you\'ve sunk deep in my thoughts about you as game developers.  You don\'t have my respect anymore, I\'m sorry....\n\n\n\nThanks,\n\n\n\nAll help appreciated.\n\n\n\nCheers to all other people having problem, I feel your anger.\n\n\n\nUnclePunk', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533625, 176640, 1040, 101606, 1072936800, '', 'Forgot to say I have the european version.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533736, 176640, 1040, 101606, 1072936800, '', 'No one knows how to fix? I want Valve og moderators to help me out.. or at least come with some commentaries', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533749, 176640, 1040, 101607, 1072936800, '', 'the following thread describes not 100% your problem, but goes a little bit the same way:\n\n\n\n/forums/show...threadid=176562 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=176562)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533798, 176640, 1040, 101608, 1072936800, 'Same Here', 'Ive got exactly the same problem. I bought retail version in Uk, and heave done everything as far as I9 can see to install correctly, then get the same error message. I rang the help line and they said to get the lastest firmwars for my dvd drive, which I did with no effect. Then they said I should flash my motherboard, which I certainly did not do. I\'m stuck now!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533814, 176640, 1040, 101609, 1072936800, '', 'Hi,\n\n\n\nJust out of interest how many drives do you have in your PC which are capable of reading a DVD?\n\n\n\nThe reason I ask is that I have both a DVD-ROM and DVD+RW drive.  For some weird reason I found that although I installed the game on my DVD-ROM (F[] when it came to play it I was getting the same error you are.\n\n\n\nThe way I fixed it was quite simple - I stuck the DVD in the DVD+RW Drive (G[] instead.  I guess it enumerates the devices and just uses the last one - I don\'t think this is Valves fault though - I think it\'s something to do with the SecuROM copy protection.\n\n\n\nCheers\n\n\n\nPete', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1533832, 176640, 1040, 101606, 1072936800, '', 'I only have on DVD-drive in my computer (or disc readers in general), which I bought yesterday to be able to play Half-Life 2.\n\n\n\nOf course it\'s Valves fault it doesn\'t work. They\'re the ones that made Steam check for disc when playing. Even when auth with Steam server and CD-key check is okay.\n\n\n\nI just don\'t like this.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1550237, 176640, 1040, 101610, 1072936800, '', 'I have the same error [] . ppl say that the it depens on your dvd-drive. Old versions work fine, new one doesn\'t (not sure). Well I hope they fix it []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1555589, 176640, 1040, 101611, 1072936800, 'Badly thought out', 'I get this same issue, but it isn\'t DVD -ROM related.  If I retry and retry again and again, eventually it works.\n\n\n\nMy DVD is clean and working etc etc.\n\n\n\nI\'ve raised it with Steam but, obviously, they haven\'t been bothered to actually respond - good grief no!  Support a pi55ed off customer, not their style....\n\n\n\nWhen I get a response I will post it here - absolute promise!!  If you don\'t see it posted then you know why!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1558241, 176640, 1040, 101606, 1072936800, 'Solutions', 'I suggest you try this forum thread. There\'s a lot of help there..\n\nMaybe you\'ll find your solution there too.. I do. But I hope it\'s only temporary, untill Valve (maybe?) release a NO CD patch.\n\n\n\nGood luck!\n\n\n\nHERE: http://www.forumplanet.com/planetha...amp;tid=1529738 (http://www.forumplanet.com/planethalflife/topic.asp?fid=6549&tid=1529738)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1563561, 176640, 1040, 101611, 1072936800, 'Wierd', 'Right, anyone suffering from this problem, I\'ve found a solution that worked for me.....  NO THANKS TO STEAM WHO STILL HAVEN\'T RESPONDED....\n\n\n\nTry opening the DVD drive, then close it, then wait for the DVD to speed up, then click on \'halflife2\'.\n\n\n\nWorks for me - hell knows why......', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1563855, 176640, 1040, 101612, 1072936800, '', 'Hey that worked for me aswell! im so happy lol, i put the cd in then when i heard it spinning really fast i hit the hl2 icon in the desktop then 1-2min later i was playing [] maybe this will work with other ppl...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1578810, 176640, 1040, 101611, 1072936800, 'Hmmmm', 'Apparently not 100% efficient!  \n\n\n\nTook several goes and a reboot to get it started today.\n\n\n\nI\'m not a pirate but Steam are forcing me to start searching the hacker pages looking for a NOCD patch....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1635083, 176640, 1040, 101611, 1072936800, 'You\'re all quiet over there...', 'Still no reply from Steam......\n\n\n\nNice of them to care so much about their customers.....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1635103, 176640, 1040, 101612, 1072936800, '', 'you can download a no cd patch now.(not from steam or valve)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534464, 176796, 1040, 101613, 1072936800, 'Nausia while playing...', 'Anyone else becoming nautious while playing?  This limits my gaming time to an hour at most because I have to rest afterward.  I\'ve played UT/2003/2004 and HL1, Quake III, and many other FPS games and have never become sick while playing.  Do I need to see a doctor or is this game just too immersive for me?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534483, 176796, 1040, 101141, 1072936800, '', 'It is the level of detail. It is the exact opposite of motion sickness, your brain thinks you are moving but your body doesn\'t.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534560, 176796, 1040, 101614, 1072936800, 'Nauseous', 'Glad Im not the only one, yesterday I almost threw-up, thought it was the pepsi on an empty stomache....\n\n\n\nI am impressed and sickened (literally) by the level of detail, now we just need a roller coaster mod, and we can all vomit in the safety of our own homes.\n\n\n\n\n\nAwesome job valve!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534563, 176796, 1040, 101615, 1072936800, '', 'Ever read the game warnings?  They talk about that exact thing-and prescribe limiting yourself to about an hour.\n\n\n\nOr was that 4 hours when it comes to HL2? Oh, well, I\'ll just go with that. []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534571, 176796, 1040, 100228, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by tachyon99 \n\n\n\n\n\nOr was that 4 hours when it comes to HL2? Oh, well, I\'ll just go with that. []  \n\n\n\nlol,\n\n\n\nI experienced something but I just ignored it and well into my 3rd hour I guess it went away.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534622, 176796, 1040, 101616, 1072936800, '', 'In Iceland, we play for many hours! About 10 hours or more! We dont have anything else to do because there is so much snow and volcanos so we are afraid of our snowhouses melting. So we are living in the school!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534637, 176796, 1040, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'It seems the refresh rate is locked at 60Hz for HL2 and this is causing some problems like headaches and things.\n\n\n\nDownload ReForce and use it so it overrides the 60Hz.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534642, 176796, 1040, 101617, 1072936800, '', 'Is this nausia thing limited to CRT:s and does it go away if you play on a TFT , LCD wich is more smoothier (less sharper)? Thinking of bying a TFT and need arguments.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534650, 176796, 1040, 101618, 1072936800, '', 'Are you serious?\n\n\n\nI have the exact same problem! After an hour or so I just can�t continue playing...\n\n\n\nNothing we can do about that? (Turn down resolution, refresh rate or something??)\n\n\n\nI know there�s a general warning to almost all new games..but I always thought that would only concern ppl with epilepsy or smth. I want to be able to play longer than that without...well...throwing up.. []\n\n\n\nGreetings, Ceeves\n\n\n\nEdit 1:\n\n@Cpt. Kirk: Dunno, yesterday I played on that huge Plasma display (42 Inches) up at my grandparents place... Took a bit longer (probably because I did not sit right in front of it like I do with my CRT monitor) but eventually I got nausea from that too... []\n\n\n\n@ Smash: I did that, let Refreshlock auto-detect my monitor refresh rates and resolutions (1024x768 at 85Hz) and still get the same bad effect.. []\n\n\n\nEdit 2:\n\nHad to correct myself: I did not use Refreshlock, instead I used RefreshForce which is said to be a permanent solution..?!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534660, 176796, 1040, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Ceeves \n\nNothing we can do about that? (Turn down resolution, refresh rate or something??) \n\n\n\nPlease read my post...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534661, 176796, 1040, 101619, 1072936800, 'OpenGL vs DirectX Sickness', 'So I to get sick from playing HL2.  However, I have noticed something else I was hoping someone could confirm.\n\n\n\nI played Doom3 with full detail at 1600x1200 and I didn\'t get sick at all.\n\n\n\nIn fact it seems I only get sick playing DirectX games.  I have the same issue with Unreal.\n\n\n\nAm I making a missguided association?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534666, 176796, 1040, 100307, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by smash \n\nIt seems the refresh rate is locked at 60Hz for HL2 and this is causing some problems like headaches and things.\n\n\n\nDownload ReForce and use it so it overrides the 60Hz.  \n\n\n\nPlease consider.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534677, 176796, 1040, 101620, 1072936800, '', 'I get Nauseous when I can\'t play for a while []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534695, 176796, 1040, 101621, 1072936800, '', 'I got nauseous installing the damn thing []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1534701, 176796, 1040, 101622, 1072936800, '', 'Headaches are the only problem im getting with hl2. I love the game and the graphics look amazing on my 6800, but these dam headaches after only 3-4 hours of playing are annoying. I have played in 12 hour, 5 min piss break dod tournaments and havent experienced headaches like this.\n\n\n\nTurning on the V-sync option helps a little btw', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1535912, 177123, 1005, 101623, 1072936800, 'can i play source without extra payment if i buy hl2 in a shop?', 'I\'ve ordered halflife 2 from play.com, however i want to know whether i can play cs:source without paying anymore. I assume the shop version is just like the online bronze version but i\'m not sure. Also will there be an option to like pay 10 dollars extra or something to allow you to get other mods like halflife source.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1536848, 177123, 1005, 101624, 1072936800, '', 'The store version from ANYWHERE is the Bronze version of HL2 you can then upgrade to a silver or gold if you want through steam. The bronze version does allow you to play source.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537465, 177123, 1005, 100228, 1072936800, '', 'Collectors Edition comes with the mods HL:S CS:S', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1536064, 177159, 1013, 100045, 1072936800, 'Motion Sick?', 'A few tips I\'ve gotten to reduce motion sickness:\n\n\n\n* do what you can to increase framerate/reduce framerate fluctuation (reduce screen res, sound and video quality settings)\n\n* setting fps_max to something reasonable may help\n\n* activating mat_vsync may help\n\n* switching from FOV 75 (default) to FOV 90 may help\n\n\n\nOther tips I\'ve received:\n\n\n\n* while in vehicles, run into less things\n\n* throw up... you\'ll feel better for a while\n\n\n\n[]\n\n\n\n\n\nEdited by MATT. Also try this:\n\n\n\n(Read more at HalfLife2.net (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?t=51945).)\n\n\n\n1) Update your monitor\'s drivers.\n\n\n\n2) Find out the Maximum Refresh Rate that your monitor supports for the resolution that you prefer gaming on (lowering resolution will result in higher possible refresh rates). This step is just for informational purposes. You may skip it since Step 4 completes this.\n\n\n\n3) Download RefreshForce (Google it).\n\n\n\n4) Tell it to "Auto Find" your refresh rates and modes. Click Apply.\n\n\n\n5) Go to Steam --> Right click Half-Life 2 --> select Properties --> Launch Options.\n\n\n\nNow you can specify the width, height and refresh rate of the screen on which you will be playing. Mine, for example is this: -w 1024 -h 768 -refresh 100\n\n\n\nThis means I am running a resolution of 1024x768 at a refresh rate of 100hz.\n\n\n\n6) Click OK and close the Properties window.\n\n\n\n7) It\'s best to restart your computer now, since you applied that RefreshForce fix.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1536296, 177159, 1013, 101625, 1072936800, '', '-Sit back from the monitor. Just getting a little more perspective of your desk will help keep you from getting sick.\n\n\n\n-Turn on the lights. Staring at a monitor for hours with the lights off is going to ruin your vision and give you headaches.\n\n\n\n-Take a break every hour. Use the bathroom, grab a snack, basically just kill 15 minutes before you start playing again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1536436, 177159, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'Also during your break dont go and watch TV. Give your eyes a break. Ive already read some places that people have busted a blood vessel in thier eye because they played for 10-12 hours straight.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537237, 177159, 1013, 101626, 1072936800, 'Eyes vs Ears', 'Motion sickness is caused when there is a difference between what your inner ear is telling your brain and what your eyes see.\n\n\n\nIf you\'re in a car that\'s moving but you are reading or looking at something inside the car, your ears will perceive motion but your eyes do not.  This causes car sickness.\n\n\n\nLikewise if you\'re playing a computer game, your eyes perceive motion but your inner ears says your standing still.\n\nI think the problem may be more pronounced in Half Life 2 since it is so immersive.\n\n\n\nIf you watch gamers who play alot you may notice them moving their head around and shifting their bodies from side to side while playing.  I do this alot and my wife makes fun of me for it but I think that\'s why I don\'t get motion sick while playing.\n\n\n\nThe best solution though is to sit a little farther away from your monitor.  Just push the screen further back on your desk so that less of your field of view is taken up by the screen.  Just a little bit can help alot.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537265, 177159, 1013, 101627, 1072936800, '', 'LOL...I wish I could get good enough frome rates to get motion sick!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537367, 177159, 1013, 101628, 1072936800, '', 'I find it amazing that the game\'s graphics are so good that it\'s actually giving people motion sickness! I mean, wow...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537399, 177159, 1013, 101629, 1072936800, '', 'I got motion sick from a game once, took ages to clean out my keyboard!!!!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537679, 177159, 1013, 101630, 1072936800, '', 'motion sickness from a game...cant say that has ever happend to me. *points* weak!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537760, 177159, 1013, 101629, 1072936800, '', 'Ha, You didn\'t see what i had eaten before I got ill. Belive me it didn\'t look much different second time round.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537822, 177159, 1013, 101631, 1072936800, '', 'Great.  HL (the first) was one of the handful of games that made me violently ill with motion sickness.\n\n\n\nI can only hope that HL2 does NOT do this.  If it does I will not be able to play it.  [] [] []\n\n\n\nGuess I will find out tomorrow....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537928, 177159, 1013, 101580, 1072936800, '', 'edit', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538487, 177159, 1013, 101632, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m guessing its because I also sway when playing games\n\n\n\nStill... I get around 60fps at 1024x768 @ 120Hz\n\n\n\n...Maybe its because I\'m desensitised to it all (try playing Doom95 on "turbo" mode [] )\n\n\n\nTo me, its kinda laughable that someone might get sick from playing a game... Am I right in assuming this afflication only affects so-called "casual gamers", I\'m surprised if it does, don\'t they spend all their time playing games like GTA, Driv3r, Need for Speed, and Madden?\n\n\n\nSurely those games would induce motion sickness more easily?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538542, 177159, 1013, 101633, 1072936800, '', 'No, this does not only happen with casual gamers. I have played just about every major game for the last 7 years and Half-Life 2 is the only one that has ever caused me to feel motion sickness.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538660, 177159, 1013, 101634, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s odd that this topic came up, I actually started to feel dizzy for a while and didn\'t know if it was just me or an illusion... crazy!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538913, 177159, 1013, 101635, 1072936800, '', 'Definately weird...  I unlocked the game last night and only played for about 10 minutes before I thought I was gonna puke.  Been gaming FPSs for years... Wolf3d, doom, HL1, CS, etc...  all the same settings and never had any problems.  We\'ll see if it happens again this afternoon when I\'m home from work.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1537990, 177550, 1040, 101636, 1072936800, 'sick while playing HL2', 'Who here gets sick while playing HL2? \n\n\n\nI\'ve had this problem with HL1 where I felt nauseated and had cold sweat. The same problem also happens while playing HL2 for about 20-30 minutes then I have to stop and lay down before I throw up.\n\n\n\nNever had this experience while playing other fps games such as Halo 1/halo 2 and all the other half-life/half-life 2 mods such as, CS:S, CS 1.6, DOD, Ricochet.\n\n\n\n\n\nhmmm what gives?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538002, 177550, 1040, 100931, 1072936800, '', 'Seek medical advice.\n\n\n\nSounds like your screen refresh could be too low or you suffer from car sickness / motion sickness.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538006, 177550, 1040, 101450, 1072936800, '', 'I dont have a problem, Although I do wonder what causes it for some people cause there are a lot reporting it. I find it kinda funny but I see how  its annoying too. Maybe the graphics are too real? or monitor is too close. i dont know.\n\n\n\nCould be worse, you could have really gotten sick and ruined your keyboard.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538040, 177550, 1040, 101637, 1072936800, '', 'seems that several people have problems like this:\n\n\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?t=51442 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?t=51442)\n\n\n\nhttp://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?t=51945 (http://www.halflife2.net/forums/showthread.php?t=51945)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538044, 177550, 1040, 100056, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Thr0tt \n\nSeek medical advice.\n\n\n\nSounds like your screen refresh could be too low or you suffer from car sickness / motion sickness.  \n\n\n\nAgreed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538078, 177550, 1040, 101638, 1072936800, '', 'Yesterday a friend of mine told me he almost had to vomit after playing about an hour. I laughed at him.\n\nBut today I played the game myself and i became very sick, too.\n\n\n\nThis never happened before with no other game.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nP.S.: Okay Steam makes everyone sick, but that\'s another thing.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538088, 177550, 1040, 101639, 1072936800, 'Check it out', 'There is a thread concering motion sickness in the General posts.  Lots of advice about how to beat it.  I had the same problem when I first started playing FPS games.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538844, 177550, 1040, 101635, 1072936800, '', 'weird....  this happened to me too last night.  It\'s never happened before and i\'ve been gaming for years....  unlocked my files.  Played for about 10 minutes and had to quit because I felt like i was gonna puke.  we\'ll see if the same thing happens later when I play.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538882, 177550, 1040, 101640, 1072936800, '', 'Yep i have this too\n\n\n\nBeen playing FPS shooters since Wolf3D and never had this problem. \n\n\n\nI felt sick as a dog after playing for an hour or so.  The refresh rate was set very high too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538891, 177550, 1040, 101641, 1072936800, '', 'I had this problem with quake.  It was very annoying.  I fixed it by turning down the screen size to 640x480.  You might want to try toning down your video settings.  The less real it looks, the less sick it will make you.  It\' sucks to have to look at less than perfection, but it\'s better than not playing at all.\n\n\n\nBest of luck,\n\nGeekzilla', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538978, 177550, 1040, 101642, 1072936800, '', 'strange, how big are your monitors? I never get sick playing any games, running 1600x1200 @ 75hz on a 19" without any issue.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538985, 177550, 1040, 101643, 1072936800, '', 'The reason people are getting sick is basically because the game looks so damn good. Your brain thinks youre moving but your body doesn\'t. This conflict causes the nausea that y\'all are experiencing. I\'m experiencing nausea of my own but only because I can\'t get the damn game to work.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538992, 177550, 1040, 101644, 1072936800, '', 'Dude, this thread just BUGGED me out.  Last night after playing for about 30 minutes, after work, I just started feeling weird.  This has never happened.  Anxiety + chill feeling?  Everything the original poster said happened, i rested for about 3 hours, and felt fine.\n\n\n\n\n\nIm wondering if a programmer at Valve is up to some physiological scrupulous activity to see if they can influence our bodily functions via programming experiments LOL, testing what kind of color/light/flash sequences they can use/that are safe, using us as guinea pigs without telling us.  Who knows, maybe it was just an anxiety attack, or it was some weirdness in the game.\n\n\n\n\n\n[]', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1539031, 177550, 1040, 101189, 1072936800, '', 'maybe we need to sue Valve make us sickness..............', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1539067, 177550, 1040, 101645, 1072936800, '', 'Hehe never had motion sickness problems myself but one thing you should try is turning of the sound since there are certain frequencies that can enduce realy bad motion sickness or try playing on another computer if to see if your graphics setup is doing it?\n\n\n\nPersonaly i recon i\'d keep going even if i was sick this game is too fun!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538089, 177559, 1040, 101646, 1072936800, 'What\'s the deal with the ending? (spoiler-esque)', 'Wow, I loved the whole game... until the very end.  I was very disappointed with that ending.  Perhaps I missed something but there just seems like too many plot holes to deal with and not enough resolve.  Another 6 years to figure out what is going to happen is just too long!  I just wanted to vent my frustration to the people who\'d probably understand the most.  \n\n\n\nSpoiler: Who are the benefactors (besides the aliens controlling Earth)? The carbine soldiers are humans, right?  Why are the aliens controlling us? What are their motives? Did you kill Alyx?  Who\'s the G Man and who\'s he working for?  Why is the G Man have a hard time talking - is he an alien?  I have a hundred more questions if anyone would like to talk about HL2. \n\n\n\nAny comments on the ending? \n\n\n\nA possible discussion?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538091, 177559, 1040, 101647, 1072936800, '', 'Spoiler: I\'m not sure what to think of the ending either... like what are all those green aliens at the end like the one breen is talking to or the ones you look down on as you go up to breen\'s office?  \n\n\n\ndont kill me mods im just curious as hell cause that game rocked and im freaking out that its over', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538093, 177559, 1040, 101646, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Lord Schnimph \n\n\n\n\n\ndont kill me mods im just curious as hell cause that game rocked and im freaking out that its over  \n\n\n\n\n\nYeah I can\'t agree more', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538128, 177559, 1040, 101647, 1072936800, '', 'Spoiler: it took me forever to figure out what to do at the end', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538219, 177559, 1040, 101646, 1072936800, '', 'It\'s been hours since I beat the game and I\'m still fuming!  I need some answers to these questions.  Now as I reflect on what happened in the game I realize that not one thing was really answered.  I hear there is some easter egg on one of the vehicle levels that may explain something but i have no idea where it is - if anyone can help I\'d be very greatful.\n\n\n\nHow can valve make such a great game and not really tell you anything!  \n\n\n\nSpoiler: Alyx clearly loves Gordon. I clearly love Alyx. G Man can control time! What is going to happen to Eli and Barnie and that silly headcrab the zany professor had?!?!?!?! I need some resolve... \n\n\n\nPlease someone give me some answers! Please!?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538279, 177559, 1040, 101647, 1072936800, '', 'all i want to ask is....\n\n\n\nEXPANSION PACK?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1538290, 177559, 1040, 101648, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Lord Schnimph \n\nall i want to ask is....\n\n\n\nEXPANSION PACK?  \n\n\n\ndon\'t forget about cpl. sheppard.  he is still being held onto by the gman.  he could be the main guy in a expansion pack', '127.0.0.1', 1),
