(1576368, 182302, 1040, 101708, 1072936800, '', '/forums/...threadid=178246 (/forums/showthread.php?s=&threadid=178246)\n\nquote:Originally posted by ritalin \n\nIn that pic on the coast. You are looking through a combine binocular set up. Though it seems like an ordinary "Hey, the gman is there" situation. I zoomed in on that pic (try it yourself) he is talk to the colonol (the dude with the british accent who gives you the RPG) Check out the leet toque on his head. I\'m sure it is him. So, then you drive over to that town and everyone says "We are expecting a Gunship attack." Now how the ©©©© do they know that? Could be a few ways, intercepted radio transmissions, or maybe the Gman said it. Maybe the Gman SOLD the RPG to them (Perhaps he makes profit on war. As he says at the end of the game, "I have numerous employers who want to buy you." or whatever.) Also, when going on the underground railway (in the canel) you drop down into a broken down rail cart, with a Vort and a Resistance member. If you are quick enough, you can see the Vort, by the TV, is watching the Gman... Why? ©©©© if I know.\n\nVery relevant here ritalin.  I enjoyed reading your thoughts on the HL/2 story thus far, as well as others. I am subscribing to your thread []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1576478, 182302, 1040, 101094, 1072936800, '', 'http://www.maniscompost.com/Coast.jpg (http://www.maniscompost.com/Coast.jpg)\n\n\n\nthe coast binoculars sighting is one of three I found on my own....\n\n\n\nAfter I beat the game I cheated, and clipped across the water... to see who he was talking too.\n\n\n\njust thought I\'d share a closer image...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1581767, 182302, 1040, 101713, 1072936800, '', 'I spotted Gman two or three times in Water Hazards and once in Highway 17. That\'s all I remember.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1581854, 182302, 1040, 101714, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks! This is actually a good thread! I only noticed him a few times also. But it\'s cool, how he checks up on you. And obviously others can see and talk to him.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1582005, 182302, 1040, 101715, 1072936800, '', 'I knew it was him in Nova Prospekt!!!\n\n\n\nAnd yes he does seem to have a hand in the events that unfold who knows what his relationship is to Breen and the Benefactors.\n\n\n\nSomeone should add all the sightings in HL1/HL:S also I know in the beginning he is talking to a scientist and there are a lot of times he turns around just as some obstacle is about to get into your way.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1595491, 182302, 1040, 101708, 1072936800, '', 'Thanks for your responses, but apparently I\'m missing one sighting?!\n\n\n\nPost your thoughts and/or screenshots of this location.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1595601, 182302, 1040, 101716, 1072936800, '', 'I spotted one more occurence in Water Hazard.. You\'re speeding along a kanal with steep sides, right before the kanal splits (one side is a dead end with headcrabs, the other side leads to more open water)\n\n\n\nAnyway, before that split, there is footbridge that leads over the kanal, and he\'s walking across it. I was going full throttle on the airboat, by the time i realized it was him i was past him and when i looked back he\'d already gone', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1595655, 182302, 1040, 101717, 1072936800, '', 'You forgot the one near the playground at the trainstation.\n\n\n\nIf you go to the play ground and than into the house where you are sposed to go and you rush straight down the hall and to the right into the cinderblock pile you see a TV with G-Man on it.... Just thought you might wanna know []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1576080, 182355, 1040, 100913, 1072936800, '', 'Half-Life 2 KnowledgeBase for Retail Owners\n\n\n\nHalf-Life 2 - System Requirements (Retail) (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7141)\n\n\n\nHalf Life 2 - Unsupported Video Cards (DirectX 7.0) (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7148)\n\n\n\nHalf-Life 2 - CD Installation error when Counter-strike: Source is not selected (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7150)\n\n\n\nHalf Life 2 - Issues with SecuROM copy protection and related disk read errors. (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7163)\n\n\n\nHalf Life 2 - Invalid CD key error with Steam authentication process (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7154)\n\n\n\nHalf Life 2 - Error: "Map Version is 0, expecting 19" (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/answer.aspx?ID=7157)\n\n\n\n\n\nHalf-Life 2 KnowledgeBase Index\n\n\n\nHalf-Life 2 Help Index - OTHER Problems (http://support2.vugames.com/hl2/search.aspx)\n\n\n\n\n\nSteampowered.com Support Page\n\n\n\nAdditional support can be found at the SUPPORT (/support.php) page located at the top of the page.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1580790, 182911, 1040, 101721, 1072936800, 'City 7-steam', 'Maybe it was just a glitch, maybe a conspiracy, maybe just a dream, but when I started HL2 the first time it was like this:\n\n\n\nI start on a train and a guy says, "I didn\'t see you get on." I nudged the next guy on the train and he said, "No matter how many times I transfer, it never works and I have to start all over." When I get off the train there is a large screen monitor mounted high in all the rooms, and Gabe\'s face is on them all. He is spewing propaganda, "Welcome to City 7-Steam.....it\'s safer here..."\n\n\n\nThere are soldiers everywhere with Steam Logos on their uniforms. The first is pushing a man trying to get his luggage and zapping him with a cattle prod, saying "It\'s encrypted, just leave it alone, you can\'t use it, move along".\n\n\n\nThen I get near the fence with a rotating gate and a woman on the other side says, "Have you seen my game? Was it on that train?"\n\n\n\nAll the people are wearing the same clothes that say "customer" on them like it\'s a brand name. I go through the gate and the woman says, "I\'m waiting for my game...It\'s been 4 hours, but they\'re being nice and letting me wait!"\n\n\n\nI continue on and as I walk I hear these steam-soldiers saying things under their masks. It\'s hard to understand most of it, but I heard, "Just get in line..." and "Put in your CD...". One pushed me and said, "You! Wait! Steam is busy right now, get back!"\n\n\n\nOne man was walking back and forth like a crazy person mumbling about, "It says connect to steam, but steam says can\'t connect...I can\'t connect so I can\'t play...It says it cant connect so I should go to the steam site. The steam site says page can not be dislplayed and so I should connect to steam. I connect to steam and steam says it\'s too busy, and the game is not available..."\n\n\n\nSomeone called me "Freeman", but I was not free, I was enslaved in the cattle coral with everyone else.\n\n\n\nContinue.......', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1580799, 182911, 1040, 101722, 1072936800, '', 'muhahhahaha revenge is sweet. even when its only online.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
