(1607672, 185456, 1013, 103399, 1072936800, '', 'quote:NOTE: Entrapment is available as a defense only when an agent of the state or federal government has provided the encouragement or inducement. This defense is sometimes allowed in administrative proceedings (as for the revocation of a license to practice medicine) as well as criminal proceedings. In order to establish entrapment, the defendant has the burden of proving either that he or she would not have committed the crime but for the undue persuasion or fraud of the government agent, or that the encouragement was such that it created a risk that persons not inclined to commit the crime would commit it, depending on the jurisdiction. When entrapment is pleaded, evidence (as character evidence) regarding the defendant that might otherwise have been excluded is allowed to be admitted. \n\n\n\n\n\nThe important part there being "ENCOURAGEMENT or INDUCEMENT" even if valve did make that key available, they didn\'t encourage you to use it, that would be your decision.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1607673, 185456, 1013, 101451, 1072936800, '', 'accept that valve dosn\'t have to do anything people are stupid enough by themselfes to get into trouble', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1607680, 185456, 1013, 100042, 1072936800, '', 'You\'re right, entrapment is illegal, but if Valve revokes their intellectual property from you because you didn\'t legally and lawfully pay for the rights to use it, Valve has every right to take it from you.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1607695, 185456, 1013, 100349, 1072936800, '', 'Just to make things clear...\n\n\n\nFirst, Valve didn\'t put out any kind of fake key or fake warez to trap people.\n\n\n\nSecond, the people that had their accounts disabled had attempted to steal an item worth about $50.  20,000 accounts times $50 - that\'s about a million dollars worth of illegal attempts.  That\'s hard to ignore.\n\n\n\nThird, the number of people who actually had bought HL2 and used the CD key cheat was VERY small.  VERY small.  Most people just tried to rip off the game and not bother buying it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1607704, 185456, 1013, 100359, 1072936800, '', 'Repeat after me....\n\n\n\n\n\nDon\'t\n\nBreak\n\nThe LAW\n\n\n\nAnd no one has to worry.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1608145, 185498, 1013, 101776, 1072936800, 'Support for the 20 000?', 'I have submitted 3 tickets over the last couple of days and none have been replied to.\n\n\n\nI am one of the 20 000 who has been disabled from steam. I am however a legit owner of the game witha legit case.\n\n\n\nHowever Nobody will answer my support tickets. From the sticky waldo posted no to long ago it stated that the majority of the 20 000 did not have legal copies of the game.\n\n\n\nBut what about us that do? I am sitting here wasting time without support for a product I bought!\n\n\n\nI bet valve just looks at the support tickets that say "account disabled" and think.. "pff another game pirate" and throw it out without consideration.\n\n\n\nBy disabling those 20 000 people they have hurt a select few of us who did no wrong and now we can\'t ven get support.\n\n\n\nWhat else can I do?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1608159, 185498, 1013, 101777, 1072936800, '', 'I second that!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
