(1608321, 185498, 1013, 101782, 1072936800, '', 'If you used a Warez\'d key, then you are just as at fault as the guy who didn\'t pay for it. \n\n\n\nInstead of waiting for support you used a warez\'d key to see if your key was at fault? That\'s about the dumbest excuse I can think of. Just be a man and accept the consequences of what you did. You used a warez\'d key. That\'s all the matters in this instance. \n\n\n\nI can\'t wait until they do a mass ban of people who have been cheating as well. It\'s not like they don\'t know about it. We\'ll see a ton of threads saying, "I was just testing it out!"', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1608459, 185498, 1013, 101783, 1072936800, '', 'what can really say and that you/they were very severe in doing this action type. and it can have several cases to analyze among these 20.000 people that had their disabled bills. I am really man of assuming my actions, but I don\'t make him/it for a thing that I didn\'t do. it could be softer trying to enter in contact with each user passing the problem and trying to verify the authenticity of his/her products. the valve doesn\'t want to be harmed but this doing, what doesn\'t want her same, to their thousands of users that really bought his/her product.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1608466, 185498, 1013, 101784, 1072936800, '', 'you people crying are honestly pathetic. Cry ry cry, like every other hacker out their that gets caught they cry and plea and except valve to feel sorry for them and to unbann their accounts. Like its said it the sticky it wont happen so leave it to re', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1608483, 185498, 1013, 101785, 1072936800, '', 'hahaha you got what you deserved ûûûûers.\n\n\n\nPWNED', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1623413, 186958, 1013, 100323, 1072936800, 'HL2 Update', 'The changes in this release are directed at reducing the problem some users are experiencing with sound stuttering. The sound stuttering is not indicative of a sound problem, sound stuttering is only a symptom of texture thrashing on your video card or AGP memory. For information on how to reduce texture thrashing visit this link on our support site:\n\n\n\n/support.php/cg...php?p_faqid=280 (/support.php/cgi-bin/steampowered.cfg/php/enduser/std_adp.php?p_faqid=280)\n\n\n\nThis update will fix sound stuttering that users were experiencing that would last for longer than a few seconds during normal gameplay. This update will also eliminate this same behavior following a quicksave or autosave. There will still be a short pause while the autosave happens, but not the more drawn out stuttering behaivior.\n\n\n\nWe are still investigating another performance problem on some hardware, which will manifest where the game is getting into a state where performance drops to less than 5 fps and does not recover or crashes.\n\n\n\nNext week we will be releasing the Source SDK, along with a surprise for the community.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1623419, 186958, 1013, 100003, 1072936800, '', 'SWEET!!!!\n\n\n\nEDIT: First time ever to get firsties on an update post. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nStill really good news.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1623426, 186958, 1013, 101795, 1072936800, '', 'Nice cliffe.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
