(1624325, 187041, 1040, 100307, 1072936800, 'HL2 Patch - Nov 24 - Bug/Error Report', 'Have a new bug? Patched bug still not fixed?  Post here.\n\n\n\nPlease keep nasty comments out - if it is not suitable at all for this thread then your post will be deleted.\n\n\n\n\n\nUse This FAQ if you\'re having more problems then before with stuttering.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624404, 187041, 1040, 101799, 1072936800, 'Seems worse now', 'I used to get the audio stutter and "memory could not be read" errors. But these errors occured during gameplay or in the advanced video settings. After updating, I cannot get to the main menu. The game now boots me and gives a "memory could not be read" error during the initial loading scene, right after the valve logo...bummer.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624405, 187041, 1040, 101800, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m still experiencing audio studdering, and the autosave lag is now longer than before (was a few seconds now is going upwards of 5 seconds.) And now the game decides to crash for no apparent reason []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624411, 187041, 1040, 101801, 1072936800, '', 'it says PREPARING TO START HALFLIFE2... then nothing comes up??!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624414, 187041, 1040, 101802, 1072936800, '', 'can you confirm that this patch is intended to fix the sound stutter bug for nvidia and ati users? i think there is some confusion about this atm', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624442, 187041, 1040, 101803, 1072936800, '', 'I used to be able to play the game in 5 to 10 min. chunks,memory read error at every auto-save and loading next section.now i cant even get to the main menu.This really sucks......again', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624457, 187041, 1040, 101804, 1072936800, '', 'Howdy!\n\n\n\nThye audio stutter patch didnt work at first. Was the same as before.\n\n\n\nI then restarted windows, set my AGP size to 256 (I have 768 ram total) in the bios.\n\n\n\nThen added all the suggested console commands, (heapsize, forepreloads etc..).\n\n(I had done all these before, but they had no effect so i reset my changes).\n\n\n\nAlso made th autosave files read only!\n\n\n\nStuttering is now all but gone. I think the command that is helping the most now is\n\nsnd_async_fullyasync 1\n\n\n\nThe only time I notice anything bad now is when I fire a gun for the first time since last load, the sound lags about 1 second behind the shot animation, but thereafter its ok, and theres never any stutter.\n\n\n\namd 2600+\n\n768 ram\n\naudigy plat\n\nWD 10,000rpm sata rapter HDD\n\nATI 9700 pro (latest DNA drivers with   HL2 optimised option)\n\nwinxp sp2 proff\n\ngigabyte 7dxr motherboard', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624487, 187041, 1040, 101805, 1072936800, '', 'I actually got a Sound Loop followed by a black screen and then I saw my desktop [], and once during loading HL2 at the bar in the kmiddle that says loading it froze with a high pitched noise []..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624496, 187041, 1040, 101806, 1072936800, '', 'had an auto-update!\n\n\n\nSaw the confirmation in the monitor/update field \'HL2 100% etc.\'\n\n\n\nStarted the game (as well a new game as a previoyus save game)\n\nand things got worse. The game stutters all the time now.\n\nBefore the patch it was irritating but still playable. Now\n\nit\'s even more irritating and unplayable!\n\n\n\nWhat a nightmare!!!\n\n\n\nP4-1.8Ghz\n\n512 DDR\n\nGeForce Ti 4400\n\nCreative Soundblaster 5.1 Digital\n\nWinXP SP2', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624563, 187041, 1040, 101807, 1072936800, '', 'Unfortunately still st-stuttering here. I haven\'t gone back and tried all the tweaks again yet (*sigh*) but I thought the "patch" was supposed to fix the problem. \n\n\n\nAMD Athlon XP 2800+\n\nWindows XP Pro (SP2)\n\nRadeon 9600XT \n\nABIT NF7-S (rev 2) mobo\n\nonboard Soundstorm\n\n512 Meg PC3200 Corsair TwinX RAM', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624626, 187041, 1040, 101808, 1072936800, '', 'Shorter duration of stuttering immediately after \'Loading\', but overal much higher frequency of stuttering during general gameplay.\n\n\n\nOverall the patch seems to have made the gameplay experience worse rather than better.\n\n\n\nAsus K8VSE Deluxe\n\nAthlon 64 3400\n\n1gb Geil PC3500\n\nAsus X800 XTPE (Catalyst 4.12 Beta Drivers).\n\nAudigy 2 ZS (Creative Driver 2.1.84.50).\n\niiyama Prolite E430S (Latest iiyama drivers installed 1280x1024@75hz).\n\n2 x 160gb Western Digital SATA (RAID 0).\n\nASUS DVD-E616P2\n\nNEC 3500A DVD Writer\n\nWindows XP Home edition SP1.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624676, 187041, 1040, 101809, 1072936800, '', 'Wanna know why im really pissed? I am deployed in Iraq right now, i came home for leave to visit family on thanksgiving and bought this game hoping to take it back with me and play it when i have free time. If this problem is not fixed by the time i leave again for iraq, the 28th, then i may not be able to play this again for 6 months, so i am really upset that this game is not working. Even if they get a patch out a week later, it will be too late for me, god only knows were i will be able to hook up my laptop in iraq to connect to that darned steam. This whole steam thing just blows IMO.\n\n\n\nThanks valve, i geuss i cant expect you to work on thanksgiving, or fridays, or the weekend, looks like i am screwed, damned memory read error.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624715, 187041, 1040, 101810, 1072936800, '', 'Still cannot start up HL2.  The video runs, then it crashes with a couple error boxes popping up, \n\ncode:ErrorBoxTitle: Engine Error\nErroBoxMsg: Internal driver error in IDirect3DDevice9::Present\n\nor it will show the usual vertexbuffer unable to be locked error.  Then it shows the usual memory error at the same location as always.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624728, 187041, 1040, 101677, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m back to stuttering sound again after I fixed it using FFDShow idea... stuttering somehow seems worse then it was originally', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1624744, 187041, 1040, 101811, 1072936800, '', 'Even after the patch, it still stutters for me.\n\n\n\nRadeon 9600xt\n\n\n\nCatalyst 4.12 Beta driver\n\n\n\nPentium [4] 2.4', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1627702, 187356, 1013, 101812, 1072936800, 'Fake STEAM E-Mail !!!!', 'Please note that this is a FAKE Steam email. \n\n\n\nNever send out your username and password to anyone!\n\n\n\nForum regular Phantom informed me about an e-mail he received yesterday which tries to make people believe that the Steam Account database will be formatted soon and that the user information needs to be sent to the e-mail address supplied in the mail. \n\n\n\nOf course the mail is fake! Never send out your username and password to anyone. This should be commonly known but in regards to this mail I thought I should mention it here again. So if you get a mail like the one below, just delete it and don\'t pay any attention to it.\n\n\n\nquote:From: "Steam" < accounts@steampowered.com (mailto:accounts@steampowered.com) >\n\nReply-To: "Steam" < steam-validation@mail.com (mailto:steam-validation@mail.com) >\n\nTo: "---@hotmail.com" < ---@hotmail.com (mailto:---@hotmail.com) >\n\nSubject: Please validate your Steam Account\n\nDate: Mon, 22 Nov 2004 21:39:45 +1100\n\n\n\nDear Steam User,\n\n\n\nIn order to continue using Steam you must validate your account by \n\nforwarding this message to Steam-validation@mail.com (mailto:Steam-validation@mail.com).\n\nYou must include your account information in this format in the message:\n\nUsername: (your Steam username)\n\nE-Mail: (the email you registered your account to.)\n\nPassword: (the password you used to log in to your Steam account.)\n\n\n\nOur database will be formatted soon, due to some damage caused by some \n\nusers. We will need to record our active users and add them to our database \n\nonce again.\n\n\n\nYou must validate your account within 30 days or eles your account will \n\nget closed. Thank you for your co-operation, Best regards, Steam \n\naccount Managing Team.\n\n\n\nOriginal post by Sebastian from CSBANANA. \n\n\n\nhttp://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=31483 (http://forums.csbanana.com/showthread.php?t=31483)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1628349, 187356, 1013, 100027, 1072936800, '', 'Wow, that sucks. Stickied.\n\n\n\n(it goes without saying, yes that\'s a fake and you should just delete it if you get it)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1705219, 187356, 1013, 100913, 1072936800, '', 'Changed thread title from "Fake STEAM E-Mail !!!!" to "Important: Steam Account Stealing Scam."', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630350, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, 'Antialiasing bug Post patch.', 'Turning on AA to 2X now gives me a 50% framerate drop I did not have pre-patch. (didnt even bother 4XAA as it was already at 18fps)  Disabling the console command that is supposed to disable the patch does nothing for it either. Fix this problem and my game will be elite. []\n\n\n\n9800pro cat 4.12b\n\n\n\nSmash, can you test it on your card as I know you have ati 1280x1024 2XAA = 50% drop with AA enabled. Where i was 40fps before im now at 18-20 []\n\n\n\nOn a side note....\n\n\n\n Please enable vertex shader model 2.0 instead of 1.0 on ati cards. [] Nvidia 6800 owners would benifit from this also.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630431, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'I also recall valve saying long ago that HL2 would not support AA. Have we gone back to how it was before? Also this is a bump till I can get someone else to confirm.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630449, 187592, 1040, 101814, 1072936800, '', 'I never benchmarked the game without aa before the patch. But I can tell you that my framerate took a big dive after the patch.\n\n\n\nGood thing they are calling it a patch and not a fix.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630453, 187592, 1040, 101815, 1072936800, '', 'Your are not alone aceflier, i had played hl2 a lot with aa2x and af4x last week, and no perfs problems , after the patch it looks like the perfs are something like 40-50% decreased, what a bad news. \n\n\n\nValve, what game are you playing with your customers ?\n\nAnyway, anyone know how to disable this patch ? i don\'t want steam to decide for me what is good or not...\n\n\n\nLet\'s see if other people get this perf decrease.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630564, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'Keep this at the top. [] Sorry bump again.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630573, 187592, 1040, 101816, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Ogota07 \n\n\n\nAnyway, anyone know how to disable this patch ? i don\'t want steam to decide for me what is good or not... \n\nset mat_forcemanagedtextureintohardware to "0"  in your config file.\n\n\n\nBtw you\'re right.  I run the game at 1024 with 4x AA, and with mat_forcemanagedtextureintohardware set to 1 there\'s a framerate penalty of 25%-35% using Anand\'s timedemos as benchmarks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630607, 187592, 1040, 101814, 1072936800, '', 'I use the same anand demo\'s. I can tell you that before the patch I got 68-69fps at 1280x960 with 4xaa and 8xansio. Now with the forcemanageblahblah set to one, I get 40. Set it to 0 and I only get 42. So disabling the cvar does not undo the patch. They stuffed some code in there too.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630630, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'Ya undoing it doesnt do squat for me either. The only way to get performance where it was before is to completely turn off AA and that sucks []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630746, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'Can\'t have this on the 2nd page common people test this on you ati cards and let me know the results.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630804, 187592, 1040, 101817, 1072936800, '', 'P4 3.2GHz\n\nRadeon X800XT-PE\n\n1024MB Corsair DDR-400 (2-3-3-6)\n\nWinXP SP2 + Cat 4.12b\n\n1280x1024 6xAA, 16xAF, all in-game settings maxed\n\n\n\nPre-patch I was dropping to about 35FPS in the d1_canals_07 level (by the red barn, looking out over the water) ... Post-patch I\'m getting 14FPS. Less than half.\n\n\n\nThe rest of the game seems fine so far - peaking at about 200-250FPS with an average of about 75-100. But the water is REALLY killing me now, it was fine before the patch but now there\'s a MASSIVE hit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630832, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'I used the area before the nuclear water and you roll the explosive barrells down that slimy ramp My fps were 40fps pre patch 18 after patch. Like you said thats a huge hit.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630856, 187592, 1040, 101390, 1072936800, '', 'It seems most people are having problems with the water, possibly they added vertex anti-aliasing to the water to make it look smoother now.. I\'m at work so I can\'t check mine, will try later.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630900, 187592, 1040, 101814, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Squeetard \n\nI use the same anand demo\'s. I can tell you that before the patch I got 68-69fps at 1280x960 with 4xaa and 8xansio. Now with the forcemanageblahblah set to one, I get 40. Set it to 0 and I only get 42. So disabling the cvar does not undo the patch. They stuffed some code in there too.  \n\n\n\nMy framerate jumps up to 87 with aa set to none. So 4x aa kills me by half. wtf is with that bs? Who wants jaggies? I didn\'t pay $500 for my 6800 gt to play hl2 like a peasant.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1630932, 187592, 1040, 101813, 1072936800, '', 'I think you will find even 2xAA will cut it in half. [] Must be something clogging the pipelines with AA enabled now and its not just the water where its happening its all parts i get 70 in a lit hallway with 2XAA (230 with 0AA). Something is wrong with those numbers in themselves.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1631010, 187592, 1040, 101814, 1072936800, '', 'I will check out 2xaa.\n\n\n\nBump.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
