(1640891, 188659, 1040, 101853, 1072936800, 'CS:S Tips & Tricks', 'What are some good tips and tricks for CS:S.\n\n\n\nUse flash bangs and grnades, they are your friend.\n\n\n\nShould you quickly tap the first button ont he rifles for more acruacy ?\n\n\n\nIs zoomed once on two zoom sniper rifles as accurate as two zooms ?\n\n\n\nWhat are some good tricks and tactics for the different maps ?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1640998, 188659, 1040, 101854, 1072936800, '', '? lol? erm aim for the head?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1641012, 188659, 1040, 101855, 1072936800, '', 'Rather than sitting here drawing out in detail MY tactics for for CS and CS:S I\'m going to give you a hand in developing your own tactics.\n\n\n\nWhat should do (I\'m assuming your new to the CS world) is learn the maps first of all, thats very importiant.  Second, play with each weapon and learn its goods and bads for your particular playing style.  Some would say the AK-47 is the best and other will argue that the mp-5 is the best, it just depends on what you think is the best.  Same thing with grenades, learn the map and learn when and how you should use them for the situation your in.\n\n\n\nThere is no real stratagy guide for CS and CS:S, just play and don\'t get frustrated, eventually you\'ll be rackingup kills like your in the CAL.  Besides, even the best players have bad days where they couldn\'t kill an AFK.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1641133, 188659, 1040, 101853, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bloodchill \n\n? lol? erm aim for the head?  \n\n\n\nYeah that works somedays, depends what the CS:S hit boxes are doing at the time LOL', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1641815, 188659, 1040, 101856, 1072936800, '', 'the best trick (besides experience) is to frag, frag right and frag good\\!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1641922, 188659, 1040, 101857, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by bloodchill \n\n? lol? erm aim for the head?  \n\n\n\nbut they wont stay still long enough for me to aim []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1641933, 188659, 1040, 101856, 1072936800, '', 'hehe common problem (spray and pray is the answer lol).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642323, 188659, 1040, 101858, 1072936800, '', '1. Respect other players. Avoid going into arguments with people you don\'t know (cause it\'s pointless), like cheaters or other lamers. Everybody was a noob once. Don\'t ever accuse people of cheating (90% of the people who blame others are wrong), if there is no doubt, just say it in teamspeak.\n\n2. Learn from others. Walk along with the top players of your team (check scoreboard). Avoid being in his way and just observe what he does/how he does it and why. Avoid trying to walk alone (or camp in a corner). Work as a team as best you can (mostly it works out when teammembers see it work). Observe top players when you\'re dead.\n\n3. Learn the rules of the game (bomb placing/hostage rescueing) and live them (don\'t camp if it\'s not your objective in the game).\n\n4. Learn the maps and the starting routes.\n\n5. It\'s okay to pull back when under fire. Just reload when your safe and don\'t stay in one spot too long.\n\n6. Get used to the AK or the Colt rifle. Every weapon has it own recoil to get used too. Since these are the most common weapons (mostly laying on the ground), it\'s more efficient to start with these rifles.\n\n7. When in close encounter with an enemy, full fire, strafe and aim at the troat.\n\n8. When in middle range distance with an enemy, burst fire (2 - 4 shots at a time, depending on your hit percentage). If your enemy doesn\'t die after 2 / 3 bursts, try aiming better (chest or head).\n\n9. When in long range, crouch, aim at the head / upper chest, 2 shots at a time when crosshairs stop moving inwards. Take your time to aim (don\'t shoot just because you get hit by enemy), and you\'ll find that you\'ll win most of the time (because 80% of the community fires too inaccurate).\n\n10. Practice above steps. Practice hard. Don\'t give up. Don\'t blame others of mistakes. It\'s just a game. [] And try to believe in your hit accuracy in one point in time. When you do, you\'ll find that you can stop reloading so often, because after muchos practicos, you can kill about 5 people with one 30 bullet clip. When you do, people start to accuse you of cheating, and that\'s the point you\'ll know your above average and end up in the top 3 in each game.\n\n\n\nGood luck! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642503, 188659, 1040, 101859, 1072936800, '', 'And dont call "cheater" to every good player in game. []\n\n\n\nMany pple has been playing this game for years and anticipe almost any move you can do, and any tactic you can think without using hacks.\n\n\n\nSo try to learn from the best players, enjoy and practise till your fingers drop, and eventually you will became a good player.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642541, 188659, 1040, 101860, 1072936800, 'CS:S Tips & Tricks', 'quote:Originally posted by podge \n\nWhat are some good tips and tricks for CS:S.\n\n\n\nUse flash bangs and grnades, they are your friend.\n\n\n\nShould you quickly tap the first button ont he rifles for more acruacy ?\n\n\n\nIs zoomed once on two zoom sniper rifles as accurate as two zooms ?\n\n\n\nWhat are some good tricks and tactics for the different maps ?  \n\n\n\nTips to you, think differently than others......lol.....', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642805, 188659, 1040, 101853, 1072936800, '', 'nielsvk - Great tips, and that\'s the sort of stuff i was looking for. I have been trying the 2-4 shot mid range tactic and appears to work quiet well.\n\n\n\nDoes resoloution and graphic settings make a player better ? I\'ve heard of some people turning of fog and rain and things ?\n\n\n\ncpQ - Soemtimes work, but against good players they seem to take you out and your sitting there thinking but i was shooting so good .  LOL\n\n\n\nBullitt GT40 - You know you want to write down some tips and tactics for us.\n\n\n\nchip_[clown] - sometimes a problem, but other times it\'s funny when you can have your sights on them for a few seconds whilst they camp . .  Makes the killmuch more enjoyable when you knock someone\'s tent down.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642894, 188659, 1040, 100845, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cpQ \n\nthe best trick (besides experience) is to frag, frag right and frag good\\!  \n\n\n\nIv noticed that fraging is horrible. What i mean is throwing frags. To throw a frag, while moving, you have to be moving towards the direction you want to throw it, regardless of where your crosshair is pointed. Is it suppose to be like that, or just some kind of bug.\n\n\n\nReason for complaint: Im used to strafting sideways along a wall to a doorway, and right when i get to teh door i let go of teh nade an straft back. So that would give them less time to shot back at me, considering they are in the next room, when i have a nade in my hand, but this tactic doesnt work. [] Bug, no bug?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1642932, 188659, 1040, 101861, 1072936800, '', 'You might find that when playing a map after a few rounds things start to get predictable. This is when tactics come into play.\n\n\n\nIt\'s not enough to just be a good aim, though that is a necessity to be good. \n\n\n\nYou\'ll probably find out pretty quickly where the choke points are, where people like to take cover, where they run through etc. Just use your head.\n\n\n\nI racked up a few kills in Italy as a T by dashing down the stairs and around to the corner where the CT\'s meet before heading up the ramp towards the hostage house. I just tossed a HE grenade in there and if I was lucky it\'d land before the CT\'s got there. Then it\'d blow AS they got there. \n\n\n\nFollow up with a quick strike while they\'re in dis-array and you can get a few good kills in a single round. \n\n\n\nJust be aware of when you\'re becoming too predictable. Know the map so you can be comfortable taking a different route each time. Watch the routes the opponents take and see if you can find good ambush points. \n\n\n\nSurprise be it by rushing in unexpectedly or ambushing is a big factor in winning a gun battle. \n\n\n\nAlso, learn not to be dis-oriented by flashbangs. It\'s all situational awareness, when the lights go out, you have to know where cover is and how to get there. Experienced players will still get flashed, but they\'ll run for cover as though it didn\'t affect them. \n\nThat\'s about all I can add that hasn\'t been covered yet', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643013, 188659, 1040, 101853, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by RedSage \n\n[B]I racked up a few kills in Italy as a T by dashing down the stairs and around to the corner where the CT\'s meet before heading up the ramp towards the hostage house. I just tossed a HE grenade in there and if I was lucky it\'d land before the CT\'s got there. Then it\'d blow AS they got there. \n\n \n\n\n\nSame on aztec i saw the guy running under the wooden bridge to come up the ramp near the bomb spot closest to the start, so i ran back and threw a grenade at the top of the ramp and it got him.\n\n\n\nSo the game is more about knowing where they willbe and come from as well as shooting.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643220, 188659, 1040, 101862, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by podge \n\nSame on aztec i saw the guy running under the wooden bridge to come up the ramp near the bomb spot closest to the start, so i ran back and threw a grenade at the top of the ramp and it got him.\n\n\n\nSo the game is more about knowing where they willbe and come from as well as shooting.  \n\n\n\n\n\nthis was metion before you should learn the maps / every bomb map has two sites / A site and B site  / the bomb site you are refering to is bomb site A', '127.0.0.1', 1),
