(1643710, 188935, 1040, 103400, 1072936800, 'D3D vs Opengl..', '..no unofficial opengl renderer for halflife2 I assume..?\n\n(yes or no answers please,no flame!)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643744, 188935, 1040, 103401, 1072936800, '', 'I don\'t remember.. but I do know in farcry; which is a d3d9 game like hl2, that when you turn off d3d and opengl on. everything becomes messed up. graphicly. if you don\'t have a newer graphic card I do feel your pain.. though its not that hard to save some money for a newer card. but its proberly just one of those questions thingy threads =P\n\n\n\nhope I was a little help =D', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643761, 188935, 1040, 101957, 1072936800, '', 'AFAIK HL2 was done exclusively for D3D.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643773, 188935, 1040, 103400, 1072936800, '', '..a little..I know it is possible in farcry,and I like to mess with stuff,therefore I would like to know if opengl rendering is possible with HL2,just for testing purposes..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643785, 188935, 1040, 103402, 1072936800, '', 'I dont know much about the subject and how it works.\n\n\n\nBut i was dubious how HL2 would run on my machine on D3D, just shows that Valve are talented and tweaked everything to run perfectly ! (For me anyway)\n\n\n\nI think its the only game i played where the min and reccommened system specs actually are true !\n\n\n\nI really think Valve did an awesome job !!!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643794, 188935, 1040, 103152, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by Silent*Ninja \n\nI dont know much about the subject and how it works.\n\n\n\nBut i was dubious how HL2 would run on my machine on D3D, just shows that Valve are talented and tweaked everything to run perfectly ! (For me anyway)\n\n\n\nI think its the only game i played where the min and reccommened system specs actually are true !\n\n\n\nI really think Valve did an awesome job !!!  \n\n\n\nQuoted for truth.\n\n\n\nIt runs on my 1Ghz 256 ram pretty much OK.  Also my laptop with literally no video card (simulated gfx) runs it OK too.  GJ Valve.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1643820, 188935, 1040, 103403, 1072936800, '', 'OpenGL is more prone to cheating, simply because it is open and thus easier to work with than D3D.\n\n\n\ni love OGL too, but i\'m actually glad HL2 uses D3D, if only for the fact that it will force the current OGL cheat makers to learn new methods, thus slowing them down (for a while anyway).\n\n\n\nif i may ask, exactly what sort of OpenGL "testing purposes" were you interested in performing on HL2?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656517, 188935, 1040, 103400, 1072936800, '', '..speed/graphics comparison,vga cards compatibility,blahblah..all cr@p you can imagine []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656574, 188935, 1040, 101957, 1072936800, '', 'I can imagine wallhack, aimbot, etc, etc, etc.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656618, 188935, 1040, 103404, 1072936800, '', 'Gabe Newell himself said Direct3D, in its 9th version, is more mature than OpenGL. Because of its ready-made nature, it\'s also quicker to develop games on it. OpenGL is, inevitably, on its way out; the Doom III engine will keep it alive for a few more years, but Unreal Engine 3.0 is likely to supplant it completely, destroying OpenGL and being crowned the king of DirectX9.0.\n\n\n\nAnd to answer the original question, there will not be an OpenGL renderer for Half-Life 2 because there is no urgent need for it. Other than Linux abilities, what benefit is there to switch to OpenGL, considering it could take years to completely recode the engine to OpenGL.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656648, 188935, 1040, 101451, 1072936800, '', 'HL2 is D3D only and if you could enable OpenGL then it would look very bad commpared to what it is now since OpenGL is an outdated rendering method.  D3D supports much nicer particle fx and other things such as reflection and bumbmapping much more easyly\n\n\n\nso unless OpenGL 2.0 can get its act togather when it will be released, D3D will rule the gaming world\n\n\n\ngot to love micro$oft', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656875, 188935, 1040, 103405, 1072936800, '', 'FYI for anyone who doesn\'t remember...\n\n\n\nThe original alpha leak from E3 also had an OpenGL renderer built right in.  It supported rudimentary shaders (but this was EXTREMELY early in HL2\'s overall development).  It wasn\'t the same one from HL1 just left over.\n\n\n\nValve later worked much more closely with Microsoft, touted DX9, and also made a very lucrative marketing arrangement with ATI to promote that.\n\n\n\nBut technically there\'s no reason OpenGL can\'t do anything HL2 does right now.  The API is different (many would say much simpler and robust), but the 2.0 spec was recently ratified and released, and shaders have been in OpenGL games for a while now.\n\n\n\nBefore Doom 3, there was Tenebrae.  We had simple shaders in Call of Duty, and several other games, and things like bumpmapping have been around since 1999/2000!\n\n\n\nI remember one such game was Slave Zero and it\'s "EVBM" or environmental bumpmapping.  I\'m not sure if that had a dual DX7/OpenGL render or not back then.\n\n\n\nNow UT2003/2004 may not be quite as impressive as Doom3/HL2, but it\'s material system works under both a full DX8/9 renderer and an OpenGL driver (for compatibility and Linux support).\n\n\n\nThe OpenGL 2.0 spec allows for a lot of flexibility, so I wouldn\'t be surprised to see licensed D3 engine games in the future support a newer full OGL2 renderer (D3 uses a custom written driver by Carmack consisting of many OGL2 features under an ARB2 path).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1656894, 188935, 1040, 101141, 1072936800, '', 'HL2 would not look as beautiful in OpenGL.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1657109, 188935, 1040, 102194, 1072936800, '', 'Surprising how simple people can get brainwashed by companies like valve and M$. D3D is in no way better then OGL. It\'s just a different API, and every game that supports both has been faster in OGL so far, including Far Cry (i got a GF4 Ti4200, it might be different for your card). I got about 30-40 fps in D3D and +/- 100 in OGL, and i think OGL even looked better, but that\'s just an opinion, and you may not agree to that of course. Also, dont forget that hl1/cs runs pretty crap on D3D, and the OGL renderer is clearly superior.\n\n\n\nAll that arguments about cheating are also complete rubbish, cause you can write hacks no matter what graphics API you use.\n\n\n\nAlso, Unreal 3.0 *will* have an opengl renderer. Don\'t forget that D3D is limited to Windows OS\'s. Linux and Mac users will need an opengl renderer anyway. I think ID, with their Doom 3, made a wise choice to go with opengl (an open standard) instead of the proprietary D3D. The reason Valve chose to go with D3D-only, is because of their ties with MS, which is always a bad thing. MS doesnt care about anything but themselves and their own money, and valve probably removed the opengl renderer to do MS a favor. Valve wouldve been better off without that Gabe dude...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1657265, 188935, 1040, 103406, 1072936800, '', 'May I direct your attention to the following statistics: /status/survey.html (/status/survey.html), please pay special attention to the section Game Renderer.\n\nWhat does this tell us? It tells us that there is an OGL renderer for Half Life 2 and that the majority of the gamers use it.\n\nOr am I wrong? Can\'t believe it myself... \n\nMaybe this statistics are not for HL2 alone, but for the older titles aswell?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1646757, 189238, 1040, 101563, 1072936800, 'Stuttering problems in HL2 update', 'We have just updated the Support FAQ for this problem with the location of BETA video drivers for nVidia and ATI based cards.\n\n\n\nWe have had many reports of people having the latest official release driver versions for their video cards, but these BETA drivers seem to fix the issue for some players. \n\n\n\nYou can find the faq here:\n\n\n\n/support.php/cg...php?p_faqid=280 (/support.php/cgi-bin/steampowered.cfg/php/enduser/std_adp.php?p_faqid=280)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1646926, 189238, 1040, 101881, 1072936800, '', 'as i posted in the other thread, the 67.20 betas work great for me.  the 66.93s are awful.\n\n\n\nBFG 6800 GT\n\n\n\nand for the love of Jah please use Driver Cleaner 3 (http://www.drivercleaner.net/) to uninstall your current drivers and FOLLOW THE DIRECTIONS TO THE LETTER.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647122, 189238, 1040, 101882, 1072936800, '', 'I have the latest ATI beta\'s, i have the patch enabled and i\'m still stuttering all over the damn place.\n\n\n\nI\'m not sacrificing visual quality for the sake of a bug/issue with the engine itself. Aside from the stuttering, the game run\'s butter smooth, so it isn\'t a framerate problem.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647242, 189238, 1040, 101883, 1072936800, '', 'Excellent that you guys are aware of the community. Will try the ATi drivers tonight. \n\nIt seems the Nvidia guys are happy with the new driver.\n\nHope this works.\n\n\n\nFor guys that say this is fixed, please try the game at the point of "follow Freeman" or the last map of \'Citidel. \'', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647363, 189238, 1040, 101883, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by M�nu \n\nJust give it up they can only make the mess even worse. I can\'t believe I paid for this S H I T! []  \n\n\n\nTry the drivers out before u mock them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647432, 189238, 1040, 101884, 1072936800, 'Stuttering problems in HL2 update', 'quote:Originally posted by PatrickM \n\nWe have just updated the Support FAQ for this problem with the location of BETA video drivers for nVidia and ATI based cards.\n\n\n\nWe have had many reports of people having the latest official release driver versions for their video cards, but these BETA drivers seem to fix the issue for some players. \n\n\n\nYou can find the faq here:\n\n\n\n/support.php/cg...php?p_faqid=280 (/support.php/cgi-bin/steampowered.cfg/php/enduser/std_adp.php?p_faqid=280)  \n\n\n\n\n\nWhat a crock of S**T - Sloppy programming and not pre-loading the sounds is what is wrong (no amount of new drivers is going to fix that!)\n\n\n\nI hope Valve are worried right now (choking on turkey hopefully), they damn well should be - This game was released in a right mess (which is a shame as there is obviously a great experience in there trying to get out past the S**T programming)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647464, 189238, 1040, 101881, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cablelag \n\nFor guys that say this is fixed, please try the game at the point of "follow Freeman" or the last map of \'Citidel. \'  \n\n\n\nno problems at all.  in fact I just recorded a demo in the last part of the Citidel (d3_citidel_05.bsp).\n\n\n\nHere it is (http://www.lament.us/_temp/lament.dem)\n\n\n\nright-click, Save As.. and save into your hl2 folder.\n\n\n\nopen the console, type playdemo lament.dem\n\n\n\nwhere else is it stuttering for you guys?  give me exact mapnames and I\'ll record demos there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647499, 189238, 1040, 101885, 1072936800, '', '2.53 GHZ P4. 1GB RAM. GeForce 6800 GT 256. Generic sound card. 2 speaker sound, medium quality, game-recommended graphics settings (including 4X AA and 1024x768).\n\n\n\nLatest OFFICIAL (non-beta) nVidia drivers, game version 1.0. Quite playable, but stutters horribly before new areas load (seemingly) and before huge events like the smokestack or the dam door getting destroyed.\n\n\n\nLatest OFFICIAL (non-beta) nVidia drivers, game version 1.0.1.0 (updated!). Stutters horribly before new areas load (seemingly) and before huge events like the smokestack or the dam door getting destroyed. IN ADDITION, sound very often clicks and framerate drops are much more consistent; game is barely playable.\n\n\n\nSams as above, but with BETA nVidia drivers: No change.\n\n\n\nTo summarize, the patch SEEMS to have made the situation worse. Just a heads up.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647513, 189238, 1040, 101881, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cablelag \n\ndid u have the problem pre-driver install? What videocard?  \n\n\n\nsee my first post above: 6800 GT.\n\n\n\nmy stuttering was slightly more before the patch (but NEVER to the point where it was annoying or unplayable)\n\n\n\nbut before the patch, I also had jumped from the 61.77 drivers (good) to the 66.93s (awful) to the current 67.02 betas.\n\n\n\nafter installing the 67.02 betas, and now the patch, i\'m happy.\n\n\n\ni had also defragged my C: drive before the patch, AND verfied my HL2 cache files as per Valve\'s suggestion.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647559, 189238, 1040, 101883, 1072936800, '', 'waiting for some ATi users to chime in. I\'ll be home in about an hour to test them.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647598, 189238, 1040, 101884, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by cablelag \n\nwaiting for some ATi users to chime in. I\'ll be home in about an hour to test them.  \n\n\n\nGood Lad!   Although I am losing the will to live with regard to getting this badly programmed and tested POS to work correctly!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647730, 189238, 1040, 101886, 1072936800, '', 'While these Cats are nice drivers, they of course don\'t do anything for the hitches that many of us experience when sounds are loading from the hard drive to memory in the game rather than being cached in memory on level load. Anyhow I installed the CCC first and then installed these drivers with CCC installed. I will say this for sure, don\'t use AI as it severly hurts things. I also think the game plays better disabling the Nov 24 patch.\n\n\n\nI gots a 9800 Pro 128mb (419/364).', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647755, 189238, 1040, 101887, 1072936800, '', 'tried it(nvidia)... doesnt work. Too bad .im trying evolution drivers now.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647810, 189238, 1040, 101888, 1072936800, '', 'Using a Geforce 6800 Ultra here with the 67.02\'s and the new HL2 patch- absolutely no stutters. The game is perfect here.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1647836, 189238, 1040, 101889, 1072936800, '', 'i have read all over the web that users of the warez version have no stuttering problems. what is the difference btwn that version and the legal one that makes the difference?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1651779, 189800, 1013, 101896, 1072936800, 'lycos declares war on spam servers', 'From slashdot.org - \n\n\n\n\n\nIT: Lycos Declares War on Spam Servers\n\n\n\nPosted by michael on Friday November 26, @09:07PM\n\nfrom the spam-it-forward dept.\n\n\n\nPsychotext writes "The Register have posted a story about a new screensaver from Lycos that targets known spam servers (taken from spamcop and verified by hand) with traffic in order to raise their bandwidth costs and hopefully price them out of the game. Lycos state that this is not a DDOS as Lycos monitors the site\'s responsiveness and throttles back when the site starts to falter. The screensaver is available here for Mac OSX, Mac OS9 and Windows, though you might need to lie about what country you are from." Reader JohnGrahamCumming writes "As part of preparing for the MIT Spam Conference I\'ve put together a survey on what people are experiencing out there with spam, what they are doing about and followed it up with a test of different views of an inbox filled with spam and ham. You can take the test and be part of the survey results in January."\n\n\n\nYou can get the screensaver from here:\n\n\n\nhttp://makelovenotspam.com/intl/ (http://makelovenotspam.com/intl/)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1652099, 189800, 1013, 101897, 1072936800, '', 'I\'m thrilled by this idea.\n\n\n\nI\'ve not done any research, but I suspect there might be some legal problems with using this screen-saver in the USA. But, if it gets enough publicity, there\'s bound to be enough places around the globe that it can be run so that it does actually place some pain on the spammers.\n\n\n\nViva "Death Wish". \n\n\n\n(A Charles Bronson movie reference. \n\n IOW - vigilantism lives.)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1657305, 190391, 1013, 101898, 1072936800, 'steampowered.com uname & pw never shows up in my mail', 'I\'ve clicked \'send me my password\' about 15 times in the last week or so and each time it tells me my password is being sent to the e-mail address that i entered. \n\n\n\nAnd it\'s yet to show up.\n\n\n\nI\'ve checked my inbox and even \'junk mail\' at least twice as many times as that.\n\n\n\nI\'ve also really enjoyed waiting a day before i can even post this message because i was stuck in some kind of \'admin queue\' \n\n\n\nRegardless, i have an existing (older) account on these forums and i\'d prefer to be using it instead of this new one.\n\n\n\nOn a seperate note, every time i click \'preview post\' i keep getting reminded that this is my first post and i never actually get to preview it.\n\n\n\nIf some one could show me how i can retrieve my password to my old steampowered.com account it\'d be greatly appreciated, thanks.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1657845, 190391, 1013, 100655, 1072936800, '', 'Are you sure you\'re looking at the same email address as your old account? Maybe past accounts that were inactive have been closed.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1658043, 190391, 1013, 101899, 1072936800, '', 'if your confused as to how to see what email your account is linked to, click settings, it says "contact email" this is the email you should be checking.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1658201, 190391, 1013, 101898, 1072936800, '', 'i can\'t send an e-mail to myself through the forum\n\n\n\nSorry! That user has specified that they do not wish to receive emails through this board. If you still wish to send an email to this user, please contact the administrator and they may be able to help.\n\n\n\nmust have turned that option off\n\n\n\nbut i\'ve only ever had 2 e-mail addresses (both hotmail) i\'m absolutely positive there\'s no ghost e-mail address that i\'ve forgotton about.\n\n\n\nAlso, when you enter an invalid e-mail address to send the password to it TELLS you its invalid, so .. again its just plain not getting through..\n\n\n\nAt no point in time have i recieved a message or e-mail that anything is inactive.\n\n\n\nThis old account has almost 400 posts on its not like i made it and never used it.. i used to use it quite a bit..', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1658249, 190391, 1013, 101900, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LGB \n\ni can\'t send an e-mail to myself through the forum\n\n \n\nNot your forum account...your STEAM account. Check to make sure the contact e-mail address in that is the same one you are checking. Otherwise, dig up the e-mail from way back when you first registered Steam and use the login info from there.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1658330, 190391, 1013, 101898, 1072936800, '', 'my steam account has a different e-mail address, in which (i\'ve already tried) if i ask for my password to be sent to that account it says the e-mail address is invalid. Which is correct, i didn\'t use that e-mail address for the steampowered forums.  I know which e-mail address i used for the steampowered forum account', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1658393, 190391, 1013, 101900, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by LGB \n\nmy steam account has a different e-mail address, in which (i\'ve already tried) if i ask for my password to be sent to that account it says the e-mail address is invalid. Which is correct, i didn\'t use that e-mail address for the steampowered forums.  I know which e-mail address i used for the steampowered forum account  \n\nIS that e-mail address invalid?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
