(1673279, 191130, 1013, 101907, 1072936800, 'System specs...', 'Thanks for your replies and support guys.  But don\'t forget to post your system specs if you\'ve tried all the suggested requirements and have run out of options trying to make the game run consistently.\n\n\n\nWhat\'s really sad is that it\'s been a week since I sent SecuROM my report and I have yet to hear back from them.  Vivendi support has only repsonded ONCE to my report, telling me to delete the ClientRegistry.blob file and restart Steam.  Not to be rude here, but I get the feeling they were just blowing me off.  I mean, you\'d think that if I spent hours writing a 2000+ word error report I\'d have at least tried that suggestion already.  Now I\'m somewhat concerned as to what their next suggestion will be, if they ever bother to respond, of course;  perhaps they\'ll tell me to make sure my PC is plugged in and powered up? []\n\n\n\n\n\nMister Marbles', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1673337, 191130, 1013, 101911, 1072936800, '', 'This topic has been posted but no one replies, so i want to post here one more time, PLEASE HELP ME!!!\n\n\n\nHello Everybody, my friend has bought me a Half-Life2 from another country, and he is going to send it to me later on and he helped me to register the HL2 and CS:S in his computer, then he have played for around 2 days, and he told me to get into that account (we talked in MSN) because he said the HL2 is so cool and he wants me to play it before the disc is sent to me, then i log in the steam and download the HL2 and CS:S from Steam and i was very excited because i have fnished downloading the 4GB Half-Life2........"Wrong CD inserted" an error message pop up after i double click the HL2 logo in my game list, i don;t even know what to do, the CD takes at least a month to ship it to me, but i want to play it now, please help, thank you very much', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1673400, 191130, 1013, 101907, 1072936800, 'My system specs...', 'I really should put my money where my mouth is, but since I find that unsanitary...\n\n\n\nCPU:  Pentium IV 3.4 GHz with Hyper-Threading technology and 800 MHz FSB\n\nRAM:  1024 SDDR RAM\n\nVIDEO:  ATi X300 SE 128 MB PCI Express using Catalyst 3.11\n\nSOUND:  Creative (Labs) Sound Blaster Audigy 2 (vanilla version)\n\nOPTICAL:  1.  Samsung CD-R/RW 252S\n\n                 2.  Philips DVD+RW 8601 firmware revision 6D11\n\nGAME:  Collector\'s Edition DVD purchased at the Best Buy in Markham, Ontario, Canada\n\n\n\nI have tried all the suggestion suggestions provided me, but nothing has worked.  The game managed to boot up ONCE and only ONCE (without the crack, that is; see below) and I have no idea how or why it did then but never before or since.\n\n\n\nI have tried using the hijack "crack" for the game and, not surprisingly, the game runs beautifully.  I have managed to talk to Valve Tech Support, but after much discussion, they could not help me; they told me to get a new DVD drive (sure thing; send me the money for it and I\'ll do it).\n\n\n\nSo I\'m stuck at this point.  Either play the game "cracked" or don\'t play at all.  Plus I can\'t play CS:S because I don\'t want to play the "cracked" game while Big Broth-err, I mean Steam is connected to the Internet. []\n\n\n\n\n\nMister Marbles', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1673424, 191130, 1013, 101910, 1072936800, '', 'wait for the cd, that is your problem, you are trying to play the retail version, and you need the cd to play that. Or you can do what I am starting to consider and find the HijackHL2 crack. This basicaly changes your ver from retail to steam so you don\'t need a disk to play. I wouldn\'t recomend this however because VALVe may shut down your account if they find out you have this and then it is realy game over. I am going to drive over to VALVe on Tues and find out the answeres on wether they are actualy going to fix the SecuROM issue, and wether it is ok for me to use a no-cd patch since I paid for the retail ver and cant play it. I am not going to try the no-cd patch until I talk to VALVe however. And I would recomend you all wait for my feedback before you risk loosing your acounts.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
