(1734969, 197721, 1040, 101585, 1072936800, '', 'and don\'t forget the gravity gun...\n\nnice post btw...', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1734990, 197721, 1040, 101504, 1072936800, '', 'Don\'t spawn with granades do you? Hey the machine guns good in rooms with loads of people, one might only have 1hp left, if not i wouldn\'t bother using it.\n\n\n\nBesides about the pistol i take it you want auto aiming on it, keep it off, i don\'t need help with my aiming.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735239, 197721, 1040, 101586, 1072936800, 'sad', 'I cant BELIEVE this is serious. Half-Life 1 had Deathmatch far before halo was out, and before that, there was quake. wtf is wrong with you? so dedicated to halo that you dont realize JUST ABOUT EVERY FPS HAS DEATHMATCH!\n\n\n\nWHY THE HELL DO YOU THINK VALVe COPIED MICROSOFT? THEY GAVE YOU THE MOST LOGICAL SELECTIONS OF GUNS TO START SO YOU DONT GET YOUR ûûû BLOWN INTO A BUILDING (hilarious.) AND DIE RIGHT WHEN YOU SPAWN. OMG WHY DO YOU COMPARE HALO 2 TO HALF-LIFE 2!?! THERE\'S NO COMPARISON THERE. ONE IS THE BEST GAME EVER, AND THE OTHER IS AN OVERPUBLISIZED P.O.S.!\n\n\n\n*turns off caps, breathes*\n\n\n\nI would like the crowbar, though.\n\n\n\nalso, the mp7 or whatever in HL2 is awesome, you just suck with it. lol.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735291, 197721, 1040, 100587, 1072936800, '', 'Doom 3 expansion is copying Half-Life 2 by adding a phyics gun.  I don\'t see anyone complaining about that.  I think HL2DM is great.  I don\'t see how people could have heart attacks over the announcement of the ability to hold 2 weapons in Halo 2.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735356, 197721, 1040, 101586, 1072936800, '', 'quote:Originally posted by 3ffici3nt \n\nDoom 3 expansion is copying Half-Life 2 by adding a phyics gun.  I don\'t see anyone complaining about that.  I think HL2DM is great.  I don\'t see how people could have heart attacks over the announcement of the ability to hold 2 weapons in Halo 2.  \n\nI agree with you. Halo 2 is so overpublicized, which is one of the 2 reasons its popular: the other one being xbox\'s are cheaper than PC\'s.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735616, 197721, 1040, 101587, 1072936800, '', 'You guys have gotta remember that Half Life has this wonderful big community behind it , and extremely skilled and experienced modders (I am soooo jealous of those guys)\n\n\n\nthe other games around at the moment are having content made for them mainly by the studio that produced them.\n\n\n\nValve embraces decent mods, adds them to the list and makes sure that everyone possible can play.\n\n\n\nHL2 DM is only going to get better, and so what if the machine gun is crappy, it might make people think a little about tactics and weapon choice.\n\n\n\njust think of those maps with only grav gun enabled, aaaaah that should be sooo much fun []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735653, 197721, 1040, 101588, 1072936800, '', 'Before you claim that HL2 DM is copying Halo2 DM try playing deathmatch in a few FPS games that have come out in the past 6 years. If it\'s copying anything that thing would be Q3.\n\n\n\nIt would appear to me that the weapon values have not been changed from single player and that players have the same amount of health as a SP NPC. So they probably just did pretty close to a direct port of SP to MP with a few small changes.\n\n\n\nI\'d bet that Valve will come out with a gameplay patch in the near future which will resolve alot of the gameplay issues based on community feedback. Issues like the magnum, how a cardboard box can have an insta-kill, the annoying rocket launcher etc.\n\n\n\nBTW if you look at HL2 single player and Halo2 single player there are alot of striking similarities though.\n\nThe poppers from Halo series = the zombies with a bunch of black headcrabs on them. You have the good guys (Marines/Resistance) who fight along side you who fight against the major bad guys (covenant/combine) and then you have the zombies who kill whatever (Flood/headcrab zombies).\n\nI\'m not saying Bungie copied Valve or vice versa because that would be really dumb.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1735680, 197721, 1040, 101589, 1072936800, 'OMG', 'That post was so long I lost interest in it. Over - Analyzing. Halo 2 is a fun MP game because of the \'one of a kind\' party list, and ranking system.  Bungie.net has so many stats for a single match that it boggles me every time I look at it. \n\n\n\nPlease, don\'t flame yet. HL2 is the best game I have EVER played. HL2 DM has topped the cake, and I can\'t wait for the mods. If HL2 had the online system, and a dedicated, instant-update, online ranking system.... nothing would touch it for years.\n\n\n\nBottom line... Halo 2 has bungie.net, Half Life 2 has everything else.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1738223, 198096, 1040, 101988, 1072936800, 'Yet another temporary "stutterbug" fix until patch release...', 'System:\n\nAthlon XP2400\n\nRadeon 9700 pro\n\nNForce2 chipset\n\n1G Dual channel DDR\n\nSeagate 160 7200 IDE\n\nSBLive\n\nSP2\n\n\n\nI\'ve tried all the cvars - none of them make a difference for me.\n\n\n\nI\'ve tried all the Catalyst drivers, public and beta.  The best performing one thus far (30-60fps minus the stutter, w/2X AA, Tri-lenear AF, no V-Sync) has been the Omega drivers:\n\nhttp://www.omegadrivers.net/ (http://www.omegadrivers.net/)\n\n\n\nEverything\'s defragged.\n\n\n\nBut nothing has been able to rid me of the "stutterbug" yet...\n\n...except for one very ODD thing:\n\n\n\n***Reducing the process priority of hl2.exe from "normal" to "low" in the Windows task manager.***\n\n\n\n...don\'t ...ask ...me ...why.  It just works for me.  And at least one other forum visiter who has tried it.\n\n\n\nOn a "playability" scale of 1-10, where before doing this would be about 5, changing this setting makes it around 9.  The unbearable stuttering is now reduced to an occasional mere hiccup. I can wait no longer for a patch to enjoy this amazing game, so this will have to do for now. \n\n\n\nI am posting this for those of you desperate for a fix, willing to try something new.  I hope it helps at least a few of you.  []\n\n\n\nIf you are unfamiliar with how to do this, here is a walkthrough (it\'s quite easy, I promise):\n\n\n\n-With HL2 loaded at the menu screen, hit the keys "ctrl+alt+delete".  This will minimize the game and bring up the Windows task manager.\n\n-In the task manager, select the "Processes" tab, locate "hl2.exe" in the list of processes below, right-click, and select "Set Priority > Low".\n\n-Close the task manager and bring HL2 back to the front.  It will take about 30-40 seconds for the game to regain control.\n\n-That\'s it!\n\n\n\nHopefully, this helps you as much as it does me.  If not, doublecheck that you have absolutely NOTHING else running in the background, as the game is now temporarily set to be the least important task running on the computer and everything ELSE gets first dibbs on CPU cycles.\n\n\n\nOnce again, I don\'t know why this works (you\'d think it would be the other way around), but (for me) it does.\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nWell, I have some even more odd news to report.\n\n\n\nI just tried out some of the trainstation level first with, then without the priority tweak using my NForce Soundstorm instead of the Live and got some amusing results:\n\n\n\nWith the tweak - the same typical hiccups, but some of the dialog is out of sync - ex; Dr Kleiner\'s first line on the video screen was absent at first, only to begin playback at the same time as his second line. No major stutters.\n\n\n\nWithout the tweak (normal priority) - a few more hiccups, no major stutters yet (my Live card st-st-st-stutters like crazy at this setting), but dialog WILDLY out of sync.  None of the Dr\'s lines played back until the 3rd line, and then all at once - also, the soldier harassing the civilian lines were delayed and piled on top of one another.\n\n\n\nSo I guess if you guys are having some bad dialog sync/playback issues, this tweak might help you there as well.  []\n\n\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nGood luck, and hopefully Valve will have this all sorted out soon enough! []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1738400, 198096, 1040, 101989, 1072936800, '', 'B...b...b.....bump!', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1738621, 198096, 1040, 101990, 1072936800, '', 'If this actually works, then it\'s some very useful stuff.\n\nGood find.\n\n\n\nPersonally I don\'t have a stutter problem, so I can\'t confirm.  But it seems that there\'s many different types of stutter problems, so it\'s unlikely this will fix them all... []', '127.0.0.1', 1),
