(1790152, 202660, 1040, 102023, 1072936800, 'My gift to all: Vehicles on dedicated servers!', 'Well all, after countless and frustrating battles with the enemy (you may know him or her as source) I have fixed being able to use buggies and airboats in multiplayer dedicated servers (both linux and windows variety)...\n\n\n\nStep 1. Download http://www.jasongaunt.pwp.blueyonder.co.uk/mpjeeps.zip (http://www.jasongaunt.pwp.blueyonder.co.uk/mpjeeps.zip) and unzip it to the hlds_l folder in linux or the source dedicated server folder in windows.\n\n\n\nStep 2. Restart your server.\n\n\n\nStep 3. For test purposes you\'ll find a very early release of a map I\'m making called fun_city there too, it includes above all things a faster jeep with 2 prisoner pods attached to the rear which freely allow players to enter and disembark.\n\n\n\nHope you all have a nice xmas, Foxdie out!\n\n\n\n[Update 2004/12/10 05:58]\n\nI\'ve made a lite version of the filepack which is significantly reduced in size (5.91MB > 41KB) but I am unable to test it, it contains just the raw lst files and original buggy and airboat vehicle script files to get you going. I\'m pretty certain it\'ll work but I\'ll need feedback. You can find this version at http://www.jasongaunt.pwp.blueyonde...pjeeps-lite.zip (http://www.jasongaunt.pwp.blueyonder.co.uk/mpjeeps-lite.zip)\n\n[/update]\n\n\n\nJason "Foxdie" Bhalla-Gaunt\n\nTotal Illusions Entertainment\n\nhttp://www.totalillusions.net/ (http://www.totalillusions.net/)\n\n#is04 on irc.gamesurge.net', '127.0.0.1', 1),
