(1831845, 206297, 1013, 102076, 1072936800, 'FPS random drop problem', '** Sorry if this thread exist I swear I\'ve searched and read tons of threads without success **\n\n\n\nWell this is my problem, I play cs 1.6 or any steam game for that matter and I\'ll have 99 - 100 fps constant then a few minutes in the game it will turn into 30-40 constant\n\n\n\nThis is what I\'ve done to try and fix it\n\n-------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nReinstalled all my ATI 9600 AIW Drivers\n\nSwitched to the Omega ATI 9600 Drivers\n\nFormated my HDD \n\nFormated the Drive that Steam is on\n\nReinstalled Steam\n\nTried Random Tweaks I found on here\n\nSearch the New for any Video Card Problems\n\nDid some Benchmark test\n\nAnd Now I\'ll all out of ideas...\n\n\n\nif anyone could help it would be appreciated\n\nthanks in advanced\n\n\n\n**************************************\n\nThese are my specs\n\n\n\nOS:    WinXP Professional 5.1 Service Pack 2 (Build #2600)  \n\nCPU:     Intel Pentium 4 , 3.00 GHz  HyperThreading Enabled\n\nMobo:    Asus P4P800 Deluxe\n\nVIDEO:    Compaq V70 ALL-IN-WONDER 9600 SERIES (1024x768x32bpp 85Hz) DirectX 9C\n\nSOUND:   SoundMAX Digital Audio \n\nMEMORY:   512MB Kingston Hyper X Ram PC3200\n\nHDD:   Seagate Barracuda 7200RPM 200GB\n\nNetwork Adapter:   3Com Gigabit LOM', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1836236, 206297, 1013, 102076, 1072936800, '', 'bump', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1836996, 206297, 1013, 102077, 1072936800, '', 'There is nothing you can do about it.  It seems to be a computer & software problem with CS & HL2.\n\n\n\nI have similar FPS that you have on a:\n\n\n\nAmd Athlon XP 2600 @2.13 ghz\n\n512mb DDr 400 ram\n\n120gb hd SATA\n\nRadeon 9800 pro\n\n\n\nI experience the same problems you have, it\'s no big deal.  It runs smoothly on my buddys Athlon 64 3500 at high settings with 4x AA & Anistropic filtering.  He has 2gb ddr 400 ram.  Ocassional stutter.\n\n\n\nAll in all it still play smoothly afterwards, just be glad you don\'t the problems other people do like long loads, constant stuttering and fps drops.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1837041, 206297, 1013, 102076, 1072936800, '', 'but I do have fps drop []\n\n\n\nThanks  for replying though', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838210, 206297, 1013, 102078, 1072936800, '', 'ATI i\'m guessing ( I could be wrong though)', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838216, 206297, 1013, 102079, 1072936800, '', 'im having this, but it drops to 1-2 (or less!) fps for a few seconds every once in a while. that once in a while is normally as soon as i walk around a corner (engine loading new things?). commonly, as soon as i walk around the corner... there is an enemy. i look like a moron, because i turn the corner, then i just STAND there, because my avatar wont move (even though im holding down a move button) and i sit there for a few seconds with less than a frame a second...    needless to say, i get killed quite a lot. its rather annoying. only started a few days ago. any ideas? i havent changed anything, and i do have a good computer. it just started, with no changes.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838224, 206297, 1013, 102078, 1072936800, '', 'comps not able to process info fast enough or video card cant which causes your freezing when looking at a new object', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838266, 206297, 1013, 102079, 1072936800, '', 'once again... i have changed nothing. i have not had this problem until just a few days ago. i have a radeon 9800, over a gig of ram, a barton 3000+..... built this baby myself, i know how she runs ^^       any ideas on how to fix this? im gonna defrag and update to the newest catalyst tonight, hopefully that will help her.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838283, 206297, 1013, 102078, 1072936800, '', 'defragging can help reformatting would be a lot better and the 1st thing you install is HL2/CS  its not your video card sounds like your CPU isn\'t processing information fast enough or could be HD either way if defrag doesnt work try killing some process free up memory if that doesnt work resort to reformat.  if still doesnt work need a new Motherboard/Processor', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1838298, 206297, 1013, 102079, 1072936800, '', 'well, i HAVE been running like 50 torrents a night for the past week or so, so maybe its just now screwing with source []     also, im not going to reformat... too much stuff i want to save. lets hope this works.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1854070, 206297, 1013, 102080, 1072936800, '', 'Same here. I\'ve just reinstalled Steam and I\'m redownloading CS:S to see if it will fix the problem. My system is different - and I should be getting a perfect framerate, in fact I was until the December 2nd patch, but now my CS:S framerate is completely unstable, jumping around between 20-200, which produces a stuttering effect that makes the game unplayable, at least if you want to have fun. \n\n\n\nI\'ll tell you if reinstalling fixes it.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1854087, 206297, 1013, 102078, 1072936800, '', 'make sure your vid card doesn\'t have options on eg V-Sync and other option which can be affecting between Source and your card.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1854318, 206297, 1013, 102079, 1072936800, '', 'the strange thing is is that i KNOW where in the map the stuttering will happen, because it is always in the same places. the sniper ct spot on dust, bombsite A on dust 2.. doesnt happen in italy or aztec, except occasionally near the railing at the t spawn on italy. its only in certain spots.... i drop from 100+ fps down to less than 1, and unless i move out of that spot, i stay like that.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1854465, 206297, 1013, 102080, 1072936800, '', 'The only maps that seem to run without the stutterbug for me are de_chateau and de_piranesi.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1859680, 206297, 1013, 102080, 1072936800, '', 'Just reinstalled Steam, with no effect. Looks like I\'m not getting a fix until VALVe decides to release one. \n\n\n\nNeedless to say, I\'m not buying anything else they\'re selling.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1860328, 208788, 1013, 101358, 1072936800, 'Steam Time Machine!', 'Ever wonder what steam was like two years ago when it first came out?  The little beta program that would cause so much debate, praise and heartache had it\'s start right here, and for those of you who haven\'t been here since then, it\'s time to visit it\'s roots:\n\n\n\nhttp://www.steampowered.com (http://web.archive.org/web/20020321021820//)\n\n\n\n(For those who want to see steam\'s evolution, use this link (http://web.archive.org/web/*//) to see more.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1860369, 208788, 1013, 102090, 1072936800, '', 'Looks cool thx for the links.\n\n_________________\n\n~ Asian Pride ~  Got Rice?', '127.0.0.1', 1),
(1860419, 208788, 1013, 101448, 1072936800, '', 'Ah pooie, I wanted to join STEAM when it first came out.. oh well I got to see the 2nd website around DEC of 2003... then got problems and joined the forums in Jan. Damn has it improved.', '127.0.0.1', 1),
